window.TWG_I18N=window.TWG_I18N||{};TWG_I18N["zh-hant"]=Object.assign(TWG_I18N["zh-hant"]||{},{"21 animated films, level Spirits 2":"21 部動畫影片，烈酒二級","I'll build you a tailor-made path to pass your Spirits 2 exam. It takes 5 quick questions.":"我會為你量身打造一條通過烈酒二級考試的學習路徑，只需要回答 5 個簡短的問題。","Spirits 2 exam":"烈酒二級考試","All of Spirits 2":"烈酒二級全部內容","Lessons, flashcards and mistakes: only the Spirits 2 syllabus.":"課程、字卡和錯題：只包含烈酒二級的課程大綱。","Spirits 2 games":"烈酒二級遊戲","Short games on Spirits 2 questions and terms.":"以烈酒二級題目和術語為主的小遊戲。","Raw materials and fermentation":"原料與發酵","How distillation works":"蒸餾如何運作","After distillation":"蒸餾之後","Fruit spirits: Cognac and Armagnac":"水果烈酒：Cognac 與 Armagnac","Calvados, Grappa and Pisco":"Calvados、Grappa 與 Pisco","Irish, Canadian and Japanese whisky":"愛爾蘭、加拿大與日本威士忌","Tequila and Mezcal":"Tequila 與 Mezcal","Other flavoured spirits":"其他調味烈酒","Liqueurs":"利口酒","Aromatised wines: vermouth":"加味葡萄酒：香艾酒","Workstation, tools and glassware":"工作檯、工具與杯具","Ingredients and balance":"材料與平衡","Tasting and judging spirits":"品飲與評判烈酒","Spirits production":"烈酒的生產","The principal spirits":"主要烈酒","Flavoured spirits, liqueurs, aromatised wines":"調味烈酒、利口酒、加味葡萄酒","f3":"f3","The bar and cocktails":"酒吧與調酒","What is the correct order of the four stages of spirit production?":"烈酒生產四個階段的正確順序是什麼？","Fermentation, raw material, distillation, compulsory ageing":"發酵、原料、蒸餾、強制陳年","Raw material, fermentation, post-distillation, distillation":"原料、發酵、蒸餾後處理、蒸餾","A sugary liquid is made first, then fermented, distilled and finally prepared for sale.":"先製作含糖液體，再發酵、蒸餾，最後做好上市前的準備。","You cannot distil a liquid that does not yet contain alcohol, so fermentation must come before distillation. Post-distillation steps such as dilution or filtration come last. Ageing is not a compulsory stage for every spirit: many are never aged.":"還不含酒精的液體無法蒸餾，所以發酵一定在蒸餾之前。稀釋或過濾等蒸餾後處理排在最後。陳年並不是每種烈酒都必經的階段：許多烈酒從不陳年。","Which two things does a raw material provide to a distiller?":"原料為蒸餾師提供哪兩樣東西？","Carbohydrates and congeners":"碳水化合物和同屬物","Yeast and carbon dioxide":"酵母和二氧化碳","Colour and sweetness ready for the bottle":"可直接裝瓶的顏色和甜味","Alcohol and enzymes":"酒精和酵素","The raw material offers a carbohydrate store for yeast and a set of flavours, the congeners.":"原料提供給酵母的碳水化合物儲備，以及一組風味，也就是同屬物。","Carbohydrates are yeast food; congeners are the flavour compounds. Yeast is added by the producer and carbon dioxide is created during fermentation. Alcohol is not in the raw material: the yeast makes it.":"碳水化合物是酵母的食物；同屬物是風味化合物。酵母由生產者添加，二氧化碳則在發酵過程中產生。原料裡沒有酒精：酒精是酵母製造的。","What are the compounds responsible for a spirit's aromas and flavours called?":"為烈酒帶來香氣和風味的化合物叫做什麼？","Congeners":"同屬物","Starches":"澱粉","Congeners are the compounds that give aroma and taste.":"同屬物是帶來香氣和味道的化合物。","Some congeners come from the raw material, others form during fermentation or maturation. Enzymes convert starch into sugar; they do not provide aroma. Starch is a carbohydrate yeast cannot use directly.":"有些同屬物來自原料，有些在發酵或熟成過程中形成。酵素把澱粉轉化為糖，並不提供香氣。澱粉是酵母無法直接利用的碳水化合物。","Which of these raw materials already contains sugars that yeast can use straight away?":"下列哪一種原料本身就含有酵母可以立刻利用的糖？","Freshly harvested raw agave":"剛採收的生龍舌蘭","Sugar cane, like grapes, stores simple sugars.":"甘蔗和葡萄一樣，儲存的是單醣。","Barley and potatoes store starch, which has to be converted with enzymes. Agave stores inulin, which only becomes sugar when cooked: raw, it is not ready for yeast.":"大麥和馬鈴薯儲存的是澱粉，必須用酵素轉化。龍舌蘭儲存的是菊糖，要烹煮後才會變成糖：生的時候酵母無法利用。","In what form does agave store its carbohydrates?":"龍舌蘭以什麼形式儲存碳水化合物？","Inulin":"菊糖","Starch":"澱粉","Sucrose ready to ferment":"可直接發酵的蔗糖","Esters":"酯類","The heart of the agave keeps its reserves as inulin.":"龍舌蘭的心以菊糖的形式保存養分。","Inulin is a complex carbohydrate, like starch, but it is typical of agave; cooking turns it into sugars. Starch is found in grains and potatoes. Esters are not carbohydrates at all: they are fruity congeners formed in fermentation.":"菊糖和澱粉一樣是複雜的碳水化合物，但它是龍舌蘭特有的；烹煮會把它變成糖。澱粉存在於穀物和馬鈴薯中。酯類根本不是碳水化合物：它們是發酵中形成的果香同屬物。","During malting, what does the sprouting barley produce?":"製麥過程中，發芽的大麥會產生什麼？","Enzymes that can turn starch into sugar":"能把澱粉轉化為糖的酵素","Alcohol, which is later concentrated in the still":"酒精，之後在蒸餾器中濃縮","Inulin, which makes the grains sweeter":"菊糖，讓穀粒變得更甜","Natural yeast ready for fermentation":"可直接用來發酵的天然酵母","The young plant releases enzymes that are later used to convert starch.":"幼芽釋放出酵素，之後用來轉化澱粉。","Dampened, warm grains sprout and produce enzymes; heat then stops the growth. When the malted barley is ground and mixed with warm water, the enzymes turn starch into sugar. No alcohol forms at this stage, and yeast is added later.":"浸濕且保持溫暖的穀粒會發芽並產生酵素；接著用熱停止生長。把麥芽大麥磨碎並與溫水混合後，酵素就把澱粉轉化為糖。這個階段不會產生酒精，酵母是之後才加入的。","A producer uses corn and wheat. What is usually done to convert their starch?":"一位生產者使用玉米和小麥。通常怎麼轉化它們的澱粉？","Cooks them in water, then adds malted barley or enzymes":"先在水中烹煮，再加入麥芽大麥或酵素","Ferments them whole with no preparation at all":"完全不經處理，整粒直接發酵","Distils them straight away to extract the sugar":"立刻蒸餾以萃取糖分","Smokes them over peat to dissolve the starch":"用泥煤煙燻以溶解澱粉","Cooking makes the starch soluble, then enzymes turn it into sugar.":"烹煮讓澱粉變得可溶，接著酵素把它轉化為糖。","Grains other than barley are usually cooked rather than malted; the enzymes come from a little malted barley or bought-in preparations. Yeast cannot eat starch, so there is no fermentation without conversion. Distillation does not extract sugar, and peat only adds smoky aroma.":"大麥以外的穀物通常是烹煮而不是製麥；酵素來自少量麥芽大麥或外購的酵素製劑。酵母吃不了澱粉，所以沒有轉化就沒有發酵。蒸餾不會萃取糖分，泥煤只會增添煙燻香氣。","How is the inulin in agave turned into sugar?":"龍舌蘭中的菊糖如何變成糖？","By cooking the piña":"烹煮 piña","By malting the leaves":"把葉片拿去製麥","By adding malted barley to the raw juice":"在生汁液中加入麥芽大麥","By distilling the raw heart":"蒸餾生的龍舌蘭心","The heat of cooking converts inulin into sugars.":"烹煮的熱度把菊糖轉化為糖。","The spiky leaves are cut off and discarded: only the heart, the piña, is used; it is cooked and then crushed to release the sweet juice. Malted barley is for grain starch, not agave. Distilling before fermentation would not produce a spirit.":"帶刺的葉片會被切除丟棄：只使用心部，也就是 piña；它先經烹煮，再壓碎以釋出甜汁。麥芽大麥是用於穀物澱粉的，不是龍舌蘭。在發酵前蒸餾不會得到烈酒。","What is the heart of the agave used for spirits called?":"用來製作烈酒的龍舌蘭心叫做什麼？","Green malt":"綠麥芽","Wort":"麥汁","Pomace":"果渣","The piña is the hard core left once the leaves are removed.":"piña 是切除葉片後留下的堅硬核心。","The piña is where the plant stores its inulin, which is why it is the valuable part. Green malt is sprouted barley before it is heated. Wort is the sweet liquid made from grains, and pomace is what is left of grapes after pressing.":"piña 是植株儲存菊糖的地方，所以它是有價值的部分。綠麥芽是加熱前的發芽大麥。麥汁是用穀物製成的甜液，果渣則是葡萄壓榨後剩下的東西。","What does yeast produce during alcoholic fermentation?":"酒精發酵過程中，酵母會產生什麼？","Alcohol, carbon dioxide and congeners":"酒精、二氧化碳和同屬物","Sugar, oxygen and colour":"糖、氧氣和顏色","Starch, water and large amounts of enzymes":"澱粉、水和大量酵素","Pure ethanol only, with nothing else":"只有純乙醇，沒有別的","Yeast consumes sugar and creates alcohol, carbon dioxide and flavours.":"酵母消耗糖，並產生酒精、二氧化碳和風味。","Sugar is the yeast's food, so it is used up, not produced. Besides ethanol, other alcohols and many congeners such as fruity esters are formed: you never get pure ethanol. Carbon dioxide is a waste product that escapes into the air.":"糖是酵母的食物，所以是被消耗掉，而不是被製造出來。除了乙醇，還會形成其他醇類和許多同屬物，例如帶果香的酯類：永遠不會得到純乙醇。二氧化碳是廢棄產物，會散逸到空氣中。","In a fermentation vat the liquid bubbles as if boiling. What causes this?":"發酵槽裡的液體冒著泡，看起來像在沸騰。原因是什麼？","Carbon dioxide released by the yeast":"酵母釋放的二氧化碳","Ethanol vapour evaporating from the surface":"從表面蒸發的乙醇蒸氣","Heat added to speed up the fermentation":"為了加快發酵而加的熱","Oxygen produced by the malt enzymes":"麥芽酵素產生的氧氣","The bubbles are carbon dioxide, a waste product of fermentation.":"氣泡是二氧化碳，也就是發酵的廢棄產物。","An active fermentation looks as if it is boiling, but the liquid is not actually boiling: it is gas rising to the surface. The ethanol stays in the liquid until it is heated in a still. Enzymes do not produce oxygen.":"旺盛的發酵看起來像在沸騰，但液體其實沒有沸騰：那是氣體升到表面。乙醇會留在液體中，直到在蒸餾器中加熱。酵素不會產生氧氣。","What is the typical alcoholic strength of the liquid at the end of fermentation?":"發酵結束時，液體的酒精濃度通常是多少？","Around 8–10% abv":"大約 8–10% abv","Around 25–30% abv":"大約 25–30% abv","Around 40% abv, ready to bottle":"大約 40% abv，可直接裝瓶","Around 1–2% abv":"大約 1–2% abv","Distillers usually aim for a fermented liquid of about 8–10% abv.":"蒸餾師通常以大約 8–10% abv 的發酵液為目標。","25–30% abv is the strength of low wines after a first pot-still distillation. 40% is a typical bottling strength, reached only after distillation and dilution. Fermentation alone cannot reach these levels.":"25–30% abv 是壺式蒸餾器第一次蒸餾後低度酒的濃度。40% 是典型的裝瓶濃度，要經過蒸餾和稀釋才能達到。光靠發酵無法達到這些濃度。","When does alcoholic fermentation end?":"酒精發酵什麼時候結束？","When all the sugar has been converted":"所有的糖都被轉化之後","When the liquid reaches 40% abv":"液體達到 40% abv 時","After exactly twenty-four hours in every distillery":"在每一家蒸餾廠都是剛好二十四小時後","When starch begins to form":"澱粉開始形成時","Once the sugar is gone, the yeast has nothing left to convert.":"糖一用完，酵母就沒有東西可以轉化了。","Fermentation stops when the yeast's food runs out, usually at around 8–10% abv. 40% abv cannot be reached by fermentation. There is no fixed duration shared by everyone, and starch does not form during fermentation.":"酵母的食物耗盡時發酵就停止，通常在 8–10% abv 左右。發酵無法達到 40% abv。沒有大家通用的固定時間，發酵過程中也不會形成澱粉。","Which alcohol makes up by far the largest part of the fermented liquid?":"在發酵液中，哪一種醇所占的比例遠高於其他？","Ethanol":"乙醇","Methanol":"甲醇","Fusel alcohols":"雜醇","Ethanol accounts for the vast majority of the alcohol volume.":"乙醇占了酒精體積的絕大部分。","Methanol and fusel alcohols are present, but in much smaller amounts. Ethanol is the alcohol that distillation concentrates most and that gives a spirit its strength. Glycerol is not one of the key alcohols discussed here.":"甲醇和雜醇也存在，但量少得多。乙醇是蒸餾時濃縮最多、並賦予烈酒酒精濃度的醇。甘油不屬於這裡討論的主要醇類。","Which group of congeners, formed in fermentation, has a fruity smell?":"哪一類在發酵中形成的同屬物帶有果香？","Inulins":"菊糖","Caramels":"焦糖","Esters are fruity-smelling congeners created in fermentation.":"酯類是發酵中產生、帶果香的同屬物。","Enzymes turn starch into sugar and inulin is agave's carbohydrate: neither is an aroma. Caramel is a colouring added after distillation, not a product of fermentation.":"酵素把澱粉轉化為糖，菊糖是龍舌蘭的碳水化合物：兩者都不是香氣。焦糖色是蒸餾後添加的色素，不是發酵的產物。","Why do nearly all distillers use selected yeast?":"為什麼幾乎所有蒸餾師都使用選育酵母？","To get the same congeners every time":"為了每次都得到相同的同屬物","To reach over 20% abv during fermentation":"為了在發酵時達到 20% abv 以上","To avoid having to distil the liquid twice":"為了不必把液體蒸餾兩次","To convert starch without needing enzymes":"為了不靠酵素就能轉化澱粉","Selected yeast gives a reliable, consistent result batch after batch.":"選育酵母能一批又一批帶來可靠、一致的結果。","Many congeners are formed in fermentation, and an aroma missing after fermentation cannot appear in the spirit. That is why consistent yeast is essential. Yeast does not convert starch and does not change how many distillations are needed.":"許多同屬物在發酵中形成，發酵後缺少的香氣不可能出現在烈酒中。所以穩定一致的酵母至關重要。酵母不會轉化澱粉，也不會改變需要蒸餾的次數。","A desired aroma is missing from the fermented liquid. What will happen after distillation?":"發酵液中缺少一種想要的香氣。蒸餾後會怎麼樣？","It will also be missing from the new spirit":"新酒中同樣不會有","It will appear thanks to the heat of the still":"蒸餾器的熱會讓它出現","It will form in the heads, during the first cut of the second distillation":"它會在酒頭中形成，也就是第二次蒸餾的第一次切取時","It will develop if distilled to a higher strength":"蒸餾到更高濃度就會發展出來","Distillation can only select and concentrate what is already present.":"蒸餾只能篩選並濃縮原本就存在的東西。","The still does not create new aromas: it separates and concentrates existing ones. Distilling to a higher strength actually reduces the number of congeners. The heads contain volatile, solvent-smelling compounds, not new aromas appearing from nowhere.":"蒸餾器不會創造新的香氣：它只是分離並濃縮現有的香氣。蒸餾到更高的濃度其實會減少同屬物的數量。酒頭含有易揮發、帶溶劑氣味的化合物，而不是憑空出現的新香氣。","A US label says 90 proof. What strength is that?":"一張美國酒標上寫著 90 proof。這是多少濃度？","45% abv":"45% abv","90% abv":"90% abv","30% abv":"30% abv","60% abv":"60% abv","Two degrees proof equal 1% abv, so 90 proof = 45% abv.":"2 度 proof 等於 1% abv，所以 90 proof = 45% abv。","Simply halve the proof figure. Mixing up proof and abv would suggest 90%, the strength of a near-neutral spirit. The word 'overproof' seen on some rum labels belongs to a different, historic system that is no longer used.":"只要把 proof 的數字除以二。把 proof 和 abv 搞混會以為是 90%，那是接近中性烈酒的濃度。某些蘭姆酒酒標上的「overproof」一詞屬於另一套已不再使用的舊制度。","Which spirit is the exception because nearly all congeners are removed?":"哪一種烈酒是例外，因為幾乎所有同屬物都被去除？","Rhum agricole":"Rhum agricole","In vodka, the producer removes almost all congeners, so the raw material shows little.":"在伏特加中，生產者去除了幾乎所有同屬物，所以原料的特色不太明顯。","Tequila, Cognac and rhum agricole aim instead to keep raw-material character: Tequila, for instance, always shows earthy, peppery blue-agave notes. Vodka is designed to be almost neutral.":"Tequila、Cognac 和 rhum agricole 則力求保留原料特色：例如 Tequila 總是帶有藍色龍舌蘭的土壤和胡椒氣息。伏特加的設計就是要近乎中性。","Why can a small flaw in the raw material spoil a spirit?":"為什麼原料的小瑕疵會毀掉一款烈酒？","Because distillation concentrates it":"因為蒸餾會把它濃縮","Because yeast always turns it into pure methanol":"因為酵母總會把它變成純甲醇","Because it blocks starch conversion":"因為它會阻礙澱粉轉化","Because it darkens the spirit during final bottling":"因為它會在最後裝瓶時讓烈酒顏色變深","Distillation concentrates aromas, faulty ones included.":"蒸餾會濃縮香氣，有瑕疵的香氣也不例外。","As in a reduced sauce, something barely noticeable becomes obvious. That is why a quality spirit needs quality raw materials. The other answers describe effects that have nothing to do with concentration.":"就像收汁的醬汁一樣，原本幾乎察覺不到的東西會變得明顯。所以優質烈酒需要優質原料。其他答案描述的效果都與濃縮無關。","For a potato vodka, how is the starch converted into sugar?":"製作馬鈴薯伏特加時，澱粉如何轉化為糖？","Cooking in water, then bought-in enzymes":"先在水中烹煮，再加入外購的酵素","Malting the potatoes in a warm room":"把馬鈴薯放在溫暖的房間裡製麥","Direct fermentation of raw, chopped potatoes":"把生馬鈴薯切塊後直接發酵","Slow cooking in brick ovens, as for agave":"像龍舌蘭一樣在磚爐中慢慢烹煮","Cooked potatoes become a liquid full of dissolved starch, then enzymes turn it into sugar.":"煮過的馬鈴薯變成充滿溶解澱粉的液體，接著酵素把澱粉轉化為糖。","It is a two-step process: cooking makes the starch soluble and enzymes convert it. Potatoes are not malted, and raw they cannot ferment because yeast does not eat starch. With agave, heat alone works because inulin behaves differently from starch.":"這是兩步驟的過程：烹煮讓澱粉可溶，酵素再加以轉化。馬鈴薯不會製麥，生的也無法發酵，因為酵母不吃澱粉。龍舌蘭只靠熱就行，是因為菊糖的性質和澱粉不同。","Which statement about the sugary liquid a spirit starts from is true?":"關於烈酒起點的含糖液體，下列哪一項正確？","It can come from any farm product with carbohydrates":"可以來自任何含碳水化合物的農產品","It can only come from grapes or other fruit":"只能來自葡萄或其他水果","It must always contain at least 10% alcohol before fermentation":"發酵前一定要含有至少 10% 的酒精","It is made only from malted grains":"只能用麥芽穀物製成","Grapes, grains, cane, potatoes, agave: all that is needed is carbohydrate.":"葡萄、穀物、甘蔗、馬鈴薯、龍舌蘭：只需要有碳水化合物。","The whole aim of the first stage is to turn carbohydrates into a sugary liquid. There is no alcohol before fermentation, so the third option is impossible. Fruit and malted grains are only some of the many possible raw materials.":"第一階段的目標就是把碳水化合物變成含糖液體。發酵前沒有酒精，所以第三個選項不可能成立。水果和麥芽穀物只是眾多可用原料中的一部分。","In what form do grains store their carbohydrates?":"穀物以什麼形式儲存碳水化合物？","Simple sugars ready for the yeast":"酵母可直接利用的單醣","Inulin, like agave":"菊糖，和龍舌蘭一樣","Grains store starch, which must be turned into sugar before fermentation.":"穀物儲存的是澱粉，發酵前必須先轉化為糖。","Barley, corn, wheat and rye hold starch, which yeast cannot feed on directly. Inulin is agave's store, not that of grains. Esters are fruity congeners made during fermentation, not a plant's reserve.":"大麥、玉米、小麥和黑麥含有澱粉，酵母無法直接利用。菊糖是龍舌蘭的儲備，不是穀物的。酯類是發酵中產生的果香同屬物，不是植物的養分儲備。","Which pair of raw materials needs its carbohydrates converted before fermentation?":"哪一組原料必須先轉化碳水化合物才能發酵？","Grains and agave":"穀物和龍舌蘭","Grapes and sugar cane":"葡萄和甘蔗","Freshly picked and pressed apples and pears":"剛採收並壓榨的蘋果和梨","Grapes and molasses":"葡萄和糖蜜","Grains (starch) and agave (inulin) hold complex carbohydrates that must become sugars.":"穀物（澱粉）和龍舌蘭（菊糖）含有複雜的碳水化合物，必須先變成糖。","Grapes, fruit, cane juice and molasses already hold sugars the yeast can use. Grains need enzymes, and agave needs its piña cooked. That is why raw-material processing differs so much between spirits.":"葡萄、水果、甘蔗汁和糖蜜本來就含有酵母可以利用的糖。穀物需要酵素，龍舌蘭則需要烹煮 piña。這就是為什麼不同烈酒的原料處理方式差別這麼大。","What is the aim of the stage of selecting and processing the raw material?":"挑選和處理原料這個階段的目標是什麼？","To obtain a sugary liquid":"得到含糖液體","To obtain an already alcoholic liquid of about 10% abv":"得到已含酒精、約 10% abv 的液體","To remove all the congeners":"去除所有同屬物","The aim is to use the raw material's carbohydrates to create a sugary liquid.":"目標是利用原料的碳水化合物製作出含糖液體。","The roughly 10% alcoholic liquid only appears later, with fermentation. The raw material's congeners are often valuable, so they are not removed at this stage. Colour comes after distillation.":"約 10% 的含酒精液體要到之後發酵時才出現。原料的同屬物往往很有價值，所以這個階段不會去除。顏色是蒸餾之後才有的。","What does 'abv' mean?":"「abv」是什麼意思？","The percentage of the liquid's volume that is alcohol":"酒精占液體體積的百分比","The weight of alcohol in grams per litre":"每公升所含酒精的公克數","The proof system used in the USA":"美國使用的 proof 制度","The amount of sugar left after fermentation":"發酵後剩下的糖量","abv stands for alcohol by volume: 10% abv means a tenth of the liquid is alcohol.":"abv 代表酒精體積百分比（alcohol by volume）：10% abv 表示液體的十分之一是酒精。","It is a volume measure, not a weight. Proof is a different US scale: two degrees proof equal 1% abv. Residual sugar is irrelevant: by the end of fermentation it has all been used up.":"它是體積的度量，不是重量。proof 是美國另一套標度：2 度 proof 等於 1% abv。殘糖與此無關：發酵結束時糖已全部用完。","Which product of fermentation is treated as waste?":"發酵的哪一種產物被視為廢棄物？","The fruity-smelling esters":"帶果香的酯類","The congeners the distiller will later select in the still":"蒸餾師之後會在蒸餾器中篩選的同屬物","The CO₂ escapes: the distiller is interested in the alcohol and congeners.":"CO₂ 會散逸：蒸餾師感興趣的是酒精和同屬物。","Ethanol, esters and other congeners are exactly what distillation will select and concentrate. Carbon dioxide, by contrast, leaves the liquid as bubbles and plays no part in the spirit.":"乙醇、酯類和其他同屬物正是蒸餾要篩選並濃縮的東西。二氧化碳則以氣泡的形式離開液體，與烈酒毫無關係。","Besides ethanol, which important alcohols are found in the fermented liquid?":"除了乙醇，發酵液中還有哪些重要的醇類？","Methanol and fusel alcohols":"甲醇和雜醇","Esters and inulin":"酯類和菊糖","None: ethanol is the only alcohol yeast produce":"沒有：乙醇是酵母產生的唯一一種醇","Sugar and starch":"糖和澱粉","Alongside ethanol, by far the main one, there are methanol and fusel alcohols.":"除了占絕大多數的乙醇，還有甲醇和雜醇。","Yeast make many different alcohols, even though ethanol takes up almost all the alcohol volume. Esters are congeners and inulin is an agave carbohydrate. Sugar and starch are not alcohols.":"酵母會製造許多不同的醇，雖然乙醇幾乎占了全部的酒精體積。酯類是同屬物，菊糖是龍舌蘭的碳水化合物。糖和澱粉不是醇。","Where do the congeners in a fermented liquid come from?":"發酵液中的同屬物來自哪裡？","Partly from the raw material, partly from fermentation":"部分來自原料，部分來自發酵","Only from the raw material":"只來自原料","Only from the still, which creates them by heating the liquid":"只來自蒸餾器，由加熱液體而產生","Only from the oak barrel":"只來自橡木桶","Some congeners come straight from the raw material, others are created during fermentation.":"有些同屬物直接來自原料，有些則在發酵過程中產生。","Fruity esters, for instance, are made by yeast. The still invents no aromas: it selects and concentrates those already there. Oak adds further congeners, but only after distillation.":"例如帶果香的酯類就是酵母製造的。蒸餾器不會發明任何香氣：它只篩選並濃縮原有的香氣。橡木會再增添同屬物，但那是蒸餾之後的事。","All Tequilas share earthy, peppery notes. Where do they come from?":"所有 Tequila 都帶有土壤和胡椒氣息。它們來自哪裡？","From the raw material, blue agave":"來自原料藍色龍舌蘭","From the barrels Tequila must legally age in":"來自 Tequila 依法必須陳年的桶","From peat smoke used in cooking":"來自烹煮時使用的泥煤煙","From flavourings added after distillation":"來自蒸餾後添加的調味料","These aromas come with the raw material: an example of how much the ingredient matters.":"這些香氣隨原料而來：這個例子說明了原料有多重要。","A raw material gives two things: carbohydrates and its own set of flavours. Tequila need not be aged, peat concerns malted barley, and no added flavourings are needed for these notes.":"原料提供兩樣東西：碳水化合物和它自己的一組風味。Tequila 不一定要陳年，泥煤與麥芽大麥有關，這些氣息也不需要添加調味料。","Why are some distillers not free to choose their raw material?":"為什麼有些蒸餾師不能自由選擇原料？","Local laws set it for certain styles":"當地法律為某些類型規定了原料","Because selected yeasts work with only one sugar":"因為選育酵母只對一種糖起作用","Because column stills only accept grains":"因為柱式蒸餾器只能處理穀物","Because each country grows only one farm raw material":"因為每個國家只種植一種農業原料","Anyone making a protected style, such as Tequila, must follow its raw-material rules.":"製作受保護類型（例如 Tequila）的人，都必須遵守它的原料規定。","In principle a spirit can be made from any farm product with carbohydrates. The limits come from the law for that type of spirit. Neither yeast nor stills restrict the choice to one raw material.":"原則上，任何含碳水化合物的農產品都能製成烈酒。限制來自該類烈酒的法規。酵母和蒸餾器都不會把選擇限制在單一原料。","Which of these is NOT produced by yeast during fermentation?":"下列哪一項不是酵母在發酵過程中產生的？","Fruity-smelling esters":"帶果香的酯類","Carbon dioxide rising to the surface":"升到表面的二氧化碳","Starch is a starting carbohydrate in some raw materials, not something yeast make.":"澱粉是某些原料中起始的碳水化合物，不是酵母製造的東西。","Yeast consume sugars and produce alcohols, congeners such as esters, and carbon dioxide. Starch, by contrast, must be turned into sugar before fermentation can even start.":"酵母消耗糖，並產生醇類、酯類等同屬物和二氧化碳。澱粉則必須先變成糖，發酵才能開始。","Why is the green malt heated during malting?":"製麥過程中為什麼要加熱綠麥芽？","To stop growth once the enzymes have been made":"在酵素產生後停止生長","To ferment the grains directly":"讓穀粒直接發酵","To destroy the enzymes, which would spoil the sugar":"破壞會損害糖分的酵素","To caramelise the starch and colour the future whisky":"讓澱粉焦糖化，為日後的威士忌上色","After a few days the young plant has done its job: heat kills it and ends malting.":"幾天後幼芽已完成任務：熱把它殺死，製麥就此結束。","The enzymes are needed afterwards, when the ground malted barley is mixed with warm water to turn starch into sugar. Fermentation needs a sugary liquid and yeast, not whole grains. Whisky's colour does not come from this step.":"之後還需要酵素：把磨碎的麥芽大麥與溫水混合時，要靠它們把澱粉轉化為糖。發酵需要的是含糖液體和酵母，不是整粒穀物。威士忌的顏色不是來自這個步驟。","A distillery switches to a different yeast strain. What is most likely?":"一家蒸餾廠換用不同的酵母菌株。最可能發生什麼事？","The new spirit's aromas will change":"新酒的香氣會改變","Nothing, because distillation erases any difference":"什麼都不會變，因為蒸餾會抹去所有差異","Only the spirit's colour will change":"只有烈酒的顏色會改變","Fermentation will no longer exceed 2% abv":"發酵將無法超過 2% abv","Yeast create many congeners: a different strain changes the liquid's aroma profile and so the spirit's.":"酵母會產生許多同屬物：換一種菌株會改變液體的香氣輪廓，烈酒也就跟著改變。","That is exactly why most distillers use reliable, selected yeast. Distillation concentrates what is there; it does not erase differences. The distillate is colourless anyway, and a new yeast does not stop fermentation at such a low level.":"這正是大多數蒸餾師使用可靠的選育酵母的原因。蒸餾會濃縮現有的東西，不會抹去差異。餾出液反正是無色的，新的酵母也不會讓發酵停在這麼低的濃度。","Which statement about raw materials is FALSE?":"關於原料，下列哪一項是錯誤的？","Only grains and grapes may be used":"只能使用穀物和葡萄","They provide food for the yeast":"它們為酵母提供食物","They can give the spirit its own flavours":"它們能賦予烈酒本身的風味","They must be top quality, as flaws get concentrated":"必須品質優良，因為瑕疵會被濃縮","A spirit can be made from any farm product that contains carbohydrates.":"任何含碳水化合物的農產品都能製成烈酒。","The other three statements are true: the raw material feeds the yeast, brings its own aromatic character and must be sound, since distillation amplifies flaws too. Cane, agave, potatoes and fruit are examples beyond grains and grapes.":"其他三項都正確：原料餵養酵母、帶來自己的香氣特色，而且必須完好，因為蒸餾也會放大瑕疵。除了穀物和葡萄，甘蔗、龍舌蘭、馬鈴薯和水果都是例子。","What is the correct order of steps to make wort from barley?":"用大麥製作麥汁，正確的步驟順序是什麼？","Sprouting, heating, grinding, warm water":"發芽、加熱、磨碎、溫水","Grinding, warm water, sprouting, heating":"磨碎、溫水、發芽、加熱","Heating, sprouting, yeast, grinding":"加熱、發芽、酵母、磨碎","Sprouting, yeast, heating, warm water":"發芽、酵母、加熱、溫水","First the barley sprouts and makes enzymes, then heat stops it; next it is ground and mixed with warm water.":"大麥先發芽並產生酵素，接著用熱讓它停止；然後磨碎並與溫水混合。","In the warm water the enzymes turn starch into sugar and wort is formed. Yeast only come in afterwards, once the sweet liquid is ready. Heating before sprouting would prevent the enzymes from forming.":"在溫水中，酵素把澱粉轉化為糖，形成麥汁。酵母要等甜液準備好之後才加入。在發芽前加熱會讓酵素無法形成。","Which of these is a congener?":"下列哪一項是同屬物？","A fruity-smelling ester":"帶果香的酯類","The starch stored in cereal grains":"儲存在穀粒中的澱粉","Congeners are the compounds responsible for aromas and flavours, such as fruity esters.":"同屬物是帶來香氣和風味的化合物，例如帶果香的酯類。","Water is the main component of the fermented liquid but gives no aroma. Carbon dioxide is a waste product that escapes. Starch is a carbohydrate to be converted, not an aroma compound.":"水是發酵液的主要成分，但不帶來香氣。二氧化碳是會散逸的廢棄產物。澱粉是有待轉化的碳水化合物，不是香氣化合物。","Which statement about esters is correct?":"關於酯類，下列哪一項正確？","They are fruity congeners made in fermentation":"它們是發酵中產生的果香同屬物","They are agave's stored carbohydrates":"它們是龍舌蘭儲存的碳水化合物","They come only from the oak barrel":"它們只來自橡木桶","They are the cheesy, plastic-smelling compounds typical of the tails":"它們是酒尾典型的、帶乳酪和塑膠氣味的化合物","Esters are an important group of fruity-smelling congeners formed during fermentation.":"酯類是發酵過程中形成的一類重要的果香同屬物。","Agave's carbohydrate is inulin. Oak brings other aromas such as vanilla and spice. Cheesy, plastic notes belong to the less volatile congeners of the tails.":"龍舌蘭的碳水化合物是菊糖。橡木帶來的是香草和香料等其他香氣。乳酪和塑膠氣息屬於酒尾中較不易揮發的同屬物。","What do grain starch and agave inulin have in common?":"穀物的澱粉和龍舌蘭的菊糖有什麼共同點？","They are complex carbohydrates yeast cannot use directly":"它們是酵母無法直接利用的複雜碳水化合物","They are simple sugars ready to ferment":"它們是可直接發酵的單醣","They are fruity congeners":"它們是果香同屬物","They are alcohols formed while raw materials are cooked":"它們是烹煮原料時形成的醇類","Both are stores of complex carbohydrate that must be turned into sugars before fermentation.":"兩者都是複雜碳水化合物的儲備，發酵前必須先變成糖。","Starch needs enzymes (malted barley or bought-in enzymes), inulin needs the piña cooked. They are neither ready sugars, congeners nor alcohols: alcohol only appears with yeast.":"澱粉需要酵素（麥芽大麥或外購酵素），菊糖需要烹煮 piña。它們既不是現成的糖，也不是同屬物或醇：酒精要有酵母才會出現。","What do yeast feed on during alcoholic fermentation?":"酒精發酵過程中，酵母以什麼為食？","Unconverted starch, with no processing needed":"未經轉化的澱粉，不需任何處理","Yeast consume the sugars in the liquid and produce alcohols, congeners and carbon dioxide.":"酵母消耗液體中的糖，並產生醇類、同屬物和二氧化碳。","Ethanol and carbon dioxide are what yeast produce, not what they eat. Starch must first become sugar, which is why grains and potatoes need enzymes.":"乙醇和二氧化碳是酵母的產物，不是它們的食物。澱粉必須先變成糖，所以穀物和馬鈴薯才需要酵素。","Why does a spirit need distillation if fermentation already makes alcohol?":"既然發酵已經產生酒精，為什麼烈酒還需要蒸餾？","Fermentation only reaches about 8–10% abv":"發酵只能達到大約 8–10% abv","Fermentation only makes methanol":"發酵只會產生甲醇","Distillation is mainly there to add colour":"蒸餾主要是為了上色","Fermentation already gives 75% abv, but the liquid is cloudy and only needs clearing":"發酵已經能達到 75% abv，只是液體混濁，需要澄清而已","The fermented liquid is around 8–10% abv; distillation concentrates the ethanol and selects the congeners.":"發酵液大約是 8–10% abv；蒸餾會濃縮乙醇並篩選同屬物。","Ethanol, not methanol, is by far the main alcohol of fermentation. Newly made spirit is colourless. A level like 75% is only reached by distillation.":"發酵產生的醇以乙醇占絕大多數，不是甲醇。新酒是無色的。75% 這樣的濃度只有靠蒸餾才能達到。","Do most distillers grow their own raw material?":"大多數蒸餾師自己種植原料嗎？","No: most buy it in":"不：大多數是買進的","Yes, the law requires it everywhere":"是的，各地法律都這樣規定","Yes, all except vodka producers":"是的，除了伏特加生產者以外都是","No: they only ever buy finished spirit from others":"不：他們一律只向別人購買成品烈酒","Only a very few grow their raw material, such as some small Cognac distillers; most buy it in.":"只有極少數人自己種植原料，例如 Cognac 的一些小型蒸餾師；大多數是買進的。","There is no general obligation to grow your own. Those who start from a raw material ferment and distil it; others buy in spirit, but that is not the rule for everyone.":"沒有必須自己種植的普遍規定。從原料開始做的人會自行發酵和蒸餾；也有人買進烈酒，但這並不是所有人的做法。","A brandy distiller uses grape juice. Must any carbohydrates be converted before fermenting?":"一位白蘭地蒸餾師使用葡萄汁。發酵前需要轉化碳水化合物嗎？","No: grape juice already holds fermentable sugars":"不需要：葡萄汁本來就含有可發酵的糖","Yes, it must be malted like barley":"需要，必須像大麥一樣製麥","Yes, it must be cooked like an agave piña":"需要，必須像龍舌蘭的 piña 一樣烹煮","Yes, bought-in enzymes are needed as grapes are mostly starch":"需要，因為葡萄主要是澱粉，要用外購酵素","Grapes store their carbohydrate as sugars, so fermentation can begin straight away.":"葡萄以糖的形式儲存碳水化合物，所以可以立刻開始發酵。","Malting, cooking and enzymes are for starch and inulin, meaning grains, potatoes and agave. Grapes contain no starch to convert.":"製麥、烹煮和酵素是用來處理澱粉和菊糖的，也就是穀物、馬鈴薯和龍舌蘭。葡萄不含需要轉化的澱粉。","Which of these is NOT one of the four key production stages?":"下列哪一項不屬於四個主要生產階段？","Ageing in the bottle":"瓶中陳年","Selecting and processing the raw material":"挑選和處理原料","The four stages are raw material, fermentation, distillation and post-distillation operations.":"四個階段是原料、發酵、蒸餾和蒸餾後處理。","Bottle ageing is not part of this framework: maturation, when there is any, takes place in barrels or inert vessels, among the post-distillation operations.":"瓶中陳年不在這個架構內：如果有熟成，是在桶中或惰性容器中進行，屬於蒸餾後處理。","At which of the four stages does the distiller make choices that shape style and quality?":"蒸餾師在四個階段中的哪一個做出影響風格和品質的選擇？","At all four":"四個階段都有","Only at distillation":"只在蒸餾時","Only after distillation":"只在蒸餾之後","Only in choosing the raw material, since the rest is set by law":"只在選擇原料時，因為其他都由法律規定","At every stage, from raw material to finishing, the distiller has choices to make.":"從原料到收尾處理，每個階段蒸餾師都有選擇要做。","The laws for some spirits can limit these choices but do not remove them. Yeast, cuts, barrels and blending are all examples of decisions that change the result.":"某些烈酒的法規會限制這些選擇，但不會讓選擇消失。酵母、切取、桶和調和，都是會改變結果的決定。","What is the liquid mostly made of at the end of fermentation?":"發酵結束時，液體主要由什麼組成？","Water and alcohols":"水和醇類","Almost pure ethanol":"幾乎純的乙醇","Esters and other congeners, with very little water":"酯類和其他同屬物，水很少","The fermented liquid is mostly water and alcohols, chiefly ethanol.":"發酵液主要是水和醇類，其中以乙醇為主。","By the end of fermentation the sugar is used up. At 8–10% abv the ethanol is far from pure. Congeners matter hugely for aroma but are a small part of the volume.":"發酵結束時糖已經用完。8–10% abv 的乙醇離純還很遠。同屬物對香氣極為重要，但只占體積的一小部分。","Which of these could NOT be the raw material for a spirit?":"下列哪一項不可能作為烈酒的原料？","Sea salt":"海鹽","Rice":"米","Dates, rich in natural sugars":"富含天然糖分的椰棗","A spirit needs a farm product containing carbohydrates; salt is neither agricultural nor a source of sugar.":"烈酒需要含碳水化合物的農產品；鹽既不是農產品，也不是糖的來源。","Potatoes and rice hold starch to convert, dates ready sugars: all could in principle become a spirit. Without carbohydrates, yeast would have nothing to turn into alcohol.":"馬鈴薯和米含有待轉化的澱粉，椰棗含有現成的糖：原則上都能製成烈酒。沒有碳水化合物，酵母就沒有東西可以轉化為酒精。","Malting barley, cooking agave and pressing fruit: which stage do these belong to?":"大麥製麥、烹煮龍舌蘭、壓榨水果：這些屬於哪個階段？","Post-distillation operations, before bottling":"裝瓶前的蒸餾後處理","These are all ways of getting a sugary liquid to ferment from the raw material.":"這些都是從原料得到可發酵含糖液體的方法。","Fermentation only starts afterwards, when yeast is added to the sugary liquid. Distillation and later steps work on an already alcoholic liquid.":"發酵要到之後才開始，也就是在含糖液體中加入酵母時。蒸餾和之後的步驟處理的是已含酒精的液體。","One litre of fermented liquid at 10% abv: how much alcohol does it contain?":"一公升 10% abv 的發酵液含有多少酒精？","About 100 ml":"大約 100 ml","About 10 ml":"大約 10 ml","About 200 ml, since it is counted in proof":"大約 200 ml，因為是用 proof 計算","About 10 grams of unconverted sugar":"大約 10 公克未轉化的糖","10% of the volume is alcohol: in 1,000 ml that is about 100 ml.":"體積的 10% 是酒精：1,000 ml 中大約有 100 ml。","abv is a percentage of volume, not a weight or a sugar measure. Proof is another way of writing it (10% abv = 20 proof), but it does not change the real amount of alcohol.":"abv 是體積百分比，不是重量，也不是糖的度量。proof 是另一種寫法（10% abv = 20 proof），但不會改變實際的酒精量。","From about 10% after fermentation to about 75% after distillation: roughly how much is the ethanol concentrated?":"從發酵後約 10% 到蒸餾後約 75%：乙醇大約被濃縮了多少倍？","About seven and a half times":"大約七倍半","About twice":"大約兩倍","About a hundred times":"大約一百倍","It is not concentrated: only the liquid's colour changes":"沒有濃縮：只有液體的顏色改變","Going from 10% to 75% means concentrating the ethanol about 7.5 times.":"從 10% 到 75% 表示乙醇被濃縮了大約 7.5 倍。","This concentrating effect also applies to the congeners kept, and to any flaws in the raw material, which is why sound ingredients matter. Newly made spirit stays colourless.":"這種濃縮效果也適用於保留下來的同屬物，以及原料的任何瑕疵，所以完好的原料很重要。新酒仍然是無色的。","To select and concentrate parts of the liquid":"篩選並濃縮液體中的某些部分","To turn sugar into alcohol using heat":"用熱把糖變成酒精","To give colour and sweetness to the fermented liquid before sale":"在上市前為發酵液增添顏色和甜味","To remove all the alcohol except water":"去除所有酒精，只留下水","Distillation picks out certain parts, mainly ethanol and wanted congeners, and leaves others behind.":"蒸餾挑出某些部分，主要是乙醇和想要的同屬物，並把其他部分留下。","Sugar becomes alcohol during fermentation, not in the still. A newly made spirit is colourless and dry: colour and sweetness only come later. Water is precisely the part that is largely discarded.":"糖是在發酵時變成酒精的，不是在蒸餾器中。新酒無色且不甜：顏色和甜味都是之後才有的。水正是大部分被捨棄的部分。","Why is the vapour from a boiling fermented liquid more alcoholic than the liquid?":"為什麼發酵液沸騰時的蒸氣比液體本身含更多酒精？","Ethanol boils at a lower temperature than water":"乙醇的沸點比水低","Water boils at a lower temperature than ethanol":"水的沸點比乙醇低","The copper in the still turns water into alcohol":"蒸餾器的銅把水變成酒精","The yeast keeps fermenting inside the hot still":"酵母在高溫的蒸餾器裡繼續發酵","Ethanol is more volatile, so a larger share of it goes into the vapour.":"乙醇更容易揮發，所以有更大比例進入蒸氣。","Pure ethanol boils at about 78 °C and water at 100 °C: that difference is what makes separation possible. Copper does not create alcohol, and yeast does not survive boiling.":"純乙醇大約在 78 °C 沸騰，水在 100 °C：這個差異讓分離成為可能。銅不會產生酒精，酵母也無法在沸騰中存活。","What are the individual parts of a liquid to be distilled called?":"待蒸餾液體中的各個組成部分叫做什麼？","Fractions":"餾分","Cuts":"切取點","Plates":"蒸餾板","Low wines":"低度酒","Each component with its own boiling point is called a fraction.":"每個有自己沸點的成分稱為一個餾分。","A cut is the moment the flow is redirected. Plates are parts of a column still. Low wines are the liquid from the first pot-still distillation.":"切取點是把酒液流向改道的時刻。蒸餾板是柱式蒸餾器的零件。低度酒是壺式蒸餾器第一次蒸餾得到的液體。","At roughly what temperature does pure ethanol boil?":"純乙醇大約在幾度沸騰？","Pure ethanol boils at about 78 °C, below water.":"純乙醇大約在 78 °C 沸騰，低於水。","100 °C is the boiling point of water. It is precisely because ethanol boils lower that the vapour becomes richer in alcohol. The other temperatures match neither substance.":"100 °C 是水的沸點。正因為乙醇的沸點較低，蒸氣中的酒精才會變多。其他溫度與這兩種物質都不相符。","Which statement about newly made spirits is true?":"關於新酒，下列哪一項正確？","They are colourless and dry":"無色且不甜","They are golden and slightly sweet":"金黃色且略帶甜味","They already have their bottled colour, but are dry":"已有裝瓶時的顏色，但不甜","They are colourless but hold residual sugar from the fruit":"無色，但含有來自水果的殘糖","Every spirit leaves the still clear as water and without sugar.":"所有烈酒離開蒸餾器時都像水一樣清澈，而且不含糖。","Sugar is not volatile and does not pass into the vapour, so it stays in the still. Colour comes from oak or from colouring added after distillation. Even fruit spirits therefore come off dry.":"糖不具揮發性，不會進入蒸氣，所以留在蒸餾器中。顏色來自橡木或蒸餾後添加的色素。因此就連水果烈酒蒸餾出來時也是不甜的。","Which part of the distillate has a marked solvent smell?":"餾出液的哪個部分帶有明顯的溶劑氣味？","The heads":"酒頭","The heart":"酒心","The tails":"酒尾","The liquid waste":"廢液","The heads hold the most volatile, solvent-smelling compounds.":"酒頭含有最易揮發、帶溶劑氣味的化合物。","The heads come off first precisely because they boil before ethanol. The tails, which come last, smell more of cheese and plastic. The heart carries ethanol and pleasant aromas, while the waste is mostly water.":"酒頭最先流出，正是因為它們比乙醇更早沸騰。最後流出的酒尾聞起來比較像乳酪和塑膠。酒心帶有乙醇和宜人的香氣，廢液則大部分是水。","Which part of the distillate becomes the spirit that is sold?":"餾出液的哪個部分會成為販售的烈酒？","The heads, because they are the most alcoholic":"酒頭，因為酒精濃度最高","The tails, because they have more aroma":"酒尾，因為香氣更多","The liquid left at the bottom of the still":"留在蒸餾器底部的液體","The heart holds the ethanol and the congeners that give the wanted character.":"酒心含有乙醇，以及帶來所需特色的同屬物。","Heads and tails contain too many unpleasant compounds, solvent-like and cheesy or plastic respectively. The liquid at the bottom is mostly water and is thrown away.":"酒頭和酒尾含有太多令人不悅的化合物，分別帶溶劑味以及乳酪或塑膠味。底部的液體大部分是水，會被丟棄。","Which aromas signal that the tails are arriving?":"哪些香氣代表酒尾即將出現？","Cheesy and plastic notes":"乳酪和塑膠氣息","Very sharp solvent and nail-varnish notes":"非常刺鼻的溶劑和指甲油氣息","Fresh, fruity ester notes":"清新的果香酯類氣息","Tails bring less volatile compounds that smell cheesy and plastic.":"酒尾帶來較不易揮發、聞起來像乳酪和塑膠的化合物。","A solvent smell is typical of the heads, at the start. Fruity esters are among the welcome aromas of the heart. Vanilla and coconut come from oak, so after distillation.":"溶劑氣味是開頭的酒頭的典型特徵。帶果香的酯類是酒心中受歡迎的香氣之一。香草和椰子來自橡木，所以是蒸餾之後才有的。","In what order do the parts of the distillate come off the still?":"餾出液的各個部分依什麼順序流出蒸餾器？","Heads, heart, tails":"酒頭、酒心、酒尾","Heart, heads, tails":"酒心、酒頭、酒尾","Tails, heart, heads":"酒尾、酒心、酒頭","Heads, tails, heart":"酒頭、酒尾、酒心","The most volatile compounds come first, then ethanol, then the least volatile.":"最易揮發的化合物最先出來，然後是乙醇，最後是最不易揮發的。","The order follows boiling points: heads boil before ethanol, the heart centres on ethanol, and tails boil after. Water, the least volatile, remains mostly as waste.":"順序依沸點而定：酒頭比乙醇先沸騰，酒心以乙醇為中心，酒尾則在之後沸騰。最不易揮發的水大部分留下來成為廢液。","What is left as liquid waste at the end of distillation?":"蒸餾結束時，留下來的廢液是什麼？","Mostly water":"大部分是水","Mostly ethanol":"大部分是乙醇","Mostly solvent-smelling compounds":"大部分是帶溶劑氣味的化合物","Mostly fruity esters":"大部分是帶果香的酯類","Water is the least volatile fraction and stays behind as waste.":"水是最不易揮發的餾分，會留下來成為廢液。","Ethanol and esters belong to the heart and are collected. Solvent-like compounds are very volatile and come off first, in the heads. The watery liquid left over is discarded.":"乙醇和酯類屬於酒心，會被收集起來。帶溶劑味的化合物非常容易揮發，最先在酒頭中流出。剩下的含水液體會被丟棄。","What happens to the aromas when a spirit is distilled to a higher strength?":"把烈酒蒸餾到更高濃度時，香氣會怎麼樣？","They decrease":"減少","They increase":"增加","They stay the same; only the alcohol changes":"保持不變；只有酒精改變","They become more woody and spicy":"變得更有木質和香料氣息","The more ethanol is concentrated, the more congeners are left behind.":"乙醇濃縮得越多，留下不取的同屬物就越多。","This is the golden rule: high strength means little aroma, right up to neutral spirit. Woody and spicy aromas come from oak maturation, not distillation. The amount of congeners changes along with the strength.":"這是黃金法則：濃度高就代表香氣少，一直到中性烈酒為止。木質和香料香氣來自橡木桶熟成，不是蒸餾。同屬物的量會隨濃度一起改變。","A spirit was collected at around 75% abv. What aroma intensity would you expect?":"一款烈酒在大約 75% abv 時收集。你預期它的香氣強度如何？","Medium or pronounced":"中等或明顯","Neutral, almost odourless":"中性，幾乎沒有氣味","Light, like a Scottish grain whisky":"清淡，像蘇格蘭穀物威士忌","Impossible to say without ageing":"沒有陳年就無法判斷","At about 75% abv many congeners remain: aroma is medium or pronounced.":"在大約 75% abv 時仍保留許多同屬物：香氣中等或明顯。","Aroma only becomes light at around 90% abv, as in Scottish grain whisky, and neutral at 95–96%. Distillation strength already predicts intensity, before any ageing.":"香氣要到大約 90% abv 才變得清淡，例如蘇格蘭穀物威士忌；到 95–96% 則成為中性。蒸餾濃度在任何陳年之前就已經能預測香氣強度。","What is a spirit distilled to about 95–96% abv, with very few congeners, called?":"蒸餾到大約 95–96% abv、同屬物極少的烈酒叫做什麼？","Pronounced heart spirit":"香氣明顯的酒心烈酒","Rancio spirit":"Rancio 烈酒","At this strength the aroma is neutral, hence the name neutral spirit.":"在這個濃度下香氣是中性的，因此稱為中性烈酒。","Low wines are weak, around 25–30% abv, and come from the first pot-still distillation. 'Rancio' describes leather and mushroom notes from long oak ageing, not a strength.":"低度酒濃度低，大約 25–30% abv，來自壺式蒸餾器的第一次蒸餾。「rancio」描述的是長期橡木桶陳年帶來的皮革和蘑菇氣息，不是濃度。","A producer wants a spirit that strongly expresses its raw material. What should be avoided?":"一位生產者想要一款強烈表現原料特色的烈酒。應該避免什麼？","Distilling to a very high strength":"蒸餾到非常高的濃度","Collecting the heart at around 75% abv":"在大約 75% abv 時收集酒心","Separating the heads from the rest of the spirit at the start":"在一開始把酒頭與其餘的酒液分開","Using top-quality raw material":"使用頂級品質的原料","A very high strength strips out most raw-material congeners.":"非常高的濃度會去除大部分來自原料的同屬物。","Collecting at about 75% keeps plenty of aroma, which is exactly what is wanted. Removing the heads only takes out solvent-like compounds, and excellent raw material always helps. The danger is pushing towards neutral spirit.":"在大約 75% 收集能保留豐富的香氣，這正是所需要的。去除酒頭只會帶走溶劑味的化合物，優良的原料也總是有幫助。危險在於把濃度推向中性烈酒。","What is a common level of ethanol concentration reached by distillation?":"蒸餾常見的乙醇濃縮幅度是多少？","From about 10% to about 75% abv":"從大約 10% 到大約 75% abv","From about 40% to about 100% abv":"從大約 40% 到大約 100% abv","From about 1% to about 10% abv":"從大約 1% 到大約 10% abv","From about 10% to about 40% abv, ready for bottling":"從大約 10% 到大約 40% abv，可直接裝瓶","A typical step takes the fermented liquid from about 10% to about 75% abv.":"典型的做法是把發酵液從大約 10% 提高到大約 75% abv。","Some spirits stay below 75%, others reach 96%, but never 100%. The starting liquid is not at 40%: it is around 10%. 40% is often the selling strength, reached by adding water after distillation.":"有些烈酒低於 75%，有些達到 96%，但絕不會到 100%。起始液體不是 40%，而是 10% 左右。40% 通常是販售濃度，是蒸餾後加水達到的。","Why does a spirit collected at around 90% abv have a light aroma?":"為什麼在大約 90% abv 收集的烈酒香氣清淡？","Many congeners have been left behind":"許多同屬物被留下不取","The high strength destroys aromas through the heat of the still":"高濃度透過蒸餾器的熱破壞了香氣","It still contains a lot of heads":"它仍含有大量酒頭","It was filtered through oak":"它經過橡木過濾","As strength rises, more and more congeners stay behind, so aromas fade.":"隨著濃度升高，越來越多同屬物被留下，所以香氣變淡。","It is not heat that destroys aromas: it is separation, which leaves congeners behind. Heads would give a solvent smell, not a light aroma. Oak adds aromas rather than removing them.":"破壞香氣的不是熱，而是分離：它把同屬物留了下來。酒頭會帶來溶劑氣味，而不是清淡的香氣。橡木是增添香氣，而不是去除香氣。","Which of these spirits is typically made from neutral spirit?":"下列哪一種烈酒通常以中性烈酒製成？","Vodka is based on neutral spirit, with very few congeners.":"伏特加以中性烈酒為基礎，同屬物極少。","Bourbon, Armagnac and rhum agricole are distilled to lower strengths, even in columns, and keep a medium or pronounced aroma. This shows that the strength reached matters most.":"Bourbon、Armagnac 和 rhum agricole 蒸餾到較低的濃度（即使使用蒸餾柱），並保有中等或明顯的香氣。這說明了最重要的是達到的濃度。","Besides how much alcohol to concentrate, what does the distiller decide?":"除了要把酒精濃縮到多少，蒸餾師還要決定什麼？","Which congeners to keep in the spirit":"在烈酒中保留哪些同屬物","How much sugar to leave in the newly made spirit":"在新酒中留下多少糖","What colour to give the spirit during distillation":"蒸餾時要給烈酒什麼顏色","How much yeast to add to the still":"要在蒸餾器中加入多少酵母","Distillation is also about choosing the aromas that will give character.":"蒸餾也是在挑選能帶來特色的香氣。","A newly made spirit is always dry and colourless, so sugar and colour are not decided in the still. Yeast works during fermentation, before distillation.":"新酒一定是不甜且無色的，所以糖和顏色不是在蒸餾器中決定的。酵母在蒸餾之前的發酵階段發揮作用。","Which group of fractions makes up the heart of the distillate?":"哪一組餾分構成餾出液的酒心？","Ethanol and congeners with a similar boiling point":"乙醇和沸點相近的同屬物","Congeners that boil before ethanol":"比乙醇先沸騰的同屬物","Congeners that boil after ethanol, along with some water":"比乙醇晚沸騰的同屬物，加上一些水","Water alone, stripped of all aroma":"只有水，不含任何香氣","The heart brings together ethanol and aromas boiling at similar temperatures.":"酒心匯集了乙醇和在相近溫度沸騰的香氣。","Congeners that boil earlier form the heads; those that boil later form the tails. Water is the waste. It is precisely the congeners close to ethanol that give the spirit its personality.":"較早沸騰的同屬物形成酒頭；較晚沸騰的形成酒尾。水是廢液。賦予烈酒個性的，正是那些接近乙醇的同屬物。","What happens to the vapour when it reaches the condenser?":"蒸氣到達冷凝器時會怎麼樣？","It cools and turns back into liquid":"冷卻並變回液體","It heats further and becomes more alcoholic":"進一步加熱，酒精濃度變得更高","It ferments again thanks to the yeast":"靠酵母再次發酵","It turns into sugar, which is then discarded":"變成糖，然後被丟棄","The condenser cools the vapour and turns it back into liquid.":"冷凝器冷卻蒸氣，把它變回液體。","Distilling means heating, letting the vapour rise and then condensing it: the resulting liquid is stronger than the original. There is no fermentation or sugar formation in the condenser.":"蒸餾就是加熱、讓蒸氣上升，再把它冷凝：得到的液體比原本的濃度更高。冷凝器中不會發酵，也不會形成糖。","A spirit smells too strongly of cheese. What has probably happened?":"一款烈酒的乳酪味太重。可能發生了什麼事？","Too much of the tails got into the heart":"太多酒尾進入了酒心","Too much of the heads got into the heart":"太多酒頭進入了酒心","It was distilled too high, close to neutral spirit":"蒸餾濃度太高，接近中性烈酒","Fermentation produced too many esters":"發酵產生了太多酯類","Cheesy notes are typical of the tails: the second cut came too late.":"乳酪氣息是酒尾的典型特徵：第二次切取做得太晚。","Too much heads would give a solvent smell. A very high strength would make the spirit nearly neutral, not more marked. Esters smell fruity. In small amounts these aromas can be part of the character; in excess they are faults.":"酒頭太多會帶來溶劑氣味。非常高的濃度會讓烈酒近乎中性，而不是特徵更鮮明。酯類聞起來是果香。這些香氣少量時可以是特色的一部分；過量就是缺陷。","An aged brandy has a lovely amber colour. Where does this colour come from?":"一款陳年白蘭地有漂亮的琥珀色。這個顏色來自哪裡？","From steps after distillation, such as oak":"來自蒸餾後的步驟，例如橡木桶","From grape skins, which colour the spirit in the still":"來自葡萄皮，在蒸餾器中為烈酒上色","From the tails, which are naturally dark":"來自酒尾，它們天生顏色深","From distilling to a very high strength":"來自蒸餾到非常高的濃度","Every spirit comes off colourless: colour comes later, from oak or colouring.":"所有烈酒蒸餾出來都是無色的：顏色是之後才有的，來自橡木或色素。","Skin pigments are not volatile and do not pass into the vapour, so the spirit stays clear as water. Tails and strength affect aroma, not colour. The same goes for sweetness, which a newly made spirit does not have.":"果皮的色素不具揮發性，不會進入蒸氣，所以烈酒像水一樣清澈。酒尾和濃度影響的是香氣，不是顏色。甜味也是一樣，新酒並沒有甜味。","Between water and ethanol, which is less volatile?":"水和乙醇，哪一個較不易揮發？","They are exactly as volatile as each other":"兩者的揮發性完全相同","It depends on the type of still used":"取決於使用的蒸餾器類型","Water boils at 100 °C and ethanol at about 78 °C, so water is less volatile.":"水在 100 °C 沸騰，乙醇大約在 78 °C，所以水較不易揮發。","Being more volatile means evaporating more easily, at a lower temperature. This difference is what makes distillation possible. Volatility belongs to the substance, not the still.":"更易揮發的意思是更容易蒸發，溫度更低就能蒸發。這個差異讓蒸餾成為可能。揮發性是物質本身的性質，與蒸餾器無關。","At what temperature does pure water boil?":"純水在幾度沸騰？","Water boils at 100 °C, higher than ethanol (about 78 °C).":"水在 100 °C 沸騰，高於乙醇（約 78 °C）。","78 °C is the boiling point of pure ethanol. Because ethanol boils first, the vapours from a boiling alcoholic liquid are richer in alcohol than the liquid itself.":"78 °C 是純乙醇的沸點。因為乙醇先沸騰，含酒精液體沸騰時的蒸氣比液體本身含更多酒精。","When a 10% abv liquid starts to boil, roughly what strength are the first vapours?":"10% abv 的液體開始沸騰時，最初的蒸氣大約是多少濃度？","About 50% abv":"大約 50% abv","About 10% abv, like the liquid":"大約 10% abv，和液體一樣","About 96% abv":"大約 96% abv","Under 5% abv, because water evaporates first":"低於 5% abv，因為水先蒸發","Ethanol, being more volatile, concentrates in the vapour: a 10% liquid gives vapours of about 50%.":"乙醇較易揮發，會在蒸氣中濃縮：10% 的液體產生約 50% 的蒸氣。","The vapours are always more alcoholic than the boiling liquid, so they do not stay at 10%. 96% is only reached with many distillations in a column. Water is less volatile than ethanol, so it does not evaporate first.":"蒸氣的酒精濃度總是比沸騰的液體高，所以不會停在 10%。96% 只有在蒸餾柱中經過多次蒸餾才能達到。水比乙醇不易揮發，所以不會先蒸發。","Which sequence describes any distillation?":"哪一組順序可以描述任何蒸餾？","Heat, condense the vapours, collect the liquid":"加熱、冷凝蒸氣、收集液體","Cool, filter, heat":"冷卻、過濾、加熱","Condense the liquid, then boil it in the condenser":"冷凝液體，再在冷凝器中煮沸","Add yeast, heat, bottle straight away":"加酵母、加熱、立刻裝瓶","The alcoholic liquid is heated into vapour, which is condensed and collected as a new liquid.":"含酒精的液體被加熱成蒸氣，蒸氣經冷凝後收集成新的液體。","The condenser cools vapours; it does not boil anything. Yeast belong to fermentation, which comes first. Filtration is a finishing step after distillation.":"冷凝器是冷卻蒸氣的，不會煮沸任何東西。酵母屬於先進行的發酵階段。過濾是蒸餾後的收尾步驟。","The heads are mainly congeners with a boiling point…":"酒頭主要是沸點……的同屬物","lower than ethanol's":"比乙醇低","higher than ethanol's":"比乙醇高","the same as water's":"和水相同","similar to ethanol's, like the best aromas in the heart":"與乙醇相近，就像酒心中最好的香氣","The heads are the most volatile compounds: they boil before ethanol and arrive first.":"酒頭是最易揮發的化合物：它們比乙醇先沸騰，最先出現。","Congeners with higher boiling points make up the tails. Those close to ethanol go into the heart, and water mostly stays behind as liquid waste.":"沸點較高的同屬物構成酒尾。接近乙醇的進入酒心，水則大部分留下來成為廢液。","The tails are mainly made up of congeners…":"酒尾主要由……的同屬物組成","less volatile than ethanol":"比乙醇不易揮發","more volatile than ethanol, smelling of solvent":"比乙醇更易揮發、帶溶劑氣味","created by the heat of the still":"由蒸餾器的熱所產生","that boil at the same temperature as ethanol":"與乙醇在相同溫度沸騰","The tails come last because their congeners have higher boiling points.":"酒尾最後才出現，因為其中的同屬物沸點較高。","Once ethanol and its similar congeners run low in the liquid, the less volatile compounds start to concentrate in the vapour: cheesy and plastic notes. Solvent-smelling compounds are the heads. The still does not create congeners; it selects them.":"當液體中的乙醇和相近的同屬物變少，較不易揮發的化合物就開始在蒸氣中濃縮：乳酪和塑膠氣息。帶溶劑氣味的化合物是酒頭。蒸餾器不會創造同屬物，只會篩選。","Why do the heads come off the condenser first?":"為什麼酒頭最先從冷凝器流出？","The most volatile parts concentrate in the vapours first":"最易揮發的部分最先在蒸氣中濃縮","They are the heaviest parts and drop straight down":"它們是最重的部分，直接往下掉","The distiller adds them at the start to clean the still":"蒸餾師在一開始加入它們來清潔蒸餾器","They form in the condenser while the cooling water is still warm":"它們在冷卻水還溫熱時於冷凝器中形成","The principle is always the same: whatever is most volatile passes into the vapour first.":"原理始終相同：最易揮發的東西最先進入蒸氣。","The heads are compounds already in the liquid, neither added by the distiller nor formed in the condenser. Weight is irrelevant; boiling point is what counts.":"酒頭是液體中原本就有的化合物，既不是蒸餾師加入的，也不是在冷凝器中形成的。重量無關緊要；重要的是沸點。","Why is the heads phase short, only around ten minutes?":"為什麼酒頭階段很短，只有十分鐘左右？","Those congeners run out of the liquid very quickly":"這些同屬物很快就從液體中耗盡","The distiller turns off the heat to avoid them":"蒸餾師關掉熱源來避開它們","The condenser holds almost all of them back":"冷凝器把它們幾乎全部擋住","They turn into ethanol after a few minutes of boiling in the liquid":"它們在液體中沸騰幾分鐘後變成乙醇","The most volatile compounds are few and pass quickly into the vapour, so their level in the liquid drops fast.":"最易揮發的化合物數量少，很快就進入蒸氣，所以它們在液體中的含量迅速下降。","Once the solvent smell no longer dominates, the distiller makes the cut and the heart begins. Heating continues, the condenser lets everything through and no congener turns into ethanol.":"一旦溶劑氣味不再是主導，蒸餾師就進行切取，酒心開始。加熱持續進行，冷凝器讓所有東西通過，也沒有任何同屬物會變成乙醇。","What do the choices about what to keep and what to reject depend on?":"保留什麼、捨棄什麼，取決於什麼？","The distiller's preferences and the type of spirit":"蒸餾師的偏好和烈酒的類型","Only on the yeast used in fermentation":"只取決於發酵所用的酵母","A fixed rule that is the same for every spirit":"一條對所有烈酒都相同的固定規則","The outside temperature":"室外氣溫","Where the cuts fall depends on the style sought and the distiller's preferences.":"切取點落在哪裡，取決於追求的風格和蒸餾師的偏好。","There is no single rule: one distiller may want a wider, richer heart, another a cleaner, lighter one. Yeast affects which congeners exist but does not decide the cuts. Climate does not decide what to keep.":"沒有單一的規則：有的蒸餾師想要較寬、較豐富的酒心，有的想要較乾淨、較清淡的。酵母影響的是有哪些同屬物，但不決定切取點。氣候不會決定要保留什麼。","What is the highest strength distillation can reach?":"蒸餾能達到的最高濃度是多少？","About 75% abv":"大約 75% abv","100% abv, pure alcohol":"100% abv，純酒精","About 86% abv":"大約 86% abv","With enough plates a column reaches 95–96% abv, the level of neutral spirit.":"只要蒸餾板夠多，蒸餾柱可達 95–96% abv，也就是中性烈酒的濃度。","75% is a common level, not the maximum. 100% is not reached by distillation. 96% is only possible in a column, never in a pot still.":"75% 是常見的濃度，不是上限。蒸餾無法達到 100%。96% 只有蒸餾柱才能做到，壺式蒸餾器絕對不行。","Two spirits come from the same fermented liquid: A collected at 70% abv, B at 94%. Which will have more aroma?":"兩款烈酒來自同一批發酵液：A 在 70% abv 收集，B 在 94%。哪一款香氣較多？","A, because it keeps more congeners":"A，因為保留了更多同屬物","B, because stronger alcohol carries more aroma":"B，因為酒精越濃，帶的香氣越多","Neither: they will smell the same as the starting liquid is the same":"都不是：起始液體相同，聞起來也會一樣","B, because it has lost more water":"B，因為失去了更多水","The higher the distillation strength, the more congeners are left behind and the less aroma the spirit has.":"蒸餾濃度越高，留下不取的同屬物越多，烈酒的香氣就越少。","The starting liquid is the same, but distillation selects different parts of it. Approaching 95–96%, the aroma becomes almost neutral. Losing water concentrates the ethanol, not the aromas.":"起始液體相同，但蒸餾篩選了其中不同的部分。接近 95–96% 時，香氣幾乎變成中性。失去水分濃縮的是乙醇，不是香氣。","Why can a neutral spirit not express its raw material?":"為什麼中性烈酒無法表現它的原料？","Nearly all congeners have been left behind":"幾乎所有同屬物都被留下不取","Because it is always made from potatoes":"因為它一定是用馬鈴薯做的","Because it is aged for a long time in inert glass vessels":"因為它在惰性的玻璃容器中長期陳年","Because it is distilled without fermentation":"因為它不經發酵就蒸餾","At 95–96% abv so few congeners remain that the aroma is neutral, whatever the raw material.":"在 95–96% abv 時留下的同屬物極少，不論用什麼原料，香氣都是中性的。","Neutral spirit can be made from any raw material, not just potatoes. Inert vessels remove no aroma. Without fermentation there would be no alcohol to distil.":"中性烈酒可以用任何原料製成，不只是馬鈴薯。惰性容器不會去除香氣。沒有發酵就沒有酒精可以蒸餾。","Which of these does distillation NOT do?":"下列哪一項不是蒸餾的作用？","Make the spirit sweet":"讓烈酒變甜","Concentrate the ethanol":"濃縮乙醇","Select some congeners and reject others":"篩選某些同屬物並捨棄其他的","Leave much of the fermented liquid's water behind":"把發酵液中大部分的水留下","Every newly made spirit is dry: any sugar is added later.":"所有新酒都是不甜的：如果有糖，都是之後才加的。","Concentrating ethanol, choosing congeners and separating water are exactly what distillation does. Sweetness is a finishing choice, sometimes compulsory, as for liqueurs.":"濃縮乙醇、挑選同屬物和分離水分，正是蒸餾的作用。甜味是收尾階段的選擇，有時是強制規定，例如利口酒。","A customer asks why their rum tastes sweet if distillation makes dry spirits. What do you answer?":"一位顧客問：既然蒸餾得到的是不甜的烈酒，為什麼他的蘭姆酒喝起來是甜的？你怎麼回答？","Sugar can be added after distillation":"蒸餾後可以加糖","The cane sugar passes intact into the vapour":"甘蔗的糖原封不動地進入蒸氣","Rums are not distilled, only fermented":"蘭姆酒沒有蒸餾，只有發酵","The tails contain sugar and are left in the heart":"酒尾含有糖，並被留在酒心裡","All newly made spirits are dry; some rums are sweetened during finishing for balance and style.":"所有新酒都是不甜的；有些蘭姆酒在收尾階段為了平衡和風格而加糖。","Sugar does not pass into the vapour: it stays behind or has already been eaten by the yeast. Rum is a true distilled spirit. Tails give cheesy, plastic notes, not sweetness.":"糖不會進入蒸氣：它留在原處，或早已被酵母吃掉。蘭姆酒是貨真價實的蒸餾烈酒。酒尾帶來乳酪和塑膠氣息，不是甜味。","A spirit smells of solvent, almost like nail-varnish remover. What probably happened?":"一款烈酒帶有溶劑味，幾乎像去光水。可能發生了什麼事？","The cut from heads to heart came too late":"從酒頭切換到酒心的切取做得太晚","Too much of the tails was collected":"收集了太多酒尾","The spirit stayed too long in the barrel":"烈酒在桶中放得太久","The condenser's cooling water was too cold for the whole run":"整個蒸餾過程中冷凝器的冷卻水太冷","A solvent smell is typical of the heads: if too many got into the heart, you notice.":"溶劑氣味是酒頭的典型特徵：如果太多酒頭進入酒心，就會察覺到。","Tails instead bring cheesy and plastic notes. The barrel adds vanilla, spice and, with time, rancio, not solvent. A cold condenser is simply doing its job.":"酒尾帶來的則是乳酪和塑膠氣息。桶帶來香草、香料，時間久了還有 rancio，不是溶劑味。冷凝器冷只是在做它該做的事。","Why are the congeners with a boiling point similar to ethanol so important?":"為什麼沸點與乙醇相近的同屬物這麼重要？","They give the spirit its distinctive character":"它們賦予烈酒獨特的特色","They give the spirit its colour":"它們賦予烈酒顏色","They smell of solvent and must be removed":"它們帶溶劑氣味，必須去除","They make the newly made spirit sweeter":"它們讓新酒變得更甜","They come off with ethanol in the heart and define the spirit's aromatic identity.":"它們在酒心中與乙醇一起流出，決定了烈酒的香氣特徵。","A newly made spirit is colourless and dry, so these congeners give neither colour nor sweetness. The solvent smell belongs to the more volatile heads.":"新酒無色且不甜，所以這些同屬物既不帶來顏色，也不帶來甜味。溶劑氣味屬於更易揮發的酒頭。","Into which four groups can the fractions of a fermented liquid be divided?":"發酵液的餾分可以分成哪四組？","More volatile congeners, ethanol and similar, less volatile congeners, water":"較易揮發的同屬物、乙醇和相近者、較不易揮發的同屬物、水","Sugars, starch, yeast, water":"糖、澱粉、酵母、水","Heads, heart, tails, low wines":"酒頭、酒心、酒尾、低度酒","Esters, methanol, colour, water":"酯類、甲醇、顏色、水","They are grouped by volatility: more volatile than ethanol, ethanol and similar, less volatile, and water.":"它們依揮發性分組：比乙醇更易揮發、乙醇和相近者、較不易揮發，以及水。","These groups roughly match heads, heart, tails and liquid waste. Low wines, by contrast, are the product of the first distillation. Sugar and starch are gone by the end of fermentation, and there is no colour to separate.":"這幾組大致對應酒頭、酒心、酒尾和廢液。低度酒則是第一次蒸餾的產物。糖和澱粉在發酵結束時已經不存在，也沒有顏色可以分離。","A producer wants an almost neutral base to flavour. To what strength should it be distilled?":"一位生產者想要一款近乎中性的基酒來調味。應該蒸餾到多少濃度？","95–96% abv":"95–96% abv","25–30% abv":"25–30% abv","About 75% abv, like a good pot-still spirit":"大約 75% abv，像優質的壺式蒸餾烈酒","About 60% abv":"大約 60% abv","At 95–96% very few congeners remain: the base is neutral and leaves room for added flavours.":"在 95–96% 時留下的同屬物極少：基酒是中性的，為添加的風味留出空間。","This is why most flavoured spirits start from neutral spirit. At 75% or below the spirit keeps a marked raw-material aroma. 25–30% is the strength of low wines.":"所以大多數調味烈酒都從中性烈酒開始。在 75% 或更低時，烈酒保有明顯的原料香氣。25–30% 是低度酒的濃度。","What happens as the distillation strength rises from 75% to 90% abv?":"蒸餾濃度從 75% 升到 90% abv 時會發生什麼事？","Fewer congeners remain and the aroma turns light":"留下的同屬物變少，香氣變得清淡","The aroma grows stronger because the alcohol is more concentrated":"香氣變得更強，因為酒精更濃","The spirit gains colour":"烈酒有了顏色","The spirit becomes sweet":"烈酒變甜","As strength rises, more and more congeners are left behind: by about 90% the aroma is light.":"隨著濃度升高，越來越多同屬物被留下不取：到大約 90% 時香氣就很清淡。","More alcohol does not mean more aroma; quite the opposite. Colour and sweetness do not come from distillation, which always yields a colourless, dry liquid.":"酒精越多不代表香氣越多；恰恰相反。顏色和甜味不是來自蒸餾，蒸餾得到的永遠是無色、不甜的液體。","Why does the distiller keep smelling the flow from the condenser?":"為什麼蒸餾師要不斷聞冷凝器流出的酒液？","To decide when to make the cuts":"決定什麼時候切取","To check the spirit's colour":"檢查烈酒的顏色","To know when to add the yeast":"知道什麼時候加酵母","To know when to add finishing sugar to the heart":"知道什麼時候在酒心中加入收尾用的糖","The nose signals the end of the heads (no more solvent) and the arrival of the tails (cheese, plastic).":"鼻子能分辨酒頭的結束（不再有溶劑味）和酒尾的到來（乳酪、塑膠）。","Newly made spirit is always colourless, so there is no colour to check. Yeast work in fermentation, earlier. Any sugar is only added during finishing, not in the still.":"新酒一定是無色的，所以沒有顏色可以檢查。酵母在更早的發酵階段作用。如果加糖，也只在收尾階段，不是在蒸餾器中。","What separates a 'light' spirit at 90% from a neutral spirit at 96%?":"90% 的「清淡」烈酒和 96% 的中性烈酒有什麼區別？","The light one still keeps a little aroma":"清淡的仍保留一點香氣","The light one is always made in a pot still":"清淡的一定是用壺式蒸餾器做的","The neutral one has more congeners than the light one":"中性的同屬物比清淡的多","Nothing: they are two names for exactly the same style":"沒有區別：只是同一種風格的兩個名稱","At 90% a few congeners remain and the aroma is light; at 95–96% so few remain that it is neutral.":"在 90% 時還留有少許同屬物，香氣清淡；在 95–96% 時留下的極少，成為中性。","Both styles are made in column stills: a pot still cannot reach these strengths. Raising the strength reduces congeners rather than adding them. The difference is small but real.":"兩種風格都用柱式蒸餾器製作：壺式蒸餾器達不到這些濃度。提高濃度是減少同屬物，而不是增加。差異雖小，但確實存在。","A distiller cuts to tails earlier than usual. What is the most likely effect?":"一位蒸餾師比平常更早切到酒尾。最可能的效果是什麼？","Fewer heavy congeners and a cleaner spirit":"較重的同屬物變少，烈酒更乾淨","More solvent smell in the heart":"酒心中的溶劑氣味變多","More cheesy, plastic notes in the spirit":"烈酒中的乳酪、塑膠氣息變多","A more coloured, sweeter heart than usual":"酒心比平常顏色更深、更甜","Stopping the heart earlier keeps out some of the less volatile congeners typical of the tails.":"提早結束酒心，能把一部分酒尾典型的、較不易揮發的同屬物擋在外面。","Solvent belongs to the heads, at the start, and does not depend on the second cut. Cheesy notes would increase with a later cut, not an earlier one. The heart stays colourless and dry either way.":"溶劑味屬於開頭的酒頭，與第二次切取無關。乳酪氣息在切取較晚時才會增加，而不是較早時。無論如何酒心都是無色且不甜的。","What is the heads cut for?":"切除酒頭的目的是什麼？","To keep solvent-smelling congeners out of the spirit":"不讓帶溶劑氣味的同屬物進入烈酒","To remove water from the spirit":"去除烈酒中的水","To throw away all excess ethanol":"丟掉所有多餘的乙醇","To collect the cheesy and plastic notes":"收集乳酪和塑膠氣息","The first, very volatile fractions smell of solvent and are separated so as not to spoil the heart.":"最初那些非常易揮發的餾分帶有溶劑氣味，要分離出來，以免破壞酒心。","Water mostly stays at the bottom as waste; it does not come off first. Ethanol is what the distiller wants to keep. Cheesy and plastic notes come with the tails, at the end.":"水大部分留在底部成為廢液，不會最先流出。乙醇是蒸餾師想保留的東西。乳酪和塑膠氣息是最後隨酒尾出現的。","A spirit is collected at 75% abv but sold at 40%. Where does the difference come from?":"一款烈酒在 75% abv 收集，卻以 40% 販售。差別從何而來？","From adding water before bottling":"裝瓶前加水","From a second fermentation in bottle":"瓶中二次發酵","From alcohol evaporating during the few minutes the heads are collected":"收集酒頭的那幾分鐘內酒精蒸發","From chill-filtration, which removes alcohol":"冷凝過濾去除了酒精","Almost every spirit is brought down to bottling strength with pure water.":"幾乎所有烈酒都用純水降到裝瓶濃度。","Dilution is a finishing step that makes the spirit more enjoyable for most people. There is no second fermentation in bottle, and chill-filtration removes haze, not alcohol.":"稀釋是收尾步驟，讓烈酒對大多數人來說更好入口。瓶中不會二次發酵，冷凝過濾去除的是混濁，不是酒精。","Which statement about the strength spirits are distilled to is true?":"關於烈酒的蒸餾濃度，下列哪一項正確？","It varies widely: some stay below 75%, others reach 96%":"差異很大：有些低於 75%，有些達到 96%","It is always 75% abv by law":"依法一律是 75% abv","It is always the same as the bottled strength":"一律與裝瓶濃度相同","It never goes above 50%, the strength of the first vapours":"絕不會超過 50%，也就是最初蒸氣的濃度","A common level is about 75%, but some spirits are well below and others go up to 96%.":"常見的濃度是 75% 左右，但有些烈酒遠低於此，有些則高達 96%。","Distillation strength is a style choice: the lower it is, the more congeners remain. Bottled strength is usually lower because water is added. With several distillations the 50% of the first vapours is easily exceeded.":"蒸餾濃度是風格上的選擇：濃度越低，保留的同屬物越多。裝瓶濃度通常較低，因為加了水。經過多次蒸餾，很容易超過最初蒸氣的 50%。","Why does simple boiling not fully separate ethanol from water?":"為什麼單純煮沸無法完全分離乙醇和水？","The vapours contain both, just with more ethanol":"蒸氣中兩者都有，只是乙醇較多","Water never evaporates":"水永遠不會蒸發","All the ethanol stays in the liquid":"所有乙醇都留在液體中","Water and ethanol boil at exactly the same temperature":"水和乙醇在完全相同的溫度沸騰","When the liquid boils, the vapours are richer in ethanol but still contain water.":"液體沸騰時，蒸氣含有較多乙醇，但仍然含有水。","That is why several distillations, one after another or on the plates of a column, are needed to raise strength. Water (100 °C) and ethanol (about 78 °C) boil at different temperatures, but both pass partly into the vapour.":"所以要提高濃度，就需要多次蒸餾，不論是一次接一次，還是在蒸餾柱的蒸餾板上進行。水（100 °C）和乙醇（約 78 °C）的沸點不同，但兩者都會有一部分進入蒸氣。","What most directly decides the aroma intensity of a newly made spirit?":"什麼最直接決定新酒的香氣強度？","The strength at which it is collected":"收集時的濃度","The colour of the fermented liquid":"發酵液的顏色","The amount of sugar added after bottling":"裝瓶後添加的糖量","The lower the collection strength, the more congeners remain and the more intense the aroma.":"收集濃度越低，保留的同屬物越多，香氣就越濃郁。","At about 75% the aroma is medium or pronounced, at about 90% light, at 95–96% neutral. The fermented liquid's colour does not pass into the distillate. Any sugar is added before bottling and does not change the basic aroma intensity.":"在大約 75% 時香氣中等或明顯，大約 90% 時清淡，95–96% 時中性。發酵液的顏色不會進入餾出液。如果加糖，是在裝瓶前加的，不會改變基本的香氣強度。","Why do most flavoured spirits start from neutral spirit?":"為什麼大多數調味烈酒都從中性烈酒開始？","To let the added flavours show as much as possible":"讓添加的風味盡可能突顯","Because neutral spirit is already sweet":"因為中性烈酒本來就是甜的","Because neutral spirit is already golden":"因為中性烈酒本來就是金黃色的","Because it is the only spirit the law lets be sold below 40% abv":"因為它是法律唯一允許以低於 40% abv 販售的烈酒","With very few congeners of its own, neutral spirit does not mask the added botanicals and fruit.":"中性烈酒本身的同屬物極少，不會掩蓋添加的植物性原料和水果。","Like any newly made spirit, neutral spirit is colourless and dry. There are exceptions, such as spiced rum based on golden rum. Bottling strength does not depend on the type of base spirit.":"和所有新酒一樣，中性烈酒無色且不甜。也有例外，例如以金色蘭姆酒為基底的香料蘭姆酒。裝瓶濃度與基酒的類型無關。","What material are nearly all pot stills made of?":"幾乎所有壺式蒸餾器都用什麼材料製成？","Copper":"銅","Stainless steel":"不鏽鋼","Oak wood":"橡木","Copper is easy to shape and conducts heat well.":"銅容易塑形，導熱也好。","Stainless steel and glass are found instead in the inert vessels used to store unaged spirits. Oak is used for maturation barrels, not for stills.":"不鏽鋼和玻璃則用於存放未陳年烈酒的惰性容器。橡木用來製作熟成用的桶，不是蒸餾器。","What is the most common heat source for a pot still today?":"現今壺式蒸餾器最常見的熱源是什麼？","Steam, in coils or a jacket":"蒸汽，透過盤管或夾套","A gas burner under the pot, in almost every distillery":"壺身下方的瓦斯爐，幾乎每家蒸餾廠都用","A wood fire":"柴火","The sun":"太陽","Most modern stills are heated by steam.":"大多數現代蒸餾器都以蒸汽加熱。","Steam runs through internal coils or an external jacket. Direct heat, such as a gas burner, is now rare, with the notable exception of Cognac, where the law requires it.":"蒸汽流經內部的盤管或外部的夾套。瓦斯爐這類直火加熱如今已很少見，值得注意的例外是 Cognac，法律規定必須使用直火。","For which spirit does the law require a pot still heated by direct fire?":"法律規定哪一種烈酒必須使用直火加熱的壺式蒸餾器？","Scottish grain whisky":"蘇格蘭穀物威士忌","Light rum":"清淡型蘭姆酒","For Cognac, direct heating is a legal requirement.":"對 Cognac 來說，直火加熱是法定要求。","Cognac is the best-known exception to the steam rule. Vodka, grain whisky and light rum are distilled to high strength, typically in columns, so this rule does not apply to them.":"Cognac 是蒸汽通則中最知名的例外。伏特加、穀物威士忌和清淡型蘭姆酒都蒸餾到高濃度，通常使用蒸餾柱，所以這項規定不適用於它們。","What is the job of the lyne arm on a pot still?":"壺式蒸餾器上林恩臂（lyne arm）的功能是什麼？","It links the still head to the condenser":"連接蒸餾器頂部和冷凝器","It empties the pot at the end of a run":"在蒸餾結束時排空壺身","It heats the liquid with pressurised steam inside the pot":"在壺身內用加壓蒸汽加熱液體","It cools the vapours with cold water":"用冷水冷卻蒸氣","The lyne arm is the pipe carrying vapours from the still head to the condenser.":"林恩臂是把蒸氣從蒸餾器頂部送到冷凝器的管子。","Emptying is the drain's job, heating is the heat source's and cooling is the condenser's. The lyne arm is simply the route the vapours take to where they will become liquid again.":"排空是排放口的工作，加熱是熱源的工作，冷卻是冷凝器的工作。林恩臂只是蒸氣前往重新變成液體之處的通道。","Which part of a pot still holds the liquid to be distilled?":"壺式蒸餾器的哪個部分盛裝待蒸餾的液體？","The swan neck":"天鵝頸","The lyne arm":"林恩臂","The pot is the vessel that is filled and heated.":"壺身是裝料並加熱的容器。","The swan neck and lyne arm carry vapours, not the starting liquid. The condenser receives the vapours and turns them into new spirit.":"天鵝頸和林恩臂輸送的是蒸氣，不是起始液體。冷凝器接收蒸氣，並把它變成新酒。","In a shell and tube condenser, what turns the vapours back into liquid?":"在殼管式冷凝器中，什麼讓蒸氣變回液體？","Contact with pipes full of cold liquid":"接觸裝滿冷液體的管子","Direct contact with high-pressure steam":"直接接觸高壓蒸汽","Adding cold water straight into the spirit":"把冷水直接加進烈酒","Passing through activated charcoal":"通過活性碳","The vapours touch cooled pipes, usually holding cold water, and condense.":"蒸氣碰到冷卻的管子（通常裝著冷水）就會冷凝。","The coolant never mixes with the spirit: it flows inside the pipes and must be constantly refreshed to stay cold. High-pressure steam heats rather than cools, and activated charcoal is used for filtering.":"冷卻液絕不會與烈酒混合：它在管內流動，必須不斷更新才能保持低溫。高壓蒸汽是用來加熱而不是冷卻的，活性碳則用於過濾。","What is the other, older type of condenser sometimes seen?":"有時還能見到的另一種較古老的冷凝器是什麼？","The worm tub":"蟲桶冷凝器（worm tub）","The bubble cap":"泡罩","The downcomer":"降液管","The demijohn":"玻璃罈","The worm tub is a coiled pipe sitting in a tank of cold water.":"蟲桶冷凝器是浸在冷水槽中的一條盤繞的管子。","Bubble caps and downcomers are parts of the plates in a column still. A demijohn is a glass vessel used to store very old spirits, not a condenser.":"泡罩和降液管是柱式蒸餾器蒸餾板上的零件。玻璃罈是用來存放極老烈酒的玻璃容器，不是冷凝器。","What is the aim of the first distillation in a pot still?":"壺式蒸餾器第一次蒸餾的目的是什麼？","To remove some of the water from the fermented liquid":"去除發酵液中的一部分水","To separate heads, heart and tails precisely":"精確分離酒頭、酒心和酒尾","To make a spirit ready for sale at 75% abv":"製作 75% abv、可直接販售的烈酒","To give the spirit a copper colour before it goes into oak":"在入橡木桶前為烈酒染上銅色","The first distillation removes water and produces stronger low wines.":"第一次蒸餾去除水分，產生濃度較高的低度酒。","The precise cuts and collection of the heart happen in the second distillation. After the first run the liquid is only 25–30% abv, so it is not a saleable spirit. Copper does not colour the spirit.":"精確的切取和酒心的收集在第二次蒸餾中進行。第一次蒸餾後液體只有 25–30% abv，所以還不是可販售的烈酒。銅不會為烈酒上色。","What is the liquid from the first pot-still distillation called?":"壺式蒸餾器第一次蒸餾得到的液體叫做什麼？","Heart":"酒心","The first run produces low wines, at 25–30% abv.":"第一次蒸餾產生低度酒，濃度為 25–30% abv。","The heart is only collected in the second distillation. Wort is the sweet grain liquid before fermentation. Neutral spirit needs 95–96% abv, impossible in a pot still.":"酒心要到第二次蒸餾才收集。麥汁是發酵前的穀物甜液。中性烈酒需要 95–96% abv，壺式蒸餾器不可能達到。","What is the typical strength of low wines?":"低度酒的典型濃度是多少？","8–10% abv":"8–10% abv","70–75% abv":"70–75% abv","90–96% abv":"90–96% abv","Low wines are usually between 25% and 30% abv.":"低度酒通常在 25% 至 30% abv 之間。","8–10% is the strength of the starting fermented liquid. Around 75% is where the heart of the second distillation sits. 90–96% can only be reached with a column still.":"8–10% 是起始發酵液的濃度。75% 左右是第二次蒸餾酒心所在的位置。90–96% 只有柱式蒸餾器才能達到。","Why are low wines so low in strength?":"為什麼低度酒的濃度這麼低？","Collecting all the alcohol means collecting lots of water too":"要收集所有酒精，就會同時收集到大量的水","The copper absorbs much of the ethanol during the first distillation":"第一次蒸餾時銅吸收了大量乙醇","Water is added by law":"法律規定要加水","The heads are left in":"酒頭被留在裡面","The flow's strength drops for hours, and everything is collected so as not to lose alcohol and aromas.":"流出酒液的濃度會持續下降好幾個小時，而為了不損失酒精和香氣，全部都會收集起來。","At first the vapour is around 50% abv, but most of the alcohol and aromas are still in the pot. Carrying on down to about 1% abv collects more and more water. Copper does not absorb ethanol and there is no compulsory addition of water.":"一開始蒸氣大約是 50% abv，但大部分的酒精和香氣仍留在壺身裡。持續蒸餾到約 1% abv，會收集到越來越多的水。銅不會吸收乙醇，也沒有強制加水的規定。","In the second distillation, what tells the distiller it is time for the first cut?":"在第二次蒸餾中，什麼讓蒸餾師知道該做第一次切取了？","The solvent smell no longer dominates":"溶劑氣味不再是主導","Cheesy and plastic notes appear":"出現乳酪和塑膠氣息","The flow drops to 1% abv and the pot is nearly empty":"酒液濃度降到 1% abv，壺身幾乎空了","The spirit turns golden":"烈酒變成金黃色","When the solvent-smelling heads end, collection switches to the heart.":"帶溶劑氣味的酒頭結束時，就改為收集酒心。","Cheesy and plastic notes signal the second cut instead, into the tails. 1% abv marks the end of distillation. The spirit does not change colour in the still: it stays colourless.":"乳酪和塑膠氣息代表的是第二次切取，也就是進入酒尾。1% abv 代表蒸餾結束。烈酒在蒸餾器中不會變色：始終是無色的。","What is a 'cut' in pot-still distillation?":"在壺式蒸餾中，「切取」是什麼？","Switching the tank the flow is collected in":"更換收集酒液的槽","Adding water to lower the strength before bottling":"裝瓶前加水降低濃度","Mixing spirits of different ages":"混合不同年數的烈酒","Suddenly switching off the heat source":"突然關掉熱源","Making a cut means redirecting the flow from the condenser to another tank.":"切取就是把冷凝器流出的酒液改導向另一個槽。","The first cut separates heads from heart, the second heart from tails. Reducing with water and blending happen after distillation. The still is only switched off at the end, when the flow reaches about 1% abv.":"第一次切取分開酒頭和酒心，第二次分開酒心和酒尾。加水降度和調和都在蒸餾之後進行。蒸餾器要到最後、酒液濃度降到約 1% abv 時才關閉。","What goes into the pot for the second distillation?":"第二次蒸餾時，壺身裡裝的是什麼？","Low wines plus heads and tails from the last batch":"低度酒加上上一批的酒頭和酒尾","Only the fermented liquid at 10% abv":"只有 10% abv 的發酵液","The previous batch's heart, to make it even stronger":"上一批的酒心，讓它變得更濃","The watery waste from the first distillation":"第一次蒸餾的含水廢液","Heads and tails from the previous cycle join the new low wines.":"上一輪的酒頭和酒尾會與新的低度酒合在一起。","The fermented liquid is used in the first distillation. The heart is the final product and is not redistilled. The watery waste is thrown away because it is mostly water.":"發酵液用於第一次蒸餾。酒心是最終產品，不會再蒸餾。含水的廢液因為大部分是水，所以被丟棄。","Why are heads and tails put into the next distillation instead of being thrown away?":"為什麼酒頭和酒尾要放進下一次蒸餾，而不是丟掉？","They still contain plenty of ethanol and positive aromas":"它們仍含有大量乙醇和好的香氣","They are the finest part and need concentrating further":"它們是最精華的部分，需要進一步濃縮","They give colour to the next spirit":"它們為下一批烈酒帶來顏色","The law forbids throwing them away":"法律禁止丟棄","As well as unwanted compounds, they hold alcohol and good aromas worth recovering.":"除了不想要的化合物，它們還含有值得回收的酒精和好香氣。","Heads and tails are not the prized part: in excess they give solvent or cheesy smells. Redistilling them recovers what is good in them. They add no colour, because every spirit comes off colourless.":"酒頭和酒尾並不是珍貴的部分：過量時會帶來溶劑或乳酪氣味。再蒸餾可以回收其中好的東西。它們不會增添顏色，因為所有烈酒蒸餾出來都是無色的。","What aroma intensity does a pot-still spirit typically have?":"壺式蒸餾烈酒的香氣強度通常如何？","Medium to pronounced":"中等到明顯","Light, like a filtered vodka":"清淡，像過濾過的伏特加","Always very delicate, whatever the cut":"不論怎麼切取，總是非常細緻","Imprecise separation lets many congeners through with the ethanol.":"分離不精確，讓許多同屬物隨乙醇一起通過。","A pot still cannot reach neutral-spirit strengths, so it does not produce neutral or light spirits like vodka. Where the cuts fall changes the style, but the aroma generally stays marked.":"壺式蒸餾器達不到中性烈酒的濃度，所以做不出伏特加那樣中性或清淡的烈酒。切取點的位置會改變風格，但香氣通常仍然鮮明。","A distiller with only a pot still wants to make neutral spirit at 96% abv. What happens?":"一位只有壺式蒸餾器的蒸餾師想做 96% abv 的中性烈酒。結果會怎樣？","It cannot be done: that strength needs a column still":"做不到：這個濃度需要柱式蒸餾器","It works with two distillations":"蒸餾兩次就可以","It works if direct fire is used, as in Cognac":"像 Cognac 一樣用直火就可以","It works by discarding the tails and keeping only the heads":"丟掉酒尾、只留酒頭就可以","In a pot still, 96% abv simply cannot be reached.":"壺式蒸餾器根本達不到 96% abv。","Every batch requires recovering all the alcohol, which dilutes the ethanol with water. Only a column still, with many simultaneous distillations, reaches such high strengths. The heating method does not change this limit, and the heads are solvent-smelling compounds.":"每一批都要回收所有的酒精，這就讓乙醇被水稀釋。只有柱式蒸餾器能靠許多同時進行的蒸餾達到這麼高的濃度。加熱方式不會改變這個極限，而酒頭是帶溶劑氣味的化合物。","Why is pot-still distillation called a batch process?":"為什麼壺式蒸餾被稱為批次製程？","It is filled, run, emptied and started again":"裝料、蒸餾、清空，再重新開始","It takes a non-stop flow of pre-heated fermented liquid":"它接收不間斷流入的預熱發酵液","It makes several different spirits at once":"它同時製作好幾種不同的烈酒","It distils only once a year":"它一年只蒸餾一次","Each load is separate: one cycle must finish before the next begins.":"每一次裝料都是獨立的：一個循環結束後，下一個才能開始。","A continuous flow of pre-heated liquid is typical of a column still, which can run without stopping. A pot still does not make several spirits at once and runs many times a year, batch after batch.":"連續流入預熱液體是柱式蒸餾器的典型做法，它可以不停運轉。壺式蒸餾器不會同時製作好幾種烈酒，而且一年運作很多次，一批接一批。","Down to what strength of flow are the tails collected before the still is shut down?":"酒尾要收集到酒液濃度降到多少，才關閉蒸餾器？","About 1% abv":"大約 1% abv","About 25% abv":"大約 25% abv","Tails are collected until the flow falls to about 1% abv.":"酒尾一直收集到酒液濃度降到約 1% abv。","This recovers almost all the remaining alcohol, which goes back into the next batch. 75% is the average strength of the heart and 25% that of low wines. Stopping earlier would waste ethanol in the residue.":"這樣可以回收幾乎所有剩下的酒精，並放回下一批。75% 是酒心的平均濃度，25% 是低度酒的濃度。提早停止會把乙醇浪費在殘液裡。","A distiller widens the heart cut to take in a little more of the tails. What is the likely effect?":"一位蒸餾師放寬酒心的切取範圍，多收一點酒尾。可能的效果是什麼？","A more intense, fuller-flavoured spirit":"烈酒更濃郁、風味更飽滿","A more neutral spirit, close to vodka":"烈酒更中性，接近伏特加","A paler-coloured spirit":"烈酒顏色更淺","A spirit with a stronger solvent smell, typical of the first fractions":"烈酒有更強的溶劑氣味，也就是最初餾分的典型氣味","More heavy fractions in the heart mean more intense aromas, up to the risk of tail notes.":"酒心裡較重的餾分越多，香氣就越濃郁，甚至有出現酒尾氣息的風險。","Tails carry less volatile congeners: in small doses they add body and character, in excess cheesy notes. The solvent smell comes from the heads, at the start. Colour does not change, because the spirit stays colourless.":"酒尾帶有較不易揮發的同屬物：少量時增添酒體和特色，過量則出現乳酪氣息。溶劑氣味來自開頭的酒頭。顏色不會改變，因為烈酒始終是無色的。","Which sequence describes the vapours' path through a pot still?":"哪一組順序描述了蒸氣在壺式蒸餾器中的路徑？","Pot, still head, swan neck, lyne arm, condenser":"壺身、蒸餾器頂部、天鵝頸、林恩臂、冷凝器","Pot, lyne arm, condenser, swan neck, still head":"壺身、林恩臂、冷凝器、天鵝頸、蒸餾器頂部","Condenser, pot, still head, lyne arm, drain":"冷凝器、壺身、蒸餾器頂部、林恩臂、排放口","Drain, pot, condenser, still head, lyne arm":"排放口、壺身、冷凝器、蒸餾器頂部、林恩臂","Vapours rise from the pot into the still head, narrow through the swan neck, and the lyne arm takes them to the condenser.":"蒸氣從壺身上升到蒸餾器頂部，經天鵝頸收窄，再由林恩臂送到冷凝器。","The condenser is always the last stop, where the vapours become liquid again. The drain is not part of the vapour path: it only empties the pot at the end of a run.":"冷凝器永遠是最後一站，蒸氣在那裡重新變成液體。排放口不在蒸氣的路徑上：它只在蒸餾結束時排空壺身。","Why must the condenser's cooling water be constantly refreshed?":"為什麼冷凝器的冷卻水必須不斷更新？","Otherwise it warms up and stops condensing the vapours":"否則它會變熱，無法再冷凝蒸氣","Because it mixes into the spirit and lowers its strength":"因為它會混入烈酒並降低濃度","To stop the copper changing the colour of the newly made spirit":"防止銅改變新酒的顏色","Because it is also used to fill the pot":"因為它也用來注滿壺身","The coolant must stay cold to turn the vapours back into liquid.":"冷卻液必須保持低溫，才能把蒸氣變回液體。","The hot vapours pass their heat to the water in the pipes: if it is not replaced, it warms up and condensation stops. The water flows separately from the spirit, so it does not dilute it. Copper does not colour the spirit, and the pot is filled with the liquid to be distilled.":"高溫的蒸氣把熱傳給管中的水：如果不更換，水會變熱，冷凝就停止了。水與烈酒分開流動，所以不會稀釋烈酒。銅不會為烈酒上色，壺身裝的是待蒸餾的液體。","What is the drain on a pot still for?":"壺式蒸餾器的排放口有什麼用途？","To empty the still after use":"使用後排空蒸餾器","To let the heads out":"讓酒頭流出","To send the tails back into the pot during distillation":"在蒸餾過程中把酒尾送回壺身","To inject steam into the liquid":"把蒸汽注入液體","The drain, at the bottom of the pot, lets it be emptied at the end of a run.":"排放口位於壺身底部，可在蒸餾結束時把它排空。","This is where the watery residue that is discarded comes out. Heads and tails leave via the condenser and are collected in a tank for the next batch, not during the same run. Steam comes through coils or a jacket.":"被丟棄的含水殘液就是從這裡排出。酒頭和酒尾經由冷凝器流出，收集在槽中供下一批使用，而不是在同一次蒸餾中使用。蒸汽則經由盤管或夾套進入。","In which two ways can steam heat a pot still?":"蒸汽可以用哪兩種方式加熱壺式蒸餾器？","Internal coils or an external jacket":"內部盤管或外部夾套","Direct injection into the condenser or the lyne arm":"直接注入冷凝器或林恩臂","A gas burner or a wood fire":"瓦斯爐或柴火","A heat exchanger on the still head or swan neck":"裝在蒸餾器頂部或天鵝頸上的熱交換器","Steam runs through coils inside the pot or through an external jacket around it.":"蒸汽流經壺身內的盤管，或圍繞壺身的外部夾套。","Most modern stills are heated this way. Gas and wood are direct fire, rare today except in Cognac. Heat goes to the pot, not to the upper parts or the condenser, which must stay cold.":"大多數現代蒸餾器都這樣加熱。瓦斯和木柴屬於直火，除了 Cognac 以外如今已很少見。熱是加在壺身上，不是上方的部位或冷凝器，冷凝器必須保持低溫。","Which heat source do Cognac stills usually use today?":"現今 Cognac 的蒸餾器通常使用哪種熱源？","Gas burners":"瓦斯爐","Internal steam coils":"內部蒸汽盤管","An external steam jacket":"外部蒸汽夾套","Steam injected straight into the wine":"直接注入葡萄酒的蒸汽","Cognac requires direct fire, which today almost always means gas burners.":"Cognac 規定使用直火，如今幾乎都是瓦斯爐。","Coils and jackets are the usual heating elsewhere, but Cognac's rules require a flame. Direct steam injection is found in some large column stills.":"盤管和夾套是其他地方常見的加熱方式，但 Cognac 的規定要求用火焰。直接注入蒸汽則見於一些大型柱式蒸餾器。","Besides being easy to shape, why is copper used for stills?":"除了容易塑形，蒸餾器為什麼使用銅？","It conducts heat well":"導熱良好","It gives the spirit colour":"為烈酒帶來顏色","It adds sugar to the spirit":"為烈酒增添糖分","It lets a pot still reach 96% abv":"讓壺式蒸餾器達到 96% abv","Copper is easy to shape and transfers heat well, which is why nearly all pot stills are copper.":"銅容易塑形，傳熱效果好，所以幾乎所有壺式蒸餾器都是銅製的。","The spirit leaving the still is colourless and dry anyway. The 96% limit comes from how pot stills work, not from the metal: a column is needed.":"離開蒸餾器的烈酒反正都是無色且不甜的。96% 的極限來自壺式蒸餾器的運作方式，不是金屬：需要用蒸餾柱。","In a shell and tube condenser, where does the vapour enter and where does the spirit leave?":"在殼管式冷凝器中，蒸氣從哪裡進入，烈酒從哪裡流出？","Vapour enters at the top, liquid leaves at the bottom":"蒸氣從頂部進入，液體從底部流出","Vapour enters at the bottom, liquid leaves at the top":"蒸氣從底部進入，液體從頂部流出","In and out through the same pipe, passing through the cooling water":"進出都經同一條管子，並穿過冷卻水","It enters from the side and returns to the pot":"從側面進入，再流回壺身","Vapour enters at the top, meets tubes of cold water, condenses and runs down: new spirit leaves at the bottom.":"蒸氣從頂部進入，碰到裝著冷水的管子後冷凝並往下流：新酒從底部流出。","Vapour and cooling water never mix: heat passes through the metal tubes. This is the most common condenser today. The condensed spirit goes to the collecting tanks, not back into the pot.":"蒸氣和冷卻水絕不會混合：熱透過金屬管傳遞。這是現今最常見的冷凝器。冷凝後的烈酒流向收集槽，不會回到壺身。","Which of these parts is NOT found on a pot still?":"下列哪個零件不在壺式蒸餾器上？","The lyne arm leading to the condenser":"通往冷凝器的林恩臂","The drain":"排放口","The downcomer belongs to a column still's plates: it sends overflowing liquid down to the plate below.":"降液管屬於柱式蒸餾器的蒸餾板：它把溢出的液體送到下一層蒸餾板。","Swan neck, lyne arm and drain are typical pot-still parts, along with heat source, pot, still head and condenser. Plates, bubble caps and downcomers are the heart of a column still.":"天鵝頸、林恩臂和排放口是壺式蒸餾器的典型零件，另外還有熱源、壺身、蒸餾器頂部和冷凝器。蒸餾板、泡罩和降液管則是柱式蒸餾器的核心。","What is the still filled with for the first distillation?":"第一次蒸餾時，蒸餾器裡裝的是什麼？","The fermented liquid, about 10% abv":"發酵液，約 10% abv","Low wines at 25–30% abv":"25–30% abv 的低度酒","Low wines plus heads and tails from the last run":"低度酒加上上一次蒸餾的酒頭和酒尾","Diluted neutral spirit":"稀釋過的中性烈酒","The first distillation starts from the fermented liquid, usually about 10% abv.":"第一次蒸餾從發酵液開始，通常約 10% abv。","Low wines are the result of the first distillation and go, with heads and tails, into the second. Diluted neutral spirit is used for redistilling with botanicals, not for making a base spirit.":"低度酒是第一次蒸餾的成果，會與酒頭和酒尾一起進入第二次蒸餾。稀釋過的中性烈酒用於與植物性原料一起再蒸餾，不是用來製作基酒。","For how long is liquid collected in the first distillation?":"第一次蒸餾要收集液體多久？","For hours, until the flow drops to about 1% abv":"好幾個小時，直到酒液濃度降到約 1% abv","For about 10–15 minutes, like the heads":"大約 10–15 分鐘，和酒頭一樣","As long as the flow is above 75% abv":"只要酒液濃度高於 75% abv 就繼續","Only while 50% vapour comes off, about half an hour":"只在流出 50% 蒸氣的期間，大約半小時","Collection runs for several hours, until the flow reaches about 1% abv, so almost all the alcohol is recovered.":"收集持續好幾個小時，直到酒液濃度降到約 1% abv，這樣幾乎所有酒精都能回收。","Stopping after half an hour would leave most of the alcohol and good congeners in the pot. The first distillation has no heads or heart cuts; those belong to the second.":"半小時後就停止，會把大部分的酒精和好的同屬物留在壺身裡。第一次蒸餾沒有酒頭或酒心的切取；那些屬於第二次蒸餾。","The first vapours of the first distillation are about 50% abv. Why not stop there?":"第一次蒸餾最初的蒸氣大約是 50% abv。為什麼不就此停止？","Most of the alcohol and aromas are still in the pot":"大部分的酒精和香氣仍在壺身裡","Because the law requires at least eight hours":"因為法律規定至少要八小時","Because those vapours are only water":"因為那些蒸氣只是水","Because the liquid has not finished fermenting at that point":"因為液體到那時還沒發酵完成","To recover the alcohol and positive congeners the still must run for hours, collecting a lot of water too.":"要回收酒精和好的同屬物，蒸餾器必須運作好幾個小時，同時也收集到大量的水。","That is why low wines only reach 25–30% abv. The first vapours are rich in alcohol, not just water. Fermentation is over before the liquid enters the still, and no fixed duration is imposed.":"所以低度酒只有 25–30% abv。最初的蒸氣富含酒精，不只是水。發酵在液體進入蒸餾器之前就結束了，也沒有規定固定的時間。","What happens to the watery liquid left in the pot after the first distillation?":"第一次蒸餾後留在壺身裡的含水液體怎麼處理？","It is discarded":"丟棄","It is added to the low wines":"加進低度酒","It is used to dilute the heart":"用來稀釋酒心","It is kept with the heads and tails for the next batch":"與酒頭和酒尾一起保留給下一批","The watery residue in the pot is waste and is thrown away.":"壺身裡的含水殘液是廢液，會被丟棄。","Only the heads and tails of the second distillation are recycled, as they still hold ethanol and useful aromas. The residue is almost pure water. Spirits are diluted with completely pure water.":"只有第二次蒸餾的酒頭和酒尾會回收再用，因為它們仍含有乙醇和有用的香氣。殘液幾乎是純水。稀釋烈酒用的是完全純淨的水。","At least how many distillations does a pot still need to make a spirit?":"用壺式蒸餾器製作烈酒，至少需要蒸餾幾次？","One for each plate":"每層蒸餾板一次","The fermented liquid must be distilled at least twice: first into low wines, then into the actual spirit.":"發酵液至少要蒸餾兩次：先成為低度酒，再成為真正的烈酒。","A single distillation only gives low wines at 25–30%. Some producers distil three times, but two is the minimum. Plates belong to column stills, not pot stills.":"只蒸餾一次只能得到 25–30% 的低度酒。有些生產者蒸餾三次，但兩次是最低限度。蒸餾板屬於柱式蒸餾器，不是壺式蒸餾器。","What is the aim of the second distillation?":"第二次蒸餾的目的是什麼？","To make a saleable spirit of ethanol and similar congeners":"製作由乙醇和相近同屬物構成、可販售的烈酒","To remove some water from the fermented liquid":"去除發酵液中的一部分水","To give the spirit colour and sweetness":"為烈酒帶來顏色和甜味","To reach 96% abv for a fully neutral spirit":"達到 96% abv，得到完全中性的烈酒","The second distillation selects and concentrates ethanol and congeners of similar boiling point, producing the spirit to be sold.":"第二次蒸餾篩選並濃縮乙醇和沸點相近的同屬物，產出要販售的烈酒。","Removing water from the fermented liquid is the first distillation's job. Colour and sweetness come later, if the producer chooses. 96% is impossible in a pot still.":"去除發酵液中的水是第一次蒸餾的工作。顏色和甜味是之後才有的，視生產者的選擇而定。壺式蒸餾器不可能達到 96%。","How long do the heads usually last in the second distillation?":"第二次蒸餾中，酒頭通常持續多久？","About 10–15 minutes":"大約 10–15 分鐘","Several hours":"好幾個小時","About 1 minute":"大約 1 分鐘","All night, until the heart arrives":"一整夜，直到酒心出現","After about 10–15 minutes the flow no longer smells of solvent and the distiller cuts to the heart.":"大約 10–15 分鐘後，酒液不再有溶劑味，蒸餾師就切到酒心。","It is the heart and then the tails that last for hours. Head compounds are few and run out quickly, so this phase is short.":"持續好幾個小時的是酒心和之後的酒尾。酒頭的化合物數量少，很快就耗盡，所以這個階段很短。","Where are the heads collected during the second distillation?":"第二次蒸餾時，酒頭收集在哪裡？","In a separate tank that will also take the tails":"在另一個槽裡，之後也會收酒尾","In the same tank as the heart":"和酒心在同一個槽","Straight into the drain":"直接流進排放口","In barrels, to age them separately":"裝進桶中，另外陳年","The heads go into their own tank; after the second cut the tails are added to it.":"酒頭進入專屬的槽；第二次切取後，酒尾也加進這個槽。","This tank's contents will go into the next second distillation with the new low wines. Mixing it into the heart would bring solvent and plastic smells. It is neither discarded nor aged.":"這個槽裡的東西會與新的低度酒一起進入下一次的第二次蒸餾。把它混進酒心會帶來溶劑和塑膠氣味。它既不會被丟棄，也不會陳年。","What strength is the heart in its tank typically at the end of the second distillation?":"第二次蒸餾結束時，槽中酒心的濃度通常是多少？","About 25–30% abv":"大約 25–30% abv","About 40% abv, ready to bottle":"大約 40% abv，可直接裝瓶","When heart collection stops, the tank typically holds liquid of about 75% abv.":"停止收集酒心時，槽中的液體通常大約是 75% abv。","25–30% is the strength of low wines, and 96% is only reached in a column. 40% is a selling strength, reached later by adding water.":"25–30% 是低度酒的濃度，96% 只有蒸餾柱才能達到。40% 是販售濃度，之後加水才達到。","After the second cut, where is the tails flow sent?":"第二次切取後，酒尾流向哪裡？","To the tank that already holds the heads":"流向已經裝著酒頭的槽","To the heart tank":"流向酒心的槽","Straight into barrels":"直接入桶","Into the first-distillation pot, with the fermented liquid":"流進第一次蒸餾的壺身，與發酵液一起","The tails are collected with the heads, until the flow drops to about 1% abv.":"酒尾與酒頭收集在一起，直到酒液濃度降到約 1% abv。","Heads and tails go back into the next second distillation with the low wines, not into the first. In the heart they would add cheesy and plastic notes.":"酒頭和酒尾會與低度酒一起回到下一次的第二次蒸餾，而不是第一次。它們如果進入酒心，會帶來乳酪和塑膠氣息。","Why does a pot-still spirit keep so much character?":"為什麼壺式蒸餾烈酒能保有這麼多特色？","Separation is imprecise: many congeners come off with the ethanol":"分離不精確：許多同屬物隨乙醇一起流出","Copper adds its own aromas":"銅會增添它自己的香氣","It is only distilled once":"只蒸餾一次","The heads and tails are left in the heart for more flavour":"為了更多風味，酒頭和酒尾被留在酒心裡","A pot still does not separate precisely: many congeners are concentrated with the ethanol, hence its medium to pronounced aroma.":"壺式蒸餾器的分離並不精確：許多同屬物與乙醇一起被濃縮，所以香氣中等到明顯。","Copper is about shape and heat, not an aroma source here. There are at least two distillations. Heads and tails do not stay in the heart; they are separated and recycled into the next batch.":"銅的重點在於形狀和導熱，在這裡不是香氣來源。至少要蒸餾兩次。酒頭和酒尾不會留在酒心裡；它們被分離出來，並回收到下一批。","A distiller decides to throw away the heads and tails instead of reusing them. What is lost?":"一位蒸餾師決定丟掉酒頭和酒尾，不再重複使用。會損失什麼？","Ethanol and good congeners they still contain":"其中仍含有的乙醇和好的同屬物","Nothing: they hold only unwanted compounds":"沒有損失：裡面只有不想要的化合物","The colour they would have given the spirit":"它們原本會帶給烈酒的顏色","The sugar needed to ferment the next batch":"下一批發酵所需的糖","Heads and tails contain unwanted compounds but also plenty of ethanol and positive congeners: discarding them is wasteful.":"酒頭和酒尾含有不想要的化合物，但也含有大量乙醇和好的同屬物：丟掉很浪費。","That is why they go back into the next second distillation. They are colourless and hold no sugar, which is not needed at that stage anyway: fermentation is over.":"所以它們會回到下一次的第二次蒸餾。它們無色，也不含糖，而且那個階段本來就不需要糖：發酵已經結束了。","Which of these does NOT go into the still for the second distillation?":"下列哪一項不會進入第二次蒸餾的蒸餾器？","Fresh fermented liquid":"新鮮的發酵液","The low wines":"低度酒","The heads from the previous second distillation":"上一次第二次蒸餾的酒頭","The tails from the previous second distillation":"上一次第二次蒸餾的酒尾","Fermented liquid goes into the first distillation; the second takes low wines plus the previous run's heads and tails.":"發酵液進入第一次蒸餾；第二次蒸餾用的是低度酒加上上一次的酒頭和酒尾。","Recycling heads and tails in each second distillation avoids losing ethanol and positive aromas. The roughly 10% fermented liquid must first lose water in the first distillation.":"在每次第二次蒸餾中回收酒頭和酒尾，可避免損失乙醇和好的香氣。約 10% 的發酵液必須先在第一次蒸餾中去除水分。","Which pair of strengths is correct?":"哪一組濃度是正確的？","Low wines 25–30%, heart about 75%":"低度酒 25–30%，酒心約 75%","Low wines about 75%, heart 25–30%":"低度酒約 75%，酒心 25–30%","Low wines 10%, heart 96%":"低度酒 10%，酒心 96%","Low wines 50%, heart 40%, the bottling strength":"低度酒 50%，酒心 40%，即裝瓶濃度","Low wines come off at 25–30% abv; the heart of the second distillation reaches about 75%.":"低度酒流出時為 25–30% abv；第二次蒸餾的酒心達到約 75%。","Each distillation concentrates the alcohol, so the heart is stronger than the low wines, not the reverse. 10% is the fermented liquid, and 96% is impossible in a pot still.":"每次蒸餾都會濃縮酒精，所以酒心比低度酒濃，而不是相反。10% 是發酵液，96% 在壺式蒸餾器中不可能達到。","What happens right after the second cut?":"第二次切取之後緊接著發生什麼事？","Tails are collected until the flow falls to about 1%":"收集酒尾，直到酒液濃度降到約 1%","The still is shut down at once":"立刻關閉蒸餾器","Heart collection begins":"開始收集酒心","New low wines are added to the still-boiling pot":"在仍沸騰的壺身中加入新的低度酒","After the second cut the flow, now tails, goes to the heads tank until about 1% abv; then the still is shut down.":"第二次切取後，流出的酒液已是酒尾，會流向酒頭的槽，直到約 1% abv；然後關閉蒸餾器。","The heart starts at the first cut, not the second. A pot still works in batches: no liquid is added mid-run. At the end the watery residue is thrown away.":"酒心從第一次切取開始，不是第二次。壺式蒸餾器以批次運作：蒸餾中途不會加入液體。最後含水的殘液會被丟棄。","Why can low wines not be sold as a spirit?":"為什麼低度酒不能當作烈酒販售？","They are weak and not yet split into heads, heart and tails":"濃度低，而且還沒分成酒頭、酒心和酒尾","They still contain all the sugar":"仍含有全部的糖","They are already coloured by the copper":"已經被銅染色","They are too strong, above 90% abv, for any drinker":"濃度太高，超過 90% abv，沒有人能喝","Low wines, at 25–30%, are the base for the second distillation, which makes the spirit to be sold.":"低度酒濃度為 25–30%，是第二次蒸餾的基礎，第二次蒸餾才做出要販售的烈酒。","They still hold unwanted compounds, since no cuts are made in the first distillation. Sugar was used up in fermentation and the distillate is colourless. 25–30% is far from 90%.":"它們仍含有不想要的化合物，因為第一次蒸餾不做切取。糖已在發酵中用完，餾出液是無色的。25–30% 離 90% 還很遠。","During a pot-still run, how does the strength of the flow from the condenser change?":"在壺式蒸餾的過程中，冷凝器流出酒液的濃度如何變化？","It falls as the alcohol in the pot runs down":"隨著壺身裡的酒精減少而下降","It stays the same from start to finish":"從頭到尾保持不變","It keeps rising, up to 96% abv":"持續上升，直到 96% abv","It rises and falls with the cooling water temperature":"隨冷卻水的溫度而升降","As the run goes on, less and less alcohol remains in the pot, so the flow gets more and more watery.":"隨著蒸餾進行，壺身裡的酒精越來越少，所以流出的酒液含水越來越多。","That is why the still is shut down when the flow reaches about 1% abv. In a batch process the liquid is not renewed, so strength can neither stay constant nor climb to 96%.":"所以酒液濃度降到約 1% abv 時就關閉蒸餾器。在批次製程中液體不會補充，所以濃度既不可能保持恆定，也不可能升到 96%。","Which heat source is now rare on pot stills?":"壺式蒸餾器現在很少使用哪一種熱源？","Direct flame, such as a gas burner":"直接火焰，例如瓦斯爐","Steam in general":"一般的蒸汽","Almost all modern stills are steam-heated; direct fire is rare, except in Cognac.":"幾乎所有現代蒸餾器都用蒸汽加熱；直火很少見，Cognac 除外。","Internal coils and external jackets are the two common ways to use steam. Cognac is the obvious exception, since its law requires a flame.":"內部盤管和外部夾套是使用蒸汽的兩種常見方式。Cognac 是明顯的例外，因為它的法規要求用火焰。","Which type of condenser is most common today?":"現今最常見的是哪一種冷凝器？","Shell and tube":"殼管式","An ice tank above the still head":"蒸餾器頂部上方的冰槽","None: the vapours cool in the air in the lyne arm":"沒有：蒸氣在林恩臂的空氣中冷卻","The shell and tube condenser is the most common: vapours meet tubes full of cold water.":"殼管式冷凝器最常見：蒸氣碰到裝滿冷水的管子。","The worm tub is an older design, compulsory in Cognac but rare elsewhere. Every still needs a real condenser with constantly refreshed coolant.":"蟲桶冷凝器是較古老的設計，在 Cognac 是強制規定，但其他地方很少見。每座蒸餾器都需要真正的冷凝器，並不斷更新冷卻液。","On a Scottish-style pot still, which part sits between the still head and the lyne arm?":"在蘇格蘭式的壺式蒸餾器上，哪個部分位於蒸餾器頂部和林恩臂之間？","The pot full of liquid to distil":"裝滿待蒸餾液體的壺身","Above the still head the still narrows into the swan neck, from which the lyne arm leads to the condenser.":"蒸餾器頂部往上收窄成天鵝頸，林恩臂再從那裡通往冷凝器。","The vapour path is pot, still head, swan neck, lyne arm, condenser. The drain is at the bottom of the pot and only empties it. (In Cognac the names differ: there the 'swan neck' is the tube leading to the condenser.)":"蒸氣的路徑是壺身、蒸餾器頂部、天鵝頸、林恩臂、冷凝器。排放口在壺身底部，只用來排空。（在 Cognac 名稱不同：那裡的「天鵝頸」是通往冷凝器的管子。）","Which of these is a classic example of a pot-still spirit?":"下列哪一項是壺式蒸餾烈酒的經典例子？","Scotch malt whisky":"Scotch 麥芽威士忌","Vodka":"伏特加","The neutral spirit used as a gin base":"用作琴酒基底的中性烈酒","Scotch malt whisky is made in copper pot stills, with a medium to pronounced aroma.":"Scotch 麥芽威士忌用銅製壺式蒸餾器製作，香氣中等到明顯。","Vodka, neutral spirit and grain whisky need strengths (90–96%) only a column can reach. Cognac is another classic pot-still spirit.":"伏特加、中性烈酒和穀物威士忌需要的濃度（90–96%）只有蒸餾柱才能達到。Cognac 是另一種經典的壺式蒸餾烈酒。","Which coolant is usually used in a condenser?":"冷凝器通常使用哪種冷卻液？","Cold water":"冷水","High-pressure steam":"高壓蒸汽","Still-warm low wines from the last run":"上一次蒸餾留下、仍溫熱的低度酒","Condensers usually use cold water, constantly refreshed so it stays cold.":"冷凝器通常使用冷水，並不斷更新以保持低溫。","High-pressure steam is for heating, not cooling. Spirit and low wines are liquids to distil, not coolants.":"高壓蒸汽是用來加熱的，不是冷卻。烈酒和低度酒是待蒸餾的液體，不是冷卻液。","In the second distillation described, how many collecting tanks are used, and for what?":"在所描述的第二次蒸餾中，使用幾個收集槽？各做什麼用？","Two: one for heads and tails, one for the heart":"兩個：一個裝酒頭和酒尾，一個裝酒心","Just one, for the whole flow":"只有一個，裝全部酒液","Three: heads, heart and tails kept apart for good":"三個：酒頭、酒心和酒尾永久分開","Two: one for low wines, one for the pot's watery residue":"兩個：一個裝低度酒，一個裝壺身的含水殘液","Heads and tails share one tank; the heart goes into another.":"酒頭和酒尾共用一個槽；酒心進入另一個槽。","Heads and tails go together because they share the same fate: going back into the next second distillation. The watery residue is drained and discarded, and low wines are the product of the first distillation.":"酒頭和酒尾放在一起，因為它們的去向相同：回到下一次的第二次蒸餾。含水殘液會被排掉丟棄，低度酒則是第一次蒸餾的產物。","How long does heart collection usually last in the second distillation?":"第二次蒸餾中，酒心通常收集多久？","A few seconds":"幾秒鐘","Several days, until the flow smells of solvent again":"好幾天，直到酒液再次出現溶劑味","The heart is collected for several hours, until the cheesy, plastic notes of the tails appear.":"酒心會收集好幾個小時，直到出現酒尾的乳酪、塑膠氣息。","The 10–15 minutes are the length of the heads. At the end of the heart it is not solvent that returns but the less volatile tails.":"10–15 分鐘是酒頭的長度。酒心結束時出現的不是溶劑味，而是較不易揮發的酒尾。","What does the bubble cap do on a column-still plate?":"柱式蒸餾器蒸餾板上的泡罩有什麼作用？","It forces vapour through the liquid on the plate":"迫使蒸氣穿過蒸餾板上的液體","It carries overflowing liquid to the plate below":"把溢出的液體送到下一層蒸餾板","It cools the vapour back into liquid, like a condenser":"像冷凝器一樣把蒸氣冷卻成液體","It lets the distiller look inside the column":"讓蒸餾師觀察蒸餾柱內部","The cap makes vapour bubble through the liquid, keeping it boiling.":"泡罩讓蒸氣在液體中冒泡通過，使液體保持沸騰。","Moving liquid downwards is the downcomer's job. The portholes are for looking inside. The bubble cap does not cool anything: in fact the vapour's heat keeps the liquid on the plate boiling.":"把液體往下送是降液管的工作。觀察窗是用來看內部的。泡罩不會冷卻任何東西：事實上，蒸氣的熱讓蒸餾板上的液體保持沸騰。","What is the downcomer for?":"降液管有什麼用途？","It sends overflowing liquid down to the plate below":"把溢出的液體送到下一層蒸餾板","It sends vapour up to the plate above":"把蒸氣送到上一層蒸餾板","It draws the heads off the top of the column":"從蒸餾柱頂部抽出酒頭","It injects high-pressure steam into the base":"把高壓蒸汽注入底部","When a plate fills up, the liquid overflows down the downcomer.":"蒸餾板滿了之後，液體就經降液管往下溢流。","The liquid going down is mostly water and less volatile fractions. Vapour rises instead through the central hole and bubble cap. Heads and heating steam have their own outlets and inlets.":"往下流的液體大部分是水和較不易揮發的餾分。蒸氣則是經由中央的孔和泡罩上升。酒頭和加熱用的蒸汽各有自己的出口和入口。","Where does distillation happen in a column still?":"在柱式蒸餾器中，蒸餾發生在哪裡？","On every plate at the same time":"在每一層蒸餾板上同時進行","Only in the base, the hottest part":"只在最熱的底部","Only on the top plate, near the summit":"只在靠近頂端的最上層蒸餾板","First in the base and then, once finished, on the next plate":"先在底部，完成後再到下一層蒸餾板","Each plate is a small distillation and they all run together.":"每一層蒸餾板都是一次小型蒸餾，而且全部同時進行。","It is this simultaneity that makes the column so efficient: there is no need to wait for one distillation to end before another begins. The base supplies the heat, but separation happens over the whole height of the tower.":"正是這種同時性讓蒸餾柱如此有效率：不必等一次蒸餾結束才開始另一次。底部提供熱，但分離發生在整座塔的高度上。","Why does the fermented liquid enter the column already pre-heated?":"為什麼發酵液進入蒸餾柱時已經預熱？","To keep the base, the hottest part, close to boiling":"讓最熱的底部保持接近沸騰","To kill any yeast still alive":"殺死任何還活著的酵母","To convert the last starch into sugar":"把最後的澱粉轉化為糖","To give it colour before distillation":"在蒸餾前為它上色","The base powers the whole column, so incoming liquid must be nearly boiling.":"底部為整座蒸餾柱提供動力，所以進入的液體必須接近沸騰。","If it came in cold, the base would cool and the column's balance would break. Starch conversion happens before fermentation, and colour never arises during distillation.":"如果進來的是冷液體，底部會降溫，蒸餾柱的平衡就會被打破。澱粉轉化發生在發酵之前，蒸餾過程中也絕不會產生顏色。","Where are the tails drawn off in a column still?":"在柱式蒸餾器中，酒尾從哪裡抽出？","From one of the lower plates":"從較低的某一層蒸餾板","From the top of the column":"從蒸餾柱頂部","From the plate just below the top, with the heads":"從頂部正下方的蒸餾板，與酒頭一起","From the condenser, at the end of each batch":"從冷凝器，在每一批結束時","Less volatile fractions concentrate low down and are taken off there.":"較不易揮發的餾分集中在低處，並在那裡取出。","The more volatile heads rise towards the top and are taken off near there. A column does not work in batches, so there is no 'end of batch': tails leave as a constant flow.":"較易揮發的酒頭往頂部上升，並在靠近頂部處取出。蒸餾柱不是批次運作，所以沒有「一批結束」：酒尾以持續的流量排出。","When is a column still said to be 'in balance'?":"什麼時候說柱式蒸餾器處於「平衡」狀態？","When volume in equals volume out":"進入的體積等於流出的體積時","When every plate has the same alcoholic strength":"每一層蒸餾板的酒精濃度都相同時","When the spirit coming out reaches 40% abv":"流出的烈酒達到 40% abv 時","When the column is stopped for routine cleaning":"蒸餾柱停機做例行清潔時","If what goes in equals what comes out, the column can run continuously.":"如果進去的等於出來的，蒸餾柱就能連續運轉。","Plates have different strengths: that is exactly what separates the fractions along the column. 40% is a bottling strength, not a distillation strength. A stopped column is not working at all.":"各層蒸餾板的濃度不同：這正是沿著蒸餾柱分離餾分的原因。40% 是裝瓶濃度，不是蒸餾濃度。停機的蒸餾柱根本沒有在運作。","Why can a column still reach 96% abv when a pot still cannot?":"為什麼柱式蒸餾器能達到 96% abv，壺式蒸餾器卻不行？","It need not recover all of one batch's alcohol before the next":"它不必在下一批之前回收一批中所有的酒精","It uses a stronger fermented liquid, around 40% abv":"它使用較濃的發酵液，大約 40% abv","It is always made of copper":"它一定是銅製的","It is heated by direct fire, which concentrates ethanol more":"它用直火加熱，更能濃縮乙醇","Ethanol rises and water falls continuously, with no need to dilute to recover each batch.":"乙醇持續上升、水持續下降，不必為了回收每一批而稀釋。","In a pot still, lots of water is collected so as not to lose alcohol. A column, with enough plates, concentrates ethanol plate after plate. The fermented liquid is around 10% in both cases, and steam heating is the norm.":"在壺式蒸餾器中，為了不損失酒精會收集到大量的水。蒸餾柱只要蒸餾板夠多，就能一層一層地濃縮乙醇。兩種情況下發酵液都是 10% 左右，蒸汽加熱則是常態。","Which of these spirits, although column-distilled, has a medium or pronounced aroma?":"下列哪一種烈酒雖然用蒸餾柱蒸餾，卻有中等或明顯的香氣？","Bourbon is column-distilled to a fairly low strength and keeps plenty of character.":"Bourbon 用蒸餾柱蒸餾到相當低的濃度，保有豐富的特色。","Like Armagnac and rhum agricole, Bourbon shows that a column can make expressive spirits. Vodka and neutral spirit are made at 95–96% abv; light rums are distilled at around 90%, with a light aroma.":"和 Armagnac、rhum agricole 一樣，Bourbon 說明了蒸餾柱也能做出表現力強的烈酒。伏特加和中性烈酒在 95–96% abv 製成；清淡型蘭姆酒蒸餾到約 90%，香氣清淡。","What style results from drawing the heart from a plate at about 90% abv?":"從大約 90% abv 的蒸餾板抽取酒心，會得到什麼風格？","Medium, identical to a pot-still spirit":"中等，與壺式蒸餾烈酒完全相同","At around 90% abv few congeners remain and the aroma is light.":"在大約 90% abv 時留下的同屬物很少，香氣清淡。","This is the style of some light rums and Scottish grain whisky. For a neutral spirit you need 95–96%. A pot still cannot reach 90%, so the comparison does not hold.":"這是某些清淡型蘭姆酒和蘇格蘭穀物威士忌的風格。中性烈酒需要 95–96%。壺式蒸餾器達不到 90%，所以這個比較不成立。","Which statement about column stills is true?":"關於柱式蒸餾器，下列哪一項正確？","It can make spirits from neutral to pronounced":"能做出從中性到香氣明顯的各種烈酒","It only ever makes neutral spirits, suitable only for vodka":"永遠只能做中性烈酒，只適合伏特加","It cannot go above 75% abv":"無法超過 75% abv","It must be emptied after every distillation":"每次蒸餾後都必須清空","It depends on which plate, and so which strength, the heart is drawn from.":"這取決於從哪一層蒸餾板、也就是在哪個濃度抽取酒心。","Armagnac, Bourbon and rhum agricole prove that a column does not mean neutrality. It can go well above 75%, up to 96%. It runs continuously, without being emptied every cycle.":"Armagnac、Bourbon 和 rhum agricole 證明了蒸餾柱不等於中性。它可以遠高於 75%，高達 96%。它連續運轉，不必每個循環都清空。","How does a heat exchanger work on a column still?":"柱式蒸餾器上的熱交換器如何運作？","Steam heats outside pipes without touching the liquid":"蒸汽加熱外部管路，不接觸液體","Steam is mixed straight into the fermented liquid in every column":"在每一座蒸餾柱中，蒸汽都直接混入發酵液","A gas flame heats the bottom of the column":"瓦斯火焰加熱蒸餾柱底部","Cold water cools the top of the column":"冷水冷卻蒸餾柱頂部","Heat passes through the metal pipework: steam and liquid stay apart.":"熱透過金屬管路傳遞：蒸汽和液體保持分開。","Boiling liquid from the base circulates through outside pipes heated by high-pressure steam. Direct steam injection exists, but only in some larger columns, not all. Direct flames are not the usual way to heat columns.":"底部沸騰的液體在外部管路中循環，由高壓蒸汽加熱。直接注入蒸汽的做法確實存在，但只見於某些較大的蒸餾柱，不是全部。直接火焰不是加熱蒸餾柱的常見方式。","Why are the heads collected near the top of the column?":"為什麼酒頭在靠近蒸餾柱頂部處收集？","They are the most volatile fractions and rise highest":"它們是最易揮發的餾分，升得最高","They are the heaviest fractions and float":"它們是最重的餾分，會浮起來","They are pushed up by the water coming down":"它們被往下流的水推上去","They contain most of the column's water":"它們含有蒸餾柱中大部分的水","Because they boil before ethanol, the heads reach the very top.":"因為比乙醇先沸騰，酒頭會到達最頂端。","Each congener concentrates at the level where it becomes the least volatile, and the most volatile fractions of all reach the top. Water, by contrast, falls to the base and becomes waste. Heads are usually drawn from a plate just below the top.":"每種同屬物都集中在它成為最不易揮發者的那個高度，而最易揮發的餾分會到達頂部。水則落到底部成為廢液。酒頭通常從頂部正下方的蒸餾板抽出。","A distillery wants a characterful spirit but only has a column still. What should it do?":"一家蒸餾廠想要有特色的烈酒，卻只有柱式蒸餾器。應該怎麼做？","Draw the heart from a lower-strength plate":"從濃度較低的蒸餾板抽取酒心","Draw the heart from the highest plate, as close to the top as possible":"從最高的蒸餾板抽取酒心，盡量靠近頂部","Add more plates to raise the strength":"增加蒸餾板來提高濃度","Give up: it cannot be done in a column":"放棄：蒸餾柱做不到","At lower strength, around 75%, plenty of congeners remain, so more aroma.":"在較低的濃度（75% 左右）會保留大量同屬物，所以香氣更多。","The higher the draw-off, the higher the strength and the more neutral the spirit; adding plates pushes the same way. Armagnac, Bourbon and rhum agricole show that a column can give plenty of character.":"抽取的位置越高，濃度越高，烈酒也越中性；增加蒸餾板的效果也是同一個方向。Armagnac、Bourbon 和 rhum agricole 說明了蒸餾柱也能做出豐富的特色。","What leaves from the base of a column still?":"從柱式蒸餾器底部排出的是什麼？","Watery liquid waste":"含水的廢液","The solvent-smelling heads":"帶溶劑氣味的酒頭","The heart at 96% abv":"96% abv 的酒心","Vapour heading to the condenser":"前往冷凝器的蒸氣","Watery liquid is drained from the base, the lowest and hottest part.":"含水的液體從底部排出，那是最低也最熱的部分。","Water is the least volatile fraction and sinks to the bottom. Heads and high-strength hearts are found higher up, where the vapour is most alcoholic.":"水是最不易揮發的餾分，會沉到底部。酒頭和高濃度的酒心在更高的位置，那裡的蒸氣酒精濃度最高。","Why are column stills, though 'continuous', stopped from time to time?":"柱式蒸餾器雖然是「連續式」的，為什麼還是要不時停機？","For cleaning":"為了清潔","To empty out the heads collected in the batch":"為了清出這一批收集到的酒頭","To run the second distillation with the low wines":"為了用低度酒進行第二次蒸餾","To let the liquid rest on the plates":"為了讓液體在蒸餾板上靜置","In theory they can run forever; in practice they are stopped for cleaning.":"理論上它們可以永遠運轉；實際上會停機清潔。","Batches, low wines and second distillations belong to the pot-still world. In a column, heads leave as a constant flow, with no need to wait for a cycle to end.":"批次、低度酒和第二次蒸餾屬於壺式蒸餾器的世界。在蒸餾柱中，酒頭以持續的流量排出，不必等一個循環結束。","On a column plate, compared with the boiling liquid, the vapour rising to the next plate is…":"在蒸餾柱的蒸餾板上，與沸騰的液體相比，升往上一層的蒸氣……","Richer in volatile fractions":"含有更多易揮發的餾分","Richer in water":"含有更多水","Identical in make-up":"組成完全相同","Richer in cheesy, plastic-smelling tails":"含有更多帶乳酪、塑膠氣味的酒尾","As in any distillation, vapour concentrates the more volatile fractions.":"和任何蒸餾一樣，蒸氣會濃縮較易揮發的餾分。","That is why the vapour powers an even more concentrated distillation on the plate above. Water and tails, being less volatile, stay in the liquid and go down the downcomer.":"所以這些蒸氣會在上一層蒸餾板推動一次更濃縮的蒸餾。水和酒尾較不易揮發，留在液體中並經降液管往下流。","What are the porthole windows along a column still for?":"柱式蒸餾器上的觀察窗有什麼用途？","To watch what is happening on each plate":"觀察每一層蒸餾板上的情況","To let carbon dioxide escape":"讓二氧化碳散逸","To draw off the heads":"抽出酒頭","To let in air that oxidises the spirit and adds aromas":"讓空氣進入，使烈酒氧化並增添香氣","The portholes let the distiller see and monitor each plate.":"觀察窗讓蒸餾師可以查看並監控每一層蒸餾板。","Carbon dioxide is released during fermentation, before distillation. Heads are drawn off through a dedicated outlet near the top. The oxidation that enriches aromas happens in barrels, not in the column.":"二氧化碳是在蒸餾之前的發酵過程中釋放的。酒頭經由靠近頂部的專用出口抽出。能豐富香氣的氧化發生在桶中，不是在蒸餾柱裡。","Which is the hottest part of a working column still?":"運轉中的柱式蒸餾器，哪個部分最熱？","The base":"底部","The top":"頂部","The plate the heads come from":"抽出酒頭的那層蒸餾板","The middle plate, halfway up the tower":"位於塔身一半高度的中間蒸餾板","The base is the hottest zone and its heat powers the whole column.":"底部是最熱的區域，它的熱推動整座蒸餾柱。","Going up, the temperature drops because the vapours become richer in volatile fractions, which boil at lower temperatures. That is why the heads come out at the top and water stays at the bottom. Incoming liquid is pre-heated precisely so as not to cool the base.":"越往上溫度越低，因為蒸氣含有越來越多易揮發的餾分，它們的沸點較低。所以酒頭從頂部出來，水留在底部。進入的液體之所以預熱，正是為了不讓底部降溫。","Where do the vapours rising through a column plate pass?":"上升通過蒸餾板的蒸氣從哪裡經過？","Through the large hole in the centre of the plate":"經過蒸餾板中央的大孔","Through the downcomer":"經過降液管","Through the porthole windows":"經過觀察窗","Through outside pipes that bypass the plate completely":"經過完全繞過蒸餾板的外部管路","Vapours rise from below through the large central hole, covered by the bubble cap.":"蒸氣從下方經由中央的大孔上升，大孔上方蓋著泡罩。","The bubble cap then forces them through the liquid on the plate. The downcomer is for the opposite path, liquid going down. Portholes are only for watching, and vapour bypassing the plate would distil nothing.":"泡罩接著迫使它們穿過蒸餾板上的液體。降液管走的是相反的路徑，讓液體往下流。觀察窗只用來觀看，而繞過蒸餾板的蒸氣什麼也蒸餾不了。","What keeps the liquid on each plate boiling?":"什麼讓每一層蒸餾板上的液體保持沸騰？","The heat of the vapours passing through it":"穿過液體的蒸氣所帶的熱","A flame under each plate":"每層蒸餾板下方的火焰","The cold water from the condenser":"來自冷凝器的冷水","An electric element inside each bubble cap":"每個泡罩內的電熱元件","Hot vapours rising from below give up heat to the liquid on the plate and keep it boiling.":"從下方上升的高溫蒸氣把熱傳給蒸餾板上的液體，讓它保持沸騰。","All the energy comes from the base, the hottest part; from there heat climbs plate by plate with the vapours. There are no flames or elements on individual plates, and cold water condenses rather than heats.":"所有能量都來自最熱的底部；熱從那裡隨蒸氣一層一層往上。個別的蒸餾板上沒有火焰或加熱元件，冷水則是用來冷凝，不是加熱。","What is the liquid going down the downcomer mainly made of?":"經降液管往下流的液體主要由什麼組成？","Water and the least volatile fractions":"水和最不易揮發的餾分","Fresh fermented liquid just fed in at the top":"剛從頂部注入的新鮮發酵液","The plate fills with water and the least volatile fractions; when it overflows, the downcomer takes them to the plate below.":"蒸餾板上積滿水和最不易揮發的餾分；溢出時，降液管把它們帶到下一層蒸餾板。","Ethanol and the heads, being more volatile, tend to rise with the vapours. In the simplified column the fermented liquid enters at the base, not the top.":"乙醇和酒頭較易揮發，傾向隨蒸氣上升。在簡化的蒸餾柱中，發酵液從底部進入，不是頂部。","What powers the distillation on the plate above?":"什麼推動上一層蒸餾板的蒸餾？","The vapours rising from the plate below":"從下一層蒸餾板上升的蒸氣","The liquid coming down the downcomer":"經降液管流下來的液體","The condenser at the top of the column":"蒸餾柱頂部的冷凝器","Heat from the lit portholes":"有照明的觀察窗發出的熱","Each plate's vapours, richer in volatile fractions, rise and boil the liquid on the plate above.":"每一層蒸餾板的蒸氣含有更多易揮發的餾分，上升後讓上一層蒸餾板的液體沸騰。","It is a chain: each plate gets heat and vapour from the one below. Downcomer liquid goes down and carries no heat upward. The condenser cools; it does not heat.":"這是一條鏈：每層蒸餾板都從下一層得到熱和蒸氣。降液管的液體往下流，不會把熱往上帶。冷凝器是冷卻的，不是加熱的。","Which description of the flows in a working column is correct?":"下列哪一項正確描述了運轉中蒸餾柱的流動？","Vapour rises, liquid falls":"蒸氣上升，液體下降","Liquid rises, vapour falls":"液體上升，蒸氣下降","Everything rises to the top":"所有東西都升到頂部","Nothing moves until a cut is made, as in a pot still":"和壺式蒸餾器一樣，切取之前什麼都不動","There is a constant flow of vapour up and liquid down through the plates.":"蒸氣持續往上、液體持續往下，穿過各層蒸餾板。","Ethanol goes up and water comes down, so the fractions separate along the height. A column has no time-based cuts like a pot still: fractions leave continuously from different points.":"乙醇往上、水往下，所以餾分沿著高度分離。蒸餾柱不像壺式蒸餾器那樣按時間切取：餾分從不同位置連續排出。","Where are the heads usually drawn off in a column still?":"在柱式蒸餾器中，酒頭通常從哪裡抽出？","From a plate just below the top":"從頂部正下方的蒸餾板","From the base":"從底部","From one of the lowest plates":"從最低的幾層蒸餾板之一","From the downcomer of the middle plate, halfway up":"從位於一半高度的中間蒸餾板的降液管","The most volatile fractions rise to the top; the distiller takes a continuous flow of heads from a plate just below it.":"最易揮發的餾分升到頂部；蒸餾師從頂部正下方的蒸餾板持續取出酒頭。","Watery waste leaves from the base and tails are drained from low plates. The heart is drawn from whichever plate gives the desired strength.":"含水的廢液從底部排出，酒尾從低層蒸餾板排出。酒心則從能得到所需濃度的那層蒸餾板抽取。","Besides heat exchangers, how are some large column stills heated?":"除了熱交換器，一些大型柱式蒸餾器還用什麼方式加熱？","By injecting steam straight into the still":"把蒸汽直接注入蒸餾器","With a wood fire under the base":"在底部下方燒柴火","With hot water from a worm tub condenser":"用蟲桶冷凝器的熱水","With electric elements fitted on every bubble cap":"在每個泡罩上裝電熱元件","In some larger stills steam is injected directly into the column.":"在一些較大的蒸餾器中，蒸汽直接注入蒸餾柱。","Columns are typically steam-heated: either via a heat exchanger, where steam and liquid never touch, or by direct injection. Wood fires, worm tubs and plate heaters are not part of this picture.":"蒸餾柱通常用蒸汽加熱：透過熱交換器（蒸汽和液體不接觸），或直接注入。柴火、蟲桶冷凝器和蒸餾板加熱器都不在其中。","Why does a column with few plates struggle to make neutral spirit?":"為什麼蒸餾板少的蒸餾柱很難做出中性烈酒？","Fewer plates mean fewer distillations and a lower top strength":"蒸餾板越少，蒸餾次數越少，最高濃度也越低","Because short columns have no hot base":"因為矮蒸餾柱沒有高溫的底部","Because extra plates add aromas to the spirit":"因為多加的蒸餾板會為烈酒增添香氣","Because without many plates a column cannot run continuously":"因為沒有很多蒸餾板，蒸餾柱就無法連續運轉","Each plate is one distillation: enough plates are needed to climb to 95–96% abv.":"每一層蒸餾板就是一次蒸餾：需要足夠的蒸餾板才能升到 95–96% abv。","Even a short column has a hot base and runs continuously. Plates add no aromas; on the contrary, more plates mean more congeners left behind.":"即使是矮蒸餾柱也有高溫的底部，也是連續運轉。蒸餾板不會增添香氣；相反地，蒸餾板越多，留下不取的同屬物越多。","Compared with a tall column, what characterises a short column with few plates?":"與高蒸餾柱相比，蒸餾板少的矮蒸餾柱有什麼特點？","A lower top strength and a spirit with more congeners":"最高濃度較低，烈酒含較多同屬物","It always makes purer neutral spirit":"做出的中性烈酒一定更純","It works in batches like a pot still":"像壺式蒸餾器一樣以批次運作","It never needs to draw off heads, tails or watery waste":"從不需要抽出酒頭、酒尾或含水廢液","With fewer plates the column cannot reach the highest strengths, so the spirit keeps more character.":"蒸餾板較少時，蒸餾柱達不到最高的濃度，所以烈酒保有更多特色。","The number of plates is what allows 96%, so neutral spirit needs tall columns. Even a short column runs continuously and separates heads, tails and waste.":"蒸餾板的數量是達到 96% 的關鍵，所以中性烈酒需要高蒸餾柱。即使是矮蒸餾柱也連續運轉，並分離酒頭、酒尾和廢液。","What is the main operating difference between a column and a pot still?":"蒸餾柱和壺式蒸餾器在運作上的主要差別是什麼？","The column runs non-stop; the pot still is filled and emptied":"蒸餾柱不停運轉；壺式蒸餾器要裝料和清空","The column works in batches; the pot still runs continuously":"蒸餾柱以批次運作；壺式蒸餾器連續運轉","The column uses no heat":"蒸餾柱不用熱","The column does not separate heads and tails; they all end up in the spirit":"蒸餾柱不分離酒頭和酒尾；它們全都進入烈酒","The column takes a constant feed and produces continuously; the pot still works batch by batch.":"蒸餾柱持續進料並連續產出；壺式蒸餾器則是一批一批地運作。","The column also needs heat, usually steam, and does separate heads and tails, drawing them continuously from different plates. It only stops for periodic cleaning.":"蒸餾柱同樣需要熱，通常是蒸汽，而且確實會分離酒頭和酒尾，從不同的蒸餾板連續抽出。它只在定期清潔時停機。","Each congener reaches a plate where it is the least volatile. What happens above that plate?":"每種同屬物都會到達它成為最不易揮發者的那層蒸餾板。在那層之上會怎麼樣？","Its concentration falls away quickly":"它的濃度迅速下降","Its concentration keeps rising":"它的濃度持續上升","It turns into ethanol":"它變成乙醇","It stays the same on every plate up to the top":"一直到頂部，每層蒸餾板都保持不變","Above the plate where it is least volatile, that congener gets left behind and almost disappears.":"在它最不易揮發的那層蒸餾板之上，這種同屬物就被留下，幾乎消失。","This spreads congeners along the height: the most volatile at the top, the least volatile low down. So the higher the draw, the fewer aromas. Congeners do not turn into ethanol.":"這讓同屬物沿著高度分布：最易揮發的在頂部，最不易揮發的在低處。所以抽取位置越高，香氣越少。同屬物不會變成乙醇。","In a column with 40 plates, what can the distiller choose?":"在一座有 40 層蒸餾板的蒸餾柱中，蒸餾師可以選擇什麼？","Which plate to draw the heart from":"從哪一層蒸餾板抽取酒心","How many hours the heads should last":"酒頭要持續幾個小時","The colour of the spirit":"烈酒的顏色","How much sugar to send into the vapour to sweeten the heart":"要讓多少糖進入蒸氣來為酒心增甜","In theory the distiller can draw the heart from the plate with the strength, and so the style, required.":"理論上，蒸餾師可以從具有所需濃度（也就是所需風格）的蒸餾板抽取酒心。","In a column the heads leave continuously, not for a set number of hours. The spirit is colourless and dry: any colour or sugar comes later, and sugar does not enter the vapour.":"在蒸餾柱中，酒頭是連續排出的，不是持續固定的幾個小時。烈酒無色且不甜：顏色或糖都是之後才有的，而且糖不會進入蒸氣。","One spirit drawn at 75% from a column, another collected at 75% in a pot still. How will they compare?":"一款烈酒從蒸餾柱在 75% 抽取，另一款在壺式蒸餾器中於 75% 收集。兩者相比如何？","Very similar in aroma intensity":"香氣強度非常相近","The column one will be neutral":"蒸餾柱的那款會是中性的","The pot-still one will be neutral":"壺式蒸餾器的那款會是中性的","The column one will already be coloured, the pot-still one colourless":"蒸餾柱的那款已有顏色，壺式蒸餾器的那款無色","At the same 75% both keep plenty of congeners: a medium or pronounced aroma.":"同樣在 75% 時，兩者都保留大量同屬物：香氣中等或明顯。","The collection strength matters more than the type of still. Neutrality only comes at about 95–96%. Every newly made spirit is colourless.":"收集濃度比蒸餾器的類型更重要。中性只有在大約 95–96% 才出現。所有新酒都是無色的。","Which of these column-made spirits is NOT considered characterful?":"下列用蒸餾柱製作的烈酒中，哪一種不被認為有鮮明特色？","Armagnac":"Armagnac","Bourbon":"Bourbon","Scottish grain whisky is distilled to about 90%, so its aroma is light.":"蘇格蘭穀物威士忌蒸餾到大約 90%，所以香氣清淡。","Armagnac, Bourbon and rhum agricole are drawn at lower strengths and stay aromatic though column-made. This shows a column can give any style, from pronounced to neutral.":"Armagnac、Bourbon 和 rhum agricole 在較低的濃度抽取，雖然用蒸餾柱製作，仍然香氣豐富。這說明蒸餾柱能做出任何風格，從香氣明顯到中性都可以。","In a column that is already running, where is there boiling liquid?":"在已經運轉的蒸餾柱中，哪裡有沸騰的液體？","On every plate and in the base":"每一層蒸餾板和底部","Only in the base":"只有底部","Only on the top plate":"只有最上層蒸餾板","Only in the condenser, where vapours become liquid again":"只有冷凝器，蒸氣在那裡重新變成液體","When the column is running, every plate and the base hold boiling liquid.":"蒸餾柱運轉時，每一層蒸餾板和底部都有沸騰的液體。","This is exactly what allows a distillation on every plate at the same time. The condenser, by contrast, cools vapours: nothing boils there.":"這正是讓每層蒸餾板能同時進行蒸餾的原因。冷凝器則是冷卻蒸氣：那裡沒有東西在沸騰。","For a simple water-ethanol mix in a column, how does strength change going up plate by plate?":"對蒸餾柱中單純的水和乙醇混合液來說，一層一層往上時濃度如何變化？","It increases at every plate":"每一層都升高","It decreases at every plate":"每一層都降低","It stays the same on every plate":"每一層都相同","It rises to halfway, then falls back to 10% at the top":"升到一半高度，然後在頂部降回 10%","Each plate selects and concentrates ethanol, so strength climbs plate after plate.":"每一層蒸餾板都篩選並濃縮乙醇，所以濃度一層一層攀升。","The distiller can draw liquid from whichever plate has reached the required strength. With enough plates it reaches 96%. Water, meanwhile, flows down to the base.":"蒸餾師可以從達到所需濃度的任何一層蒸餾板抽取液體。蒸餾板夠多就能達到 96%。同時，水往下流到底部。","In a running column with 30 plates, how many distillations happen at once?":"在一座運轉中、有 30 層蒸餾板的蒸餾柱裡，同時發生幾次蒸餾？","About 30, one per plate":"大約 30 次，每層蒸餾板一次","Just one, as in a pot still":"只有一次，和壺式蒸餾器一樣","Two, as in double distillation":"兩次，和二次蒸餾一樣","None: distillation only happens in the condenser at the top":"沒有：蒸餾只發生在頂部的冷凝器","A distillation takes place on every plate, and they all happen at the same time.":"每一層蒸餾板上都進行一次蒸餾，而且全部同時發生。","This is the key point of a column: many simultaneous, continuous distillations. A pot still does one at a time. The condenser turns vapour back into liquid; it does not distil.":"這是蒸餾柱的關鍵：許多同時進行、連續不斷的蒸餾。壺式蒸餾器一次只做一次蒸餾。冷凝器把蒸氣變回液體，並不蒸餾。","Why does a column separate fractions more precisely than a pot still?":"為什麼蒸餾柱分離餾分比壺式蒸餾器更精確？","Simultaneous distillations spread them along its height":"同時進行的蒸餾讓餾分沿著高度分布","Because it is always made of copper":"因為它一定是銅製的","Because it uses direct fire, which is more precise than steam":"因為它使用直火，比蒸汽更精確","Because it only distils very sugary liquids":"因為它只蒸餾含糖量很高的液體","With continuous, simultaneous distillations on every plate, each fraction concentrates at a particular height.":"每層蒸餾板上連續、同時進行蒸餾，每種餾分就集中在特定的高度。","So the distiller can draw heads, heart and tails from different points very precisely. Columns are usually steam-heated and distil fermented, not sugary, liquids.":"所以蒸餾師可以非常精確地從不同位置抽出酒頭、酒心和酒尾。蒸餾柱通常用蒸汽加熱，蒸餾的是發酵過的液體，不是含糖液體。","Which statement about a column's outlets is FALSE?":"關於蒸餾柱的出口，下列哪一項是錯誤的？","The heads leave from the base":"酒頭從底部排出","The tails are drained from a low plate":"酒尾從低層蒸餾板排出","Watery waste leaves from the base":"含水的廢液從底部排出","The heart is drawn from the plate with the strength wanted":"酒心從具有所需濃度的蒸餾板抽取","The heads, the most volatile fractions, leave near the top, not from the base.":"酒頭是最易揮發的餾分，從靠近頂部處排出，不是底部。","The other three are correct: tails from low plates, watery waste from the base, heart from the chosen plate. If what goes in equals what comes out, the column is in balance.":"其他三項都正確：酒尾來自低層蒸餾板，含水廢液來自底部，酒心來自選定的蒸餾板。如果進去的等於出來的，蒸餾柱就處於平衡。","In the simplified column, where does the pre-heated fermented liquid enter?":"在簡化的蒸餾柱中，預熱過的發酵液從哪裡進入？","Into the base":"進入底部","At the top":"在頂部","Into the condenser":"進入冷凝器","Straight into the heart tank":"直接進入酒心的槽","The liquid flows continuously into the base, the hottest part, as close to boiling as possible.":"液體持續流入最熱的底部，溫度盡可能接近沸騰。","The energy powering the whole column comes from the base. The top is where the most volatile fractions gather, and the condenser and tank receive what has already been distilled.":"推動整座蒸餾柱的能量來自底部。頂部是最易揮發的餾分聚集的地方，冷凝器和槽接收的則是已經蒸餾過的東西。","Where is a 96% spirit drawn off compared with a 90% one?":"與 90% 的烈酒相比，96% 的烈酒從哪裡抽出？","From a higher plate":"從較高的蒸餾板","From a lower plate":"從較低的蒸餾板","From the same plate, but later in the day":"從同一層蒸餾板，但在當天較晚的時候","From the base, where the liquid is hottest and most concentrated":"從底部，那裡的液體最熱、最濃","Strength increases going up, so 96% is found higher than 90%.":"濃度越往上越高，所以 96% 的位置比 90% 高。","In a column, style depends on where you draw, not when: the process is continuous. The base is the hottest part but also the most watery, where waste leaves.":"在蒸餾柱中，風格取決於從哪裡抽取，而不是什麼時候：這個過程是連續的。底部最熱，但含水也最多，廢液就從那裡排出。","Which of these parts belongs to a column still?":"下列哪個零件屬於柱式蒸餾器？","The still head, olive-shaped in Cognac":"蒸餾器頂部，在 Cognac 呈橄欖形","The bubble cap, on the plates, forces vapour through the liquid: a typical column part.":"泡罩位於蒸餾板上，迫使蒸氣穿過液體：是典型的蒸餾柱零件。","Swan neck, lyne arm and still head are pot-still parts. The key column parts are heat source, plates, bubble caps and downcomers.":"天鵝頸、林恩臂和蒸餾器頂部是壺式蒸餾器的零件。蒸餾柱的關鍵零件是熱源、蒸餾板、泡罩和降液管。","In a column's heat exchanger, what circulates through the outside pipes?":"在蒸餾柱的熱交換器中，在外部管路裡循環的是什麼？","The column's boiling alcoholic liquid":"蒸餾柱中沸騰的含酒精液體","Cold water for condensing":"冷凝用的冷水","Tails to be recycled":"待回收的酒尾","The finished spirit, which then goes straight to bottle":"成品烈酒，之後直接裝瓶","The boiling liquid circulates through pipes outside the still, heated by high-pressure steam.":"沸騰的液體在蒸餾器外的管路中循環，由高壓蒸汽加熱。","Steam and liquid never touch: heat passes through the metal. Cold water belongs to the condenser. Spirit almost never goes straight to bottle: there is nearly always some finishing.":"蒸汽和液體絕不接觸：熱透過金屬傳遞。冷水屬於冷凝器。烈酒幾乎從不直接裝瓶：幾乎都會有一些收尾處理。","Moving up a working column still, how does the temperature change?":"在運轉中的柱式蒸餾器裡往上走，溫度如何變化？","It falls: the base is the hottest part":"下降：底部是最熱的部分","It rises: the top is the hottest part":"上升：頂部是最熱的部分","It is identical on every plate":"每一層蒸餾板都相同","It depends only on the air temperature in the still house":"只取決於蒸餾室的氣溫","The base is hottest; higher up are ever more volatile fractions that boil at lower temperatures.":"底部最熱；越往上是越易揮發的餾分，沸點越低。","That is why water and the least volatile compounds gather low and the heads at the top. Heat comes from the base and rises with the vapour, so temperature cannot be the same everywhere.":"所以水和最不易揮發的化合物聚集在低處，酒頭在頂部。熱來自底部並隨蒸氣上升，所以溫度不可能處處相同。","Compared with a pot still, how do the heads leave a column still?":"與壺式蒸餾器相比，酒頭如何離開柱式蒸餾器？","As a continuous flow, all the time":"以連續的流量，一直不停","Only during the first 10–15 minutes":"只在最初的 10–15 分鐘","Only at the end of the day, before cleaning":"只在一天結束、清潔之前","Never: in a column the heads stay in the heart and are never separated":"永遠不會：在蒸餾柱中酒頭留在酒心裡，從不分離","In a column the heads leave non-stop from a plate near the top, whereas in a pot still they come only at the start of a run.":"在蒸餾柱中，酒頭不停地從靠近頂部的蒸餾板排出；在壺式蒸餾器中，它們只在蒸餾開始時出現。","The same goes for the tails, drained continuously from a low plate. The 10–15 minutes apply to the pot still. A column separates fractions very precisely rather than leaving them in the heart.":"酒尾也是一樣，從低層蒸餾板連續排出。10–15 分鐘指的是壺式蒸餾器。蒸餾柱非常精確地分離餾分，而不是把它們留在酒心裡。","A distiller draws the heart at 95–96% from a tall column. What is this spirit suited to?":"一位蒸餾師從高蒸餾柱在 95–96% 抽取酒心。這款烈酒適合做什麼？","A vodka or a neutral base for flavouring":"伏特加，或用來調味的中性基酒","A Cognac":"Cognac","A very aromatic high-ester rum":"香氣非常濃郁的高酯蘭姆酒","A characterful malt whisky":"特色鮮明的麥芽威士忌","At 95–96% the spirit is neutral: ideal for vodka or as a base for flavoured spirits.":"在 95–96% 時烈酒是中性的：最適合做伏特加，或作為調味烈酒的基酒。","Cognac, malt whisky and high-ester rum need plenty of congeners and are made in pot stills at much lower strengths. At that strength nothing of their character would remain.":"Cognac、麥芽威士忌和高酯蘭姆酒需要大量同屬物，用壺式蒸餾器在低得多的濃度製作。在那樣的濃度下，它們的特色將蕩然無存。","Which statement about column still designs is true?":"關於柱式蒸餾器的設計，下列哪一項正確？","They vary a lot but all work on the same principles":"差異很大，但都依相同的原理運作","They are identical in every distillery":"每家蒸餾廠的都一模一樣","Only one type of plate is allowed by law":"法律只允許一種蒸餾板","Each design relies on a completely different physical principle":"每種設計依據的物理原理完全不同","Columns come in many shapes and plate designs, but all rely on continuous distillation across several plates.":"蒸餾柱有許多形狀和蒸餾板設計，但都依靠在多層蒸餾板上連續蒸餾。","The bubble-cap plate is a common design, not the only one. The principles stay the same: rising vapour, falling liquid, fractions separated along the height.":"泡罩蒸餾板是常見的設計，不是唯一的一種。原理始終相同：蒸氣上升、液體下降、餾分沿高度分離。","What are column stills typically heated with?":"柱式蒸餾器通常用什麼加熱？","Steam":"蒸汽","The direct flame of a gas burner":"瓦斯爐的直接火焰","Sunlight through the portholes":"透過觀察窗照進來的陽光","Hot water leaving the condenser":"從冷凝器流出的熱水","Column stills are usually steam-heated, through heat exchangers or, in larger ones, by direct injection.":"柱式蒸餾器通常用蒸汽加熱，透過熱交換器，或在較大的蒸餾器中直接注入。","Direct flame is typical of some pot stills, as in Cognac. Portholes are for watching the plates, and condenser water would not be hot enough to boil the base.":"直接火焰是某些壺式蒸餾器的典型做法，例如 Cognac。觀察窗是用來觀察蒸餾板的，冷凝器的水也不夠熱，無法讓底部沸騰。","In what order do post-distillation operations usually happen?":"蒸餾後處理通常依什麼順序進行？","Maturation, other flavours, blending, finishing":"熟成、其他風味、調和、收尾處理","Finishing, blending, maturation, other flavours":"收尾處理、調和、熟成、其他風味","Blending, finishing, other flavours, maturation":"調和、收尾處理、其他風味、熟成","Other flavours, finishing, maturation, blending":"其他風味、收尾處理、熟成、調和","First maturation, then flavouring, blending and finally finishing for the bottle.":"先熟成，再調味、調和，最後做裝瓶前的收尾處理。","Finishing, which covers dilution, colour, sugar and filtration, is always the last step before bottling. Not every spirit goes through every stage: it depends on the law and the producer's choices.":"收尾處理包括稀釋、調色、加糖和過濾，永遠是裝瓶前的最後一步。並非每種烈酒都經過每個階段：這取決於法規和生產者的選擇。","Which aromas typically come from oak?":"哪些香氣通常來自橡木？","Vanilla, coconut, cinnamon, clove":"香草、椰子、肉桂、丁香","Pear, apple, banana":"梨、蘋果、香蕉","Solvent, nail varnish, glue":"溶劑、指甲油、膠水","Black pepper and earth, like cooked blue agave":"黑胡椒和土壤，像煮熟的藍色龍舌蘭","Vanilla, coconut, cinnamon and clove are among the most common oak aromas.":"香草、椰子、肉桂和丁香是最常見的橡木香氣。","Fruit notes come rather from raw materials and fermentation, solvent notes from the heads. Earthy, peppery notes are typical of agave as a raw material, not of oak.":"水果氣息多半來自原料和發酵，溶劑氣息來自酒頭。土壤和胡椒氣息是龍舌蘭這種原料的典型特徵，不是橡木的。","What does 'rancio' mean in an aged spirit?":"在陳年烈酒中，「rancio」是什麼意思？","Leather and mushroom notes from oxygen and time":"氧氣和時間帶來的皮革和蘑菇氣息","A fault caused by a broken barrel":"桶子破損造成的缺陷","The solvent smell of the first fractions off the still":"蒸餾器最初餾分的溶劑氣味","Colour added with caramel":"用焦糖色添加的顏色","Over time, congeners react with oxygen to create leather and mushroom notes.":"隨著時間，同屬物與氧氣反應，產生皮革和蘑菇氣息。","Rancio is a prized feature of long-aged spirits, not a fault. A solvent smell belongs to the heads. Caramel only affects colour and has no taste.":"rancio 是長期陳年烈酒備受珍視的特徵，不是缺陷。溶劑氣味屬於酒頭。焦糖色只影響顏色，沒有味道。","What is the 'angels' share'?":"什麼是「天使的分享」（angels' share）？","Water and alcohol evaporating from the barrel":"從桶中蒸發的水和酒精","Spirit left soaked into the wood when the barrel is emptied":"清空桶子時仍滲在木頭裡的烈酒","Heads discarded during distillation":"蒸餾時丟棄的酒頭","The haze removed by chill-filtration":"冷凝過濾去除的混濁物","It is the water and ethanol that evaporate through the wood during maturation.":"它是熟成過程中透過木頭蒸發的水和乙醇。","This evaporation concentrates the remaining congeners, making very old spirits intense and complex. Liquid soaked into the wood matters instead when choosing a barrel's previous contents.":"這種蒸發會濃縮留下的同屬物，讓極老的烈酒濃郁而複雜。滲在木頭裡的液體，則是在選擇桶子先前裝過什麼時才有關係。","How does a barrel smooth away a young spirit's harshness?":"桶子如何讓年輕烈酒的粗糙感變得柔順？","The charred inner layer captures some congeners":"炙燒過的內層會抓住一些同屬物","The wood adds sugar to the spirit":"木頭為烈酒增添糖分","The wood lowers the strength by absorbing alcohol":"木頭吸收酒精而降低濃度","Oxygen turns all the ethanol into water":"氧氣把所有乙醇變成水","The carbon from the inside char or toast holds on to harsh congeners.":"內部炙燒或烘烤產生的碳會抓住粗糙的同屬物。","This layer, called char or toast, is created when the barrel is made. The wood adds no sugar and does not turn ethanol into water. Oxygen creates new aromas, such as rancio.":"這一層稱為炙燒層（char）或烘烤層（toast），是製桶時形成的。木頭不會增添糖分，也不會把乙醇變成水。氧氣會產生新的香氣，例如 rancio。","Which barrel gives the most colour and flavour to a spirit?":"哪一種桶為烈酒帶來最多顏色和風味？","A brand-new barrel":"全新的桶","A barrel already used three or four times":"已經用過三、四次的桶","A very old barrel with no aromas of its own left":"已經沒有自身香氣的極老的桶","A glass demijohn":"玻璃罈","A barrel gives most on its first use, then less each time.":"桶子第一次使用時給得最多，之後每次遞減。","A re-used barrel is not inferior: it gives less, which may be exactly what a delicate style needs. Glass is inert and gives neither colour nor flavour.":"重複使用的桶並不比較差：它給得較少，而這可能正是細緻風格所需要的。玻璃是惰性的，既不帶來顏色，也不帶來風味。","A producer puts a whisky into former wine barrels for a few months. Which factor is being used?":"一位生產者把威士忌放進裝過葡萄酒的桶中幾個月。運用的是哪一項因素？","The barrel's previous contents":"桶子先前裝過的東西","The warehouse temperature":"酒庫的溫度","Activated charcoal filtration, which strips aroma and colour":"活性碳過濾，會去除香氣和顏色","Wine left in the wood seeps out and adds flavour, sometimes a little colour.":"留在木頭裡的葡萄酒滲出來，增添風味，有時還有一點顏色。","This practice, called finishing, is common for some Scotch whiskies. Temperature affects the speed of maturation, not wine flavour. Activated charcoal would remove aromas rather than add them.":"這種做法稱為過桶（finishing），常見於某些 Scotch 威士忌。溫度影響的是熟成的速度，不是葡萄酒風味。活性碳會去除香氣，而不是增添。","Why does a Kentucky Bourbon tend to mature faster than a Scotch?":"為什麼肯塔基州的 Bourbon 往往比 Scotch 熟成得快？","Hot summers speed up exchanges between spirit and wood":"炎熱的夏天加快了烈酒與木頭之間的交換","The cool, damp climate slows evaporation and concentrates aromas faster":"涼爽潮濕的氣候減緩蒸發，並更快地濃縮香氣","Glass barrels are used":"使用玻璃桶","More caramel is added":"加了更多焦糖色","In heat the spirit moves in and out of the wood faster, extracting colour and flavour.":"在高溫下，烈酒更快地進出木頭，萃取出顏色和風味。","Kentucky has very hot summers and Scotland cooler ones, so Bourbon reaches maturity sooner and with a deeper colour. Caramel only changes colour, not maturation, and barrels are made of wood.":"肯塔基州夏天非常炎熱，蘇格蘭較涼爽，所以 Bourbon 更早成熟，顏色也更深。焦糖色只改變顏色，不影響熟成，而桶是木頭做的。","A spirit rests for a few weeks in a steel tank before bottling. What will it be like?":"一款烈酒裝瓶前在鋼槽中靜置幾週。它會是什麼樣子？","Colourless and almost unchanged":"無色，幾乎沒有變化","Golden, with vanilla notes":"金黃色，帶香草氣息","Amber, with the leather and mushroom notes of rancio":"琥珀色，帶 rancio 的皮革和蘑菇氣息","Sweeter, because the steel releases sugar":"更甜，因為鋼會釋出糖","Steel is inert: it adds no colour or flavour, and a short rest changes very little.":"鋼是惰性的：不增添顏色或風味，短暫靜置幾乎不會帶來改變。","Such a spirit is called 'unaged'. Vanilla, golden colour and rancio need wood and, for rancio, a long time. Steel releases no sugar.":"這樣的烈酒稱為「未陳年」。香草、金黃色和 rancio 需要木頭，rancio 還需要很長的時間。鋼不會釋出糖。","What happens to a spirit kept for many months in an inert vessel?":"在惰性容器中存放好幾個月的烈酒會怎麼樣？","It becomes smoother and fuller but stays colourless":"變得更柔順、更飽滿，但仍然無色","It turns golden":"變成金黃色","It develops strong vanilla and coconut notes":"發展出強烈的香草和椰子氣息","It loses half its volume by evaporating through the walls":"透過容器壁蒸發而損失一半的體積","After some months the texture changes, but the colour does not.":"幾個月後質地會改變，但顏色不會。","This evolution can carry on for years, though maturing spirits this way is rare. Colour and vanilla or coconut aromas come only from oak. Steel and glass do not let the spirit evaporate the way wood does.":"這種變化可以持續好幾年，不過用這種方式熟成烈酒很少見。顏色以及香草或椰子香氣只來自橡木。鋼和玻璃不像木頭那樣會讓烈酒蒸發。","Why are some very old Cognacs moved into glass demijohns?":"為什麼有些極老的 Cognac 會移到玻璃罈中？","To stop oxidation and concentration":"停止氧化和濃縮","To give them more colour":"讓顏色更深","To speed up maturation and get more oak notes":"加快熟成並得到更多橡木氣息","So they can be sold as 'unaged'":"這樣就能以「未陳年」販售","Glass is inert and halts development: the spirit stays as it is.":"玻璃是惰性的，會讓變化停止：烈酒維持原樣。","These precious reserves are then used sparingly in the finest blends. Glass adds no colour or flavour and speeds nothing up. Having already spent years in oak, they could not be called unaged.":"這些珍貴的庫存之後會少量用在最頂級的調和中。玻璃不增添顏色或風味，也不會加快任何過程。它們已經在橡木桶中度過多年，不可能稱為未陳年。","Which flavouring technique also extracts colour from botanicals?":"哪一種調味技術也會從植物性原料中萃取顏色？","Redistillation in a vacuum still at low temperature":"在真空蒸餾器中低溫再蒸餾","Activated charcoal filtration":"活性碳過濾","Maceration leaves botanicals in the alcohol, drawing out colour and a broad range of flavour.":"浸漬是把植物性原料留在酒精中，萃取出顏色和範圍廣泛的風味。","Colour is not volatile, so it does not pass through any distillation, even under vacuum. Activated charcoal, on the contrary, removes colour.":"顏色不具揮發性，所以無法通過任何蒸餾，即使在真空下也一樣。活性碳則相反，會去除顏色。","Why is very strong alcohol often diluted with water for maceration?":"為什麼浸漬時常把濃度很高的酒精加水稀釋？","Too-strong alcohol would extract unpleasant flavours":"濃度太高的酒精會萃取出不好的風味","To stop the botanical floating on the surface throughout the maceration":"防止植物性原料在整個浸漬過程中浮在表面","To reach selling strength straight away":"立刻達到販售濃度","Because the law forbids neutral spirit":"因為法律禁止使用中性烈酒","With alcohol that is too high, unwanted flavours are extracted too.":"酒精濃度太高時，不想要的風味也會被萃取出來。","Highly rectified alcohol is diluted so that only good flavours are extracted. Selling strength is set later, at finishing. Neutral spirit is in fact a common base for macerations and redistillations.":"高度精餾的酒精要經過稀釋，才能只萃取好的風味。販售濃度是之後在收尾階段才決定的。中性烈酒其實是浸漬和再蒸餾常用的基酒。","A producer wants to capture the fresh aroma of cucumber. Which equipment suits best?":"一位生產者想捕捉小黃瓜的清新香氣。哪一種設備最適合？","A vacuum still":"真空蒸餾器","A direct-fired still, like those used for Cognac":"直火蒸餾器，像 Cognac 使用的那種","An activated charcoal filter":"活性碳過濾器","Under vacuum, liquids boil at lower temperatures and delicate aromas are not damaged.":"在真空下，液體在較低的溫度沸騰，細緻的香氣不會受損。","The high temperatures of a normal still, especially a direct-fired one, damage fragile aromas like cucumber. Oak would add its own flavours, and activated charcoal would remove the very congeners being sought.":"一般蒸餾器的高溫，尤其是直火蒸餾器，會破壞小黃瓜這類脆弱的香氣。橡木會增添自己的風味，活性碳則會去除正想保留的同屬物。","What is the technique of blending bought-in artificial flavourings into a base spirit sometimes called?":"把外購的人工香料調入基酒的技術，有時稱為什麼？","Cold compounding means blending artificial flavours into the spirit, with no extraction or distillation.":"冷混法（cold compounding）是把人工香料調入烈酒，不經萃取或蒸餾。","Maceration and redistillation work with real botanicals or fruit. In whisky language, finishing means a final spell in barrels that held another liquid, such as wine.":"浸漬和再蒸餾使用的是真正的植物性原料或水果。在威士忌的用語中，過桶（finishing）指的是最後在裝過其他液體（例如葡萄酒）的桶中存放一段時間。","What are the two main goals of blending?":"調和的兩個主要目標是什麼？","Colour and sweetness":"顏色和甜味","Higher strength and fewer congeners in the end product":"讓最終產品濃度更高、同屬物更少","Speed and saving money":"速度和省錢","Blending gives the same product every time and builds complexity.":"調和讓產品每次都相同，並增加複雜度。","Colour and sweetness are adjusted in finishing; they are not the purpose of blending. Strength and congeners depend mainly on distillation. Blending in fact demands a wide choice and great care.":"顏色和甜味在收尾階段調整，不是調和的目的。濃度和同屬物主要取決於蒸餾。調和其實需要廣泛的選擇和極大的細心。","Why is blending for consistency especially important for oak-matured spirits?":"為什麼以一致性為目的的調和，對橡木桶熟成的烈酒特別重要？","Each barrel can give a very different result":"每個桶的結果可能非常不同","Barrels add varying amounts of sugar":"桶會增添不等量的糖","Wood turns the spirit into neutral spirit":"木頭把烈酒變成中性烈酒","The law requires at least a hundred barrels in every single batch":"法律規定每一批至少要用一百個桶","Differences between barrels can be considerable, and blending evens them out.":"桶與桶之間的差異可能相當大，調和能把它們拉平。","Age, previous contents and position in the warehouse make every barrel unique. Wood adds no sugar and does not make spirit neutral; it adds flavour. There is no legal minimum number of barrels.":"年數、先前裝過的東西和在酒庫中的位置，讓每個桶都獨一無二。木頭不會增添糖分，也不會讓烈酒變中性；它增添的是風味。法律沒有規定最少的桶數。","A blender adds a little very old spirit to a young one. What is the aim?":"一位調和師在年輕的烈酒中加入少量極老的烈酒。目的是什麼？","To create balance and complexity":"創造平衡和複雜度","To lower the young spirit's strength without using water":"不用水就降低年輕烈酒的濃度","To make it colourless":"讓它變成無色","To remove the need to filter":"省去過濾的需要","Old spirit brings depth and young spirit freshness: together they create new balance.":"老酒帶來深度，年輕的酒帶來清新：合在一起創造出新的平衡。","On its own a very old spirit can be too intense and a young one too simple. Strength is set with water during finishing; colour and filtration are separate matters.":"極老的烈酒單獨喝可能太濃郁，年輕的則太簡單。濃度是在收尾階段用水調整的；顏色和過濾是另外的事。","Why are nearly all spirits diluted with water before bottling?":"為什麼幾乎所有烈酒在裝瓶前都要加水稀釋？","To make them more enjoyable for most people":"讓大多數人更容易享用","To give them colour":"為它們增添顏色","To add oak flavours without using a barrel":"不用桶子就增添橡木風味","To stop haze forming in the cold":"防止在低溫時形成混濁","Very high alcohol is challenging: water makes it more approachable.":"非常高的酒精濃度不容易入口：水讓它更平易近人。","Completely pure water is used, adding neither colour nor flavour. Cold haze is removed by filtration. Undiluted spirits exist, but they are rare and aimed at enthusiasts.":"使用的是完全純淨的水，不增添顏色或風味。低溫造成的混濁是靠過濾去除的。未經稀釋的烈酒確實存在，但很少見，是針對愛好者的。","What is usually used to adjust the colour of an oak-matured spirit?":"通常用什麼來調整橡木桶熟成烈酒的顏色？","Activated charcoal":"活性碳","Concentrated fruit juice":"濃縮果汁","Sugar burnt directly in the still":"直接在蒸餾器中燒焦的糖","Caramel is a tasteless food-grade colouring, very effective even in small doses.":"焦糖色是沒有味道的食用色素，即使用量很少也非常有效。","It is used to keep colour the same from batch to batch. Activated charcoal does the opposite: it removes colour. Other natural or artificial colourings are used mainly for flavoured spirits and liqueurs.":"用它是為了讓每一批的顏色保持相同。活性碳的作用相反：它去除顏色。其他天然或人工色素主要用於調味烈酒和利口酒。","In which category is adding sugar a legal requirement?":"在哪一個類別中，加糖是法定要求？","All brandies, including long-aged ones":"所有白蘭地，包括長期陳年的","Malt whisky":"麥芽威士忌","In liqueurs, added sugar is required by law.":"在利口酒中，法律規定必須加糖。","Some brandies and rums may have sugar added for balance and style, but that is a choice, not a rule for all. Every spirit starts out dry; sweetness only comes from a later addition.":"有些白蘭地和蘭姆酒可能為了平衡和風格而加糖，但那是一種選擇，不是所有酒款的規定。所有烈酒一開始都是不甜的；甜味只來自之後的添加。","How does chill-filtration work?":"冷凝過濾如何運作？","The spirit is chilled, haze forms and is filtered out":"把烈酒降溫，混濁物形成後再濾除","The spirit is passed through a very fine activated charcoal filter":"讓烈酒通過非常細的活性碳濾器","The spirit is put in barrels in a cold cellar":"把烈酒裝桶，放在寒冷的酒窖裡","Ice is added to every bottle":"每一瓶都加入冰塊","The haze that cold would cause is removed before bottling.":"低溫會造成的混濁在裝瓶前就被去除。","That way the spirit stays clear even when served cold. It should not change the taste, though not everyone agrees. Activated charcoal is a different, far more drastic filtration.":"這樣烈酒即使冰飲也保持清澈。它應該不會改變味道，不過並非人人都同意。活性碳則是另一種強烈得多的過濾。","For which spirit is activated charcoal filtration often used to remove remaining congeners?":"哪一種烈酒常用活性碳過濾來去除剩餘的同屬物？","Non-chill-filtered malt whisky":"非冷凝過濾的麥芽威士忌","Very old Cognac":"極老的 Cognac","Activated charcoal strips the last congeners from neutral spirit: typical of vodka.":"活性碳去除中性烈酒中最後的同屬物：這是伏特加的典型做法。","It is also used for some white rums, since it removes colour too. Whisky, Cognac and Bourbon rely instead on the character and colour from oak, so removing them would defeat the purpose.":"它也用於某些白蘭姆酒，因為它同時會去除顏色。威士忌、Cognac 和 Bourbon 則仰賴橡木帶來的特色和顏色，去除它們就失去意義了。","A label says 'non-chill-filtered'. What does it tell the buyer?":"酒標上寫著「non-chill-filtered」。這告訴買家什麼？","The spirit has not been chill-filtered":"這款烈酒沒有經過冷凝過濾","The spirit must only be served at room temperature":"這款烈酒只能在室溫下飲用","The spirit has never been in a barrel":"這款烈酒從未入過桶","The spirit contains caramel added to even out batch colour":"這款烈酒添加了焦糖色，讓各批顏色一致","The producer signals that chill-filtration was skipped to preserve character.":"生產者表示略過了冷凝過濾，以保留特色。","Some producers believe even the most careful filtration takes something away, and they advertise skipping it. The term says nothing about serving temperature, ageing or colouring; in the cold, though, the spirit may turn hazy.":"有些生產者認為，即使最謹慎的過濾也會帶走一些東西，所以會標榜不做過濾。這個術語與飲用溫度、陳年或調色無關；不過在低溫下烈酒可能變混濁。","What is the main aim of post-distillation operations?":"蒸餾後處理的主要目的是什麼？","To give the spirit the right colour, aroma, sweetness and strength":"讓烈酒有合適的顏色、香氣、甜度和濃度","To raise the strength above 96%":"把濃度提高到 96% 以上","To turn starch into sugar":"把澱粉變成糖","To separate heads and tails from the heart, still mixed until now":"把到目前為止仍混在一起的酒頭和酒尾與酒心分開","After distillation the spirit is adjusted so it reaches the shelf with the intended colour, aroma, sweetness and strength.":"蒸餾之後要調整烈酒，讓它上架時具有預期的顏色、香氣、甜度和濃度。","Heads and tails are separated during distillation, not afterwards. Converting starch belongs to the raw-material stage. No later step raises strength above 96%; usually water is added instead.":"酒頭和酒尾是在蒸餾時分離的，不是之後。轉化澱粉屬於原料階段。之後沒有任何步驟會把濃度提高到 96% 以上；通常反而是加水。","What are a barrel's staves?":"桶的桶板是什麼？","Strips of wood bent into shape and held by metal hoops":"彎曲成形、用金屬箍固定的木條","The layer of carbon inside the barrel":"桶內的碳層","The metal hoops that close the barrel":"封住桶子的金屬箍","The glass vessels used to keep the oldest spirits":"用來存放最老烈酒的玻璃容器","A barrel is built from staves: wooden strips bent into shape and held together by metal hoops.":"桶子由桶板組成：彎曲成形並用金屬箍固定在一起的木條。","The inner carbon layer is called char or toast. The hoops hold the staves but are not the staves. Glass vessels for very old spirits are demijohns.":"內部的碳層稱為炙燒層或烘烤層。金屬箍固定桶板，但不是桶板。存放極老烈酒的玻璃容器是玻璃罈。","Which colour sequence describes a spirit ageing for a long time in oak?":"哪一組顏色順序描述了烈酒在橡木桶中長期陳年的變化？","Colourless, lemon, gold, amber, brown":"無色、檸檬色、金黃色、琥珀色、棕色","Brown, amber, gold, lemon, colourless":"棕色、琥珀色、金黃色、檸檬色、無色","Colourless, pink, red, brown":"無色、粉紅色、紅色、棕色","It stays colourless: colour only comes from caramel":"維持無色：顏色只來自焦糖色","The colourless spirit turns lemon and then gold; long maturation takes it to amber and finally brown.":"無色的烈酒先變成檸檬色，再變成金黃色；長期熟成讓它變成琥珀色，最後是棕色。","Colour comes from the wood and then deepens with oxygen and time. Caramel only corrects it for consistency; it does not create it. Pink or red tones are not part of oak ageing.":"顏色來自木頭，再隨氧氣和時間加深。焦糖色只是為了一致性而修正顏色，並不創造顏色。粉紅或紅色調不屬於橡木桶陳年。","How does oxygen reach the spirit inside a barrel?":"氧氣如何到達桶內的烈酒？","It enters through the wood":"透過木頭進入","It is pumped in":"用幫浦打進去","It is already in the caramel":"本來就在焦糖色裡","It does not: the barrel is fully airtight, like a demijohn":"到不了：桶子像玻璃罈一樣完全密閉","Wood lets oxygen through, which reacts with the congeners and creates new aromas.":"木頭讓氧氣通過，氧氣與同屬物反應，產生新的香氣。","These reactions create rancio notes such as leather and mushroom, and darken the colour. It is precisely to stop oxidation that very old Cognacs are moved into glass demijohns.":"這些反應產生皮革和蘑菇等 rancio 氣息，並讓顏色變深。極老的 Cognac 移到玻璃罈中，正是為了停止氧化。","How much of their volume can barrels of very old spirits lose?":"裝著極老烈酒的桶可能損失多少體積？","Nothing, as wood is waterproof":"完全不會，因為木頭不透水","Exactly a quarter, set by law":"剛好四分之一，由法律規定","Through evaporation, the 'angels' share', very old barrels can lose over half their contents.":"透過蒸發，也就是「天使的分享」，極老的桶可能損失超過一半的內容物。","Losses can be very high and depend on time and conditions, not a fixed rule. Wood lets water, alcohol and oxygen through: it is not waterproof.":"損失可能非常高，取決於時間和環境，沒有固定的規則。木頭會讓水、酒精和氧氣通過：它並不是不透水的。","What effect does the angels' share have on the spirit left in the barrel?":"天使的分享對留在桶中的烈酒有什麼影響？","It concentrates the congeners: more intense, complex aromas":"濃縮同屬物：香氣更濃郁、更複雜","It makes it more neutral":"讓它更中性","It makes it sweeter because only water evaporates":"讓它更甜，因為只有水蒸發","None: volume is lost but the taste stays identical":"沒有影響：體積減少，但味道完全相同","Water and ethanol evaporate; the remaining congeners concentrate and very old spirits become extraordinarily aromatic.":"水和乙醇蒸發；留下的同屬物被濃縮，極老的烈酒因此香氣格外豐富。","The spirit does not become more neutral; quite the reverse. Alcohol evaporates as well as water, and oak adds no sugar. The volume loss is exactly what changes the flavour intensity.":"烈酒不會變得更中性；恰恰相反。酒精和水一樣會蒸發，橡木也不會增添糖分。體積的損失正是改變風味強度的原因。","When is the carbon layer (char or toast) inside a barrel created?":"桶內的碳層（炙燒層或烘烤層）是什麼時候形成的？","When the barrel is made":"製桶的時候","During distillation":"蒸餾的時候","Slowly, over years of ageing":"在多年陳年中慢慢形成","By adding activated charcoal to the spirit before filling":"裝桶前在烈酒中加入活性碳","The charred or toasted layer forms while the barrel is being made.":"炙燒或烘烤層是在製桶過程中形成的。","This carbon captures some congeners and smooths the harshness of young spirits. Activated charcoal, by contrast, is a filtration tool, used for example for vodka and white rums.":"這層碳會抓住一些同屬物，讓年輕烈酒的粗糙感變得柔順。活性碳則是一種過濾工具，例如用於伏特加和白蘭姆酒。","A barrel is being filled for the third time. What can be said?":"一個桶正要第三次裝酒。可以怎麼說？","It will give less colour and flavour, but is not necessarily worse":"它給的顏色和風味會較少，但不一定比較差","It will give more colour than a new barrel":"它給的顏色會比新桶多","It is always inferior and should be scrapped":"它一定比較差，應該報廢","It will have no effect at all, just like a steel tank":"它完全沒有作用，就像鋼槽一樣","Each reuse gives less colour and flavour; the choice depends on the style wanted.":"每次重複使用，給的顏色和風味都會減少；怎麼選擇取決於想要的風格。","A new barrel gives the most, but for some styles that would be too much. A used barrel still lets in oxygen and concentrates the spirit: it is not an inert vessel.":"新桶給得最多，但對某些風格來說那會太多。用過的桶仍然會讓氧氣進入並濃縮烈酒：它不是惰性容器。","Why must producers manage barrel quality so carefully?":"為什麼生產者必須這麼仔細地管理桶的品質？","Poor-quality wood can ruin a spirit":"品質差的木頭會毀掉烈酒","Because the law bans used barrels":"因為法律禁止使用舊桶","Because barrels set the bottling strength":"因為桶決定裝瓶濃度","Because poor barrels keep all the alcohol and give back only water":"因為劣質的桶會留住所有酒精，只還回水","The barrel provides much of an aged spirit's flavour, so faulty wood spoils it.":"桶提供了陳年烈酒的大部分風味，所以有缺陷的木頭會毀掉它。","Barrels need the same care as fermentation and distillation. Used barrels are common and legitimate, and bottling strength is set with water.":"桶需要和發酵、蒸餾同等的用心。舊桶很常見，也完全正當，而裝瓶濃度是用水調整的。","A label describes a spirit as 'unaged'. What does this suggest?":"酒標把一款烈酒描述為「unaged」（未陳年）。這代表什麼？","A short rest in inert vessels, no colour from wood":"在惰性容器中短暫靜置，沒有來自木頭的顏色","Years in new oak barrels":"在新橡木桶中存放多年","A spirit coloured with caramel":"用焦糖色上色的烈酒","A spirit bottled without any dilution or filtration":"未經任何稀釋或過濾就裝瓶的烈酒","'Unaged' spirits are usually stored briefly in steel or glass: they stay colourless and almost unchanged.":"「未陳年」的烈酒通常在鋼或玻璃容器中短暫存放：保持無色，幾乎沒有變化。","The term is about maturation, not dilution or filtration, which may still happen. Caramel is mainly used to even out the colour of oak-aged spirits.":"這個術語說的是熟成，不是稀釋或過濾，後兩者仍然可能進行。焦糖色主要用來讓橡木桶陳年烈酒的顏色一致。","Which of these is NOT an effect of long storage in glass or steel?":"下列哪一項不是在玻璃或鋼製容器中長期存放的效果？","The spirit becomes smoother":"烈酒變得更柔順","The spirit becomes more mouthfilling":"烈酒變得更飽滿","The spirit keeps slowly evolving for years":"烈酒持續緩慢變化好幾年","Inert vessels give no colour: the spirit stays colourless even after years.":"惰性容器不帶來顏色：即使過了多年，烈酒仍然無色。","After a few months the spirit grows smoother and more mouthfilling, and this can go on for years, though maturing this way is rare. Colour, however, never changes.":"幾個月後烈酒會變得更柔順、更飽滿，而且可以持續好幾年，不過這樣熟成很少見。但顏色永遠不會改變。","Why might a producer choose an inert vessel instead of oak?":"為什麼生產者可能選擇惰性容器而不是橡木桶？","To avoid changing the spirit's colour and flavour":"避免改變烈酒的顏色和風味","To darken it faster":"讓它更快變深","To concentrate it through a large angels' share in a few months":"在幾個月內透過大量的天使的分享把它濃縮","Oak changes colour and flavour a lot; it does not suit some spirits, so steel or glass is used.":"橡木會大幅改變顏色和風味；它不適合某些烈酒，所以使用鋼或玻璃。","Darkening, adding vanilla and concentrating by evaporation are all barrel effects, exactly what an inert vessel avoids. The spirit stays clear and true to its original character.":"顏色變深、增添香草和透過蒸發濃縮都是桶的效果，正是惰性容器要避免的。烈酒保持清澈，忠於原本的特色。","Why can a blender not follow a fixed recipe year after year?":"為什麼調和師不能年復一年照著固定的配方做？","Spirits change or stop being available":"烈酒會改變，或不再有貨","Because the law requires a new recipe every year":"因為法律規定每年要有新配方","Because consumers want a different taste in every batch":"因為消費者希望每一批的味道都不同","Because barrels always give the same result, so recipes are pointless":"因為桶的結果總是相同，所以配方毫無意義","Over the years components change or run out, so many options are needed to reach the same result.":"多年下來，各個成分會改變或用完，所以需要許多選項才能達到相同的結果。","The goal is consistency from batch to batch, not variety. Barrels differ a great deal, which is exactly why blending is essential.":"目標是每一批都一致，不是多樣化。桶與桶之間差異很大，這正是調和不可或缺的原因。","What does a blender need to deliver consistency and complexity?":"調和師需要什麼才能做到一致性和複雜度？","The widest possible range of different spirits":"盡可能廣泛的各種不同烈酒","A single spirit from a single barrel":"來自單一桶的單一烈酒","Only spirits of the same age":"只有同樣年數的烈酒","Only column spirits, since they are the most consistent":"只有蒸餾柱烈酒，因為它們最一致","Pot and column spirits of various ages, matured in different barrels and conditions, give the blender more routes.":"不同年數、在不同的桶和環境中熟成的壺式和柱式蒸餾烈酒，給調和師更多條路可走。","A single component cannot be blended, and sticking to one age or one still type narrows the options. The more ingredients there are, the easier it is to reproduce the same taste.":"單一成分無法調和，只用一種年數或一種蒸餾器也會限縮選項。材料越多，就越容易重現相同的味道。","Why is a very old spirit often not bottled on its own?":"為什麼極老的烈酒通常不單獨裝瓶？","It can be so intense that it lacks balance":"它可能濃郁到失去平衡","Because it has lost all its colour":"因為它已失去所有顏色","Because it has become neutral":"因為它已變成中性","Because the law forbids selling spirits over twenty years old":"因為法律禁止販售超過二十年的烈酒","On its own a very old spirit can be too intense; added in small doses to a young one it creates balance.":"極老的烈酒單獨喝可能太濃郁；少量加進年輕的烈酒則能創造平衡。","Young spirits often lack depth and very old ones balance: together they give what neither has alone. With age colour darkens and aromas concentrate rather than vanish.":"年輕的烈酒往往缺乏深度，極老的則缺乏平衡：合在一起就有了各自所沒有的東西。隨著年數增加，顏色變深，香氣濃縮，而不是消失。","How often is a spirit bottled just as it comes off the still?":"烈酒照蒸餾出來的原樣直接裝瓶的情況有多常見？","Hardly ever":"幾乎沒有","Almost always":"幾乎都是","Only for column spirits":"只有蒸餾柱烈酒","Always, as the law bans any step after distillation":"一律如此，因為法律禁止蒸餾後的任何步驟","It would be possible, but almost no one does it: distillers choose among several finishing steps.":"是可以這麼做，但幾乎沒有人這樣做：蒸餾師會在幾種收尾步驟中做選擇。","Before bottling, water is usually added and, depending on the case, colour adjusted, sugar added or the spirit filtered. Laws regulate these steps rather than banning them.":"裝瓶前通常會加水，並視情況調整顏色、加糖或過濾。法律是規範這些步驟，而不是禁止。","What kind of water is used to bring a spirit down to bottling strength?":"把烈酒降到裝瓶濃度，用的是什麼樣的水？","Completely pure water":"完全純淨的水","The still-warm condenser water":"仍溫熱的冷凝器用水","The watery residue from the pot, which keeps some aroma":"壺身裡的含水殘液，它保有一些香氣","Dilution uses completely pure water, so the spirit is not altered.":"稀釋使用完全純淨的水，所以烈酒不會被改變。","The pot residue is waste and is discarded. Cooling water is only for the condenser. Any impurity in the water would end up in the glass.":"壺身的殘液是廢液，會被丟棄。冷卻水只供冷凝器使用。水中的任何雜質最後都會進到杯子裡。","In most cases, what is a spirit's legal minimum bottling strength?":"在大多數情況下，烈酒的法定最低裝瓶濃度是多少？","40% abv in the USA, 37.5% abv in the EU":"美國 40% abv，歐盟 37.5% abv","37.5% abv in the USA, 40% abv in the EU":"美國 37.5% abv，歐盟 40% abv","30% abv everywhere":"各地都是 30% abv","There is no minimum: each producer decides freely":"沒有最低限度：每位生產者自由決定","The legal minimum is usually 40% abv in the United States and 37.5% abv in the European Union.":"法定最低濃度在美國通常是 40% abv，在歐盟是 37.5% abv。","Swapping the two figures is a common mistake. Some categories have their own rules, but a legal minimum exists. Below these levels a product cannot be sold as a spirit in those markets.":"把這兩個數字對調是常見的錯誤。有些類別有自己的規定，但法定最低限度是存在的。低於這些濃度，產品在這些市場就不能以烈酒的名義販售。","An oak-aged rum is sold water-white. Which technique could explain this?":"一款橡木桶陳年的蘭姆酒以清澈如水的樣子販售。哪一種技術可以解釋這一點？","Chill-filtration":"冷凝過濾","Adding caramel":"添加焦糖色","A final few weeks in a stainless steel tank":"最後在不鏽鋼槽中存放幾週","Activated charcoal is so fine a filter that it removes congeners and colour; it is used for some white rums.":"活性碳是非常細的濾材，能去除同屬物和顏色；用於某些白蘭姆酒。","Chill-filtration only removes haze, not colour. Caramel adds colour rather than removing it. An inert vessel does not change colour: it neither adds nor removes it.":"冷凝過濾只去除混濁，不去除顏色。焦糖色是增添顏色，而不是去除。惰性容器不會改變顏色：既不增添也不去除。","How long can a maceration last, and what can speed it up?":"浸漬可以持續多久？什麼能加快它？","From a few hours to several months; heat is sometimes used":"從幾小時到幾個月；有時會加熱","Always exactly 24 hours, cold":"一律剛好 24 小時，冷浸","Several years, and only in oak barrels":"好幾年，而且只在橡木桶中","A few minutes, since longer contact would evaporate all the alcohol":"幾分鐘，因為接觸更久會讓酒精全部蒸發","A maceration can last a few hours or several months, and heat helps extract more flavour.":"浸漬可以持續幾小時或好幾個月，加熱有助於萃取更多風味。","There is no fixed length: it depends on the botanical and the style sought. Maceration usually happens in tanks, often with botanicals in bags for easy removal, not necessarily in barrels.":"沒有固定的長度：取決於植物性原料和追求的風格。浸漬通常在槽中進行，常把植物性原料裝在袋子裡以便取出，不一定在桶中。","A spirit flavoured by redistilling with botanicals is sometimes called…":"與植物性原料一起再蒸餾而調味的烈酒，有時稱為……","a distillate":"餾出液（distillate）","a tincture":"酊劑（tincture）","A spirit made by redistilling with botanicals is sometimes simply called a 'distillate'.":"與植物性原料一起再蒸餾製成的烈酒，有時就簡稱為「餾出液」（distillate）。","A tincture is instead the result of maceration. Molasses and wort are sugary starting liquids for rum and whisky, not flavoured spirits.":"酊劑（tincture）則是浸漬的成果。糖蜜和麥汁是蘭姆酒和威士忌起點的含糖液體，不是調味烈酒。","In redistillation with botanicals, how does the distiller control the flavour?":"與植物性原料一起再蒸餾時，蒸餾師如何控制風味？","By taking the heart cut while the wanted aromas come off":"在想要的香氣流出時切取酒心","By adding caramel at the end":"在最後加入焦糖色","By leaving the botanicals in a barrel for years":"把植物性原料留在桶中好幾年","By distilling everything uncut, then filtering through activated charcoal":"不做切取地全部蒸餾，再用活性碳過濾","The most volatile aromas come off first and the least volatile last; the distiller takes the heart when the right ones arrive.":"最易揮發的香氣最先流出，最不易揮發的最後；蒸餾師在合適的香氣出現時切取酒心。","It is the same principle as pot-still distillation. Caramel only gives colour, activated charcoal would strip the very aromas wanted, and leaving botanicals in a barrel is not redistillation.":"這和壺式蒸餾的原理相同。焦糖色只帶來顏色，活性碳會去除正想要的香氣，而把植物性原料留在桶中並不是再蒸餾。","A brand never handles botanicals itself but uses natural flavours. How?":"一個品牌從不自己處理植物性原料，卻使用天然香料。怎麼做到的？","It buys ready-made botanical flavourings from specialists":"向專業廠商購買現成的植物性香料","It gets them from the oak barrel":"從橡木桶取得","It creates them during fermentation":"在發酵中產生","It extracts them from caramel, which also holds natural fruit and spice flavours":"從焦糖色中萃取，它也含有天然的水果和香料風味","Some brands buy pre-prepared botanical flavourings from specialists and blend them into their spirit.":"有些品牌向專業廠商購買預先製備的植物性香料，再調入自己的烈酒。","These are natural flavours prepared elsewhere, not created in fermentation or barrel. Caramel is a tasteless colouring. When the flavour is artificial, the term is cold compounding.":"這些是在別處製備的天然香料，不是在發酵或桶中產生的。焦糖色是沒有味道的色素。如果香料是人工的，就稱為冷混法。","What is an artificial flavouring?":"什麼是人工香料？","A man-made flavour similar to those found in nature":"人造的、與自然界中的風味相似的香料","A fruit extract made by maceration":"以浸漬製成的水果萃取物","A flavour that comes from oak":"來自橡木的風味","A herbal aroma captured in a vacuum still":"用真空蒸餾器捕捉的草本香氣","An artificial flavour is man-made but imitates natural tastes; specialist producers supply it.":"人工香料是人造的，但模仿天然的味道；由專業生產商供應。","Maceration and vacuum stills work with real fruit and botanicals, so they give natural flavours. Oak is another natural source. Artificial flavours are added to the spirit by cold compounding.":"浸漬和真空蒸餾器使用真正的水果和植物性原料，所以得到的是天然風味。橡木是另一個天然來源。人工香料是以冷混法加入烈酒的。","What are 'botanicals' usually taken to mean?":"「植物性原料」（botanicals）通常指什麼？","The herbs and spices used by distillers":"蒸餾師使用的香草和香料","Only juniper berries":"只有杜松子","Artificial colourings in liqueurs":"利口酒中的人工色素","The grains and fruit used as raw materials to ferment":"用來發酵的穀物和水果原料","There is no universal definition, but the term normally covers the many herbs and spices used for flavouring.":"沒有通用的定義，但這個術語通常涵蓋用來調味的各種香草和香料。","Juniper is an important botanical, but not the only one. Grains and fruit for fermenting are raw materials, not flavouring botanicals. Colourings give no flavour.":"杜松子是重要的植物性原料，但不是唯一的。用來發酵的穀物和水果是原料，不是調味用的植物性原料。色素不帶來風味。","Which of these is NOT one of the four groups of post-distillation operations?":"下列哪一項不屬於蒸餾後處理的四組操作？","Adding other flavours, for example with botanicals":"添加其他風味，例如使用植物性原料","Malting prepares the raw material, before fermentation even starts.":"製麥是在處理原料，發酵都還沒開始。","The four groups are maturation, adding other flavours, blending and finishing, usually in that order. Not every spirit goes through all of them.":"四組是熟成、添加其他風味、調和和收尾處理，通常依這個順序。並非每種烈酒都經過全部四組。","Does every spirit go through all the post-distillation operations?":"每種烈酒都經過所有的蒸餾後處理嗎？","No: it depends on the law and the distiller's choices":"不：取決於法規和蒸餾師的選擇","Yes, otherwise it cannot be bottled":"是的，否則無法裝瓶","No: only oak-aged spirits receive any treatment":"不：只有橡木桶陳年的烈酒才會經過處理","What happens after distillation depends both on the rules for the type of spirit and on the producer's choices.":"蒸餾之後做什麼，既取決於該類烈酒的規定，也取決於生產者的選擇。","An unaged spirit skips oak maturation, and adding flavours mainly concerns flavoured spirits and liqueurs. Unaged spirits are often diluted and filtered too.":"未陳年的烈酒略過橡木桶熟成，添加風味則主要與調味烈酒和利口酒有關。未陳年的烈酒也常經過稀釋和過濾。","Which products is adding other flavours mainly limited to?":"添加其他風味主要限於哪些產品？","Cognac and Armagnac":"Cognac 和 Armagnac","Scotch malt whiskies":"Scotch 麥芽威士忌","All spirits aged over ten years":"所有陳年超過十年的烈酒","Adding flavours is typical of flavoured spirits, such as gin and flavoured vodka, and of liqueurs.":"添加風味是調味烈酒（例如琴酒和調味伏特加）以及利口酒的典型做法。","Brandies and whiskies get their character from raw material, distillation and barrel. Age is irrelevant: an old spirit does not get added flavours just because it is old.":"白蘭地和威士忌的特色來自原料、蒸餾和桶。年數無關緊要：老酒不會只因為老就添加風味。","Which of these is NOT an effect of an oak barrel on a spirit?":"下列哪一項不是橡木桶對烈酒的作用？","Making the spirit sweet":"讓烈酒變甜","Adding colour and congeners":"增添顏色和同屬物","Concentrating the spirit by evaporation":"透過蒸發濃縮烈酒","Removing harshness through the charred inner layer":"透過炙燒過的內層去除粗糙感","The barrel gives colour, flavour, oxidation, concentration and smoothness, but not sugar.":"桶帶來顏色、風味、氧化、濃縮和柔順感，但不帶來糖。","Sweetness, if any, is a finishing choice using added sugar. Vanilla and coconut notes can smell sweet, but the spirit stays dry.":"如果有甜味，那是收尾階段用加糖做出的選擇。香草和椰子氣息聞起來可能很甜美，但烈酒仍然是不甜的。","Which of these aromas comes from oxidation over time rather than directly from the wood?":"下列哪一種香氣來自隨時間的氧化，而不是直接來自木頭？","Coconut":"椰子","Clove":"丁香","Notes such as mushroom and leather (rancio) come from congeners reacting with oxygen during long maturation.":"蘑菇和皮革等氣息（rancio）來自長期熟成中同屬物與氧氣的反應。","Vanilla, coconut, cinnamon and clove are instead among the commonest aromas given directly by oak, even over fairly short periods.":"香草、椰子、肉桂和丁香則是橡木直接賦予的最常見香氣，即使時間相當短也會有。","A flavoured spirit is made with a single technique, for example one maceration. What usually happens next?":"一款調味烈酒只用單一技術製成，例如一次浸漬。接下來通常怎麼做？","Usually no blending is needed: it is prepared for sale":"通常不需要調和：直接做上市準備","By law it must be aged in oak":"依法必須在橡木桶中陳年","It must always be redistilled twice":"一定要再蒸餾兩次","It must always be blended with spirits made by other techniques":"一定要與用其他技術製成的烈酒調和","When only one technique is used, blending is usually unnecessary and the spirit is made ready for sale straight away.":"只用一種技術時，通常不需要調和，烈酒可以立刻做上市準備。","Other producers, by contrast, make several flavoured spirits by different techniques and then blend them. No general rule imposes oak or double redistillation.":"其他生產者則會用不同技術製作幾種調味烈酒，再加以調和。沒有任何通則強制要求橡木桶或二次再蒸餾。","In redistillation for flavouring, what usually goes into the pot still?":"為了調味而再蒸餾時，壺式蒸餾器裡通常裝什麼？","Diluted neutral spirit with fruit and botanicals":"稀釋過的中性烈酒，加上水果和植物性原料","10% fermented liquid and yeast":"10% 的發酵液和酵母","Low wines, heads and tails":"低度酒、酒頭和酒尾","Caramel and artificial flavourings bought from specialists":"焦糖色和向專業廠商購買的人工香料","Typically diluted neutral spirit is redistilled with fruit and botanicals, sometimes after a short maceration.":"通常是把稀釋過的中性烈酒與水果和植物性原料一起再蒸餾，有時先短暫浸漬。","Fermented liquid, low wines, heads and tails belong to making a base spirit. Caramel and artificial flavourings are added cold, without distilling.":"發酵液、低度酒、酒頭和酒尾屬於基酒的製作。焦糖色和人工香料是冷加的，不經蒸餾。","Why are botanicals often put in bags during maceration?":"為什麼浸漬時常把植物性原料裝在袋子裡？","To make them easier to remove afterwards":"方便之後取出","To stop them giving off colour":"防止它們釋出顏色","To isolate one precise aroma":"分離出某一種特定的香氣","To protect them from heat, which is never used in maceration":"保護它們不受熱，浸漬從不加熱","The bags make it easy to lift the botanicals out of the alcohol at the end of maceration.":"袋子讓人在浸漬結束時能輕鬆把植物性原料從酒精中取出。","Maceration extracts colour and a broad range of flavours but cannot isolate a single aroma. Heat is in fact sometimes used to extract more.":"浸漬會萃取顏色和範圍廣泛的風味，但無法分離出單一香氣。事實上有時會加熱來萃取更多。","Which flavouring technique can NOT isolate particular aromas?":"哪一種調味技術無法分離出特定的香氣？","Redistillation in a pot still":"在壺式蒸餾器中再蒸餾","Redistillation in a vacuum still":"在真空蒸餾器中再蒸餾","Redistillation with a very narrow heart cut":"以非常窄的酒心切取再蒸餾","Maceration extracts everything together, colour and many flavours, but cannot select among them.":"浸漬會把所有東西一起萃取出來，包括顏色和許多風味，但無法從中挑選。","With redistillation, aromas come off in order of volatility and the distiller chooses which to keep with the cuts. A vacuum still works at lower temperatures and protects delicate aromas.":"再蒸餾時，香氣依揮發性的順序流出，蒸餾師用切取來選擇保留哪些。真空蒸餾器在較低的溫度下運作，能保護細緻的香氣。","In what form do natural flavours added to spirits usually come?":"添加到烈酒中的天然風味通常以什麼形式出現？","Fruit or botanicals":"水果或植物性原料","Approved chemical dyes":"核准使用的化學染料","Lab-made flavours that imitate those found in nature":"實驗室製造、模仿自然界風味的香料","Natural flavours mostly come from fruit or botanicals, meaning herbs and spices.":"天然風味大多來自水果或植物性原料，也就是香草和香料。","Man-made flavours imitating nature are by definition artificial. Colourings and caramel give colour, not flavour.":"模仿自然的人造風味，依定義就是人工的。色素和焦糖色帶來的是顏色，不是風味。","What is 'finishing' among the post-distillation operations?":"在蒸餾後處理中，「收尾處理」（finishing）是什麼？","The final preparation of the spirit for bottling":"裝瓶前對烈酒做的最後準備","The last tails cut in the still":"在蒸餾器中最後一次切取酒尾","A compulsory spell in ex-wine barrels for every spirit":"每種烈酒都必須在葡萄酒桶中存放一段時間","The end of fermentation, when the yeast have used all the sugar":"發酵結束，酵母用完所有的糖","Finishing covers the last adjustments before bottling: water, colour, sugar, filtration.":"收尾處理包括裝瓶前的最後調整：水、顏色、糖、過濾。","Do not confuse it with the ex-wine cask 'finishes' of some whiskies, which are a maturation technique, not an obligation. Cuts belong to distillation and the end of the sugars to fermentation.":"不要把它和某些威士忌的葡萄酒桶「過桶」（finish）混淆，那是一種熟成技術，不是義務。切取屬於蒸餾，糖用完則屬於發酵。","What kind of grape do distillers usually prefer for grape brandy?":"製作葡萄白蘭地時，蒸餾師通常偏好哪一種葡萄？","Acidic white grapes with little aroma":"酸度高、香氣少的白葡萄","Black grapes rich in tannin and deep colour":"單寧豐富、顏色深的紅葡萄","Very ripe white grapes with low acidity":"非常成熟、酸度低的白葡萄","Dried grapes with highly concentrated sugar":"糖分高度濃縮的風乾葡萄","Acidic, neutral white grapes make plain wine, but distillation concentrates their delicate notes.":"酸度高、中性的白葡萄釀出的酒平淡無奇，但蒸餾會濃縮它們細緻的氣息。","The base wine does not need to be pleasant to drink: what matters is that distillation lifts its delicate floral and fruity aromas. Acidity also helps keep the wine fresh until it is distilled. Tannic black grapes, low-acid grapes or dried grapes do not meet these needs.":"基酒不需要好喝：重要的是蒸餾能突顯它細緻的花香和果香。酸度也有助於讓葡萄酒在蒸餾前保持新鮮。單寧重的紅葡萄、低酸的葡萄或風乾葡萄都不符合這些需求。","Why do fruit distilleries work with locally grown fruit?":"為什麼水果蒸餾廠使用當地種植的水果？","Fruit spoils quickly and develops off-aromas":"水果很快就會腐壞，並產生異味","The law everywhere bans moving fresh fruit":"各地法律都禁止運送新鮮水果","Distant fruit holds too much sugar for the yeast to handle":"遠地的水果含糖太多，酵母處理不了","Fruit has to be distilled whole, without pressing":"水果必須整顆蒸餾，不經壓榨","After picking, fruit deteriorates fast, so it must be processed straight away.":"水果採收後很快就變質，所以必須立刻加工。","The off-aromas that develop in spoiling fruit would carry through into the spirit. There is no general ban on transport, and fruit is normally crushed and pressed before fermentation rather than distilled whole.":"水果腐壞時產生的異味會一路帶進烈酒。沒有禁止運送的通則，而且水果通常先壓碎、壓榨再發酵，而不是整顆蒸餾。","Why must wine made for distillation be distilled within a few months?":"為什麼用來蒸餾的葡萄酒必須在幾個月內蒸餾？","Acidity and alcohol protect it only for a limited time":"酸度和酒精只能在有限的時間內保護它","Because the yeast starts producing sugar again":"因為酵母會重新開始製造糖","Because the wine becomes too strong for traditional stills to handle":"因為葡萄酒會變得太烈，傳統蒸餾器處理不了","Because the law requires distilling it before harvest":"因為法律規定要在採收前蒸餾","The protection from acidity and alcohol is not absolute, so the wine does not keep for long.":"酸度和酒精提供的保護並不是絕對的，所以葡萄酒無法久放。","Grapes are harvested once a year, so the wine has to wait before distillation. Acidity and alcohol keep it fresh, but only for a few months. Yeast does not produce sugar, it consumes it, and wine does not get stronger by sitting in a tank.":"葡萄一年採收一次，所以葡萄酒必須等待蒸餾。酸度和酒精讓它保持新鮮，但只有幾個月。酵母不會製造糖，而是消耗糖；葡萄酒放在槽裡也不會變得更烈。","What is pomace?":"什麼是果渣（pomace）？","The grape skins left over from winemaking":"釀酒後剩下的葡萄皮","The yeast sediment at the bottom of wine tanks":"酒槽底部的酵母沉澱物","The juice that runs from grapes before pressing":"葡萄壓榨前流出的汁液","The heads and tails discarded while distilling grape wine":"蒸餾葡萄酒時丟棄的酒頭和酒尾","Pomace is the mass of skins winemakers discard, which can be turned into a spirit.":"果渣是釀酒師丟棄的一堆葡萄皮，可以製成烈酒。","Pomace is used for spirits such as grappa. Yeast sediment, free-run juice and heads and tails are all different things: none of them is the mass of skins left after pressing.":"果渣用來製作 grappa 這類烈酒。酵母沉澱物、自流汁以及酒頭和酒尾都是不同的東西：沒有一樣是壓榨後剩下的那堆葡萄皮。","How is a fermentable liquid obtained from white grape pomace?":"如何從白葡萄果渣得到可發酵的液體？","They are mixed with water and the liquid is fermented":"與水混合，再讓液體發酵","They are distilled at once, as they are already soaked in alcohol":"立刻蒸餾，因為它們已經浸滿酒精","They are steeped in neutral spirit and then redistilled":"浸泡在中性烈酒中，再重新蒸餾","They are sun-dried and then cane sugar is added":"曬乾後再加入蔗糖","White skins, removed before fermentation, still hold juice: adding water gives a liquid to ferment.":"白葡萄的皮在發酵前就被移除，仍含有葡萄汁：加水就能得到可發酵的液體。","In white winemaking the skins are removed before fermentation, so they hold no alcohol, just some juice. It is black grape pomace that arrives already alcoholic, because it ferments with the juice. Steeping in neutral spirit is used for some low-juice fruits, not for pomace.":"釀造白酒時，皮在發酵前就被移除，所以不含酒精，只有一些葡萄汁。紅葡萄果渣才是送來時就含有酒精，因為它與葡萄汁一起發酵。浸泡在中性烈酒中的做法用於某些出汁少的水果，不是果渣。","A distillery receives black grape pomace from a red wine cellar. What can it do?":"一家蒸餾廠從紅酒酒窖收到紅葡萄果渣。它可以怎麼做？","Distil it straight away, as it already contains alcohol":"立刻蒸餾，因為果渣已含有酒精","Add water and yeast, then wait several weeks before distilling":"加水和酵母，等幾週後再蒸餾","Press it to obtain sweet, unfermented juice":"壓榨以取得未發酵的甜汁","Store it in oak for a year before distilling":"在橡木桶中存放一年後再蒸餾","Black skins ferment with the juice, so they arrive soaked in wine and can be distilled at once.":"紅葡萄的皮與葡萄汁一起發酵，所以送來時浸滿了葡萄酒，可以立刻蒸餾。","In red winemaking the skins stay with the juice throughout fermentation to give colour; after draining and pressing, some wine is still left in them. Adding water and yeast is the method for white pomace, and there is no sweet juice left because the sugar has already fermented.":"釀造紅酒時，皮在整個發酵過程中都與葡萄汁在一起，以帶來顏色；排汁和壓榨後，皮裡仍留有一些葡萄酒。加水和酵母是白葡萄果渣的做法，而且已經沒有甜汁了，因為糖已經發酵完。","Two spirits are made from one batch of grapes: one from the wine, one from the pomace. What sets the pomace spirit apart?":"用同一批葡萄製作兩款烈酒：一款用葡萄酒，一款用果渣。果渣烈酒有什麼不同？","Herbaceous and spicy notes":"草本和香料氣息","An identical taste but a darker colour from the skins":"味道完全相同，但因為果皮而顏色較深","Vanilla and coconut aromas even without wood":"即使沒有木頭也有香草和椰子香氣","A much higher natural sweetness":"天然甜度高得多","The skins give pomace spirits their typical herbaceous, spicy character.":"葡萄皮賦予果渣烈酒典型的草本、香料特色。","The two spirits would taste very different, not just look different; in fact, freshly distilled spirits are colourless. Vanilla and coconut are typical oak aromas, and no spirit contains sugar as it leaves the still.":"兩款烈酒的味道會非常不同，不只是外觀不同；事實上剛蒸餾出來的烈酒都是無色的。香草和椰子是典型的橡木香氣，而任何烈酒離開蒸餾器時都不含糖。","Why are some fruits steeped in neutral spirit and redistilled instead of being fermented?":"為什麼有些水果是浸泡在中性烈酒中再蒸餾，而不是發酵？","They give little juice, or fermentation aromas are to be avoided":"它們出汁少，或是想避免發酵的香氣","They contain too much acid for yeast to survive":"它們含酸太多，酵母無法存活","So the spirit can age faster in oak":"這樣烈酒在橡木桶中能更快陳年","European law bans fermenting any fruit other than grapes":"歐洲法律禁止發酵葡萄以外的任何水果","Maceration is used when juice is scarce or when a profile free of fermentation aromas is wanted.":"出汁少，或想要沒有發酵香氣的風味輪廓時，就使用浸漬。","Some fruits are hard to press for enough juice to ferment; in other cases the distiller wants a purer profile. These spirits can be thought of as high-quality flavoured vodkas. Apples, pears, plums and cherries are fermented all the time, so no such ban exists.":"有些水果很難壓榨出足夠發酵的汁；另一些情況則是蒸餾師想要更純淨的輪廓。這些烈酒可以看成高品質的調味伏特加。蘋果、梨、李子和櫻桃一直都在發酵，所以沒有這種禁令。","Which type of still makes most high-quality fruit spirits?":"大多數高品質水果烈酒用哪一種蒸餾器製作？","Multi-plate column still":"多層蒸餾板的柱式蒸餾器","No still at all: maceration only":"完全不用蒸餾器：只做浸漬","Glass vacuum still":"玻璃真空蒸餾器","Many still types are used worldwide, but most top fruit spirits come from pot stills.":"世界各地使用許多種蒸餾器，但大多數頂級水果烈酒來自壺式蒸餾器。","A pot still keeps plenty of fruit aroma. A column taken up to neutral spirit would strip out exactly the character being sought. There are notable exceptions, such as Armagnac's short column, but those columns are designed to keep character.":"壺式蒸餾器能保留豐富的水果香氣。蒸餾到中性烈酒的蒸餾柱，會去除的正是所追求的特色。也有值得注意的例外，例如 Armagnac 的矮蒸餾柱，但那些蒸餾柱是為了保留特色而設計的。","Many top producers age young brandy for a year or two in new barrels, then in older ones. Why?":"許多頂尖生產者把年輕的白蘭地先放在新桶中一、兩年，再放進較舊的桶。為什麼？","For clear oak character that does not swamp fruit and flowers":"得到清晰的橡木特色，又不蓋過果香和花香","To remove all the colour picked up in the new barrels entirely":"完全去除在新桶中得到的顏色","Because old barrels add sugar to the spirit":"因為舊桶會為烈酒增添糖分","To raise the alcoholic strength before bottling":"在裝瓶前提高酒精濃度","New oak gives a clear imprint, then older barrels let the spirit develop without piling on more wood.":"新橡木桶留下清晰的印記，接著較舊的桶讓烈酒繼續發展，而不再堆疊更多木質味。","The goal is balance between wood and fruit. Older barrels do not remove colour; they simply give less flavour. Barrels do not add sugar, and with evaporation over time the strength tends to fall rather than rise.":"目標是木頭和果香之間的平衡。較舊的桶不會去除顏色，只是給的風味較少。桶不會增添糖分，而且隨著時間蒸發，濃度往往是下降而不是上升。","Where is the Cognac production area?":"Cognac 的產區在哪裡？","Just north of Bordeaux":"就在波爾多北邊","South of Bordeaux":"波爾多以南","In Normandy, in northern France":"法國北部的諾曼第","In the Rhône Valley":"隆河谷","Cognac comes from a delimited area just north of Bordeaux in south-west France.":"Cognac 來自法國西南部、就在波爾多北邊的一個劃定產區。","South of Bordeaux is Armagnac country, and Normandy is the home of Calvados. A handy memory trick: Cognac above Bordeaux, Armagnac below.":"波爾多以南是 Armagnac 的地盤，諾曼第則是 Calvados 的故鄉。一個好記的口訣：Cognac 在波爾多上面，Armagnac 在下面。","Which grape variety supplies the vast majority of grapes for Cognac?":"哪一個葡萄品種供應了 Cognac 絕大部分的葡萄？","Ugni Blanc dominates Cognac: neutral wine, but a spirit with a signature aroma.":"白玉霓在 Cognac 占主導地位：葡萄酒中性，烈酒卻有招牌香氣。","Muscat is an aromatic grape linked to pisco and some grappas. Baco matters in Armagnac, where it brings prune notes. Chardonnay plays no part in these spirits.":"蜜思嘉是芳香型葡萄，與 pisco 和某些 grappa 有關。巴科在 Armagnac 很重要，帶來李子乾氣息。夏多內在這些烈酒中沒有角色。","Which signature aromas does Ugni Blanc give once distilled?":"白玉霓蒸餾後帶來哪些招牌香氣？","Raisin and violet":"葡萄乾和紫羅蘭","Prune and tobacco":"李子乾和菸草","Baked apple and caramel":"烤蘋果和焦糖","Herbaceous, spicy notes from the skins":"來自果皮的草本、香料氣息","Although it makes low-aroma wine, Ugni Blanc gives spirits with raisin and violet notes.":"白玉霓釀出的葡萄酒雖然香氣少，卻能做出帶葡萄乾和紫羅蘭氣息的烈酒。","Prune is the hallmark of Baco in Armagnac, apple points to Calvados, and herbaceous, spicy notes mark pomace spirits. Ugni Blanc itself also changes character from one sub-region to another.":"李子乾是巴科在 Armagnac 的標誌，蘋果指向 Calvados，草本、香料氣息則是果渣烈酒的特徵。白玉霓本身也會隨子產區不同而改變特色。","By when must the distillation of a Cognac harvest be finished?":"Cognac 一個年份的蒸餾必須在什麼時候之前完成？","By the end of March the following year":"隔年三月底之前","By the end of December the same year":"同年十二月底之前","Before the next harvest, roughly one year later":"下一次採收之前，大約一年後","There is no deadline: it is distilled as needed":"沒有期限：需要時再蒸餾","The rules require distillation to finish by the end of March after the autumn harvest.":"規定要求在秋季採收後的三月底之前完成蒸餾。","The deadline also fits the fact that the wine only stays fresh for a few months. December would be too early to distil the whole crop, while waiting a full year or having no deadline would leave the wine open to spoilage.":"這個期限也符合葡萄酒只能保鮮幾個月的事實。十二月要蒸餾完全部收成太早，而等上整整一年或沒有期限，則會讓葡萄酒有變質的風險。","Which statement about Cognac stills is correct?":"關於 Cognac 的蒸餾器，下列哪一項正確？","Direct flame heat and a worm tub condenser":"直火加熱和蟲桶冷凝器","Steam heating and modern shell-and-tube condensers":"蒸汽加熱和現代的殼管式冷凝器","A single distillation in a short continuous column":"在矮的連續式蒸餾柱中蒸餾一次","Stainless steel stills heated by electric elements":"以電熱元件加熱的不鏽鋼蒸餾器","Cognac stills must be heated by direct flame and use the traditional worm tub.":"Cognac 的蒸餾器必須以直火加熱，並使用傳統的蟲桶冷凝器。","These are two features now rare elsewhere: direct flame heating (today gas) and the worm tub, a coiled copper pipe in a water tank as big as the still. Cognac requires two distillations in copper pot stills: no column, no stainless steel, no modern condenser.":"這兩項特點如今在其他地方都很少見：直火加熱（現在用瓦斯）和蟲桶冷凝器，也就是放在與蒸餾器一樣大的水槽中的盤繞銅管。Cognac 規定在銅製壺式蒸餾器中蒸餾兩次：不用蒸餾柱、不用不鏽鋼、不用現代冷凝器。","An Armagnac label shows a year, for example 1995. What does it mean?":"一瓶 Armagnac 的酒標上有一個年份，例如 1995。這是什麼意思？","All the grapes were harvested that year":"所有葡萄都在那一年採收","It is the year the producing estate was founded":"那是生產酒莊創立的年份","It is the year the blend was bottled":"那是調和酒裝瓶的年份","It shows the oldest spirit included in the blend of ages":"它表示不同年數的調和中最老的烈酒","A vintage Armagnac comes only from grapes of that harvest, with no blending of ages.":"年份 Armagnac 只來自該年採收的葡萄，沒有調和不同年數的酒。","Vintage-dated spirits are common in Armagnac and rare in Cognac. The year is not a founding date or a bottling date. For blends, age terms refer to the youngest spirit, not the oldest.":"標示年份的烈酒在 Armagnac 很常見，在 Cognac 則很少見。這個年份不是創立日期，也不是裝瓶日期。對調和酒來說，年數術語指的是最年輕的烈酒，不是最老的。","What is the minimum time any Cognac must spend in oak?":"任何 Cognac 至少必須在橡木桶中存放多久？","No minimum: there is also a clear, unaged Cognac":"沒有最低限度：也有清澈、未陳年的 Cognac","Every Cognac must spend at least two years in oak barrels.":"每款 Cognac 都必須在橡木桶中存放至少兩年。","Two years is the minimum for the youngest level, VS. There is no unaged Cognac: it is Armagnac that has Blanche, which has no Cognac equivalent. Many producers go well beyond the minimums anyway.":"兩年是最年輕的等級 VS 的最低要求。沒有未陳年的 Cognac：有 Blanche 的是 Armagnac，Cognac 沒有對應的類型。反正許多生產者都遠遠超過最低要求。","On a Cognac, what do the terms VS, VSOP or XO refer to?":"在 Cognac 上，VS、VSOP 或 XO 這些術語指的是什麼？","The age of the youngest spirit in the blend":"調和中最年輕烈酒的年數","The average age of all the spirits making up the blend":"構成調和的所有烈酒的平均年數","The age of the oldest spirit in the blend":"調和中最老烈酒的年數","The sub-region the grapes came from":"葡萄來自的子產區","Age indications guarantee the minimum age of the youngest component.":"年數標示保證的是最年輕成分的最低年數。","A blend may contain much older spirits, but the youngest one is what counts. It is not an average or a maximum. Origin is shown by names such as Grande Champagne, not by VS or XO. Outside the protected French regions these terms have no legal definition.":"調和中可能含有老得多的烈酒，但算數的是最年輕的那一款。它不是平均值，也不是最大值。產地是用 Grande Champagne 這類名稱表示的，不是 VS 或 XO。在受保護的法國產區之外，這些術語沒有法律定義。","Which Cognac sub-region is considered the best for growing grapes?":"Cognac 的哪一個子產區被認為最適合種植葡萄？","Bas Armagnac":"Bas Armagnac","Grande Champagne, near the town of Cognac, is the most highly regarded sub-region.":"靠近 Cognac 鎮的 Grande Champagne 是評價最高的子產區。","Bas Armagnac and Ténarèze are Armagnac sub-regions, not Cognac ones. Fine Champagne is not a sub-region but a blend of Grande and Petite Champagne. After Grande Champagne, the most respected areas are Petite Champagne and Borderies.":"Bas Armagnac 和 Ténarèze 是 Armagnac 的子產區，不是 Cognac 的。Fine Champagne 不是子產區，而是 Grande Champagne 和 Petite Champagne 的調和。在 Grande Champagne 之後，最受推崇的是 Petite Champagne 和 Borderies。","What does Fine Champagne on a Cognac label mean?":"Cognac 酒標上的 Fine Champagne 是什麼意思？","A blend of Grande (min. 50%) and Petite Champagne":"Grande Champagne（至少 50%）和 Petite Champagne 的調和","A Cognac finished in casks that once held sparkling wine":"在裝過氣泡酒的桶中過桶的 Cognac","A Cognac made 100% from Petite Champagne grapes only":"100% 只用 Petite Champagne 葡萄製成的 Cognac","An age indication above XO":"高於 XO 的年數標示","Fine Champagne combines spirits from Grande Champagne, at least half, and Petite Champagne.":"Fine Champagne 結合了 Grande Champagne（至少一半）和 Petite Champagne 的烈酒。","Here Champagne names Cognac sub-regions, not sparkling wine. A Cognac made only from Petite Champagne grapes would carry that sub-region's name. Fine Champagne is about origin, not age.":"這裡的 Champagne 是 Cognac 子產區的名稱，不是氣泡酒。只用 Petite Champagne 葡萄製成的 Cognac 會標示該子產區的名稱。Fine Champagne 說的是產地，不是年數。","Which are the two important Armagnac sub-regions?":"Armagnac 的兩個重要子產區是哪兩個？","Bas Armagnac and Ténarèze":"Bas Armagnac 和 Ténarèze","Grande Champagne and Petite Champagne":"Grande Champagne 和 Petite Champagne","Borderies and Fine Champagne":"Borderies 和 Fine Champagne","Normandy and Lower Normandy":"諾曼第和下諾曼第","Bas Armagnac and Ténarèze are the two sub-region names to know in Armagnac.":"Bas Armagnac 和 Ténarèze 是 Armagnac 必須知道的兩個子產區名稱。","Grande Champagne, Petite Champagne and Borderies belong to Cognac, and Fine Champagne is a blend, not a sub-region. Normandy is Calvados country.":"Grande Champagne、Petite Champagne 和 Borderies 屬於 Cognac，Fine Champagne 是調和，不是子產區。諾曼第是 Calvados 的地盤。","Why are some very old Cognacs transferred into glass demijohns?":"為什麼有些極老的 Cognac 會轉移到玻璃罈中？","To halt their evolution and use them sparingly in top blends":"停止它們的變化，並少量用於頂級調和","To darken their colour before selling them on their own":"在單獨販售前讓顏色變深","To raise their strength through water evaporation":"透過水分蒸發提高濃度","To speed up oxidation and build more rancio within a few months":"加快氧化，在幾個月內累積更多 rancio","Glass stops the effect of oak and oxygen, keeping the spirit in its ideal state.":"玻璃阻斷橡木和氧氣的作用，讓烈酒維持在理想狀態。","When the cellar master judges that cask and oxygen can no longer improve the spirit, it moves into glass, which is inert. These precious spirits are rarely sold alone: they add depth and complexity to prestige blends. Glass does not darken, concentrate or speed up oxidation.":"當酒窖總管判斷桶和氧氣已無法再讓烈酒變得更好，就把它移到惰性的玻璃中。這些珍貴的烈酒很少單獨販售：它們為頂級調和增添深度和複雜度。玻璃不會讓顏色變深、不會濃縮，也不會加快氧化。","A customer notices that a Cognac has a slightly rich, smooth texture without tasting sweet. What is a likely explanation?":"一位顧客注意到某款 Cognac 的質地略顯豐潤柔順，喝起來卻不甜。可能的解釋是什麼？","A small sugar addition, a traditional practice":"加了少量的糖，這是傳統做法","The copper still leaves sugar in the spirit":"銅製蒸餾器把糖留在烈酒中","The worm tub holds back alcohol and lets grape sugar through":"蟲桶冷凝器擋住酒精，讓葡萄的糖通過","It was distilled from dried grapes":"它是用風乾葡萄蒸餾的","Most Cognacs are lightly sweetened before bottling, making them off-dry.":"大多數 Cognac 在裝瓶前會稍微加糖，成為微甜（off-dry）。","A spirit leaving the still contains no sugar, whatever the grape or still: sugar does not distil. A small dose added afterwards gives a hint of syrupy texture without making the spirit taste sweet. In Cognac this is a long-standing practice and an integral part of production.":"離開蒸餾器的烈酒不含糖，不論用什麼葡萄或蒸餾器：糖無法蒸餾。之後加入少量的糖，會帶來一絲糖漿般的質地，卻不會讓烈酒喝起來是甜的。在 Cognac 這是由來已久的做法，也是生產中不可或缺的一部分。","At a tasting, a Cognac shows distinct fruit and oak and a slightly sharp texture. Which level is most likely?":"在一場品飲中，某款 Cognac 表現出分明的果香和橡木味，質地略顯銳利。最可能是哪個等級？","A blend enriched with demijohn-aged spirits":"加入玻璃罈陳放烈酒的調和","Relatively young VS Cognacs show clear fruit and oak and can feel a little sharp.":"相對年輕的 VS Cognac 表現出清晰的果香和橡木味，口感可能有點銳利。","With age, Cognac becomes richer and more integrated. The best XO and Hors d'âge Cognacs combine raisin, flowers, oak and rancio with a silky texture. Demijohn spirits go into prestige blends, so they would give an even more mature profile.":"隨著年數增加，Cognac 變得更豐富、更融合。最好的 XO 和 Hors d'âge Cognac 結合了葡萄乾、花香、橡木和 rancio，質地如絲。玻璃罈中的烈酒用於頂級調和，所以會帶來更成熟的輪廓。","Where is Armagnac made?":"Armagnac 在哪裡生產？","In Normandy":"在諾曼第","In Burgundy":"在勃根地","Grapes for Armagnac must come from an area south of Bordeaux.":"Armagnac 的葡萄必須來自波爾多以南的一個產區。","North of Bordeaux is Cognac, and Normandy, too cool for vines, makes Calvados from apples and pears. Burgundy is not a benchmark area for these spirits.":"波爾多以北是 Cognac；諾曼第對葡萄樹來說太涼，用蘋果和梨製作 Calvados。勃根地不是這些烈酒的代表產區。","Which grape often gives Armagnac a characteristic prune aroma?":"哪一種葡萄常讓 Armagnac 帶有典型的李子乾香氣？","Baco is responsible for the characteristic prune aroma of many Armagnacs.":"巴科是許多 Armagnac 典型李子乾香氣的來源。","Folle Blanche brings pronounced floral and fruity notes instead, and Ugni Blanc raisin and violet. Muscat is not a key Armagnac grape: it is typical of pisco and some aromatic grappas.":"白福爾帶來的是明顯的花香和果香，白玉霓則是葡萄乾和紫羅蘭。蜜思嘉不是 Armagnac 的主要品種：它是 pisco 和某些芳香型 grappa 的典型品種。","Why does column-distilled Armagnac stay full of character?":"為什麼用蒸餾柱蒸餾的 Armagnac 仍然充滿特色？","The column is short, with few plates, and distils to low strength":"蒸餾柱很矮、蒸餾板少，蒸餾到低濃度","The column has a great many plates and reaches neutral spirit":"蒸餾柱有非常多蒸餾板，達到中性烈酒","All the character comes from steeping fruit after distillation":"所有特色都來自蒸餾後浸泡水果","It is distilled three times in a column to concentrate aroma":"在蒸餾柱中蒸餾三次以濃縮香氣","A short column with few plates gives a low-strength spirit that keeps many congeners.":"蒸餾板少的矮蒸餾柱做出低濃度的烈酒，保留許多同屬物。","The higher the distillation strength, the less aroma remains, so a column taken to neutral spirit would give an almost characterless product. Armagnac's character comes from fermented fruit and distillation, not from later maceration. Extra distillations would raise strength, not character.":"蒸餾濃度越高，留下的香氣越少，所以蒸餾到中性烈酒的蒸餾柱會做出幾乎沒有特色的產品。Armagnac 的特色來自發酵的水果和蒸餾，不是之後的浸漬。多蒸餾幾次會提高濃度，而不是特色。","A bartender wants a colourless Armagnac with lively fruit for a cocktail. What fits?":"一位調酒師想為一款調酒找一瓶無色、果香鮮活的 Armagnac。哪一款合適？","A Blanche, perhaps from Folle Blanche":"Blanche，也許是白福爾做的","A vintage Armagnac from a very old year":"非常老的年份的年份 Armagnac","An XO Armagnac charcoal-filtered to strip out its colour":"用木炭過濾去除顏色的 XO Armagnac","A Ténarèze Armagnac aged in new barrels":"在新桶中陳年的 Ténarèze Armagnac","Blanche never sees oak, so it is colourless, and Folle Blanche gives it expressive fruit.":"Blanche 從不接觸橡木，所以是無色的，白福爾則賦予它奔放的果香。","Blanche is made like other Armagnacs but without oak ageing. An old vintage or an Armagnac aged in new barrels will have colour and woody notes. Filtering an XO to remove its colour would not make it a recognised style and would strip out much of its aroma.":"Blanche 的做法和其他 Armagnac 一樣，只是不經橡木桶陳年。老年份或在新桶中陳年的 Armagnac 會有顏色和木質氣息。過濾 XO 來去除顏色並不會讓它成為公認的類型，還會去除大部分香氣。","Which statement about fruit spirits in general is true?":"關於水果烈酒整體，下列哪一項正確？","Any fruit can be used to make one":"任何水果都可以用來製作","Only grapes and apples are legally allowed":"法律只允許葡萄和蘋果","They must always spend at least two years in oak barrels":"一律必須在橡木桶中存放至少兩年","They are made only in France and Italy":"只在法國和義大利生產","Any fruit can become a spirit, which is why the category is so varied and found worldwide.":"任何水果都能製成烈酒，所以這個類別非常多樣，世界各地都有。","Wherever fruit is grown, a spirit is sooner or later made from it: cherries, plums, raspberries and many more. Many fruit spirits, such as grappa, usually never see wood. France and Italy are benchmarks, but not the only homes: think of South American pisco.":"凡是種水果的地方，遲早會有人用它做烈酒：櫻桃、李子、覆盆子等等。許多水果烈酒（例如 grappa）通常從不接觸木頭。法國和義大利是標竿，但不是唯一的產地：想想南美洲的 pisco。","A distiller steeps raspberries in neutral spirit and then redistils it. How can this spirit best be viewed?":"一位蒸餾師把覆盆子浸泡在中性烈酒中，再重新蒸餾。這款烈酒最好怎麼看待？","As a high-quality flavoured vodka":"高品質的調味伏特加","As a pomace brandy":"果渣白蘭地","As a brandy, since it is made from fruit juice fermented in a tank":"白蘭地，因為它用在槽中發酵的果汁製成","As a liqueur, since it always contains added sugar":"利口酒，因為它一定含有添加的糖","With no fermentation, the fruit flavours a neutral spirit: the result is closest to a fine flavoured vodka.":"沒有發酵，水果只是為中性烈酒調味：成品最接近優質的調味伏特加。","These spirits go by many local names, but the logic is that of flavoured vodka: a neutral base plus fruit aroma. There is no wine or fermented juice, so it is not a brandy, and grape skins play no part. Nothing requires added sugar, so it is not necessarily a liqueur.":"這些烈酒在各地有許多名稱，但邏輯就是調味伏特加：中性基酒加上水果香氣。沒有葡萄酒或發酵果汁，所以不是白蘭地，葡萄皮也沒有參與。沒有規定必須加糖，所以不一定是利口酒。","Which fruits are processed much like grapes, by pressing them and fermenting the juice?":"哪些水果的處理方式和葡萄很像，都是壓榨後讓果汁發酵？","Apples and pears":"蘋果和梨","Agave and sugar cane":"龍舌蘭和甘蔗","Barley and corn":"大麥和玉米","Juniper berries and coriander seeds":"杜松子和芫荽籽","Apples and pears are crushed and pressed, and their sugary juice ferments just like grape juice.":"蘋果和梨經過壓碎和壓榨，含糖的果汁就像葡萄汁一樣發酵。","The same pattern applies to cherries, plums, strawberries and raspberries. Agave and cane are the raw materials of Tequila and rum, not fruit. Barley and corn are starchy grains, while juniper and coriander are gin botanicals.":"櫻桃、李子、草莓和覆盆子也是同樣的模式。龍舌蘭和甘蔗是 Tequila 和蘭姆酒的原料，不是水果。大麥和玉米是含澱粉的穀物，杜松子和芫荽籽則是琴酒的植物性原料。","When white grapes are made into wine for brandy, what happens to the skins and seeds?":"白葡萄釀成用來做白蘭地的葡萄酒時，皮和籽怎麼處理？","They are removed after pressing, before fermentation":"壓榨後、發酵前就移除","They ferment with the juice to give colour":"與葡萄汁一起發酵以帶來顏色","They stay in the still to add aroma during distillation":"留在蒸餾器中，在蒸餾時增添香氣","They are added back to the wine just before distilling":"在蒸餾前才重新加回葡萄酒","White grapes are crushed and pressed; skins and seeds are set aside and only the juice ferments.":"白葡萄經過壓碎和壓榨；皮和籽被擱在一旁，只有汁液發酵。","A wine brandy needs only the juice: the white skins set aside can, however, become the base of a pomace spirit. Fermenting with skins for colour is how red wine is made. Putting skins back into the wine or the still would bring herbaceous pomace notes, not those of a wine brandy.":"葡萄酒白蘭地只需要汁液：不過擱在一旁的白葡萄皮可以成為果渣烈酒的原料。帶皮發酵以取得顏色是紅酒的釀法。把皮放回葡萄酒或蒸餾器會帶來果渣的草本氣息，而不是葡萄酒白蘭地的氣息。","Why does pomace from a red wine cellar already contain alcohol?":"為什麼來自紅酒酒窖的果渣已經含有酒精？","The skins fermented with the juice and pressing never gets all the wine out":"皮與葡萄汁一起發酵，而壓榨永遠無法把葡萄酒全部榨出","Red wine producers add spirit to the skins before sending them off":"紅酒生產者在送出葡萄皮前先加了烈酒","Black grape skins naturally hold alcohol even before fermentation":"紅葡萄的皮在發酵前就天然含有酒精","Yeast keeps fermenting the dry skins for months after pressing":"壓榨後酵母還繼續讓乾的葡萄皮發酵好幾個月","In red winemaking the skins stay in the juice throughout fermentation and hold on to some wine even after pressing.":"釀造紅酒時，皮在整個發酵過程中都泡在葡萄汁裡，即使壓榨後仍留有一些葡萄酒。","After fermentation the wine is drained off and the skins are pressed, but some wine always stays trapped, which is why they can be distilled at once. No one adds spirit to the pomace, and alcohol only comes from fermenting sugar. Pressed skins do not go on fermenting for months.":"發酵後把葡萄酒排出並壓榨葡萄皮，但總有一些葡萄酒被困在裡面，所以可以立刻蒸餾。沒有人在果渣中加烈酒，酒精只來自糖的發酵。壓榨過的皮不會繼續發酵好幾個月。","Which statement about pomace is NOT correct?":"關於果渣，下列哪一項不正確？","White grape pomace is distilled at once, with no fermentation":"白葡萄果渣不經發酵就立刻蒸餾","It is the mass of skins discarded by winemakers":"它是釀酒師丟棄的一堆葡萄皮","The skins give pomace spirits their herbaceous and spicy notes":"葡萄皮賦予果渣烈酒草本和香料氣息","Black grape pomace reaches the distillery already soaked in wine":"紅葡萄果渣送到蒸餾廠時已經浸滿葡萄酒","White skins are removed before fermentation: they hold juice, not alcohol, so they must first be fermented with water.":"白葡萄的皮在發酵前就被移除：裡面有葡萄汁，沒有酒精，所以必須先加水發酵。","Distilling with no fermentation only works for black pomace, which fermented along with the red wine. The other three statements are true: pomace is the discarded skins, it brings herbaceous and spicy notes, and black pomace already contains alcohol. The trap is mixing up the two colours.":"不經發酵就蒸餾只適用於紅葡萄果渣，因為它已隨紅酒一起發酵。其他三項都正確：果渣是被丟棄的葡萄皮，它帶來草本和香料氣息，而紅葡萄果渣已含有酒精。陷阱在於把兩種顏色搞混。","Why do grape brandy producers value the same variety grown in different areas?":"為什麼葡萄白蘭地的生產者重視在不同區域種植的同一品種？","Each area gives grapes of a different quality and more blending options":"每個區域的葡萄品質不同，調和的選項也更多","The law requires at least three areas in every brandy":"法律規定每款白蘭地至少要用三個區域","Grapes from different areas ferment at different speeds, which saves time in the cellar":"不同區域的葡萄發酵速度不同，可節省酒窖的時間","Mixing areas is the only way to raise the alcohol level":"混合不同區域是提高酒精濃度的唯一方法","The same variety changes character with where it grows, and that diversity enriches the blends.":"同一品種會隨種植地點改變特色，這種多樣性讓調和更豐富。","Variety and growing site are two levers distillers use to get different spirits for blending: Cognac, with its sub-regions, is the example. No general rule sets a number of areas. Fermentation speed and alcohol level are not the reason for this choice.":"品種和種植地點是蒸餾師用來取得不同烈酒以供調和的兩種手段：有多個子產區的 Cognac 就是例子。沒有通則規定區域的數量。發酵速度和酒精濃度不是這樣選擇的原因。","Why do grape distillers have to store wine before distilling it?":"為什麼葡萄蒸餾師必須在蒸餾前先存放葡萄酒？","Grapes are picked once a year, but distilling it all takes months":"葡萄一年採收一次，但全部蒸餾完要好幾個月","Wine must age three years before it may be distilled":"葡萄酒必須陳年三年才能蒸餾","Freshly made wine is too strong to be distilled safely":"剛釀好的葡萄酒太烈，無法安全蒸餾","The yeast has to be removed by a long rest in oak casks":"必須在橡木桶中長時間靜置來去除酵母","There is only one harvest, so the wine waits its turn for a few months, protected by its acidity and alcohol.":"一年只有一次採收，所以葡萄酒要排隊等幾個月，靠它的酸度和酒精保護。","Stills cannot distil all the wine in a few days, so the wine waits. No years of ageing are needed; in fact the wine must be distilled within a few months. Wine is far weaker than a spirit, and oak is not how yeast is removed.":"蒸餾器無法在幾天內蒸餾完所有的葡萄酒，所以葡萄酒要等待。不需要陳年好幾年；事實上葡萄酒必須在幾個月內蒸餾。葡萄酒比烈酒淡得多，而橡木桶也不是去除酵母的方法。","For grape brandies, which source of blending variety is relatively uncommon?":"對葡萄白蘭地來說，哪一種調和多樣性的來源相對少見？","Using different types of still":"使用不同類型的蒸餾器","Using different grape varieties":"使用不同的葡萄品種","Using grapes grown in different areas of the same producing region":"使用同一產區內不同區域種植的葡萄","Making different choices during maturation":"在熟成時做出不同的選擇","Grape brandy makers get variety mainly from grapes, areas and maturation, rarely from different stills.":"葡萄白蘭地的生產者主要從葡萄、區域和熟成取得多樣性，很少靠不同的蒸餾器。","Unlike some other categories, such as certain rums, grape brandies rarely combine spirits from different stills. Varieties, areas and maturation choices are the classic levers, though local law may limit them. In Cognac, for example, the type of still is fixed.":"與某些其他類別（例如某些蘭姆酒）不同，葡萄白蘭地很少結合來自不同蒸餾器的烈酒。品種、區域和熟成的選擇是經典的手段，不過當地法律可能加以限制。例如在 Cognac，蒸餾器的類型是固定的。","Pot or column: what often decides which still a fruit spirit producer uses?":"壺式還是柱式：水果烈酒生產者用哪一種蒸餾器，往往由什麼決定？","Local laws":"當地法律","The colour of the harvested fruit":"採收水果的顏色","The size of the crop in that particular year":"該年收成的多寡","The yeast strain used for fermentation":"發酵所用的酵母菌株","Both still types are possible for fruit spirits, but local law often decides which one is used.":"水果烈酒兩種蒸餾器都可以用，但往往由當地法律決定用哪一種。","Cognac must use pot stills, while Armagnac almost always uses its short column: both are examples of local rules. Fruit colour, crop size and yeast affect style, but they do not decide the type of still.":"Cognac 必須用壺式蒸餾器，Armagnac 則幾乎都用它的矮蒸餾柱：兩者都是當地規定的例子。水果顏色、收成多寡和酵母會影響風格，但不決定蒸餾器的類型。","Among fruit spirits not made from grapes, which are the exception in normally being matured in oak?":"在不是用葡萄做的水果烈酒中，哪一種是通常會在橡木桶中熟成的例外？","Apple brandies":"蘋果白蘭地","Cherry spirits":"櫻桃烈酒","Central European plum spirits":"中歐的李子烈酒","Raspberry spirits made by maceration":"以浸漬製成的覆盆子烈酒","Like grape brandies, apple brandies are usually oak-matured; other fruit spirits rest in inert vessels.":"和葡萄白蘭地一樣，蘋果白蘭地通常在橡木桶中熟成；其他水果烈酒則在惰性容器中靜置。","Cherries, plums and berries give spirits prized for purity and expressiveness, which wood would mask, so they rest in steel or glass. Normandy's Calvados is the classic oak-aged apple brandy. Pomace spirits such as grappa usually skip wood too.":"櫻桃、李子和莓果做出的烈酒以純淨和表現力著稱，木頭會把這些掩蓋，所以它們在鋼或玻璃容器中靜置。諾曼第的 Calvados 是經典的橡木桶陳年蘋果白蘭地。grappa 這類果渣烈酒通常也不過木桶。","At a tasting, some people prefer not to add water to fruit spirits. Why?":"在品飲時，有些人偏好不在水果烈酒中加水。為什麼？","Water can make the aromas less clear":"水可能讓香氣變得不那麼清晰","Water instantly turns every fruit spirit cloudy":"水會立刻讓所有水果烈酒變混濁","They are already bottled at a very low strength":"它們裝瓶時的濃度本來就很低","Water wipes out every oak note and leaves only alcohol, making them impossible to judge":"水會抹去所有橡木氣息、只留下酒精，讓人無法評判","Water usually opens up aromas, but with fruit spirits it sometimes blurs them, in which case they are best tasted neat.":"水通常能讓香氣展開，但對水果烈酒有時反而讓香氣模糊，這時最好純飲品嚐。","For other spirits, diluting half and half, always in the same way, is advised so comparisons are fair. With fruit spirits some people find the aromas less clear, so they may skip this step. Cloudiness, low strength or oak notes, which many fruit spirits do not even have, are not the reason.":"對其他烈酒，建議一律以相同方式一比一稀釋，這樣比較才公平。對水果烈酒，有些人覺得香氣會變得不清晰，所以可能略過這一步。混濁、濃度低或橡木氣息（許多水果烈酒根本沒有）都不是原因。","Before distillation, what is the wine made from Ugni Blanc like?":"蒸餾前，白玉霓釀出的葡萄酒是什麼樣子？","Rather thin and not aromatic":"相當單薄，沒有什麼香氣","Deeply coloured and tannic":"顏色深、單寧重","Intensely floral, like a Muscat":"花香濃郁，像蜜思嘉","Sweet, low in acid and already high in alcohol":"甜、酸度低，而且酒精已經很高","Ugni Blanc makes plain, unaromatic wine, but once distilled it reveals raisin and violet.":"白玉霓釀出平淡、不芳香的葡萄酒，但蒸餾後會展現葡萄乾和紫羅蘭。","It is an acidic, neutral white grape, exactly the profile distillers look for. Colour and tannin belong to black grapes; intense aroma is typical of Muscat, the aromatic grape of pisco. A sweet, low-acid wine would keep poorly while waiting to be distilled.":"它是酸度高、中性的白葡萄，正是蒸餾師想要的輪廓。顏色和單寧屬於紅葡萄；濃郁的香氣是蜜思嘉的特徵，也就是 pisco 的芳香型葡萄。甜而低酸的葡萄酒在等待蒸餾時很難保存。","How many sub-regions is the Cognac area divided into?":"Cognac 產區分成幾個子產區？","Six":"六個","Ten":"十個","Cognac has six sub-regions, three of which are especially highly regarded.":"Cognac 有六個子產區，其中三個評價特別高。","Three is a trap: those are the most prized sub-regions and the ones seen most on labels, not the total. Two is the number of key Armagnac sub-regions. Ten matches no division at all.":"三個是陷阱：那是最受珍視、最常出現在酒標上的子產區，不是總數。兩個是 Armagnac 主要子產區的數目。十個則與任何劃分都不相符。","Which three Cognac sub-regions are most likely to appear on a label?":"Cognac 的哪三個子產區最可能出現在酒標上？","Grande Champagne, Petite Champagne and Borderies":"Grande Champagne、Petite Champagne 和 Borderies","Bas Armagnac, Ténarèze and Grande Champagne":"Bas Armagnac、Ténarèze 和 Grande Champagne","Fine Champagne, Napoléon and Hors d'âge":"Fine Champagne、Napoléon 和 Hors d'âge","Normandy, Borderies and Petite Champagne":"諾曼第、Borderies 和 Petite Champagne","They are the three most prized sub-regions, all around the town of Cognac.":"它們是最受珍視的三個子產區，都在 Cognac 鎮周圍。","Bas Armagnac and Ténarèze belong to Armagnac, and Normandy is the home of Calvados. Napoléon and Hors d'âge are age terms, and Fine Champagne is a blend of two sub-regions, not a sub-region itself.":"Bas Armagnac 和 Ténarèze 屬於 Armagnac，諾曼第是 Calvados 的故鄉。Napoléon 和 Hors d'âge 是年數術語，Fine Champagne 是兩個子產區的調和，本身不是子產區。","A Cognac label says Borderies. What does this mean?":"一瓶 Cognac 的酒標寫著 Borderies。這是什麼意思？","All the grapes come from the Borderies sub-region":"所有葡萄都來自 Borderies 子產區","At least half of the grapes come from Borderies":"至少一半的葡萄來自 Borderies","The Cognac was matured in a warehouse located there":"這款 Cognac 在位於那裡的酒庫中熟成","It is a blend of Borderies and Grande Champagne":"它是 Borderies 和 Grande Champagne 的調和","If a sub-region is named on the label, 100% of the grapes must come from there.":"如果酒標上標示某個子產區，葡萄必須 100% 來自那裡。","The 50% threshold applies only to Grande Champagne inside a Fine Champagne, not to single sub-regions. The name says where the grapes grew, not where the spirit matured. A blend of Borderies and Grande Champagne cannot carry either name.":"50% 的門檻只適用於 Fine Champagne 中的 Grande Champagne，不適用於單一子產區。這個名稱說的是葡萄在哪裡生長，不是烈酒在哪裡熟成。Borderies 和 Grande Champagne 的調和不能標示其中任何一個名稱。","Where are the Cognac sub-regions considered the best located?":"被認為最好的 Cognac 子產區位於哪裡？","Around the town of Cognac itself":"就在 Cognac 鎮周圍","Along the Atlantic coast, far from the town":"沿著大西洋岸，遠離該鎮","Near the Pyrenees, in the part south of Bordeaux":"靠近庇里牛斯山，在波爾多以南的部分","On the hills of Normandy":"在諾曼第的山丘上","Grande Champagne, Petite Champagne and Borderies surround the town that gives the spirit its name.":"Grande Champagne、Petite Champagne 和 Borderies 環繞著這款烈酒得名的城鎮。","The whole Cognac area lies just north of Bordeaux, with its quality heart around the town. South of Bordeaux is Armagnac country, not Cognac. Normandy, in northern France, is the land of Calvados.":"整個 Cognac 產區就在波爾多北邊，品質的核心在該鎮周圍。波爾多以南是 Armagnac 的地盤，不是 Cognac。法國北部的諾曼第則是 Calvados 的產地。","A Cognac blends 40% Grande Champagne and 60% Petite Champagne. Can it be labelled Fine Champagne?":"一款 Cognac 調和了 40% Grande Champagne 和 60% Petite Champagne。它可以標示為 Fine Champagne 嗎？","No: Grande Champagne must make up at least half":"不行：Grande Champagne 必須至少占一半","Yes: any blend of the two sub-regions qualifies":"可以：這兩個子產區的任何調和都符合資格","Yes, provided it is at least an XO with long ageing":"可以，只要至少是經過長期陳年的 XO","No: Fine Champagne must be 100% Grande Champagne":"不行：Fine Champagne 必須是 100% Grande Champagne","Fine Champagne requires Grande and Petite Champagne with at least 50% Grande Champagne, so 40% is not enough.":"Fine Champagne 要求 Grande Champagne 和 Petite Champagne，其中 Grande Champagne 至少 50%，所以 40% 不夠。","The two sub-regions are right, but the proportion is not. A 100% Grande Champagne would simply be called Grande Champagne. Age is irrelevant: Fine Champagne tells you where the grapes came from, not how long the Cognac aged.":"兩個子產區是對的，但比例不對。100% Grande Champagne 就直接稱為 Grande Champagne。年數無關緊要：Fine Champagne 告訴你葡萄來自哪裡，不是 Cognac 陳年了多久。","A Cognac blends spirits from Grande Champagne and Borderies. Which origin term can it carry?":"一款 Cognac 調和了 Grande Champagne 和 Borderies 的烈酒。它可以標示哪一個產地術語？","Just Cognac, with no sub-region name and no Fine Champagne":"只能標 Cognac，沒有子產區名稱，也不能標 Fine Champagne","Grande Champagne, since it contains some":"Grande Champagne，因為裡面含有一些","Borderies, if that sub-region dominates the blend":"Borderies，如果這個子產區在調和中占多數","A sub-region on the label needs 100% of its grapes from there, and Fine Champagne allows only Grande and Petite Champagne.":"酒標上的子產區要求葡萄 100% 來自那裡，而 Fine Champagne 只允許 Grande Champagne 和 Petite Champagne。","Borderies is highly regarded but is not part of Fine Champagne, which covers only the two Champagnes. Neither Grande Champagne nor Borderies can appear alone, because neither accounts for all the grapes. That leaves just the name Cognac.":"Borderies 評價很高，但不屬於 Fine Champagne，後者只涵蓋兩個 Champagne。Grande Champagne 和 Borderies 都不能單獨出現，因為兩者都沒有涵蓋全部的葡萄。剩下的就只有 Cognac 這個名稱。","How many times is Cognac distilled, and in what stills?":"Cognac 蒸餾幾次？用什麼蒸餾器？","Twice, in copper pot stills":"兩次，用銅製壺式蒸餾器","Once, in a short column with few plates":"一次，用蒸餾板少的矮蒸餾柱","Three times, in copper pot stills":"三次，用銅製壺式蒸餾器","Continuously, in a tall column with many plates":"連續蒸餾，用蒸餾板多的高蒸餾柱","The law requires double distillation in copper pot stills.":"法律規定在銅製壺式蒸餾器中進行二次蒸餾。","The short column with few plates belongs to Armagnac, while a tall column would make a much lighter spirit. Triple pot distillation is typical of many Irish whiskeys, not Cognac.":"蒸餾板少的矮蒸餾柱屬於 Armagnac，高蒸餾柱則會做出清淡得多的烈酒。壺式三次蒸餾是許多愛爾蘭威士忌的典型做法，不是 Cognac。","In a Cognac distillery, what is the chapiteau?":"在 Cognac 的蒸餾廠中，chapiteau 是什麼？","The olive-shaped still head":"橄欖形的蒸餾器頂部","The curved tube carrying vapours to the condenser":"把蒸氣送到冷凝器的彎管","The cold water tank holding the coil":"裝著盤管的冷水槽","The pot where the wine is heated at the start of each run":"每次蒸餾開始時加熱葡萄酒的壺身","Chapiteau is the local name for the still head, often olive-shaped in Cognac.":"chapiteau 是蒸餾器頂部在當地的名稱，在 Cognac 常呈橄欖形。","Still heads come in many shapes and sizes; in Cognac the term is chapiteau. The curved tube to the condenser is the col de cygne, and the tank with the coil is the worm tub. The pot is the vessel that holds the wine.":"蒸餾器頂部有許多形狀和大小；在 Cognac 這個術語是 chapiteau。通往冷凝器的彎管是 col de cygne，裝著盤管的水槽是蟲桶冷凝器。壺身是盛裝葡萄酒的容器。","In Cognac terms, what is the col de cygne?":"在 Cognac 的用語中，col de cygne 是什麼？","The swan neck linking the still head to the condenser":"連接蒸餾器頂部和冷凝器的天鵝頸","The olive-shaped head sitting on top of the pot":"位於壺身上方的橄欖形頂部","The copper coil sunk in the condenser's cold water":"浸在冷凝器冷水中的銅製盤管","The drain at the bottom of the pot":"壺身底部的排放口","Col de cygne means swan neck: the curving tube between the still head and the condenser.":"col de cygne 的意思是天鵝頸：蒸餾器頂部和冷凝器之間的彎管。","In Scotland the same terms can mean slightly different parts, but in Cognac the swan neck is this tube. The olive-shaped head is the chapiteau, and the coil belongs to the worm tub. The drain empties the pot at the end of a run.":"在蘇格蘭，同樣的術語可能指稍微不同的部位，但在 Cognac，天鵝頸就是這條管子。橄欖形的頂部是 chapiteau，盤管則屬於蟲桶冷凝器。排放口在蒸餾結束時排空壺身。","How does the worm tub required in Cognac work?":"Cognac 規定使用的蟲桶冷凝器如何運作？","Vapours condense in a coil sunk in a big tank of cold water":"蒸氣在浸於大型冷水槽的盤管中冷凝","Vapours rise through many plates and condense at the top of a column":"蒸氣穿過許多蒸餾板上升，並在蒸餾柱頂部冷凝","Cold water flows through many small tubes inside a narrow vessel":"冷水流經狹窄容器內的許多小管","The hot spirit is left to cool overnight in oak casks":"把熱的烈酒放在橡木桶中冷卻一整夜","A single copper coil runs through a tank as big as the still, filled with constantly renewed cold water.":"單一條銅製盤管穿過與蒸餾器一樣大的水槽，槽中裝滿不斷更新的冷水。","It is an old design, whereas almost everywhere else uses modern shell-and-tube condensers, the ones with many small tubes. Plates belong to column stills, which Cognac does not use. Wood is for maturing the spirit, not condensing it.":"這是古老的設計，而幾乎其他所有地方都使用現代的殼管式冷凝器，也就是有許多小管的那種。蒸餾板屬於柱式蒸餾器，Cognac 並不使用。木頭是用來熟成烈酒的，不是用來冷凝。","Many large Cognac houses buy spirit from independent distillers. Why?":"許多大型 Cognac 酒商向獨立蒸餾師購買烈酒。為什麼？","They cannot make all they need, so others distil it to their recipe":"他們無法自己做出所需的全部產量，所以由別人依他們的配方蒸餾","The law forbids large houses from owning stills":"法律禁止大型酒商擁有蒸餾器","Bought-in spirit is exempt from two years in oak":"買進的烈酒可免除兩年橡木桶的規定","So it can be sold as a single small producer's Cognac":"這樣就能當作單一小生產者的 Cognac 販售","Demand exceeds their capacity, so they hand part of the distilling to others who follow their recipe.":"需求超過他們的產能，所以把一部分蒸餾交給遵循其配方的其他人。","This spirit is used alongside what the house makes itself. At the other end, some small Cognac distillers grow the grapes they then ferment, distil and mature. Every Cognac, bought in or not, follows the same rules, including two years in oak.":"這些烈酒會與酒商自己做的一起使用。另一端則有一些小型 Cognac 蒸餾師自己種葡萄，再自行發酵、蒸餾和熟成。每款 Cognac，不論是否買進，都遵守相同的規定，包括兩年橡木桶。","What do the letters VSOP stand for?":"VSOP 這幾個字母代表什麼？","VSOP stands for Very Superior Old Pale; VS is Very Special and XO is Extra Old.":"VSOP 代表 Very Superior Old Pale；VS 是 Very Special，XO 是 Extra Old。","The abbreviations are in English by trading tradition, but in Cognac they have a precise legal meaning. Very Special belongs to VS, not VSOP. Vintage is unrelated: these terms give a minimum age, not a harvest year.":"這些縮寫因貿易傳統而使用英文，但在 Cognac 有明確的法律意義。Very Special 屬於 VS，不是 VSOP。Vintage（年份）與此無關：這些術語表示最低年數，不是採收年份。","On a Cognac, which terms belong to the same top age category as XO?":"在 Cognac 上，哪些術語與 XO 屬於同一個最高年數類別？","Napoléon and Hors d'âge":"Napoléon 和 Hors d'âge","VS and VSOP":"VS 和 VSOP","Fine Champagne and Borderies, shown on the same label":"標在同一張酒標上的 Fine Champagne 和 Borderies","Blanche and Vintage":"Blanche 和 Vintage","Napoléon and Hors d'âge are age terms that guarantee the same minimum as XO.":"Napoléon 和 Hors d'âge 是年數術語，保證的最低年數與 XO 相同。","VS and VSOP are younger categories. Fine Champagne and Borderies tell you where the grapes came from, not the age. Blanche and Vintage are styles typical of Armagnac, rare or absent in Cognac.":"VS 和 VSOP 是較年輕的類別。Fine Champagne 和 Borderies 告訴你葡萄來自哪裡，不是年數。Blanche 和 Vintage 是 Armagnac 的典型類型，在 Cognac 很少見或不存在。","Compared with a VS from the same producer, what does a VSOP usually show?":"與同一生產者的 VS 相比，VSOP 通常表現出什麼？","More richness and body, with some aromas of maturity":"更豐富、酒體更飽滿，帶一些成熟的香氣","A lighter, sharper texture with less oak":"質地更輕、更銳利，橡木味更少","A clear colour and pure grape aromas, with no trace of oak":"顏色清澈、葡萄香氣純淨，沒有一絲橡木味","Marked prune notes from Baco grapes":"來自巴科葡萄的明顯李子乾氣息","VSOP is richer and fuller than VS and starts to show aromas of maturity.":"VSOP 比 VS 更豐富、更飽滿，並開始出現成熟的香氣。","A slightly sharp texture is typical of young VS. Every Cognac spends at least two years in oak, so a clear, unoaked colour is impossible. Baco's prune note is an Armagnac trait.":"略顯銳利的質地是年輕 VS 的典型特徵。每款 Cognac 都在橡木桶中至少兩年，所以不可能有清澈、未過桶的顏色。巴科的李子乾氣息是 Armagnac 的特徵。","A Cognac shows seamlessly blended raisin, floral, oak and rancio notes, with a smooth mouthfeel. Which category does it best match?":"一款 Cognac 表現出融合無間的葡萄乾、花香、橡木和 rancio 氣息，口感柔順。它最符合哪個類別？","A fine XO":"優質的 XO","A typical VS":"典型的 VS","A Blanche Armagnac made only from Folle Blanche":"只用白福爾製成的 Blanche Armagnac","A young VSOP straight out of new casks":"剛從新桶取出的年輕 VSOP","Rancio and a seamless harmony of fruit, flowers and oak are the hallmark of the best XOs.":"rancio 以及果香、花香和橡木的和諧融合，是最好的 XO 的標誌。","Rancio comes from many years of contact with wood and oxygen, which a VS or young VSOP has not had. VS shows distinct fruit and oak, sometimes with a sharp texture. A Blanche never sees oak, so it can have neither oak notes nor rancio.":"rancio 來自與木頭和氧氣多年的接觸，VS 或年輕的 VSOP 沒有這樣的經歷。VS 表現出分明的果香和橡木味，有時質地銳利。Blanche 從不接觸橡木，所以既不可能有橡木氣息，也不可能有 rancio。","In a tasting note, how is the sweetness of a typical Cognac best described?":"在品飲筆記中，典型 Cognac 的甜度最好怎麼描述？","Dry, because no spirit ever receives sugar":"不甜，因為沒有任何烈酒會加糖","Medium, with an obvious sweetness":"中等，有明顯的甜味","Sweet, like a liqueur":"甜，像利口酒","Most Cognacs get a small sugar addition: they do not taste sweet, but the texture gives it away.":"大多數 Cognac 會加少量的糖：喝起來不甜，但質地洩露了這一點。","Tasting assesses sugar added after distillation, a traditional practice in Cognac. Medium and sweet describe clearly noticeable sweetness, whereas a typical Cognac does not taste sweet. Dry would only be right with no addition at all.":"品飲時評估的是蒸餾後添加的糖，這在 Cognac 是傳統做法。中等和甜描述的是清楚可察覺的甜味，而典型的 Cognac 喝起來並不甜。只有完全沒加糖時，不甜才是正確的。","Why do Cognac houses mature spirits in warehouses in different places?":"為什麼 Cognac 酒商把烈酒放在不同地點的酒庫中熟成？","Different conditions create variety for blending":"不同的環境為調和創造多樣性","The law makes each sub-region keep its spirits apart":"法律要求每個子產區的烈酒分開存放","To cut to zero the evaporation each cask loses every year":"把每個桶每年的蒸發損失降到零","Because one warehouse may hold only one age category":"因為一座酒庫只能存放一個年數類別","Temperature and conditions change from one warehouse to another, and so does maturation: more variety for the blender.":"溫度和環境因酒庫而異，熟成也跟著不同：調和師有更多樣的選擇。","In Cognac, using different warehouses has become a speciality, alongside varieties, sub-regions and ages. No law requires sub-regions or ages to be stored separately by warehouse. Evaporation, the angels' share, cannot be eliminated.":"在 Cognac，使用不同的酒庫已成為一門專長，與品種、子產區和年數並列。沒有法律規定子產區或年數必須分酒庫存放。蒸發，也就是天使的分享，是無法消除的。","Where do rancio aromas such as leather and mushroom in a very old Cognac mainly come from?":"極老的 Cognac 中，皮革和蘑菇等 rancio 香氣主要來自哪裡？","Slow reactions between spirit and oak compounds and oxygen":"烈酒與橡木化合物和氧氣之間緩慢的反應","From grape skins left to ferment with the base wine":"來自與基酒一起發酵的葡萄皮","From the copper of the worm tub coil":"來自蟲桶冷凝器盤管的銅","From the small sugar addition made just before final bottling":"來自最後裝瓶前加入的少量糖","Over time, compounds from the spirit and the oak react with each other and with oxygen entering through the wood, creating rancio.":"隨著時間，烈酒和橡木的化合物彼此反應，也與透過木頭進入的氧氣反應，產生 rancio。","That is why rancio is found in spirits aged for a long time in cask, such as fine XOs. Skins give herbaceous notes to pomace spirits, not rancio. Copper and sugar affect purity and texture; they do not create leather or mushroom.":"所以 rancio 出現在長期桶陳的烈酒中，例如優質的 XO。葡萄皮為果渣烈酒帶來草本氣息，不是 rancio。銅和糖影響的是純淨度和質地；它們不會產生皮革或蘑菇氣息。","Which comparison between Cognac and Armagnac producers is correct?":"關於 Cognac 和 Armagnac 的生產者，下列哪一項比較是正確的？","Cognac is dominated by big companies, Armagnac by small producers":"Cognac 由大公司主導，Armagnac 由小生產者主導","Both are dominated by four big companies":"兩者都由四家大公司主導","Armagnac is dominated by big companies, Cognac by small family farms":"Armagnac 由大公司主導，Cognac 由小型家庭農場主導","Both are made only by cooperatives":"兩者都只由合作社生產","Four big companies dominate Cognac, while small producers are the norm in Armagnac.":"四家大公司主導 Cognac，小生產者則是 Armagnac 的常態。","That is why Armagnac labels often say Château, marking a small producer. Cognac has small distillers too, but the market is in the hands of the big houses. Cooperatives are not the dominant model in either region.":"所以 Armagnac 的酒標上常寫著 Château，代表小生產者。Cognac 也有小型蒸餾師，但市場掌握在大酒商手中。合作社在兩個產區都不是主流模式。","Which grape variety is the most widely planted in Armagnac?":"Armagnac 種植最廣的是哪一個葡萄品種？","Ugni Blanc":"白玉霓","Folle Blanche":"白福爾","As in Cognac, the most widely planted variety is Ugni Blanc.":"和 Cognac 一樣，種植最廣的品種是白玉霓。","The difference is that Armagnac makes much more use of the other permitted varieties. Baco and Folle Blanche are the most important of these and bring typical traits, but they are not the most planted. Muscat is pisco's aromatic grape.":"差別在於 Armagnac 更常使用其他獲准的品種。巴科和白福爾是其中最重要的，帶來典型的特徵，但不是種植最多的。蜜思嘉是 pisco 的芳香型葡萄。","What type of still is most Armagnac distilled in?":"大多數 Armagnac 用哪一種蒸餾器蒸餾？","A short continuous column unique to the region":"該產區特有的矮連續式蒸餾柱","A copper pot still, double distilled as in Cognac":"銅製壺式蒸餾器，像 Cognac 一樣二次蒸餾","A tall multi-plate column for neutral spirit":"製作中性烈酒的多層蒸餾板高蒸餾柱","A system of three pot stills":"三座壺式蒸餾器組成的系統","Armagnac uses its own continuous column, which must be short with few plates.":"Armagnac 使用自己的連續式蒸餾柱，必須矮而蒸餾板少。","Double pot distillation is Cognac's rule. A tall column with many plates would give an almost neutral spirit, the opposite of Armagnac style. Three stills in a row are not part of this region's tradition.":"壺式二次蒸餾是 Cognac 的規定。蒸餾板多的高蒸餾柱會做出近乎中性的烈酒，與 Armagnac 的風格相反。三座蒸餾器串聯不屬於這個產區的傳統。","Are pot stills allowed in Armagnac?":"Armagnac 允許使用壺式蒸餾器嗎？","Yes, but they are very rarely used":"允許，但很少使用","No, the law bans them outright":"不允許，法律完全禁止","Yes, and they produce most Armagnac":"允許，而且大多數 Armagnac 用它製作","Only for Blanche meant for cocktails, never for aged Armagnac":"只限用於調酒的 Blanche，陳年 Armagnac 絕不使用","Pot stills are permitted, but almost every producer prefers the local column.":"壺式蒸餾器是允許的，但幾乎每位生產者都偏好當地的蒸餾柱。","The key point is rarity, not a ban: the short column is the near-universal choice. Blanche is distilled exactly like other Armagnacs; the only difference is that it skips oak.":"重點是少見，不是禁止：矮蒸餾柱幾乎是所有人的選擇。Blanche 的蒸餾方式和其他 Armagnac 完全一樣；唯一的差別是它不過橡木桶。","What do Armagnac, Bourbon and rhum agricole have in common?":"Armagnac、Bourbon 和 rhum agricole 有什麼共同點？","Characterful spirits made in a column at fairly low strength":"都是用蒸餾柱在相當低的濃度製成、特色鮮明的烈酒","They must all mature in new charred oak":"都必須在炙燒過的新橡木桶中熟成","They are all made from acidic, low-aroma white grapes grown in France":"都用法國種植、酸度高而香氣少的白葡萄製成","They are all double distilled in pot stills":"都在壺式蒸餾器中蒸餾兩次","All three leave a column at a strength low enough to keep plenty of congeners, so they are full of character.":"三者離開蒸餾柱時的濃度都夠低，保留了大量同屬物，所以特色十足。","They show that a column does not have to mean a light spirit: what matters is the strength at which the hearts are drawn off. New charred oak is a Bourbon rule, not an Armagnac one. Only Armagnac comes from grapes, and none of the three is typically double pot distilled.":"它們說明蒸餾柱不一定代表清淡的烈酒：重要的是抽取酒心時的濃度。炙燒過的新橡木桶是 Bourbon 的規定，不是 Armagnac 的。只有 Armagnac 來自葡萄，而三者通常都不是壺式二次蒸餾。","A label reads Ténarèze. What is it?":"酒標上寫著 Ténarèze。它是什麼？","An Armagnac sub-region":"Armagnac 的子產區","A Cognac age term":"Cognac 的年數術語","A grape variety used for Blanche Armagnac":"用於 Blanche Armagnac 的葡萄品種","A type of copper worm tub condenser":"一種銅製的蟲桶冷凝器","Ténarèze is, with Bas Armagnac, one of Armagnac's two important sub-regions.":"Ténarèze 與 Bas Armagnac 是 Armagnac 的兩個重要子產區。","Age terms are abbreviations such as VS, VSOP and XO. The variety suited to Blanche is Folle Blanche. The worm tub is typical of Cognac.":"年數術語是 VS、VSOP 和 XO 這類縮寫。適合 Blanche 的品種是白福爾。蟲桶冷凝器是 Cognac 的典型設備。","How is Blanche Armagnac made?":"Blanche Armagnac 是怎麼做的？","Like other Armagnacs, but with no oak maturation":"和其他 Armagnac 一樣，但不經橡木桶熟成","From pomace instead of wine":"用果渣而不是葡萄酒","By steeping fresh grapes in neutral spirit and redistilling it all":"把新鮮葡萄浸泡在中性烈酒中，再全部重新蒸餾","In a pot still, then charcoal-filtered":"用壺式蒸餾器，再以木炭過濾","Blanche follows the same process as any Armagnac; the only difference is that it never sees oak and stays colourless.":"Blanche 的製程和任何 Armagnac 相同；唯一的差別是它從不接觸橡木，保持無色。","The base is still wine, usually distilled in the local column. Pomace makes a different kind of spirit, and steeping in neutral spirit applies to other fruits. The lack of colour comes not from filtering but from wood never being involved.":"基底仍然是葡萄酒，通常用當地的蒸餾柱蒸餾。果渣做出的是另一種烈酒，浸泡在中性烈酒中則適用於其他水果。沒有顏色不是因為過濾，而是因為從來沒有用到木頭。","Which statement about vintage-dated brandies is correct?":"關於標示年份的白蘭地，下列哪一項正確？","They are common in Armagnac but rare in Cognac":"在 Armagnac 很常見，在 Cognac 很少見","They are common in Cognac but banned in Armagnac":"在 Cognac 很常見，在 Armagnac 被禁止","The year shows the average age of a blend of different ages":"年份表示不同年數調和的平均年數","They are banned in both Cognac and Armagnac":"在 Cognac 和 Armagnac 都被禁止","Vintages are a hallmark of Armagnac, whereas nearly all Cognac is a blend of ages.":"年份酒是 Armagnac 的標誌，而幾乎所有 Cognac 都是不同年數的調和。","A vintage Armagnac comes from grapes of a single harvest, so it is not a blend of ages and the year is not an average. In Cognac, vintages exist but are rare, not banned.":"年份 Armagnac 來自單一採收年的葡萄，所以不是不同年數的調和，年份也不是平均值。在 Cognac，年份酒存在但很少見，並未被禁止。","A brandy made outside the French regions says VSOP on the label. What does that term guarantee?":"一款在法國產區之外製作的白蘭地，酒標上寫著 VSOP。這個術語保證什麼？","No legally defined age":"沒有法律定義的年數","The same minimum years in oak as Cognac":"與 Cognac 相同的最低橡木桶年數","That it was made from Ugni Blanc grown in the Cognac area":"它用 Cognac 產區種植的白玉霓製成","That it was distilled in France and bottled abroad":"它在法國蒸餾、在國外裝瓶","These terms are widely copied, but outside the French regions that regulate them they have no legal definition.":"這些術語被廣泛仿用，但在規範它們的法國產區之外，並沒有法律定義。","The law forbids false statements on labels, but it does not define every term used. The same goes, for example, for XO on a rum: in Cognac it has a precise meaning, elsewhere it does not. The term says nothing about the grape or where it was distilled.":"法律禁止酒標上的不實陳述，但並沒有定義每一個使用的術語。舉例來說，蘭姆酒上的 XO 也是如此：在 Cognac 它有明確的意義，在別處則沒有。這個術語與葡萄或蒸餾地點無關。","In which French region is Calvados made?":"Calvados 在法國的哪個地區生產？","Normandy":"諾曼第","The area just south of Bordeaux":"就在波爾多南邊的地區","Calvados must be made in specific parts of Normandy, in northern France.":"Calvados 必須在法國北部諾曼第的特定區域生產。","The area south of Bordeaux is Armagnac. Burgundy and Provence are not benchmark areas for apple brandy. Normandy lies in the far north, where vines struggle and apple trees thrive instead.":"波爾多以南的地區是 Armagnac。勃根地和普羅旺斯不是蘋果白蘭地的代表產區。諾曼第位於最北邊，那裡葡萄樹難以生長，蘋果樹卻長得很好。","Which fruit is Calvados made from?":"Calvados 用什麼水果製成？","Apples and pears, mostly apples":"蘋果和梨，以蘋果為主","White grapes and apples in equal parts":"白葡萄和蘋果各半","Only pears, grown anywhere in France":"只用梨，可在法國任何地方種植","Plums and cherries steeped in neutral spirit":"浸泡在中性烈酒中的李子和櫻桃","Calvados is made from apples and pears, with apples far more widely grown.":"Calvados 用蘋果和梨製成，其中蘋果的種植廣泛得多。","Grapes do not grow well in Normandy, so they play no part in Calvados. Pears are used but in smaller amounts, and the fruit must come from the defined area, not anywhere in France. Steeping in neutral spirit belongs to other fruits and styles.":"葡萄在諾曼第長得不好，所以與 Calvados 無關。梨也會使用，但量較少，而且水果必須來自劃定的產區，不是法國任何地方。浸泡在中性烈酒中屬於其他水果和類型。","Why is Calvados made from apples rather than grapes?":"為什麼 Calvados 用蘋果而不是葡萄製作？","Grapes do not grow well in Normandy":"葡萄在諾曼第長得不好","Normandy's grapes are legally reserved for making sparkling wine":"諾曼第的葡萄依法保留給氣泡酒","Apples give more alcohol and let producers skip fermentation":"蘋果產生的酒精更多，還能省去發酵","Grapes cannot be distilled in pot stills":"葡萄不能在壺式蒸餾器中蒸餾","Northern France is poorly suited to vines, while apple trees thrive there.":"法國北部不適合葡萄樹，蘋果樹在那裡卻生長旺盛。","Every fruit spirit is built on locally grown fruit. Apples, like grapes, must be pressed and their juice fermented: no fruit lets you skip fermentation. Grapes distil perfectly well in pot stills, as Cognac shows.":"每一種水果烈酒都建立在當地種植的水果上。蘋果和葡萄一樣，必須壓榨並讓果汁發酵：沒有任何水果能省去發酵。葡萄在壺式蒸餾器中蒸餾毫無問題，Cognac 就是證明。","Which stills are used for Calvados?":"Calvados 使用哪些蒸餾器？","A variety of pot stills and short columns":"各種壺式蒸餾器和矮蒸餾柱","Only very tall columns that produce neutral spirit":"只用製作中性烈酒的極高蒸餾柱","No still: the fruit is steeped straight in spirit":"不用蒸餾器：水果直接浸泡在烈酒中","Only low-temperature vacuum stills":"只用低溫真空蒸餾器","Calvados producers use pot stills and short columns to make characterful spirits.":"Calvados 的生產者使用壺式蒸餾器和矮蒸餾柱，製作特色鮮明的烈酒。","The goal is to keep the aroma of the fruit. A column taken to neutral spirit would wipe most of it out. Calvados comes from fermented, distilled juice, not maceration, and vacuum stills are not part of its tradition.":"目標是保留水果的香氣。蒸餾到中性烈酒的蒸餾柱會抹去大部分香氣。Calvados 來自發酵並蒸餾的果汁，不是浸漬，真空蒸餾器也不屬於它的傳統。","Why does even a very old Calvados keep a clear apple aroma?":"為什麼即使是極老的 Calvados 也保有清晰的蘋果香氣？","It ages in large oak vessels that give little oak flavour":"它在大型橡木容器中陳年，得到的橡木風味很少","Fresh apple juice is always added just before bottling":"裝瓶前一律加入新鮮蘋果汁","It ages in glass with no contact with wood":"它在玻璃中陳年，不接觸木頭","It is distilled so strong that the aromas become fixed":"它蒸餾到非常高的濃度，讓香氣固定下來","Large vessels give less oak flavour than barrels, so the apple stays in front.":"大型容器給的橡木風味比桶子少，所以蘋果香仍在最前面。","Calvados ages in oak, not glass, but the large size of the vessels limits the wood's imprint. Adding juice is not part of production. A higher distillation strength would actually reduce aroma rather than fix it.":"Calvados 在橡木中陳年，不是玻璃，但容器的大尺寸限制了木頭的印記。加果汁不是製程的一部分。更高的蒸餾濃度其實會減少香氣，而不是固定香氣。","In a blind tasting, a very old amber brandy still shows an intense apple aroma. What is it most likely to be?":"在一場盲品中，一款極老的琥珀色白蘭地仍表現出濃郁的蘋果香氣。它最可能是什麼？","An aged Calvados":"陳年的 Calvados","A Grande Champagne XO Cognac":"Grande Champagne XO Cognac","A vintage Armagnac with plenty of Baco":"含大量巴科的年份 Armagnac","A grappa rested two years in steel tanks":"在鋼槽中靜置兩年的 grappa","Calvados, even when very old, keeps a pronounced, recognisable apple aroma.":"Calvados 即使非常老，仍保有明顯而可辨認的蘋果香氣。","An XO Cognac would lean towards raisin, flowers, oak and rancio, and an Armagnac with Baco towards prunes. A grappa rested in steel would be colourless, not amber, with herbaceous notes.":"XO Cognac 會偏向葡萄乾、花香、橡木和 rancio，含巴科的 Armagnac 則偏向李子乾。在鋼槽中靜置的 grappa 會是無色的，不是琥珀色，並帶草本氣息。","What is grappa made from?":"grappa 用什麼製成？","Grape pomace":"葡萄果渣","Freshly fermented white wine":"剛發酵完成的白葡萄酒","Raisins steeped in spirit":"浸泡在烈酒中的葡萄乾","Grappa is Italy's pomace spirit, made from the skins left over from winemaking.":"grappa 是義大利的果渣烈酒，用釀酒剩下的葡萄皮製成。","Distilled white wine would give a grape brandy like Cognac or Armagnac, not grappa. Apples and pears are the base of Calvados. Grappa comes from fermenting and distilling pomace, not from maceration.":"蒸餾白葡萄酒會得到 Cognac 或 Armagnac 那樣的葡萄白蘭地，不是 grappa。蘋果和梨是 Calvados 的原料。grappa 來自果渣的發酵和蒸餾，不是浸漬。","A Spanish producer distils pomace exactly as in Italy. Can the spirit be called grappa?":"一位西班牙生產者以和義大利完全相同的方式蒸餾果渣。這款烈酒可以叫做 grappa 嗎？","No, the name is reserved for Italy":"不行，這個名稱保留給義大利","Yes, if only Italian grape varieties are used":"可以，只要只用義大利葡萄品種","Yes, as long as the spirit is never aged in oak":"可以，只要烈酒從不在橡木桶中陳年","Yes, because grappa is a generic word for any pomace spirit":"可以，因為 grappa 是任何果渣烈酒的通稱","Only pomace spirits made in Italy can be called grappa.":"只有在義大利製作的果渣烈酒才能叫做 grappa。","The name depends on where the spirit is made, not on the grape or how it is matured. Pomace spirits are made in many countries, Spain included, but under their own names. Grappa is therefore not a generic term.":"名稱取決於烈酒在哪裡製作，不是葡萄或熟成方式。許多國家都生產果渣烈酒，包括西班牙，但用的是各自的名稱。所以 grappa 不是通稱。","What is a classic unaged grappa usually like?":"經典的未陳年 grappa 通常是什麼樣子？","Colourless, herbaceous, sometimes a little sharp":"無色、草本，有時略顯銳利","Amber, with vanilla and coconut notes from oak":"琥珀色，帶橡木的香草和椰子氣息","Golden, with an intense baked-apple aroma":"金黃色，帶濃郁的烤蘋果香氣","Brown, sweet and creamy like a liqueur":"棕色、甜而滑順，像利口酒","Without oak grappa stays colourless; the skins give herbaceous notes and a sometimes sharp texture.":"沒有橡木，grappa 保持無色；葡萄皮帶來草本氣息和有時略顯銳利的質地。","Amber colour and vanilla and coconut notes come from oak, which is not the norm for grappa. Baked apple is typical of Calvados. Grappa is not a liqueur: it is neither sweetened nor creamy.":"琥珀色以及香草和椰子氣息來自橡木，這對 grappa 來說不是常態。烤蘋果是 Calvados 的典型特徵。grappa 不是利口酒：既不加糖，也不滑順如奶油。","What does a Moscato grappa add compared with one from neutral grapes?":"與用中性葡萄做的 grappa 相比，蜜思嘉（Moscato）grappa 多了什麼？","Floral and fruity notes over the herbaceous base":"在草本基調上多了花香和果香","A golden colour from the aromatic skins":"來自芳香果皮的金黃色","Natural sweetness that survives distillation":"通過蒸餾仍保留的天然甜味","Prune and rancio notes that are typical of long ageing":"長期陳年典型的李子乾和 rancio 氣息","Moscato is an aromatic grape: its floral and fruity aromas sit on top of the pomace's herbaceous notes.":"蜜思嘉是芳香型葡萄：它的花香和果香疊在果渣的草本氣息之上。","Expressing the grape variety is one of the ways the best grappas stand out. Freshly distilled spirits are colourless and sugar-free whatever the grape. Prune and rancio would point to a grape like Baco or long oak ageing.":"表現葡萄品種是最好的 grappa 脫穎而出的方式之一。不論用什麼葡萄，剛蒸餾出來的烈酒都無色且不含糖。李子乾和 rancio 指向巴科這類葡萄或長期的橡木桶陳年。","A grappa rests for eighteen months in steel before bottling. What can be expected?":"一款 grappa 裝瓶前在鋼槽中靜置十八個月。可以預期什麼？","Still colourless, but fuller and smoother":"仍然無色，但更飽滿、更柔順","A golden colour and vanilla aromas":"金黃色和香草香氣","No change at all: inert vessels have no effect, even after years":"完全沒有變化：惰性容器即使過了多年也沒有作用","Rancio notes such as leather and mushroom":"皮革和蘑菇等 rancio 氣息","Resting a year or more in inert vessels makes grappa fuller and smoother without adding colour.":"在惰性容器中靜置一年以上，會讓 grappa 更飽滿、更柔順，而不增添顏色。","After some months, even in an inert vessel, a spirit becomes smoother and rounder, so it is wrong to say nothing changes. Colour and vanilla come only from oak, while rancio develops from long interaction between spirit, wood and oxygen in a barrel.":"幾個月後，即使在惰性容器中，烈酒也會變得更柔順、更圓潤，所以說沒有任何變化是錯的。顏色和香草只來自橡木，rancio 則是烈酒、木頭和氧氣在桶中長期交互作用發展出來的。","Which of these fruit spirits is normally matured in oak?":"下列哪一種水果烈酒通常在橡木中熟成？","Classic grappa":"經典的 grappa","Peruvian pisco":"秘魯 pisco","Blanche Armagnac":"Blanche Armagnac","Like most apple and grape brandies, Calvados is matured in oak, in large vessels.":"和大多數蘋果和葡萄白蘭地一樣，Calvados 在橡木中熟成，使用大型容器。","Pomace spirits such as grappa usually rest in inert vessels. In Peru the law requires pisco to be unaged, and Blanche is by definition an Armagnac that never sees oak.":"grappa 這類果渣烈酒通常在惰性容器中靜置。在秘魯，法律規定 pisco 不得陳年，而 Blanche 依定義就是從不接觸橡木的 Armagnac。","Which countries are the home of pisco?":"pisco 的故鄉是哪些國家？","Chile and Peru":"智利和秘魯","Mexico and Spain":"墨西哥和西班牙","Argentina and Uruguay":"阿根廷和烏拉圭","Brazil and Colombia":"巴西和哥倫比亞","Pisco is the grape brandy of Chile and Peru.":"pisco 是智利和秘魯的葡萄白蘭地。","Mexico and Spain make grape and pomace brandies, but not pisco. Brazil is linked to cachaça, a cane spirit. Pisco belongs to the two Andean countries on the Pacific coast.":"墨西哥和西班牙生產葡萄和果渣白蘭地，但不是 pisco。巴西與 cachaça 這種甘蔗烈酒有關。pisco 屬於太平洋岸的這兩個安地斯國家。","What kind of grape is used for pisco?":"pisco 使用哪一種葡萄？","Highly aromatic grapes such as Muscats":"香氣濃郁的葡萄，例如蜜思嘉","Neutral, very acidic white grapes like Ugni Blanc":"像白玉霓那樣中性、酸度很高的白葡萄","Only black grape pomace left from red winemaking":"只用釀紅酒剩下的紅葡萄果渣","Sun-dried grapes to concentrate the sugar":"曬乾以濃縮糖分的葡萄","Pisco is made from highly aromatic grapes, especially the Muscat family.":"pisco 用香氣濃郁的葡萄製成，尤其是蜜思嘉家族。","It is the classic case of distillers choosing aromatic grapes for intense grape aromas. Neutral, acidic grapes like Ugni Blanc are Cognac's choice. Pisco is a grape brandy, not a pomace spirit, and is not made from dried grapes.":"這是蒸餾師為了濃郁的葡萄香氣而選擇芳香型葡萄的經典例子。白玉霓那樣中性、高酸的葡萄是 Cognac 的選擇。pisco 是葡萄白蘭地，不是果渣烈酒，也不是用風乾葡萄做的。","Which type of still is pisco made in?":"pisco 用哪一種蒸餾器製作？","Continuous column making neutral spirit":"製作中性烈酒的連續式蒸餾柱","The short column typical of Armagnac":"Armagnac 典型的矮蒸餾柱","It is not distilled: grapes are steeped in spirit":"不經蒸餾：葡萄浸泡在烈酒中","Pisco is distilled in pot stills, which preserve its aromas.":"pisco 在壺式蒸餾器中蒸餾，能保留它的香氣。","A column taken to neutral spirit would remove exactly the grape aromas pisco is valued for. The short column is an Armagnac speciality. Pisco is made by distilling fermented grape wine, not by maceration.":"蒸餾到中性烈酒的蒸餾柱會去除的，正是 pisco 受人珍視的葡萄香氣。矮蒸餾柱是 Armagnac 的特色。pisco 是蒸餾發酵的葡萄酒製成的，不是靠浸漬。","Which statement about Peruvian pisco is correct?":"關於秘魯 pisco，下列哪一項正確？","By law it must be unaged":"依法不得陳年","It must spend at least two years in French oak barrels":"必須在法國橡木桶中存放至少兩年","It is made only from black grape pomace":"只用紅葡萄果渣製成","It is always distilled in continuous columns":"一律在連續式蒸餾柱中蒸餾","In Peru the law requires pisco to be unaged.":"在秘魯，法律規定 pisco 不得陳年。","That is why Peruvian pisco relies entirely on pure fruity and floral aromas. Two years in oak is Cognac's minimum, not pisco's. Pisco is an aromatic grape brandy distilled in pot stills, not a column-distilled pomace spirit.":"所以秘魯 pisco 完全仰賴純淨的果香和花香。兩年橡木桶是 Cognac 的最低要求，不是 pisco 的。pisco 是在壺式蒸餾器中蒸餾的芳香型葡萄白蘭地，不是用蒸餾柱蒸餾的果渣烈酒。","A customer asks for a pisco with a light touch of wood. What can be suggested?":"一位顧客想要一款帶一點木質感的 pisco。可以推薦什麼？","A Chilean pisco briefly matured in wood":"在木桶中短暫熟成的智利 pisco","A Peruvian pisco aged for several years in new barrels":"在新桶中陳年數年的秘魯 pisco","An XO pisco, since the term guarantees six years in oak":"XO pisco，因為這個術語保證六年橡木桶","None: no pisco anywhere may touch wood":"沒有：任何地方的 pisco 都不能接觸木頭","Chile makes some wood-matured piscos, usually for a short time to keep the fruit.":"智利生產一些經木桶熟成的 pisco，通常時間很短，以保留果香。","The ban on ageing applies in Peru, not Chile, so it is wrong that no pisco may touch wood. Age terms such as XO are only legally defined in the protected French regions; elsewhere they guarantee nothing.":"禁止陳年的規定適用於秘魯，不是智利，所以說任何 pisco 都不能接觸木頭是錯的。XO 這類年數術語只在受保護的法國產區有法律定義；在別處不保證任何事。","What are the best piscos noted for?":"最好的 pisco 以什麼著稱？","Pure, pronounced fruity and floral aromas":"純淨而明顯的果香和花香","Rancio and oak notes after decades in cask":"在桶中數十年後的 rancio 和橡木氣息","The herbaceous, spicy notes typical of pomace":"果渣典型的草本、香料氣息","An almost neutral profile, to be used just like vodka":"近乎中性的輪廓，用法就像伏特加","Aromatic grapes, pot stills and little or no wood give pure fruity and floral aromas.":"芳香型葡萄、壺式蒸餾器，加上很少或完全不用木頭，帶來純淨的果香和花香。","Rancio and oak need long cask ageing, which most piscos never get. Herbaceous notes are the mark of pomace spirits like grappa. A neutral profile would be the opposite of what aromatic grapes are chosen for.":"rancio 和橡木需要長期桶陳，大多數 pisco 從未經歷。草本氣息是 grappa 這類果渣烈酒的標誌。中性的輪廓則與選擇芳香型葡萄的目的相反。","Where must the apples for Calvados be grown?":"Calvados 的蘋果必須種在哪裡？","In the defined parts of Normandy where it is made":"在生產它的諾曼第劃定區域內","Anywhere in France":"法國任何地方","Anywhere in the EU, as long as they are cider apples":"歐盟任何地方，只要是釀蘋果酒用的蘋果","Anywhere, as long as distillation takes place in Normandy":"任何地方，只要蒸餾在諾曼第進行","Like the agave for Tequila, the fruit for Calvados must be grown in the defined production area.":"就像 Tequila 的龍舌蘭一樣，Calvados 的水果必須種在劃定的產區內。","Most spirits can use raw material from anywhere: Scotch, for example, buys grain from several countries. Calvados is an exception, like Tequila. Distilling apples grown elsewhere would not be enough, even in a Normandy distillery.":"大多數烈酒可以使用任何地方的原料：例如 Scotch 就從好幾個國家購買穀物。Calvados 和 Tequila 一樣是例外。蒸餾別處種的蘋果是不夠的，即使是在諾曼第的蒸餾廠。","In what order do the main steps of Calvados production happen?":"Calvados 生產的主要步驟依什麼順序進行？","Extract the juice, ferment it, distil it, mature it in oak":"榨汁、發酵、蒸餾、在橡木中熟成","Distil the apples, then ferment, then press":"蒸餾蘋果，再發酵，再壓榨","Steep apples in neutral spirit, redistil and bottle unaged":"把蘋果浸泡在中性烈酒中，再蒸餾，不陳年就裝瓶","Ferment whole apples, age them in cask, then distil":"整顆蘋果發酵、入桶陳年，再蒸餾","The juice taken from the fruit is fermented and distilled, and the spirit then matures in oak vessels.":"從水果取得的果汁經過發酵和蒸餾，烈酒再於橡木容器中熟成。","It is the same path as grape brandy: first sugar becomes alcohol, then distillation concentrates it, then comes maturation. Without fermentation there is no alcohol to distil. Steeping in neutral spirit is a method for other fruits, and Calvados is not an unaged spirit.":"這和葡萄白蘭地是同一條路：先是糖變成酒精，再由蒸餾濃縮，然後熟成。沒有發酵就沒有酒精可以蒸餾。浸泡在中性烈酒中是其他水果的做法，而 Calvados 不是未陳年的烈酒。","Which comparison between Calvados and Cognac stills is correct?":"關於 Calvados 和 Cognac 的蒸餾器，下列哪一項比較是正確的？","Calvados may use pot stills or short columns; Cognac only double pot distillation":"Calvados 可用壺式蒸餾器或矮蒸餾柱；Cognac 只能壺式二次蒸餾","Both must use a worm tub condenser":"兩者都必須使用蟲桶冷凝器","Calvados uses only tall columns, Cognac only pot stills":"Calvados 只用高蒸餾柱，Cognac 只用壺式蒸餾器","Both use the same short column as Armagnac":"兩者都使用和 Armagnac 相同的矮蒸餾柱","Calvados producers choose among various pot stills and short columns, while Cognac strictly requires pot stills.":"Calvados 的生產者可在各種壺式蒸餾器和矮蒸餾柱中選擇，Cognac 則嚴格規定使用壺式蒸餾器。","The worm tub is required only in Cognac. Tall columns would give too light a spirit, and Calvados aims for character. The typical short column is Armagnac's, and Cognac does not use it.":"只有 Cognac 規定使用蟲桶冷凝器。高蒸餾柱會做出太清淡的烈酒，而 Calvados 追求的是特色。典型的矮蒸餾柱是 Armagnac 的，Cognac 並不使用。","Why do Calvados distillers use pot stills and short columns?":"為什麼 Calvados 的蒸餾師使用壺式蒸餾器和矮蒸餾柱？","To make characterful spirits":"製作特色鮮明的烈酒","To make neutral spirit to sell to vodka producers":"製作中性烈酒賣給伏特加生產者","Because cider would boil over in a tall column during distillation":"因為蘋果酒在高蒸餾柱中蒸餾時會沸溢","To strip out all apple aroma before maturation":"在熟成前去除所有蘋果香氣","These stills keep plenty of congeners, so the spirit holds on to the character of the fruit.":"這些蒸餾器保留大量同屬物，所以烈酒留住了水果的特色。","The whole point of Calvados is its apple aroma, which stays recognisable even after many years. Making neutral spirit or stripping aromas would go against that aim. No technical problem stops cider being distilled in a column: it is a style choice.":"Calvados 的重點就是它的蘋果香氣，即使多年後仍可辨認。製作中性烈酒或去除香氣都違背這個目標。沒有任何技術問題阻止蘋果酒在蒸餾柱中蒸餾：這是風格的選擇。","A customer asks for an oak-aged French apple brandy. What can be suggested?":"一位顧客想要一款橡木桶陳年的法國蘋果白蘭地。可以推薦什麼？","A Calvados":"Calvados","A grappa":"grappa","A Peruvian pisco":"秘魯 pisco","A Blanche Armagnac made from Folle Blanche":"用白福爾製成的 Blanche Armagnac","Calvados is Normandy's apple (and pear) brandy, matured in oak.":"Calvados 是諾曼第的蘋果（和梨）白蘭地，在橡木中熟成。","Grappa and pisco are grape spirits: the first Italian and made from pomace, the second South American and unaged by law in Peru. Blanche Armagnac is French but grape-based and unoaked.":"grappa 和 pisco 是葡萄烈酒：前者來自義大利，用果渣製成；後者來自南美洲，在秘魯依法不得陳年。Blanche Armagnac 是法國的，但以葡萄為原料，而且不過橡木桶。","Which statement about Calvados is NOT correct?":"關於 Calvados，下列哪一項不正確？","It is usually bottled young and colourless":"通常年輕、無色時就裝瓶","It comes from Normandy":"來自諾曼第","It can include some pears as well as apples":"除了蘋果，也可以含一些梨","It matures in oak vessels":"在橡木容器中熟成","Calvados is normally oak-matured, so it is not a young, colourless spirit.":"Calvados 通常在橡木中熟成，所以不是年輕、無色的烈酒。","The other three statements are true: Normandy, apples with a smaller share of pears, and oak maturation. Among non-grape fruit spirits, apple brandies are precisely the exception that goes into wood. The young, colourless style better describes grappa and pisco.":"其他三項都正確：諾曼第、蘋果加上少部分的梨，以及橡木熟成。在非葡萄的水果烈酒中，蘋果白蘭地正是進木桶的例外。年輕、無色的風格更適合描述 grappa 和 pisco。","France is home to three great fruit spirits. Which trio is correct?":"法國是三大水果烈酒的故鄉。哪一組是正確的？","Cognac, Armagnac and Calvados":"Cognac、Armagnac 和 Calvados","Cognac, grappa and pisco":"Cognac、grappa 和 pisco","Armagnac, Calvados and Chilean pisco":"Armagnac、Calvados 和智利 pisco","Calvados, Muscat grappa and Tequila":"Calvados、蜜思嘉 grappa 和 Tequila","Cognac and Armagnac are grape brandies, and Calvados is an apple and pear brandy: all three French.":"Cognac 和 Armagnac 是葡萄白蘭地，Calvados 是蘋果和梨白蘭地：三者都是法國的。","They are benchmarks that producers worldwide aspire to or draw on. Grappa is Italian, pisco comes from Chile and Peru, and Tequila is a Mexican agave spirit.":"它們是世界各地生產者嚮往或借鏡的標竿。grappa 是義大利的，pisco 來自智利和秘魯，Tequila 則是墨西哥的龍舌蘭烈酒。","How does Calvados maturation usually differ from Cognac's?":"Calvados 的熟成通常與 Cognac 有什麼不同？","Calvados uses large oak vessels; Cognac uses casks, often new then older ones":"Calvados 使用大型橡木容器；Cognac 使用桶子，常先用新桶再用舊桶","Calvados matures in steel, Cognac in oak":"Calvados 在鋼中熟成，Cognac 在橡木中","Calvados matures in small new charred casks, like Bourbon":"Calvados 像 Bourbon 一樣在炙燒過的小型新桶中熟成","None: both spend ten years in glass":"沒有不同：兩者都在玻璃中存放十年","Calvados's large vessels give little oak, while Cognac seeks a clear but balanced oak imprint.":"Calvados 的大型容器給的橡木味很少，Cognac 則追求清晰而平衡的橡木印記。","That is why an old Calvados still smells of apple, while a Cognac weaves oak and fruit together. Steel would give neither colour nor oak notes. New charred oak is the Bourbon rule, and glass is only used to preserve some very old Cognacs.":"所以老的 Calvados 仍然有蘋果香，Cognac 則把橡木和果香交織在一起。鋼既不帶來顏色，也不帶來橡木氣息。炙燒過的新橡木桶是 Bourbon 的規定，玻璃則只用來保存某些極老的 Cognac。","Which country set the benchmark for pomace spirits?":"哪一個國家為果渣烈酒立下了標竿？","Pomace spirits are made everywhere, but the benchmark is Italian grappa.":"果渣烈酒到處都有生產，但標竿是義大利的 grappa。","France is the benchmark for wine and apple brandies, not pomace. Chile is home to pisco, distilled from wine made from aromatic grapes. Mexico makes grape and pomace brandies but is not the benchmark.":"法國是葡萄酒白蘭地和蘋果白蘭地的標竿，不是果渣烈酒。智利是 pisco 的故鄉，它用芳香型葡萄釀的葡萄酒蒸餾而成。墨西哥生產葡萄和果渣白蘭地，但不是標竿。","What always appears prominently on a grappa label?":"grappa 的酒標上一定會醒目地出現什麼？","The word grappa":"grappa 這個字","The harvest year":"採收年份","The type of oak used for the compulsory ageing":"強制陳年所用的橡木種類","The term Hors d'âge":"Hors d'âge 這個術語","The name grappa, reserved for Italy, always stands out on the label.":"保留給義大利的 grappa 這個名稱，在酒標上總是很醒目。","The grape variety may appear next to it, but a vintage is not a typical element. There is no compulsory oak ageing: classic grappa never sees wood. Hors d'âge is a Cognac age term.":"旁邊可能出現葡萄品種，但年份不是典型的要素。沒有強制的橡木桶陳年：經典的 grappa 從不接觸木頭。Hors d'âge 是 Cognac 的年數術語。","A grappa label names a single grape variety. What does this tell you?":"一瓶 grappa 的酒標標示了單一葡萄品種。這告訴你什麼？","The pomace comes from that variety; other grappas come from a mix":"果渣來自那個品種；其他 grappa 則來自混合品種","That the grappa rested a year in wood":"這款 grappa 在木桶中靜置了一年","That the law makes every Italian grappa name one single variety":"法律規定每款義大利 grappa 都要標示單一品種","That it was distilled from wine, not pomace":"它是用葡萄酒蒸餾的，不是果渣","Many grappas are made from one variety, such as Moscato, and say so; others come from a blend of varieties.":"許多 grappa 用單一品種製成（例如蜜思嘉），並標示出來；其他則來自多個品種的混合。","The variety lets a precise character come through, very clear with aromatic grapes. There is no single-variety obligation, and the grape name says nothing about resting. Grappa is always a pomace spirit, never a wine spirit.":"品種讓明確的特色得以展現，用芳香型葡萄時尤其清楚。沒有單一品種的義務，葡萄名稱也與靜置無關。grappa 一定是果渣烈酒，絕不是葡萄酒烈酒。","In which two ways do the best grappa producers go beyond the basic style?":"最好的 grappa 生產者用哪兩種方式超越基本風格？","They express the grape variety and rest it a year or more in inert vessels":"表現葡萄品種，並在惰性容器中靜置一年以上","They age it in new oak and add sugar":"在新橡木桶中陳年並加糖","They use only black pomace and distil in a column":"只用紅葡萄果渣，並用蒸餾柱蒸餾","They add fresh fruit and filter through charcoal":"加入新鮮水果並用木炭過濾","The best grappas let the variety speak and gain a fuller, smoother texture through a long rest in inert vessels.":"最好的 grappa 讓品種說話，並透過在惰性容器中長時間靜置，得到更飽滿、更柔順的質地。","Basic grappa is herbaceous and sometimes sharp: variety and resting are the two ways past that template. New oak and sugar would change the spirit's nature. Pomace colour, columns, added fruit or charcoal are not part of this approach.":"基本的 grappa 帶草本味，有時銳利：品種和靜置是超越這個樣板的兩種方式。新橡木桶和糖會改變烈酒的本質。果渣的顏色、蒸餾柱、添加水果或木炭都不屬於這種做法。","A young grappa feels a little sharp on the palate. Is this a fault?":"一款年輕的 grappa 在口中略顯銳利。這是缺陷嗎？","No, a sharp texture can be typical":"不是，銳利的質地可以是典型特徵","Yes, it shows it was distilled from wine instead of pomace":"是，這表示它是用葡萄酒而不是果渣蒸餾的","Yes, it is a sign of damage from casks that were too old":"是，這是桶子太老造成損害的跡象","No, it proves long ageing":"不是，這證明它經過長期陳年","Classic unaged grappas can have a slightly sharp texture as well as herbaceous notes.":"經典的未陳年 grappa 除了草本氣息，也可能有略顯銳利的質地。","It is precisely to soften it that the best producers rest it at length in inert vessels. Wood plays no part, since classic grappa never sees it. A long rest would give a smoother texture, not a sharper one.":"最好的生產者讓它在惰性容器中長時間靜置，正是為了讓它變柔和。木頭沒有參與，因為經典的 grappa 從不接觸木頭。長時間靜置會讓質地更柔順，而不是更銳利。","Which comparison between grappa and Calvados maturation is correct?":"關於 grappa 和 Calvados 的熟成，下列哪一項比較是正確的？","Grappa usually rests in inert vessels; Calvados matures in oak":"grappa 通常在惰性容器中靜置；Calvados 在橡木中熟成","Both mature in large oak vessels that give little oak":"兩者都在給橡木味很少的大型橡木容器中熟成","Grappa matures in oak, Calvados in steel":"grappa 在橡木中熟成，Calvados 在鋼中","Both are bottled with no rest at all":"兩者都完全不靜置就裝瓶","Classic grappa never sees wood; Calvados, like other apple brandies, matures in oak.":"經典的 grappa 從不接觸木頭；Calvados 和其他蘋果白蘭地一樣，在橡木中熟成。","Large oak vessels are typical of Calvados, not grappa. The other two options reverse or erase what really happens. Even the simplest grappa rests at least briefly in inert vessels before bottling.":"大型橡木容器是 Calvados 的典型做法，不是 grappa 的。另外兩個選項把實際情況顛倒或抹去了。即使最簡單的 grappa，裝瓶前也至少會在惰性容器中短暫靜置。","A producer distils Moscato pomace and rests the grappa for two years in glass. Which description fits best?":"一位生產者蒸餾蜜思嘉果渣，並讓 grappa 在玻璃中靜置兩年。哪一項描述最貼切？","Colourless, floral and fruity over herbaceous, with a full, smooth texture":"無色，草本基調上帶花香和果香，質地飽滿柔順","Golden, with vanilla and toasty notes":"金黃色，帶香草和烘烤氣息","Amber, with baked apple and rancio":"琥珀色，帶烤蘋果和 rancio","Almost neutral, aroma-free, for use like vodka":"近乎中性、沒有香氣，用法像伏特加","Moscato adds flowers and fruit to the herbaceous pomace notes, and the long rest in glass brings fullness without colour.":"蜜思嘉在果渣的草本氣息上增添花香和果香，在玻璃中長時間靜置則帶來飽滿感，而不帶來顏色。","Glass is inert: it gives no colour or vanilla, which rules out the golden and amber options. Baked apple points to Calvados, and rancio comes from contact with wood and oxygen. An aromatic grape makes the grappa anything but neutral.":"玻璃是惰性的：不帶來顏色或香草，這就排除了金黃色和琥珀色的選項。烤蘋果指向 Calvados，rancio 來自與木頭和氧氣的接觸。芳香型葡萄讓這款 grappa 絕對不是中性的。","Which of these is NOT a feature of classic grappa?":"下列哪一項不是經典 grappa 的特徵？","Oak maturation to give it colour":"以橡木熟成來取得顏色","Made from pomace":"用果渣製成","Made in Italy":"在義大利製作","Pronounced herbaceous notes and sometimes a slightly sharp texture":"明顯的草本氣息，有時質地略顯銳利","Classic grappa is not oak-matured and is colourless.":"經典的 grappa 不經橡木熟成，而且是無色的。","Pomace, Italian origin and herbaceous notes are typical traits, and sharpness can show in young grappas. Wood is not part of the classic model: it rests briefly in inert vessels.":"果渣、義大利產地和草本氣息是典型特徵，年輕的 grappa 也可能顯得銳利。木頭不屬於經典的模式：它只在惰性容器中短暫靜置。","Why do pisco producers choose highly aromatic grapes?":"為什麼 pisco 的生產者選擇香氣濃郁的葡萄？","For a spirit with pronounced grape aromas":"做出葡萄香氣明顯的烈酒","To get more alcohol from fermentation":"從發酵得到更多酒精","Because aromatic grapes ferment much faster than others":"因為芳香型葡萄發酵得比其他葡萄快得多","To mask the skins' herbaceous notes after long ageing in wood":"在長期木桶陳年後掩蓋果皮的草本氣息","Varieties such as the Muscat family give spirits that smell intensely of the grape itself.":"蜜思嘉家族這類品種做出的烈酒，聞起來有濃郁的葡萄本身的香氣。","It is the opposite choice to most brandies, which start from neutral grapes. Aroma is the goal, not alcohol level or fermentation speed. Pisco is made from wine, not pomace, and usually skips wood.":"這與大多數白蘭地的選擇相反，它們從中性葡萄開始。目標是香氣，不是酒精濃度或發酵速度。pisco 用葡萄酒製成，不是果渣，而且通常不過木桶。","Why do Chilean piscos that see wood usually stay there only briefly?":"為什麼經過木桶的智利 pisco 通常只在裡面短暫停留？","To keep their vibrant fruit":"保留鮮活的果香","Because Chilean law bans more than a month":"因為智利法律禁止超過一個月","Because pisco almost entirely evaporates after a few weeks in cask":"因為 pisco 在桶中幾週後就幾乎全部蒸發","Only to take on colour with no change in aroma":"只是為了上色，香氣不變","A short stay keeps the fruity and floral aromas, pisco's great strength, in the foreground.":"短暫停留能讓果香和花香（pisco 最大的優點）保持在最前面。","The short time is a style choice, not a one-month legal limit. Evaporation affects every spirit in cask, but not that fast. Wood always gives aromas too, not just colour.":"時間短是風格的選擇，不是一個月的法定限制。蒸發會影響桶中的每一種烈酒，但不會那麼快。木頭一定也會帶來香氣，不只是顏色。","In a Pisco Sour, which ingredient gives a smooth, silky texture?":"在 Pisco Sour 中，哪一種材料帶來柔順如絲的質地？","Soda water":"蘇打水","Crushed ice left in the glass to the end":"一直留在杯中的碎冰","A few dashes of bitters":"幾滴苦精","Egg white, shaken with the other ingredients, makes the drink especially smooth and mouth-filling: it is essential in a Pisco Sour.":"蛋白與其他材料一起搖盪，讓飲品格外柔順飽滿：它在 Pisco Sour 中不可或缺。","Soda water lengthens Collins-style drinks, not classic sours. A Pisco Sour is strained, so no ice stays in the glass. Bitters add aroma and bitterness, not texture.":"蘇打水是用來拉長 Collins 類飲品的，不是經典酸酒。Pisco Sour 要濾出，所以杯中不留冰塊。苦精增添的是香氣和苦味，不是質地。","Which ingredients make a classic Pisco Sour?":"經典的 Pisco Sour 用哪些材料？","Pisco, lime juice, simple syrup, egg white":"Pisco、萊姆汁、糖漿、蛋白","Pisco, lemon juice, triple sec":"Pisco、檸檬汁、triple sec","Pisco, ginger beer, lime":"Pisco、薑汁啤酒、萊姆","Pisco, cola, a lime wedge and plenty of cubed ice":"Pisco、可樂、一片萊姆角和大量方冰塊","It is a sour: strong (pisco), sour (lime) and sweet (syrup), plus egg white for texture.":"它是一款酸酒：強（pisco）、酸（萊姆）和甜（糖漿），加上帶來質地的蛋白。","Lemon and triple sec recall the Sidecar pattern, a more complex sour. Ginger beer and lime are the base of a Moscow Mule, and cola of a Cuba Libre: both highballs, not sours.":"檸檬和 triple sec 讓人想到 Sidecar 的模式，那是更複雜的酸酒。薑汁啤酒和萊姆是 Moscow Mule 的基礎，可樂則是 Cuba Libre 的：兩者都是高球，不是酸酒。","How is a Pisco Sour made?":"Pisco Sour 怎麼調製？","Shaken over ice and strained":"加冰搖盪後濾出","Built over ice and topped with soda":"在冰塊上直調，再加滿蘇打水","Stirred at length in a mixing glass, never shaken":"在攪拌杯中長時間攪拌，絕不搖盪","Poured straight into the glass with no ice":"不加冰，直接倒進杯中","Like every sour, it is shaken with ice to chill it and give it a light texture, then strained.":"和所有酸酒一樣，加冰搖盪以冰鎮並帶來輕盈的質地，再濾出。","Shaking is also essential to whip the egg white. Soda turns a sour into a long Collins-style drink. Stirring would not emulsify the egg white, and with no ice the drink is neither chilled nor diluted.":"搖盪也是把蛋白打發所必需的。蘇打水會把酸酒變成 Collins 類的長飲。攪拌無法讓蛋白乳化，而不加冰的話，飲品既沒有冰鎮也沒有稀釋。","Which of these spirits is normally NOT matured in oak?":"下列哪一種烈酒通常不在橡木中熟成？","A VSOP Cognac from a single sub-region":"來自單一子產區的 VSOP Cognac","A vintage Bas Armagnac":"年份 Bas Armagnac","Calvados, Cognac and vintage Armagnac all mature in oak: Cognac for at least two years, vintage Armagnac often for a very long time. The trap is thinking a sub-region or vintage changes the relationship with wood: it does not.":"Calvados、Cognac 和年份 Armagnac 都在橡木中熟成：Cognac 至少兩年，年份 Armagnac 往往非常久。陷阱在於以為子產區或年份會改變與木頭的關係：並不會。","Which statement about pisco is NOT correct?":"關於 pisco，下列哪一項不正確？","It is a pomace spirit, like grappa":"它是果渣烈酒，和 grappa 一樣","It is distilled in pot stills":"它在壺式蒸餾器中蒸餾","It comes from aromatic grapes, mainly of the Muscat family":"它來自芳香型葡萄，主要是蜜思嘉家族","Most pisco is bottled without any ageing":"大多數 pisco 不經任何陳年就裝瓶","Pisco is a grape brandy made from wine of aromatic grapes, not from skins.":"pisco 是用芳香型葡萄的葡萄酒製成的葡萄白蘭地，不是用葡萄皮。","That is why pisco shows pure fruit and floral aromas rather than the herbaceous, spicy notes of pomace. The other statements are true: pot stills, aromatic grapes and, mostly, no ageing.":"所以 pisco 表現出純淨的果香和花香，而不是果渣的草本、香料氣息。其他幾項都正確：壺式蒸餾器、芳香型葡萄，以及大多不陳年。","Besides Chile and Peru, which countries are noted for unaged grape and pomace brandies?":"除了智利和秘魯，哪些國家以未陳年的葡萄和果渣白蘭地聞名？","Spain, South Africa and Mexico":"西班牙、南非和墨西哥","Scotland, Ireland and Japan":"蘇格蘭、愛爾蘭和日本","Canada, the USA and Jamaica":"加拿大、美國和牙買加","Norway, Sweden and Finland, with their flavoured spirits":"挪威、瑞典和芬蘭，以及它們的調味烈酒","Spain, South Africa and Mexico are notable examples of young grape and pomace brandies.":"西班牙、南非和墨西哥是年輕葡萄和果渣白蘭地值得注意的例子。","Scotland, Ireland and Japan are known above all for whisky, as are Canada and the USA, while Jamaica is known for rum. The Nordic countries are not a benchmark for grape brandies.":"蘇格蘭、愛爾蘭和日本最為人所知的是威士忌，加拿大和美國也是，牙買加則以蘭姆酒聞名。北歐國家不是葡萄白蘭地的標竿。","Which area is renowned for spirits made from plums, cherries, strawberries and raspberries?":"哪個地區以李子、櫻桃、草莓和覆盆子製成的烈酒聞名？","Central Europe":"中歐","The Caribbean":"加勒比海","Normandy, alongside Calvados":"諾曼第，與 Calvados 並列","South America, next to Chilean and Peruvian pisco":"南美洲，與智利和秘魯的 pisco 並列","Spirits from these fruits are a speciality of Central Europe.":"用這些水果製成的烈酒是中歐的特產。","The Caribbean is tied to rum. Normandy is the land of apple and pear brandy, and South America of grape-based pisco. None of these is the benchmark for plums and berries.":"加勒比海與蘭姆酒相連。諾曼第是蘋果和梨白蘭地的產地，南美洲則是以葡萄為原料的 pisco。它們都不是李子和莓果烈酒的標竿。","What are Central European fruit spirits prized for?":"中歐的水果烈酒因什麼而受珍視？","Expressiveness and purity":"表現力和純淨度","Long oak ageing and rancio notes":"長期橡木桶陳年和 rancio 氣息","The herbaceous, spicy notes typical of grape pomace":"葡萄果渣典型的草本、香料氣息","Strong sweetness, close to a liqueur":"強烈的甜味，接近利口酒","They are valued for the expressiveness and purity of the fruit.":"它們因水果的表現力和純淨度而受到重視。","These spirits usually rest in inert vessels, so oak and rancio are not their signature. Herbaceous notes are typical of pomace spirits. Liqueur-like sweetness is not part of this style.":"這些烈酒通常在惰性容器中靜置，所以橡木和 rancio 不是它們的標誌。草本氣息是果渣烈酒的典型特徵。利口酒般的甜味不屬於這種風格。","In a blind tasting, a colourless spirit shows intense floral and fresh grape aromas, with no herbaceous or oak notes. What is it most likely to be?":"在一場盲品中，一款無色烈酒表現出濃郁的花香和新鮮葡萄香氣，沒有草本或橡木氣息。它最可能是什麼？","A pisco":"pisco","A classic grappa from neutral grapes":"用中性葡萄做的經典 grappa","A VS Cognac":"VS Cognac","A young Calvados just out of its large oak vessels":"剛離開大型橡木容器的年輕 Calvados","Aromatic grapes, pot stills and no wood: pisco gives pure, floral and fruity grape aromas.":"芳香型葡萄、壺式蒸餾器、不用木頭：pisco 帶來純淨的花香和果香型葡萄香氣。","A grappa from neutral grapes would show pronounced herbaceous notes from the skins. VS Cognac and Calvados both see oak, so they would have colour; the Cognac would show oak notes and the Calvados would smell of apple, not grape.":"用中性葡萄做的 grappa 會表現出來自果皮的明顯草本氣息。VS Cognac 和 Calvados 都經過橡木，所以會有顏色；Cognac 會有橡木氣息，Calvados 聞起來則是蘋果，不是葡萄。","What is the main raw material difference between pisco and grappa?":"pisco 和 grappa 在原料上的主要差別是什麼？","Pisco comes from wine of aromatic grapes, grappa from pomace":"pisco 來自芳香型葡萄釀的葡萄酒，grappa 來自果渣","Both come from pomace":"兩者都來自果渣","Pisco comes from apples and grappa from fermented grape juice":"pisco 來自蘋果，grappa 來自發酵的葡萄汁","Grappa uses only Muscat juice, pisco only black pomace":"grappa 只用蜜思嘉的汁，pisco 只用紅葡萄果渣","Pisco is a wine brandy, grappa a pomace spirit: both from grapes, but from different parts.":"pisco 是葡萄酒白蘭地，grappa 是果渣烈酒：兩者都來自葡萄，但用的部位不同。","That is why grappa has herbaceous notes while pisco relies on pure fruit and flowers. Muscat is shared by both, but in grappa it is the pomace that is distilled, not the juice. Neither comes from apples.":"所以 grappa 有草本氣息，pisco 則仰賴純淨的果香和花香。兩者都會用蜜思嘉，但 grappa 蒸餾的是果渣，不是葡萄汁。兩者都不來自蘋果。","Which comparison between the grapes for Cognac and for pisco is correct?":"關於 Cognac 和 pisco 所用的葡萄，下列哪一項比較是正確的？","Cognac: acidic, neutral Ugni Blanc; pisco: aromatic Muscat-family grapes":"Cognac：酸度高、中性的白玉霓；pisco：芳香的蜜思嘉家族葡萄","Both use neutral grapes":"兩者都用中性葡萄","Both use highly aromatic grapes":"兩者都用香氣濃郁的葡萄","Cognac mainly uses Muscat, pisco mainly Ugni Blanc":"Cognac 主要用蜜思嘉，pisco 主要用白玉霓","Cognac starts from a neutral grape whose finesse emerges in distillation; pisco picks aromatic grapes for an intense grape perfume.":"Cognac 從中性葡萄開始，細緻感在蒸餾中浮現；pisco 則挑選芳香型葡萄，以得到濃郁的葡萄香。","These are two opposite philosophies: aroma revealed by distillation and oak versus aroma coming straight from the grape. Options that make them the same or swap them are wrong.":"這是兩種相反的理念：一種是由蒸餾和橡木展現香氣，另一種是香氣直接來自葡萄。把兩者說成相同或對調的選項都是錯的。","Which pairing of spirit and usual maturation is correct?":"下列哪一組烈酒與常見熟成方式的配對是正確的？","Calvados: large oak vessels; Peruvian pisco: no wood":"Calvados：大型橡木容器；秘魯 pisco：不用木頭","Grappa: new oak; Calvados: stainless steel":"Grappa：新橡木桶；Calvados：不鏽鋼","Chilean pisco: many years in oak; grappa: charred casks":"智利 pisco：橡木桶中多年；grappa：炙燒過的桶","Calvados: glass; VS Cognac: steel":"Calvados：玻璃；VS Cognac：鋼","Calvados matures in large oak vessels; Peruvian pisco is unaged by law.":"Calvados 在大型橡木容器中熟成；秘魯 pisco 依法不得陳年。","Classic grappa never sees wood, and Calvados does not mature in steel. Chilean pisco, when it does see wood, stays there only briefly. Every Cognac, even VS, spends at least two years in oak.":"經典的 grappa 從不接觸木頭，Calvados 也不在鋼中熟成。智利 pisco 即使過木桶，也只短暫停留。每款 Cognac，即使是 VS，都在橡木桶中至少兩年。","Which two features do all of the world's whiskies share?":"全世界的威士忌都有哪兩項共同特徵？","They are made from grain and matured in oak":"用穀物製成，並在橡木桶中熟成","They are distilled twice in pot stills only":"只在壺式蒸餾器中蒸餾兩次","They are made from malted barley and smoked with peat":"用麥芽大麥製成，並以泥煤煙燻","They spend at least four years in new barrels":"在新桶中存放至少四年","Grain and oak maturation are what every whisky has in common.":"穀物和橡木桶熟成是所有威士忌的共同點。","Beyond these two points, whiskies vary enormously: grains, still types and casks change from country to country. Many whiskies use column stills, not only pot stills, and peat is a choice rather than a rule. New barrels are compulsory for bourbon but rare in Scotland.":"除了這兩點，威士忌的差異極大：穀物、蒸餾器類型和桶都因國家而異。許多威士忌使用柱式蒸餾器，不只是壺式蒸餾器，泥煤則是一種選擇，不是規定。新桶對 bourbon 是強制規定，在蘇格蘭卻很少見。","Why is barley malted before whisky is made?":"為什麼製作威士忌前要先把大麥製麥？","To develop enzymes that turn starch into sugar":"產生能把澱粉轉化為糖的酵素","To raise the amount of protein in the grain":"提高穀物中的蛋白質含量","To get rid of the wild yeasts living on the outer husk of the grain":"去除附在穀粒外殼上的野生酵母","To give the whisky its golden colour straight away":"立刻賦予威士忌金黃的顏色","Sprouting produces enzymes that later convert the grain's starch into fermentable sugar.":"發芽會產生酵素，之後把穀物的澱粉轉化為可發酵的糖。","Yeast ferments sugar, not starch, so without enzymes there would be no fermentation. Malting does not colour the whisky, which gets its colour in the barrel, nor does it remove yeasts. Protein content is not what the distiller is after.":"酵母發酵的是糖，不是澱粉，所以沒有酵素就不會有發酵。製麥不會為威士忌上色（顏色是在桶中得到的），也不會去除酵母。蛋白質含量不是蒸餾師追求的東西。","What is green malt?":"什麼是綠麥芽？","Sprouted barley that has not yet been heated":"已發芽但尚未加熱的大麥","Barley harvested before it is fully ripe":"完全成熟前就採收的大麥","Malted barley that has already been smoked over a peat fire":"已經用泥煤火煙燻過的麥芽大麥","The grain residue left after distillation":"蒸餾後剩下的穀物殘渣","Green malt is barley that has begun to sprout, before the heating that stops growth.":"綠麥芽是已開始發芽、但尚未經過停止生長的加熱步驟的大麥。","'Green' refers to a stage, not to colour or ripeness in the field. Peat can be used precisely while the green malt is being heated, so smoked malt is already malted barley. The residue left after distillation is something else entirely.":"「綠」指的是一個階段，不是顏色或田間的成熟度。泥煤正是可以在加熱綠麥芽時使用，所以煙燻麥芽已經是麥芽大麥了。蒸餾後剩下的殘渣則完全是另一回事。","By heating the grains":"加熱穀粒","By adding yeast to the grains":"在穀粒中加入酵母","By soaking the grains in cold water":"把穀粒浸泡在冷水中","By keeping the grains in the dark for several weeks":"把穀粒放在黑暗中幾個星期","Heat kills the young plant while keeping the enzymes it has made.":"熱會殺死幼芽，同時保留它產生的酵素。","After a few days the young plant has made enough enzymes and must be stopped, or it would use up the starch to grow. Water and damp are used at the start to trigger sprouting; yeast comes in only later, on the sugary wort. Darkness would not stop germination.":"幾天後幼芽已產生足夠的酵素，必須讓它停止，否則它會耗用澱粉來生長。水和濕氣是在一開始用來觸發發芽的；酵母要到之後才加入含糖的麥汁中。黑暗並不會停止發芽。","What is the sweet liquid made by mixing ground malted barley with warm water called?":"把磨碎的麥芽大麥與溫水混合而成的甜液叫做什麼？","Malt syrup":"麥芽糖漿","Wort is the sugary liquid that will be fermented and then distilled.":"麥汁是之後要發酵再蒸餾的含糖液體。","The mash bill is the grain recipe, not the liquid. Sour mash is an American technique that adds the acidic still residue back to the fermenter. Malt syrup is not a term used at this stage of production.":"mash bill 是穀物配方，不是液體。sour mash 是美國的一種技術，把蒸餾器的酸性殘液加回發酵槽。麥芽糖漿不是這個生產階段使用的術語。","How are corn and rye usually prepared so that sugar can be obtained from them?":"玉米和黑麥通常怎麼處理，才能從中得到糖？","They are cooked, then malted barley is added":"先烹煮，再加入麥芽大麥","They are malted like barley, then smoked":"像大麥一樣製麥，再煙燻","They are fermented whole, without being ground or cooked first":"不磨碎也不烹煮，整粒發酵","They are mixed with cane sugar before fermenting":"發酵前與蔗糖混合","Cooking makes the starch soluble, then enzymes from malted barley turn it into sugar.":"烹煮讓澱粉變得可溶，接著麥芽大麥的酵素把它轉化為糖。","As a rule, barley is malted while other grains are cooked at high temperature. Whole grains would not yield sugar on their own; enzymes are needed. Adding cane sugar is not part of whisky making.":"一般來說，大麥用製麥，其他穀物則以高溫烹煮。整粒穀物本身不會產生糖；需要酵素。添加蔗糖不屬於威士忌的製程。","Why does a bourbon, though made mostly from corn, contain a small share of malted barley?":"為什麼 bourbon 雖然主要用玉米製成，卻含有少量的麥芽大麥？","For its enzymes":"為了它的酵素","To add smoky notes":"增添煙燻氣息","To lighten the final colour":"讓最後的顏色變淺","To meet a minimum barley share that the law requires":"符合法律規定的最低大麥比例","Malted barley's enzymes convert the starch of the cooked grains into sugar.":"麥芽大麥的酵素把烹煮過的穀物的澱粉轉化為糖。","Only a little is needed, as the barley's enzymes are enough for all the starch. The bourbon rule concerns corn (at least 51%), not a barley share. Peat smoke is not typical of bourbon, and barley is not used to change colour.":"只需要一點點，因為大麥的酵素足以處理所有的澱粉。bourbon 的規定針對的是玉米（至少 51%），不是大麥的比例。泥煤煙不是 bourbon 的典型特徵，大麥也不是用來改變顏色的。","In American whiskey, what is the mash bill?":"在美國威士忌中，mash bill 是什麼？","The combination of grains used":"所用穀物的組合","The tax document that travels with each barrel":"隨每個桶附帶的稅務文件","The minimum time spent in barrel":"在桶中的最短時間","The acidic residue put back into the fermenter":"放回發酵槽的酸性殘液","The mash bill is the grain recipe that shapes the whiskey's style.":"mash bill 是決定威士忌風格的穀物配方。","Each distillery chooses its proportions of corn, rye, wheat and malted barley to get its style. The acidic residue put back into fermentation is sour mash, a different label term. Maturation time is linked to terms such as straight.":"每家蒸餾廠自行決定玉米、黑麥、小麥和麥芽大麥的比例，以做出自己的風格。放回發酵的酸性殘液是 sour mash，那是另一個酒標術語。熟成時間則與 straight 這類術語有關。","What is the minimum share of corn in the grains of a bourbon?":"bourbon 的穀物中，玉米的最低比例是多少？","A bourbon must be made from at least 51% corn.":"bourbon 必須用至少 51% 的玉米製成。","The 51% figure makes corn the dominant grain while leaving room for flavouring grains such as rye and wheat. 100% corn would leave no room for the malted barley needed for enzymes. 40% is the minimum bottling strength in the USA, not a grain share.":"51% 這個數字讓玉米成為主要穀物，同時為黑麥和小麥等調味穀物留出空間。100% 玉米就沒有空間容納提供酵素所需的麥芽大麥。40% 是美國的最低裝瓶濃度，不是穀物比例。","Where can bourbon be produced?":"bourbon 可以在哪裡生產？","Only in the state of Kentucky":"只能在肯塔基州","Only in Kentucky and the neighbouring state of Tennessee":"只能在肯塔基州和相鄰的田納西州","In any country in North America":"北美洲的任何國家","Bourbon can be made anywhere in the USA, even though almost all of it comes from Kentucky.":"bourbon 可以在美國任何地方製作，雖然幾乎全都來自肯塔基州。","The link with Kentucky is historical and commercial, not a legal requirement. Tennessee has its own category, Tennessee Whiskey, with extra rules. Bourbon is a product of the USA, so a Canadian whisky cannot use the name.":"與肯塔基州的連結是歷史和商業上的，不是法律要求。田納西州有自己的類別 Tennessee Whiskey，並有額外的規定。bourbon 是美國的產品，所以加拿大威士忌不能使用這個名稱。","In what type of barrel must bourbon be matured?":"bourbon 必須在哪一種桶中熟成？","Oak that previously held Sherry":"先前裝過 Sherry 的橡木桶","Oak casks that were already used for another whiskey":"已經用於其他威士忌的橡木桶","Inert stainless steel vessels":"惰性的不鏽鋼容器","The law requires new, charred oak barrels.":"法律規定使用炙燒過的新橡木桶。","New oak gives lots of colour and flavour, which is part of why bourbon tastes so bold. Because these barrels cannot be reused for bourbon, many end up in Scotland. Ex-Sherry casks are typical of Scotch, and steel would give neither colour nor oak flavour.":"新橡木桶帶來大量顏色和風味，這是 bourbon 風味如此強勁的部分原因。因為這些桶不能再用於 bourbon，許多最後都到了蘇格蘭。Sherry 桶是 Scotch 的典型做法，鋼則不會帶來顏色或橡木風味。","Which aromas does new charred oak typically give to bourbon?":"炙燒過的新橡木桶通常為 bourbon 帶來哪些香氣？","Vanilla, coconut and sweet spice":"香草、椰子和甜香料","Peat smoke, iodine and seaweed":"泥煤煙、碘和海藻","Dried fruit, orange peel and sun-dried raisins":"果乾、橙皮和日曬葡萄乾","Cut grass, pear and white flowers":"青草、梨和白花","New oak is rich in compounds that recall vanilla, coconut and sweet spice.":"新橡木富含讓人聯想到香草、椰子和甜香料的化合物。","A barrel gives the most flavour the first time it is used. Peat smoke comes from the malt, not the barrel, and dried fruit and orange peel are linked more with ex-Sherry casks. Grassy and floral notes belong to young, light spirits.":"桶子第一次使用時給的風味最多。泥煤煙來自麥芽，不是桶；果乾和橙皮則多與 Sherry 桶有關。青草和花香氣息屬於年輕、清淡的烈酒。","What is the maximum strength to which bourbon may be distilled?":"bourbon 最高可以蒸餾到多少濃度？","80% abv (160 proof)":"80% abv（160 proof）","95% abv (190 proof)":"95% abv（190 proof）","40% abv (80 proof)":"40% abv（80 proof）","No limit, as long as it is later diluted with water":"沒有限制，只要之後加水稀釋","Bourbon cannot be distilled above 80% abv, so that plenty of flavour is kept.":"bourbon 的蒸餾濃度不得超過 80% abv，這樣才能保留豐富的風味。","The higher the distillation strength, the more neutral the spirit becomes. A low limit keeps congeners and helps create bourbon's bold style. 95% abv is close to light or neutral spirits, and 40% abv is a bottling strength.":"蒸餾濃度越高，烈酒越中性。較低的上限能保留同屬物，有助於形成 bourbon 強勁的風格。95% abv 接近清淡或中性的烈酒，40% abv 則是裝瓶濃度。","Which combination of rules best explains bourbon's bold flavours and warming texture?":"哪一組規定最能解釋 bourbon 強勁的風味和溫熱的口感？","Lots of corn, low distillation strength, new oak":"大量玉米、低蒸餾濃度、新橡木桶","Peated malted barley, short pot stills and ex-Sherry casks":"泥煤麥芽大麥、矮壺式蒸餾器和 Sherry 桶","High-strength distillation and long filtering through activated charcoal":"高濃度蒸餾和長時間的活性碳過濾","Triple distillation and unmalted barley":"三次蒸餾和未發芽大麥","High corn, lightly rectified spirit and new oak together give a rich, warming whiskey.":"高比例玉米、精餾程度低的烈酒和新橡木桶，共同造就豐富而溫熱的威士忌。","Low distillation strength keeps many congeners and new oak adds lots of flavour. Peat, pot stills and ex-Sherry casks describe malt Scotch instead, while triple distillation and unmalted barley are Irish traits. High strength and activated charcoal would push towards a neutral spirit.":"低蒸餾濃度保留許多同屬物，新橡木桶則增添大量風味。泥煤、壺式蒸餾器和 Sherry 桶描述的是麥芽 Scotch，三次蒸餾和未發芽大麥則是愛爾蘭的特徵。高濃度和活性碳會把酒推向中性烈酒。","What does rye bring when it is included in a bourbon recipe?":"黑麥加入 bourbon 的配方時，會帶來什麼？","Spicy, rye-bread notes":"辛香、黑麥麵包的氣息","A soft, smooth character":"柔和、順口的特色","The enzymes needed to convert the other grains' starch":"轉化其他穀物澱粉所需的酵素","Sweetcorn aromas":"甜玉米香氣","Rye is a flavouring grain that adds spice and rye-bread notes.":"黑麥是調味穀物，增添辛香和黑麥麵包氣息。","Each grain in the mash bill has a role: softness comes from wheat, enzymes from malted barley and sweetcorn aromas from the corn itself. The more rye, the more peppery the bourbon.":"mash bill 中的每種穀物都有自己的角色：柔和來自小麥，酵素來自麥芽大麥，甜玉米香氣來自玉米本身。黑麥越多，bourbon 的胡椒味越重。","A distiller wants a softer, rounder bourbon. Which flavouring grain suits this best?":"一位蒸餾師想要更柔和、更圓潤的 bourbon。哪一種調味穀物最合適？","Barley malted over a peat fire":"用泥煤火製麥的大麥","Wheat contributes a soft, smooth character.":"小麥帶來柔和、順口的特色。","Rye would go the other way, towards a spicy, peppery profile. Peated malt would add smoke, and unmalted barley is linked mainly with Irish whiskey, giving spicy and oily notes.":"黑麥會往相反的方向走，偏向辛香、帶胡椒味的輪廓。泥煤麥芽會增添煙燻味，未發芽大麥則主要與愛爾蘭威士忌有關，帶來辛香和油潤的氣息。","Why does bourbon matured in Kentucky gain colour faster than Scotch matured in Scotland?":"為什麼在肯塔基州熟成的 bourbon 比在蘇格蘭熟成的 Scotch 更快上色？","Hot summers speed up the exchange between spirit and wood":"炎熱的夏天加快了烈酒與木頭之間的交換","Much more caramel is added in Kentucky":"肯塔基州加了多得多的焦糖色","Corn is a darker grain than barley":"玉米是比大麥顏色更深的穀物","American barrels are much smaller than Scottish casks":"美國的桶比蘇格蘭的桶小得多","Heat makes the spirit move in and out of the staves more quickly.":"熱讓烈酒更快地進出桶板。","Warehouse temperature is a key choice: the warmer it is, the more colour and flavour the wood gives. Bourbon's new barrels also give more colour than the used casks of Scotland. Straight bourbon cannot have added colour, and colour does not come from the grain.":"酒庫的溫度是關鍵的選擇：越溫暖，木頭給的顏色和風味越多。bourbon 的新桶給的顏色也比蘇格蘭的舊桶多。straight bourbon 不能添加色素，而顏色也不是來自穀物。","What is the Lincoln County Process?":"什麼是 Lincoln County Process？","Filtering new spirit through maple charcoal before barrelling":"新酒入桶前先用楓木炭過濾","Charring the inside of barrels with maple wood":"用楓木炙燒桶的內部","Adding the acidic still residue back to the fermenter":"把蒸餾器的酸性殘液加回發酵槽","Finishing the whiskey in Port casks for a few months":"把威士忌放在 Port 桶中過桶幾個月","It is the maple-charcoal filtering required for Tennessee Whiskey.":"它是 Tennessee Whiskey 規定的楓木炭過濾。","The filtering happens on freshly made spirit, before it enters the barrel. Adding acidic residue back to fermentation is sour mash, and finishing in wine casks is wood finishing, more typical of Scotch. Charring barrels is a separate step.":"過濾的對象是剛做好的新酒，在入桶之前。把酸性殘液加回發酵是 sour mash，在葡萄酒桶中過桶則是 wood finishing，更常見於 Scotch。炙燒桶子是另一個步驟。","What is the main purpose of charcoal filtering for Tennessee Whiskey?":"Tennessee Whiskey 用木炭過濾的主要目的是什麼？","To soften the spirit before it goes into barrel":"在入桶前讓烈酒變柔和","To strip all the colour from the whiskey after barrel ageing":"在桶陳後去除威士忌的所有顏色","To add a smoky peat aroma":"增添泥煤的煙燻香氣","To raise the alcoholic strength":"提高酒精濃度","The charcoal smooths the young spirit's rough edges, so it goes into barrel softer.":"木炭磨去年輕烈酒的粗糙稜角，讓它更柔和地入桶。","Filtering happens before maturation, so it does not remove the colour the whiskey later gains in barrel. Maple charcoal adds no peat smoke, and filtering does not raise strength. The typical result is a notably smooth whiskey.":"過濾在熟成之前進行，所以不會去除威士忌之後在桶中得到的顏色。楓木炭不會增添泥煤煙，過濾也不會提高濃度。典型的成果是格外柔順的威士忌。","Which statement about Tennessee Whiskey is correct?":"關於 Tennessee Whiskey，下列哪一項正確？","It must be made in Tennessee, from at least 51% corn":"必須在田納西州製作，玉米至少 51%","It must contain at least 51% rye and be matured in used barrels":"必須含至少 51% 的黑麥，並在舊桶中熟成","It can be made anywhere in the USA":"可以在美國任何地方製作","It is distilled only in pot stills":"只用壺式蒸餾器蒸餾","Tennessee Whiskey follows bourbon's basic rules but is tied to the state of Tennessee.":"Tennessee Whiskey 遵循 bourbon 的基本規定，但與田納西州綁在一起。","Like bourbon, it uses at least 51% corn and new charred oak, and adds charcoal filtering. It is bourbon, not Tennessee Whiskey, that can be made anywhere in the USA. A 51% rye share defines rye whiskey.":"和 bourbon 一樣，它使用至少 51% 的玉米和炙燒過的新橡木桶，再加上木炭過濾。可以在美國任何地方製作的是 bourbon，不是 Tennessee Whiskey。51% 的黑麥比例定義的是 rye whiskey。","What legally separates an American rye whiskey from a bourbon?":"在法律上，美國的 rye whiskey 與 bourbon 有什麼區別？","At least 51% of the grain is rye":"穀物中至少 51% 是黑麥","It is matured in used oak casks":"在舊橡木桶中熟成","It is filtered through maple charcoal before it goes into barrel":"入桶前用楓木炭過濾","It is only made in Canada":"只在加拿大製作","Rye follows the bourbon method, but with rye as the main grain.":"Rye 沿用 bourbon 的做法，但以黑麥為主要穀物。","Otherwise production is almost identical, including the use of new charred barrels. Charcoal filtering is the Tennessee Whiskey trait. Canada has its own 'rye' with different rules, but American rye whiskey is made in the USA.":"除此之外製程幾乎相同，包括使用炙燒過的新桶。木炭過濾是 Tennessee Whiskey 的特徵。加拿大有自己的「rye」，規定不同，但美國的 rye whiskey 是在美國製作的。","A customer wants an American whiskey with notes of spice, lemon zest and rye bread. What should be suggested?":"一位顧客想要一款帶香料、檸檬皮和黑麥麵包氣息的美國威士忌。應該推薦什麼？","A rye whiskey":"Rye whiskey","A wheat-heavy bourbon":"小麥比例高的 bourbon","A Tennessee Whiskey with a soft, sweetcorn-led profile":"柔和、以甜玉米為主的 Tennessee Whiskey","An unaged corn whiskey":"未陳年的玉米威士忌","Spice, lemon zest and rye bread are the hallmarks of rye whiskey.":"香料、檸檬皮和黑麥麵包是 rye whiskey 的標誌。","The high rye share gives a lively, peppery profile. Wheat would make a bourbon softer, and Tennessee Whiskey is known for sweetcorn, vanilla and smoothness. A young corn whiskey would be dominated by sweet grain.":"高比例的黑麥帶來活潑、帶胡椒味的輪廓。小麥會讓 bourbon 更柔和，Tennessee Whiskey 則以甜玉米、香草和柔順著稱。年輕的玉米威士忌會以甜美的穀物味為主。","What does the word 'straight' guarantee on a bourbon label?":"bourbon 酒標上的「straight」保證什麼？","At least 2 years in new oak, no added colour or flavour":"在新橡木桶中至少 2 年，不添加色素或香料","Bottled undiluted, at the strength it came out of the cask":"未經稀釋，以出桶時的濃度裝瓶","Whiskey from a single barrel":"來自單一桶的威士忌","Distillation in a single pass":"只蒸餾一次","Straight means at least two years in new barrels with nothing added for colour or flavour.":"Straight 表示在新桶中至少兩年，而且沒有添加任何增色或增味的東西。","If a straight bourbon contains whiskey under four years old, its age must be stated. One barrel is 'single barrel', and undiluted bottling is shown with other terms. Straight says nothing about the number of distillations.":"如果 straight bourbon 含有不滿四年的威士忌，就必須標示年數。單一桶是「single barrel」，未稀釋裝瓶則用其他術語表示。Straight 與蒸餾次數無關。","An American label reads '90 proof'. What is the alcoholic strength?":"一張美國酒標上寫著「90 proof」。酒精濃度是多少？","40% abv":"40% abv","50% abv":"50% abv","Two degrees of proof equal 1% abv, so 90 proof is 45% abv.":"2 度 proof 等於 1% abv，所以 90 proof 是 45% abv。","Simply halve the proof figure. 90% abv would mean confusing the two scales, while 40% abv is 80 proof and 50% abv is 100 proof.":"只要把 proof 的數字除以二。90% abv 是把兩種標度搞混了，40% abv 是 80 proof，50% abv 是 100 proof。","What does 'sour mash' mean on an American whiskey label?":"美國威士忌酒標上的「sour mash」是什麼意思？","Acidic residue from the still was added back to the fermenter":"蒸餾器的酸性殘液被加回發酵槽","The whiskey has a deliberately sour taste":"這款威士忌刻意做成酸的味道","Lemon juice was added just before the whiskey was bottled":"威士忌裝瓶前加了檸檬汁","A technique required for every bourbon":"每款 bourbon 都必須使用的技術","Sour mash means reusing the acidic residue from the base of the column still in fermentation.":"Sour mash 指的是把柱式蒸餾器底部的酸性殘液重新用於發酵。","The technique is widely used but not required by law. The name does not describe the taste of the finished whiskey, which is not sour, and has nothing to do with adding citrus.":"這項技術使用很廣，但法律並未強制。這個名稱不是在描述成品威士忌的味道（它並不酸），也與添加柑橘無關。","Which of these American label terms has NO legal definition?":"下列美國酒標術語中，哪一個沒有法律定義？","How small a 'small batch' must be is not set by law.":"「small batch」要多小，法律並沒有規定。","Small batch means a blend of a few selected casks, but the number is up to the producer. Straight, bourbon and Tennessee Whiskey, by contrast, have precise rules on grain, barrels, place or ageing time. Single barrel, for its part, means one cask judged exceptional.":"Small batch 指的是少數精選桶的調和，但桶數由生產者決定。Straight、bourbon 和 Tennessee Whiskey 則對穀物、桶、產地或陳年時間有明確的規定。至於 single barrel，指的是被評為特別出色的單一桶。","In botanical terms, what are the cereals used to make whisky?":"從植物學來說，用來製作威士忌的穀物是什麼？","The seeds of various species of grass":"各種禾本科植物的種子","The swollen roots of perennial plants":"多年生植物膨大的根","The sugary stems of tropical plants grown for several years":"種植數年的熱帶植物含糖的莖","The fleshy heart of succulent plants":"多肉植物肉質的心","Each grain is the seed of a grass, able to grow into a new plant.":"每一粒穀物都是禾本科植物的種子，能長成新的植株。","Barley, corn, wheat and rye are all grasses. Sugary stems describe sugar cane (rum) and the fleshy heart describes agave (Tequila, Mezcal). Roots play no part in whisky.":"大麥、玉米、小麥和黑麥都是禾本科植物。含糖的莖說的是甘蔗（蘭姆酒），肉質的心說的是龍舌蘭（Tequila、Mezcal）。根在威士忌中沒有角色。","Why does a cereal grain hold a store of starch?":"為什麼穀粒中儲存著澱粉？","To feed the young plant until it has grown its own leaves":"在幼苗長出自己的葉子之前供給養分","To protect the grain from insects while it is stored over winter":"在冬季儲存期間保護穀粒不受昆蟲侵害","To attract wild yeasts":"吸引野生酵母","To give the grain its colour":"賦予穀粒顏色","Starch is the energy reserve that feeds the sprout in its first days.":"澱粉是幼芽最初幾天的能量儲備。","The distiller exploits exactly this reserve: once turned into sugar, starch becomes fermentable. Yeasts are not drawn to starch, which they cannot use, and starch neither colours nor protects the grain.":"蒸餾師利用的正是這份儲備：澱粉一旦變成糖，就可以發酵。酵母不會被澱粉吸引，因為它們無法利用澱粉；澱粉也不會為穀粒上色或提供保護。","Which of these cereals is NOT one of the four main whisky grains?":"下列哪一種穀物不屬於威士忌的四種主要穀物？","Oats":"燕麥","The four key grains are barley, corn, wheat and rye.":"四種關鍵穀物是大麥、玉米、小麥和黑麥。","Rye, wheat and corn appear in American and Canadian recipes, and barley dominates in Scotland and Ireland. The law often decides which grains a category may use.":"黑麥、小麥和玉米出現在美國和加拿大的配方中，大麥則在蘇格蘭和愛爾蘭占主導地位。某個類別可以使用哪些穀物，往往由法律決定。","When corn is cooked, what does the heat do to its starch?":"烹煮玉米時，熱對它的澱粉有什麼作用？","It makes it soluble":"讓它變得可溶","It turns it straight into alcohol, with no need for yeast":"直接把它變成酒精，不需要酵母","It destroys it completely":"把它完全破壞","It caramelises it":"讓它焦糖化","Cooking at high temperature dissolves the starch into the liquid, ready for the enzymes.":"高溫烹煮讓澱粉溶入液體，準備好讓酵素作用。","Cooking produces neither sugar nor alcohol: the enzymes of malted barley and then yeast are still needed. If the starch were destroyed or caramelised, there would be nothing left to turn into sugar.":"烹煮既不產生糖，也不產生酒精：仍然需要麥芽大麥的酵素，再加上酵母。如果澱粉被破壞或焦糖化，就沒有東西可以轉化為糖了。","What is the correct order for getting sugar from corn?":"從玉米取得糖的正確順序是什麼？","Grind, cook in water, cool, add malted barley":"磨碎、在水中烹煮、冷卻、加入麥芽大麥","Sprout, heat, grind, add yeast":"發芽、加熱、磨碎、加入酵母","Grind, add malted barley, cook for a long time at high heat, cool":"磨碎、加入麥芽大麥、長時間高溫烹煮、冷卻","Cook the whole grain, distil, then grind":"整粒烹煮、蒸餾，再磨碎","Corn is ground and cooked; once the liquid has cooled, malted barley is added for its enzymes.":"玉米先磨碎並烹煮；液體冷卻後，再加入麥芽大麥以取得酵素。","Sprouting and heating describes malting barley, not handling corn. Adding the malted barley before cooking exposes it to the heat, whereas it goes into the cooled liquid. Nothing is distilled before sugar has been obtained and fermented.":"發芽和加熱描述的是大麥的製麥，不是玉米的處理。在烹煮前加入麥芽大麥會讓它受熱，而它其實是加進冷卻後的液體裡。在取得糖並發酵之前，不會蒸餾任何東西。","During malting, what conditions is the barley kept in so that it starts to sprout?":"製麥時，大麥要放在什麼環境中才會開始發芽？","Somewhere warm and damp":"溫暖潮濕的地方","In a cold, dry room, in the dark for weeks":"寒冷乾燥的房間，在黑暗中放幾個星期","Soaked in alcohol":"浸泡在酒精中","Over a peat fire":"在泥煤火上","Warmth and moisture wake the grain up, so it sprouts and releases enzymes.":"溫暖和濕氣喚醒穀粒，讓它發芽並釋放酵素。","Cold and dry keep the grain dormant, the opposite of what is wanted. Fire (peat or otherwise) only comes at the end, to stop the green malt growing. Alcohol would kill the sprout.":"寒冷和乾燥讓穀粒保持休眠，與所需的相反。火（不論是不是泥煤）只在最後才用，以停止綠麥芽的生長。酒精會殺死幼芽。","Roughly how long does the sprouting stage of malting last?":"製麥的發芽階段大約持續多久？","A few days":"幾天","A few minutes":"幾分鐘","Several months, until the first leaves appear":"好幾個月，直到長出第一批葉子","Three years":"三年","After a few days the plant has made its enzymes and growth is stopped.":"幾天後植株已產生酵素，生長就被停止。","A few minutes would not be enough for the grain to sprout. Letting it grow for months would use up the starch the distiller wants to turn into sugar. Three years is Scotch's minimum maturation, nothing to do with malting.":"幾分鐘不夠讓穀粒發芽。讓它長好幾個月會耗盡蒸餾師想要轉化為糖的澱粉。三年是 Scotch 的最低熟成時間，與製麥無關。","The green malt has just been heated. What are the grains now called?":"綠麥芽剛剛加熱完成。這些穀粒現在叫做什麼？","Malted barley":"麥芽大麥","Barley mash bill":"大麥 mash bill","Heating ends malting: the grains have become malted barley.":"加熱讓製麥結束：穀粒已成為麥芽大麥。","Wort is the sweet liquid made later, by grinding the malted barley and mixing it with warm water. The mash bill is the grain recipe. Green malt is the name for the sprouted barley before it is heated.":"麥汁是之後把麥芽大麥磨碎並與溫水混合而成的甜液。mash bill 是穀物配方。綠麥芽是發芽大麥在加熱前的名稱。","Before it is mixed with warm water, what is malted barley turned into?":"與溫水混合之前，麥芽大麥要先變成什麼？","A coarse flour":"粗磨的粉","A very fine paste that has already fermented":"已經發酵的極細糊狀物","Toasted flakes":"烘烤過的麥片","Whole grains, left intact so no enzymes are lost":"保持完整的整粒穀物，以免損失酵素","Malted barley is ground into a coarse flour, then mixed with warm water.":"麥芽大麥先磨成粗粉，再與溫水混合。","Grinding opens the grain so the enzymes can reach the starch in the water; leaving it whole would make conversion far less effective. Fermentation only comes later, with the wort. Toasted flakes are not part of the process.":"磨碎能打開穀粒，讓酵素在水中接觸到澱粉；保持整粒會讓轉化的效果差很多。發酵要到之後才進行，對象是麥汁。烘烤麥片不屬於這個製程。","What often limits a whisky distiller's choice of grains, stills and length of ageing?":"威士忌蒸餾師對穀物、蒸餾器和陳年時間的選擇，往往受什麼限制？","The warehouse climate":"酒庫的氣候","The yeast strain available that season":"當季可取得的酵母菌株","The colour consumers expect to see in the glass":"消費者期望在杯中看到的顏色","Each country's law sets the permitted grains, still types and minimum ageing.":"各國法律規定了允許使用的穀物、蒸餾器類型和最低陳年時間。","Warehouse climate affects how fast a spirit matures, not the rules. Yeast and colour are technical or commercial choices but do not decide which grains or stills are allowed. Examples: 51% corn for bourbon, pot stills for Scottish single malt.":"酒庫的氣候影響的是烈酒熟成的速度，不是規定。酵母和顏色是技術或商業上的選擇，但不決定允許使用哪些穀物或蒸餾器。例子：bourbon 的 51% 玉米、蘇格蘭 single malt 的壺式蒸餾器。","In whisky blending, what are 'flavouring spirits'?":"在威士忌調和中，「調味烈酒」（flavouring spirits）是什麼？","Pronounced spirits blended with lighter spirits distilled to a higher strength":"香氣明顯的烈酒，用來與蒸餾到較高濃度的清淡烈酒調和","Flavourings added after distillation to adjust the taste":"蒸餾後添加、用來調整味道的香料","Neutral whiskies distilled to 96% abv that form the base of almost every blend":"蒸餾到 96% abv、構成幾乎所有調和酒基底的中性威士忌","Heads and tails recovered from the still":"從蒸餾器回收的酒頭和酒尾","They are characterful spirits that bring aroma to a lighter base.":"它們是特色鮮明的烈酒，為較清淡的基酒帶來香氣。","They are not added flavourings: they are real whiskies, just more intense. The light part is not a 96% neutral spirit, and heads and tails go back into the next distillation, not into the blend. Other producers use only pronounced spirits and find complexity through different ages or woods.":"它們不是添加的香料：它們是真正的威士忌，只是更濃郁。清淡的部分並不是 96% 的中性烈酒，而酒頭和酒尾是回到下一次蒸餾，不是進入調和。也有生產者只用香氣明顯的烈酒，透過不同的年數或木桶來取得複雜度。","Where is the vast majority of bourbon produced?":"絕大多數的 bourbon 在哪裡生產？","In Kentucky":"肯塔基州","In Tennessee":"田納西州","In Canada, near the US border":"加拿大，靠近美國邊界","In California":"加州","Bourbon may be made anywhere in the USA, but nearly all of it comes from Kentucky.":"bourbon 可以在美國任何地方製作，但幾乎全都來自肯塔基州。","Tennessee is the other big whiskey state, but it has its own category, Tennessee Whiskey. Bourbon must be made in the USA, so Canada is ruled out. California is not a traditional bourbon centre.":"田納西州是另一個威士忌大州，但它有自己的類別 Tennessee Whiskey。bourbon 必須在美國製作，所以加拿大被排除。加州不是傳統的 bourbon 中心。","Which type of still do most bourbon producers use?":"大多數 bourbon 生產者使用哪一種蒸餾器？","The pot still, with triple distillation":"壺式蒸餾器，三次蒸餾","A peat-fired pot still":"燒泥煤的壺式蒸餾器","No still: bourbon is made by maceration":"不用蒸餾器：bourbon 是浸漬而成的","Most bourbon comes from column stills, but at a deliberately low strength.":"大多數 bourbon 來自柱式蒸餾器，但刻意蒸餾到較低的濃度。","Triple pot distillation is the Irish malt tradition. Peat is used to smoke malt, not to heat stills. Every whisky is distilled, so maceration alone is not enough.":"壺式三次蒸餾是愛爾蘭麥芽威士忌的傳統。泥煤是用來煙燻麥芽的，不是用來加熱蒸餾器。所有威士忌都要蒸餾，所以光靠浸漬是不夠的。","In a Kentucky bourbon distillery, people talk about the 'beer still'. What is it?":"在肯塔基州的 bourbon 蒸餾廠，人們會提到「beer still」。它是什麼？","A column still":"柱式蒸餾器","The vat where wort is fermented to make beer for sale":"把麥汁發酵成啤酒來販售的槽","A small still for samples":"做樣品用的小型蒸餾器","The store for new barrels":"存放新桶的倉庫","It is the Kentucky name for the column in which the fermented liquid is distilled.":"它是肯塔基州對蒸餾發酵液的蒸餾柱的稱呼。","The fermented liquid is often called 'beer', hence the name, but the distillery does not sell beer. It is neither a sample still nor a warehouse. From outside it has no windows, but round fittings show where the plates are.":"發酵液常被稱為「beer」，名稱由此而來，但蒸餾廠並不賣啤酒。它既不是樣品蒸餾器，也不是倉庫。從外面看它沒有窗戶，但圓形的配件顯示出蒸餾板的位置。","On its own, what style of whiskey does corn tend to give?":"單獨使用時，玉米往往做出什麼風格的威士忌？","Fairly soft, with sweetcorn notes":"相當柔和，帶甜玉米氣息","Very spicy, with rye-bread and lemon-zest notes":"非常辛香，帶黑麥麵包和檸檬皮氣息","Smoky and medicinal":"煙燻且帶藥水味","Malty, with porridge notes":"麥芽味，帶麥片粥氣息","Corn gives a relatively soft spirit that smells of sweetcorn.":"玉米做出相對柔和、聞起來有甜玉米味的烈酒。","Spice and rye bread are typical of rye, medicinal smoke comes from peat and porridge from malted barley. Precisely because corn is soft, bourbon makers add 'flavouring grains' for extra character.":"辛香和黑麥麵包是黑麥的典型特徵，帶藥水味的煙燻來自泥煤，麥片粥來自麥芽大麥。正因為玉米柔和，bourbon 的生產者才加入「調味穀物」來增添特色。","In bourbon making, when are the different grains brought together?":"製作 bourbon 時，不同的穀物在什麼時候合在一起？","After malting or cooking, for starch conversion":"在製麥或烹煮之後，進行澱粉轉化時","Only after distillation, by blending spirits from different grains":"蒸餾後才合，把不同穀物的烈酒調和起來","In the barrel, during maturation":"在桶中，熟成期間","Once malted or cooked, the grains are mixed so the enzymes can convert all the starch.":"穀物經製麥或烹煮後就混合在一起，讓酵素轉化所有的澱粉。","The mash bill is set at the start: it is the mix of grains that ferments and is distilled together. Blending separate spirits, mixing in barrel or at bottling is not the bourbon method, and without malted barley mixed in with the other grains their starch would not be converted.":"mash bill 在一開始就確定：它是一起發酵、一起蒸餾的穀物組合。把分開的烈酒調和、在桶中或裝瓶時混合，都不是 bourbon 的做法；而且如果麥芽大麥沒有和其他穀物混在一起，那些穀物的澱粉就無法轉化。","Why does the low distillation strength required for bourbon add to its intense flavour?":"為什麼 bourbon 規定的低蒸餾濃度有助於它濃郁的風味？","Because more congeners stay in the spirit":"因為更多同屬物留在烈酒中","Because a low strength makes more water evaporate during distillation":"因為低濃度讓蒸餾時蒸發更多的水","Because sugar from the corn carries into the spirit":"因為玉米的糖被帶進烈酒","Because column stills add woody aroma":"因為柱式蒸餾器增添木質香氣","The lower the strength, the more aromatic compounds remain in the spirit.":"濃度越低，留在烈酒中的香氣化合物越多。","This is the general rule of distillation: high strength means less aroma. Sugar does not distil, so every new spirit is dry. Stills do not create woody aroma: that comes from the barrel.":"這是蒸餾的通則：濃度高就代表香氣少。糖無法蒸餾，所以所有新酒都是不甜的。蒸餾器不會產生木質香氣：那來自桶。","Why do bourbon's barrels give it so much flavour?":"為什麼 bourbon 的桶為它帶來這麼多風味？","Because they are new":"因為它們是新的","Because they held Sherry before reaching the distillery":"因為它們到蒸餾廠之前裝過 Sherry","Because they are made of maple":"因為它們是楓木做的","Because they are very large":"因為它們非常大","A barrel gives the most colour and flavour the first time it is used.":"桶子第一次使用時給的顏色和風味最多。","Bourbon must use new charred oak, never Sherry casks. Maple is used for the charcoal in the Lincoln County Process, not for barrels. A large barrel gives proportionally less flavour, not more.":"bourbon 必須使用炙燒過的新橡木桶，絕不用 Sherry 桶。楓木用於 Lincoln County Process 的木炭，不是做桶。大桶給的風味按比例是更少，而不是更多。","Which palate texture is typical of a bourbon?":"bourbon 典型的口感質地是什麼？","Warming, sometimes sharp":"溫熱，有時銳利","Watery and almost neutral, like a diluted vodka":"水感、近乎中性，像稀釋的伏特加","Sweet and creamy like a liqueur":"甜而滑順，像利口酒","Fizzy":"有氣泡","Lots of corn, low strength and new oak give intense flavours and warmth on the palate.":"大量玉米、低濃度和新橡木桶，帶來濃郁的風味和口中的溫熱感。","A bourbon is not neutral: it is the opposite of vodka. It is not a liqueur, so it is not required to be sweetened. No whisky of this kind is fizzy.":"bourbon 不是中性的：它與伏特加恰恰相反。它不是利口酒，所以沒有必須加糖的規定。這類威士忌都沒有氣泡。","Which statement about bourbon and the column still is correct?":"關於 bourbon 和柱式蒸餾器，下列哪一項正確？","It shows a column still can make a characterful spirit":"它說明柱式蒸餾器也能做出特色鮮明的烈酒","A column always gives a neutral spirit, so bourbon owes all its aroma to the barrel":"蒸餾柱一定做出中性烈酒，所以 bourbon 的香氣全靠桶","The law bans column stills for bourbon":"法律禁止 bourbon 使用柱式蒸餾器","Column stills are only used for wheated bourbon":"柱式蒸餾器只用於小麥比例高的 bourbon","Drawn off at a moderate strength, column spirit keeps plenty of congeners.":"在適中的濃度抽取時，蒸餾柱的烈酒保留大量同屬物。","A column only gives a neutral spirit when pushed to 95-96% abv; bourbon stops at 80% at most. The law does not ban the column, it is the most common tool, and it is not tied to any one grain. Armagnac and rhum agricole are other characterful column spirits.":"蒸餾柱只有推到 95–96% abv 時才會做出中性烈酒；bourbon 最多只到 80%。法律並不禁止蒸餾柱，它是最常見的工具，也不限於任何一種穀物。Armagnac 和 rhum agricole 是其他特色鮮明的蒸餾柱烈酒。","In a maturation warehouse, why do the top barrels not mature like the bottom ones, and how does the blender use this?":"在熟成酒庫中，為什麼上層的桶和下層的桶熟成情況不同？調和師如何利用這一點？","It is hotter at the top; the differences enrich the blend":"上層較熱；這些差異讓調和更豐富","It is colder at the top, so those barrels are rejected for giving whiskeys that are too light":"上層較冷，所以那些桶因做出太清淡的威士忌而被淘汰","There is more light at the top, which bleaches the spirit":"上層光線較多，會讓烈酒褪色","There is no difference between levels":"各層之間沒有差別","Heat speeds up exchange with the wood; blenders combine barrels from different levels.":"熱會加快與木頭的交換；調和師把不同樓層的桶結合起來。","Warehouses are always hotter at the top than at the bottom, whatever the local climate. Top barrels mature faster and gain more colour: they are not rejected but used to build the blend. Light is not the factor at work.":"不論當地氣候如何，酒庫的上層總是比下層熱。上層的桶熟成較快，顏色也較深：它們不會被淘汰，而是用來組成調和。光線不是這裡起作用的因素。","A Tennessee distiller makes a 51% corn whiskey in new charred barrels but skips charcoal filtering. What follows?":"一位田納西州的蒸餾師用炙燒過的新桶製作 51% 玉米的威士忌，但略過木炭過濾。結果是什麼？","As a rule, it cannot call it Tennessee Whiskey":"原則上不能稱為 Tennessee Whiskey","None: charcoal filtering is just an optional tradition some follow":"沒有影響：木炭過濾只是部分人遵循的非強制傳統","It must call it rye whiskey":"必須稱為 rye whiskey","It must age it at least four more years":"必須至少再陳年四年","For Tennessee Whiskey, filtering through maple charcoal is compulsory.":"對 Tennessee Whiskey 來說，楓木炭過濾是強制規定。","The Lincoln County Process is required by law; a single distillery is exempt. Without filtering, the whiskey could still qualify as bourbon, which can be made anywhere in the USA. Rye needs 51% rye, and no rule demands extra years.":"Lincoln County Process 是法律要求的；只有一家蒸餾廠獲得豁免。沒有過濾，這款威士忌仍可符合 bourbon 的資格，因為 bourbon 可以在美國任何地方製作。Rye 需要 51% 黑麥，也沒有規定要多陳幾年。","Which description fits a Tennessee Whiskey most precisely?":"哪一項描述最精確地符合 Tennessee Whiskey？","A straight bourbon made in Tennessee and charcoal filtered":"在田納西州製作並經木炭過濾的 straight bourbon","A rye whiskey aged in Sherry casks in Tennessee":"在田納西州用 Sherry 桶陳年的 rye whiskey","A blend of light corn whiskey and flavouring whiskeys, distilled to high strength as in Canada":"清淡玉米威士忌與調味威士忌的調和，像加拿大一樣蒸餾到高濃度","A triple-distilled malt":"三次蒸餾的麥芽威士忌","It follows straight bourbon rules, plus the origin and the Lincoln County Process.":"它遵循 straight bourbon 的規定，再加上產地和 Lincoln County Process。","That is why it shares bourbon's 51% corn and new charred barrels. Sherry casks are not allowed for bourbon. The light corn blend describes Canada and triple distillation describes Ireland.":"所以它和 bourbon 一樣有 51% 玉米和炙燒過的新桶。bourbon 不允許使用 Sherry 桶。清淡的玉米調和描述的是加拿大，三次蒸餾描述的是愛爾蘭。","Which of these rules applies to both bourbon and Tennessee Whiskey?":"下列哪一項規定同時適用於 bourbon 和 Tennessee Whiskey？","Maturation in new charred-oak barrels":"在炙燒過的新橡木桶中熟成","Maple-charcoal filtering before barrelling":"入桶前用楓木炭過濾","Production limited to one state":"生產限於單一州","At least 51% rye in the recipe, for spicy, rye-bread notes":"配方中至少 51% 黑麥，以得到辛香、黑麥麵包的氣息","Both mature in new charred oak and start from at least 51% corn.":"兩者都在炙燒過的新橡木桶中熟成，並以至少 51% 的玉米為起點。","Maple charcoal and the one-state rule only concern Tennessee Whiskey; bourbon can be made anywhere in the USA. 51% rye is the rule for rye whiskey.":"楓木炭和單一州的規定只與 Tennessee Whiskey 有關；bourbon 可以在美國任何地方製作。51% 黑麥是 rye whiskey 的規定。","Which profile describes the best-known Tennessee Whiskey in the category?":"哪一種輪廓描述了這個類別中最知名的 Tennessee Whiskey？","Smooth, with sweetcorn, vanilla and banana":"柔順，帶甜玉米、香草和香蕉","Smoky and briny, with seaweed and smoked fish notes":"煙燻而帶鹹味，有海藻和煙燻魚的氣息","Grassy, with agave notes":"青草味，帶龍舌蘭氣息","Neutral and colourless":"中性且無色","The category leader is known for a smooth texture and notes of sweetcorn, vanilla and banana.":"這個類別的領導品牌以柔順的質地以及甜玉米、香草和香蕉氣息聞名。","The smoothness reflects charcoal filtering, the vanilla new oak and the sweetcorn the recipe. Smoke and seaweed are peat notes, typical of Islay. Agave belongs to Tequila, and a whiskey aged in new oak is never colourless.":"柔順反映了木炭過濾，香草來自新橡木桶，甜玉米來自配方。煙燻和海藻是泥煤氣息，是 Islay 的典型特徵。龍舌蘭屬於 Tequila，而在新橡木桶中陳年的威士忌絕不會是無色的。","Which statement about American rye whiskey today is correct?":"關於現今的美國 rye whiskey，下列哪一項正確？","Demand is growing and its style is evolving fast":"需求正在成長，風格也快速演變","It is a declining category that hardly any distillery still makes":"它是沒落的類別，幾乎沒有蒸餾廠還在做","It is made in a completely different way from bourbon":"它的做法與 bourbon 完全不同","It must be made in Kentucky":"必須在肯塔基州製作","Rye is increasingly popular and, as more distillers make it, its style is changing quickly.":"Rye 越來越受歡迎，而隨著更多蒸餾師投入，它的風格正快速改變。","Rye is made almost exactly like bourbon: the main change is the leading grain (at least 51% rye). No rule ties it to Kentucky. It is a growing category, not a declining one.":"Rye 的做法幾乎和 bourbon 一模一樣：主要的不同是主導的穀物（至少 51% 黑麥）。沒有規定把它限制在肯塔基州。它是成長中的類別，不是沒落的類別。","When tasting, which group of aromas usually points to rye?":"品飲時，哪一組香氣通常指向黑麥？","Gingerbread, peppercorn, allspice":"薑餅、胡椒粒、多香果","Popcorn and sweetcorn":"爆米花和甜玉米","Porridge, flour, husk":"麥片粥、麵粉、穀殼","Molasses, caramel and burnt sugar, typical of cane raw materials":"糖蜜、焦糖和焦糖化的糖，是甘蔗原料的典型特徵","Rye brings spicy notes: rye bread, gingerbread, peppercorn, allspice.":"黑麥帶來辛香氣息：黑麥麵包、薑餅、胡椒粒、多香果。","Popcorn and sweetcorn point to corn, porridge and flour to malted barley. Molasses and burnt sugar belong to sugar cane, that is, rum.":"爆米花和甜玉米指向玉米，麥片粥和麵粉指向麥芽大麥。糖蜜和焦糖化的糖屬於甘蔗，也就是蘭姆酒。","An American whiskey smells of popcorn and sweetcorn. Which grain is probably dominant?":"一款美國威士忌聞起來有爆米花和甜玉米味。主導的穀物可能是哪一種？","Barley smoked with peat while drying the malt":"烘乾麥芽時用泥煤煙燻的大麥","Popcorn and sweetcorn are typical corn aromas, the base of bourbon.":"爆米花和甜玉米是典型的玉米香氣，而玉米是 bourbon 的基礎。","Rye would give spice and rye bread, peat would give smoke and medicinal notes. Wheat shows more as softness on the palate than as popcorn aromas.":"黑麥會帶來香料和黑麥麵包，泥煤會帶來煙燻和藥水味。小麥更多表現為口中的柔和感，而不是爆米花香氣。","Besides bourbon, which American whiskey can carry the word 'straight' on its label?":"除了 bourbon，哪一種美國威士忌的酒標上可以標示「straight」？","None: the term is reserved for bourbon alone by law":"沒有：法律把這個術語保留給 bourbon","A corn-based Canadian whisky":"以玉米為主的加拿大威士忌","An unaged whiskey":"未陳年的威士忌","'Straight' can also be used for rye, on the same conditions.":"在相同的條件下，「straight」也可以用於 rye。","The term is not exclusive to bourbon. A Canadian whisky does not follow US rules. An unaged whiskey cannot be straight, which requires at least two years in new oak.":"這個術語不是 bourbon 專屬的。加拿大威士忌不遵循美國的規定。未陳年的威士忌不可能是 straight，因為它要求在新橡木桶中至少兩年。","A straight bourbon has been aged for three years. What must the label show?":"一款 straight bourbon 陳年了三年。酒標上必須標示什麼？","An age statement":"年數標示","The words 'small batch'":"「small batch」字樣","The name of the county where the raw materials were grown":"種植原料的郡名","Nothing in particular":"沒有特別要求","Below four years old, a straight bourbon must state its age on the label.":"不滿四年的 straight bourbon 必須在酒標上標示年數。","At three years the whiskey already has the two-year minimum to be straight, but being under four, its age must appear. 'Small batch' is optional and has no legal definition. Grain origin need not be shown: producers can buy grain anywhere.":"三年的威士忌已經達到 straight 的兩年最低要求，但因為不滿四年，必須標出年數。「Small batch」是非強制的，也沒有法律定義。穀物產地不需要標示：生產者可以在任何地方購買穀物。","A bourbon is bottled at 50% abv. How is that written in proof?":"一款 bourbon 以 50% abv 裝瓶。用 proof 怎麼寫？","160 proof, the maximum allowed":"160 proof，允許的最大值","In the US system proof is double the alcohol percentage: 50 × 2 = 100.":"在美國的制度中，proof 是酒精百分比的兩倍：50 × 2 = 100。","50 proof would be only 25% abv and 25 proof 12.5%. 160 proof (80% abv) is bourbon's maximum distillation strength, not a bottling strength.":"50 proof 只有 25% abv，25 proof 是 12.5%。160 proof（80% abv）是 bourbon 的最高蒸餾濃度，不是裝瓶濃度。","Is the sour mash technique compulsory for bourbon?":"sour mash 技術對 bourbon 是強制規定嗎？","No, but it is widely used":"不是，但使用很廣","Yes, for every American whiskey without exception":"是，所有美國威士忌無一例外","Yes, but only for bourbon made outside Kentucky and sold abroad":"是，但只針對在肯塔基州以外製作並銷往國外的 bourbon","No, because it is banned":"不是，因為它被禁止","The law does not require it, but most American distillers use it.":"法律並未要求，但大多數美國蒸餾師都使用。","Sour mash means returning the acidic residue from the base of the column still to the fermenter. It is neither banned nor compulsory, for any production area.":"Sour mash 指的是把柱式蒸餾器底部的酸性殘液送回發酵槽。不論在哪個產區，它既沒有被禁止，也不是強制的。","An American label says 'Single Barrel'. What does it indicate?":"一張美國酒標上寫著「Single Barrel」。這代表什麼？","The whiskey comes from one barrel judged exceptional":"威士忌來自一個被評為特別出色的桶","The whiskey was distilled only once in a traditional pot still":"威士忌只在傳統壺式蒸餾器中蒸餾一次","The whiskey comes from one distillery":"威士忌來自單一蒸餾廠","The whiskey is made from one grain only":"威士忌只用一種穀物製成","Single Barrel means one cask, chosen for its quality.":"Single Barrel 指的是單一個桶，因品質而被選出。","It says nothing about the number of distillations or the grains. 'One distillery' is what 'single' means on Scottish labels, not 'single barrel'.":"它與蒸餾次數或穀物無關。「單一蒸餾廠」是蘇格蘭酒標上「single」的意思，不是「single barrel」。","What does 'Small Batch' describe on an American whiskey?":"在美國威士忌上，「Small Batch」描述的是什麼？","A blend of a few selected casks":"少數精選桶的調和","A batch of no more than ten casks, as set by US law":"依美國法律規定、不超過十個桶的一批","A whiskey distilled in a small pot still":"用小型壺式蒸餾器蒸餾的威士忌","A whiskey aged in small barrels":"在小桶中陳年的威士忌","The distiller blends a small number of chosen casks, for a higher-quality product.":"蒸餾師調和少量挑選過的桶，做出品質更高的產品。","How 'small' the batch must be is not defined by law, so there is no fixed number of casks. The term is not about the size of the still or of the barrels.":"這一批要多「小」，法律並沒有定義，所以沒有固定的桶數。這個術語與蒸餾器或桶的大小無關。","A label reads 'Kentucky Straight Bourbon Whiskey – 100 proof'. What can be deduced for sure?":"酒標上寫著「Kentucky Straight Bourbon Whiskey – 100 proof」。可以確定推論出什麼？","At least 51% corn, 2+ years in new oak, 50% abv":"玉米至少 51%、新橡木桶 2 年以上、50% abv","Maple-charcoal filtered, aged four years and bottled at 100% abv":"楓木炭過濾、陳年四年，並以 100% abv 裝瓶","Made from 100% corn, with added caramel":"用 100% 玉米製成，並添加焦糖色","Drawn from a single barrel":"取自單一桶","Bourbon = 51%+ corn; straight = 2+ years in new oak, nothing added; 100 proof = 50% abv.":"Bourbon = 玉米 51% 以上；straight = 新橡木桶 2 年以上、不添加任何東西；100 proof = 50% abv。","Charcoal filtering is for Tennessee Whiskey, and 100 proof does not mean 100% alcohol. 'Straight' forbids added colour, so no caramel, and 100% corn is not required. 'Single barrel' would have to appear on the label.":"木炭過濾是 Tennessee Whiskey 的做法，100 proof 也不代表 100% 酒精。「Straight」禁止添加色素，所以沒有焦糖色，也不要求 100% 玉米。「Single barrel」則必須出現在酒標上才算。","A customer wants an American whiskey that was filtered through maple charcoal before going into barrel. What should be offered?":"一位顧客想要一款入桶前經過楓木炭過濾的美國威士忌。應該提供什麼？","A Tennessee Whiskey":"Tennessee Whiskey","A straight rye whiskey":"Straight rye whiskey","A single barrel bourbon bottled undiluted":"未經稀釋裝瓶的 single barrel bourbon","Maple-charcoal filtering (the Lincoln County Process) is compulsory for Tennessee Whiskey.":"楓木炭過濾（Lincoln County Process）是 Tennessee Whiskey 的強制規定。","Neither rye nor bourbon is required to use this filtering, whatever the label. Canada follows its own rules and does not use this process as a defining feature.":"不論酒標怎麼寫，rye 和 bourbon 都沒有規定要用這種過濾。加拿大遵循自己的規定，也不以這個製程為界定特徵。","Which of these is NOT a bourbon rule?":"下列哪一項不是 bourbon 的規定？","It must contain at least 51% corn":"必須含至少 51% 的玉米","It must mature in new charred-oak barrels":"必須在炙燒過的新橡木桶中熟成","It may not be distilled above 80% abv, that is 160 proof":"蒸餾濃度不得超過 80% abv，也就是 160 proof","Bourbon can be made anywhere in the USA, even though Kentucky dominates.":"bourbon 可以在美國任何地方製作，雖然肯塔基州占主導地位。","Kentucky is just the main production area, not a requirement. The other three are true: corn, new charred oak and a capped distillation strength are bourbon's legal basics.":"肯塔基州只是主要產區，不是要求。其他三項都正確：玉米、炙燒過的新橡木桶和有上限的蒸餾濃度，是 bourbon 的法定基本條件。","A US distiller ages its corn whiskey in second-hand barrels. Why can it not call it bourbon?":"一位美國蒸餾師把玉米威士忌放在二手桶中陳年。為什麼不能稱為 bourbon？","Bourbon requires new charred-oak barrels":"bourbon 規定使用炙燒過的新橡木桶","Bourbon requires barrels that held sweet wine":"bourbon 規定使用裝過甜酒的桶","Bourbon cannot be aged in wood, only in stainless steel to stay pure":"bourbon 不能在木桶中陳年，只能用不鏽鋼以保持純淨","Bourbon requires maple barrels":"bourbon 規定使用楓木桶","By law, bourbon matures in new charred-oak barrels.":"依法，bourbon 在炙燒過的新橡木桶中熟成。","This is exactly why barrels used for bourbon are sold on and reused, for example in Scotland. Sweet wine, steel and maple are not part of bourbon rules.":"這正是 bourbon 用過的桶會被轉賣再利用的原因，例如賣到蘇格蘭。甜酒、鋼和楓木都不在 bourbon 的規定中。","A US distiller distils a corn mash up to 85% abv. Can it be called bourbon?":"一位美國蒸餾師把玉米糖化醪蒸餾到 85% abv。可以稱為 bourbon 嗎？","No: the distillation limit is 80% abv":"不行：蒸餾上限是 80% abv","Yes, if it then ages it at least two years in new charred-oak barrels":"可以，只要之後在炙燒過的新橡木桶中陳年至少兩年","Yes, because bourbon must exceed 95%":"可以，因為 bourbon 必須超過 95%","Yes, if it is made in Kentucky":"可以，只要在肯塔基州製作","Bourbon may not exceed 80% abv (160 proof) at distillation.":"bourbon 蒸餾時不得超過 80% abv（160 proof）。","The limit is there to keep aroma: no amount of ageing or choice of location can make up for distilling too high. 95% and above is neutral-spirit level, the opposite of bourbon.":"這個上限是為了保留香氣：不論陳年多久或選在哪裡生產，都無法彌補蒸餾濃度過高。95% 以上是中性烈酒的水準，與 bourbon 相反。","A producer wants to add a little caramel to its straight bourbon to even out the colour. Is that allowed?":"一位生產者想在 straight bourbon 中加一點焦糖色來讓顏色一致。可以嗎？","No: 'straight' forbids added colour or flavour":"不行：「straight」禁止添加色素或香料","Yes, because caramel is tasteless and US law always allows it without limit":"可以，因為焦糖色沒有味道，美國法律一律允許且不設限","Yes, if it says so on the label":"可以，只要在酒標上註明","Yes, but only after four years":"可以，但要滿四年之後","A straight whiskey may not receive colour or flavour: all its colour comes from the oak.":"Straight 威士忌不得添加色素或香料：它所有的顏色都來自橡木。","Caramel is indeed tasteless and used in many spirits, but the definition of 'straight' rules it out. Neither a label mention nor greater age changes the rule.":"焦糖色確實沒有味道，也用於許多烈酒，但「straight」的定義排除了它。在酒標上註明或年數更高都不會改變這項規定。","What is the minimum maturation required for every Scotch whisky?":"所有 Scotch 威士忌的最低熟成要求是什麼？","Three years in oak":"在橡木桶中三年","Two years in new oak":"在新橡木桶中兩年","Twelve years in barrels made of any wood":"在任何木材製成的桶中十二年","No minimum if an age is stated":"如果標示年數就沒有最低限度","All Scotch must spend at least three years in oak casks in Scotland.":"所有 Scotch 都必須在蘇格蘭的橡木桶中存放至少三年。","The minimum applies to every type, single malts and blends alike. Two years in new oak recalls the American 'straight' rule, and twelve years is a common age statement, not a requirement. An age on the label comes on top of the minimum; it does not replace it.":"這個最低要求適用於每一種類型，single malt 和調和威士忌都一樣。新橡木桶兩年讓人想到美國的「straight」規定，十二年是常見的年數標示，不是要求。酒標上的年數是在最低要求之上，不能取代它。","What raw material is single malt Scotch made from?":"Single malt Scotch 用什麼原料製成？","Malted barley only":"只用麥芽大麥","At least 51% malted barley, the rest corn":"至少 51% 麥芽大麥，其餘是玉米","Malted and unmalted barley in equal parts":"麥芽大麥和未發芽大麥各半","Any grain at all, as long as it is distilled in a pot still":"任何穀物都可以，只要用壺式蒸餾器蒸餾","Single malt Scotch is made exclusively from malted barley.":"Single malt Scotch 只用麥芽大麥製成。","The word malt on the label guarantees 100% malted barley. 51% thresholds belong to American rules, and unmalted barley is typical of Irish whiskey. A pot still is required, but on its own it does not define a malt.":"酒標上的 malt 一詞保證 100% 麥芽大麥。51% 的門檻屬於美國的規定，未發芽大麥則是愛爾蘭威士忌的典型特徵。壺式蒸餾器是必要的，但光靠它並不能定義麥芽威士忌。","How is single malt Scotch distilled?":"Single malt Scotch 怎麼蒸餾？","In pot stills, usually twice":"用壺式蒸餾器，通常兩次","In a column still, to a very high strength":"用柱式蒸餾器，到非常高的濃度","In a column still, then filtered through maple charcoal before casking":"用柱式蒸餾器，入桶前再以楓木炭過濾","Just once, in a copper still":"只用銅製蒸餾器蒸餾一次","Scottish malt whisky uses pot stills, most often with double distillation.":"蘇格蘭麥芽威士忌使用壺式蒸餾器，最常見的是二次蒸餾。","High-strength column distillation is used for grain whisky. Maple-charcoal filtering belongs to Tennessee Whiskey. Triple pot distillation is the Irish tradition.":"高濃度的蒸餾柱蒸餾用於穀物威士忌。楓木炭過濾屬於 Tennessee Whiskey。壺式三次蒸餾是愛爾蘭的傳統。","On a Scotch label, what does the word 'single' mean?":"在 Scotch 的酒標上，「single」是什麼意思？","All the whisky comes from one distillery":"所有威士忌都來自單一蒸餾廠","The whisky comes from just one cask":"威士忌只來自一個桶","The whisky was distilled only once":"威士忌只蒸餾一次","The whisky comes from a single year's barley harvest":"威士忌來自單一年份採收的大麥","Single means the whisky is the product of one distillery.":"Single 表示這款威士忌是單一蒸餾廠的產品。","A single malt is still a blend of several casks of different ages from the same distillery. One cask would be described with another term. Single says nothing about the number of distillations or the barley harvest year.":"Single malt 仍然是同一家蒸餾廠數個不同年數的桶的調和。單一個桶會用另一個術語描述。Single 與蒸餾次數或大麥的採收年份無關。","Which statement about a single malt Scotch is correct?":"關於 single malt Scotch，下列哪一項正確？","It is a blend of whiskies of different ages from one distillery":"它是來自單一蒸餾廠、不同年數威士忌的調和","It always contains whisky of one age only":"它永遠只含單一年數的威士忌","It combines malt and grain from several distilleries":"它結合了多家蒸餾廠的麥芽威士忌和穀物威士忌","It must be bottled without added water, at full cask strength":"必須不加水、以完整的原桶強度裝瓶","Even a single malt is a blend, but only of whiskies from the same distillery.":"即使是 single malt 也是調和，只不過用的都是同一家蒸餾廠的威士忌。","Combining younger and older whiskies brings balance and complexity. Malt and grain from different distilleries describes a Blended Scotch. Undiluted bottling is an option (cask strength), not a single malt requirement.":"結合較年輕和較老的威士忌能帶來平衡和複雜度。來自不同蒸餾廠的麥芽威士忌和穀物威士忌描述的是 Blended Scotch。未稀釋裝瓶是一種選擇（cask strength），不是 single malt 的要求。","What is peat?":"什麼是泥煤？","Damp, partly decayed vegetation cut from the ground":"從地裡切下來、潮濕且部分腐爛的植物","A kind of maple-wood charcoal":"一種楓木炭","The grain residue left at the bottom of the still after distillation":"蒸餾後留在蒸餾器底部的穀物殘渣","A seaweed typical of the Scottish islands":"蘇格蘭島嶼常見的一種海藻","Peat is damp, partly decayed vegetation that can be burnt once dried.":"泥煤是潮濕、部分腐爛的植物，乾燥後可以燃燒。","When burnt, it gives a very aromatic smoke that can flavour the malt. Maple charcoal is linked to Tennessee Whiskey, and still residue plays no such role. The sea-like notes of some whiskies do not make peat a seaweed.":"燃燒時它會產生香氣非常濃郁的煙，可以為麥芽增添風味。楓木炭與 Tennessee Whiskey 有關，蒸餾器的殘渣則沒有這種作用。某些威士忌帶有海洋般的氣息，但這不代表泥煤是海藻。","At which stage does peat give whisky its smoky aroma?":"泥煤在哪個階段賦予威士忌煙燻香氣？","When it is burnt to heat the green malt":"燃燒它來加熱綠麥芽時","When it is added to the wort during fermentation":"在發酵時把它加入麥汁時","When it is used to char the inside of the casks before filling":"裝桶前用它炙燒桶內部時","When the whisky is filtered through peat":"用泥煤過濾威士忌時","Peat smoke clings to the grains at the end of malting and carries into the finished whisky.":"泥煤煙在製麥的最後附著在穀粒上，並一路帶進成品威士忌。","Peat is a fuel: its effect comes from the smoke surrounding the green malt as it is heated. It is not added to the wort, it is not used on Scottish casks, which are almost always second-hand, and it is not a filter.":"泥煤是燃料：它的作用來自加熱綠麥芽時包圍著它的煙。它不會加進麥汁，也不用在蘇格蘭的桶上（那些桶幾乎都是二手的），更不是濾材。","A Scottish distillery uses very short pot stills. What style of spirit is most likely?":"一家蘇格蘭蒸餾廠使用非常矮的壺式蒸餾器。最可能做出什麼風格的烈酒？","More pronounced and aromatic":"香氣更明顯、更濃郁","Lighter and more delicate":"更清淡、更細緻","Completely neutral, with almost no recognisable aroma":"完全中性，幾乎沒有可辨認的香氣","Automatically smoky":"自然就有煙燻味","Short stills tend to give spirits with more pronounced aromas.":"矮蒸餾器往往做出香氣更明顯的烈酒。","A still does not create flavour, but its shape and height influence style: tall stills give lighter spirits. A neutral spirit would need a high-strength column still. Smokiness comes from peat, not still shape.":"蒸餾器不會創造風味，但它的形狀和高度會影響風格：高蒸餾器做出較清淡的烈酒。中性烈酒需要高濃度的柱式蒸餾器。煙燻味來自泥煤，不是蒸餾器的形狀。","Where do most of the casks used in Scotland come from?":"蘇格蘭使用的桶大多來自哪裡？","From the bourbon industry":"來自 bourbon 產業","From the Sherry bodegas of Jerez":"來自 Jerez 的 Sherry 酒窖","From Scottish cooperages that make only brand-new casks":"來自只做全新桶的蘇格蘭製桶廠","From Cognac producers":"來自 Cognac 生產者","Most Scottish casks are second-hand and come from bourbon.":"蘇格蘭的桶大多是二手的，來自 bourbon。","Bourbon must use new barrels, so used ones become available to Scotland. Ex-Sherry casks are important but far fewer. New oak is rarely used in Scotland.":"bourbon 必須使用新桶，所以用過的桶就能供應給蘇格蘭。Sherry 桶很重要，但數量少得多。蘇格蘭很少使用新橡木桶。","Which aromas are typically linked to ex-bourbon casks in Scotch?":"在 Scotch 中，哪些香氣通常與 bourbon 桶有關？","Subtle coconut, vanilla and spice":"淡淡的椰子、香草和香料","Dried fruit and orange peel":"果乾和橙皮","Peat smoke, tar and very intense medicinal notes":"泥煤煙、焦油和非常強烈的藥水味","Pear, green apple and grass":"梨、青蘋果和青草","Ex-bourbon casks give subtle coconut, vanilla and spice.":"Bourbon 桶帶來淡淡的椰子、香草和香料。","These are the same aromas new oak gives bourbon, but gentler because the cask has been used before. Dried fruit and orange are typical of ex-Sherry casks, and smoke comes from peat. Pear and grass are more the aromas of young spirit.":"這些就是新橡木桶帶給 bourbon 的香氣，只是因為桶已經用過而比較溫和。果乾和橙皮是 Sherry 桶的典型特徵，煙燻則來自泥煤。梨和青草比較是年輕烈酒的香氣。","A customer wants a Scotch with dried fruit and orange peel notes. Which label clue could guide them?":"一位顧客想要一款帶果乾和橙皮氣息的 Scotch。酒標上的哪個線索可以引導他？","Ex-Sherry cask maturation or finish":"Sherry 桶熟成或過桶","Maturation only in new, heavily charred oak barrels":"只在重度炙燒的新橡木桶中熟成","Islay region":"Islay 產區","Ex-Sherry casks are linked with dried fruit and orange peel.":"Sherry 桶與果乾和橙皮有關。","These casks are seasoned in Jerez before travelling to Scotland and release some of the wine they absorbed. New oak would bring vanilla and coconut, while Islay points to peat smoke. Non-chill-filtered is about filtration, not flavour profile.":"這些桶在運往蘇格蘭前先在 Jerez 潤桶，並釋出一些吸收的葡萄酒。新橡木桶會帶來香草和椰子，Islay 則指向泥煤煙。Non-chill-filtered 說的是過濾，不是風味輪廓。","What happens to ex-Sherry casks before they reach Scotland?":"Sherry 桶在抵達蘇格蘭之前經過什麼處理？","They are seasoned with wine in Jerez":"在 Jerez 用葡萄酒潤桶","They are filled with bourbon for two years":"裝 bourbon 兩年","They are heavily charred and rinsed several times to remove all trace of wine":"重度炙燒並沖洗數次，以去除所有葡萄酒的痕跡","They are smoked over peat":"用泥煤煙燻","The casks are seasoned with wine in Jerez, the Sherry region, and then shipped to Scotland.":"這些桶在 Sherry 的產區 Jerez 用葡萄酒潤桶，再運往蘇格蘭。","The whole point is for the wood to hold some wine, which later passes into the whisky, so removing it would make no sense. Bourbon and peat have nothing to do with this preparation. These casks are fewer than ex-bourbon ones.":"重點就是要讓木頭留住一些葡萄酒，之後再進入威士忌，所以去除它毫無道理。bourbon 和泥煤與這項準備無關。這些桶比 bourbon 桶少。","What is a wood finish in malt whisky?":"麥芽威士忌的 wood finish（過桶）是什麼？","A short final spell in a cask that held wine or another spirit":"最後在裝過葡萄酒或其他烈酒的桶中短暫存放","Chill-filtration just before bottling":"裝瓶前的冷凝過濾","Sanding the inside of new barrels":"打磨新桶的內部","Adding caramel to keep the colour even from batch to batch":"添加焦糖色，讓各批顏色一致","In a finish, the whisky spends a short time at the end of maturation in a different cask that held wine or spirit.":"過桶時，威士忌在熟成的最後階段，短暫存放在另一個裝過葡萄酒或烈酒的桶中。","Liquid held in the staves seeps out and adds flavour, and sometimes colour, to the whisky. Port or Sherry casks are typical examples. Chill-filtration and caramel are pre-bottling adjustments, not a spell in cask.":"留在桶板裡的液體滲出來，為威士忌增添風味，有時還有顏色。Port 桶或 Sherry 桶是典型的例子。冷凝過濾和焦糖色是裝瓶前的調整，不是在桶中存放。","Which statement about the use of oak in Scotland is correct?":"關於蘇格蘭對橡木桶的使用，下列哪一項正確？","New oak is rarely used":"很少使用新橡木桶","The law requires new charred barrels":"法律規定使用炙燒過的新桶","Ex-Sherry casks are by far the most common type in every distillery":"Sherry 桶在每家蒸餾廠都是遠遠最常見的類型","Mostly inert steel vessels are used":"大多使用惰性的鋼製容器","Scotland prefers second-hand casks to new oak.":"蘇格蘭偏好二手桶，而不是新橡木桶。","Used casks give gentler aromas, leaving room for the malt's own character. It is bourbon that must use new charred oak. Ex-Sherry casks are fewer than ex-bourbon ones, and Scotch must mature in oak, not steel.":"用過的桶帶來較溫和的香氣，為麥芽本身的特色留出空間。必須使用炙燒過的新橡木桶的是 bourbon。Sherry 桶比 bourbon 桶少，而 Scotch 必須在橡木中熟成，不是鋼。","How is Scottish grain whisky made?":"蘇格蘭穀物威士忌是怎麼做的？","From mixed grains, in column stills, to high strength":"用混合穀物，以柱式蒸餾器蒸餾到高濃度","From malted barley only, in pot stills":"只用麥芽大麥，以壺式蒸餾器蒸餾","From at least 51% rye, to a low strength, in new charred oak":"用至少 51% 的黑麥，蒸餾到低濃度，放進炙燒過的新橡木桶","From peated barley with triple distillation":"用泥煤大麥，三次蒸餾","Grain whisky uses a mix of grains and is distilled to high strength in a column still.":"穀物威士忌使用混合穀物，並在柱式蒸餾器中蒸餾到高濃度。","The result is a whisky with a light flavour intensity. Malted barley only and pot stills describe malt whisky. 51% rye and low strength recall American rye whiskey.":"成品是風味強度清淡的威士忌。只用麥芽大麥和壺式蒸餾器描述的是麥芽威士忌。51% 黑麥和低濃度讓人想到美國的 rye whiskey。","Making up Blended Scotch":"用來組成 Blended Scotch","Being bottled on its own as a flagship premium product":"作為旗艦級高級產品單獨裝瓶","Finishing single malts":"為 single malt 過桶","Diluting whisky before bottling":"裝瓶前用來稀釋威士忌","Almost all grain whisky goes into Blended Scotch.":"幾乎所有穀物威士忌都用於 Blended Scotch。","Grain whisky is very rarely sold on its own; its light profile acts as a base for the malt. A finish is a spell in cask, not an addition of whisky. Pure water, not more whisky, is used to dilute.":"穀物威士忌很少單獨販售；它清淡的輪廓是麥芽威士忌的基底。過桶是在桶中存放一段時間，不是添加威士忌。稀釋用的是純水，不是更多的威士忌。","What is a Blended Scotch Whisky?":"什麼是 Blended Scotch Whisky？","A blend of malt and grain whiskies from different distilleries":"來自不同蒸餾廠的麥芽威士忌和穀物威士忌的調和","A blend of malts from one distillery":"來自單一蒸餾廠的麥芽威士忌的調和","Scotch whisky mixed with bourbon":"Scotch 威士忌與 bourbon 的混合","A single malt finished in wine casks":"在葡萄酒桶中過桶的 single malt","Blended Scotch combines malt whisky and grain whisky from several distilleries.":"Blended Scotch 結合了多家蒸餾廠的麥芽威士忌和穀物威士忌。","Malts from one distillery make a single malt, which is also a blend but does not carry this label. All the whisky must be Scottish. A single malt with a finish is still a single malt.":"來自單一蒸餾廠的麥芽威士忌是 single malt，它也是調和，但不用這個標示。所有威士忌都必須是蘇格蘭的。過桶的 single malt 仍然是 single malt。","Which statement about the quality of Blended Scotch is correct?":"關於 Blended Scotch 的品質，下列哪一項正確？","Some rank among the finest Scotch whiskies":"有些名列最出色的 Scotch 威士忌","They are always inferior to any single malt":"一律不如任何 single malt","By law they must spend at least twelve years in cask":"依法必須在桶中存放至少十二年","They cannot contain whisky older than three years":"不能含有超過三年的威士忌","Although many blends are young, outstanding ones exist and are counted among Scotland's best whiskies.":"雖然許多調和威士忌很年輕，但也有傑出的酒款，名列蘇格蘭最好的威士忌。","Most blends are little more than three years old, but three years is a minimum, not a maximum. No rule requires twelve years. Blend describes a production method, not a quality level.":"大多數調和威士忌只比三年多一點，但三年是最低限度，不是上限。沒有規定要求十二年。調和描述的是生產方式，不是品質等級。","A Blended Scotch states '12 years' on the label. What does this mean?":"一款 Blended Scotch 的酒標上寫著「12 years」。這是什麼意思？","The youngest whisky in the blend is 12 years old":"調和中最年輕的威士忌是 12 年","The blend has an average age of 12 years":"調和的平均年數是 12 年","The oldest whisky used in the blend is exactly 12 years old":"調和中使用的最老威士忌剛好是 12 年","The whisky was bottled 12 years ago":"這款威士忌是 12 年前裝瓶的","The age statement shows the youngest whisky: every component is at least 12 years old.":"年數標示指的是最年輕的威士忌：每個成分都至少 12 年。","The blend may also include older whiskies, so the average age is often higher. It is neither an average nor the oldest component. Also, age counts only time in cask, not in bottle.":"調和中也可能含有更老的威士忌，所以平均年數往往更高。它既不是平均值，也不是最老的成分。此外，年數只計算在桶中的時間，不算瓶中的時間。","What does 'non-chill-filtered' mean on a whisky label?":"威士忌酒標上的「non-chill-filtered」是什麼意思？","The whisky was not chill-filtered before bottling":"威士忌在裝瓶前沒有經過冷凝過濾","The whisky must always be served at room temperature":"威士忌一律必須在室溫下飲用","The whisky was not filtered through maple charcoal before going into cask":"威士忌入桶前沒有經過楓木炭過濾","The whisky contains no caramel":"威士忌不含焦糖色","The producer skipped chill-filtration just before bottling.":"生產者略過了裝瓶前的冷凝過濾。","Chill-filtration stops whisky from turning hazy with cold or water; some believe it also removes flavour and texture. No caramel is shown by 'natural colour'. Maple charcoal relates to Tennessee Whiskey, and the term gives no serving instructions.":"冷凝過濾能防止威士忌遇冷或加水時變混濁；有些人認為它也會去除風味和質地。不含焦糖色是用「natural colour」表示的。楓木炭與 Tennessee Whiskey 有關，這個術語也不提供飲用方式的指示。","A customer adds cold water to a whisky and it turns cloudy. Which technique, if the producer had used it, would have prevented this?":"一位顧客在威士忌中加了冷水，結果變混濁了。如果生產者用了哪一種技術，就能避免這種情況？","A final spell in ex-Sherry casks":"最後在 Sherry 桶中存放一段時間","Bottling at full cask strength, with no water added":"以完整的原桶強度裝瓶，不加水","Chill-filtration removes in advance the substances that cause haze.":"冷凝過濾會事先去除造成混濁的物質。","The producer chills the whisky, lets the haze form and filters it out. A non-chill-filtered whisky may cloud, but that is not a fault. Caramel and finishing do not affect clarity, and bottling at cask strength does nothing to prevent haze.":"生產者把威士忌降溫，讓混濁物形成，再濾除。非冷凝過濾的威士忌可能變混濁，但那不是缺陷。焦糖色和過桶不影響清澈度，以原桶強度裝瓶也無法防止混濁。","What does 'cask strength' mean on a whisky label?":"威士忌酒標上的「cask strength」是什麼意思？","Bottled without dilution with water":"未加水稀釋就裝瓶","Matured in especially sturdy casks":"在特別堅固的桶中熟成","Made from the contents of a single exceptional cask":"用單一個特別出色的桶的內容物製成","Matured in new casks that give a lot of oak flavour to the whisky":"在為威士忌帶來大量橡木風味的新桶中熟成","Cask strength means the whisky is bottled at the strength it had in cask, with no water added.":"Cask strength 表示威士忌以它在桶中的濃度裝瓶，沒有加水。","Strength is therefore often well above 40%, and the whisky is aimed at enthusiasts. The term says nothing about cask type or sturdiness, nor whether it comes from a single cask.":"所以濃度往往遠高於 40%，是針對愛好者的威士忌。這個術語與桶的類型或堅固程度無關，也不表示是否來自單一桶。","A Scotch label says 'natural colour'. What does this mean?":"一瓶 Scotch 的酒標寫著「natural colour」。這是什麼意思？","No caramel has been added":"沒有添加焦糖色","The whisky has never been in a cask":"威士忌從未入過桶","The colour comes only from peated barley":"顏色只來自泥煤大麥","The whisky was filtered through activated charcoal to remove all its colour":"威士忌用活性碳過濾，去除了所有顏色","Natural colour means all the colour comes from the casks, with no caramel.":"Natural colour 表示所有顏色都來自桶，沒有焦糖色。","Many producers use small amounts of caramel to keep colour consistent from batch to batch. Scotch is always matured in cask, and peat gives aroma, not colour. Activated charcoal would make the whisky colourless.":"許多生產者使用少量焦糖色，讓各批顏色保持一致。Scotch 一定在桶中熟成，泥煤帶來的是香氣，不是顏色。活性碳會讓威士忌變成無色。","Which of these is one of the five Scotch whisky regions?":"下列哪一個是 Scotch 威士忌的五個產區之一？","Campbeltown is one of the five regions, alongside Islay, Highland, Speyside and Lowland.":"Campbeltown 是五個產區之一，另外還有 Islay、Highland、Speyside 和 Lowland。","Lincoln County names the Tennessee Whiskey filtering process. Ténarèze is an Armagnac area and Fins Bois a Cognac cru: French brandy names, not whisky ones.":"Lincoln County 是 Tennessee Whiskey 過濾製程的名稱。Ténarèze 是 Armagnac 的區域，Fins Bois 是 Cognac 的 cru：都是法國白蘭地的名稱，不是威士忌的。","What does a region name on a single malt label tell you with certainty?":"Single malt 酒標上的產區名稱能確定告訴你什麼？","Where the distillery is":"蒸餾廠的所在地","The exact style you will find in the glass":"你會在杯中喝到的確切風格","The type of casks in which the whisky was matured":"威士忌熟成所用的桶型","Where the barley was grown":"大麥的種植地","The region only guarantees where in Scotland the distillery is.":"產區只保證蒸餾廠位於蘇格蘭的哪裡。","It is not a reliable guide to style, since very different whiskies sit within each region; Islay, mostly peaty, is the exception. Casks and barley origin depend on the distillery's choices. These names appear mainly on single malts, rarely on blends.":"它不是判斷風格的可靠依據，因為每個產區內都有非常不同的威士忌；大多帶泥煤味的 Islay 是例外。桶和大麥產地取決於蒸餾廠的選擇。這些名稱主要出現在 single malt 上，很少出現在調和威士忌上。","A customer wants a clearly smoky, peaty single malt. Which region on the label is the most reliable clue?":"一位顧客想要一款煙燻、泥煤味鮮明的 single malt。酒標上的哪個產區是最可靠的線索？","On Islay the vast majority of whiskies show a distinct peat aroma.":"在 Islay，絕大多數的威士忌都有鮮明的泥煤香氣。","Islay is the exception to the rule that a region does not indicate style. Other regions have both peated and unpeated whiskies, so the name alone is not enough: check the distillery's information.":"Islay 是「產區不代表風格」這條規則的例外。其他產區既有泥煤威士忌，也有無泥煤的，所以光看名稱不夠：要查蒸餾廠的資訊。","Where must a Single Malt Scotch Whisky be made?":"Single Malt Scotch Whisky 必須在哪裡製作？","In Scotland":"在蘇格蘭","Anywhere in the UK, as long as Scottish malted barley is used":"英國任何地方，只要使用蘇格蘭的麥芽大麥","In any country that follows the Scottish method":"任何遵循蘇格蘭做法的國家","Only on the island of Islay":"只在 Islay 島上","By law, Single Malt Scotch must be made in Scotland.":"依法，Single Malt Scotch 必須在蘇格蘭製作。","The rest of the UK does not count, and the barley need not be Scottish. Japan follows the Scottish model but its whisky is not Scotch. Islay is just one of the five regions.":"英國的其他地方不算，大麥也不必是蘇格蘭的。日本沿用蘇格蘭的模式，但它的威士忌不是 Scotch。Islay 只是五個產區之一。","Where do Scotch whisky producers buy their grain?":"Scotch 威士忌的生產者在哪裡購買穀物？","From a number of countries":"從好幾個國家","Only from Scottish fields, as the law demands for every Scotch category":"只來自蘇格蘭的田地，因為法律對每個 Scotch 類別都這樣要求","Only from the distillery itself":"只來自蒸餾廠自己","Only from the USA":"只來自美國","The grain for Scotch can come from anywhere: it is bought from several countries.":"Scotch 的穀物可以來自任何地方：是從好幾個國家買來的。","Unlike Tequila or Calvados, the raw material does not have to come from a set area. Very few distillers grow their own grain, and no rule requires the USA.":"與 Tequila 或 Calvados 不同，原料不必來自特定區域。極少數蒸餾師自己種植穀物，也沒有規定要用美國的。","What flavour does barley give to every Scottish malt whisky?":"大麥為每一款蘇格蘭麥芽威士忌帶來什麼風味？","Malt and cereal":"麥芽和穀物","Dried fruit and orange peel, as after time in a Sherry cask":"果乾和橙皮，就像在 Sherry 桶中存放過一樣","Coconut and vanilla":"椰子和香草","Barley always gives a background of malt and cereal.":"大麥總是帶來麥芽和穀物的底蘊。","Peat smoke only appears if peat was used to heat the green malt, so not in all of them. Dried fruit and orange come from ex-Sherry casks, coconut and vanilla from ex-bourbon casks.":"只有用泥煤加熱綠麥芽時才會出現泥煤煙，所以不是每一款都有。果乾和橙皮來自 Sherry 桶，椰子和香草來自 bourbon 桶。","Which statement about pot stills in Scottish distilleries is correct?":"關於蘇格蘭蒸餾廠的壺式蒸餾器，下列哪一項正確？","They do not create flavour, but their shape affects the style":"它們不創造風味，但形狀會影響風格","They create the whisky's vanilla aromas":"它們創造了威士忌的香草香氣","They all have the same shape, set by law":"它們的形狀都一樣，由法律規定","Their height has no effect on the spirit; only the number of distillations matters":"高度對烈酒沒有影響；只有蒸餾次數才重要","The still selects aromas; its shape and height steer the style.":"蒸餾器篩選香氣；它的形狀和高度引導風格。","A still adds no new flavours: it decides which congeners get through. Vanilla comes from oak. Shapes vary widely between distilleries, and height matters: short stills give more pronounced spirits, tall ones lighter.":"蒸餾器不會增添新的風味：它決定哪些同屬物能通過。香草來自橡木。各蒸餾廠的形狀差異很大，高度也有影響：矮蒸餾器做出香氣更明顯的烈酒，高的則較清淡。","A Scottish distillery uses notably tall pot stills. Which style of spirit is most likely?":"一家蘇格蘭蒸餾廠使用特別高的壺式蒸餾器。最可能做出什麼風格的烈酒？","Lighter":"較清淡","More pronounced, with lots of heavy congeners":"香氣更明顯，帶大量較重的同屬物","Smokier":"煙燻味更重","Completely neutral, like a column-distilled vodka":"完全中性，像蒸餾柱蒸餾的伏特加","Tall stills give lighter spirits; short ones give more aromatic spirits.":"高蒸餾器做出較清淡的烈酒；矮的做出香氣更濃郁的烈酒。","Intensity with heavy congeners is what short stills tend to give. Smoke depends on peat, not height. A pot still never produces a neutral spirit.":"帶較重同屬物的濃郁感是矮蒸餾器往往做出的效果。煙燻味取決於泥煤，不是高度。壺式蒸餾器絕不會做出中性烈酒。","What has to be done to peat before it can be burnt for the malt?":"泥煤要經過什麼處理，才能燃燒來烘麥芽？","Dry it":"乾燥","Ferment it":"發酵","Soak it in whisky for a few months to flavour it":"在威士忌中浸泡幾個月來增添風味","Distil it":"蒸餾","Peat is cut damp from the ground and only burns once it has dried.":"泥煤從地裡切下來時是潮濕的，乾燥後才能燃燒。","Once dry it burns with a very aromatic smoke that clings to the green malt. It is not fermented, distilled or put into the whisky: it works only through its smoke.":"乾燥後它燃燒時會產生香氣非常濃郁的煙，附著在綠麥芽上。它不經發酵、蒸餾，也不會放進威士忌裡：它只透過煙發揮作用。","Which group of descriptors usually signals a peated whisky?":"哪一組描述詞通常代表泥煤威士忌？","Medicinal, smoked fish, seaweed":"藥水味、煙燻魚、海藻","Pear, apple, white flowers":"梨、蘋果、白花","Rye bread, lemon zest, peppercorn and other spices":"黑麥麵包、檸檬皮、胡椒粒和其他香料","Peat smoke is described with medicinal, smoked-fish and seaweed notes.":"泥煤煙會用藥水味、煙燻魚和海藻等氣息來描述。","Vanilla and coconut come from oak, especially ex-bourbon. Pear and apple are fruity, not peaty. Rye bread and lemon describe American rye whiskey.":"香草和椰子來自橡木，尤其是 bourbon 桶。梨和蘋果是果香，不是泥煤味。黑麥麵包和檸檬描述的是美國的 rye whiskey。","A distillery stops using peat and heats its green malt with another fuel. What changes in the whisky?":"一家蒸餾廠停止使用泥煤，改用其他燃料加熱綠麥芽。威士忌會有什麼改變？","It loses the smoke but keeps the malt and cereal notes":"失去煙燻味，但保留麥芽和穀物氣息","It can no longer be called single malt":"不能再稱為 single malt","It becomes a grain whisky":"變成穀物威士忌","Nothing changes: peat smoke only develops during cask maturation":"沒有改變：泥煤煙只在桶中熟成時才發展出來","Smoke only comes from burning peat; the malty character comes from the barley itself.":"煙燻味只來自燃燒泥煤；麥芽特色則來自大麥本身。","Peat is an option, not a rule: a single malt may be peated or not, and that does not turn it into grain whisky. The smoke is added at the end of malting, not in the cask.":"泥煤是選項，不是規定：single malt 可以有泥煤味，也可以沒有，這不會讓它變成穀物威士忌。煙是在製麥的最後加上的，不是在桶中。","Why might a Scottish distiller choose a cask that has already been used several times?":"為什麼蘇格蘭的蒸餾師可能選擇已經用過好幾次的桶？","It gives less oak and lets the spirit show":"它給的橡木味較少，讓烈酒本身展現出來","Because each reuse increases the colour and flavour the cask passes on":"因為每次重複使用，桶傳遞的顏色和風味都會增加","Because the law bans casks used fewer than three times":"因為法律禁止使用不滿三次的桶","Because it adds peat smoke":"因為它增添泥煤煙","Each reuse gives less colour and flavour: it is a style choice, not a flaw.":"每次重複使用給的顏色和風味都更少：這是風格的選擇，不是缺陷。","A cask gives the most when new and then less and less, not more. No law sets a minimum number of uses. Peat acts on the malt, not the cask.":"桶在全新時給得最多，之後越來越少，而不是越來越多。沒有法律規定最少的使用次數。泥煤作用在麥芽上，不是桶上。","Which wine region supplies the second important type of cask used in Scotland?":"哪一個葡萄酒產區供應蘇格蘭第二重要的桶型？","Jerez, in southern Spain":"西班牙南部的 Jerez","Kentucky, in the USA":"美國的肯塔基州","Cognac, in western France":"法國西部的 Cognac","The Douro Valley in Portugal, home of the Port used in the casks":"葡萄牙的斗羅河谷，桶中所裝 Port 的故鄉","Ex-Sherry casks come from Jerez, where they are seasoned with wine before shipping to Scotland.":"Sherry 桶來自 Jerez，在運往蘇格蘭前先在那裡用葡萄酒潤桶。","Kentucky supplies the first type, ex-bourbon casks, which are the majority. Port or other spirit casks are mostly used for short finishes, not as the second main type.":"肯塔基州供應的是第一種桶型，也就是占多數的 bourbon 桶。Port 桶或其他烈酒桶大多用於短期過桶，不是第二種主要桶型。","Compared with ex-bourbon casks, how common are ex-Sherry casks in Scotland?":"與 bourbon 桶相比，Sherry 桶在蘇格蘭有多常見？","Far less common":"少得多","Far more common, because they are compulsory for single malt":"多得多，因為 single malt 必須使用","About equally common":"大約一樣常見","Banned in Scotland":"在蘇格蘭被禁止","Most casks come from bourbon; Sherry casks are relatively few.":"大多數的桶來自 bourbon；Sherry 桶相對較少。","No cask type is compulsory for single malt, as long as it is oak. Ex-Sherry casks are allowed and prized for dried fruit and orange notes, but remain a minority.":"Single malt 沒有強制使用哪一種桶，只要是橡木就可以。Sherry 桶是允許的，並因果乾和橙皮氣息而受珍視，但仍是少數。","During a cask finish, how does the finishing barrel add flavour to the whisky?":"過桶時，過桶用的桶如何為威士忌增添風味？","Liquid soaked into the staves comes out into the whisky":"滲在桶板裡的液體釋放到威士忌中","The producer openly adds some of the cask's former wine to the whisky":"生產者公開把桶先前裝的葡萄酒加一些到威士忌裡","The barrel is charred again":"桶重新炙燒","The barrel is filled with peat smoke":"桶中灌滿泥煤煙","What remains in the wood comes back out into the new contents, bringing flavour and sometimes colour.":"留在木頭裡的東西會回到新的內容物中，帶來風味，有時還有顏色。","No wine is poured into the whisky: the soaked wood gives up what it holds. Re-charring or peat smoke are not part of a finish.":"沒有把葡萄酒倒進威士忌：是浸透的木頭釋出它所含的東西。重新炙燒或泥煤煙都不屬於過桶。","A single malt says 'Port Cask Finish'. What does this mean?":"一款 single malt 標示「Port Cask Finish」。這是什麼意思？","After its main maturation, a short spell in an ex-Port cask":"主要熟成之後，在 Port 桶中短暫存放","It spent its whole life in Port casks":"它一直都在 Port 桶中","It is a blend of whisky and Port":"它是威士忌和 Port 的調和","It was distilled in Portugal by a Scottish distillery, from local malted barley":"它由蘇格蘭蒸餾廠在葡萄牙用當地的麥芽大麥蒸餾","'Finish' means a short final spell in a different cask, here ex-Port.":"「Finish」表示最後在另一種桶（這裡是 Port 桶）中短暫存放。","A finish comes at the end, not for the whole maturation. No Port is added to the whisky: only what the wood had absorbed. Scotch must be made in Scotland.":"過桶是在最後進行，不是整個熟成期。威士忌中沒有加入 Port：只有木頭吸收的部分。Scotch 必須在蘇格蘭製作。","Which of these barrels could NOT be used for a wood finish?":"下列哪一種桶不能用來過桶？","A brand-new barrel, never filled":"從未裝過酒的全新桶","A barrel that held Sherry":"裝過 Sherry 的桶","A barrel that held Port":"裝過 Port 的桶","A barrel that held another fine spirit from another region":"裝過其他產區優質烈酒的桶","A finishing barrel must have held wine or a spirit: that is what brings the flavour.":"過桶用的桶必須裝過葡萄酒或烈酒：風味就是這樣來的。","Finishing relies on previous contents left in the staves; a new barrel has none. Port, Sherry and casks from other fine wine and spirit regions have all been used.":"過桶靠的是留在桶板裡的先前內容物；新桶什麼都沒有。Port 桶、Sherry 桶和來自其他優質葡萄酒及烈酒產區的桶都有人使用。","Why does Scottish grain whisky have a light flavour?":"為什麼蘇格蘭穀物威士忌的風味清淡？","It is distilled to a high strength in a column":"它在蒸餾柱中蒸餾到高濃度","It matures in Sherry casks":"它在 Sherry 桶中熟成","It is made only from malted barley, which gives little aroma":"它只用麥芽大麥製成，香氣很少","It is heavily diluted with water before going into cask for three years":"它在入桶三年前用水大幅稀釋","At high strength in a column, few congeners remain, so the aroma is light.":"在蒸餾柱中蒸餾到高濃度時，留下的同屬物很少，所以香氣清淡。","Grain whisky is made from a mix of grains, not only malted barley, and barley actually gives malty notes. Sherry casks would add flavour, not remove it. Dilution lowers alcohol but does not remove congeners.":"穀物威士忌用混合穀物製成，不只是麥芽大麥，而且大麥其實會帶來麥芽氣息。Sherry 桶會增添風味，不是去除。稀釋降低的是酒精，不會去除同屬物。","How often is Scottish grain whisky sold on its own, in a bottle?":"蘇格蘭穀物威士忌多常單獨裝瓶販售？","Very rarely":"非常少","Almost always; it is the best-selling category":"幾乎都是；它是最暢銷的類別","Never: the law forbids it in all cases":"從不：法律在任何情況下都禁止","Only when it is over twenty years old and from one selected cask":"只有超過二十年且來自單一精選桶時","Bottled grain whiskies exist, so it is not banned, but they are very rare. No age or single-cask rule applies. What sells most are blends, where grain is the light base.":"瓶裝的穀物威士忌確實存在，所以並未被禁止，但非常少見。沒有年數或單一桶的規定。賣得最多的是調和威士忌，穀物威士忌是其中清淡的基底。","What is most Blended Scotch Whisky like?":"大多數 Blended Scotch Whisky 是什麼樣子？","Affordable and little more than three years old":"價格實惠，只比三年多一點","Very expensive and at least twenty years old":"非常昂貴，至少二十年","Bottled at full cask strength, without reducing with water":"以完整的原桶強度裝瓶，不加水降度","Made only from malts":"只用麥芽威士忌製成","Most blends are inexpensive and only just over the three-year minimum.":"大多數調和威士忌價格不高，只剛超過三年的最低要求。","There are also outstanding blends sold at very high prices, but they are a minority. Cask strength applies to a few speciality bottlings. A Blended Scotch combines malt and grain, not only malts.":"也有以極高價格販售的傑出調和威士忌，但它們是少數。Cask strength 只適用於少數特殊裝瓶。Blended Scotch 結合麥芽威士忌和穀物威士忌，不只是麥芽威士忌。","Which of these Scotch whiskies can contain spirit made in a column still?":"下列哪一種 Scotch 威士忌可以含有柱式蒸餾器製作的烈酒？","A Blended Scotch Whisky":"Blended Scotch Whisky","A Single Malt Scotch Whisky":"Single Malt Scotch Whisky","A single malt finished in a Sherry cask":"在 Sherry 桶中過桶的 single malt","A peated Islay single malt bottled at cask strength":"以 cask strength 裝瓶的 Islay 泥煤 single malt","A blend contains grain whisky, which is made in column stills.":"調和威士忌含有穀物威士忌，而它是用柱式蒸餾器製作的。","All single malts, finished or not, peated or not, must be distilled in pot stills. Finishing, peat and cask strength do not change that rule.":"所有 single malt，不論是否過桶、是否有泥煤味，都必須用壺式蒸餾器蒸餾。過桶、泥煤和 cask strength 都不會改變這條規定。","A whisky combines malts from several Scottish distilleries with grain whisky. What is it called?":"一款威士忌結合了多家蘇格蘭蒸餾廠的麥芽威士忌和穀物威士忌。它叫做什麼？","Scotch whisky with a regional statement, such as 'Highland'":"標示產區（例如「Highland」）的 Scotch 威士忌","Malt plus grain, from different distilleries: that is the definition of Blended Scotch.":"麥芽加穀物，來自不同蒸餾廠：這就是 Blended Scotch 的定義。","'Single' means one distillery, so neither single malt nor single grain fits. Regions rarely appear on blends and do not define the category anyway.":"「Single」表示單一蒸餾廠，所以 single malt 和 single grain 都不符合。產區很少出現在調和威士忌上，而且本來就不定義類別。","On which Scotch whiskies do region names usually appear?":"產區名稱通常出現在哪些 Scotch 威士忌上？","On single malts, rarely on blends":"Single malt 上，很少出現在調和威士忌上","On blends, hardly ever on single malts":"調和威士忌上，幾乎不出現在 single malt 上","On all of them, because it is compulsory":"全部都有，因為是強制規定","Only on Lowland grain whiskies, where the mention is traditional":"只在 Lowland 的穀物威士忌上，那裡有標示的傳統","Single malts come from one distillery, so from one place; blends come from many.":"Single malt 來自單一蒸餾廠，所以來自單一地點；調和威士忌則來自許多地方。","A blend often combines distilleries from different regions, so naming one region makes little sense. The mention is not compulsory and is not linked to grain whisky.":"調和威士忌常結合不同產區的蒸餾廠，所以只標一個產區沒有什麼意義。標示不是強制的，也與穀物威士忌無關。","A customer thinks all Speyside single malts taste the same. What is the most accurate reply?":"一位顧客認為所有 Speyside 的 single malt 喝起來都一樣。最準確的回答是什麼？","The region shows where the distillery is, not the style":"產區表示蒸餾廠在哪裡，不是風格","True: the law gives each region a style, with set casks and stills":"沒錯：法律為每個產區規定了風格，以及固定的桶和蒸餾器","True: they are all heavily peated":"沒錯：它們全都有重泥煤味","Speyside only makes blends":"Speyside 只生產調和威士忌","A region name only tells you for sure where the distillery is.":"產區名稱只能確定告訴你蒸餾廠在哪裡。","Peat, still shape and casks vary from distillery to distillery, even within one region. No law sets a regional style. Strong peat is typical of Islay, which is the exception.":"泥煤、蒸餾器形狀和桶因蒸餾廠而異，即使在同一個產區內也一樣。沒有法律規定產區風格。強烈的泥煤味是 Islay 的典型特徵，而它是例外。","Which of these names is NOT one of the five Scotch whisky regions?":"下列哪一個名稱不是 Scotch 威士忌的五個產區之一？","Hebrides":"Hebrides","The five regions are Islay, Highland, Campbeltown, Speyside and Lowland.":"五個產區是 Islay、Highland、Campbeltown、Speyside 和 Lowland。","The Hebrides are an archipelago, but they are not among the five official whisky regions. Speyside, Lowland and Highland are, along with Islay and Campbeltown.":"Hebrides 是一個群島，但不在五個官方威士忌產區之列。Speyside、Lowland 和 Highland 則是，另外還有 Islay 和 Campbeltown。","Into how many whisky regions is Scotland divided?":"蘇格蘭分成幾個威士忌產區？","Two: Highlands and Lowlands, split by a line from coast to coast":"兩個：Highlands 和 Lowlands，以一條橫貫兩岸的線劃分","There are five regions: Islay, Highland, Campbeltown, Speyside and Lowland.":"有五個產區：Islay、Highland、Campbeltown、Speyside 和 Lowland。","Don't confuse the three-year minimum with the number of regions. Highland and Lowland are two of the five, not the only ones. Twelve is a common age on labels, not a number of regions.":"不要把三年的最低要求和產區數目搞混。Highland 和 Lowland 是五個中的兩個，不是全部。十二是酒標上常見的年數，不是產區數目。","Which of the five Scotch whisky regions is an island?":"Scotch 威士忌的五個產區中，哪一個是島嶼？","Campbeltown, on the mainland's west coast":"Campbeltown，位於本島西岸","Islay is an island, and most of its whiskies have a clear peaty aroma.":"Islay 是一座島，那裡大多數的威士忌都有清楚的泥煤香氣。","Speyside, Lowland and Campbeltown are on the mainland. Islay is also the only region whose name is a fairly reliable style clue, thanks to peat.":"Speyside、Lowland 和 Campbeltown 都在本島上。因為泥煤的關係，Islay 也是唯一一個名稱可以相當可靠地提示風格的產區。","A whisky list shows Islay, Highland, Lowland and Campbeltown. Which name completes the five regions?":"一份威士忌酒單列出 Islay、Highland、Lowland 和 Campbeltown。哪一個名稱能補齊五個產區？","Lincoln County, the name of a filtering process":"Lincoln County，一種過濾製程的名稱","Speyside is the fifth Scotch whisky region.":"Speyside 是 Scotch 威士忌的第五個產區。","Jerez is the Sherry area that supplies some casks. Kentucky and Lincoln County relate to American whiskey, not Scotland.":"Jerez 是供應部分桶的 Sherry 產區。肯塔基州和 Lincoln County 與美國威士忌有關，不是蘇格蘭。","A single malt is labelled '18 years old'. Which whiskies can it contain?":"一款 single malt 標示「18 years old」。它可以含有哪些威士忌？","Whiskies of 18 years or older, from the same distillery":"來自同一家蒸餾廠、18 年或更老的威士忌","Whiskies of various ages, as long as the average is 18":"各種年數的威士忌，只要平均是 18 年","Only whiskies of exactly 18 years":"只有剛好 18 年的威士忌","Whiskies of 18 years or more from several distilleries, plus some grain":"來自多家蒸餾廠、18 年以上的威士忌，再加一些穀物威士忌","The age is that of the youngest whisky: everything is 18 or older, from one distillery.":"年數是最年輕威士忌的年數：全部都是 18 年或更老，來自單一蒸餾廠。","It is not an average, so no younger whisky. The blend may include older whiskies, not just exactly 18. Several distilleries plus grain describes a Blended Scotch, not a single malt.":"它不是平均值，所以沒有更年輕的威士忌。調和中可以含有更老的威士忌，不只是剛好 18 年的。多家蒸餾廠加上穀物威士忌描述的是 Blended Scotch，不是 single malt。","Why do some producers choose not to chill-filter their whisky?":"為什麼有些生產者選擇不對威士忌做冷凝過濾？","They believe it removes flavour and texture":"他們認為它會去除風味和質地","Because Scottish law bans chill-filtration for all single malts":"因為蘇格蘭法律禁止所有 single malt 做冷凝過濾","To make the whisky clearer":"讓威士忌更清澈","To raise the alcohol strength":"提高酒精濃度","Some believe chill-filtration strips out character; others disagree.":"有些人認為冷凝過濾會去除特色；也有人不同意。","It is a choice, not a rule: many single malts are chill-filtered. Skipping it actually makes the whisky more prone to haze, not clearer, and it does not change the strength.":"這是一種選擇，不是規定：許多 single malt 都經過冷凝過濾。略過它其實會讓威士忌更容易混濁，而不是更清澈，也不會改變濃度。","How is chill-filtration carried out?":"冷凝過濾是怎麼進行的？","Chill, let the haze form, then filter it out":"降溫，讓混濁物形成，再濾除","Pass the warm whisky through maple charcoal":"讓溫熱的威士忌通過楓木炭","Freeze the whisky solid and discard the alcohol-rich part that stays liquid":"把威士忌完全冷凍，再丟掉仍是液態、酒精含量高的部分","Add ice to the casks":"在桶中加冰","Cold brings out the haze, which the filter then catches.":"低溫讓混濁物浮現，濾器再把它攔下。","Maple charcoal is Tennessee's Lincoln County Process, before barrelling. Freezing or icing casks is not part of it. The aim is to stop the whisky clouding in the bottle or with cold water.":"楓木炭是田納西州的 Lincoln County Process，在入桶前進行。冷凍或在桶中加冰都不屬於這個製程。目的是防止威士忌在瓶中或加冷水時變混濁。","Why do many Scottish blenders add a little caramel?":"為什麼許多蘇格蘭的調和師會加一點焦糖色？","To keep the same colour from batch to batch":"讓每一批的顏色保持相同","To sweeten the whisky and soften its taste, as with liqueurs":"像利口酒一樣讓威士忌變甜、味道更柔和","To add toffee notes":"增添太妃糖氣息","To make the whisky age faster":"讓威士忌更快熟成","Caramel corrects colour for consistency between batches, not taste.":"焦糖色修正的是顏色，讓各批一致，不是味道。","The caramel used is a tasteless food colouring, so it neither sweetens nor adds toffee. It has no effect on maturation speed, which depends on cask and temperature.":"使用的焦糖色是沒有味道的食用色素，所以既不增甜，也不增添太妃糖味。它對熟成速度沒有影響，熟成速度取決於桶和溫度。","Which statement about the caramel used in whisky is correct?":"關於威士忌使用的焦糖色，下列哪一項正確？","It is tasteless and only a little is needed":"它沒有味道，而且只需要一點點","Large amounts are used to add body and sweetness":"大量使用以增加酒體和甜味","It is always shown on the label as 'natural colour'":"一律在酒標上標示為「natural colour」","It is banned in all Scotch":"所有 Scotch 都禁止使用","It is a very effective, tasteless food colouring: small doses are enough.":"它是非常有效、沒有味道的食用色素：少量就足夠。","It is not used for body or sweetness. 'Natural colour' means exactly the opposite: no caramel added. Caramel is allowed in much Scotch, though some producers choose not to use it.":"它不是用來增加酒體或甜味的。「Natural colour」的意思恰恰相反：沒有添加焦糖色。許多 Scotch 都允許使用焦糖色，不過有些生產者選擇不用。","How common are Scotch whiskies bottled at 'cask strength'?":"以「cask strength」裝瓶的 Scotch 威士忌有多常見？","There are few: they are speciality bottlings":"很少：它們是特殊裝瓶","They are standard for all single malts and most blends":"是所有 single malt 和大多數調和威士忌的標準做法","They are compulsory for Islay Scotch":"是 Islay Scotch 的強制規定","They do not exist in Scotland":"在蘇格蘭不存在","Only a small number of speciality whiskies are bottled without added water.":"只有少數特殊的威士忌不加水就裝瓶。","Most Scotch is diluted before bottling. Islay has no strength rules of its own, and cask strength does exist in Scotland, even though it is rare.":"大多數 Scotch 在裝瓶前都經過稀釋。Islay 沒有自己的濃度規定，而 cask strength 在蘇格蘭確實存在，只是很少見。","A customer finds a cask strength whisky too fiery. What is sensible advice?":"一位顧客覺得一款 cask strength 威士忌太嗆。什麼是合理的建議？","Add a little water":"加一點水","Warm the glass to evaporate the alcohol":"把杯子加熱讓酒精蒸發","Add a spoon of sugar to balance the strength":"加一匙糖來平衡濃度","Give up: a cask strength whisky cannot be diluted without ruining it":"放棄：cask strength 威士忌一稀釋就毀了","A little water lowers the strength in the glass and often opens up the aromas.":"一點水能降低杯中的濃度，也常讓香氣展開。","Cask strength only means the producer did not dilute: the drinker can. Warming the glass or adding sugar does not solve anything. If it is not chill-filtered it may turn slightly hazy, which is normal.":"Cask strength 只表示生產者沒有稀釋：飲用者可以自己加水。加熱杯子或加糖都解決不了問題。如果沒有經過冷凝過濾，它可能會略微混濁，這是正常的。","A Scotch with no caramel, aged briefly in casks used several times. Which colour is most likely?":"一款不加焦糖色、在用過好幾次的桶中短暫陳年的 Scotch。最可能是什麼顏色？","Deep, almost brown":"很深，幾乎是棕色","Opaque":"不透明","Dark amber, like a bourbon aged for years in the Kentucky heat":"深琥珀色，像在肯塔基州的高溫中陳年多年的 bourbon","Tired casks, little time and no caramel give a pale colour.":"疲乏的桶、時間短、沒有焦糖色，顏色就會很淺。","A deep colour comes from long ageing, new oak or lots of caramel. 'Opaque' is for liquids you cannot see through, like cream liqueurs. Bourbon colours fast because of new casks and heat.":"深色來自長期陳年、新橡木桶或大量焦糖色。「不透明」用於看不透的液體，例如奶油利口酒。bourbon 因為新桶和高溫而很快上色。","A single malt is sold by an independent bottler that does no distilling. What does the label usually show?":"一款 single malt 由不從事蒸餾的獨立裝瓶商販售。酒標上通常標示什麼？","Which distillery the whisky came from":"威士忌來自哪一家蒸餾廠","That it is a Blended Scotch":"它是 Blended Scotch","That it is not Scotch, because it was not bottled at the distillery":"它不是 Scotch，因為不是在蒸餾廠裝瓶","The name of the barley field":"大麥田的名稱","The independent bottler makes clear on the label which distillery the spirit came from.":"獨立裝瓶商會在酒標上清楚標明烈酒來自哪一家蒸餾廠。","Buying spirit to sell under one's own name is normal in the industry. The whisky is still a single malt from one distillery and still Scotch. Barley origin need not be shown.":"買進烈酒再以自己的名義販售，在業界很正常。這款威士忌仍然是來自單一蒸餾廠的 single malt，也仍然是 Scotch。大麥產地不需要標示。","A malt spirit has spent two years in oak in Scotland. Can it be sold as Scotch whisky?":"一款麥芽烈酒在蘇格蘭的橡木桶中存放了兩年。可以當作 Scotch 威士忌販售嗎？","No: it needs at least three years":"不行：至少需要三年","Yes, because as for American straight whiskey, two years in oak is enough":"可以，因為和美國的 straight 威士忌一樣，橡木桶兩年就夠了","Yes, if it is peated":"可以，只要有泥煤味","Yes, if it carries a region name":"可以，只要標示產區名稱","Every Scotch must spend at least three years in oak.":"每款 Scotch 都必須在橡木桶中存放至少三年。","Two years is the American rule for 'straight', not the Scotch rule. Peat and a region name do not change the minimum ageing.":"兩年是美國「straight」的規定，不是 Scotch 的規定。泥煤和產區名稱都不會改變最低陳年要求。","Which group of aromas comes from malted barley?":"哪一組香氣來自麥芽大麥？","Rye bread, pepper and allspice":"黑麥麵包、胡椒和多香果","Dried fruit and orange peel, typical of casks seasoned in Jerez":"果乾和橙皮，是在 Jerez 潤過的桶的典型特徵","Agave and olive":"龍舌蘭和橄欖","Malt gives cereal notes: porridge, flour, husk, malt.":"麥芽帶來穀物氣息：麥片粥、麵粉、穀殼、麥芽。","Rye bread and allspice belong to rye. Dried fruit and orange come from ex-Sherry casks, not the grain. Agave and olive describe Tequila and Mezcal.":"黑麥麵包和多香果屬於黑麥。果乾和橙皮來自 Sherry 桶，不是穀物。龍舌蘭和橄欖描述的是 Tequila 和 Mezcal。","Can a heavily peated single malt be balanced?":"重泥煤的 single malt 可以是平衡的嗎？","Yes, if the peat does not overwhelm all other flavours":"可以，只要泥煤沒有壓過其他所有風味","No, a peated whisky is unbalanced by definition":"不行，泥煤威士忌依定義就是失衡的","Yes, but only if diluted to 20% abv":"可以，但只有稀釋到 20% abv 時","No, unless it has been mixed with plenty of grain whisky to soften the smoke":"不行，除非混入大量穀物威士忌來柔化煙燻味","A strong character stays balanced if it leaves room for other flavours.":"強烈的特色只要為其他風味留出空間，仍然是平衡的。","Balance does not require everything to be moderate. Heavy dilution is not the test, and a single malt mixed with grain whisky would no longer be a single malt.":"平衡並不要求每樣東西都適中。大幅稀釋不是判斷標準，而混入穀物威士忌的 single malt 就不再是 single malt 了。","When water is added, a 'non-chill-filtered' single malt turns slightly hazy. What should be concluded?":"加水後，一款「non-chill-filtered」的 single malt 略微變混濁。應該得出什麼結論？","It is normal for an unfiltered whisky":"對未過濾的威士忌來說這很正常","The whisky is faulty and should be returned to the shop":"威士忌有缺陷，應該退回店家","It shows the whisky contains aniseed, which clouds strongly with water":"這表示威士忌含有茴香，遇水會明顯變混濁","The producer watered the whisky down":"生產者在威士忌裡摻了水","Without chill-filtration, cold or water can cause a slight haze.":"沒有經過冷凝過濾，低溫或水就可能造成輕微混濁。","For most spirits haze is a fault, but not for those deliberately left unfiltered. Strong clouding with water (louching) is typical of aniseed spirits, not whisky. Dilution by the producer does not cause this haze.":"對大多數烈酒來說混濁是缺陷，但對刻意不過濾的烈酒則不是。遇水明顯變混濁（louching）是茴香烈酒的典型特徵，不是威士忌。生產者的稀釋不會造成這種混濁。","A label reads: 'Highland Single Malt – Sherry Cask Finish – Natural Colour – Non-Chill-Filtered'. Which deduction is correct?":"酒標上寫著：「Highland Single Malt – Sherry Cask Finish – Natural Colour – Non-Chill-Filtered」。哪一項推論正確？","Its colour comes only from the casks":"它的顏色只來自桶","It spent its whole maturation in Sherry casks":"它整個熟成期都在 Sherry 桶中","It comes from several Highland distilleries, combined in a regional blend":"它來自多家 Highland 蒸餾廠，合成一款產區調和","It is bottled at cask strength":"它以 cask strength 裝瓶","'Natural colour' means no caramel: all the colour comes from the oak.":"「Natural colour」表示沒有焦糖色：所有顏色都來自橡木。","'Finish' only means a short final spell in a Sherry cask. 'Single' means one distillery. Non-chill-filtered does not mean cask strength: that would need its own mention.":"「Finish」只表示最後在 Sherry 桶中短暫存放。「Single」表示單一蒸餾廠。Non-chill-filtered 不代表 cask strength：那需要另外標示。","Which practice is NOT allowed for a Single Malt Scotch Whisky?":"Single Malt Scotch Whisky 不允許哪一種做法？","Distilling it in a column still":"用柱式蒸餾器蒸餾","Using peat to heat the green malt":"用泥煤加熱綠麥芽","Finishing it for some months in a cask that held Port":"在裝過 Port 的桶中過桶幾個月","Blending young and old whiskies from the same distillery":"調和同一家蒸餾廠年輕和老的威士忌","Single malt must be distilled in pot stills.":"Single malt 必須用壺式蒸餾器蒸餾。","Peat is optional, cask finishing is common and blending different ages from one distillery is normal: every single malt is such a blend.":"泥煤是可選的，過桶很常見，調和同一家蒸餾廠不同年數的酒也很正常：每款 single malt 都是這樣的調和。","Why are there so many ex-bourbon casks in Scotland?":"為什麼蘇格蘭有這麼多 bourbon 桶？","Bourbon must use new casks, so used ones are sold on":"bourbon 必須使用新桶，所以用過的桶就被轉賣","Because Scottish law requires only American casks for every whisky":"因為蘇格蘭法律規定每款威士忌只能用美國桶","Because they add a strong peaty flavour":"因為它們增添強烈的泥煤風味","Because they are the only casks with no colour":"因為它們是唯一不帶顏色的桶","Bourbon can only use each barrel once, so used barrels become available.":"bourbon 每個桶只能用一次，所以用過的桶就釋出來了。","No Scottish law requires American casks: Sherry casks are used too. Peat does not come from the cask. Ex-bourbon casks give colour and subtle coconut, vanilla and spice.":"沒有蘇格蘭法律規定使用美國桶：Sherry 桶也有人用。泥煤不是來自桶。Bourbon 桶帶來顏色以及淡淡的椰子、香草和香料。","Which pairing of Scotch whisky type and still is correct?":"下列哪一組 Scotch 威士忌類型與蒸餾器的配對是正確的？","Malt: pot still; grain: column still":"麥芽：壺式蒸餾器；穀物：柱式蒸餾器","Malt: column still; grain: pot still":"麥芽：柱式蒸餾器；穀物：壺式蒸餾器","Both in column stills":"兩者都用柱式蒸餾器","Both in pot stills, because column stills are banned across Scotland":"兩者都用壺式蒸餾器，因為蘇格蘭全境禁用柱式蒸餾器","Malt is distilled in pot stills, grain whisky in column stills.":"麥芽威士忌用壺式蒸餾器蒸餾，穀物威士忌用柱式蒸餾器。","The column still is not banned in Scotland: it is exactly what grain whisky uses, distilled to high strength. Single malt, by contrast, is tied by law to the pot still.":"柱式蒸餾器在蘇格蘭並未被禁止：穀物威士忌用的正是它，並蒸餾到高濃度。Single malt 則依法與壺式蒸餾器綁在一起。","Which rule applies to ALL Scotch whisky, malt, grain and blends alike?":"哪一項規定適用於所有 Scotch 威士忌，不論麥芽、穀物或調和？","At least three years in oak in Scotland":"在蘇格蘭的橡木桶中至少三年","Distillation in pot stills":"用壺式蒸餾器蒸餾","Region name always shown on the label, next to the age":"產區名稱一律標在酒標上，緊鄰年數","The three-year minimum in oak applies to every Scottish whisky.":"橡木桶三年的最低要求適用於每一款蘇格蘭威士忌。","Pot stills and malted barley only are single malt rules, not grain whisky rules. Regions appear mainly on single malts, rarely on blends.":"壺式蒸餾器和只用麥芽大麥是 single malt 的規定，不是穀物威士忌的。產區主要出現在 single malt 上，很少出現在調和威士忌上。","A distillery wants its malt to show more dried fruit and orange peel without changing the spirit. Which technique suits best?":"一家蒸餾廠想讓它的麥芽威士忌表現出更多果乾和橙皮，又不改變烈酒本身。哪一種技術最合適？","A finish in an ex-Sherry cask":"在 Sherry 桶中過桶","Heating the green malt over peat for longer than usual":"用泥煤加熱綠麥芽比平常更久","Using taller stills":"使用更高的蒸餾器","Chill-filtering it":"做冷凝過濾","Ex-Sherry casks are linked to dried fruit and orange peel.":"Sherry 桶與果乾和橙皮有關。","Peat adds smoke, not fruit. Taller stills would change the spirit, making it lighter. Chill-filtration is for clarity and adds no aroma.":"泥煤增添的是煙燻味，不是果香。更高的蒸餾器會改變烈酒，讓它更清淡。冷凝過濾是為了清澈度，不增添香氣。","Why are vanilla and coconut intense in a bourbon but only subtle in a Scotch aged in an ex-bourbon cask?":"為什麼香草和椰子在 bourbon 中很濃郁，在 bourbon 桶陳年的 Scotch 中卻只是淡淡的？","The cask has already been used and gives less flavour":"桶已經用過，給的風味較少","Scotch is filtered through maple charcoal, which removes most wood notes":"Scotch 經過楓木炭過濾，去除了大部分木質氣息","The casks are rinsed with salt water":"桶用鹽水沖洗過","Scotch matures for less than a year":"Scotch 熟成不到一年","A cask gives the most when new; on its second use it passes on much less.":"桶在全新時給得最多；第二次使用時傳遞的就少得多。","Scotland's cooler climate also slows exchange with the wood. Maple charcoal is for Tennessee Whiskey, before barrelling. Scotch ages at least three years, not under one.":"蘇格蘭較涼爽的氣候也減緩了與木頭的交換。楓木炭用於 Tennessee Whiskey，在入桶之前。Scotch 至少陳年三年，不是不到一年。","Which type of whisky dominates Canadian production?":"哪一種威士忌在加拿大的生產中占主導地位？","Blends":"調和威士忌","Single malts":"Single malt","Single-barrel whiskies":"單一桶威士忌","Unaged whiskies":"未陳年的威士忌","Canadian whisky is dominated by blends.":"加拿大威士忌以調和威士忌為主。","Canadian producers build their brands by combining a light base whisky with a small share of more pronounced whiskies. Single malts and single-barrel whiskies exist elsewhere but are not the core of Canadian production. Like all whisky, Canadian whisky is matured in oak.":"加拿大的生產者把清淡的基礎威士忌與少量香氣較明顯的威士忌結合，建立自己的品牌。Single malt 和單一桶威士忌在別處存在，但不是加拿大生產的核心。和所有威士忌一樣，加拿大威士忌在橡木桶中熟成。","How is a typical Canadian blend put together?":"典型的加拿大調和威士忌是怎麼組成的？","Lots of light corn whisky, a little flavouring whisky":"大量清淡的玉米威士忌，加一點調味威士忌","Lots of peated malt and a little grain":"大量泥煤麥芽威士忌和少量穀物威士忌","Equal parts of pot still and column still whiskies":"壺式和柱式蒸餾的威士忌各半","Only rye whiskies distilled to low strength and aged in brand-new oak":"只用蒸餾到低濃度、在全新橡木桶中陳年的黑麥威士忌","The base is a light corn whisky distilled to high strength, lifted by a small dose of flavouring whisky.":"基底是蒸餾到高濃度的清淡玉米威士忌，再用少量調味威士忌提味。","The flavouring whisky gives character, while high-strength corn gives lightness. Peated malt is more typical of Scotland, and combining pot and column still spirits is the formula of many Irish whiskeys. Rye alone at low strength would describe an American rye.":"調味威士忌帶來特色，高濃度的玉米威士忌帶來清淡感。泥煤麥芽更是蘇格蘭的典型，結合壺式和柱式蒸餾的烈酒則是許多愛爾蘭威士忌的配方。只用低濃度的黑麥描述的是美國的 rye。","Which grain are Canadian flavouring whiskies most often made from?":"加拿大的調味威士忌最常用哪一種穀物製成？","The most common flavouring whiskies in Canada are made from rye.":"加拿大最常見的調味威士忌是用黑麥做的。","Corn, by contrast, is the light base of the blend, distilled to high strength. Unmalted barley is an Irish feature, and rice is not one of the typical whisky grains.":"玉米則是調和中清淡的基底，蒸餾到高濃度。未發芽大麥是愛爾蘭的特色，米也不是典型的威士忌穀物。","In Canada, when can the term 'Canadian Rye Whisky' be used?":"在加拿大，什麼情況下可以使用「Canadian Rye Whisky」這個術語？","Whatever the share of rye in the blend":"不論調和中黑麥的比例是多少","Only with at least 51% rye in the grain":"只有穀物中黑麥至少 51% 時","Only if it is made from 100% rye":"只有用 100% 黑麥製成時","Only if it has spent at least two years in new, charred oak barrels":"只有在炙燒過的新橡木桶中存放至少兩年時","In Canada, 'Rye' may be used regardless of how much rye is in the final blend.":"在加拿大，不論最終調和中有多少黑麥，都可以使用「Rye」。","The name reflects the tradition of rye flavouring whiskies, not a minimum percentage. 51% rye and two years in new oak are American rules, for rye whiskey and for the term straight.":"這個名稱反映的是黑麥調味威士忌的傳統，不是最低百分比。51% 黑麥和新橡木桶兩年是美國的規定，分別針對 rye whiskey 和 straight 這個術語。","Why do many big Canadian brands have a very soft character?":"為什麼許多加拿大大品牌的特色非常柔和？","Because of the high share of corn whisky":"因為玉米威士忌的比例很高","Because they are filtered through maple charcoal before casking":"因為入桶前經過楓木炭過濾","Because they are distilled three times":"因為蒸餾三次","Because a lot of sugar is added just before bottling":"因為裝瓶前加了大量的糖","A high proportion of light corn whisky gives a soft, gentle blend.":"高比例的清淡玉米威士忌讓調和柔和溫順。","Corn whisky is distilled to high strength and carries little flavour. Maple-charcoal filtering is linked to Tennessee Whiskey, and triple distillation to Ireland. Sugar does not explain the Canadian style.":"玉米威士忌蒸餾到高濃度，帶的風味很少。楓木炭過濾與 Tennessee Whiskey 有關，三次蒸餾與愛爾蘭有關。糖不能解釋加拿大的風格。","A customer finds a big Canadian blend too gentle and wants more flavour. What should they look for?":"一位顧客覺得某款加拿大大品牌調和威士忌太溫和，想要更多風味。應該找什麼？","A whisky with more spirit from other grains":"含有更多其他穀物烈酒的威士忌","A whisky with an even higher share of corn":"玉米比例更高的威士忌","A whisky distilled to an even higher strength, to concentrate the flavours as much as possible":"蒸餾到更高濃度、以盡量濃縮風味的威士忌","A whisky filtered through activated charcoal":"經活性碳過濾的威士忌","More flavouring whisky from grains other than corn gives a bolder profile.":"更多用玉米以外的穀物做的調味威士忌，會讓輪廓更鮮明。","More corn would mean even more softness. Distilling to a higher strength makes a spirit more neutral, not more flavoursome. Activated charcoal can strip congeners and colour, so it would reduce flavour.":"更多玉米代表更柔和。蒸餾到更高的濃度會讓烈酒更中性，而不是更有風味。活性碳會去除同屬物和顏色，所以會減少風味。","In which pair of countries is it usually spelt 'whiskey', with an e?":"哪兩個國家通常拼成帶 e 的「whiskey」？","Ireland and the USA":"愛爾蘭和美國","Scotland and Canada":"蘇格蘭和加拿大","Japan and Scotland":"日本和蘇格蘭","Canada and the USA":"加拿大和美國","Ireland and the USA typically use the spelling 'whiskey'.":"愛爾蘭和美國通常使用「whiskey」這個拼法。","Scotland and Canada write 'whisky', without the e. Japan, following the Scottish model, also uses 'whisky'. The spelling on the label is therefore a first clue to origin.":"蘇格蘭和加拿大寫成不帶 e 的「whisky」。沿用蘇格蘭模式的日本也用「whisky」。所以酒標上的拼法是判斷產地的第一個線索。","Blends of pot and column still spirits":"壺式和柱式蒸餾烈酒的調和","Peated single malts distilled twice":"蒸餾兩次的泥煤 single malt","Whiskeys of at least 51% corn matured in new, charred oak barrels":"玉米至少 51%、在炙燒過的新橡木桶中熟成的威士忌","Unaged column still spirits":"未陳年的柱式蒸餾烈酒","Most Irish whiskeys combine pot still and column still spirits.":"大多數愛爾蘭威士忌結合了壺式蒸餾和柱式蒸餾的烈酒。","Some pot-still malt whiskey exists, but it is a smaller part. Peat is rare in Ireland and the malt tradition is triple distillation. 51% corn with new oak describes bourbon.":"也有一些壺式蒸餾的麥芽威士忌，但占比較小。泥煤在愛爾蘭很少見，麥芽威士忌的傳統是三次蒸餾。51% 玉米加新橡木桶描述的是 bourbon。","What is the traditional distillation method for Irish malt whiskey?":"愛爾蘭麥芽威士忌的傳統蒸餾方式是什麼？","Triple distillation in pot stills":"在壺式蒸餾器中三次蒸餾","Double distillation in pot stills":"在壺式蒸餾器中二次蒸餾","One pass through a column still, then filtering through maple-wood charcoal":"通過柱式蒸餾器一次，再用楓木炭過濾","A single pot still distillation":"只用壺式蒸餾器蒸餾一次","Irish malts are traditionally distilled three times in pot stills.":"愛爾蘭麥芽威士忌傳統上在壺式蒸餾器中蒸餾三次。","Triple distillation helps give Irish whiskeys their lighter style. Double distillation is the norm for most Scottish malts. Column plus maple charcoal recalls Tennessee Whiskey.":"三次蒸餾有助於讓愛爾蘭威士忌有較清淡的風格。二次蒸餾是大多數蘇格蘭麥芽威士忌的常態。蒸餾柱加楓木炭讓人想到 Tennessee Whiskey。","A customer loves very peaty whiskies and asks for a similar Irish whiskey. What is the best reply?":"一位顧客喜歡泥煤味很重的威士忌，想找類似的愛爾蘭威士忌。最好的回答是什麼？","Peat is rarely used in Ireland":"愛爾蘭很少使用泥煤","All Irish whiskeys are heavily peated":"所有愛爾蘭威士忌都有重泥煤味","Triple distillation always makes the smoky flavour much stronger":"三次蒸餾一定會讓煙燻風味強得多","Unmalted barley gives an intense peat aroma":"未發芽大麥帶來濃郁的泥煤香氣","Peat is rare in Irish whiskey, even in the malts.":"泥煤在愛爾蘭威士忌中很少見，即使是麥芽威士忌也一樣。","For a peaty profile, Islay is a better place to look. Triple distillation makes spirit lighter, not smokier, and unmalted barley gives spicy, fruity or oily notes, not smoke.":"想要泥煤風味，Islay 是更好的選擇。三次蒸餾讓烈酒更清淡，而不是更煙燻；未發芽大麥帶來的是辛香、果香或油潤的氣息，不是煙燻味。","Which aromas does unmalted barley give to Irish whiskey?":"未發芽大麥為愛爾蘭威士忌帶來哪些香氣？","Spicy, fruity or oily":"辛香、果香或油潤","Peat smoke and iodine":"泥煤煙和碘味","Vanilla, coconut and the sweet spice typical of new oak":"新橡木桶典型的香草、椰子和甜香料","Sweetcorn and banana":"甜玉米和香蕉","Unmalted barley brings notes described as spicy, fruity or oily.":"未發芽大麥帶來被形容為辛香、果香或油潤的氣息。","It is one of the most characteristic features of many Irish whiskeys. Smoke comes from peat, which is rare in Ireland; vanilla and coconut come from new oak; sweetcorn and banana are typical of Tennessee Whiskey.":"這是許多愛爾蘭威士忌最具代表性的特徵之一。煙燻味來自泥煤，在愛爾蘭很少見；香草和椰子來自新橡木桶；甜玉米和香蕉是 Tennessee Whiskey 的典型特徵。","Compared with Scotch, how is the style of Irish whiskey generally described?":"與 Scotch 相比，愛爾蘭威士忌的風格一般怎麼描述？","More marked by new oak, with lots of vanilla and coconut":"新橡木桶的印記更重，有大量香草和椰子","Stronger in alcohol by law":"依法酒精濃度更高","Irish whiskeys are typically lighter than Scotch.":"愛爾蘭威士忌通常比 Scotch 清淡。","Triple distillation, rare use of peat and blends with column still spirits all add to this lightness. Today, though, with many new distilleries, Irish styles are increasingly varied. New oak is bourbon's trait, and no rule makes Irish whiskey stronger.":"三次蒸餾、很少使用泥煤，以及與柱式蒸餾烈酒調和，都增添了這種清淡感。不過如今有許多新蒸餾廠，愛爾蘭的風格越來越多樣。新橡木桶是 bourbon 的特徵，也沒有規定讓愛爾蘭威士忌濃度更高。","What has changed in Irish whiskey in recent years?":"近年來愛爾蘭威士忌有什麼改變？","More distilleries and a wider range of styles":"蒸餾廠變多，風格也更多樣","The law now requires every producer to use peat":"法律現在規定每位生產者都要使用泥煤","Triple distillation has been banned in every distillery on the island":"島上每家蒸餾廠都禁止三次蒸餾","Blends have disappeared from the market":"調和威士忌已從市場上消失","The number of Irish distilleries has grown, and with it the variety of styles.":"愛爾蘭蒸餾廠的數量增加了，風格的多樣性也隨之增加。","The classic style remains light, with pot and column blends and triple-distilled malts, but it now sits alongside many new offerings. No rule has imposed peat or banned triple distillation, and blends are still the majority.":"經典的風格仍然清淡，有壺式與柱式的調和以及三次蒸餾的麥芽威士忌，但如今與許多新產品並存。沒有規定強制使用泥煤或禁止三次蒸餾，調和威士忌仍占多數。","Which production model does Japanese whisky follow?":"日本威士忌沿用哪一種生產模式？","The Scottish model":"蘇格蘭模式","The American bourbon model":"美國的 bourbon 模式","The Irish model, with triple distillation and unmalted barley":"愛爾蘭模式，三次蒸餾並使用未發芽大麥","The rye-based Canadian model":"以黑麥為主的加拿大模式","Japan makes whisky following the Scottish model.":"日本沿用蘇格蘭模式製作威士忌。","As in Scotland, grain whisky is distilled in column stills and malt whisky in pot stills, and both malts and blends are sold. Triple distillation, unmalted barley, corn with new oak, or rye-led blends belong to other traditions.":"和蘇格蘭一樣，穀物威士忌用柱式蒸餾器蒸餾，麥芽威士忌用壺式蒸餾器，麥芽威士忌和調和威士忌都有販售。三次蒸餾、未發芽大麥、玉米加新橡木桶，或以黑麥為主的調和，都屬於其他傳統。","Which categories of whisky do Japanese distilleries make and sell?":"日本的蒸餾廠生產並販售哪些類別的威士忌？","Both malt and blended whiskies":"麥芽威士忌和調和威士忌都有","Only malt whiskies, never blends":"只有麥芽威士忌，從不做調和","Only blends, because there are no pot stills in Japan at all":"只有調和威士忌，因為日本完全沒有壺式蒸餾器","Only grain whiskies sold on their own":"只有單獨販售的穀物威士忌","Using the grain and malt whiskies they make, Japanese producers create both malts and blends.":"日本的生產者用自己做的穀物威士忌和麥芽威士忌，製作麥芽威士忌和調和威士忌。","Japanese distilleries use both column stills and pot stills. Just as in Scotland, grain whisky mainly serves the blends and is not the main product sold on its own.":"日本的蒸餾廠同時使用柱式蒸餾器和壺式蒸餾器。和蘇格蘭一樣，穀物威士忌主要供調和使用，不是單獨販售的主要產品。","What usually sets the style of Japanese whisky apart from many Scotch whiskies?":"日本威士忌的風格通常與許多 Scotch 威士忌有什麼不同？","A purer style, with fewer malty, cereal notes":"風格更純淨，麥芽和穀物氣息較少","Much more intense peat smoke":"泥煤煙濃郁得多","Spicy, oily notes from the unmalted barley used in almost every recipe":"幾乎每個配方都用的未發芽大麥帶來辛香、油潤的氣息","A rye-dominated character":"以黑麥為主的特色","Japanese whiskies tend towards a purer style, less marked by malt and cereal.":"日本威士忌偏向更純淨的風格，麥芽和穀物的印記較少。","While following the Scottish model, Japan has developed its own character. Unmalted barley is an Irish trait, and rye marks American and Canadian ryes. Nothing suggests Japanese whisky is typically peatier than Scotch.":"日本雖然沿用蘇格蘭模式，卻發展出自己的特色。未發芽大麥是愛爾蘭的特徵，黑麥則是美國和加拿大 rye 的標誌。沒有跡象顯示日本威士忌通常比 Scotch 更有泥煤味。","In which pair of countries is it spelt 'whisky', without an e?":"哪兩個國家拼成不帶 e 的「whisky」？","The USA and Canada, because they follow the same North American rules":"美國和加拿大，因為兩國遵循相同的北美規定","Ireland and Scotland":"愛爾蘭和蘇格蘭","Scotland and Canada write 'whisky'; Ireland and the USA usually write 'whiskey'.":"蘇格蘭和加拿大寫成「whisky」；愛爾蘭和美國通常寫成「whiskey」。","Canada and the USA are neighbours but share neither spelling nor rules. Ireland normally uses the e, like the USA. A trick: countries with an e in their English name (Ireland, United States) write 'whiskey'.":"加拿大和美國是鄰國，但拼法和規定都不相同。愛爾蘭和美國一樣通常帶 e。一個訣竅：英文國名中有 e 的國家（Ireland、United States）寫成「whiskey」。","In Canadian blends, what makes the corn base whisky so gentle?":"在加拿大的調和威士忌中，什麼讓玉米基礎威士忌這麼溫和？","It is distilled to a high strength":"它蒸餾到高濃度","It is aged in Sherry casks":"它在 Sherry 桶中陳年","It is triple distilled in pot stills, as in the Irish tradition":"它依愛爾蘭傳統在壺式蒸餾器中三次蒸餾","It is sweetened":"它加了糖","The higher the distillation strength, the less aroma remains: hence the gentleness.":"蒸餾濃度越高，留下的香氣越少：所以溫和。","Sherry casks would add dried fruit, not lightness. Triple pot distillation belongs to Irish malts, not Canadian corn whiskies. Sugar does not explain a light style.":"Sherry 桶會增添果乾味，不是清淡感。壺式三次蒸餾屬於愛爾蘭麥芽威士忌，不是加拿大的玉米威士忌。糖不能解釋清淡的風格。","Which comparison between American rye whiskey and Canadian Rye Whisky is correct?":"關於美國的 rye whiskey 和 Canadian Rye Whisky，下列哪一項比較是正確的？","Only the American one requires at least 51% rye":"只有美國的要求黑麥至少 51%","Both require at least 51% rye":"兩者都要求黑麥至少 51%","Only the Canadian one needs 51% rye, while the American can contain very little":"只有加拿大的需要 51% 黑麥，美國的可以只含很少","Neither contains any rye":"兩者都不含黑麥","In Canada 'Rye' can be used whatever the share of rye in the blend.":"在加拿大，不論調和中黑麥的比例是多少，都可以使用「Rye」。","In the USA rye follows bourbon rules with rye in place of corn (51%+). In Canada the name comes from rye flavouring whiskies, even if corn dominates the blend. Both contain rye, in different amounts.":"在美國，rye 遵循 bourbon 的規定，只是以黑麥取代玉米（51% 以上）。在加拿大，這個名稱來自黑麥調味威士忌，即使調和中以玉米為主。兩者都含黑麥，只是量不同。","Which statement about Canadian whisky styles is correct?":"關於加拿大威士忌的風格，下列哪一項正確？","They range from very soft to more flavoursome":"從非常柔和到風味較濃都有","They are all heavily peated":"全都有重泥煤味","There is only one style, set by law for every distillery":"只有一種風格，由法律為每家蒸餾廠規定","They are all single malts":"全都是 single malt","The range is wide, depending on the share of corn whisky in the blend.":"範圍很廣，取決於調和中玉米威士忌的比例。","Big brands are soft thanks to lots of corn; more whisky from other grains gives more character. Peat is not a Canadian trait, and Canada is dominated by blends, not single malts.":"大品牌因為大量玉米而柔和；其他穀物的威士忌越多，特色越鮮明。泥煤不是加拿大的特徵，加拿大以調和威士忌為主，不是 single malt。","Which description does NOT fit a typical Canadian blend?":"下列哪一項描述不符合典型的加拿大調和威士忌？","It is mostly pot-still malted barley whisky":"主要是壺式蒸餾的麥芽大麥威士忌","It contains a lot of light corn whisky":"含有大量清淡的玉米威士忌","It includes a small share of flavouring whisky, often rye, for character":"含有少量調味威士忌（常是黑麥）以增添特色","It may be labelled 'Rye Whisky'":"可以標示為「Rye Whisky」","A Canadian blend is built on light corn whisky, not on pot-still malt.":"加拿大調和威士忌建立在清淡的玉米威士忌上，不是壺式蒸餾的麥芽威士忌。","The other three are true: a light corn base, a little flavouring whisky (usually rye) and the option to call it Rye whatever the rye share. Pot-still malt is the heart of Scottish single malts.":"其他三項都正確：清淡的玉米基底、少量調味威士忌（通常是黑麥），以及不論黑麥比例多少都可以稱為 Rye。壺式蒸餾的麥芽威士忌是蘇格蘭 single malt 的核心。","Besides blends, which type of whiskey is also made in Ireland?":"除了調和威士忌，愛爾蘭還生產哪一種威士忌？","Pot-still malt whiskey":"壺式蒸餾的麥芽威士忌","Tennessee Whiskey, filtered through maple charcoal before barrelling":"入桶前經楓木炭過濾的 Tennessee Whiskey","Alongside blends, Ireland also makes pot-still malt whiskey.":"除了調和威士忌，愛爾蘭也生產壺式蒸餾的麥芽威士忌。","Tennessee Whiskey and bourbon are American categories tied to the USA, and Scotch must be made in Scotland. None of them can come from Ireland.":"Tennessee Whiskey 和 bourbon 是與美國綁定的美國類別，Scotch 則必須在蘇格蘭製作。它們都不可能來自愛爾蘭。","How many times are an Irish malt and most Scottish single malts traditionally distilled?":"愛爾蘭麥芽威士忌和大多數蘇格蘭 single malt 傳統上各蒸餾幾次？","Ireland three, Scotland two":"愛爾蘭三次，蘇格蘭兩次","Ireland two, Scotland three":"愛爾蘭兩次，蘇格蘭三次","Both once, in a column":"兩者都用蒸餾柱蒸餾一次","Both three, a rule shared by the two countries since the 1800s":"兩者都三次，是兩國自 19 世紀以來的共同規定","Irish malts are traditionally distilled three times, Scottish ones usually twice.":"愛爾蘭麥芽威士忌傳統上蒸餾三次，蘇格蘭的通常兩次。","Both countries use pot stills for malt, not columns. Ireland's third distillation helps give a lighter style. No shared rule imposes three distillations.":"兩國的麥芽威士忌都用壺式蒸餾器，不是蒸餾柱。愛爾蘭的第三次蒸餾有助於形成較清淡的風格。沒有共同的規定強制三次蒸餾。","Why are Irish malts usually lighter than Scottish ones?":"為什麼愛爾蘭麥芽威士忌通常比蘇格蘭的清淡？","Triple distillation and rare use of peat":"三次蒸餾，而且很少使用泥煤","Because they are column distilled to 96% abv like a neutral spirit":"因為像中性烈酒一樣用蒸餾柱蒸餾到 96% abv","Because they mature for only a few months":"因為只熟成幾個月","Because they are made from corn":"因為用玉米製成","An extra distillation lightens the spirit, and without peat there is no smoke.":"多一次蒸餾讓烈酒更清淡，沒有泥煤就沒有煙燻味。","Irish malts are pot distilled, not column distilled to neutral. Lightness does not come from short maturation or corn: a malt is made from malted barley.":"愛爾蘭麥芽威士忌是用壺式蒸餾器蒸餾的，不是用蒸餾柱蒸餾到中性。清淡不是來自熟成時間短或玉米：麥芽威士忌用麥芽大麥製成。","Which ingredient is a distinctive feature of many Irish whiskeys?":"哪一種材料是許多愛爾蘭威士忌的鮮明特色？","At least 51% corn in the recipe, as in American bourbon":"配方中至少 51% 玉米，和美國 bourbon 一樣","Peated malt":"泥煤麥芽","Unmalted barley, common in Ireland, gives spicy, fruity or oily notes.":"未發芽大麥在愛爾蘭很常見，帶來辛香、果香或油潤的氣息。","51% corn is the bourbon rule. Peat is rarely used in Ireland. Agave is the raw material of Tequila and Mezcal.":"51% 玉米是 bourbon 的規定。泥煤在愛爾蘭很少使用。龍舌蘭是 Tequila 和 Mezcal 的原料。","In Japan, which type of still is used to make grain whisky?":"在日本，穀物威士忌用哪一種蒸餾器製作？","In column stills":"柱式蒸餾器","In pot stills, with triple distillation":"壺式蒸餾器，三次蒸餾","In peat-heated stills":"以泥煤加熱的蒸餾器","None is made in Japan; it is all imported ready-made from Scotland":"日本不生產；全部從蘇格蘭進口成品","As in Scotland, Japanese grain whisky is made in column stills and malt in pot stills.":"和蘇格蘭一樣，日本的穀物威士忌用柱式蒸餾器製作，麥芽威士忌用壺式蒸餾器。","Triple pot distillation is the Irish malt tradition. Peat smokes malt; it does not heat stills. Japanese distilleries make both grain and malt.":"壺式三次蒸餾是愛爾蘭麥芽威士忌的傳統。泥煤用來煙燻麥芽，不是加熱蒸餾器。日本的蒸餾廠穀物威士忌和麥芽威士忌都做。","A customer likes the structure of Scotch but finds it too malty and cereal-like. Which whisky could be suggested?":"一位顧客喜歡 Scotch 的結構，但覺得麥芽和穀物味太重。可以推薦哪一種威士忌？","A Japanese whisky":"日本威士忌","A heavily peated Islay single malt bottled at cask strength":"以 cask strength 裝瓶的 Islay 重泥煤 single malt","An American rye whiskey":"美國的 rye whiskey","Japanese whisky follows the Scottish model but has a purer, less malty style.":"日本威士忌沿用蘇格蘭模式，但風格更純淨、麥芽味較少。","A peated Islay is still a malt Scotch, with intense smoke on top. Rye and Tennessee are American whiskeys with a different structure: rye spice, or corn and new oak.":"泥煤味的 Islay 仍然是麥芽 Scotch，還多了濃郁的煙燻味。Rye 和 Tennessee 是結構不同的美國威士忌：黑麥的辛香，或是玉米加新橡木桶。","In which country are whiskies mostly blends of light corn whisky with a little rye flavouring whisky?":"哪一個國家的威士忌大多是清淡的玉米威士忌加一點黑麥調味威士忌的調和？","Japan, faithfully following the Scottish blend model":"日本，忠實沿用蘇格蘭的調和模式","It is the typical Canadian formula: a light corn base and a touch of rye.":"這是典型的加拿大配方：清淡的玉米基底加一點黑麥。","Irish blends combine pot- and column-still spirits, often with unmalted barley. Japan and Scotland combine barley malt and grain whisky, not a blend led by corn and rye.":"愛爾蘭的調和威士忌結合壺式和柱式蒸餾的烈酒，常含未發芽大麥。日本和蘇格蘭結合的是大麥麥芽威士忌和穀物威士忌，不是以玉米和黑麥為主的調和。","Mostly blends of pot and column spirit, triple-distilled malts, unmalted barley, rare peat: which country is this?":"大多是壺式和柱式烈酒的調和、三次蒸餾的麥芽威士忌、未發芽大麥、很少用泥煤：這是哪個國家？","The USA, in the state of Tennessee":"美國，在田納西州","These are all typical traits of Irish whiskey.":"這些都是愛爾蘭威士忌的典型特徵。","In Scotland malts are usually distilled twice and peat is common in some areas. Canada relies on light corn, Tennessee on corn and maple charcoal.":"在蘇格蘭，麥芽威士忌通常蒸餾兩次，泥煤在某些地區很常見。加拿大靠的是清淡的玉米威士忌，田納西州則是玉米和楓木炭。","A bartender swaps the rye in a Manhattan. Which pairing is correct?":"一位調酒師更換 Manhattan 中的 rye。哪一組配對是正確的？","Irish whiskey: Emerald; Scotch: Rob Roy":"愛爾蘭威士忌：Emerald；Scotch：Rob Roy","Irish whiskey: Rob Roy; Scotch: Emerald":"愛爾蘭威士忌：Rob Roy；Scotch：Emerald","Irish whiskey: Sazerac; Scotch: Old Fashioned":"愛爾蘭威士忌：Sazerac；Scotch：Old Fashioned","With any whisky it is still a Manhattan; the name never changes":"用任何威士忌都還是 Manhattan；名稱永遠不變","With Irish whiskey a Manhattan becomes an Emerald; with Scotch, a Rob Roy.":"用愛爾蘭威士忌，Manhattan 就變成 Emerald；用 Scotch 則是 Rob Roy。","Rob Roy is a Scottish name, and Emerald recalls the Emerald Isle, Ireland. Sazerac and Old Fashioned are other spirit-forward cocktails, not Manhattan variants. With bourbon, though, the name stays Manhattan.":"Rob Roy 是蘇格蘭的名字，Emerald 則讓人想到翡翠島愛爾蘭。Sazerac 和 Old Fashioned 是其他烈酒主導型調酒，不是 Manhattan 的變化版。不過用 bourbon 時，名稱仍然是 Manhattan。","What goes into an Irish coffee?":"Irish coffee 裡有什麼？","Coffee, Irish whiskey, sugar, cream":"咖啡、愛爾蘭威士忌、糖、鮮奶油","Coffee, Scotch whisky, honey, milk":"咖啡、Scotch 威士忌、蜂蜜、牛奶","Cold coffee, Irish whiskey, crushed ice, mint syrup and mint leaves":"冰咖啡、愛爾蘭威士忌、碎冰、薄荷糖漿和薄荷葉","Tea, Irish whiskey, lemon":"茶、愛爾蘭威士忌、檸檬","Hot coffee, Irish whiskey, sugar and cream, served in a toddy glass.":"熱咖啡、愛爾蘭威士忌、糖和鮮奶油，用 toddy 杯盛裝。","It is a hot drink, so no ice: that is why it is served in a toddy glass, one of the few glasses designed for hot drinks. Scotch or tea would make a completely different drink.":"它是熱飲，所以不加冰：因此用 toddy 杯盛裝，這是少數為熱飲設計的杯子之一。用 Scotch 或茶會變成完全不同的飲品。","Which group lists the five countries with an established reputation for premium whisky?":"哪一組列出了在高級威士忌方面享有既定聲譽的五個國家？","USA, Canada, Scotland, Ireland, Japan":"美國、加拿大、蘇格蘭、愛爾蘭、日本","France, Italy, Spain, Scotland, Ireland":"法國、義大利、西班牙、蘇格蘭、愛爾蘭","Mexico, Peru, Chile, USA, Canada":"墨西哥、秘魯、智利、美國、加拿大","Poland, Russia, Sweden, Finland and Scotland, the homes of grain spirits":"波蘭、俄羅斯、瑞典、芬蘭和蘇格蘭，穀物烈酒的故鄉","The USA, Canada, Scotland, Ireland and Japan are the big names in premium whisky.":"美國、加拿大、蘇格蘭、愛爾蘭和日本是高級威士忌的大國。","France, Italy and Spain are known for wine and fruit spirits, Mexico, Peru and Chile for Tequila, Mezcal and Pisco. Poland, Russia, Sweden and Finland are the traditional vodka countries.":"法國、義大利和西班牙以葡萄酒和水果烈酒聞名，墨西哥、秘魯和智利以 Tequila、Mezcal 和 Pisco 聞名。波蘭、俄羅斯、瑞典和芬蘭是傳統的伏特加國家。","Bourbon and Canadian base whisky both use lots of corn. Why is the Canadian one much lighter?":"Bourbon 和加拿大的基礎威士忌都使用大量玉米。為什麼加拿大的清淡得多？","It is distilled to a much higher strength":"它蒸餾到高得多的濃度","It uses a different corn variety, grown only in Canada's coldest provinces":"它使用不同的玉米品種，只種在加拿大最冷的省份","It is not aged in wood":"它不在木桶中陳年","It is filtered through maple charcoal":"它經過楓木炭過濾","Bourbon stops at 80% abv; Canadian base whisky is taken much higher.":"Bourbon 止於 80% abv；加拿大的基礎威士忌蒸餾到高得多的濃度。","Same raw material, different choices: distillation strength decides how many congeners remain. All whisky matures in oak, and maple charcoal is a Tennessee feature. Corn variety is not the factor here.":"同樣的原料，不同的選擇：蒸餾濃度決定留下多少同屬物。所有威士忌都在橡木桶中熟成，楓木炭是田納西州的特色。玉米品種不是這裡的因素。","What do Scottish and Japanese whisky production have in common?":"蘇格蘭和日本的威士忌生產有什麼共同點？","Malt in pot stills, grain in columns, both malts and blends":"麥芽用壺式蒸餾器、穀物用蒸餾柱，麥芽威士忌和調和威士忌都有","Both mainly use corn and rye, as in North American blends":"兩者都主要使用玉米和黑麥，像北美的調和威士忌","Both triple distil all their malts":"兩者的麥芽威士忌都全部三次蒸餾","Both sell only single malts":"兩者都只賣 single malt","Japan adopted the Scottish model: two kinds of spirit and two categories on sale.":"日本採用了蘇格蘭模式：兩種烈酒，兩個販售類別。","Corn and rye as main grains describe North America. Triple distillation is Irish, not Scottish or Japanese. Both countries also sell blends.":"以玉米和黑麥為主要穀物描述的是北美。三次蒸餾是愛爾蘭的，不是蘇格蘭或日本的。兩國也都賣調和威士忌。","What do most Irish whiskeys and Blended Scotch have in common?":"大多數愛爾蘭威士忌和 Blended Scotch 有什麼共同點？","They combine pot-still and column-still spirits":"它們結合壺式蒸餾和柱式蒸餾的烈酒","They are made from at least 51% corn and aged in new charred oak":"它們用至少 51% 的玉米製成，並在炙燒過的新橡木桶中陳年","They come from a single distillery":"它們來自單一蒸餾廠","Both bring together pot-still and column-still spirit.":"兩者都結合了壺式蒸餾和柱式蒸餾的烈酒。","Peat is rare in Ireland and optional in Scotland. 51% corn and new oak are bourbon rules. A Blended Scotch, by definition, comes from several distilleries.":"泥煤在愛爾蘭很少見，在蘇格蘭則是可選的。51% 玉米和新橡木桶是 bourbon 的規定。Blended Scotch 依定義來自多家蒸餾廠。","Which statement about Irish whiskey is correct?":"關於愛爾蘭威士忌，下列哪一項正確？","Its styles are more varied than in the past":"它的風格比過去更多樣","No malt is made any more, since every distillery makes only column blends":"已不再生產麥芽威士忌，因為每家蒸餾廠都只做蒸餾柱的調和","Peat is used in almost every whiskey":"幾乎每款威士忌都使用泥煤","The number of distilleries is falling":"蒸餾廠的數量正在減少","With more distilleries, Ireland now offers a wider range of styles.":"蒸餾廠變多了，愛爾蘭如今提供更多樣的風格。","Alongside blends, pot-still malt is still made. Peat remains rare, and distilleries are increasing, not falling.":"除了調和威士忌，壺式蒸餾的麥芽威士忌仍在生產。泥煤仍然少見，蒸餾廠是在增加，不是減少。","Which of these whiskies usually has the softest, lightest style?":"下列哪一種威士忌通常風格最柔和、最清淡？","A big-brand Canadian blend":"加拿大大品牌的調和威士忌","An Islay single malt":"Islay single malt","A straight American rye whiskey, with its marked rye spice":"美國的 straight rye whiskey，帶鮮明的黑麥辛香","A bourbon":"Bourbon","Big Canadian blends are soft because of their high share of light corn whisky.":"加拿大的大品牌調和威士忌很柔和，因為清淡的玉米威士忌比例很高。","Islay is known for intense peat, rye for spice and bourbon for bold flavours and a warming texture, thanks to low strength and new oak.":"Islay 以濃郁的泥煤聞名，rye 以辛香聞名，bourbon 則因低蒸餾濃度和新橡木桶而以強勁的風味和溫熱的口感聞名。","A Japanese blended whisky most likely combines…":"日本的調和威士忌最可能結合了……","column-still grain whisky and pot-still malt":"柱式蒸餾的穀物威士忌和壺式蒸餾的麥芽威士忌","corn whiskey and rye whiskey":"玉米威士忌和 rye whiskey","triple-distilled malts with unmalted barley, in the Irish tradition":"依愛爾蘭傳統三次蒸餾的麥芽威士忌與未發芽大麥","whisky and liqueur":"威士忌和利口酒","As in Scotland, Japanese blends combine malt and grain whisky.":"和蘇格蘭一樣，日本的調和威士忌結合麥芽威士忌和穀物威士忌。","Corn and rye describe Canada, triple distillation and unmalted barley Ireland. A whisky blend contains no liqueur, which is a separate, always-sweetened category.":"玉米和黑麥描述的是加拿大，三次蒸餾和未發芽大麥描述的是愛爾蘭。調和威士忌不含利口酒，那是另一個一定加糖的類別。","Under international laws and agreements, what can anyone expect on seeing the word 'whisky' on a label, in any country?":"依照國際法規和協議，在任何國家的酒標上看到「whisky」這個字，都可以期待什麼？","That it is made from grain":"它是用穀物製成的","That it was aged at least three years in Scotland":"它在蘇格蘭陳年了至少三年","That it contains at least 51% corn, as international rules require":"它依國際規定含至少 51% 的玉米","On the fundamental point the laws agree: whisky is made from grain.":"在最根本的這一點上，各國法規是一致的：威士忌用穀物製成。","Three years in Scotland applies only to Scotch, 51% corn only to bourbon and Tennessee. Pot stills are required for Scottish single malt, but many whiskies worldwide use column stills.":"在蘇格蘭三年只適用於 Scotch，51% 玉米只適用於 bourbon 和 Tennessee。壺式蒸餾器是蘇格蘭 single malt 的要求，但全世界許多威士忌都使用柱式蒸餾器。","A Canadian whisky is labelled 'Rye Whisky'. Which grain probably makes up most of the blend?":"一款加拿大威士忌標示為「Rye Whisky」。調和中占大部分的可能是哪一種穀物？","Rye, at least 51%, as Canadian law requires for that name":"黑麥，至少 51%，因為加拿大法律對這個名稱有此要求","Peated malted barley":"泥煤麥芽大麥","A typical Canadian blend is mostly light corn whisky; rye is the flavouring touch.":"典型的加拿大調和威士忌大部分是清淡的玉米威士忌；黑麥只是調味的點綴。","In Canada the name 'Rye' needs no minimum share of rye: it applies whatever the amount. Peat is not typical of Canada, and unmalted barley is an Irish feature.":"在加拿大，「Rye」這個名稱不需要黑麥的最低比例：不論多少都適用。泥煤不是加拿大的典型特徵，未發芽大麥則是愛爾蘭的特色。","Some producers use only pronounced spirits and find complexity through different ages and woods; others combine a little pronounced spirit with lots of light whisky. Which approach is typical of Canada?":"有些生產者只用香氣明顯的烈酒，透過不同的年數和木桶取得複雜度；另一些則把少量香氣明顯的烈酒與大量清淡的威士忌結合。哪一種做法是加拿大的典型？","The second: a little flavouring whisky, lots of light whisky":"第二種：少量調味威士忌，大量清淡威士忌","The first: only pronounced spirits of different ages":"第一種：只用不同年數的香氣明顯的烈酒","Neither, because blending is banned in Canada and only single-cask whiskies are sold":"都不是，因為加拿大禁止調和，只賣單一桶威士忌","Both equally, with no preference":"兩種一樣多，沒有偏好","Canada combines a little flavouring whisky (often rye) with a light, high-strength corn base.":"加拿大把少量調味威士忌（常是黑麥）與清淡、高濃度的玉米基底結合。","The first approach, only pronounced spirits, is closer to a single malt, which is still a blend of ages from one distillery. In Canada blending is the norm, not banned.":"第一種做法，也就是只用香氣明顯的烈酒，比較接近 single malt，它仍是同一家蒸餾廠不同年數的調和。在加拿大，調和是常態，並未被禁止。","Many Irish whiskeys contain unmalted barley. How does its starch become sugar?":"許多愛爾蘭威士忌含有未發芽大麥。它的澱粉如何變成糖？","It is cooked, then malted barley supplies the enzymes":"先烹煮，再由麥芽大麥提供酵素","The yeast turns the starch straight into alcohol":"酵母把澱粉直接變成酒精","It is dried over a peat fire until the starch turns sweet":"在泥煤火上烘乾，直到澱粉變甜","Charcoal filtering after distillation releases its sugars":"蒸餾後的木炭過濾釋放出它的糖","Unmalted grains are cooked to make the starch soluble, then enzymes from malted barley convert it.":"未發芽的穀物先烹煮讓澱粉可溶，再由麥芽大麥的酵素加以轉化。","Yeast can only ferment sugar, not starch, so conversion has to happen first. A peat fire, when used, dries the green malt and adds smoke, not sugar. Filtering comes after distillation, far too late to create fermentable sugar.":"酵母只能發酵糖，不能發酵澱粉，所以必須先轉化。泥煤火（如果使用）是用來烘乾綠麥芽並增添煙燻味，不是糖。過濾在蒸餾之後，太晚了，無法產生可發酵的糖。","Apart from being made from grain, what do the premium whiskies of Ireland, Canada, Japan, Scotland and the USA have in common?":"除了用穀物製成，愛爾蘭、加拿大、日本、蘇格蘭和美國的高級威士忌還有什麼共同點？","At least 51% corn in the grain recipe":"穀物配方中至少 51% 玉米","A duty to blend spirits from several different distilleries":"必須調和多家不同蒸餾廠的烈酒","Grain and oak maturation are the two shared points; style varies with grains, distillation strength and barrels.":"穀物和橡木桶熟成是兩個共同點；風格則隨穀物、蒸餾濃度和桶而異。","Triple distillation is typical of Irish malts, not of the other countries. The 51% corn rule belongs to Bourbon and Tennessee Whiskey. Scottish single malts come from just one distillery by definition, so blending across distilleries is not a shared duty.":"三次蒸餾是愛爾蘭麥芽威士忌的典型做法，不是其他國家的。51% 玉米的規定屬於 Bourbon 和 Tennessee Whiskey。蘇格蘭 single malt 依定義只來自一家蒸餾廠，所以跨蒸餾廠調和不是共同的義務。","The light corn whisky in a Canadian blend is distilled to a high strength. Which still makes this possible?":"加拿大調和威士忌中的清淡玉米威士忌蒸餾到高濃度。哪一種蒸餾器讓這成為可能？","A pot still used for a single distillation":"只蒸餾一次的壺式蒸餾器","A pot still with a very long lyne arm":"林恩臂非常長的壺式蒸餾器","A pot still followed by a maple-charcoal filter":"壺式蒸餾器後接楓木炭濾器","Only a column, with its many plates, reaches the high strengths that give such a light whisky.":"只有具備許多蒸餾板的蒸餾柱，才能達到做出這麼清淡的威士忌所需的高濃度。","A pot still works in batches and gives lower strengths with more congeners, so it suits flavouring whiskies, not the light base. A long lyne arm shifts the style a little but cannot reach column strengths. The maple-charcoal filter is Tennessee's Lincoln County Process and is not a still at all.":"壺式蒸餾器以批次運作，濃度較低、同屬物較多，所以適合調味威士忌，不適合清淡的基底。長的林恩臂會稍微改變風格，但達不到蒸餾柱的濃度。楓木炭濾器是田納西州的 Lincoln County Process，根本不是蒸餾器。","Tasting an Irish whiskey, you find spicy, fruity and slightly oily notes. Which ingredient best explains them?":"品嚐一款愛爾蘭威士忌時，你發現辛香、果香和略帶油潤的氣息。哪一種材料最能解釋它們？","A high share of corn":"高比例的玉米","Rye flavouring whisky, as used in Canada":"黑麥調味威士忌，像加拿大使用的","Unmalted barley, a hallmark of many Irish whiskeys, gives spicy, fruity or oily aromas.":"未發芽大麥是許多愛爾蘭威士忌的標誌，帶來辛香、果香或油潤的香氣。","Peat would give smoky notes and is rare in Ireland. Corn gives a soft, sweet character, typical of Bourbon and the Canadian base. Rye gives spicy rye-bread notes, but it is Canada's flavouring grain, not the Irish signature.":"泥煤會帶來煙燻氣息，而且在愛爾蘭很少見。玉米帶來柔和、甜美的特色，是 Bourbon 和加拿大基底的典型。黑麥帶來辛香的黑麥麵包氣息，但它是加拿大的調味穀物，不是愛爾蘭的招牌。","A rare Irish whiskey shows smoky aromas. At which stage did the smoke most likely get in?":"一款少見的愛爾蘭威士忌表現出煙燻香氣。煙燻味最可能在哪個階段進入？","When the green malt was heated over a peat fire":"在泥煤火上加熱綠麥芽時","During fermentation, thanks to a special yeast":"發酵時，靠特殊的酵母","At the third distillation, because the pot still was heated by direct fire":"第三次蒸餾時，因為壺式蒸餾器用直火加熱","When it was diluted with water before bottling":"裝瓶前加水稀釋時","If peat is the fuel used to heat the green malt, its smoke passes into the malted barley and then into the whiskey.":"如果用泥煤作為加熱綠麥芽的燃料，它的煙會進入麥芽大麥，再進入威士忌。","Yeast creates fruity and floral congeners, not smoke. The way a still is heated does not put peat aromas into the spirit. Dilution water should be clean and neutral. Since peat is rarely used in Ireland, a smoky whiskey is an exception.":"酵母產生的是果香和花香的同屬物，不是煙。蒸餾器的加熱方式不會把泥煤香氣帶進烈酒。稀釋用的水應該乾淨而中性。由於愛爾蘭很少使用泥煤，煙燻味的威士忌是例外。","Which of these features is NOT typical of Irish whiskey?":"下列哪一項特徵不是愛爾蘭威士忌的典型？","Malts distilled twice, as in Scotland":"和蘇格蘭一樣蒸餾兩次的麥芽威士忌","Blends of pot-still and column-still spirits":"壺式蒸餾和柱式蒸餾烈酒的調和","The use of unmalted barley in the recipe":"配方中使用未發芽大麥","A style that is generally lighter than Scotch":"整體上比 Scotch 清淡的風格","Irish malt is traditionally distilled three times, not twice.":"愛爾蘭麥芽威士忌傳統上蒸餾三次，不是兩次。","Double distillation is the norm for most Scottish single malts. Pot-and-column blends, unmalted barley and a lighter style are all typical Irish traits. Triple distillation is part of what makes Irish malts lighter.":"二次蒸餾是大多數蘇格蘭 single malt 的常態。壺式與柱式的調和、未發芽大麥和較清淡的風格都是典型的愛爾蘭特徵。三次蒸餾是讓愛爾蘭麥芽威士忌較清淡的原因之一。","Which of these freshly made spirits was most likely distilled to the highest strength?":"下列剛做好的新酒中，哪一種最可能蒸餾到最高的濃度？","The corn base whisky for a Canadian blend":"加拿大調和威士忌用的玉米基礎威士忌","A new-make spirit destined to become Bourbon":"準備做成 Bourbon 的新酒","An Irish pot-still whiskey, distilled three times":"蒸餾三次的愛爾蘭壺式蒸餾威士忌","A Japanese malt made in pot stills":"用壺式蒸餾器做的日本麥芽威士忌","The Canadian base is distilled to a high strength in a column to give a light whisky.":"加拿大的基底用蒸餾柱蒸餾到高濃度，做出清淡的威士忌。","Bourbon is often column-distilled too, but the law requires a fairly low distillation strength to keep flavour. Pot stills, even with three runs, stay below column strengths. That is why Canadian corn whisky is much softer than Bourbon.":"Bourbon 也常用蒸餾柱蒸餾，但法律要求相當低的蒸餾濃度以保留風味。壺式蒸餾器即使蒸餾三次，濃度仍低於蒸餾柱。所以加拿大的玉米威士忌比 Bourbon 柔和得多。","You compare an Irish pot-still whiskey with a Japanese single malt. Which difference is most likely?":"你比較一款愛爾蘭壺式蒸餾威士忌和一款日本 single malt。最可能有什麼差別？","Only the Irish one is likely to contain unmalted barley":"只有愛爾蘭的可能含有未發芽大麥","Only the Japanese one is column-distilled":"只有日本的用蒸餾柱蒸餾","Only the Irish one is made from grain":"只有愛爾蘭的用穀物製成","Only the Japanese one must legally contain at least 51% corn":"只有日本的依法必須含至少 51% 的玉米","Unmalted barley is an Irish trait; Japanese malt follows the Scottish model, malted barley in pot stills.":"未發芽大麥是愛爾蘭的特徵；日本麥芽威士忌沿用蘇格蘭模式，用壺式蒸餾器蒸餾麥芽大麥。","In Japan the column is used for grain whisky, not for malt. Every whisky, everywhere, is made from grain. The 51% corn rule applies to American Bourbon, not to Japan.":"在日本，蒸餾柱用於穀物威士忌，不是麥芽威士忌。任何地方的威士忌都是用穀物做的。51% 玉米的規定適用於美國的 Bourbon，不是日本。","What raw material is every rum made from?":"所有蘭姆酒都用什麼原料製成？","Sugar beet":"甜菜","Malted grains":"麥芽穀物","Any sugary agricultural material":"任何含糖的農業原料","Rum, in every style, is always made from sugar cane.":"蘭姆酒不論哪種風格，一律用甘蔗製成。","Whether fresh juice or molasses is used, the source is always cane. Beet gives sugar but not rum, and it was France's preference for beet that freed up the French islands' cane juice for distilling. \"Any agricultural material\" describes vodka, not rum.":"不論使用新鮮甘蔗汁還是糖蜜，來源都是甘蔗。甜菜能製糖，但做不出蘭姆酒；正是法國偏好甜菜，才讓法屬島嶼的甘蔗汁空出來可以蒸餾。「任何農業原料」描述的是伏特加，不是蘭姆酒。","The thick residue left after sugar is extracted":"提取糖之後剩下的濃稠殘餘物","The juice freshly pressed from cane stems":"從甘蔗莖新鮮壓榨的汁液","A caramel syrup used to colour dark rums":"用來為深色蘭姆酒上色的焦糖糖漿","The fermented liquid ready for distilling":"可以拿去蒸餾的發酵液","Molasses is the sticky by-product of refining cane sugar.":"糖蜜是精煉蔗糖時產生的黏稠副產品。","The sugar industry heats cane juice and crystallises out the sugar; what is left is molasses, better quality early in refining and poorer at the end. Fresh juice is a different raw material, caramel is a colouring, and the fermented liquid comes later in the process.":"製糖業把甘蔗汁加熱並讓糖結晶析出；剩下的就是糖蜜，精煉初期的品質較好，最後的較差。新鮮甘蔗汁是另一種原料，焦糖色是色素，發酵液則是製程中較後面的東西。","Why is molasses diluted with water before fermentation?":"為什麼糖蜜在發酵前要加水稀釋？","Its sugar content is too high to ferment":"它的含糖量太高，無法發酵","To remove its dark colour before distillation":"在蒸餾前去除它的深色","To lower its acidity, which would kill all the yeast":"降低它的酸度，否則會殺死所有酵母","To produce a low-strength rum straight away":"直接做出低濃度的蘭姆酒","Molasses is so concentrated in sugar that yeast could not get started.":"糖蜜的糖濃度太高，酵母無法開始作用。","The water brings the sugar down to a level at which yeast can work. Colour is not removed at this stage, and the rum's strength depends on distillation, not on how the molasses is diluted. Acidity is not the reason for adding water.":"加水把糖降到酵母能運作的程度。這個階段不會去除顏色，而蘭姆酒的濃度取決於蒸餾，不是糖蜜怎麼稀釋。酸度不是加水的原因。","Which aromas are typical of rums made from sugar cane juice?":"哪些香氣是甘蔗汁蘭姆酒的典型特徵？","Vegetal, grassy and fruity":"植物、青草和果香","Smoky, earthy and peaty":"煙燻、土壤和泥煤","Vanilla, coconut and toasted wood":"香草、椰子和烘烤木頭","Honey, white flowers and candied fruit":"蜂蜜、白花和糖漬水果","Fresh juice gives rums a marked vegetal, grassy and fruity character.":"新鮮甘蔗汁賦予蘭姆酒鮮明的植物、青草和果香特色。","These aromas link rhum agricole and cachaça, especially when distilled to a low strength. Vanilla and coconut come from oak, not from the raw material. Smoky, earthy notes point to Mezcal or certain whiskies rather than cane juice rum.":"這些香氣是 rhum agricole 和 cachaça 的共同點，尤其是蒸餾到低濃度時。香草和椰子來自橡木，不是原料。煙燻、土壤氣息指向 Mezcal 或某些威士忌，而不是甘蔗汁蘭姆酒。","What gives high-ester rums their pungent fruity aroma?":"什麼讓高酯蘭姆酒有刺激的果香？","Ester-rich fermentation plus pot stills":"富含酯類的發酵加上壺式蒸餾器","Long ageing in new oak barrels":"在新橡木桶中長期陳年","Column distillation to more than 90% abv":"用蒸餾柱蒸餾到 90% abv 以上","Adding tropical fruit before bottling":"裝瓶前加入熱帶水果","Ester-boosting fermentations combined with pot stills create the high-ester style.":"促進酯類生成的發酵，結合壺式蒸餾器，造就了高酯風格。","Esters are fruity congeners created during fermentation; a pot still, distilling to a low strength, keeps them. A column above 90% would do the opposite, stripping out most aromas. Ageing does not create this character, and adding fruit would turn the rum into a flavoured spirit.":"酯類是發酵中產生的果香同屬物；壺式蒸餾器蒸餾到低濃度，能把它們保留下來。90% 以上的蒸餾柱則相反，會去除大部分香氣。陳年不會創造這種特色，而加水果會讓蘭姆酒變成調味烈酒。","In rum making, what does the word \"mark\" mean?":"在蘭姆酒的製作中，「mark」這個字是什麼意思？","An individual newly made rum":"一款個別的新製蘭姆酒","A legal ageing category":"法定的陳年類別","A quality grade of the molasses used":"所用糖蜜的品質等級","The trade name of the bottled rum":"瓶裝蘭姆酒的商品名稱","\"Mark\" is the name for each rum fresh off the still.":"「Mark」是每一款剛離開蒸餾器的蘭姆酒的名稱。","Blenders combine different marks, light and heavy, to build a rum's style. It is not an age category or a molasses grade. Nor is it a brand name: in this context it is purely a technical term for a component spirit.":"調和師結合輕盈和厚重的不同 mark，建構蘭姆酒的風格。它不是年數類別，也不是糖蜜等級。它也不是品牌名稱：在這裡它純粹是指作為成分的烈酒的技術術語。","Which description fits a light mark?":"哪一項描述符合輕盈型 mark（light mark）？","Column distilled to high strength, light aroma":"用蒸餾柱蒸餾到高濃度，香氣清淡","Pot distilled to low strength, intense aroma":"用壺式蒸餾器蒸餾到低濃度，香氣濃郁","Briefly aged rum then softened with caramel":"短暫陳年再用焦糖色柔化的蘭姆酒","Ester-rich rum used to give lift to blends":"富含酯類、用來為調和提味的蘭姆酒","Light marks come from column stills, often above 90% abv, with little aroma intensity.":"輕盈型 mark 來自柱式蒸餾器，常高於 90% abv，香氣強度低。","The higher the distillation strength, the fewer congeners remain, so the fewer aromas. Pot stills at low strength and an ester-rich profile describe heavy marks instead. Caramel and sugar are later finishing touches, not a type of mark.":"蒸餾濃度越高，留下的同屬物越少，香氣也越少。低濃度的壺式蒸餾器和富含酯類的輪廓描述的是厚重型 mark。焦糖色和糖是之後的收尾調整，不是 mark 的類型。","Which type of still is normally used for heavy marks?":"厚重型 mark（heavy mark）通常使用哪一種蒸餾器？","Column still with many plates":"蒸餾板很多的柱式蒸餾器","Hybrid still with a rectifying column":"帶精餾柱的混合式蒸餾器","No still at all: they are re-fermented rums":"完全不用蒸餾器：它們是再發酵的蘭姆酒","Heavy marks are distilled to a low strength, normally in pot stills.":"厚重型 mark 蒸餾到低濃度，通常使用壺式蒸餾器。","Caribbean distillers own some truly unusual pot stills and use them skilfully to create fruity or rich, savoury styles. Some heavy marks also come from short columns, but never from columns with lots of plates, which push strength up and strip aromas out. Rum is always distilled.":"加勒比海的蒸餾師擁有一些非常特別的壺式蒸餾器，並純熟地運用它們做出果香型或豐厚鹹鮮的風格。有些厚重型 mark 也來自矮蒸餾柱，但絕不會來自蒸餾板很多的蒸餾柱，因為那會把濃度推高並去除香氣。蘭姆酒一定經過蒸餾。","What is virtually the only production rule shared by all rums?":"幾乎是所有蘭姆酒唯一共同的生產規定是什麼？","It must not be rectified into a neutral spirit":"不得精餾成中性烈酒","It must spend at least a year in oak casks":"必須在橡木桶中存放至少一年","It must be distilled twice in a pot still":"必須在壺式蒸餾器中蒸餾兩次","It must be produced in a Caribbean country":"必須在加勒比海國家生產","Apart from not becoming a neutral spirit, rum has very few rules.":"除了不能變成中性烈酒，蘭姆酒的規定非常少。","That freedom explains the huge range of styles: columns and pot stills of every kind are used, and ageing is optional. Many rums never see wood, and rum is made wherever cane grows, Brazil included.":"這種自由解釋了它風格範圍之廣：各種蒸餾柱和壺式蒸餾器都有人使用，陳年也是可選的。許多蘭姆酒從不接觸木頭，而且凡是種甘蔗的地方都生產蘭姆酒，包括巴西。","A briefly aged rum is filtered through activated charcoal. What is the result?":"一款短暫陳年的蘭姆酒用活性碳過濾。結果是什麼？","A white rum that keeps some smoothness":"保有一些柔順感的白蘭姆酒","A dark rum with strong toasted oak notes":"帶強烈烘烤橡木氣息的深色蘭姆酒","A neutral rum that legally becomes vodka":"在法律上變成伏特加的中性蘭姆酒","A stronger rum with all its esters concentrated":"濃度更高、所有酯類都被濃縮的蘭姆酒","Filtering removes the colour, but some of the smoothness from short ageing remains.":"過濾去除了顏色，但短暫陳年帶來的柔順感仍保留一部分。","It is a common technique for many white rums: they rarely show obvious oak, yet feel smoother than a rum that never saw wood. Charcoal does not raise the strength, concentrate esters or turn rum into vodka.":"這是許多白蘭姆酒常用的技術：它們很少表現出明顯的橡木味，卻比從未接觸木頭的蘭姆酒更柔順。木炭不會提高濃度、濃縮酯類，也不會把蘭姆酒變成伏特加。","Why are many rums, especially oak-matured ones, sweetened before release?":"為什麼許多蘭姆酒，尤其是橡木桶熟成的，在上市前會加糖？","Sugar complements their fruity and rancio notes":"糖能襯托它們的果香和 rancio 氣息","Sugar is legally required in all golden rums":"法律規定所有金色蘭姆酒都必須加糖","Sugar stops oxidation once the bottle is opened":"糖能在開瓶後阻止氧化","Sugar replaces caramel and supplies all the colour":"糖取代焦糖色並提供所有顏色","A little sweetness flatters fruity and rancio aromas and makes the rum more delicious.":"一點甜味能襯托果香和 rancio 香氣，讓蘭姆酒更美味。","Sweetening is the producer's choice, not a rule, and it needs a light hand: too much sugar dominates and unbalances the rum. Sugar does not provide colour, which comes from oak or caramel, and it is not a preservative once the bottle is open.":"加糖是生產者的選擇，不是規定，而且下手要輕：糖太多會喧賓奪主，讓蘭姆酒失衡。糖不提供顏色（顏色來自橡木或焦糖色），開瓶後也不是防腐劑。","Which statement about rum blending is correct?":"關於蘭姆酒的調和，下列哪一項正確？","Even single-distillery rums usually combine several marks":"即使是單一蒸餾廠的蘭姆酒，通常也結合數種 mark","Blending is banned for rums that carry an age statement":"標示年數的蘭姆酒禁止調和","Only light marks are blended, since heavy marks are too aromatic":"只有輕盈型 mark 會被調和，因為厚重型 mark 香氣太濃","Blending happens before distillation, by mixing molasses":"調和在蒸餾前進行，把糖蜜混合起來","Rum is almost always a blend, even when it comes from just one distillery.":"蘭姆酒幾乎都是調和的，即使只來自一家蒸餾廠。","Blenders use light and heavy marks and the character of individual distilleries to build complexity. Heavy marks, precisely because they are intense, add depth in small amounts. Blending involves finished spirits, not molasses.":"調和師運用輕盈型和厚重型 mark，以及個別蒸餾廠的特色來建構複雜度。厚重型 mark 正因為濃郁，少量就能增添深度。調和的對象是成品烈酒，不是糖蜜。","Where does a typical golden rum get most of its colour?":"典型的金色蘭姆酒大部分的顏色來自哪裡？","From oak, with a little caramel for consistency":"來自橡木，再加一點焦糖色以求一致","From the dark molasses used as raw material":"來自作為原料的深色糖蜜","Only from caramel, as it never goes into wood":"只來自焦糖色，因為它從不入木桶","From cane juice oxidising during fermentation":"來自甘蔗汁在發酵時氧化","Most golden rums owe their colour to oak maturation.":"大多數金色蘭姆酒的顏色來自橡木桶熟成。","Caramel keeps the shade the same from batch to batch. Spirit always comes off the still colourless, whatever the raw material. \"Only caramel\" describes many dark rums, or Gold Tequila, rather than a typical golden rum.":"焦糖色讓每一批的色調保持相同。不論用什麼原料，烈酒離開蒸餾器時都是無色的。「只來自焦糖色」描述的是許多深色蘭姆酒或 Gold Tequila，而不是典型的金色蘭姆酒。","A customer tastes a dark rum: it shows cane aromas but no sign of ageing in aroma or texture. What is likely?":"一位顧客品嚐一款深色蘭姆酒：它有甘蔗香氣，但香氣和質地上都沒有陳年的跡象。可能的情況是什麼？","Its colour comes mainly from caramel":"它的顏色主要來自焦糖色","It has been aged for many years in new casks":"它在新桶中陳年了很多年","It is a charcoal-filtered rhum agricole from Martinique":"它是經木炭過濾的馬丁尼克 rhum agricole","Its colour comes from high-quality molasses":"它的顏色來自高品質的糖蜜","Most dark rums get their colour from heavy caramel additions, not long ageing.":"大多數深色蘭姆酒的顏色來自大量添加的焦糖色，不是長期陳年。","A genuinely long-aged rum would show rancio notes such as black banana, leather and meat, plus a softer texture. A charcoal-filtered rum would be white, not dark. Molasses does not colour the spirit, which comes off the still colourless.":"真正長期陳年的蘭姆酒會表現出黑香蕉、皮革和肉味等 rancio 氣息，質地也更柔和。經木炭過濾的蘭姆酒會是白色的，不是深色。糖蜜不會為烈酒上色，烈酒離開蒸餾器時是無色的。","Which notes do heavy marks develop after very long ageing?":"厚重型 mark 經過非常長期的陳年後會發展出哪些氣息？","Over-ripe banana, bruised fruit and rancio":"過熟香蕉、碰傷的水果和 rancio","Cut grass, green pepper and fresh citrus":"青草、青椒和新鮮柑橘","Smoke, ash and wet earth":"煙、灰燼和濕土","Complete neutrality with only alcohol notes":"完全中性，只有酒精味","Long maturation brings ripe, bruised fruit and rancio character.":"長期熟成帶來熟透、碰傷的水果和 rancio 特色。","Rancio covers black banana, leather and meaty notes typical of genuinely aged dark rums. Grass and green pepper are youthful aromas from cane juice or agave. Neutrality is vodka's goal, not rum's.":"Rancio 涵蓋黑香蕉、皮革和肉味等氣息，是真正陳年的深色蘭姆酒的典型特徵。青草和青椒是來自甘蔗汁或龍舌蘭的年輕香氣。中性是伏特加的目標，不是蘭姆酒的。","Where in the Caribbean may the term rhum agricole be used?":"在加勒比海，哪裡可以使用 rhum agricole 這個術語？","Only in Martinique and Guadeloupe":"只有馬丁尼克和瓜地洛普","On any island that uses cane juice":"任何使用甘蔗汁的島嶼","Only in Jamaica and Barbados":"只有牙買加和巴貝多","In all former French colonies on the American mainland":"美洲大陸上所有的前法國殖民地","In the Caribbean only cane juice rums from Martinique and Guadeloupe can be called rhum agricole.":"在加勒比海，只有馬丁尼克和瓜地洛普的甘蔗汁蘭姆酒可以稱為 rhum agricole。","Other islands make cane juice rum too, but cannot use this term. Jamaica and Barbados belong to the British tradition, which is mostly molasses-based. The option about former colonies is far broader than the real rule.":"其他島嶼也生產甘蔗汁蘭姆酒，但不能使用這個術語。牙買加和巴貝多屬於英式傳統，大多以糖蜜為原料。關於前殖民地的選項比實際規定寬鬆得多。","Why did the French islands develop a tradition of cane juice rum?":"為什麼法屬島嶼發展出甘蔗汁蘭姆酒的傳統？","France favoured sugar from beet":"法國偏好用甜菜製糖","Local molasses was too poor and acidic to ferment":"當地的糖蜜品質太差、太酸，無法發酵","The French Navy demanded a much lighter rum":"法國海軍要求清淡得多的蘭姆酒","Modern columns arrived there before anywhere else":"現代蒸餾柱最先傳到那裡","With sugar made at home from beet, the islands' cane juice was free to be distilled.":"既然本國用甜菜製糖，島上的甘蔗汁就可以拿去蒸餾。","France protected its own beet farmers, so the islands' cane juice was not needed by the sugar industry. The naval ration belongs to the British tradition, and modern columns are linked instead to the Cuban style.":"法國保護本國的甜菜農，所以製糖業不需要島上的甘蔗汁。海軍配給屬於英式傳統，現代蒸餾柱則與古巴風格有關。","Which country is famous for very fruity high-ester marks?":"哪一個國家以果香非常濃郁的高酯 mark 聞名？","Guadeloupe":"瓜地洛普","Jamaica is the benchmark for intensely fruity high-ester rums.":"牙買加是果香濃烈的高酯蘭姆酒的標竿。","These marks are rarely used alone because they are too pungent, but blenders seek them out for aromatic lift. Jamaica also makes some of the most aromatic high-ester white rums. Cuba and Guatemala follow the lighter Spanish style; Guadeloupe follows the French cane juice style.":"這些 mark 因為太刺激而很少單獨使用，但調和師會特地找它們來提升香氣。牙買加也生產一些香氣最濃郁的高酯白蘭姆酒。古巴和瓜地馬拉走較清淡的西班牙風格；瓜地洛普走法式的甘蔗汁風格。","What do Guyana's traditional marks bring to blends?":"蓋亞那的傳統 mark 為調和帶來什麼？","Richness, weight and suitability for long ageing":"豐厚、重量感，並適合長期陳年","Grassy freshness typical of fresh cane juice":"新鮮甘蔗汁典型的青草清新感","Lightness and neutrality for Cuban-style white rums":"清淡和中性，用於古巴風格的白蘭姆酒","A smoky aroma from oven cooking":"烤爐烹煮帶來的煙燻香氣","Guyana's marks are rich and weighty, ideal for long oak maturation.":"蓋亞那的 mark 豐厚而有重量，非常適合長期橡木桶熟成。","Unlike Jamaican rums of a similar age, they give blends palate weight and mouthfeel, whether young or old. Grassy freshness belongs to cane juice rums such as agricole, and lightness to the Spanish style. Smoky notes are not part of this picture.":"與年數相近的牙買加蘭姆酒不同，它們不論年輕或陳年，都為調和帶來口中的重量和口感。青草清新感屬於 agricole 這類甘蔗汁蘭姆酒，清淡則屬於西班牙風格。煙燻氣息不在其中。","Which style of white rum is the most popular worldwide?":"哪一種白蘭姆酒風格在全世界最受歡迎？","The light, smooth Cuban style":"清淡柔順的古巴風格","The very aromatic Jamaican high-ester style":"香氣非常濃郁的牙買加高酯風格","White rhum agricole, vegetal and intense":"白色 rhum agricole，植物氣息濃烈","Unaged, lightly sweetened cachaça":"未陳年、略微加糖的 cachaça","The light, smooth Cuban-style white is the best-selling white rum style.":"清淡柔順的古巴風格白蘭姆酒是最暢銷的白蘭姆酒風格。","Born in Cuba from high-strength column marks softened by a short spell in oak, it suits cocktails perfectly. Jamaican and agricole whites are much more intense and niche. Cachaça is huge in volume, but almost all of it is drunk in Brazil.":"它誕生於古巴，用高濃度的蒸餾柱 mark 經短暫橡木桶存放而變得柔和，非常適合調酒。牙買加和 agricole 的白蘭姆酒濃烈得多，也較小眾。Cachaça 的產量極大，但幾乎都在巴西喝掉。","Which description of cachaça is correct?":"關於 cachaça，下列哪一項描述正確？","Brazilian cane juice rum, often unaged":"巴西的甘蔗汁蘭姆酒，常不經陳年","Brazilian molasses rum, always aged in oak":"巴西的糖蜜蘭姆酒，一律在橡木桶中陳年","Agave spirit made in southern Brazil":"巴西南部生產的龍舌蘭烈酒","Caribbean rum sold mainly for export":"主要用於出口的加勒比海蘭姆酒","Cachaça is Brazil's cane juice rum, mostly unaged.":"Cachaça 是巴西的甘蔗汁蘭姆酒，大多不經陳年。","Brazil is the world's largest rum producer, and almost all cachaça is drunk at home. Many are lightly sweetened, and the best show vegetal, grassy and fruity aromas. It is not an agave spirit, and it is not mainly an export product.":"巴西是全世界最大的蘭姆酒生產國，幾乎所有 cachaça 都在國內飲用。許多酒款略微加糖，最好的表現出植物、青草和果香。它不是龍舌蘭烈酒，也不是以出口為主的產品。","A rum label says \"overproof\". What does it indicate?":"一瓶蘭姆酒的酒標寫著「overproof」。這代表什麼？","An unusually high alcoholic strength":"酒精濃度特別高","Longer ageing than the average for the category":"陳年時間比該類別的平均更長","A rum inspected and approved by the British Navy":"經英國海軍檢驗認可的蘭姆酒","Strength measured on the American proof scale":"以美國 proof 標度測量的濃度","\"Overproof\" flags a rum bottled well above normal strength.":"「Overproof」表示這款蘭姆酒的裝瓶濃度遠高於一般水準。","The term comes from the old British gunpowder test: 100 proof was about 57% abv, and anything above it was over proof. It is no longer an official measure. It says nothing about age and should not be confused with the US proof system, which works differently.":"這個術語來自古老的英國火藥測試：100 proof 大約是 57% abv，高於這個數值就是 over proof。它已不再是官方的度量。它與年數無關，也不應與運作方式不同的美國 proof 制度混淆。","What should you know about age statements on Caribbean rums?":"關於加勒比海蘭姆酒的年數標示，你應該知道什麼？","Their meaning varies from producer to producer":"它們的意義因生產者而異","They always give the age of the youngest rum in the blend":"它們一律表示調和中最年輕蘭姆酒的年數","They are banned on all multi-island rums":"所有跨島調和的蘭姆酒都禁止標示","They show the years spent in bottle before sale":"它們表示販售前在瓶中存放的年數","There is no single rule, so a number on the label can mean different things.":"沒有單一的規定，所以酒標上的數字可能有不同的意思。","Unlike spirits with precise laws, a number on a rum can refer to the youngest component, the oldest or a kind of average. Even abbreviations borrowed from other categories guarantee nothing. Time in bottle does not count as ageing.":"與有明確法規的烈酒不同，蘭姆酒上的數字可能指最年輕的成分、最老的成分，或某種平均值。即使是借自其他類別的縮寫也不保證任何事。瓶中的時間不算陳年。","A bartender wants a smooth golden rum with obvious vanilla and a touch of sweetness. Which style fits?":"一位調酒師想要一款柔順、有明顯香草味並略帶甜味的金色蘭姆酒。哪一種風格合適？","Spanish style":"西班牙風格","French style, cane juice based and fairly dry":"法式風格，以甘蔗汁為原料，相當不甜","Jamaican style, ester-rich and very pungent":"牙買加風格，富含酯類、非常刺激","Unaged white cachaça from Brazil":"巴西未陳年的白色 cachaça","Spanish-style golden rums are smooth, with oak vanilla and often added sugar.":"西班牙風格的金色蘭姆酒很柔順，帶橡木的香草味，並常加糖。","This style uses a high proportion of light marks and is usually medium in aroma intensity. French golden rums stay dry or off-dry and keep the vegetal cane character. Jamaican rums are too pungent, and an unaged cachaça shows no oak vanilla.":"這種風格使用高比例的輕盈型 mark，香氣強度通常中等。法式金色蘭姆酒保持不甜或微甜，並保有甘蔗的植物特色。牙買加蘭姆酒太刺激，而未陳年的 cachaça 沒有橡木的香草味。","When sugar cane is harvested, why are the stems cut close to the ground?":"採收甘蔗時，為什麼要貼近地面砍莖？","So the roots survive and the plant regrows":"讓根存活，植株才能重新生長","Because the sugar is found only in the lowest part of the stem":"因為糖只存在於莖的最下段","So the roots can be fermented too":"這樣根也能拿去發酵","To remove the leaves in one pass":"一次把葉子去掉","Sugar cane lives for several years: cutting low keeps the roots so new stems can grow.":"甘蔗能活好幾年：貼地砍能保住根，讓新的莖長出來。","The leaves are stripped first, but that is not why the cut is low. The sugar is spread through the whole stem, and roots are never fermented: it is the juice pressed from the stems that becomes rum.":"葉子會先去掉，但那不是貼地砍的原因。糖分布在整根莖中，根也從不拿去發酵：變成蘭姆酒的是從莖壓榨出來的汁。","Where can rum be made?":"蘭姆酒可以在哪裡製作？","Wherever it is hot enough to grow cane":"任何熱到能種甘蔗的地方","Only on the Caribbean islands":"只在加勒比海島嶼","Only in former British, French and Spanish colonies":"只在英國、法國和西班牙的前殖民地","Only where the law recognises a geographical indication":"只在法律承認地理標示的地方","Rum is made around the world wherever sugar cane thrives.":"全世界凡是甘蔗長得好的地方都生產蘭姆酒。","The Caribbean is the most celebrated centre, but not the only one: Brazil, for example, is the largest producer in the world. There is no single geographical indication for rum, and colonial traditions explain styles, not where rum may be made.":"加勒比海是最著名的中心，但不是唯一的：例如巴西就是全世界最大的生產國。蘭姆酒沒有單一的地理標示，殖民傳統解釋的是風格，不是哪裡可以生產蘭姆酒。","A producer wants to make rum from cane juice. What happens straight after harvest?":"一位生產者想用甘蔗汁做蘭姆酒。採收後緊接著做什麼？","The stems are milled and the juice ferments at once":"把莖壓榨，汁液立刻發酵","The juice is heated until sugar crystals form":"把汁加熱到形成糖結晶","The juice is diluted with plenty of water as it is too sugary":"用大量的水稀釋甘蔗汁，因為糖分太高","The stems are cooked to turn starch into sugar":"烹煮甘蔗莖，把澱粉變成糖","Cane juice is released in a mill and can be fermented immediately.":"甘蔗汁在壓榨機中釋出，可以立刻發酵。","Heating juice to crystallise sugar is what the sugar industry does, and it leaves molasses. It is molasses, not juice, that needs diluting. Cane already contains sugar, so no starch conversion is needed.":"把甘蔗汁加熱讓糖結晶是製糖業的做法，剩下的是糖蜜。需要稀釋的是糖蜜，不是甘蔗汁。甘蔗本來就含有糖，所以不需要轉化澱粉。","What are most rums made from?":"大多數蘭姆酒用什麼製成？","Beet sugar":"甜菜糖","Cooked, caramelised cane syrup":"煮過、焦糖化的甘蔗糖漿","Most cane juice goes into sugar, and distillers mainly use its by-product, molasses.":"大部分甘蔗汁用來製糖，蒸餾師主要使用它的副產品糖蜜。","Fresh juice is used, but only for a minority, such as rhum agricole and cachaça. Beet can never make rum: every rum comes from cane. Caramelised syrup is not a rum raw material.":"新鮮甘蔗汁也有人用，但只占少數，例如 rhum agricole 和 cachaça。甜菜永遠做不出蘭姆酒：所有蘭姆酒都來自甘蔗。焦糖化的糖漿不是蘭姆酒的原料。","In sugar refining, which molasses is of the highest quality?":"在製糖過程中，哪一種糖蜜品質最高？","The molasses from the start of the process":"製程一開始的糖蜜","The molasses from the end of the process":"製程最後的糖蜜","Molasses that has been aged in cask before fermenting":"發酵前先在桶中陳年的糖蜜","All molasses is of equal quality":"所有糖蜜的品質都一樣","Molasses comes in grades: the first to come off is best, the last is poorest.":"糖蜜有等級之分：最先產出的最好，最後的最差。","The more sugar is removed, the poorer the residue becomes, so the final molasses is the lowest grade. Not all molasses is equal, and molasses is never cask-aged: only the spirit may mature in wood.":"取走的糖越多，殘餘物就越貧乏，所以最後的糖蜜等級最低。並非所有糖蜜都一樣，糖蜜也從不桶陳：只有烈酒才會在木桶中熟成。","What do rum producers often try to boost during fermentation?":"蘭姆酒生產者在發酵時常設法提高什麼？","Fruity esters":"帶果香的酯類","Smoky aromas":"煙燻香氣","The dark colour of the fermented liquid":"發酵液的深色","The leftover sweetness in the wash":"發酵液中殘留的甜味","Fermentation creates congeners, and rum makers often aim for more fruity esters.":"發酵會產生同屬物，蘭姆酒生產者常追求更多帶果香的酯類。","This is taken furthest in Jamaica, with its high-ester rums. Smoke does not come from fermentation, colour is adjusted after distillation, and every new spirit is dry: wash sweetness never reaches the rum.":"把這一點做到極致的是牙買加的高酯蘭姆酒。煙燻味不是來自發酵，顏色是蒸餾後才調整的，而所有新酒都是不甜的：發酵液的甜味永遠到不了蘭姆酒裡。","To what strength are light marks often distilled?":"輕盈型 mark 常蒸餾到多少濃度？","Above 90% abv":"90% abv 以上","Around 60% abv":"60% abv 左右","Exactly 57.15% abv, the old British proof":"剛好 57.15% abv，也就是舊的英國 proof","96% abv, like neutral spirit":"96% abv，像中性烈酒一樣","Light marks come off a column at high strength, often over 90% abv, with light flavour.":"輕盈型 mark 從蒸餾柱流出時濃度很高，常超過 90% abv，風味清淡。","Rum may not be rectified into neutral spirit, so 96% is wrong. 57.15% relates to overproof bottling, not distillation. Around 60% is typical of heavy spirits, not light marks.":"蘭姆酒不得精餾成中性烈酒，所以 96% 是錯的。57.15% 與 overproof 的裝瓶有關，不是蒸餾。60% 左右是厚重烈酒的典型，不是輕盈型 mark。","Which statement about light marks is true?":"關於輕盈型 mark，下列哪一項正確？","They are also oak-aged and are key to many golden rums":"它們也會在橡木桶中陳年，是許多金色蘭姆酒的關鍵","They are only ever used for unaged white rums":"它們只用於未陳年的白蘭姆酒","They are mostly made in very small pot stills":"它們大多用非常小的壺式蒸餾器製作","They are too pungent to be used without blending":"它們太刺激，不調和就無法使用","Light marks make many white rums, but are also matured in oak and matter greatly in golden rums.":"輕盈型 mark 做出許多白蘭姆酒，但也會在橡木桶中熟成，對金色蘭姆酒非常重要。","White rum is their main use, but not the only one. They are made in columns, not small pot stills. Excessive pungency is a feature of some heavy marks, such as high-ester ones.":"白蘭姆酒是它們的主要用途，但不是唯一的。它們用蒸餾柱製作，不是小型壺式蒸餾器。過度刺激是某些厚重型 mark（例如高酯的）的特點。","Why are many cane juice rums distilled to a low strength in short columns?":"為什麼許多甘蔗汁蘭姆酒用矮蒸餾柱蒸餾到低濃度？","The low strength accentuates the cane juice flavours":"低濃度能突顯甘蔗汁的風味","Because the law bans pot stills for cane juice":"因為法律禁止甘蔗汁使用壺式蒸餾器","To produce a neutral spirit with no cane taste":"做出沒有甘蔗味的中性烈酒","So the rum can be bottled overproof":"這樣蘭姆酒才能以 overproof 裝瓶","A short column gives a low-strength heavy mark that keeps the vegetal cane character.":"矮蒸餾柱做出低濃度的厚重型 mark，保留甘蔗的植物特色。","There is no pot still ban: rum has very few rules. A neutral spirit is not even allowed as rum. Overproof is about bottling strength, not still choice.":"沒有禁用壺式蒸餾器的規定：蘭姆酒的規定非常少。中性烈酒甚至不能算是蘭姆酒。Overproof 說的是裝瓶濃度，不是蒸餾器的選擇。","Why are many heavy marks not used on their own?":"為什麼許多厚重型 mark 不單獨使用？","They are so intense they are used to add depth to blends":"它們非常濃烈，是用來為調和增添深度的","The law requires them to be at least half light marks":"法律規定其中至少一半要是輕盈型 mark","Their strength is too low to be bottled":"它們的濃度太低，無法裝瓶","They cannot be aged in oak":"它們不能在橡木桶中陳年","With their pronounced aroma, many heavy marks are used by blenders to add depth and complexity.":"許多厚重型 mark 香氣明顯，調和師用它們來增添深度和複雜度。","There is no rule on rum blend proportions. A low distillation strength is still well above bottling strength, so it is no obstacle. On the contrary, heavy marks are often oak-matured, sometimes for a very long time.":"蘭姆酒的調和比例沒有規定。低蒸餾濃度仍遠高於裝瓶濃度，所以不成問題。相反地，厚重型 mark 常在橡木桶中熟成，有時非常久。","What range of styles do Caribbean heavy marks cover?":"加勒比海的厚重型 mark 涵蓋哪些風格？","From very fruity to rich and savoury":"從果香非常濃郁到豐厚鹹鮮","Always neutral and light":"一律中性而清淡","Only smoky, earthy styles similar to mezcal":"只有類似 mezcal 的煙燻、土壤風格","Only vegetal cane juice styles":"只有帶植物氣息的甘蔗汁風格","Thanks to unique and varied stills, distillers make heavy marks ranging from fruity (high ester) to rich and savoury.":"靠著獨特多樣的蒸餾器，蒸餾師做出從果香型（高酯）到豐厚鹹鮮的各種厚重型 mark。","Neutral and light describes light marks, not heavy ones. Smoke is typical of pit-roasted mezcal, not rum. Vegetal cane character is one possible style, not the only one.":"中性而清淡描述的是輕盈型 mark，不是厚重型。煙燻是窯坑烘烤的 mezcal 的典型特徵，不是蘭姆酒。甘蔗的植物特色是可能的風格之一，不是唯一的。","Which kind of cask is most often used to mature rum?":"熟成蘭姆酒最常用哪一種桶？","Previously used casks":"先前用過的桶","New charred oak casks, as required by law":"炙燒過的新橡木桶，依法律規定","New chestnut casks":"新的栗木桶","For rum, reused casks are more common than new ones.":"對蘭姆酒來說，重複使用的桶比新桶更常見。","New charred oak is a bourbon rule, not a rum rule; rum has very few rules. Steel is an inert vessel: it stores rum but does not mature it.":"炙燒過的新橡木桶是 bourbon 的規定，不是蘭姆酒的；蘭姆酒的規定非常少。鋼是惰性容器：它存放蘭姆酒，但不會讓它熟成。","In broad terms, what decides the final style of a rum blend?":"大致來說，什麼決定了蘭姆酒調和的最終風格？","Whether light or heavy marks are the majority":"輕盈型還是厚重型 mark 占多數","The island where it is bottled":"裝瓶所在的島嶼","The colour of the bottle glass":"酒瓶玻璃的顏色","The number of distilleries, which must legally be at least three":"蒸餾廠的數目，依法至少要三家","A blend dominated by light marks will be light; with many heavy marks it will be more intense.":"以輕盈型 mark 為主的調和會很清淡；厚重型 mark 多的則更濃烈。","No law sets a number of distilleries: even single-distillery rums usually blend several marks. Where it is bottled and the glass colour do not change the taste.":"沒有法律規定蒸餾廠的數目：即使是單一蒸餾廠的蘭姆酒，通常也調和數種 mark。在哪裡裝瓶和玻璃的顏色都不會改變味道。","Which is NOT a usual finishing technique for rum after blending?":"下列哪一項不是蘭姆酒調和後常見的收尾技術？","Redistilling with spices":"與香料一起再蒸餾","Adding caramel for colour":"添加焦糖色來調色","Adding sugar before release":"上市前加糖","The three classic techniques are charcoal filtration, caramel and sugar; redistilling with spices is not one of them.":"三種經典技術是木炭過濾、焦糖色和糖；與香料一起再蒸餾不在其中。","Even spiced rum is not redistilled: spices are usually added by maceration, since redistilling would strip colour and aged character. Charcoal, caramel and sugar, on the other hand, are all widespread.":"即使是香料蘭姆酒也不會再蒸餾：香料通常以浸漬加入，因為再蒸餾會去除顏色和陳年特色。木炭、焦糖色和糖則都很普遍。","What can happen if too much sugar is added to a rum?":"如果蘭姆酒加了太多糖，會怎麼樣？","Sugar dominates and unbalances the rum":"糖喧賓奪主，讓蘭姆酒失衡","The rum starts fermenting again in the bottle":"蘭姆酒在瓶中重新開始發酵","It loses the right to be called rum and becomes a liqueur":"它失去稱為蘭姆酒的資格，變成利口酒","It turns hazy when it is chilled":"冰鎮時變混濁","A little sugar lifts fruity and rancio notes, but too much masks them and upsets the balance.":"一點糖能提升果香和 rancio 氣息，但太多會把它們蓋住並破壞平衡。","At spirit strength, yeast cannot restart fermentation. Haze when chilled is prevented by filtration and has nothing to do with sugar. The problem is one of taste, not legal name.":"在烈酒的濃度下，酵母無法重新啟動發酵。冰鎮時的混濁是靠過濾防止的，與糖無關。問題在於味道，不是法定名稱。","A customer finds a golden rum smooth and slightly sweet. Where does the sweetness come from?":"一位顧客覺得某款金色蘭姆酒柔順且略帶甜味。甜味來自哪裡？","Cane sugar that passes unchanged into the spirit":"原封不動進入烈酒的蔗糖","Molasses, which makes every rum naturally sweet":"糖蜜，它讓所有蘭姆酒天然帶甜","The activated charcoal used for filtration":"過濾用的活性碳","Every newly made spirit is dry; sweetness in rum always comes from added sugar.":"所有新酒都是不甜的；蘭姆酒的甜味一律來自添加的糖。","Sugar does not distil: it stays behind. Molasses and cane give aromas, not sweetness. Activated charcoal removes colour and congeners; it adds no sugar.":"糖無法蒸餾：它留在原處。糖蜜和甘蔗帶來的是香氣，不是甜味。活性碳去除顏色和同屬物；它不會增添糖。","Can a water-white rum have spent time in oak?":"清澈如水的蘭姆酒有可能在橡木桶中存放過嗎？","Yes, its colour may have been filtered out":"有，它的顏色可能被過濾掉了","No, white rum may legally never touch wood":"沒有，白蘭姆酒依法不得接觸木頭","No, oak always gives a colour that cannot be removed":"沒有，橡木帶來的顏色永遠無法去除","Yes, but only if it is a rhum agricole":"有，但只限 rhum agricole","Some white rums are briefly matured and then decoloured with activated charcoal.":"有些白蘭姆酒經過短暫熟成，再用活性碳脫色。","There is no wood ban for white rums, and oak colour can indeed be removed. The technique is not limited to rhum agricole: it is used across the Caribbean.":"白蘭姆酒沒有禁用木桶的規定，橡木的顏色也確實可以去除。這項技術不限於 rhum agricole：整個加勒比海都在用。","What aroma intensity do most white rums have?":"大多數白蘭姆酒的香氣強度如何？","Light, though some are pronounced":"清淡，不過有些很明顯","Always pronounced, since they are unaged":"一律明顯，因為未經陳年","None: they are neutral spirits":"沒有：它們是中性烈酒","Medium, as set by each island's law":"中等，由各島的法律規定","White rums range from light to pronounced, but most are light.":"白蘭姆酒從清淡到明顯都有，但大多數是清淡的。","Very aromatic whites exist, such as Jamaican high-ester rums or rhum agricole, but they are a minority. Rum cannot be neutral, and no law sets intensity.":"香氣非常濃郁的白蘭姆酒確實存在，例如牙買加的高酯蘭姆酒或 rhum agricole，但它們是少數。蘭姆酒不可以是中性的，也沒有法律規定香氣強度。","For a golden rum producer, what is the key style choice?":"對金色蘭姆酒的生產者來說，關鍵的風格選擇是什麼？","The ratio of light to heavy marks":"輕盈型與厚重型 mark 的比例","Which legal age category to print on the label":"在酒標上印哪一個法定年數類別","Whether to use molasses or beet":"用糖蜜還是甜菜","Whether to redistil the aged blend in a hybrid still":"是否用混合式蒸餾器把陳年的調和酒再蒸餾","There are no legal categories for golden rums: style depends mainly on the light/heavy balance.":"金色蘭姆酒沒有法定類別：風格主要取決於輕盈與厚重的平衡。","Precisely because there are no legal categories, the choice rests with the producer and local tradition. Beet cannot make rum, and redistilling an aged rum would strip its colour and character.":"正因為沒有法定類別，選擇權在生產者和當地傳統手上。甜菜做不出蘭姆酒，而把陳年蘭姆酒再蒸餾會去除它的顏色和特色。","Which notes point to a dark rum that has truly had a long time in oak?":"哪些氣息指向真正在橡木桶中存放很久的深色蘭姆酒？","Black banana, meat and leather":"黑香蕉、肉味和皮革","Cut grass, bell pepper and pepper":"青草、甜椒和胡椒","Smoke, earth and pit-roasted vegetables":"煙燻、土壤和窯烤蔬菜","Only caramel and sugar, with no other aromas":"只有焦糖和糖，沒有其他香氣","Long ageing develops rancio: black banana, meaty and leathery notes.":"長期陳年會發展出 rancio：黑香蕉、肉味和皮革氣息。","Grass and pepper suggest cane juice or agave; smoke and earth suggest mezcal. A dark rum tasting only of caramel and sugar is probably coloured, not long-aged.":"青草和胡椒暗示甘蔗汁或龍舌蘭；煙燻和土壤暗示 mezcal。只有焦糖和糖味的深色蘭姆酒很可能是染色的，不是長期陳年的。","Why is colour a tricky way to classify rums?":"為什麼用顏色來分類蘭姆酒並不可靠？","Colour can be added or removed":"顏色可以添加，也可以去除","Colour changes each time the bottle is opened":"每次開瓶顏色都會改變","The law forbids stating colour on the label":"法律禁止在酒標上標示顏色","All rums are the same colour when they leave the cask":"所有蘭姆酒出桶時顏色都相同","Filtering and caramel change colour, so it does not reliably reveal age or style.":"過濾和焦糖色會改變顏色，所以它無法可靠地顯示年數或風格。","Even so, colour is popular because it is visual and handy for multi-island blends. No law bans \"white\" or \"dark\", and the colour from wood varies widely with time and cask.":"即便如此，顏色仍很受歡迎，因為它一目了然，對跨島調和的蘭姆酒也很方便。沒有法律禁止「white」或「dark」，而木頭帶來的顏色會隨時間和桶有很大的差異。","So why is classifying rum by colour still so common?":"那麼，為什麼用顏色分類蘭姆酒仍然這麼普遍？","It is visual and handy for multi-island blends":"它一目了然，對跨島調和也很方便","It is the only system recognised by law in every producing country":"它是每個生產國法律唯一承認的制度","It always shows the rum's age precisely":"它總能精確顯示蘭姆酒的年數","It shows which raw material was used":"它顯示用了哪一種原料","Colour is instantly visible and groups blends of mixed origin, which is why consumers like it.":"顏色一眼就看得到，還能把不同產地的調和歸在一起，所以消費者喜歡。","Colour categories are not legally defined and do not guarantee age, since filtering and caramel alter it. A white rum can come from molasses or cane juice alike.":"顏色類別沒有法律定義，也不保證年數，因為過濾和焦糖色會改變它。白蘭姆酒可以來自糖蜜，也可以來自甘蔗汁。","Which three European countries colonised the Caribbean, leaving distinct rum traditions?":"哪三個歐洲國家殖民了加勒比海，留下各具特色的蘭姆酒傳統？","Britain, France and Spain":"英國、法國和西班牙","Portugal, France and the Netherlands":"葡萄牙、法國和荷蘭","Spain, Italy and Britain":"西班牙、義大利和英國","France, Germany and Spain":"法國、德國和西班牙","Caribbean rum traditions divide into British, French and Spanish styles.":"加勒比海的蘭姆酒傳統分為英式、法式和西班牙式風格。","Portugal is linked to Brazil and cachaça, outside the Caribbean split. Italy and Germany left no recognised rum tradition in the Caribbean.":"葡萄牙與巴西和 cachaça 有關，不在加勒比海的劃分之內。義大利和德國在加勒比海沒有留下公認的蘭姆酒傳統。","Why did the British Caribbean islands develop a tradition of heavy marks?":"為什麼英屬加勒比海島嶼發展出厚重型 mark 的傳統？","The Navy ration needed a rum with plenty of character":"海軍配給需要特色十足的蘭姆酒","Britain banned column stills in its colonies":"英國禁止殖民地使用柱式蒸餾器","The British preferred rum undiluted":"英國人偏好不稀釋的蘭姆酒","Cane juice was kept for beet sugar":"甘蔗汁被留給甜菜製糖","The British Navy served rum diluted, sweetened and with lime: it needed a rum rich in heavy marks.":"英國海軍供應的蘭姆酒要稀釋、加糖並加萊姆：需要富含厚重型 mark 的蘭姆酒。","Precisely because it was diluted with water, the rum needed lots of character. There was no column ban. The beet story concerns France and explains rhum agricole, not the British style.":"正因為要加水稀釋，蘭姆酒才需要大量的特色。當時沒有禁用蒸餾柱。甜菜的故事與法國有關，解釋的是 rhum agricole，不是英式風格。","Which two countries supplied the main rums for the British Navy blend?":"哪兩個國家供應英國海軍調和所用的主要蘭姆酒？","Jamaica and Guyana":"牙買加和蓋亞那","Cuba and Puerto Rico":"古巴和波多黎各","Martinique and Guadeloupe":"馬丁尼克和瓜地洛普","Brazil and Venezuela":"巴西和委內瑞拉","Jamaica and Guyana each made a different style, which were blended for the Navy.":"牙買加和蓋亞那各自做出不同的風格，再調和起來供海軍使用。","Cuba and Puerto Rico represent the Spanish style, Martinique and Guadeloupe the French one. Brazil and Venezuela were never British colonies.":"古巴和波多黎各代表西班牙風格，馬丁尼克和瓜地洛普代表法式風格。巴西和委內瑞拉從來不是英國殖民地。","How are Jamaican high-ester marks usually used?":"牙買加的高酯 mark 通常怎麼使用？","In small doses, to give blends an aromatic lift":"少量使用，為調和提升香氣","Bottled on their own as flagship aged rums":"單獨裝瓶，作為旗艦級陳年蘭姆酒","As a neutral base for spiced rums":"作為香料蘭姆酒的中性基酒","Redistilled to make them lighter and softer before use":"使用前再蒸餾，讓它更清淡、更柔和","On their own they would be too pungent; in blends they add dramatic fruit.":"單獨喝會太刺激；在調和中它們增添強烈的果香。","Blenders still seek them out, which is also why many Jamaican rums are notably fruity. They are the opposite of a neutral base, and redistilling them would erase the very character that makes them valuable.":"調和師仍然特地找它們，這也是許多牙買加蘭姆酒果香格外突出的原因。它們與中性基酒恰恰相反，而再蒸餾會抹去讓它們有價值的那份特色。","Which white rums can match an unaged rhum agricole for aroma intensity?":"哪些白蘭姆酒在香氣強度上能與未陳年的 rhum agricole 相比？","Jamaican high-ester white rums":"牙買加的高酯白蘭姆酒","Cuban-style white rums":"古巴風格的白蘭姆酒","Barbados white rums":"巴貝多的白蘭姆酒","Any white rum charcoal-filtered after brief ageing":"任何短暫陳年後經木炭過濾的白蘭姆酒","Jamaican high-ester whites are among the very few rums as intense as a young agricole.":"牙買加的高酯白蘭姆酒是極少數和年輕 agricole 一樣濃烈的蘭姆酒。","The Cuban style is deliberately light and smooth, and Barbados makes gentler rums. Filtering after brief ageing gives smoothness, not aromatic intensity.":"古巴風格刻意做得清淡柔順，巴貝多則生產較溫和的蘭姆酒。短暫陳年後過濾帶來的是柔順，不是香氣強度。","How does the Barbados rum style compare with Jamaica and Guyana?":"與牙買加和蓋亞那相比，巴貝多的蘭姆酒風格如何？","Smoother, softer and less pronounced":"更柔順、更柔和，香氣較不明顯","More pungent and richer in esters":"更刺激，酯類更豐富","More vegetal, because it is made from fresh cane juice":"植物氣息更重，因為用新鮮甘蔗汁製成","Heavier and suited to very long ageing":"更厚重，適合非常長期的陳年","Barbados, an important British island, makes rums that are softer and less marked than Jamaica's or Guyana's.":"巴貝多是重要的英屬島嶼，生產的蘭姆酒比牙買加或蓋亞那的更柔和、特徵較不鮮明。","Pungent esters are Jamaica's signature, and richness for long ageing is Guyana's. Fresh cane juice is the basis of the French tradition, not the British one.":"刺激的酯類是牙買加的招牌，適合長期陳年的豐厚感則是蓋亞那的。新鮮甘蔗汁是法式傳統的基礎，不是英式的。","A blender wants to add palate weight and mouthfeel to a rum. Which marks would traditionally be chosen?":"一位調和師想為蘭姆酒增添口中的重量和口感。傳統上會選哪些 mark？","Marks from Guyana":"蓋亞那的 mark","Column light marks above 90% abv":"90% abv 以上的蒸餾柱輕盈型 mark","Charcoal-filtered Cuban-style white rums":"經木炭過濾的古巴風格白蘭姆酒","Young cachaça":"年輕的 cachaça","Guyana marks, young or old, are sought after precisely for the weight and mouthfeel they bring.":"蓋亞那的 mark 不論年輕或陳年，正是因為能帶來重量和口感而受到青睞。","Light marks and Cuban whites lighten a blend rather than add body. Young cachaça mainly brings vegetal cane aromas, not richness.":"輕盈型 mark 和古巴的白蘭姆酒會讓調和更清淡，而不是增加酒體。年輕的 cachaça 主要帶來甘蔗的植物香氣，不是豐厚感。","Which type of still is typically used for French-style rums?":"法式風格的蘭姆酒通常使用哪一種蒸餾器？","Short continuous column stills":"矮的連續式柱式蒸餾器","Very tall multi-plate columns, up to neutral spirit":"蒸餾到中性烈酒的極高多層蒸餾板蒸餾柱","Directly fired clay stills":"直火加熱的陶製蒸餾器","Only double-distilling pot stills":"只用二次蒸餾的壺式蒸餾器","French cane juice rum comes from short columns, giving a vegetal, ester-rich character.":"法式甘蔗汁蘭姆酒來自矮蒸餾柱，帶有植物氣息和豐富的酯類。","A column taken to neutral spirit is banned for any rum. Clay stills belong to Ancestral Mezcal. Pot stills make many British heavy marks but are not the hallmark of the French style.":"蒸餾到中性烈酒的蒸餾柱對任何蘭姆酒都是禁止的。陶製蒸餾器屬於 Ancestral Mezcal。壺式蒸餾器做出許多英式厚重型 mark，但不是法式風格的標誌。","What are French-style white rums mostly made for?":"法式風格的白蘭姆酒主要是為了什麼而製作的？","Mixed drinks, where other ingredients balance their intense aromas":"混合飲料，由其他材料來平衡它們濃烈的香氣","Sipping neat as a digestif":"作為餐後酒純飲慢品","Adding body to British blends":"為英式調和增加酒體","Compulsory ageing":"強制陳年","They are among the most pronounced rums on sale and work best in mixed drinks.":"它們是市面上香氣最明顯的蘭姆酒之一，用在混合飲料中效果最好。","Some are more restrained but keep an expressive aroma. Body in British blends comes from Guyana, and no ageing is required for whites.":"有些較為內斂，但仍保有奔放的香氣。英式調和的酒體來自蓋亞那，白蘭姆酒也沒有陳年的要求。","Compared with the Spanish style, what are French-style golden rums usually like?":"與西班牙風格相比，法式風格的金色蘭姆酒通常是什麼樣子？","Drier, still showing cane juice character":"較不甜，仍表現出甘蔗汁的特色","Sweeter and more vanilla-led":"更甜，更以香草為主","Completely neutral after ageing":"陳年後完全中性","Always caramel-coloured and never oak-aged":"一律用焦糖色上色，從不過橡木桶","Ageing mellows the cane character, and these rums are usually dry or off-dry.":"陳年讓甘蔗特色變得圓熟，這些蘭姆酒通常不甜或微甜。","Sweetness and vanilla are Spanish-style traits. French golden rums are rarely bone dry, but they are not sweet either. Their colour comes from wood, and rum is never neutral.":"甜味和香草是西班牙風格的特徵。法式金色蘭姆酒很少完全不甜，但也不是甜的。它們的顏色來自木頭，而蘭姆酒絕不是中性的。","Which profile best describes Spanish-style rums?":"哪一種輪廓最能描述西班牙風格的蘭姆酒？","Light to medium intensity, smooth texture":"香氣強度清淡到中等，質地柔順","Very pungent and fruity, rich in esters":"非常刺激而帶果香，富含酯類","Vegetal and grassy, from fresh cane juice":"植物和青草氣息，來自新鮮甘蔗汁","Smoky and earthy, with a heavy, oily body":"煙燻和土壤味，酒體厚重油潤","The Spanish style aims for restrained intensity and a smooth palate.":"西班牙風格追求內斂的香氣強度和柔順的口感。","Pungent esters are Jamaican and vegetal cane juice character is French. Smoke and earth belong to no traditional rum style.":"刺激的酯類是牙買加的，甘蔗汁的植物特色是法式的。煙燻和土壤味不屬於任何傳統的蘭姆酒風格。","Which two choices by Cuban producers created the most popular white rum style?":"古巴生產者的哪兩項選擇創造了最受歡迎的白蘭姆酒風格？","Higher-strength marks and short ageing":"較高濃度的 mark 和短暫陳年","Fresh cane juice and clay stills":"新鮮甘蔗汁和陶製蒸餾器","Ester-rich fermentations and pot stills":"富含酯類的發酵和壺式蒸餾器","Long ageing in new casks and plenty of added spices":"在新桶中長期陳年並添加大量香料","New column technology gave high-strength marks, and short ageing made them softer.":"新的蒸餾柱技術帶來高濃度的 mark，短暫陳年讓它們更柔和。","Esters and pot stills are the Jamaican route to intense rum, the opposite of the Cuban style. Long ageing and spices would not give a light white rum.":"酯類和壺式蒸餾器是牙買加做出濃烈蘭姆酒的路線，與古巴風格相反。長期陳年和香料做不出清淡的白蘭姆酒。","Which marks usually dominate Spanish-style golden rums?":"西班牙風格的金色蘭姆酒通常以哪些 mark 為主？","Light marks":"輕盈型 mark","High-ester heavy marks":"高酯的厚重型 mark","Cane juice marks from short columns":"矮蒸餾柱的甘蔗汁 mark","A legally fixed half-and-half split":"法律規定的各半比例","A high share of light marks, plus oak vanilla and some sugar, gives the typical smoothness.":"高比例的輕盈型 mark，加上橡木的香草味和一些糖，帶來典型的柔順感。","High-ester heavy marks are Jamaican and cane juice marks are French. There are no legal proportions for golden rums: the producer decides.":"高酯的厚重型 mark 是牙買加的，甘蔗汁 mark 是法式的。金色蘭姆酒沒有法定比例：由生產者決定。","Which country is NOT associated with the Spanish rum style?":"哪一個國家與西班牙式蘭姆酒風格無關？","Barbados is a British-tradition island; the others are Spanish-speaking.":"巴貝多是英式傳統的島嶼；其他都是西班牙語國家。","Guatemala, Panama and Venezuela, along with Cuba and Puerto Rico, are linked with smooth rums, often medium-sweet. Barbados also makes smooth rums, but within the British tradition.":"瓜地馬拉、巴拿馬和委內瑞拉，連同古巴和波多黎各，都與柔順、常為中等甜度的蘭姆酒有關。巴貝多也生產柔順的蘭姆酒，但屬於英式傳統。","Which country is the world's largest rum producer?":"哪一個國家是全世界最大的蘭姆酒生產國？","Brazil":"巴西","Martinique":"馬丁尼克","Brazil is the largest producer, mainly thanks to cachaça.":"巴西是最大的生產國，主要靠 cachaça。","Jamaica, Cuba and Martinique are famous for style, not volume. Cachaça is made in greater quantity than all the world's vodka, but nearly all of it is drunk in Brazil.":"牙買加、古巴和馬丁尼克以風格聞名，不是產量。Cachaça 的產量比全世界的伏特加還多，但幾乎都在巴西喝掉。","Which statement about cachaça is true?":"關於 cachaça，下列哪一項正確？","More is made than all the world's vodka, but it is mostly drunk in Brazil":"產量比全世界的伏特加還多，但大多在巴西飲用","It is mostly exported to the Caribbean for blending":"大多出口到加勒比海供調和使用","It is made from top-grade molasses":"用最高等級的糖蜜製成","It is always aged and bone dry":"一律經過陳年，而且完全不甜","Cachaça production is huge but almost all of it stays in Brazil.":"Cachaça 的產量極大，但幾乎都留在巴西。","Cachaça is made from cane juice, not molasses. Most is unaged and often lightly sweetened, so it is not \"always aged and dry\".":"Cachaça 用甘蔗汁製成，不是糖蜜。大多不經陳年，並常略微加糖，所以並不是「一律陳年且不甜」。","How did British sailors test rum strength, giving rise to the term \"proof\"?":"英國水手如何測試蘭姆酒的濃度，並由此產生了「proof」一詞？","They mixed it with gunpowder to see if it would burn":"把它與火藥混合，看能不能點燃","They weighed it against the same volume of seawater":"拿它與同體積的海水比重量","They froze it to see if it turned cloudy":"把它冷凍，看會不會變混濁","They measured its colour":"測量它的顏色","If the rum-and-gunpowder mix burned, the rum was at least 57.15% abv, defined as \"100 proof\".":"如果蘭姆酒和火藥的混合物能燃燒，蘭姆酒就至少是 57.15% abv，定義為「100 proof」。","The other tests have nothing to do with the term's origin. Colour says nothing about strength, and haze on chilling depends on other compounds, not alcohol.":"其他測試都與這個術語的由來無關。顏色與濃度無關，冰鎮時的混濁取決於其他化合物，不是酒精。","One US rum says \"80 proof\", another rum says \"overproof\". What does this mean?":"一款美國蘭姆酒寫著「80 proof」，另一款蘭姆酒寫著「overproof」。這是什麼意思？","The first is 40% abv; the second refers to an old British system":"第一款是 40% abv；第二款指的是舊的英國制度","Both use the same system and the second is above 100":"兩者用的是同一套制度，第二款高於 100","The first is 80% abv; the second is below 40% abv":"第一款是 80% abv；第二款低於 40% abv","Both are legal terms that guarantee the rum's age":"兩者都是保證蘭姆酒年數的法定術語","In the USA 2 proof = 1% abv, so 80 proof = 40%; \"overproof\" comes from the historic British system.":"在美國 2 proof = 1% abv，所以 80 proof = 40%；「overproof」則來自歷史上的英國制度。","They are two different systems: the US one is in use, the British one is no longer a regulated measure. Neither says anything about age, and overproof means high strength, not low.":"這是兩套不同的制度：美國的仍在使用，英國的已不再是受規範的度量。兩者都與年數無關，overproof 的意思是高濃度，不是低濃度。","In the old British system, what was an \"under proof\" rum?":"在舊的英國制度中，「under proof」的蘭姆酒是什麼？","A rum below 57.15% abv":"低於 57.15% abv 的蘭姆酒","A rum aged less than one year":"陳年不滿一年的蘭姆酒","A rum that failed the Navy's quality rules":"不符合海軍品質規定的蘭姆酒","A rum below 40% abv":"低於 40% abv 的蘭姆酒","57.15% abv was 100 proof: below it was \"under proof\", above it \"over proof\".":"57.15% abv 是 100 proof：低於它是「under proof」，高於它是「over proof」。","The term is only about strength, not age or quality. 40% is a common bottling strength today, but it has nothing to do with the British threshold.":"這個術語只與濃度有關，與年數或品質無關。40% 是現今常見的裝瓶濃度，但與英國的門檻毫無關係。","Today, what status does \"overproof\" have on a rum label?":"如今，「overproof」在蘭姆酒酒標上的地位是什麼？","Just a historic reference, not a regulated measure":"只是歷史上的說法，不是受規範的度量","It is the official measure used by the British authorities":"是英國主管機關使用的官方度量","It guarantees at least three years in cask":"保證在桶中至少三年","It shows the rum has been redistilled":"表示蘭姆酒經過再蒸餾","The term signals an unusually high strength, but the system is no longer used by distillers or authorities.":"這個術語表示濃度特別高，但這套制度已不再為蒸餾師或主管機關所用。","It says nothing about age or distillation. Today strength is given in % abv, and in the USA also in US proof, which is a different system.":"它與年數或蒸餾無關。現今濃度以 % abv 表示，在美國也用美國 proof，那是另一套制度。","A customer sees \"XO\" on a rum and assumes it means the same as on Cognac. What is the right reply?":"一位顧客在蘭姆酒上看到「XO」，以為和 Cognac 上的意思一樣。正確的回答是什麼？","On rum, \"XO\" carries no legal guarantee":"在蘭姆酒上，「XO」沒有任何法律保證","True, Cognac's rules apply to every spirit":"沒錯，Cognac 的規定適用於所有烈酒","\"XO\" on rum always means at least twenty years of ageing":"蘭姆酒上的「XO」一律表示至少陳年二十年","\"XO\" on rum only shows it was made from molasses":"蘭姆酒上的「XO」只表示它用糖蜜製成","Rum age terms are not regulated as Cognac's are: their meaning depends on the producer.":"蘭姆酒的年數術語不像 Cognac 那樣受規範：它們的意義取決於生產者。","Some XO rums do meet Cognac-like standards, but that is the producer's choice. The law only bans false claims; it does not define every term. \"XO\" says nothing about raw material.":"有些 XO 蘭姆酒確實達到類似 Cognac 的標準，但那是生產者的選擇。法律只禁止不實的宣稱，並沒有定義每一個術語。「XO」與原料無關。","A Caribbean label says \"rhum agricole\". What does that tell you about the raw material?":"一張加勒比海的酒標寫著「rhum agricole」。這告訴你原料是什麼？","It comes from fresh cane juice":"來自新鮮甘蔗汁","It comes from top-grade molasses":"來自最高等級的糖蜜","It comes from organically grown cane, with no origin rule":"來自有機種植的甘蔗，沒有產地規定","It comes from refined cane sugar dissolved in water":"來自溶於水的精製蔗糖","\"Rhum agricole\" means a cane juice rum, and in the Caribbean only from Martinique and Guadeloupe.":"「Rhum agricole」表示甘蔗汁蘭姆酒，在加勒比海只能來自馬丁尼克和瓜地洛普。","\"Agricole\" does not mean organic: it shows the juice never went through the sugar industry. Molasses and refined sugar are both sugar-industry products.":"「Agricole」不是有機的意思：它表示甘蔗汁從未經過製糖業。糖蜜和精製糖都是製糖業的產品。","Why are rum labelling terms only loosely defined?":"為什麼蘭姆酒的標示術語定義得很鬆散？","No single overarching set of rules controls them":"沒有單一、通盤的規定來管理它們","Because producers must change them every year":"因為生產者每年都必須更改","Because rum may not show any age or colour terms at all":"因為蘭姆酒完全不能標示任何年數或顏色術語","Because every island sets them with identical rules":"因為每個島都用完全相同的規定來制定","Rum is made in many countries with no common rulebook, so many terms vary in meaning.":"蘭姆酒在許多國家生產，沒有共同的規範，所以許多術語的意義各不相同。","Age and colour often appear on labels: the problem is that their meaning is not uniform. If every island had identical rules the terms would be clear, but they do not.":"年數和顏色常出現在酒標上：問題在於它們的意義並不統一。如果每個島的規定都相同，術語就會很清楚，但事實並非如此。","In what form does agave store its carbohydrate reserves?":"龍舌蘭以什麼形式儲存碳水化合物？","Sucrose":"蔗糖","Cellulose":"纖維素","Agave stores inulin in its hard core.":"龍舌蘭把菊糖儲存在堅硬的核心裡。","Inulin cannot be fermented directly; the heat of cooking must turn it into sugars. Starch is the reserve found in grains and potatoes, converted with enzymes. Sucrose is the ready-made sugar in cane, and cellulose makes up fibres.":"菊糖無法直接發酵；必須靠烹煮的熱把它變成糖。澱粉是穀物和馬鈴薯中的儲備，用酵素轉化。蔗糖是甘蔗中現成的糖，纖維素則構成纖維。","What is the piña?":"什麼是 piña？","The agave's core once the leaves are removed":"切除葉片後的龍舌蘭核心","The agave flower, picked before it wilts":"在凋謝前摘下的龍舌蘭花","The tropical fruit added to some Tequilas":"加進某些 Tequila 的熱帶水果","The fibrous residue left after distillation":"蒸餾後剩下的纖維殘渣","The piña is the plant's core, left once roots and leaves are cut away.":"piña 是植株的核心，是切掉根和葉之後留下的部分。","It gets its name from looking like a pineapple, but it is not a fruit. It is the inulin-rich part that is cooked, crushed and fermented. The flower appears only once, at the end of the plant's life, and harvest should happen before that.":"它因為看起來像鳳梨而得名，但不是水果。它是富含菊糖的部分，要經過烹煮、壓碎和發酵。花只在植株生命的最後開一次，採收應該在那之前進行。","Why must the piña be cooked before fermentation?":"為什麼 piña 必須在發酵前烹煮？","Heat turns the inulin into sugars":"熱把菊糖變成糖","Heat removes the spines and wax from the leaves":"熱去除葉片上的刺和蠟","Heat kills the wild yeasts living in the plant":"熱殺死生活在植株裡的野生酵母","Heat always gives the spirit a smoky taste":"熱一定會讓烈酒帶煙燻味","Without heat, inulin does not become fermentable sugar.":"沒有熱，菊糖就不會變成可發酵的糖。","Cooking is the step that makes sugars available to yeast. The leaves are cut off beforehand, not cooked. Smoke depends on the method: pit roasting adds it, Tequila's steaming does not, so cooking does not always make a spirit smoky.":"烹煮是讓酵母能利用糖的步驟。葉片事先就切除了，不會烹煮。煙燻味取決於方法：窯坑烘烤會增添煙燻味，Tequila 的蒸煮則不會，所以烹煮不一定讓烈酒帶煙燻味。","How is agave traditionally cooked for Tequila?":"Tequila 的龍舌蘭傳統上怎麼烹煮？","Slowly steamed in brick ovens":"在磚爐中慢慢蒸煮","Roasted in stone-lined pits under a layer of earth":"在鋪石的窯坑中、蓋上一層土烘烤","Boiled directly in the still before distillation":"蒸餾前直接在蒸餾器中煮沸","Dried in the sun for several weeks":"在太陽下曬乾幾個星期","Tequila's traditional method is slow steaming in brick ovens.":"Tequila 的傳統做法是在磚爐中慢慢蒸煮。","Many now use pressurised steam ovens, which are much faster, but care is needed not to burn the agave. Pit roasting over hot stones is Mezcal's traditional method and the source of its smoke. The other options would not properly convert the inulin.":"現在許多人使用加壓蒸汽爐，速度快得多，但要小心別把龍舌蘭燒焦。在熱石頭上的窯坑烘烤是 Mezcal 的傳統做法，也是它煙燻味的來源。其他選項無法正確轉化菊糖。","In agave spirit production, what is meant by \"formulation\"?":"在龍舌蘭烈酒的生產中，「formulation」（調配）指的是什麼？","Making up the sweet liquid for fermentation":"配製用來發酵的甜液","Choosing the blend recipe just before bottling":"裝瓶前選定調和配方","Officially registering the agave variety used":"正式登記所用的龍舌蘭品種","Adding abocado to colour Gold Tequila":"加入 abocado 為 Gold Tequila 上色","Formulation is the stage where the sweet liquid for fermentation is made up.":"調配是配製發酵用甜液的階段。","This is when Tequila producers may add non-agave sugars, up to 49%, or choose to stay 100% agave. The best also add piña fibres here. Abocado is added much later, before bottling, and blending is a separate stage.":"Tequila 的生產者就是在這時可以加入非龍舌蘭的糖（最多 49%），或選擇維持 100% agave。最好的生產者也在這時加入 piña 的纖維。Abocado 要到很後面、裝瓶前才加，調和則是另一個階段。","Why do some quality producers add piña fibres to the fermenter?":"為什麼有些重視品質的生產者在發酵槽中加入 piña 纖維？","To intensify the agave character":"加強龍舌蘭的特色","So they can claim more years of ageing on the label":"這樣就能在酒標上宣稱更多的陳年年數","To filter the liquid and make it clearer and more neutral":"過濾液體，讓它更清澈、更中性","To replace yeast with a natural fermentation":"用天然發酵取代酵母","Fibres in the ferment help maximise agave flavours.":"發酵時帶著纖維，有助於把龍舌蘭風味發揮到極致。","It is a hallmark of the best Tequilas and a requirement for Artisanal and Ancestral Mezcal. It has nothing to do with age and does not make the spirit more neutral; if anything, the opposite. Yeast is still essential for any alcoholic fermentation.":"這是最好的 Tequila 的標誌，也是 Artisanal 和 Ancestral Mezcal 的要求。它與年數無關，也不會讓烈酒更中性；恰恰相反。任何酒精發酵仍然少不了酵母。","Why are very few agave spirits aged for long periods in oak barrels?":"為什麼很少有龍舌蘭烈酒在橡木桶中長期陳年？","Oak easily overwhelms agave aromas":"橡木很容易蓋過龍舌蘭的香氣","Mexican law bans any contact with wood":"墨西哥法律禁止任何與木頭的接觸","Agave reacts with oak and becomes toxic over time":"龍舌蘭會與橡木反應，久了會產生毒性","Oak barrels are not available in Mexico":"墨西哥買不到橡木桶","Balancing agave and oak is hard, because oak dominates easily.":"龍舌蘭和橡木很難平衡，因為橡木很容易占上風。","That is why most rest in inert vessels or very large oak vats, which give little oak flavour but add smoothness and complexity. Barrel ageing does exist, and is even required for Añejo and Extra Añejo, so it is certainly not banned.":"所以大多數都在惰性容器或非常大的橡木槽中靜置，這些容器給的橡木風味很少，卻能增添柔順感和複雜度。桶陳確實存在，Añejo 和 Extra Añejo 甚至強制要求，所以當然沒有被禁止。","How are top-quality Tequila and Mezcal usually distilled?":"頂級品質的 Tequila 和 Mezcal 通常怎麼蒸餾？","Twice in pot stills":"在壺式蒸餾器中蒸餾兩次","Once in a column still to about 96% abv":"在柱式蒸餾器中蒸餾一次，到約 96% abv","In a hybrid still linked to a rectifying column":"在連接精餾柱的混合式蒸餾器中","Three times in columns, then charcoal filtered":"在蒸餾柱中蒸餾三次，再用木炭過濾","Double pot distillation keeps as much agave character as possible.":"壺式二次蒸餾能盡可能保留龍舌蘭的特色。","Tequila producers usually use large modern pot stills, while Mezcal stills are small and often home-made. Some spirits are even collected below 60% abv. Very high-strength columns and heavy filtration strip aromas away, which is vodka's goal.":"Tequila 的生產者通常使用大型的現代壺式蒸餾器，Mezcal 的蒸餾器則很小，而且常是自製的。有些烈酒甚至在低於 60% abv 時收集。濃度極高的蒸餾柱和重度過濾會去除香氣，那是伏特加的目標。","Which agave is permitted for Tequila?":"Tequila 允許使用哪一種龍舌蘭？","Blue agave only":"只有藍色龍舌蘭","Espadín agave only":"只有 espadín 龍舌蘭","Any species grown in Jalisco":"哈利斯科州種植的任何品種","A blend of at least three species":"至少三個品種的混合","Tequila is made exclusively from blue agave.":"Tequila 只用藍色龍舌蘭製成。","Although it is the largest agave spirit by volume, Tequila is limited to one variety, which originates in Jalisco. Espadín is Mezcal's main variety, and Mezcal allows several species. Growing a different agave in Jalisco is not enough to make Tequila.":"雖然 Tequila 是產量最大的龍舌蘭烈酒，卻只限使用一個品種，它原產於哈利斯科州。Espadín 是 Mezcal 的主要品種，而 Mezcal 允許使用數個品種。在哈利斯科州種別種龍舌蘭，並不足以做出 Tequila。","Which Mexican state is most important for Tequila?":"哪一個墨西哥州對 Tequila 最重要？","Jalisco is the heart of Tequila and the home of blue agave.":"哈利斯科州（Jalisco）是 Tequila 的核心，也是藍色龍舌蘭的故鄉。","Agave for Tequila can be grown in five states, but Jalisco is by far the most important. Oaxaca, by contrast, is the key state for Mezcal. A simple memory aid: Jalisco for Tequila, Oaxaca for smoky Mezcal.":"Tequila 的龍舌蘭可以種在五個州，但哈利斯科州遠遠最重要。瓦哈卡州（Oaxaca）則是 Mezcal 的關鍵州。一個簡單的記法：Jalisco 是 Tequila，Oaxaca 是煙燻的 Mezcal。","A bottle says just \"Tequila\", without \"100% agave\". What can be inferred?":"一瓶酒只寫著「Tequila」，沒有「100% agave」。可以推論出什麼？","At least 51% of the sugars came from agave":"至少 51% 的糖來自龍舌蘭","It was aged for at least one year in oak barrels":"它在橡木桶中陳年了至少一年","It is made from several agave species, not just blue":"它用數種龍舌蘭製成，不只是藍色龍舌蘭","It contains less alcohol than a 100% agave Tequila":"它的酒精比 100% agave 的 Tequila 少","Plain \"Tequila\" requires only 51% agave sugars.":"單純的「Tequila」只要求 51% 的龍舌蘭糖。","The other 49% can come from non-agave sources, which dilute the spirit's character. This Tequila still uses only blue agave; what changes is the share of non-agave sugar. The label says nothing about age or strength.":"其餘 49% 可以來自非龍舌蘭的來源，這會稀釋烈酒的特色。這種 Tequila 仍然只用藍色龍舌蘭；改變的是非龍舌蘭糖的比例。酒標與年數或濃度無關。","A bartender wants a Tequila with maximum agave character for a cocktail. What should the label say?":"一位調酒師想為一款調酒找龍舌蘭特色最鮮明的 Tequila。酒標上應該寫什麼？","100% agave":"100% agave","Long-aged Extra Añejo":"長期陳年的 Extra Añejo","100% agave guarantees that every fermented sugar came from agave.":"100% agave 保證每一分發酵的糖都來自龍舌蘭。","Non-agave sugars dilute the plant's character. Gold means a Tequila coloured with abocado, not a better one. Long ageing risks burying the agave under oak. Mixto is an informal name, not a label term, for Tequilas that are not 100% agave.":"非龍舌蘭的糖會稀釋這種植物的特色。Gold 表示用 abocado 上色的 Tequila，不是更好的 Tequila。長期陳年可能讓龍舌蘭被橡木蓋住。Mixto 是對非 100% agave 的 Tequila 的非正式稱呼，不是酒標術語。","Which statement about Gold Tequila is correct?":"關於 Gold Tequila，下列哪一項正確？","It is unaged; its colour comes from abocado":"它未經陳年；顏色來自 abocado","It has spent at least two months in large oak vats":"它在大型橡木槽中存放了至少兩個月","It is always a premium 100% agave Tequila":"它一定是高級的 100% agave Tequila","It gets its colour from pit-roasted agave":"它的顏色來自窯坑烘烤的龍舌蘭","Gold is coloured and softened with abocado, without any time in wood.":"Gold 是用 abocado 上色並變得柔和的，完全沒有在木頭中存放。","Abocado contains caramel and other ingredients designed to mimic the smoothness of ageing. Two months in oak describes Reposado. A golden colour is no guarantee of quality, and pit roasting belongs to Mezcal, not Tequila.":"Abocado 含有焦糖色和其他材料，用來模仿陳年的柔順感。在橡木中兩個月描述的是 Reposado。金黃的顏色不保證品質，窯坑烘烤則屬於 Mezcal，不是 Tequila。","Which Tequila category requires at least three years in oak barrels?":"哪一個 Tequila 類別要求在橡木桶中至少三年？","Extra Añejo must spend at least three years in oak barrels.":"Extra Añejo 必須在橡木桶中存放至少三年。","Añejo needs at least one year in barrel and Reposado at least two months, usually in very large vats. Gold is unaged; its colour comes from abocado. Long-aged categories are rare because wood tends to mask the agave.":"Añejo 需要在桶中至少一年，Reposado 至少兩個月，通常在非常大的木槽中。Gold 未經陳年；顏色來自 abocado。長期陳年的類別很少見，因為木頭往往會掩蓋龍舌蘭。","Blue agave grown at altitude: what is a typical effect on aroma?":"種在高海拔的藍色龍舌蘭：對香氣的典型影響是什麼？","Fruitier aromas":"香氣更偏果香","A much smokier, earthier character":"煙燻和土壤特色重得多","A completely neutral spirit":"完全中性的烈酒","Vanilla and coconut notes without oak":"不用橡木就有香草和椰子氣息","Blue agave from higher altitudes can give fruitier aromas.":"來自較高海拔的藍色龍舌蘭可能帶來更偏果香的香氣。","Even with a single variety, where the agave grows changes the flavour of Tequila. Smoke comes from pit roasting, typical of Mezcal, not from altitude. Vanilla and coconut come from oak, and no agave spirit aims for neutrality.":"即使只有單一品種，龍舌蘭種在哪裡也會改變 Tequila 的風味。煙燻味來自窯坑烘烤，是 Mezcal 的典型特徵，不是來自海拔。香草和椰子來自橡木，也沒有任何龍舌蘭烈酒以中性為目標。","Which state is most important for Mezcal production?":"哪一個州對 Mezcal 的生產最重要？","Oaxaca, in southern Mexico, makes the vast majority of Mezcal.":"墨西哥南部的瓦哈卡州（Oaxaca）生產了絕大部分的 Mezcal。","The Mezcal geographical indication covers several states, but Oaxaca dominates, and its main variety is espadín. Jalisco is the heart of Tequila. Mezcal production remains largely small-scale and hands-on.":"Mezcal 的地理標示涵蓋數個州，但以瓦哈卡州為主，它的主要品種是 espadín。哈利斯科州是 Tequila 的核心。Mezcal 的生產大致上仍是小規模、手工的。","Which agave variety is most widely used for Mezcal?":"Mezcal 使用最廣的是哪一個龍舌蘭品種？","Blue agave, the same one required for Tequila":"藍色龍舌蘭，和 Tequila 規定的相同","A single variety imposed by law in every state":"法律在每個州強制規定的單一品種","Wild agave picked only after flowering":"只在開花後採收的野生龍舌蘭","Espadín is Oaxaca's main variety and the most common in Mezcal.":"Espadín 是瓦哈卡州的主要品種，也是 Mezcal 中最常見的。","Unlike Tequila, Mezcal can use several agave species, and expert tasters can tell them apart. No single variety is compulsory. Harvesting after flowering would be a mistake, since the plant would have used up its inulin.":"與 Tequila 不同，Mezcal 可以使用數種龍舌蘭，品飲專家能分辨它們。沒有強制使用的單一品種。開花後採收會是錯誤，因為植株已經耗盡菊糖。","A customer notices a smoky aroma in an agave spirit. Where does it most likely come from?":"一位顧客在一款龍舌蘭烈酒中聞到煙燻香氣。它最可能來自哪裡？","Roasting the piñas in stone pits":"在石砌窯坑中烘烤 piña","Steaming in modern pressurised ovens":"在現代加壓爐中蒸煮","Abocado added before bottling":"裝瓶前加入的 abocado","A long rest in large oak vats":"在大型橡木槽中長時間靜置","Roasting piñas in fire-heated pits gives Mezcal its typical smoky notes.":"在用火加熱的窯坑中烘烤 piña，賦予 Mezcal 典型的煙燻氣息。","Smoke is the easiest way to tell Mezcal from Tequila, although its intensity varies a lot. Steaming adds no flavour to the piña. Abocado colours and softens, and large vats give very little wood flavour.":"煙燻味是分辨 Mezcal 和 Tequila 最簡單的方法，不過它的強度差異很大。蒸煮不會為 piña 增添風味。Abocado 是上色和柔化用的，大型木槽給的木頭風味非常少。","Which requirement sets Ancestral Mezcal apart from Artisanal Mezcal?":"哪一項要求讓 Ancestral Mezcal 有別於 Artisanal Mezcal？","Directly heated clay stills":"直火加熱的陶製蒸餾器","Cooking also allowed in pressurised steam ovens":"也允許用加壓蒸汽爐烹煮","Compulsory column distillation for extra purity":"為了更純淨而強制用蒸餾柱蒸餾","Fermentation without agave fibres":"發酵時不帶龍舌蘭纖維","Ancestral requires directly heated clay stills, as well as pits and no mechanical mills.":"Ancestral 要求直火加熱的陶製蒸餾器，還有窯坑和不使用機械磨碎機。","Artisanal allows directly heated metal or clay stills, brick ovens and some mills; Ancestral tightens everything: pits only, non-mechanical crushing and fibres in distillation too. Pressurised ovens and column stills are allowed only in the plain Mezcal category.":"Artisanal 允許直火加熱的金屬或陶製蒸餾器、磚爐和某些磨碎機；Ancestral 則全面收緊：只能用窯坑、非機械壓碎，蒸餾時也要帶纖維。加壓爐和柱式蒸餾器只允許用於一般的 Mezcal 類別。","What is allowed for a spirit labelled simply \"Mezcal\", with no further term?":"只標示「Mezcal」、沒有其他術語的烈酒，允許什麼？","Any cooking method and any still, columns included":"任何烹煮方式和任何蒸餾器，包括蒸餾柱","Only stone pits and clay stills":"只能用石砌窯坑和陶製蒸餾器","Only blue agave grown in Jalisco":"只能用哈利斯科州種植的藍色龍舌蘭","Only fermentation in stone vessels with agave fibres added":"只能在石製容器中帶龍舌蘭纖維發酵","The basic Mezcal class sets no limits on cooking, crushing, fermenters or type of still.":"基本的 Mezcal 等級對烹煮、壓碎、發酵容器或蒸餾器類型都沒有限制。","The Artisanal and Ancestral classes exist precisely to separate traditionally made Mezcal from industrial production. Pits and clay stills are Ancestral requirements, and stone vessels with fibres belong to Artisanal. Blue agave from Jalisco is a Tequila matter.":"Artisanal 和 Ancestral 等級的存在，正是為了把傳統製作的 Mezcal 與工業化生產區分開來。窯坑和陶製蒸餾器是 Ancestral 的要求，石製容器加纖維屬於 Artisanal。哈利斯科州的藍色龍舌蘭則是 Tequila 的事。","Where is agave native to?":"龍舌蘭原產於哪裡？","Central America":"中美洲","North Africa":"北非","The Caribbean islands":"加勒比海島嶼","South-East Asia":"東南亞","Agave is native to Central America, with hundreds of species.":"龍舌蘭原產於中美洲，有數百個品種。","Today agave grows from the southern USA into South America, but spirit production is dominated by Mexico. The Caribbean is home to rum, not agave.":"如今龍舌蘭從美國南部一直生長到南美洲，但烈酒的生產以墨西哥為主。加勒比海是蘭姆酒的故鄉，不是龍舌蘭。","What happens to an agave plant when it flowers?":"龍舌蘭開花時會怎麼樣？","It uses up all its inulin and dies":"它耗盡所有菊糖並死亡","It doubles its store of inulin":"它的菊糖儲量加倍","It starts making starch instead of inulin":"它開始製造澱粉而不是菊糖","It flowers again every year for about ten years":"它每年再開花，持續十年左右","Agave flowers just once, exhausts its reserves and dies.":"龍舌蘭只開一次花，耗盡儲備後死亡。","That is exactly why flowering is the wrong moment to harvest: the reserves are gone. Agave stores inulin, not starch, and does not flower again.":"這正是為什麼開花是錯誤的採收時機：儲備已經沒了。龍舌蘭儲存的是菊糖，不是澱粉，而且不會再次開花。","When is the ideal time to harvest agave?":"採收龍舌蘭的理想時機是什麼時候？","At peak maturity, just before it flowers":"在最成熟的時候，就在開花之前","Just after flowering, when the stalk is tallest":"剛開完花、花莖最高的時候","In its first year, when the leaves are most tender":"第一年，葉片最嫩的時候","Any time at all, since maturity makes no difference":"隨時都可以，因為成熟度沒有影響","Just before flowering the plant has the most complex aromas and the highest inulin yield.":"就在開花之前，植株有最複雜的香氣和最高的菊糖產量。","After flowering the inulin is used up and the plant dies. A young plant has not yet built reserves or aromas. The leaves are thrown away anyway.":"開花後菊糖已用完，植株也會死亡。年輕的植株還沒累積儲備或香氣。葉片反正都會丟掉。","How long can some agave species take to reach maturity?":"有些龍舌蘭品種要多久才能成熟？","15 to 20 years":"15 到 20 年","A single season, like cereals":"一個生長季，像穀物一樣","2 to 3 years":"2 到 3 年","Over 50 years, like the oaks used for casks":"超過 50 年，像製桶用的橡樹","Agave is long-lived: some species need 15–20 years.":"龍舌蘭壽命長：有些品種需要 15–20 年。","Tequila's blue agave is relatively quick at 7–10 years. No agave matures in a season or two years, and none takes as long as an oak.":"Tequila 的藍色龍舌蘭相對較快，7–10 年。沒有龍舌蘭在一季或兩年內成熟，也沒有像橡樹那麼久的。","What aromas does agave develop during its life?":"龍舌蘭在生長過程中發展出哪些香氣？","Herbaceous: bell pepper, vegetables, pepper":"草本：甜椒、蔬菜、胡椒","Floral and red-fruit, like some gins":"花香和紅色水果，像某些琴酒","Malt, bread and cereal":"麥芽、麵包和穀物","Mature agave develops complex herbaceous aromas recalling bell pepper, vegetables and pepper.":"成熟的龍舌蘭發展出複雜的草本香氣，讓人想到甜椒、蔬菜和胡椒。","Vanilla and coconut come from oak, not the plant. Malt and bread are typical of grain spirits. Flowers and red fruit are not part of the agave profile.":"香草和椰子來自橡木，不是植物。麥芽和麵包是穀物烈酒的典型特徵。花香和紅色水果不屬於龍舌蘭的輪廓。","A Tequila distillery switches to pressurised steam ovens. What is the gain, and the risk?":"一家 Tequila 蒸餾廠改用加壓蒸汽爐。好處和風險各是什麼？","Much faster, but the agave may burn":"快得多，但龍舌蘭可能燒焦","They add smoke, but the right to say \"Tequila\" is lost":"增添煙燻味，但失去標示「Tequila」的資格","They turn inulin into starch, but need enzymes":"把菊糖變成澱粉，但需要酵素","They double the sugar extracted from the leaves":"從葉片萃取的糖加倍","Pressurised steam greatly speeds cooking, but care is needed not to burn the agave in the rush.":"加壓蒸汽大幅加快烹煮，但要小心別在趕時間時把龍舌蘭燒焦。","Steam adds no smoke: that comes from pit roasting. Cooking turns inulin into sugars, not starch. The leaves are discarded before cooking.":"蒸汽不會增添煙燻味：那來自窯坑烘烤。烹煮把菊糖變成糖，不是澱粉。葉片在烹煮前就丟棄了。","How are cooked piñas usually crushed today, especially for Tequila?":"現今煮熟的 piña 通常怎麼壓碎，尤其是 Tequila？","With mechanical mills":"用機械磨碎機","With a large stone wheel":"用大石輪","By hand with wooden mallets":"用木槌手工敲打","They are not crushed but fermented whole":"不壓碎，整顆發酵","The stone wheel is traditional, but mechanical mills now dominate, especially for Tequila.":"石輪是傳統做法，但現在以機械磨碎機為主，尤其是 Tequila。","Piñas must be crushed to free the sweet juice from the fibres, then rinsed with water to extract all the sugar. For Ancestral Mezcal, mechanical mills are banned.":"piña 必須壓碎，才能把甜汁從纖維中釋放出來，接著用水沖洗以萃取所有的糖。Ancestral Mezcal 禁止使用機械磨碎機。","After crushing, why is water flushed through the piñas?":"壓碎後，為什麼要用水沖洗 piña？","To extract all the sugar":"萃取所有的糖","To cool them before a second cooking":"在第二次烹煮前讓它降溫","To wash away the smoke from cooking":"洗掉烹煮帶來的煙燻味","To lower the final strength":"降低最終的濃度","Flushing recovers the sugar still held in the crushed fibres.":"沖洗能回收仍留在壓碎纖維中的糖。","There is no second cooking, and mezcal's smoke is wanted, not washed away. Final strength is set after distillation, not at this stage.":"沒有第二次烹煮，而 mezcal 的煙燻味是想要的，不會洗掉。最終的濃度是蒸餾後才決定的，不是在這個階段。","In Tequila formulation, what is the maximum share of non-agave sugars?":"在 Tequila 的調配中，非龍舌蘭糖的最高比例是多少？","No limit, as long as there is some agave":"沒有限制，只要有一些龍舌蘭","Up to 49% of the sugars may come from other sources; at least 51% must be agave.":"最多 49% 的糖可以來自其他來源；至少 51% 必須是龍舌蘭。","51% is the agave minimum, not the cap on other sugars: the two numbers are easy to mix up. A limit definitely exists.":"51% 是龍舌蘭的最低比例，不是其他糖的上限：這兩個數字很容易搞混。限制確實存在。","What effect do non-agave sugars have on a Tequila's flavour?":"非龍舌蘭的糖對 Tequila 的風味有什麼影響？","They dilute the agave character":"稀釋龍舌蘭的特色","They make the spirit smokier":"讓烈酒更有煙燻味","They leave it sweet in the bottle":"讓瓶中的酒帶甜味","They strengthen agave's herbal, peppery notes":"加強龍舌蘭的草本、胡椒氣息","Less agave sugar means less agave aroma; the best spirits use agave sugars only.":"龍舌蘭的糖越少，龍舌蘭的香氣越少；最好的烈酒只用龍舌蘭的糖。","The added sugar ferments into alcohol: no sweetness remains in the spirit. Smoke depends on pit roasting. Herbal notes come from agave, so they decrease rather than increase.":"添加的糖會發酵成酒精：烈酒中不會留下甜味。煙燻味取決於窯坑烘烤。草本氣息來自龍舌蘭，所以是減少而不是增加。","What does \"mixto\" mean for Tequila?":"對 Tequila 來說，「mixto」是什麼意思？","An informal, non-legal name for Tequila with under 100% agave":"對非 100% agave 的 Tequila 的非正式、非法定稱呼","A legal category that must appear on the label":"必須標在酒標上的法定類別","A Tequila made from several agave species":"用數種龍舌蘭做的 Tequila","A blend of Tequila and Mezcal":"Tequila 和 Mezcal 的調和","\"Mixto\" informally means a Tequila with up to 49% non-agave sugars, but it is not a labelling term.":"「Mixto」非正式地指含有最多 49% 非龍舌蘭糖的 Tequila，但它不是標示術語。","On the label these simply say \"Tequila\", without \"100% agave\". Tequila allows only blue agave, so it cannot mix species, and there is no legal Tequila-Mezcal blend.":"這些酒在酒標上只寫「Tequila」，沒有「100% agave」。Tequila 只允許藍色龍舌蘭，所以不能混合品種，也沒有合法的 Tequila 與 Mezcal 調和。","How do the stills used for Tequila and Mezcal usually differ?":"Tequila 和 Mezcal 使用的蒸餾器通常有什麼不同？","Tequila: large and modern; Mezcal: small, often home-made":"Tequila：大型而現代；Mezcal：小型，常是自製的","Tequila uses only columns, Mezcal only pot stills":"Tequila 只用蒸餾柱，Mezcal 只用壺式蒸餾器","Tequila in direct-fired clay, Mezcal in steam-heated steel":"Tequila 用直火陶製蒸餾器，Mezcal 用蒸汽加熱的鋼製蒸餾器","No difference: the law requires the same still":"沒有不同：法律規定用相同的蒸餾器","Tequila producers usually use large modern pot stills; Mezcal producers, small and often home-made ones.":"Tequila 的生產者通常使用大型的現代壺式蒸餾器；Mezcal 的生產者使用小型、常是自製的蒸餾器。","Both may use pot or column stills, and the best are usually double-distilled in pots. Direct-fired clay is required for Ancestral Mezcal, not Tequila.":"兩者都可以使用壺式或柱式蒸餾器，最好的通常在壺式蒸餾器中蒸餾兩次。直火陶製蒸餾器是 Ancestral Mezcal 的要求，不是 Tequila 的。","At what strength are some new agave spirits collected?":"有些龍舌蘭新酒在什麼濃度收集？","Even below 60% abv":"甚至低於 60% abv","Always above 95% abv":"一律高於 95% abv","Exactly 40% abv, ready to bottle":"剛好 40% abv，可直接裝瓶","Around 90% abv, like rum light marks":"90% abv 左右，像蘭姆酒的輕盈型 mark","Some agave spirits come off at very low strengths; below 60% abv is not unusual.":"有些龍舌蘭烈酒流出時濃度非常低；低於 60% abv 並不罕見。","A low strength keeps more congeners, so more agave character. 95% abv would give an almost neutral spirit, like vodka's. 40% is a bottling strength, reached by adding water.":"低濃度保留更多同屬物，所以龍舌蘭的特色更多。95% abv 會做出近乎中性的烈酒，像伏特加那樣。40% 是裝瓶濃度，是加水達到的。","Where are most agave spirits kept after distillation?":"大多數龍舌蘭烈酒蒸餾後存放在哪裡？","In inert vessels or briefly in very large oak vats":"在惰性容器中，或短暫存放在非常大的橡木槽中","In small new oak casks for many years":"在小型新橡木桶中存放多年","In buried clay jars":"在埋入地下的陶罐中","In ex-Cognac casks for at least five years":"在 Cognac 桶中至少五年","The aim is to keep agave aromas, so inert vessels or large vats are preferred.":"目標是保留龍舌蘭香氣，所以偏好惰性容器或大型木槽。","Small new casks and long ageing would mask the agave, which is why they are rare. Clay jars and ex-Cognac casks are not the usual practice for these spirits.":"小型新桶和長期陳年會掩蓋龍舌蘭，所以很少見。陶罐和 Cognac 桶不是這些烈酒的常見做法。","What does a short spell in a very large oak vat give a Tequila?":"在非常大的橡木槽中短暫存放，會帶給 Tequila 什麼？","Little oak flavour, but more smoothness and complexity":"很少的橡木風味，但更多柔順感和複雜度","Lots of vanilla and a deep amber colour":"大量香草和深琥珀色","An intense smoky aroma, typical of Mezcal":"濃郁的煙燻香氣，是 Mezcal 的典型特徵","The right to label it \"Extra Añejo\"":"標示為「Extra Añejo」的資格","Big vats give very little oak flavour, but the short rest adds smoothness and complexity.":"大型木槽給的橡木風味非常少，但短暫靜置能增添柔順感和複雜度。","Lots of vanilla and a deep colour would need small casks and time. Smoke depends on pit roasting. Extra Añejo needs at least three years in barrels, not large vats.":"大量香草和深色需要小桶和時間。煙燻味取決於窯坑烘烤。Extra Añejo 需要在桶中至少三年，不是大型木槽。","A bottle says \"Tequila Blanco\" (or Silver). What does it say about ageing?":"一瓶酒寫著「Tequila Blanco」（或 Silver）。關於陳年，這告訴你什麼？","No ageing requirement":"沒有陳年要求","At least two months in oak":"在橡木中至少兩個月","At least a year in oak, then filtered":"在橡木中至少一年，再過濾","Coloured and softened with abocado":"用 abocado 上色並柔化","Blanco/Silver is the category with no ageing requirement.":"Blanco/Silver 是沒有陳年要求的類別。","Two months is Reposado, one year is Añejo. Abocado is used for Gold Tequila, not Blanco.":"兩個月是 Reposado，一年是 Añejo。Abocado 用於 Gold Tequila，不是 Blanco。","What is the minimum requirement for a Tequila Añejo?":"Tequila Añejo 的最低要求是什麼？","One year in oak barrels":"在橡木桶中一年","Two months in large oak vats":"在大型橡木槽中兩個月","Three years in oak barrels":"在橡木桶中三年","Six months in any vessel, even an inert one":"在任何容器中六個月，即使是惰性容器","Añejo needs at least one year in oak barrels.":"Añejo 需要在橡木桶中至少一年。","Two months is Reposado, three years is Extra Añejo. An inert vessel does not count as ageing: Añejo needs barrels.":"兩個月是 Reposado，三年是 Extra Añejo。惰性容器不算陳年：Añejo 需要桶。","Which Tequila categories must be matured in oak barrels, not just large vats?":"哪些 Tequila 類別必須在橡木桶中熟成，而不只是大型木槽？","Añejo and Extra Añejo":"Añejo 和 Extra Añejo","Blanco and Reposado":"Blanco 和 Reposado","Gold only":"只有 Gold","Every 100% agave Tequila, whatever its category":"所有 100% agave 的 Tequila，不論類別","Añejo and Extra Añejo require barrels; Reposado usually rests in very large vats.":"Añejo 和 Extra Añejo 要求用桶；Reposado 通常在非常大的木槽中靜置。","Blanco has no ageing requirement and Gold is not aged at all: its colour comes from abocado. \"100% agave\" is about sugars, not wood.":"Blanco 沒有陳年要求，Gold 則完全不陳年：它的顏色來自 abocado。「100% agave」說的是糖，不是木頭。","Besides colour, what does abocado aim to give a Gold Tequila?":"除了顏色，abocado 還想帶給 Gold Tequila 什麼？","A smoothness that mimics maturation":"模仿熟成的柔順感","A smoky roasted-agave aroma":"烘烤龍舌蘭的煙燻香氣","A higher alcoholic strength":"更高的酒精濃度","The right to say \"100% agave\"":"標示「100% agave」的資格","Abocado contains ingredients that create a smoothness meant to resemble ageing.":"Abocado 含有能創造柔順感的材料，目的是讓它像經過陳年。","Gold is not aged at all: abocado is there precisely to imitate it. It adds neither smoke nor alcohol, and \"100% agave\" depends only on the origin of the sugars.":"Gold 完全沒有陳年：abocado 正是用來模仿陳年的。它不增添煙燻味或酒精，而「100% agave」只取決於糖的來源。","Which list runs from shortest to longest minimum oak ageing?":"哪一組是依最低橡木陳年時間由短到長排列？","\"Reposado\" means rested and comes before \"Añejo\", meaning aged. Gold has no oak requirement because it is not aged: its colour is added.":"「Reposado」的意思是靜置過的，排在意思是陳年的「Añejo」之前。Gold 沒有橡木要求，因為它沒有陳年：顏色是添加的。","A label reads \"Tequila Reposado – 100% agave\". What does it tell you?":"酒標上寫著「Tequila Reposado – 100% agave」。這告訴你什麼？","Only agave sugars and at least two months in oak":"只用龍舌蘭的糖，並在橡木中至少兩個月","At least 51% agave and one year in barrel":"至少 51% 龍舌蘭，並在桶中一年","Only agave, with colour from abocado":"只用龍舌蘭，顏色來自 abocado","Several agave species, pit-roasted and distilled in clay":"數種龍舌蘭，窯坑烘烤並用陶製蒸餾器蒸餾","\"100% agave\" means all sugars came from agave; \"Reposado\", at least two months in oak.":"「100% agave」表示所有的糖都來自龍舌蘭；「Reposado」表示在橡木中至少兩個月。","51% applies to Tequila without \"100% agave\", and a year in barrel is Añejo. Abocado belongs to Gold. Several species, pits and clay describe traditional Mezcal, not Tequila.":"51% 適用於沒有「100% agave」的 Tequila，在桶中一年是 Añejo。Abocado 屬於 Gold。數個品種、窯坑和陶器描述的是傳統的 Mezcal，不是 Tequila。","In how many Mexican states may agave for Tequila be grown?":"Tequila 的龍舌蘭可以種在墨西哥的幾個州？","Only one, Jalisco":"只有一個，哈利斯科州","Every state in Mexico":"墨西哥的每一個州","Two: Jalisco and Oaxaca":"兩個：哈利斯科州和瓦哈卡州","Blue agave for Tequila may grow in five states, the most important being Jalisco.":"Tequila 的藍色龍舌蘭可以種在五個州，最重要的是哈利斯科州。","Jalisco is Tequila's heartland but not the only state allowed. Oaxaca is the centre of Mezcal, not Tequila. Tequila cannot come from any state: it is a geographical indication.":"哈利斯科州是 Tequila 的核心地帶，但不是唯一獲准的州。瓦哈卡州是 Mezcal 的中心，不是 Tequila 的。Tequila 不能來自任何一州：它是地理標示。","How long does blue agave typically take to mature?":"藍色龍舌蘭通常要多久才成熟？","7 to 10 years":"7 到 10 年","One year":"一年","30 to 40 years":"30 到 40 年","Blue agave usually needs seven to ten years.":"藍色龍舌蘭通常需要七到十年。","15–20 years applies to some slower agave species. One year is a cereal timescale, not that of a long-lived plant like agave.":"15–20 年適用於某些較慢的龍舌蘭品種。一年是穀物的時間尺度，不是龍舌蘭這種長壽植物的。","What is the botanical name of the only agave allowed for Tequila?":"Tequila 唯一允許使用的龍舌蘭，學名是什麼？","It is Agave tequilana Weber, variety azul: blue agave.":"它是 Agave tequilana Weber 的 azul 變種：藍色龍舌蘭。","Only blue agave, Agave tequilana Weber var. azul, is allowed for Tequila. Agave angustifolia (espadín) is Mezcal's main variety; salmiana and potatorum are other agaves used for some mezcals, not for Tequila.":"Tequila 只允許使用藍色龍舌蘭，也就是 Agave tequilana Weber var. azul。Agave angustifolia（espadín）是 Mezcal 的主要品種；salmiana 和 potatorum 是用於某些 mezcal 的其他龍舌蘭，不用於 Tequila。","How do the Tequila and Mezcal industries generally compare?":"Tequila 和 Mezcal 這兩個產業整體上相比如何？","Tequila: big brands at large scale; Mezcal: mostly small producers":"Tequila：大品牌、大規模；Mezcal：大多是小生產者","Tequila: mostly small producers; Mezcal: big brands":"Tequila：大多是小生產者；Mezcal：大品牌","Both are dominated by state cooperatives":"兩者都由國營合作社主導","They are one industry with the same rules and scale":"它們是同一個產業，規定和規模都相同","Tequila is dominated by big brands; Mezcal is still mostly small-scale.":"Tequila 由大品牌主導；Mezcal 仍然大多是小規模的。","Tequila is also the largest agave spirit by volume. They are two separate geographical indications, with different rules on species, cooking and stills.":"Tequila 也是產量最大的龍舌蘭烈酒。它們是兩個各自獨立的地理標示，在品種、烹煮和蒸餾器上有不同的規定。","On a label, what can the word \"Mezcal\" refer to?":"在酒標上，「Mezcal」這個字可以指什麼？","Only the Mezcal geographical indication":"只指 Mezcal 這個地理標示","Any agave spirit made in Mexico":"墨西哥製作的任何龍舌蘭烈酒","Any agave spirit worldwide, even outside Mexico":"全世界任何龍舌蘭烈酒，即使在墨西哥以外","Only a smoky Tequila":"只指帶煙燻味的 Tequila","Broadly \"mezcal\" covers all Mexican agave spirits, but on a label it refers only to the geographical indication.":"廣義的「mezcal」涵蓋所有墨西哥的龍舌蘭烈酒，但在酒標上它只指那個地理標示。","That is why the term is confusing: the everyday meaning is wider than the legal one. Tequila and Mezcal are two separate GIs, and Tequila is not a smoky version of Mezcal.":"所以這個術語容易讓人混淆：日常的意思比法律上的寬。Tequila 和 Mezcal 是兩個獨立的地理標示，Tequila 也不是 Mezcal 的煙燻版。","Which agave species may a Mezcal producer use?":"Mezcal 的生產者可以使用哪些龍舌蘭品種？","Several species, and under the 2016 law any species":"數個品種，依 2016 年的法律則是任何品種","Only blue agave, as for Tequila":"只有藍色龍舌蘭，和 Tequila 一樣","Only espadín, by law":"依法只有 espadín","Only wild species, never cultivated ones":"只有野生品種，絕不用栽培的","Unlike Tequila, Mezcal allows several species; the new law opens it to all.":"與 Tequila 不同，Mezcal 允許數個品種；新法則開放給所有品種。","Espadín is the most used, especially in Oaxaca, but it is not compulsory. Blue agave alone is the Tequila rule. No rule requires wild agaves.":"Espadín 用得最多，尤其在瓦哈卡州，但不是強制的。只用藍色龍舌蘭是 Tequila 的規定。沒有規定要求使用野生龍舌蘭。","How does traditional pit cooking for Mezcal usually work?":"Mezcal 傳統的窯坑烹煮通常怎麼進行？","Fire-heated stones, then piñas covered in earth":"用火把石頭加熱，再把 piña 用土蓋起來","Piñas are boiled in large water tanks":"把 piña 放在大水槽中煮","Piñas are steamed in brick ovens":"把 piña 放在磚爐中蒸煮","Piñas are left in the sun for weeks":"把 piña 放在太陽下幾個星期","A fire heats the stones, then the piñas are covered with earth and cook in the stored heat.":"先用火把石頭加熱，再把 piña 用土蓋住，靠蓄積的熱烹煮。","Steam in brick ovens is Tequila's traditional method and adds no smoke. Neither boiling nor sun-drying is a method used for agave.":"在磚爐中用蒸汽是 Tequila 的傳統做法，不會增添煙燻味。水煮和日曬都不是處理龍舌蘭的方法。","Why does traditional Tequila usually lack smoky aromas?":"為什麼傳統的 Tequila 通常沒有煙燻香氣？","Its piñas are steamed, which adds no flavour":"它的 piña 是蒸煮的，不會增添風味","Smoke is removed with activated charcoal":"煙燻味被活性碳去除","Blue agave cannot absorb smoke":"藍色龍舌蘭無法吸收煙","Smoke disappears during double pot distillation":"煙燻味在壺式二次蒸餾中消失","Smoke comes from pit roasting; Tequila's steam cooking adds none.":"煙燻味來自窯坑烘烤；Tequila 的蒸汽烹煮不會增添。","Smoke is a handy clue for telling Mezcal from Tequila. Double pot distillation keeps character rather than erasing it, and any agave roasted in a pit would pick up smoke.":"煙燻味是分辨 Mezcal 和 Tequila 的好線索。壺式二次蒸餾是保留特色，而不是抹去；任何龍舌蘭在窯坑中烘烤都會沾上煙燻味。","Which is NOT one of the three factors behind the best Mezcal's smoky, earthy, vegetal character?":"最好的 Mezcal 有煙燻、土壤和植物特色，下列哪一項不是背後的三個因素之一？","Long ageing in new casks":"在新桶中長期陳年","Roasting the piñas in pits":"在窯坑中烘烤 piña","Agave fibres in the fermentation":"發酵時帶著龍舌蘭纖維","Distilling to a low strength in simple pot stills":"在簡單的壺式蒸餾器中蒸餾到低濃度","Pit roasting, fibres in fermentation and low-strength distillation in simple pots: oak is not one of the three.":"窯坑烘烤、發酵時帶纖維，以及在簡單的壺式蒸餾器中低濃度蒸餾：橡木不在這三項之中。","A long spell in new casks would mask the very agave aromas these three factors build. That is why long ageing is rare for agave spirits.":"在新桶中長時間存放，會掩蓋這三個因素所建立的龍舌蘭香氣。所以龍舌蘭烈酒很少長期陳年。","A Tequila has a warming texture and pronounced agave character. Which production choices explain it?":"一款 Tequila 有溫熱的口感和明顯的龍舌蘭特色。哪些生產選擇可以解釋這一點？","Slow brick-oven cooking, fibres, low-strength double distillation":"磚爐慢煮、帶纖維、低濃度的二次蒸餾","Pressure ovens, high-strength column and charcoal filtering":"加壓爐、高濃度蒸餾柱和木炭過濾","Added non-agave sugars and abocado":"添加非龍舌蘭的糖和 abocado","Long ageing in small new charred oak barrels":"在炙燒過的小型新橡木桶中長期陳年","The best Tequilas combine slow cooking, fibres in fermentation, double pot distillation and collection at low strength.":"最好的 Tequila 結合了慢煮、發酵時帶纖維、壺式二次蒸餾，以及在低濃度收集。","A high-strength column and charcoal would strip character. Added sugars dilute the agave, and long ageing in new casks would bury it under oak.":"高濃度蒸餾柱和木炭會去除特色。添加的糖會稀釋龍舌蘭，在新桶中長期陳年則會讓它被橡木蓋住。","Which cooking method is allowed for Artisanal Mezcal but NOT for Ancestral?":"哪一種烹煮方式 Artisanal Mezcal 允許、Ancestral 卻不允許？","Brick ovens":"磚爐","Stone-lined pits":"石砌窯坑","Pressurised steam ovens":"加壓蒸汽爐","Copper pots over a wood fire":"柴火上的銅鍋","Artisanal allows pits and brick ovens; Ancestral allows pits only.":"Artisanal 允許窯坑和磚爐；Ancestral 只允許窯坑。","Pits are allowed in both categories. Pressure ovens are only permitted for plain \"Mezcal\". Copper pots are not a listed cooking method.":"兩個類別都允許窯坑。加壓爐只允許用於一般的「Mezcal」。銅鍋不是列出的烹煮方式。","For Artisanal Mezcal, where must fermentation take place?":"Artisanal Mezcal 的發酵必須在哪裡進行？","In stone pits, wood or clay, with fibres":"在石坑、木製或陶製容器中，並帶纖維","Only in temperature-controlled steel tanks":"只能在控溫的鋼槽中","In new oak barrels, without fibres":"在新橡木桶中，不帶纖維","Anywhere, as long as selected yeast is used":"哪裡都可以，只要使用選育酵母","Artisanal rules call for stone pits, wood or clay vessels, with agave fibres.":"Artisanal 的規定要求使用石坑、木製或陶製容器，並帶龍舌蘭纖維。","Steel is only allowed for plain \"Mezcal\", which has no vessel limits. Fibres are encouraged, not excluded, and yeast choice is not a category criterion.":"鋼只允許用於一般的「Mezcal」，它沒有容器限制。纖維是受鼓勵的，不是被排除的，而酵母的選擇不是分類的標準。","Why were the three Mezcal categories (Mezcal, Artisanal, Ancestral) created?":"為什麼要設立 Mezcal 的三個類別（Mezcal、Artisanal、Ancestral）？","To recognise and identify traditional methods":"承認並標明傳統做法","To show how long the Mezcal spent in cask":"表示 Mezcal 在桶中存放了多久","To show which state the Mezcal comes from":"表示 Mezcal 來自哪一州","To separate blue agave Mezcal from other species":"把藍色龍舌蘭的 Mezcal 與其他品種區分開來","The old law did not protect traditional practice; the categories help consumers spot traditional producers.":"舊法沒有保護傳統做法；這些類別幫助消費者認出傳統的生產者。","Ageing is shown by terms such as Reposado and Añejo, not by these categories. They concern cooking, crushing, fermenting and distilling methods, not origin or species.":"陳年是用 Reposado 和 Añejo 這類術語表示的，不是這些類別。它們關乎烹煮、壓碎、發酵和蒸餾的方法，不是產地或品種。","Which pair of age terms applies to Mezcal?":"哪一組年數術語適用於 Mezcal？","Reposado: 2 months in oak; Añejo: 1 year in barrels":"Reposado：橡木中 2 個月；Añejo：桶中 1 年","Reposado: 1 year; Añejo: 5 years":"Reposado：1 年；Añejo：5 年","Joven: 3 years; Ancestral: 10 years in oak barrels":"Joven：3 年；Ancestral：橡木桶中 10 年","Mezcal has no age terms":"Mezcal 沒有年數術語","As for Tequila: Reposado at least two months in oak, Añejo at least one year in barrels.":"和 Tequila 一樣：Reposado 在橡木中至少兩個月，Añejo 在桶中至少一年。","\"Joven\" means unaged Mezcal and the new law replaces it with \"Blanco\". \"Ancestral\" is about production methods, not age.":"「Joven」指未陳年的 Mezcal，新法以「Blanco」取代它。「Ancestral」說的是生產方法，不是年數。","What raw materials can vodka be made from?":"伏特加可以用什麼原料製成？","In theory, anything of agricultural origin":"理論上，任何農業來源的東西","Only grains, by law throughout the world":"只有穀物，全世界的法律都這樣規定","Only potatoes grown in Eastern Europe":"只有東歐種植的馬鈴薯","Only grains or potatoes, never any other raw material":"只有穀物或馬鈴薯，絕不用其他原料","Vodka can come from any agricultural material, although in practice the choice is narrow.":"伏特加可以來自任何農業原料，雖然實際上的選擇很窄。","Cost and consumer expectations steer most distillers towards grains and potatoes, but that is not a rule: in recent years grapes have also been used, for example. That is why the \"only grains\" and \"only grains or potatoes\" options are too restrictive.":"成本和消費者的期待讓大多數蒸餾師選擇穀物和馬鈴薯，但這不是規定：例如近年來也有人使用葡萄。所以「只有穀物」和「只有穀物或馬鈴薯」的選項都太狹隘。","In which country are potatoes a traditional raw material for vodka?":"在哪一個國家，馬鈴薯是伏特加的傳統原料？","Poland":"波蘭","In Poland, potatoes are a traditional base for vodka.":"在波蘭，馬鈴薯是伏特加的傳統原料。","Poland is one of vodka's historic homes, alongside Russia, Finland and Sweden. Mexico is home to agave spirits, Brazil to cachaça and Scotland to malt whisky; none of them is linked to potato vodka.":"波蘭是伏特加的歷史故鄉之一，另外還有俄羅斯、芬蘭和瑞典。墨西哥是龍舌蘭烈酒的故鄉，巴西是 cachaça 的，蘇格蘭是麥芽威士忌的；它們都與馬鈴薯伏特加無關。","How is grain starch for vodka usually converted today?":"現今伏特加用的穀物澱粉通常怎麼轉化？","With bought-in enzymes added to cooked grain":"在煮過的穀物中加入外購的酵素","By roasting the grain in stone-lined pits":"在鋪石的窯坑中烘烤穀物","By distilling the grain directly without fermenting it":"不經發酵，直接蒸餾穀物","By adding cane molasses to kick-start the yeast":"加入甘蔗糖蜜來啟動酵母","Many distillers buy commercial enzymes and add them to crushed grain cooked in water.":"許多蒸餾師購買商業酵素，加進在水中煮過的碎穀物裡。","Malted barley can still be used as a source of enzymes, but bought-in enzymes are now very common. Pit roasting belongs to Mezcal. Without fermentation there is no alcohol to distil, and molasses belongs to the world of rum.":"麥芽大麥仍然可以作為酵素的來源，但外購酵素現在非常普遍。窯坑烘烤屬於 Mezcal。沒有發酵就沒有酒精可以蒸餾，糖蜜則屬於蘭姆酒的世界。","Why are potatoes cooked in water before enzymes are added?":"為什麼馬鈴薯要先在水中烹煮再加酵素？","To make the starch soluble":"讓澱粉變得可溶","To remove the skins, which would taste bitter":"去除會帶苦味的皮","To caramelise the sugars and colour the vodka":"讓糖焦糖化並為伏特加上色","To turn the starch straight into alcohol":"把澱粉直接變成酒精","Cooking dissolves the starch so that enzymes can convert it into sugar.":"烹煮讓澱粉溶解，酵素才能把它轉化為糖。","It is a two-stage process: by the end of cooking the potatoes have broken down into a cloudy, starch-laden liquid, then enzymes do the conversion. Alcohol only appears once yeast ferments the sugar, and the vodka stays colourless.":"這是兩階段的過程：烹煮結束時馬鈴薯已分解成混濁、充滿澱粉的液體，接著由酵素進行轉化。酒精要等酵母發酵糖之後才出現，而伏特加始終是無色的。","Which type of still is essential to make the neutral spirit for vodka?":"製作伏特加用的中性烈酒，哪一種蒸餾器不可或缺？","A column still with many plates":"蒸餾板很多的柱式蒸餾器","A direct-fired copper pot still":"直火加熱的銅製壺式蒸餾器","A small clay still":"小型陶製蒸餾器","Two pot stills in a row":"兩座串聯的壺式蒸餾器","Only a column still with enough plates can reach 95-96% abv.":"只有蒸餾板夠多的柱式蒸餾器才能達到 95–96% abv。","Each plate in the column concentrates the ethanol a little more, and at that strength very few congeners remain. A pot still, even used twice, cannot reach those levels. Small clay stills are typical of Ancestral Mezcal.":"蒸餾柱中的每一層蒸餾板都把乙醇再濃縮一點，在那個濃度下留下的同屬物極少。壺式蒸餾器即使用兩次也達不到這種水準。小型陶製蒸餾器是 Ancestral Mezcal 的典型設備。","Which pair correctly gives the minimum strength of a neutral spirit?":"哪一組正確列出中性烈酒的最低濃度？","USA 95% abv, EU 96% abv":"美國 95% abv，歐盟 96% abv","USA 96% abv, EU 95% abv":"美國 96% abv，歐盟 95% abv","USA 90% abv, EU 92% abv":"美國 90% abv，歐盟 92% abv","USA 80% abv, EU 85% abv":"美國 80% abv，歐盟 85% abv","Neutral spirit needs at least 95% abv in the USA and 96% in the EU.":"中性烈酒在美國至少要 95% abv，在歐盟至少 96%。","Watch out for the swap, the most common trap: the EU threshold is the higher one. Around 90% abv a spirit still has a light aroma, like light rum marks or Scotch grain whisky, but it is not yet neutral.":"小心對調，這是最常見的陷阱：歐盟的門檻較高。90% abv 左右的烈酒仍有清淡的香氣，像蘭姆酒的輕盈型 mark 或 Scotch 穀物威士忌，還不算中性。","A small distiller makes low wines in a pot still and finishes in a column. What is the effect on the final flavour?":"一位小型蒸餾師用壺式蒸餾器做低度酒，再用蒸餾柱完成。對最終風味有什麼影響？","No real effect":"沒有實質影響","A far more aromatic vodka, close to a brandy":"伏特加香氣濃郁得多，接近白蘭地","A rougher vodka that always needs charcoal filtering":"伏特加較粗糙，一定需要木炭過濾","A spirit that legally cannot be called vodka":"在法律上不能稱為伏特加的烈酒","Using a pot still only for the first stage does not change the vodka's final flavour.":"只在第一階段使用壺式蒸餾器，不會改變伏特加的最終風味。","The second distillation in the column still brings the spirit up to neutral strength, erasing any pot still imprint. Small producers working in batches sometimes use this method. It neither makes the vodka more aromatic nor excludes it from the category.":"第二次在柱式蒸餾器中的蒸餾把烈酒提高到中性的濃度，抹去了壺式蒸餾器的任何印記。以批次運作的小生產者有時使用這種方法。它既不會讓伏特加更有香氣，也不會讓它被排除在這個類別之外。","A producer buys in neutral spirit, but simply diluted it feels a little rough. What is often done to make it silkier?":"一位生產者買進中性烈酒，但只是稀釋後口感有點粗糙。常用什麼做法讓它更絲滑？","Redistils it, diluted, in a hybrid still":"稀釋後用混合式蒸餾器再蒸餾","Ages it for a year in new toasted oak barrels":"在烘烤過的新橡木桶中陳年一年","Adds molasses to round out the taste":"加入糖蜜讓味道更圓潤","Bottles it at a much higher strength, above 60% abv":"以高得多的濃度裝瓶，60% abv 以上","Running the diluted spirit through a pot linked to a rectifying column improves its texture.":"讓稀釋過的烈酒通過連接精餾柱的壺身，能改善它的質地。","Although it may be described as a pot still, it is really a hybrid still: in effect, another column distillation that purifies the spirit further. Oak would add colour and flavour, molasses makes no sense after distillation, and a higher strength would not make the vodka smoother.":"雖然它可能被稱為壺式蒸餾器，但其實是混合式蒸餾器：實際上是又一次蒸餾柱蒸餾，讓烈酒更純淨。橡木會增添顏色和風味，蒸餾後加糖蜜毫無道理，更高的濃度也不會讓伏特加更柔順。","What is activated charcoal filtration used for in vodka production?":"在伏特加的生產中，活性碳過濾的用途是什麼？","To remove remaining unwanted congeners":"去除剩餘的、不想要的同屬物","To give the vodka a light smoky, toasted aroma":"為伏特加帶來淡淡的煙燻、烘烤香氣","To raise the strength before bottling":"在裝瓶前提高濃度","To convert leftover starch into fermentable sugar":"把殘留的澱粉轉化為可發酵的糖","Activated charcoal traps leftover congeners and makes vodka purer.":"活性碳會抓住殘留的同屬物，讓伏特加更純淨。","It is one of two techniques, along with additives, that some producers use after distillation; others rely on distillation alone. Charcoal adds no flavour, does not change strength and is used after distillation, long after starch is relevant.":"它和添加物是部分生產者在蒸餾後使用的兩種技術；其他生產者只靠蒸餾。木炭不增添風味、不改變濃度，而且是在蒸餾後使用，那時早已與澱粉無關。","Why do some vodka producers use additives?":"為什麼有些伏特加生產者使用添加物？","To create the desired texture":"創造想要的質地","So they can claim a geographical origin on the label":"這樣就能在酒標上宣稱地理來源","To start a second fermentation in the bottle":"啟動瓶中二次發酵","To colour the vodka like an aged spirit":"把伏特加染成陳年烈酒的顏色","Additives are mainly used to build the desired texture, sometimes with a very faint aroma.":"添加物主要用來塑造想要的質地，有時帶有非常淡的香氣。","They are bought from specialist suppliers and can be tailored to a single brand. They have nothing to do with origin, do not trigger fermentation, and unflavoured vodka stays colourless.":"它們向專業供應商購買，可以為單一品牌量身訂製。它們與產地無關，不會引發發酵，而未調味的伏特加始終是無色的。","Why is water quality so critical in vodka?":"為什麼水質對伏特加這麼關鍵？","Nearly 60% of the bottle is added water":"瓶中將近 60% 是加入的水","The water is distilled together with the fermented grain":"水與發酵的穀物一起蒸餾","The law requires Nordic spring water only":"法律規定只能用北歐的泉水","Hard water raises the final alcoholic strength":"硬水會提高最終的酒精濃度","In a 40% abv vodka, nearly 60% of the contents is water added after distillation.":"在 40% abv 的伏特加中，將近 60% 的內容物是蒸餾後加入的水。","Vodka is all about neutral aromas and delicate texture, and even small impurities in the water could spoil them. No law requires water from any specific region, and water hardness does not change the strength.":"伏特加講究的就是中性的香氣和細緻的質地，水中即使有微量雜質也可能破壞它們。沒有法律規定要用特定地區的水，水的硬度也不會改變濃度。","Which description fits a neutral-style vodka?":"哪一項描述符合中性風格的伏特加？","Minimal flavour; smooth, light and dry":"風味極淡；柔順、輕盈且不甜","Completely free of any taste or texture":"完全沒有任何味道或質地","Full and mouth-filling, with marked toasted grain notes":"飽滿豐潤，帶明顯的烘烤穀物氣息","Slightly sweet, with a touch of oak vanilla":"略甜，帶一點橡木的香草味","The neutral style has the lightest possible flavour and is smooth, light and dry.":"中性風格的風味盡可能清淡，並且柔順、輕盈、不甜。","Neutral does not mean completely tasteless; a hint of flavour always remains. A full texture belongs to the characterful style, which still shows no marked notes. Oak vanilla is out of place, since vodka is kept in inert vessels.":"中性不代表完全沒有味道；總會留下一絲風味。飽滿的質地屬於有個性的風格，但它仍然沒有明顯的氣息。橡木的香草味並不合適，因為伏特加存放在惰性容器中。","What mainly sets a characterful vodka apart from a neutral one?":"有個性的伏特加與中性伏特加的主要差別是什麼？","A fuller, more mouth-filling texture":"質地更飽滿、更豐潤","Intense fruit aromas added after distillation":"蒸餾後添加的濃郁果香","A compulsory spell in used oak casks":"必須在舊橡木桶中存放一段時間","A distillation strength below 80% abv":"蒸餾濃度低於 80% abv","Characterful vodkas keep delicate flavours but have a fuller feel in the mouth.":"有個性的伏特加保有細緻的風味，但在口中的感覺更飽滿。","Their aromas stay light enough to be called neutral; the difference is in the texture. Intense fruity aromas point to flavouring, which is another category. Oak is not part of vodka, and below 80% abv you would not get a neutral spirit.":"它們的香氣仍然清淡到可以稱為中性；差別在於質地。濃郁的果香指向調味，那是另一個類別。橡木不屬於伏特加，而低於 80% abv 就得不到中性烈酒。","An unflavoured vodka shows clearly non-neutral aromas. What is most likely?":"一款未調味的伏特加表現出明顯非中性的香氣。最可能的情況是什麼？","The aromas were added after distillation":"這些香氣是蒸餾後添加的","It comes from Polish potatoes, which always give intense aromas":"它來自波蘭馬鈴薯，那總會帶來濃郁的香氣","It was distilled above 96% abv in a column":"它在蒸餾柱中蒸餾到 96% abv 以上","It was filtered several times through activated charcoal":"它用活性碳過濾了好幾次","If the aromas cannot be called neutral, they were most probably added after distillation.":"如果香氣不能稱為中性，最可能是蒸餾後添加的。","Even characterful vodkas stay neutral on the nose; the raw material alone cannot give obvious aromas. The higher the distillation strength and the more filtering, the fewer aromas remain, so those two options point the opposite way.":"即使是有個性的伏特加，聞起來也是中性的；光靠原料不可能帶來明顯的香氣。蒸餾濃度越高、過濾越多，留下的香氣越少，所以那兩個選項指向相反的方向。","Which group lists the countries historically linked to vodka?":"哪一組列出了歷史上與伏特加相關的國家？","Russia, Poland, Finland, Sweden":"俄羅斯、波蘭、芬蘭、瑞典","Russia, France, Ireland, Mexico":"俄羅斯、法國、愛爾蘭、墨西哥","Scotland, Japan, Canada, the USA":"蘇格蘭、日本、加拿大、美國","Poland, Brazil, Jamaica, Cuba":"波蘭、巴西、牙買加、古巴","Russia, Poland, Finland and Sweden are vodka's historic homelands.":"俄羅斯、波蘭、芬蘭和瑞典是伏特加的歷史故鄉。","They still make large volumes and many of the most highly regarded vodkas, although excellent examples are now found almost everywhere. The other groups mix in countries famous for whisky, Cognac, agave spirits or rum.":"它們至今仍生產大量伏特加，以及許多評價最高的酒款，不過如今幾乎到處都有出色的例子。其他幾組混入了以威士忌、Cognac、龍舌蘭烈酒或蘭姆酒聞名的國家。","What is the key to vodka's worldwide success?":"伏特加在全世界成功的關鍵是什麼？","Neutrality and versatility":"中性和百搭","Long ageing that makes it rich and complex":"讓它豐富複雜的長期陳年","Intense, recognisable aromas from the raw material":"來自原料、濃郁而可辨認的香氣","Identical production rules in every country":"每個國家都相同的生產規定","Neutrality lets vodka clash with nothing and mix easily.":"中性讓伏特加不與任何東西衝突，容易混搭。","Precisely because it does not impose its own taste, vodka works in simple mixed drinks and in cocktails alike. It is not aged, does not rely on intense raw-material aromas, and rules differ between countries, for example on the minimum strength of neutral spirit.":"正因為它不把自己的味道強加於人，伏特加在簡單的混合飲料和調酒中都好用。它不經陳年，不靠原料的濃郁香氣，各國的規定也不同，例如中性烈酒的最低濃度。","Which grains do Eastern European vodka distillers traditionally use?":"東歐的伏特加蒸餾師傳統上使用哪些穀物？","Barley, wheat and rye":"大麥、小麥和黑麥","Corn, rice and sorghum":"玉米、米和高粱","Oats, millet and buckwheat":"燕麥、小米和蕎麥","Corn only, as for bourbon":"只用玉米，和 bourbon 一樣","Grains are major crops in Eastern Europe, and vodka mainly uses barley, wheat and rye.":"穀物是東歐的主要作物，伏特加主要使用大麥、小麥和黑麥。","In theory any agricultural material works, but the Eastern tradition rests on these three grains. Corn is bourbon's key grain, not that of traditional vodka.":"理論上任何農業原料都可以，但東歐的傳統建立在這三種穀物上。玉米是 bourbon 的關鍵穀物，不是傳統伏特加的。","Besides bought-in enzymes, what traditional enzyme source can convert grain starch for vodka?":"除了外購酵素，還有哪一種傳統的酵素來源可以轉化伏特加用的穀物澱粉？","Cane juice":"甘蔗汁","Cooked agave fibres":"煮過的龍舌蘭纖維","Malted barley contains the enzymes that turn starch into sugar.":"麥芽大麥含有把澱粉轉化為糖的酵素。","Many distillers now prefer commercial enzymes, but malt remains an option. Cane juice already contains sugar, agave fibres add aroma and charcoal is for filtering.":"許多蒸餾師現在偏好商業酵素，但麥芽仍是一種選擇。甘蔗汁本來就含有糖，龍舌蘭纖維增添的是香氣，木炭則用於過濾。","If vodka can be made from any agricultural material, why is the real choice fairly narrow?":"既然伏特加可以用任何農業原料製作，為什麼實際的選擇相當窄？","Commercial pressures and consumer expectations":"商業壓力和消費者的期待","Because EU law only allows potatoes":"因為歐盟法律只允許馬鈴薯","Because other materials will not ferment":"因為其他原料無法發酵","Because only grain can give a spirit above 95% abv":"因為只有穀物能做出 95% abv 以上的烈酒","In theory anything goes, but cost and market expectations lead to a narrow range.":"理論上什麼都可以，但成本和市場期待讓選擇範圍變窄。","No law restricts vodka to potatoes. Any sugar ferments, and high strength depends on the column, not the raw material.":"沒有法律把伏特加限制在馬鈴薯。任何糖都能發酵，高濃度取決於蒸餾柱，不是原料。","Which \"unusual\" raw material has been a notable newcomer for vodka in recent years?":"近年來，哪一種「不尋常」的原料成為伏特加引人注目的新成員？","Hops":"啤酒花","Some producers use grapes to stand out; others simply look for the cheapest material.":"有些生產者用葡萄來與眾不同；也有人只是找最便宜的原料。","Blue agave is tied to Tequila and cane juice to rum. Hops flavour beer; they are not a sugar source.":"藍色龍舌蘭與 Tequila 綁在一起，甘蔗汁則是蘭姆酒。啤酒花為啤酒調味；它不是糖的來源。","Why might a producer choose a raw material other than grain or potatoes?":"為什麼生產者可能選擇穀物或馬鈴薯以外的原料？","To use the cheapest option or to stand out":"使用最便宜的選項，或是與眾不同","Because the law makes it change every year":"因為法律要求每年更換","To avoid using a column still":"避免使用柱式蒸餾器","To be allowed to age the vodka in cask":"這樣才能把伏特加桶陳","Alternative materials either cut costs or create a point of difference.":"替代原料不是降低成本，就是創造差異點。","Whatever the material, a column is still needed to reach 95–96% abv. No law forces a change, and vodka is kept in inert vessels.":"不論用什麼原料，仍然需要蒸餾柱才能達到 95–96% abv。沒有法律強制更換，伏特加也存放在惰性容器中。","What do the potatoes look like at the end of cooking in water, before enzymes go in?":"在水中烹煮結束、加入酵素之前，馬鈴薯是什麼樣子？","Broken down into a cloudy, starchy liquid":"分解成混濁、含澱粉的液體","Whole and firm, ready for milling":"完整而結實，可以拿去磨碎","Already fermented and alcoholic":"已經發酵並含有酒精","Turned into a clear, sweet syrup":"變成清澈的甜糖漿","Cooking dissolves the starch: the potatoes break down into a cloudy liquid.":"烹煮讓澱粉溶解：馬鈴薯分解成混濁的液體。","Sugar only appears afterwards, with the enzymes, so the liquid is not yet sweet or clear. Fermentation comes later still, when yeast is added.":"糖要等之後有了酵素才出現，所以液體還不甜，也不清澈。發酵還要更晚，加入酵母時才開始。","Why can't vodka's base spirit be made with a pot still alone?":"為什麼伏特加的基酒不能只用壺式蒸餾器製作？","It cannot reach the required 95–96% abv":"它達不到所需的 95–96% abv","Because the law bans copper for vodka":"因為法律禁止伏特加使用銅","Because it would burn the potatoes and grain while cooking":"因為它會在烹煮時把馬鈴薯和穀物燒焦","Because it would add too much colour":"因為它會增添太多顏色","Only a column with enough plates can produce spirit at 95–96% abv.":"只有蒸餾板夠多的蒸餾柱才能做出 95–96% abv 的烈酒。","A pot still can still be used for a first distillation, followed by a column. Distillation adds no colour, and cooking the raw material happens beforehand, not in the still.":"壺式蒸餾器仍然可以用於第一次蒸餾，之後再用蒸餾柱。蒸餾不會增添顏色，而原料的烹煮是事先進行的，不是在蒸餾器中。","What kind of process is vodka distillation usually?":"伏特加的蒸餾通常是哪一種製程？","Continuous":"連續式","Batch-based, in clay stills":"批次式，用陶製蒸餾器","A single pot still pass at low strength":"壺式蒸餾器低濃度蒸餾一次","Triple pot distillation, as required by law":"依法規定的壺式三次蒸餾","Vodka is normally distilled in columns, continuously.":"伏特加通常在蒸餾柱中連續蒸餾。","Some small distillers work in batches with a pot still before the column, but that is the exception. A single low-strength pass would give a characterful spirit, the opposite of vodka.":"有些小型蒸餾師在蒸餾柱之前先用壺式蒸餾器以批次運作，但那是例外。只做一次低濃度蒸餾會得到有個性的烈酒，與伏特加相反。","Which producers most often make low wines in a pot still, then finish in a column?":"哪些生產者最常用壺式蒸餾器做低度酒，再用蒸餾柱完成？","Small distillers working in batches":"以批次運作的小型蒸餾師","Large brands that buy in neutral spirit":"買進中性烈酒的大品牌","Flavoured vodka producers":"調味伏特加的生產者","Only Russian distillers, as a legal requirement":"只有俄羅斯的蒸餾師，因為是法律要求","This method is sometimes used by small distilleries producing in batches.":"這種方法有時為批次生產的小型蒸餾廠所用。","The method does not change the final flavour, so it is a practical choice, not a style one. Buyers of neutral spirit have no need to make low wines, and no national law requires the technique.":"這種方法不會改變最終的風味，所以是實務上的選擇，不是風格上的。買進中性烈酒的人不需要做低度酒，也沒有任何國家的法律要求這項技術。","When a vodka producer reruns diluted neutral spirit through a hybrid still, what is really happening?":"伏特加生產者把稀釋過的中性烈酒再通過混合式蒸餾器時，實際上發生了什麼事？","Another column distillation that purifies further":"又一次蒸餾柱蒸餾，進一步純化","A pot distillation that adds lots of congeners":"增添大量同屬物的壺式蒸餾","A quick ageing step that adds colour":"增添顏色的快速陳年步驟","A herb maceration, as for gin":"像琴酒一樣浸漬香草","The hybrid still is linked to a rectifying column: in effect it is another column distillation.":"混合式蒸餾器連接著精餾柱：實際上是又一次蒸餾柱蒸餾。","The result is a silkier texture, not extra congeners or colour. No herbs are added: unflavoured vodka stays neutral.":"結果是更絲滑的質地，不是更多的同屬物或顏色。沒有加入香草：未調味的伏特加保持中性。","Many vodka producers simply dilute their spirit. How do they justify it?":"許多伏特加生產者只是把烈酒稀釋。他們的理由是什麼？","Distillation alone gives the purity and smoothness":"光靠蒸餾就能得到純淨度和柔順感","Activated charcoal is banned in many producing countries":"許多生產國禁止使用活性碳","Additives make vodka cloudy":"添加物會讓伏特加變混濁","Dilution adds grain aromas":"稀釋會增添穀物香氣","These producers argue that distillation alone delivers the purity and texture they want.":"這些生產者主張，光靠蒸餾就能得到他們想要的純淨度和質地。","Charcoal and additives are legal and widely used by other producers. Dilution water must be very pure precisely so it adds no aroma.":"木炭和添加物是合法的，也為其他生產者廣泛使用。稀釋用的水必須非常純淨，正是為了不增添任何香氣。","Which statement about vodka additives is true?":"關於伏特加的添加物，下列哪一項正確？","They are bought from suppliers and tailored to each brand":"它們向供應商購買，並為各品牌量身訂製","They are banned in all quality vodkas":"所有優質伏特加都禁止使用","They are used to add an amber colour":"它們用來增添琥珀色","They are made by redistilling heads and tails":"它們是把酒頭和酒尾再蒸餾製成的","Additives come from specialist suppliers, are tailored to the brand and may even very lightly aromatise.":"添加物來自專業供應商，為品牌量身訂製，甚至可能帶來非常淡的香氣。","They are widespread in the industry, not banned. Their main purpose is texture, not colour: vodka stays colourless.":"它們在業界很普遍，並未被禁止。主要目的是質地，不是顏色：伏特加保持無色。","At what strength is most vodka sold?":"大多數伏特加以什麼濃度販售？","57.15% abv":"57.15% abv","96% abv":"96% abv","25% abv":"25% abv","Most vodka is bottled at 40% abv.":"大多數伏特加以 40% abv 裝瓶。","96% is the strength of neutral spirit off the column, before dilution. 57.15% is the old British \"100 proof\" of rum. 25% would be too low for a standard spirit.":"96% 是中性烈酒離開蒸餾柱、稀釋前的濃度。57.15% 是蘭姆酒舊的英國「100 proof」。25% 對標準烈酒來說太低。","What can dilution water with small impurities do to a vodka?":"稀釋用的水含有少量雜質，會對伏特加造成什麼影響？","Spoil its neutral aromas and delicate texture":"破壞它中性的香氣和細緻的質地","Give it an amber colour":"讓它帶琥珀色","Make it ferment again in the bottle":"讓它在瓶中再次發酵","Raise its strength above 40% abv":"把它的濃度提高到 40% abv 以上","In such a neutral spirit, even small water impurities can be noticed.":"在這麼中性的烈酒中，水中即使少量的雜質也會被察覺。","More than any other spirit, vodka cannot afford poor water. Water adds neither colour nor alcohol, and cannot restart fermentation.":"比起其他任何烈酒，伏特加更容不得水質不佳。水不增添顏色，也不增添酒精，更無法重新啟動發酵。","Is a neutral-style vodka completely flavourless?":"中性風格的伏特加完全沒有風味嗎？","No: it has the lightest possible flavour, but not none":"不是：風味盡可能清淡，但不是沒有","Yes: the law forbids any aroma":"是：法律禁止任何香氣","Yes: it is pure diluted ethanol, just like lab alcohol":"是：它是稀釋過的純乙醇，就像實驗室的酒精","No: it always tastes clearly of its raw material":"不是：它總是清楚地帶有原料的味道","The neutral style aims for the lightest possible flavour, smooth, light and dry, but not zero.":"中性風格追求盡可能清淡的風味，柔順、輕盈、不甜，但不是零。","No law bans aromas, and it is not lab alcohol: tiny traces remain. A clear raw-material taste is closer to the characterful style, which is still delicate.":"沒有法律禁止香氣，它也不是實驗室的酒精：仍留有微量的痕跡。清楚的原料味道比較接近有個性的風格，而它仍然是細緻的。","How do producers build a range of premium \"characterful\" vodkas?":"生產者如何建立一系列高級的「有個性」伏特加？","Delicate flavours plus a smooth, mouth-filling texture":"細緻的風味，加上柔順豐潤的質地","Strong fruit and spice flavours added after distillation":"蒸餾後添加強烈的水果和香料風味","Distilling to low strength in clay stills":"用陶製蒸餾器蒸餾到低濃度","Flavour stays neutral, but delicate nuances plus a fuller texture create subtle differences.":"風味保持中性，但細緻的差別加上更飽滿的質地，創造出微妙的差異。","Strong added flavours would make a flavoured vodka, not a characterful one. Vodka is not cask-aged and not distilled to low strength: columns are needed.":"添加強烈的風味會做出調味伏特加，不是有個性的伏特加。伏特加不桶陳，也不蒸餾到低濃度：需要蒸餾柱。","A vodka label makes a big feature of being filtered. What is worth noting?":"一張伏特加酒標大力強調經過過濾。有什麼值得注意？","It is true, but many other vodkas are filtered in the same way":"這是真的，但許多其他伏特加也以同樣方式過濾","Filtering vodka is illegal, so the label is lying":"過濾伏特加是違法的，所以酒標在說謊","It means the vodka was aged and then decoloured":"這表示伏特加經過陳年再脫色","It legally guarantees there are no additives":"它在法律上保證沒有添加物","The claim is true but not unique: charcoal filtering is very common.":"這項宣稱屬實，但並不獨特：木炭過濾非常普遍。","Labels may not lie, but need not say that everyone does the same. Filtering does not rule out additives and does not imply ageing.":"酒標不能說謊，但不必說明大家都這麼做。過濾不排除添加物，也不代表陳年。","Where is vodka kept after distillation?":"伏特加蒸餾後存放在哪裡？","In inert vessels":"在惰性容器中","In new oak casks":"在新橡木桶中","In ex-bourbon casks for at least two years":"在 bourbon 桶中至少兩年","In large oak vats, like Reposado Tequila":"在大型橡木槽中，像 Reposado Tequila 一樣","Vodka is not matured: it is kept in inert vessels to stay neutral.":"伏特加不經熟成：它存放在惰性容器中以保持中性。","Any wood would add colour and aromas, against vodka's style. Ex-bourbon casks and large vats belong to other spirits.":"任何木頭都會增添顏色和香氣，違背伏特加的風格。Bourbon 桶和大型木槽屬於其他烈酒。","Outside Russia, Poland, Finland and Sweden, what can be said about vodka?":"在俄羅斯、波蘭、芬蘭和瑞典之外，關於伏特加可以怎麼說？","It is made almost everywhere, including outstanding examples":"幾乎到處都有生產，包括傑出的酒款","It may not be called vodka":"不能稱為伏特加","It is always of lower quality":"品質一定較低","It is only made as flavoured vodka":"只做成調味伏特加","Vodka is made worldwide at every level, and nearly every producing country has outstanding examples.":"全世界都生產各種等級的伏特加，幾乎每個生產國都有傑出的例子。","The four historic countries remain important and are home to many respected brands, but they own neither the name nor quality. Unflavoured vodka is made everywhere.":"這四個歷史國家仍然重要，也是許多備受推崇的品牌的故鄉，但名稱和品質都不是它們獨有的。未調味的伏特加到處都有生產。","Why does vodka work so well in both long drinks and cocktails?":"為什麼伏特加在長飲和調酒中都這麼好用？","It does not clash with other flavours":"它不與其他風味衝突","Its strong grain aroma stands up to any mixer":"它強烈的穀物香氣能抗衡任何調和飲料","It is always sweetened, so already balanced":"它一律加糖，所以本身就平衡","It is stronger than every other spirit":"它比其他所有烈酒都烈","Its neutrality lets it support other ingredients without masking them.":"它的中性讓它能襯托其他材料而不掩蓋它們。","A strong grain aroma would be the opposite of neutrality. Vodka is not sweetened like a liqueur, and is usually 40% abv, like many other spirits.":"強烈的穀物香氣與中性恰恰相反。伏特加不像利口酒那樣加糖，而且通常是 40% abv，和許多其他烈酒一樣。","Where does vodka usually rank in sales around the world?":"伏特加在全世界的銷量通常排名如何？","It is the best-selling spirit, or close to it, almost everywhere":"幾乎在各地都是最暢銷或接近最暢銷的烈酒","It sells well only in Eastern Europe and Scandinavia":"只在東歐和斯堪地那維亞賣得好","It is a niche spirit kept mainly for cocktail bars":"它是主要留給調酒吧的小眾烈酒","It sells less than any other unaged white spirit":"它賣得比其他任何未陳年的白色烈酒都少","From its Eastern European home, vodka has become the best-selling spirit, or close to it, in most of the world.":"從東歐的故鄉出發，伏特加已在世界大部分地區成為最暢銷或接近最暢銷的烈酒。","Its success comes from neutrality and versatility: it does not clash with other flavours. So it is neither a niche product nor limited to its home countries. It is made almost everywhere, at every quality level.":"它的成功來自中性和百搭：它不與其他風味衝突。所以它既不是小眾產品，也不限於它的故鄉。它幾乎到處都有生產，各種品質等級都有。","The world's largest vodka brand is the best-known example of which style?":"全世界最大的伏特加品牌是哪一種風格最知名的例子？","The neutral style":"中性風格","The characterful style":"有個性的風格","Traditional Eastern European flavoured vodka":"傳統的東歐調味伏特加","Potato vodka finished in oak barrels":"在橡木桶中過桶的馬鈴薯伏特加","The neutral style, with the lightest possible flavour, is the style of the world's biggest-selling brand.":"中性風格，也就是風味盡可能清淡，是全世界最暢銷品牌的風格。","The characterful style aims for a little more flavour and a fuller texture and is typical of premium vodkas. Flavoured vodkas are a separate category. Vodka is kept in inert vessels, not oak.":"有個性的風格追求多一點風味和更飽滿的質地，是高級伏特加的典型。調味伏特加是另一個類別。伏特加存放在惰性容器中，不是橡木。","Besides creating the desired texture, what can some vodka additives also do?":"除了創造想要的質地，有些伏特加添加物還能做什麼？","Very lightly aromatise the spirit":"為烈酒帶來非常淡的香氣","Raise it above 40% abv without more distillation":"不必再蒸餾就把它提高到 40% abv 以上","Remove the need for a column still with many plates entirely":"完全不需要蒸餾板很多的柱式蒸餾器","Give it a golden colour similar to oak":"賦予它類似橡木的金黃色","Additives, tailored to each brand, shape texture and sometimes very lightly aromatise the vodka.":"添加物為各品牌量身訂製，塑造質地，有時也為伏特加帶來非常淡的香氣。","Strength depends on distillation and dilution, not on additives. No additive can replace the column, the only still able to reach 95–96% abv. An unflavoured vodka stays colourless, so a golden tint is not what these additives are for.":"濃度取決於蒸餾和稀釋，不是添加物。沒有任何添加物能取代蒸餾柱，那是唯一能達到 95–96% abv 的蒸餾器。未調味的伏特加保持無色，所以這些添加物不是用來帶出金黃色調的。","Does a distiller need a special still to make the neutral spirit for vodka?":"蒸餾師需要特殊的蒸餾器來製作伏特加用的中性烈酒嗎？","No, a standard column with enough plates will do":"不需要，蒸餾板夠多的標準蒸餾柱就行","Yes, only a vacuum still can reach 95–96%":"需要，只有真空蒸餾器能達到 95–96%","Yes, only a hybrid still can reach that strength":"需要，只有混合式蒸餾器能達到那個濃度","No, two runs in a traditional pot still are enough":"不需要，在傳統壺式蒸餾器中蒸餾兩次就夠了","An ordinary column, if it has enough plates, reaches the required 95–96% abv.":"普通的蒸餾柱只要蒸餾板夠多，就能達到所需的 95–96% abv。","A vacuum still captures delicate botanical aromas at low temperature; it is not about high strength. A hybrid still is an option some producers use to refine texture, not a requirement. A pot still alone can never reach the strengths needed.":"真空蒸餾器是在低溫下捕捉細緻的植物香氣；它與高濃度無關。混合式蒸餾器是部分生產者用來精修質地的選項，不是要求。只靠壺式蒸餾器永遠達不到所需的濃度。","What exactly is the 'hybrid still' used by some vodka producers?":"有些伏特加生產者使用的「混合式蒸餾器」究竟是什麼？","A pot still that can be linked to a rectifying column":"可以連接精餾柱的壺式蒸餾器","A column with no plates that works in batches":"沒有蒸餾板、以批次運作的蒸餾柱","Two pot stills joined by a single swan neck":"用一條天鵝頸連接的兩座壺式蒸餾器","A pot still with an activated-charcoal filter built into its condenser":"冷凝器內建活性碳濾器的壺式蒸餾器","The hybrid combines a pot with a rectifying column: in effect, it is another column distillation.":"混合式蒸餾器結合了壺身和精餾柱：實際上是又一次蒸餾柱蒸餾。","That is why rerunning bought-in neutral spirit through a hybrid purifies it further and makes the texture silkier. A column with no plates is not a real still type. Charcoal filtration is a separate step after distillation.":"所以把買進的中性烈酒再通過混合式蒸餾器，能進一步純化並讓質地更絲滑。沒有蒸餾板的蒸餾柱不是真正的蒸餾器類型。木炭過濾是蒸餾後的另一個步驟。","How can a vodka brand be launched without distilling anything itself?":"不親自蒸餾任何東西，要怎麼推出一個伏特加品牌？","By buying neutral spirit, a widely traded commodity":"買進中性烈酒，它是交易廣泛的大宗商品","By ageing another producer's whisky in steel tanks":"把其他生產者的威士忌放在鋼槽中陳年","By bottling fermented potato liquid as it is":"把發酵的馬鈴薯液體原樣裝瓶","By redistilling gin to strip its botanicals":"把琴酒再蒸餾以去除植物性原料","Neutral spirit is bought and sold widely; diluted, and often refined further, it becomes vodka.":"中性烈酒的買賣很普遍；經過稀釋，並常再加以精修，就成為伏特加。","Simply diluted, it can feel a little rough, so many rerun it through a hybrid still. Whisky is another category, and a fermented liquid is not yet a spirit. Stripping a gin of its botanicals makes no sense when gin itself starts from neutral spirit.":"只是稀釋的話口感可能有點粗糙，所以許多人會讓它再通過混合式蒸餾器。威士忌是另一個類別，發酵液則還不是烈酒。去除琴酒的植物性原料毫無道理，因為琴酒本身就是從中性烈酒開始的。","Which of these is NOT a usual step in making an unflavoured vodka?":"下列哪一項不是製作未調味伏特加的常見步驟？","Maturing it in oak barrels":"在橡木桶中熟成","Filtering it through activated charcoal":"用活性碳過濾","Diluting it with top-quality water to bottling strength":"用頂級品質的水稀釋到裝瓶濃度","Storing it in inert vessels":"存放在惰性容器中","Vodka is kept in inert vessels: oak would add colour and aromas that go against its neutrality.":"伏特加存放在惰性容器中：橡木會增添顏色和香氣，違背它的中性。","Activated charcoal removes the last unwanted congeners and is widely used. Dilution with very pure water is essential, as nearly 60% of the bottle is water. Inert vessels are the rule precisely so the spirit does not change.":"活性碳去除最後不想要的同屬物，使用很廣。用非常純淨的水稀釋不可或缺，因為瓶中將近 60% 是水。惰性容器是通則，正是為了讓烈酒不發生變化。","A premium 'characterful' vodka has a fuller texture. How should its aroma intensity still be described?":"一款高級的「有個性」伏特加質地較飽滿。它的香氣強度仍應該怎麼描述？","Deep, as for colour":"深，和描述顏色一樣","Even characterful vodkas have very light flavours, correctly described as neutral.":"即使是有個性的伏特加，風味也非常清淡，正確的描述是中性。","The difference from the neutral style lies mainly in a rounder texture, not in aroma intensity. 'Medium' and 'pronounced' are used for most other spirits. 'Deep' is an appearance term, not a nose term. If an unflavoured vodka shows clearly non-neutral aromas, they were probably added after distillation.":"它與中性風格的差別主要在於較圓潤的質地，不是香氣強度。「中等」和「明顯」用於大多數其他烈酒。「深」是外觀的術語，不是香氣的。如果未調味的伏特加表現出明顯非中性的香氣，那很可能是蒸餾後添加的。","Which botanical must, by law, be present in every gin?":"依法，每一款琴酒都必須含有哪一種植物性原料？","Coriander seeds":"芫荽籽","Angelica root":"歐白芷根","Lemon and orange peel":"檸檬皮和橙皮","Juniper is the only botanical the law requires in gin.":"杜松子是法律規定琴酒唯一必須使用的植物性原料。","Coriander, citrus and angelica are very common, but they remain the distiller's choice. It is precisely because only juniper is compulsory that gins can have such different aromatic profiles.":"芫荽籽、柑橘和歐白芷根非常常見，但仍是蒸餾師的選擇。正因為只有杜松子是強制的，琴酒才能有這麼不同的香氣輪廓。","Which group lists the most commonly used gin botanicals after juniper?":"哪一組列出了杜松子之後最常用的琴酒植物性原料？","Coriander, citrus peel, angelica, orris":"芫荽籽、柑橘皮、歐白芷根、鳶尾根","Vanilla, cinnamon, cloves, nutmeg":"香草、肉桂、丁香、肉豆蔻","Aniseed, fennel, star anise, liquorice":"茴香籽、茴香、八角、甘草","Gentian, quinine, bitter orange and artichoke":"龍膽、奎寧、苦橙和朝鮮薊","Coriander, citrus, angelica and orris are the classic supporting botanicals.":"芫荽籽、柑橘、歐白芷根和鳶尾根是經典的配角植物性原料。","The other sets belong to other families: aniseed, fennel and liquorice define pastis; gentian and quinine are typical of bitters; vanilla and cinnamon suggest spiced rum.":"其他幾組屬於別的家族：茴香籽、茴香和甘草定義了 pastis；龍膽和奎寧是苦味酒的典型原料；香草和肉桂則讓人想到香料蘭姆酒。","In the European Union, which base spirit must a gin producer use?":"在歐盟，琴酒生產者必須使用哪一種基酒？","An aged malted-barley spirit":"陳年的麥芽大麥烈酒","A pot-distilled grape spirit":"壺式蒸餾的葡萄烈酒","Any fermented liquid, distilled directly":"任何發酵液，直接蒸餾","In the EU, gin must be made from neutral spirit.":"在歐盟，琴酒必須用中性烈酒製作。","A neutral base lets the botanicals speak without interference. Distilling straight from a fermented liquid is allowed in the USA, not the EU, and characterful spirits such as malt or grape spirits do not meet the European rule.":"中性的基底讓植物性原料不受干擾地表現。直接用發酵液蒸餾在美國是允許的，在歐盟則不行；麥芽或葡萄烈酒這類有個性的烈酒不符合歐洲的規定。","What do US rules allow gin producers to do that EU rules do not?":"美國的規定允許琴酒生產者做哪一件歐盟規定不允許的事？","Distil gin straight from a fermented liquid":"直接用發酵液蒸餾琴酒","Make gin with no juniper at all":"完全不用杜松子製作琴酒","Call a spirit aged at least three years in cask a 'gin'":"把在桶中陳年至少三年的烈酒稱為「gin」","Bottle gin below the strength of wine":"以低於葡萄酒的濃度裝瓶琴酒","In the USA, other spirits or a fermented liquid can be the starting point.":"在美國，其他烈酒或發酵液都可以作為起點。","Juniper is compulsory everywhere: without it, it is not gin. The options about ageing and strength are invented: there is no three-year cask rule for gin, and gin is not bottled at wine strength.":"杜松子到處都是強制的：沒有它就不是琴酒。關於陳年和濃度的選項是虛構的：琴酒沒有三年桶陳的規定，也不會以葡萄酒的濃度裝瓶。","Why do nearly all gins start from neutral spirit?":"為什麼幾乎所有琴酒都從中性烈酒開始？","It lets the botanicals stand out":"它讓植物性原料突顯出來","It adds notes of wood and vanilla":"它增添木質和香草氣息","It makes any later redistillation unnecessary":"它讓之後的再蒸餾變得不必要","It gives gin a natural golden colour":"它賦予琴酒天然的金黃色","A neutral background does not compete with botanical aromas.":"中性的背景不會與植物香氣競爭。","Neutral spirit has no character of its own, so it brings neither wood nor colour. In fact it is the ideal base to redistil with botanicals: redistillation remains the best method rather than becoming unnecessary.":"中性烈酒本身沒有特色，所以既不帶來木質味，也不帶來顏色。事實上它是與植物性原料一起再蒸餾的理想基酒：再蒸餾仍是最好的方法，而不是變得不必要。","A distiller wants a fuller, more intense gin. Which choice helps?":"一位蒸餾師想要更飽滿、更濃郁的琴酒。哪一項選擇有幫助？","Steep the botanicals in the spirit before distilling":"蒸餾前先把植物性原料浸泡在烈酒中","Place the botanicals in a basket reached only by vapour":"把植物性原料放在只有蒸氣能到達的籃子裡","Keep contact between botanicals and spirit to a minimum":"盡量減少植物性原料與烈酒的接觸","Use a spirit already heavily flavoured with artificial flavourings":"使用已經用人工香料重度調味的烈酒","Longer contact with the spirit extracts more flavour from the botanicals.":"與烈酒接觸得越久，從植物性原料萃取的風味越多。","The vapour basket gives the opposite, a lighter style, because the botanicals are not in contact with the boiling liquid. Artificial flavourings are not part of redistillation and are not the route to a quality gin.":"蒸氣籃的效果相反，風格較清淡，因為植物性原料不接觸沸騰的液體。人工香料不屬於再蒸餾，也不是做出優質琴酒的途徑。","Where are the botanicals placed in a 'Carterhead' still?":"在「Carterhead」蒸餾器中，植物性原料放在哪裡？","In a basket between the still and the condenser":"放在蒸餾器和冷凝器之間的籃子裡","At the bottom of the pot, sitting in the liquid":"放在壺身底部，浸在液體中","In the resting vessel, after distillation":"蒸餾後放在靜置容器中","Directly in the bottle, at the moment of packaging":"在包裝時直接放進瓶中","In this system the botanicals sit in a basket that the vapours pass through.":"在這套系統中，植物性原料放在蒸氣會穿過的籃子裡。","The basket sits in the pipe that carries vapour to the condenser, so the botanicals never touch the boiling liquid. Botanicals sitting in the pot are the first approach, not this one, and adding them in the bottle is not redistillation.":"籃子位於把蒸氣送往冷凝器的管路中，所以植物性原料從不接觸沸騰的液體。把植物性原料放在壺身裡是第一種做法，不是這一種；在瓶中加入則不是再蒸餾。","What style of gin does vapour-basket flavouring generally produce?":"用蒸氣籃調味，通常做出什麼風格的琴酒？","A lighter style":"較清淡的風格","A fuller, more powerful style":"更飽滿、更有力的風格","A sweet style, close to Old Tom":"甜的風格，接近 Old Tom","A golden-coloured style with a woody profile":"金黃色、帶木質輪廓的風格","Vapour extracts less flavour than boiling liquid, so the gin is lighter.":"蒸氣萃取的風味比沸騰的液體少，所以琴酒較清淡。","The fuller style comes instead from direct, extended contact between botanicals and spirit. The extraction method adds neither sugar nor colour: sweetness and a golden hue depend on other choices, such as sweetening or oak ageing.":"較飽滿的風格則來自植物性原料與烈酒直接而長時間的接觸。萃取方式既不增添糖，也不增添顏色：甜味和金黃色調取決於其他選擇，例如加糖或橡木桶陳年。","What is the main advantage of distilling a botanical on its own?":"單獨蒸餾一種植物性原料的主要好處是什麼？","It gives a purer flavour":"得到更純淨的風味","It lets the distiller skip the final blending stage entirely":"讓蒸餾師可以完全省去最後的調和階段","It makes the botanicals interact":"讓植物性原料彼此交互作用","It adds colour to the gin":"為琴酒增添顏色","Alone, a botanical does not interact with others and its aroma stays cleaner.":"單獨蒸餾時，植物性原料不會與其他原料交互作用，香氣保持得更乾淨。","Interaction between botanicals happens precisely when they are distilled together, so that is the opposite effect. Distilling separately also makes final blending necessary rather than unnecessary, and distillation does not add colour.":"植物性原料之間的交互作用正是在一起蒸餾時發生的，所以那是相反的效果。分開蒸餾也讓最後的調和變得必要，而不是不必要；蒸餾也不會增添顏色。","What happens when botanicals are all distilled together?":"把所有植物性原料一起蒸餾時會怎麼樣？","They interact and their flavours can change":"它們會交互作用，風味可能改變","Each keeps a perfectly separate aroma":"每一種都保有完全獨立的香氣","The gin loses its juniper flavour completely":"琴酒完全失去杜松子風味","The gin automatically becomes sweet and softer":"琴酒自動變甜、變柔和","Together in the still, botanicals influence each other during distillation.":"在蒸餾器中放在一起時，植物性原料在蒸餾過程中會互相影響。","It is precisely to avoid this interaction that some distillers run certain botanicals separately. Distilling together neither removes juniper nor adds sugar: it is the most common method for classic gins.":"有些蒸餾師把某些植物性原料分開蒸餾，正是為了避免這種交互作用。一起蒸餾既不會去除杜松子，也不會增添糖：這是經典琴酒最常見的做法。","A distiller wants one botanical, say a citrus peel, to stand out in the gin. What can be done?":"一位蒸餾師想讓某一種植物性原料（例如某種柑橘皮）在琴酒中突顯出來。可以怎麼做？","Distil it separately and add it afterwards":"把它單獨蒸餾，之後再加入","Leave it out of the gin recipe entirely":"把它完全從琴酒配方中拿掉","Raise the bottling strength":"提高裝瓶濃度","Age the gin for several years in new oak casks":"把琴酒放在新橡木桶中陳年數年","A separate distillate added at the end keeps that aroma clearer and more prominent.":"最後加入單獨蒸餾的餾出液，能讓那種香氣更清晰、更突出。","Many distillers run most botanicals together and then add one individual distillate to bring it forward. Oak would add woody notes that mask rather than highlight the citrus, and bottling strength does not choose which aroma stands out.":"許多蒸餾師把大部分植物性原料一起蒸餾，再加入某一種單獨的餾出液來突顯它。橡木會增添木質氣息，掩蓋而不是突顯柑橘味，裝瓶濃度也無法決定哪一種香氣突出。","Which statement about 'London Dry Gin' is correct?":"關於「London Dry Gin」，下列哪一項正確？","All its flavour comes from redistillation":"它所有的風味都來自再蒸餾","It must be made in the city of London":"必須在倫敦市製作","It may be sweetened after redistillation":"再蒸餾後可以加糖","It can be flavoured by adding ready-made flavourings after distilling":"可以在蒸餾後添加現成的香料來調味","London Dry takes its flavour only from redistillation with botanicals.":"London Dry 的風味只來自與植物性原料一起再蒸餾。","The name describes a method, not a place: it can be made anywhere. It is the strictest European style precisely because it bans both sweetening and flavourings added after redistillation.":"這個名稱描述的是方法，不是地點：它可以在任何地方製作。它是歐洲最嚴格的類型，正因為它既禁止加糖，也禁止在再蒸餾後添加香料。","A European gin is labelled 'Distilled Gin'. What can be inferred?":"一款歐洲琴酒標示為「Distilled Gin」。可以推論出什麼？","It is redistilled, but flavours may have been added afterwards":"它經過再蒸餾，但之後可能添加了風味","All flavours come exclusively from redistillation":"所有風味都完全來自再蒸餾","It was distilled straight from a fermented liquid":"它直接用發酵液蒸餾","It is certainly a sweetened gin":"它一定是加糖的琴酒","In the EU, 'Distilled Gin' allows flavours added after redistillation.":"在歐盟，「Distilled Gin」允許在再蒸餾後添加風味。","'All flavour from redistillation' is the US meaning of the term, or the rule for European London Dry. Direct distillation from a fermented liquid is not allowed in the EU, and the term that signals a sweet gin is 'Old Tom'.":"「所有風味來自再蒸餾」是這個術語在美國的意思，或是歐洲 London Dry 的規定。直接用發酵液蒸餾在歐盟不被允許，而表示甜琴酒的術語是「Old Tom」。","In the USA, what does the term 'Distilled Gin' guarantee?":"在美國，「Distilled Gin」這個術語保證什麼？","That all flavour comes from redistillation":"所有風味都來自再蒸餾","That the gin has been sweetened":"琴酒加了糖","That flavours were added after redistillation":"再蒸餾後添加了風味","That the gin has rested in oak casks for a period of time":"琴酒在橡木桶中靜置過一段時間","In the USA the term requires every flavour to come from redistillation.":"在美國，這個術語要求所有風味都來自再蒸餾。","It is the reverse of the European meaning, where flavours may be added afterwards. The term says nothing about sweetness or wood: those are separate pieces of information.":"這與歐洲的意思相反，在歐洲之後可以添加風味。這個術語與甜度或木頭無關：那些是另外的資訊。","What does 'Old Tom' usually indicate on a gin label?":"琴酒酒標上的「Old Tom」通常表示什麼？","A sweetened gin":"加糖的琴酒","A gin aged at least ten years":"陳年至少十年的琴酒","A gin legally required to be made in England":"依法必須在英格蘭製作的琴酒","A gin with no botanical other than juniper":"除了杜松子沒有其他植物性原料的琴酒","'Old Tom' is not legally defined but typically signals a sweetened gin.":"「Old Tom」沒有法律定義，但通常表示加糖的琴酒。","It is a historic style that predates dry gins. It implies no minimum ageing or geographical rule, and nothing limits its botanicals to juniper alone.":"它是早於不甜琴酒的歷史風格。它不代表最低陳年時間或地理規定，也沒有把植物性原料限制在杜松子一種。","Which statement about Old Tom is true?":"關於 Old Tom，下列哪一項正確？","It is a style older than dry gins":"它是比不甜琴酒更古老的風格","It is the style most strictly defined by European law":"它是歐洲法律定義最嚴格的類型","It cannot contain added sugar":"它不能含有添加的糖","It is a modern term born with craft gins":"它是隨精釀琴酒誕生的現代術語","Old Tom historically predates the dry style.":"Old Tom 在歷史上早於不甜的風格。","The strictest European style is London Dry, which bans sugar; Old Tom is not even legally defined and is usually sweet. It is not a modern invention but a revival of an old style.":"歐洲最嚴格的類型是禁止加糖的 London Dry；Old Tom 甚至沒有法律定義，而且通常是甜的。它不是現代的發明，而是舊風格的復興。","A customer notices a gin with a pale lemon colour. What is the most likely explanation?":"一位顧客注意到一款琴酒帶淡檸檬色。最可能的解釋是什麼？","It has rested in oak":"它在橡木桶中靜置過","It was made in a vapour-basket still":"它是用蒸氣籃蒸餾器製作的","It contains more juniper than usual":"它的杜松子比平常多","It was made from highly rectified neutral spirit":"它用高度精餾的中性烈酒製成","A small trend is ageing gin in oak, which gives it a pale lemon colour.":"有一股小趨勢是把琴酒放在橡木桶中陳年，這讓它帶淡檸檬色。","Most gins rest in inert vessels and are colourless. The redistillation method, the amount of juniper and the neutral spirit add no colour: a distillate stays clear.":"大多數琴酒在惰性容器中靜置，是無色的。再蒸餾的方式、杜松子的量和中性烈酒都不會增添顏色：餾出液始終是清澈的。","Which method is considered to give the best gins?":"哪一種方法被認為能做出最好的琴酒？","Redistillation with botanicals":"與植物性原料一起再蒸餾","Adding artificial flavourings to neutral spirit":"在中性烈酒中添加人工香料","Long ageing in previously used casks":"在用過的桶中長期陳年","Fermenting juniper berries":"讓杜松子發酵","The best gins come from redistilling spirit with real botanicals.":"最好的琴酒來自把烈酒與真正的植物性原料一起再蒸餾。","Artificial flavourings are legal for many gins but give less refined results. Cask ageing applies only to a minority of gins, and juniper is a flavouring botanical, not a raw material to be fermented.":"人工香料對許多琴酒來說是合法的，但成果較不細緻。桶陳只適用於少數琴酒，而杜松子是調味用的植物性原料，不是用來發酵的原料。","A bartender wants a gin flavoured only by redistillation and with no sugar. Which European label term should they look for?":"一位調酒師想要一款只靠再蒸餾調味、而且不含糖的琴酒。應該找哪一個歐洲酒標術語？","Distilled Gin, in its EU meaning":"Distilled Gin，取其歐盟的意思","Plain 'Gin', with no further wording":"單純的「Gin」，沒有其他字樣","Only London Dry combines redistillation-only flavour with a ban on sweetening.":"只有 London Dry 同時具備只靠再蒸餾取得風味和禁止加糖。","EU Distilled Gin may receive flavourings after redistillation, and Old Tom usually means a sweet gin. Plain 'Gin' may even be made with added flavourings and no redistillation at all.":"歐盟的 Distilled Gin 可以在再蒸餾後添加香料，Old Tom 通常表示甜琴酒。單純的「Gin」甚至可以只添加香料、完全不經再蒸餾。","Which other label term is used as an equivalent of 'London Dry Gin'?":"哪一個酒標術語可以當作「London Dry Gin」的同義詞？","Compound gin, made by cold-adding flavourings":"Compound gin，以冷混方式加入香料製成","Aged gin":"陳年琴酒","'Dry Gin' is the alternative name for the London Dry style.":"「Dry Gin」是 London Dry 類型的另一個名稱。","The style may appear as 'London Dry Gin' or simply 'Dry Gin', with the same rules: redistillation only and no sugar. Old Tom signals the opposite, a sweet gin, and cold-adding flavourings or ageing in wood does not fit this style.":"這個類型可以標示為「London Dry Gin」或只寫「Dry Gin」，規定相同：只靠再蒸餾，不加糖。Old Tom 表示相反的東西，也就是甜琴酒；冷混加入香料或木桶陳年都不符合這個類型。","Apart from juniper, which botanicals may a gin producer legally use?":"除了杜松子，琴酒生產者依法可以使用哪些植物性原料？","Any botanical, with no limit":"任何植物性原料，沒有限制","Only coriander, citrus, angelica and orris":"只有芫荽籽、柑橘、歐白芷根和鳶尾根","At most ten approved botanicals":"最多十種核准的植物性原料","Only plants grown in Europe":"只有歐洲種植的植物","The law requires only juniper and sets no limit on other botanicals.":"法律只要求杜松子，對其他植物性原料沒有限制。","Coriander, citrus, angelica and orris are the most common choices, not a closed list. There is no maximum number and no rule on where the plants come from. This freedom explains the huge variety of gins on the market.":"芫荽籽、柑橘、歐白芷根和鳶尾根是最常見的選擇，不是封閉的清單。沒有數量上限，也沒有規定植物的產地。這種自由解釋了市面上琴酒的多樣性。","Why have so many new styles of gin appeared in recent years?":"為什麼近年來出現這麼多新風格的琴酒？","The law leaves the choice of botanicals open":"法律不限制植物性原料的選擇","Juniper is no longer compulsory in Europe":"杜松子在歐洲不再是強制的","Aged grain spirits can now be used as the base in the EU":"歐盟現在可以用陳年穀物烈酒作為基酒","The botanical basket was only just invented":"植物籃是最近才發明的","Beyond the compulsory juniper, distillers choose freely and have exploited that freedom.":"除了強制的杜松子，蒸餾師可以自由選擇，並充分運用了這種自由。","Juniper is still compulsory everywhere, so the second option is false. In the EU the base must be neutral spirit, not an aged spirit. The botanical basket has existed for a long time and does not explain the recent boom in styles.":"杜松子在各地仍然是強制的，所以第二個選項是錯的。在歐盟，基酒必須是中性烈酒，不是陳年烈酒。植物籃已經存在很久，無法解釋近年風格的蓬勃發展。","Which of these is NOT one of the most widely used supporting botanicals in gin?":"下列哪一項不屬於琴酒中使用最廣的配角植物性原料？","Orris root":"鳶尾根","Wormwood is the signature plant of absinthe and vermouth, not of gin.":"苦艾是苦艾酒和香艾酒的招牌植物，不是琴酒的。","After juniper, the most frequent botanicals are coriander, citrus peel, angelica and orris. Wormwood gives a marked bitterness and floral scent linked to absinthe and, under EU law, to vermouth. A gin could use it, but it is not one of the classic botanicals.":"杜松子之後最常見的植物性原料是芫荽籽、柑橘皮、歐白芷根和鳶尾根。苦艾帶來鮮明的苦味和花香，與苦艾酒有關，依歐盟法律也與香艾酒有關。琴酒可以用它，但它不是經典的植物性原料。","Which two classic gin botanicals are roots?":"哪兩種經典的琴酒植物性原料是根？","Angelica and orris":"歐白芷根和鳶尾根","Coriander and juniper":"芫荽籽和杜松子","Orris and orange peel":"鳶尾根和橙皮","Juniper and angelica":"杜松子和歐白芷根","Gin uses angelica root and orris root.":"琴酒使用歐白芷的根和鳶尾的根。","Juniper is a berry and coriander is a seed, so the pairs including them are wrong. Orange peel is the skin of a fruit. The two roots bring earthy notes that support the other botanicals.":"杜松子是漿果，芫荽籽是種子，所以包含它們的組合是錯的。橙皮是水果的皮。這兩種根帶來土壤氣息，襯托其他植物性原料。","After flavouring, where are most gins usually stored before bottling?":"調味之後，大多數琴酒在裝瓶前通常存放在哪裡？","In new, toasted oak barrels":"在烘烤過的新橡木桶中","In casks that previously held Sherry":"在先前裝過 Sherry 的桶中","On the botanicals, for a second maceration":"泡在植物性原料上，做第二次浸漬","Most gins rest in inert vessels, then are diluted and bottled colourless.":"大多數琴酒在惰性容器中靜置，再稀釋並以無色裝瓶。","Oak ageing exists, but only as a small recent trend that gives a pale lemon colour. A second maceration is not a normal step: the flavour already comes from redistillation. An inert vessel adds no colour or flavour, so the gin stays clear.":"橡木桶陳年確實存在，但只是近年的小趨勢，會帶來淡檸檬色。第二次浸漬不是正常步驟：風味已經來自再蒸餾。惰性容器不增添顏色或風味，所以琴酒保持清澈。","A gin made in the USA starts from a base spirit that is not neutral. Is this allowed?":"一款美國製的琴酒從不是中性的基酒開始。這樣可以嗎？","Yes, US rules allow it":"可以，美國的規定允許","No, neutral spirit is compulsory everywhere":"不行，中性烈酒在各地都是強制的","Only if the gin is then aged in oak for a year":"只有之後在橡木桶中陳年一年才行","Only if the label says London Dry":"只有酒標寫著 London Dry 才行","In the USA, other spirits may be used, or gin may be distilled straight from a fermented liquid.":"在美國可以使用其他烈酒，也可以直接用發酵液蒸餾琴酒。","The requirement to start from neutral spirit applies in the EU, not in the USA. No ageing requirement is linked to it. London Dry describes a flavouring method, not a special permission about the base.":"必須從中性烈酒開始的要求適用於歐盟，不是美國。這與陳年要求無關。London Dry 描述的是調味方法，不是對基酒的特別許可。","Why do some gin label terms have different meanings in Europe and the USA?":"為什麼有些琴酒酒標術語在歐洲和美國的意思不同？","The rules on the base spirit differ":"關於基酒的規定不同","In Europe gin must be aged":"在歐洲琴酒必須陳年","In the USA juniper is not required by law":"在美國法律不要求杜松子","Americans only use column stills":"美國人只用柱式蒸餾器","Because the two legal systems treat the base spirit differently, the label terms diverge too.":"因為兩套法律制度對基酒的處理不同，酒標術語也跟著分歧。","The typical example is Distilled Gin, which does not guarantee the same thing in the two markets. Juniper is compulsory in both, and European gin does not have to be aged. The type of still is not the reason for the difference.":"典型的例子是 Distilled Gin，它在兩個市場保證的東西不一樣。杜松子在兩地都是強制的，歐洲的琴酒也不必陳年。蒸餾器的類型不是造成差異的原因。","In the steeping method, what goes into the pot still with the botanicals?":"在浸泡法中，與植物性原料一起放進壺式蒸餾器的是什麼？","Neutral spirit diluted with water":"加水稀釋過的中性烈酒","Freshly fermented dry white wine":"剛發酵完成的不甜白葡萄酒","Aged grain spirit at 70% abv":"70% abv 的陳年穀物烈酒","Sugar syrup to fix the aromas":"用來固定香氣的糖漿","Neutral spirit is diluted and poured into the still with the botanicals before redistilling.":"中性烈酒經過稀釋，與植物性原料一起倒進蒸餾器，再進行再蒸餾。","Wine is not the base of gin, and an aged spirit would mask the botanicals. Sugar does not distil: it would stay in the still and never reach the gin. Some distillers also let the botanicals steep for a fuller gin.":"葡萄酒不是琴酒的基底，陳年烈酒則會掩蓋植物性原料。糖無法蒸餾：它會留在蒸餾器中，永遠到不了琴酒裡。有些蒸餾師也會讓植物性原料浸泡一段時間，做出更飽滿的琴酒。","Why does the vapour-basket method give a lighter gin?":"為什麼蒸氣籃法做出的琴酒較清淡？","The botanicals never touch the boiling alcoholic liquid":"植物性原料從不接觸沸騰的含酒精液體","The law requires fewer botanicals":"法律規定使用較少的植物性原料","The gin is distilled to a lower strength":"琴酒蒸餾到較低的濃度","The botanicals are charcoal-filtered after distillation":"植物性原料在蒸餾後經過木炭過濾","Only the vapours pass through the botanicals, so they give up less flavour.":"只有蒸氣穿過植物性原料，所以它們釋出的風味較少。","A boiling alcoholic liquid extracts far more than vapour passing through. There is no legal limit on botanicals tied to this method. Distillation strength and charcoal filtration are not what makes this style light.":"沸騰的含酒精液體萃取的量遠多於穿過的蒸氣。這種方法與植物性原料的法定限制無關。蒸餾濃度和木炭過濾都不是這種風格清淡的原因。","A distiller processes every botanical separately. What happens at the end?":"一位蒸餾師把每種植物性原料分開處理。最後怎麼做？","The individual distillates are blended":"把各個餾出液調和起來","Redistils them all together a second time":"把它們全部放在一起再蒸餾第二次","Ages them in oak to marry them":"放進橡木桶陳年讓它們融合","Sells each one as a separate single-botanical gin":"每一種都當作單一植物性原料的琴酒分開販售","Distillers who process each botanical alone then blend the distillates to build the final gin.":"把每種植物性原料單獨處理的蒸餾師，之後會調和這些餾出液，組成最終的琴酒。","Redistilling everything together would cancel the method's advantage, the purity of each aroma. Oak ageing is not needed for blending. Selling one gin per botanical is not the point of this method.":"全部一起再蒸餾會抵銷這種方法的優點，也就是每種香氣的純淨度。調和不需要橡木桶陳年。每種植物性原料賣一款琴酒也不是這種方法的目的。","A distiller wants the botanicals to influence one another during distillation. Which choice fits?":"一位蒸餾師希望植物性原料在蒸餾時互相影響。哪一項選擇合適？","Distil them all together":"全部一起蒸餾","Distil them one at a time":"一次蒸餾一種","Add artificial flavourings after distillation":"蒸餾後添加人工香料","Use a low-temperature vacuum still":"使用低溫真空蒸餾器","When distilled together, botanicals interact and their flavours change and evolve.":"一起蒸餾時，植物性原料會交互作用，風味隨之改變和演變。","Distilling them one at a time is done precisely to avoid this interaction and get purer flavours. Artificial flavours added later create no interaction during distillation. A vacuum still protects delicate aromas but is not the way to make them interact.":"一次蒸餾一種正是為了避免這種交互作用，得到更純淨的風味。之後添加的人工香料不會在蒸餾時產生交互作用。真空蒸餾器能保護細緻的香氣，但不是讓它們交互作用的方法。","During gin redistillation, how does the distiller choose which botanical aromas to keep?":"在琴酒的再蒸餾中，蒸餾師如何選擇保留哪些植物香氣？","By taking the hearts cut while the wanted aromas come off":"在想要的香氣流出時切取酒心","By charcoal-filtering the distillate":"用木炭過濾餾出液","By adding sugar at the end of the run":"在蒸餾結束時加糖","By collecting only the tails, which carry heavy aromas":"只收集帶厚重香氣的酒尾","As in any pot-still distillation, the distiller controls the profile through the hearts cut.":"和任何壺式蒸餾一樣，蒸餾師透過酒心的切取來控制輪廓。","The most volatile aromas come off first and the least volatile last, so the timing of the cut decides the character. Charcoal filtration removes aroma rather than selecting it. Tails carry often unpleasant aromas, and sugar has nothing to do with selection.":"最易揮發的香氣最先流出，最不易揮發的最後，所以切取的時機決定了特色。木炭過濾是去除香氣，而不是篩選。酒尾帶的香氣往往令人不悅，而糖與篩選毫無關係。","Which statement about gins flavoured with artificial flavourings is correct?":"關於用人工香料調味的琴酒，下列哪一項正確？","They are possible, but the best gins are redistilled":"可以這樣做，但最好的琴酒是再蒸餾的","They are banned in both Europe and the USA":"在歐洲和美國都被禁止","They may be labelled London Dry Gin":"可以標示為 London Dry Gin","They are the most prized because their flavour is more stable":"它們最受珍視，因為風味更穩定","Gin can be made by adding artificial flavours, but the best quality comes from redistillation.":"琴酒可以用添加人工香料的方式製作，但最好的品質來自再蒸餾。","There is no general ban on this method. London Dry requires all flavour to come from redistillation, so it excludes added flavourings. Stability does not make these gins the most prized.":"這種方法沒有全面禁令。London Dry 要求所有風味來自再蒸餾，所以排除了添加香料。穩定性並不會讓這些琴酒成為最受珍視的。","A gin labelled London Dry Gin is made in Scotland. Is that a problem?":"一款標示 London Dry Gin 的琴酒在蘇格蘭製作。這有問題嗎？","No, London Dry is a style, not an origin":"沒有，London Dry 是類型，不是產地","Yes, it must be distilled within London":"有，必須在倫敦境內蒸餾","Yes, unless the base is Scotch whisky":"有，除非基酒是 Scotch 威士忌","No, but only if it is aged in England":"沒有，但必須在英格蘭陳年","London Dry describes how the gin is flavoured, not where it is made.":"London Dry 描述的是琴酒如何調味，不是在哪裡製作。","The style requires flavour from redistillation only and no added sugar, wherever it is made. A Scotch whisky base is not allowed in Europe, where neutral spirit is required. There is no requirement to age it in England.":"不論在哪裡製作，這個類型都要求風味只來自再蒸餾，而且不加糖。在歐洲不允許用 Scotch 威士忌作基酒，那裡規定用中性烈酒。沒有必須在英格蘭陳年的要求。","A European producer wants to add a little sugar to the gin after redistillation. Which label term is lost?":"一位歐洲生產者想在再蒸餾後為琴酒加一點糖。會失去哪一個酒標術語？","None, sugar does not affect the label":"都不會，糖不影響酒標","No sugar may be added to London Dry Gin.":"London Dry Gin 不得加糖。","A sweetened gin can still be called gin. Old Tom is in fact the term that suggests a sweetened gin. The last option is wrong because London Dry expressly forbids sugar.":"加糖的琴酒仍然可以稱為 gin。Old Tom 其實正是暗示加糖琴酒的術語。最後一個選項是錯的，因為 London Dry 明文禁止加糖。","A European producer redistils the gin and then adds a natural citrus extract. Which label term can be used?":"一位歐洲生產者把琴酒再蒸餾後，加入天然的柑橘萃取物。可以使用哪一個酒標術語？","None: any added flavour removes the right to say gin":"都不行：任何添加的風味都讓它失去標示 gin 的資格","In Europe, Distilled Gin allows flavours added after redistillation.":"在歐洲，Distilled Gin 允許在再蒸餾後添加風味。","London Dry Gin and its equivalent Dry Gin require all flavour to come from redistillation. Adding a flavour does not remove the right to the name gin. In the USA, by contrast, Distilled Gin would guarantee all flavour from redistillation.":"London Dry Gin 和同義的 Dry Gin 要求所有風味來自再蒸餾。添加風味並不會失去 gin 這個名稱的資格。在美國則相反，Distilled Gin 保證所有風味來自再蒸餾。","Which gin style is most tightly defined by EU law?":"哪一個琴酒類型在歐盟法律中定義最嚴格？","Oak-aged gin":"橡木桶陳年琴酒","Fruit-flavoured gin":"水果風味琴酒","London Dry is the most strictly regulated style: flavour from redistillation only and no sugar.":"London Dry 是規範最嚴格的類型：風味只來自再蒸餾，而且不加糖。","Old Tom has no legal definition and is only a customary indication. Oak-aged gins are a recent trend, not a codified style. Fruit gins follow the general gin rules, not a stricter definition.":"Old Tom 沒有法律定義，只是慣用的標示。橡木桶陳年琴酒是近年的趨勢，不是成文的類型。水果琴酒遵循一般的琴酒規定，不是更嚴格的定義。","Which pair correctly compares Old Tom and London Dry?":"哪一組正確比較了 Old Tom 和 London Dry？","Old Tom: usually sweetened. London Dry: no sugar":"Old Tom：通常加糖。London Dry：不加糖","Old Tom: no sugar. London Dry: sweetened":"Old Tom：不加糖。London Dry：加糖","Both: flavours added after distillation and sugar permitted":"兩者：蒸餾後添加風味，並允許加糖","Old Tom: a recent style. London Dry: the older style":"Old Tom：近年的風格。London Dry：較古老的風格","Old Tom signals a sweetened gin, while London Dry may contain no added sugar.":"Old Tom 表示加糖的琴酒，London Dry 則不得含有添加的糖。","The second option swaps the two styles. London Dry forbids both added flavours and sugar. Old Tom pre-dates dry gins, so the last option reverses the timeline.":"第二個選項把兩種類型對調了。London Dry 既禁止添加風味，也禁止加糖。Old Tom 早於不甜琴酒，所以最後一個選項把時間順序顛倒了。","Which label term means something different in the EU and in the USA?":"哪一個酒標術語在歐盟和美國的意思不同？","Distilled Gin allows added flavours in Europe, while in the USA it guarantees flavour from redistillation only.":"Distilled Gin 在歐洲允許添加風味，在美國則保證風味只來自再蒸餾。","Old Tom is not legally defined in either market. Juniper is compulsory in both. The word gin, despite different base rules, is not the classic case of a term with a double meaning.":"Old Tom 在兩個市場都沒有法律定義。杜松子在兩地都是強制的。gin 這個字雖然基酒規定不同，卻不是一詞兩義的經典例子。","Which of these is NOT one of the three ways to flavour gin by redistillation?":"下列哪一項不是以再蒸餾為琴酒調味的三種方式之一？","Steeping cold and bottling without distilling":"冷浸後不經蒸餾就裝瓶","Placing botanicals in the still with the spirit":"把植物性原料與烈酒一起放進蒸餾器","Passing the vapours through a botanical basket":"讓蒸氣穿過植物籃","Distilling botanicals separately and blending":"把植物性原料分開蒸餾再調和","Maceration without distillation gives a tincture, not a redistilled gin.":"不經蒸餾的浸漬得到的是酊劑，不是再蒸餾的琴酒。","The other three options are the three classic approaches: botanicals in the still, vapour basket, separate distillation. Simple maceration also extracts colour and cannot select aromas. So it is not a redistillation method.":"其他三個選項就是三種經典做法：植物性原料放進蒸餾器、蒸氣籃、分開蒸餾。單純的浸漬還會萃取顏色，也無法篩選香氣。所以它不是再蒸餾的方法。","What colour is the great majority of bottled gin?":"絕大多數瓶裝琴酒是什麼顏色？","Colourless":"無色","Pale lemon":"淡檸檬色","Light amber":"淺琥珀色","Faint green from the botanicals":"來自植物性原料的淡綠色","Redistillation carries no colour and gin rests in inert vessels, so it stays colourless.":"再蒸餾不會帶出顏色，琴酒又在惰性容器中靜置，所以保持無色。","Pale lemon applies only to the small niche of oak-aged gins. Amber would require long ageing, which is not typical of gin. Botanicals give colour only through maceration, not through distillation.":"淡檸檬色只適用於橡木桶陳年琴酒這個小眾領域。琥珀色需要長期陳年，那不是琴酒的典型做法。植物性原料只有透過浸漬才會帶來顏色，蒸餾則不會。","Where does the term London Dry Gin usually appear on the bottle?":"London Dry Gin 這個術語通常出現在酒瓶的哪裡？","Prominently on the front label":"醒目地標在正標上","Only on the cap, in small print":"只在瓶蓋上，用小字","On the back label among the ingredients":"在背標的成分之中","Never: the law forbids showing it":"不會出現：法律禁止標示","It is a style term that producers normally display clearly on the front.":"它是類型術語，生產者通常清楚地標在正面。","Because it guarantees a precise method, producers want to show it clearly. It is neither hidden nor forbidden. Knowing where to look helps you quickly pick a dry, redistilled gin.":"因為它保證明確的做法，生產者希望清楚地展示出來。它既沒有被隱藏，也沒有被禁止。知道要看哪裡，能幫你快速挑出不甜、經再蒸餾的琴酒。","A bartender tastes a gin with woody notes and a pale lemon colour. Which technique explains both features?":"一位調酒師品嚐一款帶木質氣息和淡檸檬色的琴酒。哪一種技術能同時解釋這兩項特徵？","A spell in oak casks":"在橡木桶中存放一段時間","The vapour basket in the still":"蒸餾器中的蒸氣籃","Distilling the angelica root separately":"把歐白芷根分開蒸餾","A larger amount of juniper in the recipe":"配方中更多的杜松子","Time in oak gives gin a pale lemon colour and some wood flavour.":"在橡木桶中的時間讓琴酒帶淡檸檬色和一些木頭風味。","The basket and separate distillation affect aroma but give no colour, because colour does not travel with vapour. More juniper makes the gin more resinous, not yellow or woody. Only the cask explains both colour and wood notes.":"蒸氣籃和分開蒸餾影響香氣，但不帶來顏色，因為顏色不會隨蒸氣移動。更多杜松子會讓琴酒更有樹脂味，而不是變黃或帶木質味。只有桶能同時解釋顏色和木質氣息。","A distiller with a traditional pot still wants a rich gin, so leaves the botanicals in the spirit overnight before distilling. What is gained?":"一位使用傳統壺式蒸餾器的蒸餾師想要豐厚的琴酒，所以在蒸餾前把植物性原料留在烈酒中一整夜。會得到什麼？","More flavour extracted from the botanicals":"從植物性原料萃取出更多風味","A gin coloured by the botanicals":"被植物性原料染色的琴酒","The right to add sugar to it":"在其中加糖的資格","A higher bottling strength":"更高的裝瓶濃度","Extended contact with the spirit extracts more flavour and gives a fuller gin.":"與烈酒長時間接觸能萃取更多風味，做出更飽滿的琴酒。","Colour extracted during steeping stays in the still: the distillate comes off colourless. Steeping does not change the sugar rules. Bottling strength depends on final dilution, not on steeping.":"浸泡時萃取的顏色留在蒸餾器中：餾出液流出時是無色的。浸泡不會改變關於糖的規定。裝瓶濃度取決於最後的稀釋，不是浸泡。","A customer wants a sweet, old-style gin for a historic recipe. Which label term should be looked for?":"一位顧客想為一個歷史酒譜找一款甜的老式琴酒。應該找哪一個酒標術語？","Distilled Gin, in its US meaning":"Distilled Gin，取其美國的意思","Old Tom pre-dates dry gins and the term usually signals a sweetened gin.":"Old Tom 早於不甜琴酒，這個術語通常表示加糖的琴酒。","London Dry Gin and Dry Gin forbid added sugar, so they are the opposite of what is wanted. Distilled Gin in the USA is about where the flavour comes from, not sweetness. Old Tom is not legally defined, but in practice it indicates a sweetened gin.":"London Dry Gin 和 Dry Gin 禁止加糖，所以與所需的相反。美國的 Distilled Gin 說的是風味的來源，不是甜度。Old Tom 沒有法律定義，但實務上表示加糖的琴酒。","What is a spirit flavoured by maceration sometimes called?":"以浸漬調味的烈酒有時叫做什麼？","A tincture":"酊劑（tincture）","A distillate":"餾出液（distillate）","A cold-compounded flavouring from a supplier":"供應商提供的冷混香料","A spirit flavoured by maceration is sometimes called a tincture.":"以浸漬調味的烈酒有時稱為酊劑（tincture）。","'Distillate' refers instead to a spirit flavoured by redistillation. Cold compounding is the blending-in of artificial flavours, and lees are a fermentation residue, not a flavouring method.":"「餾出液」（distillate）指的則是以再蒸餾調味的烈酒。冷混法是把人工香料調入，酒渣是發酵的殘餘物，不是調味方法。","What advantage does maceration have over redistillation?":"與再蒸餾相比，浸漬有什麼優點？","It also extracts colour":"它也能萃取顏色","It isolates a single aroma precisely":"它能精確分離出單一香氣","It only works with spirit at the highest possible strength":"它只適用於濃度最高的烈酒","It always requires a vacuum still":"它一定需要真空蒸餾器","Maceration brings colour and a broad range of flavours into the spirit.":"浸漬把顏色和範圍廣泛的風味帶進烈酒。","Isolating one particular aroma is exactly what maceration cannot do: that needs redistillation. Spirit that is too strong would extract unpleasant flavours, so it is often diluted, and maceration uses no still at all.":"分離出某一種特定香氣正是浸漬做不到的：那需要再蒸餾。濃度太高的烈酒會萃取出不好的風味，所以常先稀釋，而浸漬完全不用蒸餾器。","Why is a vacuum still used for botanicals such as cucumber?":"為什麼小黃瓜這類植物性原料要用真空蒸餾器？","It distils at lower temperatures":"它在較低的溫度下蒸餾","It adds a stable natural green colour to the spirit":"它為烈酒增添穩定的天然綠色","It raises the strength beyond normal":"它把濃度提高到超出一般","It removes the need for a hearts cut":"它不再需要切取酒心","In a vacuum liquids boil at lower temperatures, so fragile aromas are not damaged.":"在真空中液體在較低的溫度沸騰，所以脆弱的香氣不會受損。","Some delicate aromas break down in the heat of a normal still. Distillation adds no colour, and even under vacuum the distiller still chooses the hearts cut.":"有些細緻的香氣在一般蒸餾器的高溫下會分解。蒸餾不增添顏色，而且即使在真空下，蒸餾師仍要選擇酒心的切取。","What is 'cold compounding'?":"什麼是「cold compounding」（冷混法）？","Blending artificial flavours into a spirit":"把人工香料調入烈酒","Macerating fruit in the cold for months":"把水果冷浸好幾個月","Distilling in a vacuum still at a very low temperature":"用真空蒸餾器在非常低的溫度蒸餾","Chill-filtering the spirit":"對烈酒做冷凝過濾","It is the technique of adding artificial flavours to the base spirit.":"它是把人工香料加入基酒的技術。","Despite the word 'cold', it is not about temperature: the flavours, man-made but similar to natural ones, are simply blended in. Maceration, vacuum distillation and filtration are different processes.":"雖然有「cold」這個字，但它與溫度無關：這些人造但與天然相似的香料只是單純調入。浸漬、真空蒸餾和過濾都是不同的製程。","Why do even premium producers often use some artificial colouring?":"為什麼連高級生產者也常使用一些人工色素？","Natural colour is unstable":"天然顏色不穩定","The law bans plant-based colours completely":"法律完全禁止植物性色素","Artificial colour adds sweetness":"人工色素增添甜味","Natural colour would completely mask the botanical aroma":"天然顏色會完全掩蓋植物香氣","Plant-derived colour can vary from one bottle to the next.":"來自植物的顏色可能每一瓶都不一樣。","Most consumers would not accept bottles of different colours, so a little artificial colouring is used to keep it consistent. Plant colours are permitted, and colour neither adds sweetness nor masks aromas.":"大多數消費者無法接受顏色不同的酒瓶，所以用一點人工色素來保持一致。植物性色素是允許的，而顏色既不增添甜味，也不掩蓋香氣。","Which spirit is typically used as the base for spiced rum?":"香料蘭姆酒通常用哪一種烈酒作基酒？","A sweetened golden rum":"加糖的金色蘭姆酒","A dry, unaged white rum":"不甜、未陳年的白蘭姆酒","A neutral grain spirit with no character of its own":"本身沒有特色的中性穀物烈酒","A grape brandy":"葡萄白蘭地","Spiced rum typically starts from golden rums that have been sweetened.":"香料蘭姆酒通常從加過糖的金色蘭姆酒開始。","It is one of the exceptions to the neutral-base rule: here the rum's character is part of the product. Dry white rum is not the typical base, and a grape or grain spirit would not make a rum.":"這是中性基酒通則的例外之一：在這裡蘭姆酒的特色是產品的一部分。不甜的白蘭姆酒不是典型的基酒，而葡萄或穀物烈酒做不出蘭姆酒。","If a spiced rum uses natural flavours, why is it probably not redistilled?":"如果香料蘭姆酒使用天然風味，為什麼它很可能不經再蒸餾？","It would lose its colour and aged rum character":"它會失去顏色和陳年蘭姆酒的特色","Redistillation is banned for every kind of rum":"所有種類的蘭姆酒都禁止再蒸餾","Spices contain no volatile aromas":"香料不含易揮發的香氣","It would become too sweet":"它會變得太甜","Redistillation would strip the colour and damage the aged character.":"再蒸餾會去除顏色，並破壞陳年的特色。","That is why natural flavours in spiced rum are probably added by maceration. Spices certainly have volatile aromas, and distillation adds no sugar: if anything, it separates the spirit from sugars.":"所以香料蘭姆酒中的天然風味很可能是以浸漬加入的。香料當然有易揮發的香氣，而蒸餾不會增添糖：它反而是把烈酒與糖分開。","Which two flavours often appear among those declared for spiced rums?":"香料蘭姆酒標明的風味中，哪兩種常出現？","Vanilla and cinnamon":"香草和肉桂","Juniper and coriander":"杜松子和芫荽籽","Aniseed, star anise and liquorice":"茴香籽、八角和甘草","Gentian and quinine":"龍膽和奎寧","Vanilla and cinnamon are common to several spiced rum recipes.":"香草和肉桂是好幾種香料蘭姆酒配方的共同風味。","Full recipes stay secret, but these two flavours are often declared. Juniper and coriander point to gin, aniseed and liquorice to pastis, gentian and quinine to bitters.":"完整的配方是保密的，但這兩種風味常被標明。杜松子和芫荽籽指向琴酒，茴香籽和甘草指向 pastis，龍膽和奎寧指向苦味酒。","Which statement describes traditional Eastern European flavoured vodka?":"哪一項描述了傳統的東歐調味伏特加？","Flavoured for centuries, usually by maceration":"已調味數百年，通常以浸漬進行","A recent invention based on artificial fruit and candy flavours":"以人工水果和糖果香料為基礎的近代發明","Always redistilled in vacuum stills":"一律用真空蒸餾器再蒸餾","Flavoured only with juniper":"只用杜松子調味","Honey, fruit and spices have been used for centuries, nearly always by maceration.":"蜂蜜、水果和香料已經使用了數百年，幾乎都是以浸漬進行。","The traditional version is old; the boom in modern, sometimes artificial flavours is recent. The vacuum still is a modern technique, and a spirit flavoured mainly with juniper would be a gin.":"傳統的版本很古老；現代風味（有時是人工的）的熱潮則是近年的事。真空蒸餾器是現代技術，而主要以杜松子調味的烈酒會是琴酒。","How do premium flavoured-vodka producers usually work?":"高級調味伏特加的生產者通常怎麼做？","They macerate, then redistil":"先浸漬，再重新蒸餾","They buy ready-made artificial flavours and blend them in":"購買現成的人工香料並調入","They age the vodka in cask":"把伏特加桶陳","They add colouring only":"只添加色素","They work with the raw ingredient: maceration in neutral spirit, then redistillation.":"他們使用原始材料：在中性烈酒中浸漬，再進行再蒸餾。","This gives pure, precise fruit or botanical flavours. Artificial or ready-made flavourings are typical of inexpensive brands; cask ageing or colouring alone do not give a flavoured vodka its flavour.":"這樣能得到純淨、精確的水果或植物風味。人工或現成的香料是平價品牌的典型做法；只靠桶陳或色素無法賦予調味伏特加風味。","Which compound gives pastis, ouzo and raki their characteristic taste?":"哪一種化合物賦予 pastis、ouzo 和 raki 特有的味道？","Anethole":"茴香腦（anethole）","Vanillin extracted from toasted oak":"從烘烤橡木萃取的香草醛","Anethole is the compound shared by all aniseed spirits.":"茴香腦是所有茴香烈酒共有的化合物。","It comes mainly from aniseed, fennel and star anise. Quinine is a bittering agent typical of bitters; vanillin and tannin are linked to wood, whereas these spirits are normally unaged.":"它主要來自茴香籽、茴香和八角。奎寧是苦味酒典型的苦味劑；香草醛和單寧與木頭有關，而這些烈酒通常不經陳年。","A customer adds water to a pastis and it turns cloudy. What is this called?":"一位顧客在 pastis 中加水，結果變混濁了。這叫做什麼？","Louching":"乳濁現象（louching）","Refermentation in bottle":"瓶中再發酵","Precipitation of artificial colours":"人工色素沉澱","With water, anethole comes out of solution and makes the liquid opaque: this is louching.":"加水後，茴香腦從溶液中析出，讓液體變得不透明：這就是乳濁現象（louching）。","It is a normal, expected sign and part of the serving ritual, not a fault. Oxygen, yeast and colourings have nothing to do with it: the cause is anethole, which dissolves in alcohol but not in water.":"這是正常、預期中的現象，也是飲用儀式的一部分，不是缺陷。氧氣、酵母和色素都與此無關：原因是茴香腦，它溶於酒精而不溶於水。","Which ingredient must pastis contain, as well as aniseed, fennel and star anise?":"除了茴香籽、茴香和八角，pastis 還必須含有哪一種材料？","Juniper berries":"杜松子","Bitter orange peel and gentian root":"苦橙皮和龍膽根","Pastis must include liquorice.":"Pastis 必須含有甘草。","Wormwood is the plant that defines absinthe, not pastis. Juniper is the compulsory ingredient of gin, while bitter orange and gentian are typical of bitters.":"苦艾是定義苦艾酒的植物，不是 pastis 的。杜松子是琴酒的強制材料，苦橙和龍膽則是苦味酒的典型原料。","Which difference between absinthe and pastis is correct?":"關於苦艾酒和 pastis 的差別，下列哪一項正確？","Absinthe is not sweetened before bottling":"苦艾酒裝瓶前不加糖","Absinthe must contain liquorice, while pastis need not":"苦艾酒必須含甘草，pastis 則不必","Absinthe is aged in cask":"苦艾酒經過桶陳","Absinthe never louches":"苦艾酒從不出現乳濁現象","Pastis must be sweetened; absinthe is sweetened to taste by the drinker.":"Pastis 必須加糖；苦艾酒則由飲用者依口味自行加糖。","The other key difference is wormwood, a floral, bitter plant. Liquorice is compulsory in pastis, not absinthe; both are normally unaged and, since both contain anethole, both turn cloudy with water.":"另一個關鍵差別是苦艾，一種帶花香和苦味的植物。甘草在 pastis 中是強制的，苦艾酒則不是；兩者通常都不經陳年，而且因為都含有茴香腦，加水都會變混濁。","Why is absinthe's high bottling strength considered a distraction?":"為什麼說苦艾酒很高的裝瓶濃度容易讓人誤解？","It is drunk diluted to wine strength":"它是稀釋到葡萄酒的濃度來喝的","The alcohol almost entirely evaporates once the bottle is opened":"開瓶後酒精幾乎全部蒸發","It is actually weaker than wine":"它其實比葡萄酒淡","Added sugar lowers its strength":"添加的糖降低了它的濃度","Served as intended, with water, it is no stronger than a glass of wine.":"依應有的方式加水飲用時，它不比一杯葡萄酒烈。","Its reputation as a dangerously strong drink ignores how it is served. In the bottle it really is very strong and does not lose alcohol on opening; any sugar the drinker adds does not change that.":"說它是危險烈性飲料的名聲，忽略了它的飲用方式。在瓶中它確實非常烈，開瓶後也不會失去酒精；飲用者加的糖不會改變這一點。","Where is a bitter's bitterness detected during tasting?":"品飲時，苦味酒的苦味在哪裡察覺到？","On the nose, before even tasting the spirit":"在香氣中，還沒品嚐烈酒之前","In the colour":"在顏色中","Only in the finish, never on the tongue":"只在餘韻中，舌頭上從來沒有","Bitterness is a taste detected by the tongue, so only on the palate.":"苦味是由舌頭察覺的味覺，所以只在口中。","On the nose you pick up the botanical aromas, but not bitterness itself. Colour says nothing about taste, and the finish is still perceived on the tongue.":"在香氣中你聞到的是植物香氣，而不是苦味本身。顏色與味道無關，餘韻也仍然是在舌頭上感受的。","Which category of bitters is highly concentrated and used in dashes in cocktails?":"哪一類苦味酒高度濃縮，在調酒中以滴數使用？","Aperitif bitters":"開胃苦味酒","After-dinner digestif bitters":"餐後的消化苦味酒","Sweet, low-strength herbal liqueurs":"甜而低酒精的草本利口酒","Cocktail bitters are strong and concentrated, designed as a seasoning.":"調酒用苦精濃烈而濃縮，是設計來當調味料的。","They are never drunk on their own. Aperitif bitters are sweeter and lengthened in long drinks; digestifs are drunk after a meal, often neat. A sweet, light liqueur is the opposite of cocktail bitters.":"它們從不單獨飲用。開胃苦味酒較甜，並在長飲中拉長；消化苦味酒在餐後飲用，常是純飲。甜而清淡的利口酒則與調酒用苦精相反。","A customer wants a bitter to drink before dinner with soda and ice. Which style fits best?":"一位顧客想在晚餐前喝一杯加蘇打水和冰塊的苦味酒。哪一種類型最合適？","An aperitif bitter":"開胃苦味酒","A high-strength cocktail bitters, served neat":"高濃度的調酒用苦精，純飲","An undiluted absinthe":"未稀釋的苦艾酒","Aperitif bitters, colourful and balanced by sweetness, are made for long drinks.":"開胃苦味酒色彩鮮豔，並以甜味取得平衡，是為長飲而生的。","Cocktail bitters are far too concentrated to drink this way, and absinthe should always be diluted with water. A cream liqueur is not a bitter and is not designed for a soda aperitif.":"調酒用苦精太過濃縮，不能這樣喝，苦艾酒則一定要加水稀釋。奶油利口酒不是苦味酒，也不是為加蘇打水的開胃酒設計的。","What does the term 'botanicals' usually refer to?":"「botanicals」（植物性原料）這個術語通常指什麼？","Juniper berries only":"只有杜松子","Artificial flavourings approved by law":"法律核准的人工香料","Malted grains used for fermentation":"用來發酵的麥芽穀物","There is no universal definition, but the term covers the wide range of herbs and spices distillers use.":"沒有通用的定義，但這個術語涵蓋蒸餾師使用的各式各樣香草和香料。","Juniper is just one botanical among many. Artificial flavourings are man-made, so they are not botanicals. Malted grains are raw materials for fermentation, not flavours added to a spirit.":"杜松子只是眾多植物性原料中的一種。人工香料是人造的，所以不是植物性原料。麥芽穀物是發酵的原料，不是加進烈酒的風味。","Why is a high-strength rectified spirit often diluted before maceration?":"為什麼高濃度的精餾烈酒在浸漬前常先稀釋？","Too much alcohol extracts unwanted flavours":"酒精太多會萃取出不想要的風味","To meet the legal minimum bottling strength":"為了符合法定的最低裝瓶濃度","Because water adds colour to the botanicals":"因為水會為植物性原料增添顏色","So the product can later be called a distillate":"這樣產品之後才能稱為餾出液","If the alcohol is too strong, maceration also pulls out undesirable flavours.":"酒精太烈時，浸漬也會把不好的風味帶出來。","Final strength is adjusted at the end, not before maceration. Water adds no colour: colour comes from the botanicals themselves. Distillate is the name for a spirit flavoured by redistillation, not maceration.":"最終的濃度是在最後調整的，不是在浸漬之前。水不增添顏色：顏色來自植物性原料本身。餾出液是以再蒸餾調味的烈酒的名稱，不是浸漬。","A producer wants more flavour from a maceration without making it longer. What can be done?":"一位生產者想在不延長時間的情況下，從浸漬得到更多風味。可以怎麼做？","Apply some heat":"加一些熱","Chill the liquid below freezing":"把液體降到冰點以下","Add sugar before starting the maceration":"開始浸漬前加糖","Filter it several times through activated charcoal":"用活性碳過濾好幾次","Heat increases the amount of flavour extracted from the botanicals.":"熱會增加從植物性原料萃取的風味量。","Cold slows extraction rather than speeding it up. Sugar sweetens; it does not extract. Charcoal filtration removes flavour and colour, the exact opposite of the goal.":"低溫會減緩萃取，而不是加快。糖是增甜的，不能萃取。木炭過濾會去除風味和顏色，與目標恰恰相反。","What can maceration NOT do, unlike distillation?":"與蒸餾不同，浸漬做不到什麼？","Isolate particular aromas":"分離出特定的香氣","Extract colour from botanicals":"從植物性原料萃取顏色","Extract a broad range of flavours":"萃取範圍廣泛的風味","Last from hours to months":"持續幾小時到幾個月","Maceration extracts everything together: it cannot separate one aroma from the rest.":"浸漬把所有東西一起萃取出來：它無法把某一種香氣與其他的分開。","Extracting colour and a fuller range of flavours is exactly maceration's strength. Its variable length is also one of its features. Selecting individual aromas needs distillation and its cuts.":"萃取顏色和更完整的風味正是浸漬的強項。時間長短不一也是它的特點之一。挑選個別香氣需要蒸餾和切取。","In the trade, a flavoured spirit called a 'distillate' has been flavoured how?":"在業界，稱為「distillate」（餾出液）的調味烈酒是怎麼調味的？","By redistillation":"以再蒸餾","By simple maceration":"以單純的浸漬","By cold-adding artificial flavours":"以冷混方式加入人工香料","By ageing in previously used casks":"在用過的桶中陳年","Distillate means a spirit flavoured by redistillation with fruit or botanicals.":"餾出液指的是與水果或植物性原料一起再蒸餾而調味的烈酒。","A spirit flavoured by maceration is instead called a tincture. Adding artificial flavours is cold compounding. Cask ageing adds flavour but does not earn the name distillate.":"以浸漬調味的烈酒則稱為酊劑。加入人工香料是冷混法。桶陳會增添風味，但不能因此稱為餾出液。","A brand does not handle botanicals itself but buys ready-made natural flavourings. What does it then do?":"一個品牌不自己處理植物性原料，而是購買現成的天然香料。接下來它怎麼做？","Blends them with its chosen alcohol":"把它們與選用的酒精調和","Must redistil them in a pot still":"必須用壺式蒸餾器把它們再蒸餾","Ages them for two years in oak":"在橡木桶中陳年兩年","Has to sell the result as an artificial product":"必須把成品當作人工產品販售","Natural flavourings bought from specialist producers are simply blended with the alcohol.":"向專業生產商購買的天然香料，只要與酒精調和即可。","There is no obligation to redistil or age bought-in flavourings. They remain natural, because they come from botanicals, even if prepared by others. It is a shortcut compared with working the plants directly.":"沒有義務把外購的香料再蒸餾或陳年。它們仍然是天然的，因為來自植物性原料，即使是別人製備的。與直接處理植物相比，這是一條捷徑。","How is an artificial flavour defined?":"人工香料的定義是什麼？","Man-made, but similar to a flavour found in nature":"人造的，但與自然界中的風味相似","Extracted from a plant by distillation":"以蒸餾從植物萃取的","Any flavour bought from another producer":"任何向其他生產者購買的香料","A flavour with no equivalent in nature":"在自然界中沒有對應物的風味","It is made by people but resembles flavours found in nature.":"它是人製造的，但與自然界中的風味相似。","An extract distilled from a plant is a natural flavour. Natural flavours can also be bought from others, so buying them does not make them artificial. Artificial flavours imitate natural ones.":"從植物蒸餾出來的萃取物是天然香料。天然香料也可以向別人購買，所以購買並不會讓它變成人工的。人工香料是模仿天然香料的。","When does a flavoured spirit need no blending before sale?":"什麼情況下，調味烈酒在販售前不需要調和？","When only one technique is used":"只使用一種技術時","When the base is an aged spirit":"基酒是陳年烈酒時","Never: blending is always compulsory":"沒有這種情況：調和一律是強制的","When maceration and redistillation are combined":"結合浸漬和再蒸餾時","With a single technique the product is ready straight away; several techniques mean blending the different spirits.":"只用一種技術，產品馬上就完成；用數種技術就要把不同的烈酒調和起來。","Combining techniques produces several flavoured spirits to bring together, so it is exactly when blending is needed. Blending is not a universal obligation. The type of base does not decide whether blending is required.":"結合不同技術會產生數種要合在一起的調味烈酒，所以正是需要調和的時候。調和不是普遍的義務。基酒的類型不決定是否需要調和。","A very inexpensive flavoured vodka: which flavouring method is most likely?":"一款非常便宜的調味伏特加：最可能用哪一種調味方式？","Artificial or ready-made natural flavours":"人工香料或現成的天然香料","Fruit maceration followed by redistillation":"水果浸漬後再蒸餾","Vacuum distillation of each fruit on its own":"把每種水果單獨真空蒸餾","Ageing with the fruit in oak casks":"與水果一起放在橡木桶中陳年","Cheap brands usually add artificial flavours or natural ones prepared by others.":"便宜的品牌通常添加人工香料，或別人製備的天然香料。","Macerating then redistilling is the premium method, used by brands that work fruit and botanicals directly. Separate vacuum distillation is even more costly. Oak ageing is not a typical method for flavoured vodka.":"先浸漬再蒸餾是高級的做法，為直接處理水果和植物性原料的品牌所用。分開做真空蒸餾成本更高。橡木桶陳年不是調味伏特加的典型做法。","A vodka flavoured with bison grass belongs to which tradition?":"用野牛草調味的伏特加屬於哪一種傳統？","Modern vodkas made with artificial flavours":"用人工香料做的現代伏特加","Mediterranean aniseed spirits":"地中海的茴香烈酒","Bison grass is the best-known surviving example of a traditional Eastern European recipe.":"野牛草是流傳至今的傳統東歐配方中最知名的例子。","In Eastern Europe vodkas have been flavoured for centuries with honey, fruit, spices and herbs, usually by maceration. Modern flavoured vodkas are a recent phenomenon. Aniseed spirits and bitters are different families with other key botanicals.":"在東歐，伏特加用蜂蜜、水果、香料和香草調味已有數百年，通常以浸漬進行。現代的調味伏特加是近年的現象。茴香烈酒和苦味酒是不同的家族，有其他關鍵的植物性原料。","Which statement about modern flavoured vodkas is correct?":"關於現代的調味伏特加，下列哪一項正確？","They are a recent boom, with flavours from vanilla to chilli":"它們是近年的熱潮，風味從香草到辣椒都有","They are made only with honey and spices":"它們只用蜂蜜和香料製作","Few brands produce even one":"很少有品牌推出，連一款都沒有","They must be aged in oak":"必須在橡木桶中陳年","The growth of flavoured vodkas is recent, and flavours range from vanilla and fruit to pepper and chilli.":"調味伏特加的成長是近年的事，風味從香草、水果到胡椒和辣椒都有。","Honey and spices are more typical of the traditional recipes. Almost every vodka brand has at least one flavoured version. There is no oak-ageing requirement.":"蜂蜜和香料比較是傳統配方的典型。幾乎每個伏特加品牌都至少有一款調味版本。沒有橡木桶陳年的要求。","A customer orders raki. Which country does it traditionally come from?":"一位顧客點了 raki。它傳統上來自哪個國家？","Raki is the typical aniseed spirit of Turkey.":"Raki 是土耳其的代表性茴香烈酒。","Greece is the home of ouzo, and France of pastis and absinthe. All share the anethole flavour and turn cloudy with water. Knowing the country–spirit pairs helps a lot in exam questions.":"希臘是 ouzo 的故鄉，法國是 pastis 和苦艾酒的故鄉。它們都有茴香腦的風味，加水都會變混濁。熟記國家與烈酒的配對，對考題很有幫助。","Which plants are the main sources of anethole?":"哪些植物是茴香腦的主要來源？","Aniseed, fennel and star anise":"茴香籽、茴香和八角","Wormwood, gentian and quinine":"苦艾、龍膽和奎寧","Liquorice, cinnamon and cloves":"甘草、肉桂和丁香","Juniper, coriander and angelica":"杜松子、芫荽籽和歐白芷根","Aniseed, fennel and star anise are the main sources of anethole.":"茴香籽、茴香和八角是茴香腦的主要來源。","Gentian and quinine are bittering botanicals typical of bitters. Liquorice is compulsory in pastis but is not the main source of anethole. Juniper, coriander and angelica are the aromatic backbone of gin.":"龍膽和奎寧是苦味酒典型的苦味植物性原料。甘草在 pastis 中是強制的，但不是茴香腦的主要來源。杜松子、芫荽籽和歐白芷根是琴酒的香氣骨幹。","Which statement about aniseed spirits is correct?":"關於茴香烈酒，下列哪一項正確？","They are normally unaged":"它們通常不經陳年","They usually start from a grape brandy":"它們通常從葡萄白蘭地開始","They may only be coloured naturally":"它們只能用天然色素上色","They are nearly always drunk neat, without water":"它們幾乎都是純飲，不加水","Aniseed spirits are normally unaged.":"茴香烈酒通常不經陳年。","The typical base is neutral spirit, not grape brandy. Colour usually comes from both natural and artificial colourings. They are served heavily diluted, and turning cloudy with water is part of the ritual.":"典型的基酒是中性烈酒，不是葡萄白蘭地。顏色通常同時來自天然和人工色素。它們是大幅稀釋後飲用的，加水變混濁是儀式的一部分。","What colour is pastis normally?":"Pastis 通常是什麼顏色？","Yellow, green or green-brown":"黃色、綠色或綠棕色","Always completely colourless":"一律完全無色","Deep red, like an aperitif bitter":"深紅色，像開胃苦味酒","Amber, from ageing in oak":"琥珀色，來自橡木桶陳年","Pastis is normally coloured yellow, green or green-brown.":"Pastis 通常染成黃色、綠色或綠棕色。","Pastis is not colourless: it receives natural and artificial colourings. Bright red is typical of some aperitif bitters. Aniseed spirits are not aged, so the colour does not come from oak.":"Pastis 不是無色的：它添加了天然和人工色素。鮮紅色是某些開胃苦味酒的典型顏色。茴香烈酒不經陳年，所以顏色不是來自橡木。","When tasting a pastis, what sweetness level should be expected?":"品嚐 pastis 時，應該預期什麼甜度？","Medium or sweet":"中等或甜","Dry, like every other spirit":"不甜，和其他所有烈酒一樣","Off-dry at the most":"最多微甜","It varies, because the drinker sweetens it":"不一定，因為由飲用者自己加糖","Pastis must be sweetened, and most are medium or sweet.":"Pastis 必須加糖，大多數是中等或甜。","Added sugar rules out dry and usually off-dry too. The drinker adds water, not sugar: it is absinthe that is sweetened to taste. Liquorice also adds to the sense of sweetness.":"添加的糖排除了不甜，通常也排除微甜。飲用者加的是水，不是糖：依口味加糖的是苦艾酒。甘草也增添了甜感。","Why did pastis become the leading French aniseed spirit?":"為什麼 pastis 成為法國首屈一指的茴香烈酒？","It replaced absinthe when absinthe was banned":"苦艾酒被禁時，它取代了苦艾酒","It is the only aniseed spirit protected by EU law":"它是唯一受歐盟法律保護的茴香烈酒","It contains no sugar and is more popular":"它不含糖，更受歡迎","It is aged longer than ouzo":"它的陳年時間比 ouzo 長","Pastis took the place of absinthe, which was banned for decades from the late nineteenth century.":"苦艾酒自十九世紀末起被禁了數十年，pastis 取代了它的位置。","Pastis is in fact compulsorily sweetened. Aniseed spirits are normally unaged. The history of the absinthe ban is the real reason for pastis's success.":"Pastis 其實是強制加糖的。茴香烈酒通常不經陳年。苦艾酒禁令的歷史才是 pastis 成功的真正原因。","Why is there no guarantee about how an absinthe is made?":"為什麼苦艾酒的製作方式沒有任何保證？","There is no legal definition":"沒有法律定義","It is still banned almost everywhere":"它在幾乎所有地方仍被禁止","Every bottle is home-made":"每一瓶都是自家釀製的","Liquorice rules forbid any definition":"關於甘草的規定讓它無法定義","Absinthe is no longer banned, but the product has no legal definition.":"苦艾酒已不再被禁，但這種產品沒有法律定義。","The ban is in the past, so the second option is false. Absinthe is made in distilleries, not at home. The best, traditional method is similar to pastis, but without sugar and with wormwood.":"禁令已成過去，所以第二個選項是錯的。苦艾酒在蒸餾廠製作，不是在家裡。最好的傳統做法與 pastis 相似，但不加糖，並使用苦艾。","What does the wormwood plant bring to absinthe?":"苦艾這種植物為苦艾酒帶來什麼？","A floral aroma and a bitter taste":"花香和苦味","Sweetness and a red colour":"甜味和紅色","The cloudiness when water is added":"加水時的混濁","Vanilla and cinnamon notes":"香草和肉桂氣息","Wormwood has a distinctly floral aroma and a bitter taste.":"苦艾有鮮明的花香和苦味。","Cloudiness comes from the anethole in aniseed, not from wormwood. Absinthe is not sweetened before bottling. Vanilla and cinnamon are typical of spiced rum.":"混濁來自茴香籽中的茴香腦，不是苦艾。苦艾酒裝瓶前不加糖。香草和肉桂是香料蘭姆酒的典型風味。","Which of these is NOT a typical bittering ingredient in bitters?":"下列哪一項不是苦味酒中典型的苦味材料？","Artichoke":"朝鮮薊","Vanilla gives sweet, warm notes, not bitterness.":"香草帶來甜美、溫暖的氣息，不是苦味。","Quinine, gentian, bitter orange and artichoke are among the most used bittering agents. Bitterness is only noticed on the palate, because the tongue detects it. Sugar and aromatic botanicals then balance it.":"奎寧、龍膽、苦橙和朝鮮薊是最常用的苦味劑。苦味只在口中察覺，因為是由舌頭感知的。糖和芳香的植物性原料再加以平衡。","Why are sugar and other aromatic botanicals added to bitters?":"為什麼苦味酒中要加糖和其他芳香的植物性原料？","To balance the bitterness":"平衡苦味","To raise their alcoholic strength":"提高酒精濃度","So that they turn cloudy with water":"讓它們加水後變混濁","Because the law classes them as liqueurs":"因為法律把它們歸類為利口酒","Sugar and aromatics balance the bitter taste of the main botanicals.":"糖和芳香材料能平衡主要植物性原料的苦味。","Sugar does not raise the strength. Cloudiness is typical of aniseed spirits, not bitters. Bitters are a family of their own, even if some are fairly sweet.":"糖不會提高濃度。混濁是茴香烈酒的典型現象，不是苦味酒。苦味酒自成一個家族，即使有些相當甜。","Which category of bitters usually has pronounced bitterness and flavour and is linked to digestion?":"哪一類苦味酒通常有明顯的苦味和風味，並與消化有關？","Digestif":"消化苦味酒","Aperitif":"開胃苦味酒","Cocktail":"調酒用苦精","Cream liqueur":"奶油利口酒","Digestif bitters began as aids to digestion and are drunk after a meal.":"消化苦味酒最初是用來幫助消化的，在餐後飲用。","Aperitif bitters are brighter and balanced by sweetness, and are drunk long. Cocktail bitters are highly concentrated and used in dashes, not alone. A cream liqueur is not a bitter.":"開胃苦味酒顏色較鮮豔，以甜味取得平衡，做成長飲來喝。調酒用苦精高度濃縮，以滴數使用，不單獨飲用。奶油利口酒不是苦味酒。","Which definition best describes a liqueur?":"哪一項定義最能描述利口酒？","A flavoured, sweetened spirit":"經過調味並加糖的烈酒","An aromatised wine fortified with neutral spirit":"用中性烈酒強化的加味葡萄酒","An aged spirit with no flavourings":"沒有添加香料的陳年烈酒","An unsweetened bitter spirit":"未加糖的苦味烈酒","A liqueur is a flavoured spirit with added sugar.":"利口酒是加了糖的調味烈酒。","A fortified aromatised wine describes vermouth, which is not a liqueur. A spirit without flavourings is not a liqueur, and sweetness is exactly what an unsweetened bitter lacks.":"強化的加味葡萄酒描述的是香艾酒，它不是利口酒。沒有調味的烈酒不是利口酒，而未加糖的苦味酒缺少的正是甜味。","Which sweetness term correctly applies to all liqueurs?":"哪一個甜度術語正確地適用於所有利口酒？","Variable, from dry to sweet depending on the producing country":"不一定，依生產國從不甜到甜都有","All liqueurs, by definition, are described as sweet.":"所有利口酒依定義都描述為甜。","The legal sugar minimum changes from country to country, but the result is always a sweet product. That is why 'dry' or 'off-dry' do not describe a liqueur: those terms suit other spirits.":"法定的最低糖量因國家而異，但成品一定是甜的。所以「不甜」或「微甜」不能用來描述利口酒：這些術語適用於其他烈酒。","Which base spirit do most liqueurs use?":"大多數利口酒使用哪一種基酒？","An oak-aged Cognac":"橡木桶陳年的 Cognac","A dry, high-acid white wine":"不甜、高酸的白葡萄酒","A neutral base lets the added flavours show.":"中性的基酒讓添加的風味展現出來。","Some liqueurs start from Cognac or Scotch, but they are exceptions. Dry white wine is the base of vermouth, which is an aromatised wine, not a liqueur.":"有些利口酒從 Cognac 或 Scotch 開始，但那是例外。不甜的白葡萄酒是香艾酒的基底，而香艾酒是加味葡萄酒，不是利口酒。","Which statement about liqueur bases is true?":"關於利口酒的基酒，下列哪一項正確？","Some start from a characterful spirit":"有些從有個性的烈酒開始","By law they must always start from neutral grain spirit":"依法一律必須從中性穀物烈酒開始","They never use a distilled spirit":"它們從不使用蒸餾烈酒","They must use whisky":"它們必須使用威士忌","There are liqueurs built on Cognac or Scotch whisky.":"有些利口酒建立在 Cognac 或 Scotch 威士忌上。","A neutral base is the most common, but it is not compulsory. A liqueur is by definition a spirit, so a distilled base is always there; whisky is only one possible characterful base.":"中性基酒最常見，但不是強制的。利口酒依定義就是烈酒，所以一定有蒸餾的基酒；威士忌只是可能的有個性基酒之一。","What makes cream liqueurs technically difficult to produce?":"什麼讓奶油利口酒在技術上很難生產？","Stopping the cream forming lumps in the bottle":"防止鮮奶油在瓶中結塊","Achieving a perfectly clear, transparent colour":"做出完全清澈透明的顏色","Reaching at least 40% abv":"達到至少 40% abv","Removing all the sugar":"去除所有的糖","Cream needs complex techniques to stay stable after bottling.":"鮮奶油需要複雜的技術才能在裝瓶後保持穩定。","Cream liqueurs are among the rare opaque alcoholic drinks, so clarity is not a goal. Like all liqueurs they are sweet and may be bottled below the minimum strength of other spirits.":"奶油利口酒是少見的不透明酒精飲料，所以清澈不是目標。和所有利口酒一樣，它們是甜的，並且可以用低於其他烈酒最低濃度的濃度裝瓶。","What makes cream liqueurs almost unique among alcoholic drinks?":"什麼讓奶油利口酒在酒精飲料中幾乎獨一無二？","They are opaque":"它們是不透明的","They contain no sugar":"它們不含糖","They must be aged in oak casks":"它們必須在橡木桶中陳年","They are distilled with milk":"它們與牛奶一起蒸餾","They are among the very few truly opaque alcoholic drinks.":"它們是極少數真正不透明的酒精飲料。","The cream, added and stabilised, makes the liquid non-transparent. Like every liqueur they are sweetened; there is no oak requirement, and the cream is not distilled but incorporated with special techniques.":"加入並經過穩定處理的鮮奶油讓液體不透明。和所有利口酒一樣，它們加了糖；沒有橡木桶的要求，鮮奶油也不是蒸餾的，而是用特殊技術融入的。","An almond liqueur belongs to which flavour group?":"杏仁利口酒屬於哪一個風味類別？","Seed, nut and kernel":"種子、堅果和果核","Herb":"香草","Fresh fruit, such as citrus and berries":"新鮮水果，例如柑橘和莓果","Almond belongs to the seed, nut and kernel group.":"杏仁屬於種子、堅果和果核這一類。","The four useful groups are herb, fruit, seed-nut-kernel and cream. Almond is neither a herb nor a fresh fruit, and without cream the liqueur is not in the cream group.":"四個實用的類別是香草、水果、種子／堅果／果核，以及奶油。杏仁既不是香草，也不是新鮮水果；沒有鮮奶油，這款利口酒就不屬於奶油類。","Why do many liqueurs have very vivid colours?":"為什麼許多利口酒的顏色非常鮮豔？","Artificial colourings are widely used":"人工色素使用得很普遍","Because of long ageing in new oak casks":"因為在新橡木桶中長期陳年","Because sugar changes the colour of alcohol":"因為糖會改變酒精的顏色","Because of vacuum distillation":"因為真空蒸餾","Artificial colours are widespread and explain the bright shades.":"人工色素很普遍，這解釋了鮮豔的色調。","Colour is optional, but when present it is often artificial because natural colour is unstable. Oak gives amber tones, not blue or green, and neither sugar nor distillation creates bright colours.":"顏色不是必要的，但有顏色時常是人工的，因為天然顏色不穩定。橡木帶來的是琥珀色調，不是藍色或綠色，糖和蒸餾也都不會產生鮮豔的顏色。","Which statement about liqueur strength is correct?":"關於利口酒的濃度，下列哪一項正確？","It can be lower than other spirits":"可以比其他烈酒低","It must be at least 40% abv worldwide, without exception":"全世界都必須至少 40% abv，沒有例外","It is always above 50% abv":"一律高於 50% abv","It is the same as wine":"和葡萄酒相同","Liqueurs may be bottled below the legal minimum for other spirits.":"利口酒可以用低於其他烈酒法定最低限度的濃度裝瓶。","Other spirits usually have a minimum of 37.5% abv (EU) or 40% (USA); liqueurs are an exception. No rule puts them above 50%, and they are not tied to wine strength.":"其他烈酒的最低濃度通常是 37.5% abv（歐盟）或 40%（美國）；利口酒是例外。沒有規定要它們高於 50%，它們也與葡萄酒的濃度無關。","In a bar, which opened bottle will lose freshness fastest?":"在酒吧裡，哪一瓶開過的酒最快失去新鮮度？","A low-strength liqueur":"低濃度的利口酒","A London Dry Gin just opened and still nearly full":"剛開瓶、幾乎還是滿的 London Dry Gin","A high-strength whisky":"高濃度的威士忌","After opening, oxidation is faster in lower-strength liqueurs.":"開瓶後，低濃度利口酒的氧化較快。","Once opened, all spirits react slowly with oxygen, but lower-strength liqueurs suffer sooner. The process also speeds up once the bottle is more than half empty, not when it is nearly full.":"開瓶後，所有烈酒都會與氧氣緩慢反應，但低濃度的利口酒更早受影響。酒瓶空了一半以上時這個過程也會加快，而不是幾乎還滿的時候。","What distinguishes a liqueur from a gin or a dry flavoured vodka?":"利口酒與琴酒或不甜的調味伏特加有什麼區別？","Added sugar":"添加的糖","The presence of botanicals":"含有植物性原料","Use of a pot still for redistillation":"使用壺式蒸餾器再蒸餾","A clear colour":"清澈的顏色","Gin and flavoured vodka are flavoured like liqueurs, but only liqueurs are sweetened.":"琴酒和調味伏特加和利口酒一樣經過調味，但只有利口酒加糖。","Botanicals and redistillation are found in gin too, so they do not separate the categories. Colour is not a criterion either: many liqueurs are coloured, but some are clear.":"琴酒中也有植物性原料和再蒸餾，所以它們無法區分這些類別。顏色也不是標準：許多利口酒有顏色，但有些是清澈的。","Which statement about the colour of liqueurs is correct?":"關於利口酒的顏色，下列哪一項正確？","It is optional":"它不是必要的","It is required by law in every producing country":"每個生產國的法律都要求","It must come only from plants":"只能來自植物","It must come only from cask wood":"只能來自桶的木頭","Sugar is compulsory, colour is not: liqueurs may or may not be coloured.":"糖是強制的，顏色則不是：利口酒可以有顏色，也可以沒有。","When present, colour is often artificial, because plant-derived colour is unstable. There is no requirement for natural colour or for time in wood.":"有顏色時常是人工的，因為來自植物的顏色不穩定。沒有規定要用天然顏色，或要在木桶中存放。","What is the minimum amount of sugar a liqueur must contain?":"利口酒至少必須含有多少糖？","It varies from country to country":"因國家而異","The same figure worldwide":"全世界都是同一個數字","None: sugar is optional":"沒有：糖不是必要的","Only the natural sugar of the fruit used":"只要所用水果的天然糖分","The minimum added sugar varies by country, but all liqueurs end up sweet.":"添加糖的最低量因國家而異，但所有利口酒最後都是甜的。","There is no single worldwide threshold. Added sugar is exactly what defines a liqueur, so it is not optional. The fruit's natural sugar is not enough: liqueurs are sweetened.":"沒有全世界統一的門檻。添加的糖正是利口酒的定義，所以不是可有可無的。水果的天然糖分不夠：利口酒是另外加糖的。","A liqueur flavoured mainly with orange peel belongs to which group?":"主要以橙皮調味的利口酒屬於哪一類？","Citrus is fruit, so an orange liqueur is a fruit liqueur.":"柑橘是水果，所以柳橙利口酒是水果利口酒。","The herb group covers liqueurs based on aromatic plants, often with complex recipes. The seed group includes almonds, for example, not peels. Cream is a separate ingredient that makes the liqueur opaque.":"香草類涵蓋以芳香植物為基礎的利口酒，配方常很複雜。種子類包括杏仁等，不包括果皮。奶油則是讓利口酒不透明的另一種材料。","A liqueur has a secret recipe with dozens of aromatic plants. Which group does it go in?":"一款利口酒有用了數十種芳香植物的祕密配方。它屬於哪一類？","A liqueur built on many aromatic plants belongs to the herb group.":"建立在許多芳香植物上的利口酒屬於香草類。","Complex, secret recipes are typical of herb liqueurs. Fruit and seed point instead to one clear dominant flavour. Cream has nothing to do with the number of plants.":"複雜、祕密的配方是草本利口酒的典型。水果和種子則指向一種清楚的主導風味。奶油與植物的數量無關。","Which group of liqueurs is the most recent invention?":"哪一類利口酒是最晚出現的？","Cream liqueurs":"奶油利口酒","Herb liqueurs":"草本利口酒","Fruit liqueurs":"水果利口酒","Kernel and nut liqueurs":"果核和堅果利口酒","Using cream in liqueurs is a fairly modern invention, dating from the 1970s.":"在利口酒中使用鮮奶油是相當現代的發明，始於 1970 年代。","Herb, fruit and nut liqueurs have existed for much longer. Cream needed complex techniques to stop it forming lumps in the bottle. That is why it arrived late.":"草本、水果和堅果利口酒存在的時間長得多。鮮奶油需要複雜的技術來防止它在瓶中結塊。所以它出現得晚。","Which spirit could serve as a characterful base for a liqueur?":"哪一種烈酒可以作為利口酒有個性的基酒？","Cognac":"Cognac","A 96% neutral spirit":"96% 的中性烈酒","A charcoal-filtered vodka":"經木炭過濾的伏特加","A vermouth base wine":"香艾酒的基酒","Some liqueurs start from characterful spirits such as Cognac or Scotch whisky.":"有些利口酒從 Cognac 或 Scotch 威士忌這類有個性的烈酒開始。","Neutral spirit and filtered vodka are neutral bases, the most common but not characterful. Wine is not a spirit and does not serve as a liqueur base. A characterful base adds its own aromas to those of the botanicals.":"中性烈酒和過濾過的伏特加是中性基酒，最常見，但沒有個性。葡萄酒不是烈酒，不能作為利口酒的基酒。有個性的基酒會把自己的香氣加到植物性原料的香氣上。","What limits are there on the flavours a liqueur producer can use?":"利口酒生產者可以使用的風味有什麼限制？","No limits":"沒有限制","Only fruit grown in the region":"只能用當地種植的水果","At most three flavours per recipe":"每個配方最多三種風味","Natural flavours only, never artificial ones":"只能用天然風味，絕不用人工的","There are no limits on the possible flavours in a liqueur.":"利口酒可用的風味沒有限制。","Some producers focus on one flavour, others use complex, secret recipes. There are no geographical or numerical restrictions. Artificial colourings are also widespread, so the last option is wrong.":"有些生產者專注於一種風味，另一些使用複雜的祕密配方。沒有地理或數量上的限制。人工色素也很普遍，所以最後一個選項是錯的。","Compared with the minimum strength of most spirits (37.5% in the EU, 40% in the USA), what applies to liqueurs?":"與大多數烈酒的最低濃度（歐盟 37.5%、美國 40%）相比，利口酒適用什麼規定？","They may be bottled lower":"可以用更低的濃度裝瓶","They must exceed 45%":"必須超過 45%","They have exactly the same minimums":"最低限度完全相同","They cannot exceed 15%, like fortified wines":"不能超過 15%，像加烈酒一樣","Liqueurs may be bottled at a lower strength than other spirits.":"利口酒可以用比其他烈酒低的濃度裝瓶。","There is neither a high-strength requirement nor a 15% ceiling. Being able to go below the spirit minimums is precisely the difference. A practical consequence: opened low-strength bottles deteriorate sooner.":"既沒有高濃度的要求，也沒有 15% 的上限。能低於烈酒的最低限度正是差別所在。實務上的結果是：開過的低濃度酒瓶更早變質。","Why do most liqueurs start from neutral spirit?":"為什麼大多數利口酒從中性烈酒開始？","So the added flavours stand out":"讓添加的風味突顯出來","Because the law bans every other base":"因為法律禁止其他所有基酒","Because it gives a natural amber colour":"因為它帶來天然的琥珀色","A neutral backdrop lets the botanicals and fruit show without competition.":"中性的背景讓植物性原料和水果在沒有競爭的情況下展現。","Some liqueurs use characterful bases, so there is no ban. Neutral spirit contains no sugar: sweetness is added afterwards. It is colourless, so it gives no amber colour.":"有些利口酒使用有個性的基酒，所以沒有禁令。中性烈酒不含糖：甜味是之後添加的。它是無色的，所以不帶來琥珀色。","In a tasting, how is the colour intensity of a cream liqueur described?":"在品飲中，奶油利口酒的顏色深淺怎麼描述？","Water-white":"清澈如水","You cannot see through a cream liqueur: it is opaque.":"奶油利口酒是看不透的：它不透明。","Water-white describes clear spirits such as vodka. Pale and medium apply to coloured but see-through spirits, for example coloured by oak or caramel. Cream liqueurs are among the very few truly opaque alcoholic drinks.":"清澈如水描述的是伏特加這類清澈的烈酒。淺和中等適用於有顏色但看得透的烈酒，例如因橡木或焦糖色而有顏色的。奶油利口酒是極少數真正不透明的酒精飲料。","Which of these is NOT one of the four main liqueur groups?":"下列哪一項不屬於利口酒的四個主要類別？","Peat and smoke":"泥煤和煙燻","The four groups are herb, fruit, seed/nut/kernel and cream.":"四個類別是香草、水果、種子／堅果／果核，以及奶油。","Peat and smoke are aromas linked to how some whiskies are made, not a liqueur group. Grouping liqueurs by main flavour helps compare them. Fruit is the group missing from the wrong options.":"泥煤和煙燻是與某些威士忌製法有關的香氣，不是利口酒的類別。依主要風味把利口酒分類，有助於互相比較。水果是錯誤選項中沒有出現的那一類。","Which statement about liqueur recipes is correct?":"關於利口酒的配方，下列哪一項正確？","Some focus on one flavour, others on complex secret recipes":"有些專注於一種風味，另一些是複雜的祕密配方","They must be published on the label":"必須公布在酒標上","They always use at least twenty botanicals":"一律使用至少二十種植物性原料","They are fixed by law for each group":"由法律為每一類固定下來","Recipes range from a single flavour to complex blends, often kept secret.":"配方從單一風味到複雜的調和都有，常是保密的。","Recipes are neither public nor fixed by law. There is no minimum number of botanicals. Near-total freedom explains the huge variety of liqueurs.":"配方既不公開，也不由法律固定。沒有植物性原料的最低數量。近乎完全的自由解釋了利口酒的多樣性。","Which techniques can be used to flavour a liqueur?":"哪些技術可以用來為利口酒調味？","Maceration, redistillation or added flavourings":"浸漬、再蒸餾或添加香料","Only cask ageing":"只能桶陳","Only redistillation, as with London Dry Gin":"只能再蒸餾，和 London Dry Gin 一樣","Only fermenting fruit with sugar":"只能把水果與糖一起發酵","Liqueurs use the same techniques as other flavoured spirits, often combined.":"利口酒使用與其他調味烈酒相同的技術，常結合使用。","Ageing is not the main way to flavour a liqueur. The redistillation-only rule applies to London Dry Gin, not liqueurs. A liqueur starts from a finished spirit, not from fermenting fruit.":"陳年不是為利口酒調味的主要方式。只靠再蒸餾的規定適用於 London Dry Gin，不是利口酒。利口酒從成品烈酒開始，不是從發酵水果開始。","A liqueur is flavoured with apricot kernels. Which group does it belong to?":"一款利口酒用杏桃核調味。它屬於哪一類？","Fruit, because the apricot is a fruit":"水果，因為杏桃是水果","It is the kernel, not the flesh, that is used: the liqueur belongs to the seed, nut and kernel group.":"使用的是果核，不是果肉：這款利口酒屬於種子、堅果和果核這一類。","It is a trap: the apricot is a fruit, but the kernel has an almond-like flavour, unlike the flesh. The group depends on which part of the plant gives the flavour. Herb and cream do not apply.":"這是陷阱：杏桃是水果，但果核有類似杏仁的風味，與果肉不同。類別取決於風味來自植物的哪個部分。香草和奶油都不適用。","What is the point of grouping liqueurs by main flavour?":"依主要風味把利口酒分類，目的是什麼？","It helps compare different styles":"有助於比較不同的風格","It sets the legal minimum strength":"決定法定的最低濃度","It decides how much sugar must legally be added":"決定依法必須加多少糖","It shows which base spirit was used":"表示用了哪一種基酒","Grouping by flavour is a practical tool for comparing and contrasting styles.":"依風味分類是比較和對照風格的實用工具。","Strength and minimum sugar depend on national laws, not on the group. The base, neutral or characterful, is a separate choice. The group only describes the dominant flavour.":"濃度和最低糖量取決於各國法律，不是類別。基酒是中性還是有個性，是另一項選擇。類別只描述主導的風味。","A liqueur is flavoured mainly with mint. Which group does it belong to?":"一款利口酒主要以薄荷調味。它屬於哪一類？","Mint is a herb, so the liqueur goes in the herb group.":"薄荷是香草，所以這款利口酒屬於香草類。","The fruit group covers fruits and peels, such as orange. Seed, nut and kernel includes almonds and apricot kernels, for example. The cream group is easy to spot by its opaque look.":"水果類涵蓋水果和果皮，例如柳橙。種子、堅果和果核類包括杏仁和杏桃核等。奶油類從不透明的外觀就很容易認出來。","A liqueur brand does not handle any botanicals itself. How does it get its flavours?":"一個利口酒品牌完全不自己處理植物性原料。它的風味從哪裡來？","It buys ready-made flavourings from specialist suppliers":"向專業供應商購買現成的香料","It ages neutral spirit for a long time in new barrels":"把中性烈酒放在新桶中長期陳年","It gets all the flavour from the added sugar and colouring":"所有風味都來自添加的糖和色素","It ferments fruit together with neutral spirit directly in the bottle":"讓水果與中性烈酒直接在瓶中一起發酵","Some brands buy in pre-prepared natural or artificial flavourings and blend them with their alcohol.":"有些品牌買進預先製備的天然或人工香料，再與自己的酒精調和。","The alternatives are macerating or redistilling the botanicals in-house. Barrel ageing is not part of typical liqueur production. Sugar brings sweetness and colouring brings colour, not herb or fruit flavours. No fermentation happens in a bottle of spirit.":"其他做法是自行浸漬或再蒸餾植物性原料。桶陳不屬於典型的利口酒生產。糖帶來甜味，色素帶來顏色，而不是香草或水果風味。烈酒的瓶中不會發酵。","A producer makes a honey-and-herb liqueur on a Scotch whisky base. What kind of base is this?":"一位生產者用 Scotch 威士忌作基酒，製作蜂蜜草本利口酒。這是哪一種基酒？","A characterful base":"有個性的基酒","A neutral base":"中性基酒","A fortified-wine base, as for vermouth":"加烈酒基底，和香艾酒一樣","A banned base, because liqueurs must start from neutral spirit":"被禁止的基酒，因為利口酒必須從中性烈酒開始","A Scotch whisky brings its own aromas: it is a characterful base, like Cognac for some orange liqueurs.":"Scotch 威士忌帶來自己的香氣：它是有個性的基酒，就像某些柳橙利口酒用的 Cognac。","Most liqueurs start from neutral spirit so the added flavours stand out, but that is not a rule. Fortified wine is the base of aromatised wines, not liqueurs. Here the whisky's flavour joins those of honey and herbs.":"大多數利口酒從中性烈酒開始，讓添加的風味突顯出來，但那不是規定。加烈酒是加味葡萄酒的基底，不是利口酒的。在這裡，威士忌的風味與蜂蜜和香草的風味結合在一起。","Which of these products can be classed as a liqueur?":"下列哪一種產品可以歸類為利口酒？","A sweetened cherry spirit at 20% abv":"20% abv 的加糖櫻桃烈酒","A dry, unsweetened cherry spirit at 40% abv":"40% abv、不甜且未加糖的櫻桃烈酒","A sweetened white wine with botanicals and wormwood at 16% abv":"16% abv、加了植物性原料和苦艾的加糖白葡萄酒","A colourless spirit redistilled with juniper berries and no added sugar":"與杜松子一起再蒸餾、未加糖的無色烈酒","A liqueur is a flavoured, sweetened spirit, and it may be bottled below the minimum strength of other spirits.":"利口酒是經過調味並加糖的烈酒，可以用低於其他烈酒最低濃度的濃度裝瓶。","The dry cherry spirit is a flavoured spirit, not a liqueur, because it lacks sugar. The wine with wormwood is an aromatised wine, in fact a vermouth: it starts from wine, not spirit. The unsweetened juniper spirit is a gin.":"不甜的櫻桃烈酒是調味烈酒，不是利口酒，因為沒有糖。加了苦艾的葡萄酒是加味葡萄酒，其實就是香艾酒：它從葡萄酒開始，不是烈酒。未加糖的杜松子烈酒則是琴酒。","Why do some liqueur producers make several separate flavoured spirits, each with a different technique?":"為什麼有些利口酒生產者分別製作數種調味烈酒，每一種用不同的技術？","To blend them into a more complex final product":"把它們調和成更複雜的最終產品","So they can sell them as different flavoured vodkas":"這樣就能當作不同的調味伏特加販售","Because the law forbids using just one technique":"因為法律禁止只用一種技術","To avoid adding sugar at the end":"避免在最後加糖","Spirits flavoured by different techniques are then blended to build a complex flavour.":"用不同技術調味的烈酒之後會調和起來，建構複雜的風味。","Maceration extracts colour and a broad range of aromas; redistillation can isolate particular aromas; combining them builds complexity. Producers using a single technique usually need no blending. No law requires several techniques, and a liqueur is always sweetened.":"浸漬萃取顏色和範圍廣泛的香氣；再蒸餾可以分離出特定的香氣；結合兩者就能建構複雜度。只用一種技術的生產者通常不需要調和。沒有法律要求使用數種技術，而利口酒一定加糖。","Which base wine does a vermouth producer usually choose?":"香艾酒的生產者通常選擇哪一種基酒？","A dry, neutral, high-acid white":"不甜、中性、高酸的白酒","A tannic, highly aromatic, fruit-rich red":"單寧重、香氣濃郁、果味豐富的紅酒","A sweet wine from dried grapes":"用風乾葡萄釀的甜酒","A neutral dry white lets the botanicals shine.":"中性的不甜白酒讓植物性原料發光。","The law does not set the grape type, but a very aromatic or tannic wine would mask the botanicals. Sugar is added at blending, so there is no need to start from a sweet wine, and bubbles play no part.":"法律沒有規定葡萄的類型，但香氣很濃或單寧很重的葡萄酒會掩蓋植物性原料。糖是在調和時加入的，所以不需要從甜酒開始，氣泡也沒有角色。","Where does a red vermouth's colour usually come from?":"紅香艾酒的顏色通常來自哪裡？","Caramel added to white wine":"加進白葡萄酒的焦糖色","Long contact with black grape skins":"與紅葡萄皮長時間接觸","Young red wine":"年輕的紅酒","Most red vermouths are white wine coloured with caramel.":"大多數紅香艾酒是用焦糖色上色的白葡萄酒。","Black grapes are allowed but rarely used: red wine would bring tannins and flavours competing with the botanicals. Oak, when used, adds complexity, not red colour.":"紅葡萄是允許的，但很少使用：紅酒會帶來與植物性原料競爭的單寧和風味。橡木（如果使用）增添的是複雜度，不是紅色。","Adding alcohol brings an aromatised wine into which strength range?":"添加酒精讓加味葡萄酒進入哪一個濃度範圍？","14.5–22% abv":"14.5–22% abv","8–12% abv":"8–12% abv","37.5–40% abv, like spirits":"37.5–40% abv，和烈酒一樣","Above 50% abv":"50% abv 以上","Fortification brings the wine to 14.5–22% abv.":"強化讓葡萄酒達到 14.5–22% abv。","This is enough to stop yeast and stabilise the product, which is still a wine. Normal wine strength would not be enough, and spirit-level strengths do not apply to an aromatised wine.":"這足以讓酵母停止作用並穩定產品，而它仍然是葡萄酒。一般葡萄酒的濃度不夠，烈酒級的濃度則不適用於加味葡萄酒。","Why is fortification important in sweetened aromatised wines?":"為什麼強化對加糖的加味葡萄酒很重要？","It stops yeast refermenting the sugar":"它阻止酵母把糖重新發酵","It adds the red colour typical of aperitif vermouths":"它增添開胃香艾酒典型的紅色","It makes the wine drier":"它讓葡萄酒更不甜","It replaces the botanicals":"它取代植物性原料","The added alcohol raises strength to a level toxic to yeast.":"添加的酒精把濃度提高到對酵母有毒的程度。","Without fortification, yeast could ferment the added sugar. The alcohol also extends shelf life. Colour comes from caramel and flavour from the botanicals, not from neutral alcohol.":"沒有強化，酵母可能會發酵添加的糖。酒精也延長了保存期限。顏色來自焦糖色，風味來自植物性原料，不是中性酒精。","Why do most producers fortify with neutral alcohol?":"為什麼大多數生產者用中性酒精來強化？","It does not compete with the botanicals":"它不與植物性原料競爭","It is the only alcohol the law allows for this category":"它是法律對這個類別唯一允許的酒精","It adds sweetness":"它增添甜味","It gives the red colour":"它帶來紅色","Neutral alcohol adds no flavours that would mask the botanicals.":"中性酒精不會增添掩蓋植物性原料的風味。","Producers may also use low-strength characterful distillates, so neutral is not the only option. Sweetness and colour come from sugar and caramel respectively.":"生產者也可以使用低濃度、有個性的餾出液，所以中性不是唯一的選項。甜味和顏色分別來自糖和焦糖色。","Under European law, what must a vermouth recipe include?":"依歐洲法律，香艾酒的配方必須包含什麼？","Wormwood-family plants":"苦艾屬的植物","Liquorice, aniseed and star anise":"甘草、茴香籽和八角","Wormwood-family plants are what legally define vermouth.":"苦艾屬的植物在法律上定義了香艾酒。","Juniper defines gin, and liquorice and aniseed are typical of pastis. Red wine is not required: most red vermouths are made from white wine and caramel.":"杜松子定義琴酒，甘草和茴香籽是 pastis 的典型原料。紅酒不是必要的：大多數紅香艾酒用白葡萄酒和焦糖色製成。","Which ingredient is NOT normally part of a vermouth's final blend?":"下列哪一種材料通常不屬於香艾酒的最終調和？","Botanical distillates and tinctures":"植物性原料的餾出液和酊劑","Dry base wine":"不甜的基酒","Sugar and caramel":"糖和焦糖色","Tonic water is a bar mixer, not a vermouth ingredient.":"通寧水是酒吧的調和飲料，不是香艾酒的材料。","The blend brings together base wine, distilled alcohol, distillates and tinctures, sugar and caramel if needed. Tonic might be added when serving vermouth as a long drink, but it is not part of production.":"調和匯集了基酒、蒸餾酒精、餾出液和酊劑、糖，必要時還有焦糖色。把香艾酒做成長飲時可能會加通寧水，但那不屬於生產過程。","After blending, why does the mix rest for a few weeks in stainless steel?":"調和後，為什麼混合液要在不鏽鋼槽中靜置幾週？","To let the flavours integrate":"讓風味融合","To let the sugar added at blending ferment again":"讓調和時加入的糖再次發酵","To pick up woody flavours":"吸收木質風味","To raise the strength":"提高濃度","Resting gives the ingredients time to blend before bottling.":"靜置讓各種材料在裝瓶前有時間融合。","Fortification prevents refermentation, and stainless steel is inert, so it gives no woody flavours. Producers wanting extra complexity choose oak barrels instead, and resting does not change strength.":"強化能防止再發酵，而不鏽鋼是惰性的，所以不帶來木質風味。想要更多複雜度的生產者會改用橡木桶，而靜置不會改變濃度。","Where is the vast majority of aromatised wine still made?":"絕大多數的加味葡萄酒至今仍在哪裡生產？","The Alpine area of France and Italy":"法國和義大利的阿爾卑斯山區","The Iberian peninsula, across southern Spain and Portugal":"伊比利半島，橫跨西班牙南部和葡萄牙","California":"加州","Eastern Europe":"東歐","Most comes from an area straddling the Alps: south-east France and north-west Italy.":"大部分來自橫跨阿爾卑斯山的地區：法國東南部和義大利西北部。","New versions are now made in many countries, driven by cocktail culture, but volumes are small. Eastern Europe is linked rather to vodka, and the Iberian peninsula is known for other wines.":"在調酒文化的推動下，如今許多國家都在做新的版本，但產量很小。東歐比較與伏特加有關，伊比利半島則以其他葡萄酒聞名。","Which statement about vermouth styles is correct?":"關於香艾酒的類型，下列哪一項正確？","It comes red or white, from dry to sweet":"有紅有白，從不甜到甜都有","It only comes in a red, sweet style":"只有紅色的甜型","White vermouth is always fully dry, never sweet":"白香艾酒一律完全不甜，絕不是甜的","It is never sweetened":"從不加糖","Vermouth comes in red or white and at several sweetness levels.":"香艾酒有紅色或白色，並有數種甜度。","Colour does not decide sweetness: there are dry white vermouths and sweet ones. Most aromatised wines are sweetened, so 'never sweetened' is false.":"顏色不決定甜度：白香艾酒有不甜的，也有甜的。大多數加味葡萄酒都加糖，所以「從不加糖」是錯的。","Are aromatised wines such as vermouth spirits?":"香艾酒這類加味葡萄酒是烈酒嗎？","No, they are wines with added alcohol":"不是，它們是添加了酒精的葡萄酒","Yes, because they are redistilled with botanicals":"是，因為它們與植物性原料一起再蒸餾","Yes, they are wine-based liqueurs":"是，它們是以葡萄酒為基底的利口酒","No, they are herb-flavoured beers":"不是，它們是用香草調味的啤酒","They all start as wine: distilled alcohol is just an added ingredient.":"它們都從葡萄酒開始：蒸餾酒精只是添加的材料。","Vermouth as a whole is not redistilled: at most some botanicals are, separately. It is not a liqueur, because the base is wine, not a spirit. It is studied alongside spirits for its central role in cocktails.":"香艾酒整體並不經再蒸餾：頂多是某些植物性原料分開再蒸餾。它不是利口酒，因為基底是葡萄酒，不是烈酒。因為它在調酒中的核心角色，才與烈酒一起學習。","Why is vermouth considered the most important aromatised wine?":"為什麼香艾酒被認為是最重要的加味葡萄酒？","It is the one most often needed in cocktails":"它是調酒中最常需要的一種","It is the only one that can be aged":"它是唯一可以陳年的","It is the only one made outside the Alps":"它是唯一在阿爾卑斯山以外製作的","It is the strongest, above 30% abv":"它最烈，超過 30% abv","Vermouth is the aromatised wine that appears most often in cocktail recipes.":"香艾酒是在調酒酒譜中最常出現的加味葡萄酒。","Other aromatised wines can also be cask-aged. Most aromatised wines, vermouth included, are made precisely in the Alpine area. Strength stays within 14.5–22%, well below 30%.":"其他加味葡萄酒也可以桶陳。大多數加味葡萄酒，包括香艾酒，正是在阿爾卑斯山區製作的。濃度維持在 14.5–22% 之間，遠低於 30%。","Which grapes may be used for the base wine of an aromatised wine?":"加味葡萄酒的基酒可以使用哪些葡萄？","Any grape, white or black":"任何葡萄，白的或紅的","Only aromatic white grapes such as Muscat":"只有蜜思嘉這類芳香型白葡萄","Only black grapes, for red vermouths":"只有紅葡萄，用於紅香艾酒","Only grapes grown in Piedmont and Savoy":"只有皮埃蒙特和薩瓦種植的葡萄","There are no grape restrictions: white and black grapes may both be used.":"沒有葡萄的限制：白葡萄和紅葡萄都可以使用。","In practice neutral, high-acid white grapes are preferred, not aromatic ones, to leave room for the botanicals. Red vermouths are almost always made from white wine coloured with caramel. There is no geographical restriction on the grapes.":"實務上偏好中性、高酸的白葡萄，而不是芳香型的，好為植物性原料留出空間。紅香艾酒幾乎都用焦糖色上色的白葡萄酒製成。葡萄沒有地理限制。","How is the base wine for vermouth usually made?":"香艾酒的基酒通常怎麼釀？","Grapes are crushed and the juice is fermented straight away":"葡萄壓碎後，葡萄汁立刻發酵","Grapes are dried for months first":"葡萄先風乾好幾個月","Black grape skins are macerated at length":"紅葡萄皮長時間浸皮","Grapes are distilled and diluted with water":"把葡萄蒸餾後加水稀釋","The grapes are crushed and the sweet juice ferments at once, giving a dry wine.":"葡萄壓碎後，甜汁立刻發酵，釀成不甜的葡萄酒。","Drying grapes or long skin contact would give concentrated or coloured wines, poorly suited to showcasing botanicals. Distilling the grapes would make a spirit, not a wine. The ideal base wine is dry and neutral.":"風乾葡萄或長時間浸皮會做出濃縮或有顏色的葡萄酒，不適合襯托植物性原料。蒸餾葡萄會做出烈酒，不是葡萄酒。理想的基酒是不甜而中性的。","Besides tinctures and distillates, what other method do some producers use to flavour an aromatised wine?":"除了酊劑和餾出液，有些生產者還用什麼方法為加味葡萄酒調味？","Macerating the botanicals in the wine itself":"把植物性原料直接浸漬在葡萄酒中","Fermenting the botanicals together with the juice":"讓植物性原料與葡萄汁一起發酵","Smoking the wine over aromatic woods":"用芳香的木材煙燻葡萄酒","Distilling the whole wine with the botanicals":"把整批葡萄酒與植物性原料一起蒸餾","Some producers steep the botanicals in the wine itself rather than in alcohol.":"有些生產者把植物性原料浸泡在葡萄酒本身，而不是酒精中。","The most common method is to process each botanical separately, by redistillation or maceration in alcohol. Fermenting with botanicals and smoking are not methods used for these wines. Distilling the whole wine would turn it into a spirit.":"最常見的做法是把每種植物性原料分開處理，以再蒸餾或在酒精中浸漬。與植物性原料一起發酵和煙燻都不是這些葡萄酒使用的方法。蒸餾整批葡萄酒會把它變成烈酒。","Because alcohol is added to them, which category do aromatised wines belong to?":"因為添加了酒精，加味葡萄酒屬於哪一個類別？","Grape brandies":"葡萄白蘭地","Naturally sweet late-harvest wines":"天然甜型的晚摘葡萄酒","Adding alcohol is called fortification, which makes these products a type of fortified wine.":"添加酒精稱為強化（加烈），這讓這些產品成為加烈酒的一種。","They have no bubbles, so they are not sparkling. They remain wines, not spirits. Their sweetness comes from added sugar, not from late-picked grapes.":"它們沒有氣泡，所以不是氣泡酒。它們仍然是葡萄酒，不是烈酒。它們的甜味來自添加的糖，不是晚摘的葡萄。","Besides preventing refermentation, what does fortification give an aromatised wine?":"除了防止再發酵，強化還帶給加味葡萄酒什麼？","A longer shelf life":"更長的保存期限","A natural red colour":"天然的紅色","A woody flavour":"木質風味","The added alcohol makes the wine more stable and gives it a longer shelf life.":"添加的酒精讓葡萄酒更穩定，保存期限也更長。","Red colour in vermouth usually comes from caramel. Alcohol does not create bubbles. A woody flavour only comes if the producer uses casks, not from fortification, which normally uses neutral alcohol.":"香艾酒的紅色通常來自焦糖色。酒精不會產生氣泡。只有生產者使用木桶時才會有木質風味，它不是來自強化，強化通常使用中性酒精。","Can a producer fortify an aromatised wine with something other than neutral alcohol?":"生產者可以用中性酒精以外的東西來強化加味葡萄酒嗎？","Yes, with low-strength characterful distillates":"可以，用低濃度、有個性的餾出液","No, only neutral alcohol is permitted":"不行，只允許中性酒精","Yes, but only with peated whisky":"可以，但只能用泥煤威士忌","No, fortification is done with sugar":"不行，強化是用糖進行的","Low-strength characterful distillates may be used, although neutral alcohol is more common.":"可以使用低濃度、有個性的餾出液，不過中性酒精更常見。","Neutral alcohol is preferred because it does not compete with the botanicals, but it is not compulsory. No rule calls for peated whisky. Sugar sweetens but does not fortify: only alcohol raises the strength.":"偏好中性酒精是因為它不與植物性原料競爭，但它不是強制的。沒有規定要用泥煤威士忌。糖能增甜但不能強化：只有酒精能提高濃度。","After blending, what alternative to stainless steel do some vermouth producers use?":"調和後，除了不鏽鋼，有些香艾酒生產者還使用什麼？","Oak barrels, for extra complexity":"橡木桶，以增添複雜度","Open bottles left in the sun":"放在太陽下的開口酒瓶","Sealed amphorae buried for years":"埋在地下多年的密封陶甕","Concrete tanks with active yeast":"含有活酵母的水泥槽","Some use oak barrels, where the wine matures and gains complexity.":"有些人使用橡木桶，葡萄酒在其中熟成並增添複雜度。","Usually the blend rests a few weeks in steel to integrate the flavours. Leaving open bottles in the sun would spoil them. Active yeast would referment the sugar, which fortification is meant to prevent.":"通常調和後的酒在鋼槽中靜置幾週，讓風味融合。把開口的酒瓶放在太陽下會讓它們變質。活酵母會讓糖再發酵，而強化正是為了防止這一點。","Can aromatised wines be made outside the Alpine area of France and Italy?":"加味葡萄酒可以在法國和義大利的阿爾卑斯山區以外製作嗎？","Yes, anywhere in the world":"可以，世界任何地方都行","No, the law forbids it":"不行，法律禁止","Only within Europe":"只能在歐洲境內","Only if the base wine comes from the Alps":"只有基酒來自阿爾卑斯山才行","They can be made anywhere, and the cocktail boom has brought new, innovative versions.":"它們可以在任何地方製作，調酒熱潮也帶來了創新的新版本。","The Alpine area remains the historic and production heartland, but it is not a legal requirement. There is no obligation for an Alpine base wine or European production. The cocktail boom is drawing new producers worldwide.":"阿爾卑斯山區仍是歷史和生產的核心地帶，但不是法律要求。沒有規定基酒要來自阿爾卑斯山，或必須在歐洲生產。調酒熱潮正吸引全世界的新生產者。","Which statement about the flavourings in aromatised wines is correct?":"關於加味葡萄酒的調味料，下列哪一項正確？","Certain artificial flavours may also be used":"也可以使用某些人工香料","Recipes must be declared on the label":"配方必須標示在酒標上","Only one botanical is allowed per product":"每種產品只允許一種植物性原料","Botanicals must be grown by the producer":"植物性原料必須由生產者自己種植","As well as botanicals, producers may use certain artificial flavours.":"除了植物性原料，生產者也可以使用某些人工香料。","Recipes are almost always secret, not declared. There is no limit on the number of flavours. No rule requires producers to grow their own botanicals.":"配方幾乎都是保密的，不會標示。風味的數量沒有限制。沒有規定要求生產者自己種植植物性原料。","Which sequence best describes how vermouth is made?":"哪一組順序最能描述香艾酒的製作？","Dry wine, then alcohol, flavourings, sugar":"不甜的葡萄酒，再加酒精、調味料、糖","Sweet juice, then distillation with botanicals":"甜葡萄汁，再與植物性原料一起蒸餾","Red wine, compulsory ageing, then sugar":"紅酒、強制陳年，再加糖","Neutral spirit, then grape juice and spices":"中性烈酒，再加葡萄汁和香料","It starts with a dry wine, then alcohol, tinctures and distillates, sugar and caramel if needed are blended in.":"從不甜的葡萄酒開始，再調入酒精、酊劑和餾出液、糖，必要時還有焦糖色。","Vermouth as a whole is not distilled. The base wine is usually white and ageing is not compulsory. Starting from neutral spirit plus grape juice would not give a wine, but something closer to a liqueur.":"香艾酒整體不經蒸餾。基酒通常是白酒，陳年也不是強制的。從中性烈酒加葡萄汁開始，得到的不是葡萄酒，而是更接近利口酒的東西。","Aromatised wines are not spirits. Why do bar staff still need to know them?":"加味葡萄酒不是烈酒。為什麼酒吧人員仍然需要認識它們？","They are key ingredients in many cocktails":"它們是許多調酒的關鍵材料","They are the alcoholic base of most liqueurs":"它們是大多數利口酒的酒精基底","The law classes them as flavoured spirits":"法律把它們歸類為調味烈酒","They replace cocktail bitters in almost every classic recipe":"它們在幾乎所有經典酒譜中取代了調酒用苦精","They matter because of their role in bar and cocktail culture, above all vermouth.":"它們之所以重要，是因為在酒吧和調酒文化中的角色，尤其是香艾酒。","Vermouth is essential in, for example, the Martini, Manhattan and Negroni. Liqueurs usually start from neutral spirit, not wine. Legally, aromatised wines are fortified wines, not spirits. In spirit-forward drinks vermouth works alongside bitters but does not replace them everywhere.":"舉例來說，香艾酒在 Martini、Manhattan 和 Negroni 中不可或缺。利口酒通常從中性烈酒開始，不是葡萄酒。在法律上，加味葡萄酒是加烈酒，不是烈酒。在烈酒主導型飲品中，香艾酒與苦精搭配使用，但並不是處處取代它。","A European producer flavours a fortified, sweetened wine with herbs and citrus but no wormwood-family plants. Can it be called vermouth?":"一位歐洲生產者用香草和柑橘為一款強化並加糖的葡萄酒調味，但沒有用苦艾屬的植物。可以稱為香艾酒嗎？","No: wormwood-family plants are compulsory":"不行：苦艾屬的植物是強制的","Yes, as long as it is fortified to at least 14.5% abv":"可以，只要強化到至少 14.5% abv","Yes, if it is made in the Alpine area of France and Italy":"可以，只要在法國和義大利的阿爾卑斯山區製作","No: to be vermouth it would also have to start from a red wine":"不行：要成為香艾酒，還必須從紅酒開始","Under European law, what defines a vermouth is the use of wormwood-family plants.":"依歐洲法律，定義香艾酒的是使用苦艾屬的植物。","The 14.5–22% abv range applies to all aromatised wines, so it does not single out vermouth. The Alpine area is where most is made, but it is not a requirement. The base wine can be white or red, and most red vermouths come from white wine coloured with caramel.":"14.5–22% abv 的範圍適用於所有加味葡萄酒，所以不是香艾酒獨有的。阿爾卑斯山區是大部分產品的產地，但不是要求。基酒可以是白酒或紅酒，而大多數紅香艾酒來自用焦糖色上色的白葡萄酒。","How do vermouth producers usually handle their botanicals?":"香艾酒生產者通常怎麼處理植物性原料？","They process each one separately, then blend":"每一種分開處理，再調和","They boil them all together in the base wine":"全部放在基酒中一起煮","They put whole dried plants straight into the bottle":"把整株乾燥的植物直接放進瓶中","They ferment them with the grape juice while making the base wine":"釀基酒時讓它們與葡萄汁一起發酵","Each botanical is usually extracted on its own, by maceration or redistillation, before the final blend.":"每種植物性原料通常單獨萃取，以浸漬或再蒸餾進行，之後才做最終的調和。","Working separately gives the producer control over each aroma. Some macerate botanicals in the wine itself, but without boiling. The base wine is fermented straight away and stays dry and neutral: botanicals are not fermented with it, nor left whole in the bottle.":"分開處理讓生產者能掌控每一種香氣。有些人把植物性原料浸漬在葡萄酒本身，但不煮沸。基酒立刻發酵，並保持不甜而中性：植物性原料不與它一起發酵，也不會整株留在瓶中。","What has driven the recent wave of new, innovative aromatised wines?":"什麼推動了近年創新的加味葡萄酒新浪潮？","The growing popularity of cocktails":"調酒越來越受歡迎","A new European law banning wormwood":"禁用苦艾的歐洲新法","A shortage of neutral, high-acid white grapes":"中性、高酸白葡萄的短缺","Almost all production moving away from the Alpine area":"幾乎所有生產都移出阿爾卑斯山區","As cocktails boomed, interest in making new versions of these wines grew all over the world.":"隨著調酒蔚為風潮，全世界對製作這些葡萄酒新版本的興趣都增加了。","Wormwood-family plants are in fact compulsory for vermouth in Europe. No grape shortage explains the trend. And the vast majority of these wines is still made in the Alpine area of France and Italy, even though they are now made everywhere.":"苦艾屬的植物其實是歐洲香艾酒的強制原料。沒有葡萄短缺可以解釋這股趨勢。而且這些葡萄酒絕大部分仍在法國和義大利的阿爾卑斯山區製作，雖然如今到處都有人做。","What is usually true of a vermouth's exact botanical recipe?":"關於香艾酒確切的植物配方，通常是什麼情況？","It is a closely guarded secret":"它是嚴格保守的祕密","It is printed in full on the label":"它完整印在酒標上","It is laid down in detail by European law":"它由歐洲法律詳細規定","It is the same for every producer in a given Alpine area":"同一個阿爾卑斯山區的每位生產者都相同","There is no limit on flavours, and most producers keep their exact blend secret.":"風味沒有限制，大多數生產者對確切的配方保密。","Labels do not list the full botanical recipe. European law requires only wormwood-family plants and leaves the rest open. Each house has its own recipe, even within one area, which is exactly what makes vermouths differ.":"酒標不會列出完整的植物配方。歐洲法律只要求苦艾屬的植物，其餘不加限制。每家酒廠都有自己的配方，即使在同一個區域內也一樣，這正是香艾酒各不相同的原因。","Which vermouth ingredient is optional?":"香艾酒的哪一種材料不是必要的？","The added distilled alcohol":"添加的蒸餾酒精","Wormwood-family plants, at least in Europe":"苦艾屬的植物，至少在歐洲","Caramel is only for colour, for example in red vermouths, and is added only when needed.":"焦糖色只是為了顏色，例如用於紅香艾酒，只在需要時添加。","Without a base wine it would not be an aromatised wine. Distilled alcohol must be added to bring the strength to 14.5–22% abv. In Europe, wormwood-family plants are what defines vermouth.":"沒有基酒就不是加味葡萄酒。必須添加蒸餾酒精，把濃度提高到 14.5–22% abv。在歐洲，苦艾屬的植物是香艾酒的定義。","What are drip mats on the bar top for?":"吧檯檯面上的吧墊有什麼用途？","To catch spills":"接住灑出來的液體","To keep glasses cold":"讓杯子保持低溫","To cut garnishes safely without slipping":"安全地切裝飾物，不會滑動","To display bottles":"陳列酒瓶","Drinks are prepared on them so spills do not spread over the bar top.":"飲品在吧墊上調製，灑出來的液體就不會在檯面上擴散。","Garnishes are cut on the chopping board, and glasses are chilled in a fridge or with ice and water. Displaying bottles is the back bar's job.":"裝飾物在砧板上切，杯子則放在冰箱中或用冰和水冰鎮。陳列酒瓶是後吧檯的工作。","What does a workstation's speed rail hold?":"工作檯的快速酒架（speed rail）放的是什麼？","The house spirits":"店內的基本款烈酒","Chilled glasses ready for service":"冰鎮好、可供出酒的杯子","The most prestigious bottles to show customers":"展示給顧客看的最名貴酒瓶","Crushed ice":"碎冰","The speed rail keeps the most-used spirits within reach.":"快速酒架讓最常用的烈酒隨手可得。","Display bottles live on the back bar, ice in the ice well. Chilled glasses are kept in a fridge or cooled with ice and water while the drink is made.":"陳列用的酒瓶放在後吧檯，冰塊放在冰槽。冰鎮的杯子放在冰箱裡，或在調製飲品時用冰和水降溫。","What is the correct way to take ice from the ice well?":"從冰槽取冰的正確方式是什麼？","With a scoop or tongs":"用冰鏟或冰夾","Using the glass the drink will be served in":"用要盛裝飲品的杯子","With clean hands":"用乾淨的手","With the mixing glass":"用攪拌杯","Ice is always handled with a scoop or tongs.":"冰塊一律用冰鏟或冰夾處理。","Using the glass risks chipping it and leaving shards in the ice; hands are not hygienic, even when washed. The scoop fills shakers, mixing glasses and glasses; tongs place cubes one at a time.":"用杯子可能讓杯子缺角，把碎片留在冰裡；手即使洗過也不衛生。冰鏟用來裝滿雪克杯、攪拌杯和杯子；冰夾則一次夾放一顆冰塊。","Which tool is the easiest way to keep cocktails consistent and balanced?":"哪一種工具是讓調酒保持一致和平衡最簡單的方法？","The jigger":"量酒器（jigger）","The muddler":"搗棒","The channel knife for garnishes":"做裝飾物用的刮皮刀","The grater":"刨絲器","The jigger is calibrated to pour accurate measures.":"量酒器有刻度，能倒出準確的份量。","Without accurate measures, the balance between strong, weak, sour and sweet changes with every drink. Muddler, channel knife and grater work on aroma and garnish, not quantities.":"沒有準確的份量，強、弱、酸、甜之間的平衡每一杯都會改變。搗棒、刮皮刀和刨絲器處理的是香氣和裝飾，不是份量。","Which strainer is typically used with a mixing glass?":"哪一種隔冰匙通常與攪拌杯搭配使用？","The Julep strainer":"Julep 隔冰匙","The Hawthorne strainer with its coiled spring":"帶彈簧圈的 Hawthorne 隔冰匙","A fine sieve on its own":"單獨使用細濾網","None: it is poured straight":"不用：直接倒出","The Julep strainer pairs with the mixing glass for stirred drinks.":"Julep 隔冰匙與攪拌杯搭配，用於攪拌類飲品。","The Hawthorne goes with the shaker, often with a fine sieve for double straining. A stirred drink still has to be separated from the ice it was made on, so a strainer is needed.":"Hawthorne 與雪克杯搭配，常加上細濾網做雙重過濾。攪拌的飲品仍然要與調製時用的冰分開，所以需要隔冰匙。","What is double straining?":"什麼是雙重過濾（double straining）？","Hawthorne strainer plus fine sieve":"Hawthorne 隔冰匙加細濾網","Straining the drink twice through the same Julep strainer":"用同一支 Julep 隔冰匙把飲品過濾兩次","Using two mixing glasses":"使用兩個攪拌杯","Filtering juice before and after squeezing":"榨汁前後各過濾一次果汁","The drink is poured through a Hawthorne and a fine sieve together to remove every ice shard.":"飲品同時通過 Hawthorne 和細濾網倒出，去除每一片碎冰。","It is used for shaken drinks, because shaking breaks ice into shards. The Julep goes with stirred drinks, and juices have nothing to do with this technique.":"它用於搖盪的飲品，因為搖盪會把冰打碎。Julep 搭配攪拌類飲品，果汁則與這項技術無關。","A bartender needs narrow strips of lemon peel for a garnish. Which tool is used?":"一位調酒師需要細長的檸檬皮條做裝飾。用哪一種工具？","A channel knife":"刮皮刀（channel knife）","A peeler, suited to wide, thick pieces of peel":"削皮刀，適合寬而厚的果皮","A grater":"刨絲器","A muddler":"搗棒","The channel knife is designed to cut narrow strips of citrus peel.":"刮皮刀是設計來切出細長柑橘皮條的。","The peeler is for larger pieces of peel. The grater is used for spices like nutmeg, and the muddler crushes ingredients to release juice and oils.":"削皮刀用於較大片的果皮。刨絲器用於肉豆蔻這類香料，搗棒則用來壓碎材料以釋出汁液和精油。","What is a muddler used for?":"搗棒的用途是什麼？","Crushing lime or mint":"壓碎萊姆或薄荷","Measuring small amounts":"量取少量液體","Stirring drinks in the mixing glass to the right dilution":"在攪拌杯中把飲品攪拌到合適的稀釋度","Opening beers":"開啤酒","The muddler breaks up ingredients like lime and mint to release juice and aromatic oils.":"搗棒把萊姆和薄荷這類材料壓開，釋出汁液和芳香精油。","Measuring small amounts and stirring are the bar spoon's jobs; mixers and beers are opened with a bar blade. Delicate ingredients are easily overworked, so the muddler needs a light touch.":"量取少量液體和攪拌是吧匙的工作；調和飲料和啤酒用開瓶片打開。細緻的材料很容易處理過頭，所以用搗棒時下手要輕。","Why is the juicer considered a very important tool?":"為什麼榨汁器被認為是非常重要的工具？","Juices should always be fresh":"果汁應該永遠是新鮮的","It also crushes ice":"它也能碎冰","It lets juices keep for several days without losing quality":"它讓果汁保存數天而不損品質","It replaces the jigger":"它取代量酒器","Citrus juices must be freshly squeezed because they oxidise quickly.":"柑橘汁必須現榨，因為它們氧化得很快。","Even when stored correctly, juices deteriorate within hours, not days, which is why the best bars prepare them in batches through the night. The juicer neither crushes ice nor measures.":"即使保存得當，果汁也會在幾小時內變質，而不是幾天，所以最好的酒吧整晚分批準備。榨汁器既不碎冰，也不量取。","Which glass, with a wide bowl and narrow opening, is designed to show off oak-aged spirits?":"哪一種杯身寬、杯口窄的杯子，是設計來展現橡木桶陳年烈酒的？","The balloon (snifter)":"白蘭地杯（balloon／snifter）","The highball, tall and straight for long drinks":"高球杯，高而直，用於長飲","The shot glass":"Shot 杯","The tiki mug":"Tiki 杯","The balloon concentrates the aromas of oak-aged spirits.":"白蘭地杯能集中橡木桶陳年烈酒的香氣。","It is mostly associated with brandy but works for other spirits too. The highball is for long drinks with a mixer, the shot glass for a measure drunk in one go, the tiki mug for rum-based tiki drinks.":"它多半與白蘭地聯想在一起，但也適用於其他烈酒。高球杯用於加調和飲料的長飲，shot 杯用於一口喝完的一份酒，tiki 杯則用於以蘭姆酒為基底的 tiki 飲品。","What does serving a drink 'straight up' mean?":"飲品以「straight up」供應是什麼意思？","Without ice in the glass":"杯中不加冰","Over plenty of ice cubes":"加大量方冰塊","Topped up with soda":"加滿蘇打水","Hot, in a toddy glass with a handle":"熱飲，裝在有把手的 toddy 杯中","'Straight up' means a short drink served without ice, for example in a Martini glass.":"「Straight up」表示不加冰供應的短飲，例如裝在 Martini 杯中。","Serving over ice is called 'on the rocks'. Soda turns the drink into a long drink, and the toddy glass is for hot drinks: neither is 'straight up'.":"加冰供應稱為「on the rocks」。蘇打水會把飲品變成長飲，toddy 杯則用於熱飲：兩者都不是「straight up」。","A customer orders an Irish coffee. Which glass suits it?":"一位顧客點了 Irish coffee。適合用哪一種杯子？","A toddy glass":"Toddy 杯","A coupe":"淺碟杯（coupe）","A Margarita glass, with its wide rim":"杯口寬大的 Margarita 杯","A julep cup":"Julep 杯","The toddy glass is made for hot drinks such as Irish coffee.":"Toddy 杯是為 Irish coffee 這類熱飲設計的。","Nearly all cocktails are served cold; the toddy glass is the exception for hot drinks. Coupe and Margarita glasses are for cold short drinks, and the julep cup for a Mint Julep on crushed ice.":"幾乎所有調酒都是冷飲；toddy 杯是熱飲的例外。淺碟杯和 Margarita 杯用於冷的短飲，julep 杯則用於加碎冰的 Mint Julep。","Which glass best suits a long drink with a mixer and lots of ice, such as a gin and tonic?":"哪一種杯子最適合加調和飲料和大量冰塊的長飲，例如琴通寧？","Martini glass":"Martini 杯","Balloon, with a narrow opening that concentrates aromas":"白蘭地杯，窄杯口能集中香氣","Shot glass":"Shot 杯","The highball is the versatile glass for long drinks with a mixer and plenty of ice.":"高球杯是用途廣泛的杯子，適合加調和飲料和大量冰塊的長飲。","The Martini glass is for short drinks without ice, the balloon for sipping aged spirits, the shot glass for one measure drunk in one go. None holds the ice and mixer of a long drink.":"Martini 杯用於不加冰的短飲，白蘭地杯用於慢慢品飲陳年烈酒，shot 杯用於一口喝完的一份酒。它們都裝不下長飲的冰塊和調和飲料。","Which pear-shaped glass is used for tropical drinks like the Piña Colada?":"哪一種梨形杯用於 Piña Colada 這類熱帶飲品？","The hurricane":"Hurricane 杯","The sling":"Sling 杯","The tumbler":"平底杯","The old-style Champagne coupe":"舊式的香檳淺碟杯","The hurricane, shaped like a storm lamp, is the glass for tropical drinks.":"Hurricane 杯形狀像防風燈，是熱帶飲品的杯子。","The sling is tall and tapered on a short stem, linked to the Singapore Sling. The tumbler is short and straight, and the coupe now serves short drinks without ice.":"Sling 杯高而收窄，有短杯腳，與 Singapore Sling 有關。平底杯矮而直，淺碟杯如今用來盛裝不加冰的短飲。","How should unopened bottles of spirits ideally be stored?":"未開瓶的烈酒理想的存放方式是什麼？","Cool, at a steady temperature, out of direct sunlight":"陰涼、溫度穩定、避免陽光直射","In a sunny window, to show them to customers":"放在陽光充足的窗邊，展示給顧客看","In the freezer, every one of them":"全部放進冷凍庫","Next to the coffee machine, somewhere warm":"放在咖啡機旁邊溫暖的地方","Although they keep for a long time, spirits should be kept cool, at a stable temperature and away from sunlight.":"烈酒雖然能保存很久，仍應存放在陰涼、溫度穩定且避開陽光的地方。","Direct light and heat harm quality even in a closed bottle. The freezer is not the general rule for storage. A long shelf life does not mean they are indestructible.":"直射的光線和高溫即使對未開的酒瓶也會損害品質。冷凍庫不是存放的通則。保存期限長不代表它們不會壞。","When does an opened bottle of spirit lose freshness faster?":"開過的烈酒什麼時候更快失去新鮮度？","Once it is more than half empty":"酒瓶空了一半以上時","Only in the first hour after opening":"只在開瓶後的第一個小時","When it is full and stored upright":"裝滿並直立存放時","Never: an opened spirit does not change":"永遠不會：開過的烈酒不會改變","With more air in the bottle, oxygen exposure rises and deterioration speeds up.":"瓶中的空氣越多，接觸的氧氣越多，變質就越快。","Once opened, spirits slowly react with oxygen, so the last option is false. The risk grows with the empty space, not in the first hour. Low-strength liqueurs deteriorate even faster.":"開瓶後，烈酒會與氧氣緩慢反應，所以最後一個選項是錯的。風險隨著瓶中空間變大而增加，不是在第一個小時。低濃度的利口酒變質得更快。","In a typical bar, where does the bartender work?":"在典型的酒吧中，調酒師在哪裡工作？","Between the bar counter and the back bar":"在吧檯和後吧檯之間","In front of the counter, on the customers' side":"在吧檯前面，顧客那一側","In a separate kitchen away from the room":"在遠離營業區的獨立廚房","Behind the back bar, in the storeroom":"在後吧檯後面的儲藏室","The bar is split into counter and back bar, and the bartender works in the space between them.":"酒吧分成吧檯和後吧檯，調酒師在兩者之間的空間工作。","Everything is arranged so that movements are few and short: an ergonomic bar improves speed and quality of service. Working away from the counter would slow service. The customers' side is not a preparation area.":"一切的安排都是為了讓動作少而短：符合人體工學的酒吧能提升服務的速度和品質。離開吧檯工作會拖慢服務。顧客那一側不是調製區。","What double role does the back bar play?":"後吧檯扮演哪兩種角色？","Storage, and a showcase promoting the bar and its brands":"儲物，以及宣傳酒吧和品牌的展示櫃","Washing glasses and cutting garnishes":"洗杯子和切裝飾物","Ice well and speed rail for house spirits":"冰槽和放基本款烈酒的快速酒架","Till and cloakroom for customers":"收銀台和顧客的衣帽間","The back bar displays the full range of bottles to inspire customers and offers storage space below.":"後吧檯陳列全系列的酒瓶來吸引顧客，下方則提供儲物空間。","Washing, garnish cutting, ice and house spirits belong to the workstation, within easy reach. The back bar is more showcase than working area. Till and cloakroom are not part of its role.":"清洗、切裝飾物、冰塊和基本款烈酒屬於工作檯，都在伸手可及的地方。後吧檯與其說是工作區，不如說是展示櫃。收銀台和衣帽間不在它的角色之內。","What is usually found beneath the back-bar counter?":"後吧檯的檯面下方通常有什麼？","Fridges and shelves for wine, beer, soft drinks and glassware":"放葡萄酒、啤酒、軟性飲料和杯具的冰箱和層架","The ice well":"冰槽","The sink for tools":"洗工具的水槽","The most prestigious bottles on display":"陳列的最名貴酒瓶","Below the back-bar counter is functional storage: fridges and shelving.":"後吧檯檯面下方是實用的儲物空間：冰箱和層架。","Display bottles sit on the counter and shelves above, not below. The ice well and sink belong to the workstation behind the counter. The lower part is designed for practicality, not display.":"陳列的酒瓶放在檯面和上方的層架，不是下方。冰槽和水槽屬於吧檯後的工作檯。下方是為實用而設計的，不是為了展示。","Which of these is NOT usually found at the heart of the workstation?":"下列哪一項通常不在工作檯的核心位置？","The full range of spirits and liqueurs":"全系列的烈酒和利口酒","Ice":"冰塊","Mixers":"調和飲料","Garnish trays":"裝飾物盒","The full range of bottles is displayed on the back bar; the workstation holds only the house spirits.":"全系列的酒瓶陳列在後吧檯；工作檯只放基本款烈酒。","Ice, mixers, house spirits and garnishes are used constantly, so they are within easy reach. There is also a sink, a bin and a cutting area. Less-used bottles live on the back bar.":"冰塊、調和飲料、基本款烈酒和裝飾物隨時都在用，所以放在伸手可及的地方。那裡還有水槽、垃圾桶和切割區。較少用的酒瓶放在後吧檯。","Why is it so important to keep the soda gun clean?":"為什麼保持蘇打槍清潔這麼重要？","Some sodas contain sugar, which can encourage yeast and bacteria":"有些汽水含糖，可能助長酵母和細菌","By law it must be taken apart after every drink":"依法每調一杯就要拆開","Dirt changes the strength of the spirits":"髒污會改變烈酒的濃度","Otherwise the sodas turn fizzy":"否則汽水會起泡","Sugar in the sodas can encourage unwanted yeast or bacteria if the gun is not kept clean.":"如果蘇打槍沒有保持清潔，汽水中的糖可能助長不想要的酵母或細菌。","The soda gun is an efficient way to serve sodas and water, but it must be kept hygienic. There is no rule to dismantle it after every drink. Dirt does not change strength, and sodas are already fizzy.":"蘇打槍是供應汽水和水的高效方式，但必須保持衛生。沒有每調一杯就拆開的規定。髒污不會改變濃度，汽水本來就有氣泡。","Where can freshly squeezed juices be kept chilled and within reach?":"現榨果汁可以放在哪裡，既保持低溫又隨手可得？","In a section that uses the ice well's chilling":"放在利用冰槽冷度的隔層裡","On the speed rail, next to the spirits":"放在快速酒架上，烈酒旁邊","On the back-bar counter, on display":"放在後吧檯檯面上展示","In the sink under running water":"放在水槽裡沖著水","Many workstations have a compartment chilled by the ice well for juices and mixes.":"許多工作檯有一個靠冰槽降溫的隔層，用來放果汁和預調材料。","Fresh juices oxidise quickly and must be kept cold. The speed rail and back bar are not refrigerated. The sink is for washing equipment, not storing ingredients.":"新鮮果汁氧化得很快，必須保持低溫。快速酒架和後吧檯沒有冷藏。水槽是用來清洗器具的，不是存放材料。","A bar has no room to chill glasses in a fridge. What alternative is used?":"一家酒吧沒有空間用冰箱冰鎮杯子。有什麼替代做法？","Fill the glass with ice and water while the drink is made":"調製飲品時在杯中裝滿冰和水","Run it under hot water":"用熱水沖","Rub it with lemon peel":"用檸檬皮擦拭","Serve the drink with double ice":"供應時加雙倍的冰","Ice and water in the glass chill it within moments while the drink is being prepared.":"在調製飲品的同時，杯中的冰和水片刻就能把它冰鎮。","Hot water warms the glass, the opposite of the aim. Peel adds aroma, not cold. Double ice changes the drink and does not prepare a glass for a drink served without ice.":"熱水會讓杯子變熱，與目的相反。果皮增添的是香氣，不是冷度。雙倍的冰會改變飲品，也無法為不加冰的飲品準備好杯子。","What is the bottle pourer on frequently used bottles for?":"常用酒瓶上的酒嘴有什麼用途？","It limits the flow, making accurate pouring into a jigger easier":"限制流量，讓準確倒入量酒器更容易","It filters out impurities":"濾掉雜質","It chills the spirit as it pours":"在倒酒時冷卻烈酒","It replaces the jigger entirely":"完全取代量酒器","The pourer slows the flow and makes it easier to fill the jigger exactly.":"酒嘴減緩流速，讓人更容易把量酒器裝得剛剛好。","It neither filters nor chills the liquid. It works together with the jigger, which remains the tool for consistent measuring. Without a measure, cocktails would lose consistency.":"它既不過濾，也不冷卻液體。它與量酒器搭配使用，量酒器仍是確保份量一致的工具。沒有量具，調酒就會失去一致性。","What is a bar blade used for?":"開瓶片（bar blade）的用途是什麼？","Opening mixers and beers":"開調和飲料和啤酒","Cutting citrus peel":"切柑橘皮","Opening corked wine":"開軟木塞封口的葡萄酒","Breaking ice cubes":"敲碎冰塊","The bar blade is a flat opener for mixers and beers.":"開瓶片是扁平的開瓶器，用來開調和飲料和啤酒。","Peel is cut with a peeler or channel knife. Corked wine is opened with a waiter's friend corkscrew. Ice is handled with a scoop and tongs, not a bar blade.":"果皮用削皮刀或刮皮刀切。軟木塞封口的葡萄酒用侍酒師開瓶器打開。冰塊用冰鏟和冰夾處理，不是開瓶片。","A bartender wants to place one large ice cube neatly in a customer's glass. Which tool is used?":"一位調酒師想把一大顆冰塊整齊地放進顧客的杯中。用哪一種工具？","Ice tongs":"冰夾","The ice scoop":"冰鏟","Tongs are used to place individual cubes for a neat presentation.":"冰夾用來放置個別的冰塊，讓呈現更整齊。","The scoop fills shakers, mixing glasses or glasses with lots of ice. The muddler crushes fruit and herbs. The Julep strainer strains stirred drinks.":"冰鏟用來把大量的冰裝進雪克杯、攪拌杯或杯子。搗棒壓碎水果和香草。Julep 隔冰匙用來過濾攪拌類飲品。","Which tool is used to add a nutmeg garnish?":"哪一種工具用來添加肉豆蔻裝飾？","A juicer":"榨汁器","A fine sieve":"細濾網","A grater is used for garnishes such as nutmeg.":"刨絲器用於肉豆蔻這類裝飾。","A channel knife cuts thin strips of peel. A juicer extracts fresh juice. A fine sieve removes ice shards when double straining.":"刮皮刀切出細長的果皮條。榨汁器榨取新鮮果汁。細濾網在雙重過濾時去除碎冰。","In a two-piece shaker, where do the ingredients usually go?":"使用兩件式雪克杯時，材料通常放在哪裡？","In the smaller half":"放在較小的那一半","In the larger half, already full of crushed ice":"放在已裝滿碎冰的較大那一半","Straight into the serving glass":"直接放進出酒的杯子","In a mixing glass, then poured into the shaker":"放在攪拌杯中，再倒進雪克杯","Ingredients go into the smaller half, then the other half is fitted and the drink shaken.":"材料放進較小的那一半，再蓋上另一半搖盪。","Shaking uses cubed ice, not crushed. The serving glass is used for built drinks, not shaken ones. Going from mixing glass to shaker would be a pointless extra step.":"搖盪用的是方冰塊，不是碎冰。出酒的杯子用於直調的飲品，不是搖盪的。從攪拌杯倒到雪克杯是多此一舉的步驟。","How can the bartender control how fast the drink flows through a Hawthorne strainer?":"調酒師如何控制飲品通過 Hawthorne 隔冰匙的流速？","By adjusting the strainer's position":"調整隔冰匙的位置","By adding more ice to the shaker":"在雪克杯中加更多冰","By swapping the fine sieve for a bigger one":"把細濾網換成更大的","It cannot be done: the flow is fixed":"做不到：流速是固定的","By moving the Hawthorne strainer on the rim, the bartender controls the pouring speed.":"調酒師移動杯緣上的 Hawthorne 隔冰匙，就能控制倒出的速度。","More ice changes dilution and temperature, not pouring speed. The fine sieve catches shards; it does not regulate flow. The flow is not fixed: the strainer is designed precisely to control it.":"更多的冰改變的是稀釋度和溫度，不是倒出的速度。細濾網攔截碎冰，不調節流量。流速並不固定：隔冰匙正是設計來控制它的。","A customer wants a single measure of spirit to drink in one go. Which glass is used?":"一位顧客想要一份一口喝完的烈酒。用哪一種杯子？","A shot glass":"Shot 杯","A balloon glass":"白蘭地杯","A shot glass holds a single measure meant to be drunk in one go.":"Shot 杯裝的是一份要一口喝完的酒。","The balloon is for slowly enjoying aged spirits. The coupe is for short drinks. The tumbler holds spirits neat or on ice, to be sipped.":"白蘭地杯用來慢慢享用陳年烈酒。淺碟杯用於短飲。平底杯用來盛裝純飲或加冰、慢慢啜飲的烈酒。","Which tall, tapered glass with a short stem is linked to the Singapore Sling?":"哪一種高而收窄、有短杯腳的杯子與 Singapore Sling 有關？","The sling glass":"Sling 杯","The Margarita glass":"Margarita 杯","The Champagne flute":"香檳笛形杯","The sling glass is named after the Singapore Sling and also suits other long drinks.":"Sling 杯以 Singapore Sling 命名，也適合其他長飲。","The tiki mug is a decorated vessel for rum-based tiki cocktails. The Margarita glass is wide and shallow. The flute is narrow and tall but long-stemmed, designed for the Champagne Cocktail.":"Tiki 杯是有裝飾的容器，用於以蘭姆酒為基底的 tiki 調酒。Margarita 杯寬而淺。笛形杯窄而高，但杯腳長，是為 Champagne Cocktail 設計的。","What was the coupe historically used for, and what is it used for today?":"淺碟杯過去用來裝什麼？現在呢？","Champagne; now increasingly for short drinks":"香檳；現在越來越常用於短飲","Beer; now for long drinks":"啤酒；現在用於長飲","Brandy; now for neat spirits":"白蘭地；現在用於純飲烈酒","Hot drinks; now for Irish coffee":"熱飲；現在用於 Irish coffee","The coupe began as a Champagne glass and is increasingly used for short drinks.":"淺碟杯原本是香檳杯，現在越來越常用於短飲。","Long drinks go in a highball, not a coupe. Brandy is associated with the balloon. Hot drinks such as Irish coffee go in a toddy glass.":"長飲用高球杯，不是淺碟杯。白蘭地與白蘭地杯聯想在一起。Irish coffee 這類熱飲用 toddy 杯。","What goes into the Champagne Cocktail served in a flute?":"用笛形杯供應的 Champagne Cocktail 裡有什麼？","Cognac, sugar, bitters and Champagne":"Cognac、糖、苦精和香檳","Gin, lemon juice, syrup and Champagne":"琴酒、檸檬汁、糖漿和香檳","Vodka, peach juice and Champagne":"伏特加、水蜜桃汁和香檳","Red vermouth, aperitif bitter and Champagne":"紅香艾酒、開胃苦味酒和香檳","The Champagne Cocktail combines Cognac, sugar, bitters and Champagne.":"Champagne Cocktail 結合了 Cognac、糖、苦精和香檳。","The other recipes are made up or belong to other drinks. The flute is an example of the stemmed glasses increasingly used in bars. Cognac is the key spirit in this classic recipe.":"其他酒譜是虛構的，或屬於別的飲品。笛形杯是酒吧中越來越常用的高腳杯的例子。Cognac 是這個經典酒譜的關鍵烈酒。","Which V-shaped glass is used for short, spirit-forward drinks served without ice?":"哪一種 V 形杯用於不加冰供應的烈酒主導型短飲？","The Martini glass":"Martini 杯","The Old Fashioned tumbler":"Old Fashioned 平底杯","The highball":"高球杯","The hurricane glass":"Hurricane 杯","The V-shaped Martini glass holds short drinks served straight up.":"V 形的 Martini 杯用來盛裝 straight up 供應的短飲。","The tumbler is designed for spirits and cocktails on ice. The highball is for long drinks with a mixer and lots of ice. The hurricane is for tropical drinks.":"平底杯是為加冰的烈酒和調酒設計的。高球杯用於加調和飲料和大量冰塊的長飲。Hurricane 杯用於熱帶飲品。","A customer orders a whisky on the rocks. What does that mean, and which glass suits it?":"一位顧客點了一杯 on the rocks 的威士忌。這是什麼意思？適合用哪一種杯子？","Over ice, in a tumbler":"加冰，用平底杯","Without ice, in a coupe":"不加冰，用淺碟杯","With soda, in a highball":"加蘇打水，用高球杯","Hot, in a toddy glass":"熱飲，用 toddy 杯","On the rocks means over ice, and the tumbler is the right glass.":"On the rocks 的意思是加冰，平底杯是合適的杯子。","Without ice is called straight up, typical of the coupe and Martini glass. With soda it becomes a highball, a long drink. The toddy is for hot drinks such as Irish coffee.":"不加冰稱為 straight up，是淺碟杯和 Martini 杯的典型用法。加蘇打水就變成高球，也就是長飲。Toddy 杯用於 Irish coffee 這類熱飲。","Which cocktails is the tiki mug used for?":"Tiki 杯用於哪些調酒？","Elaborate tiki cocktails, usually rum-based":"精心調製的 tiki 調酒，通常以蘭姆酒為基底","Dry Martinis served straight up":"Straight up 供應的 Dry Martini","Aged spirits to be sipped neat":"純飲慢品的陳年烈酒","Hot coffee-based drinks":"以咖啡為基底的熱飲","The tiki mug holds elaborate tiki cocktails, usually rum-based, with a Polynesian theme.":"Tiki 杯用來盛裝精心調製的 tiki 調酒，通常以蘭姆酒為基底，帶玻里尼西亞主題。","Tiki is an exuberant sub-culture of the cocktail scene. Martinis go in the V-shaped glass. Aged spirits are enjoyed in a balloon and hot drinks in a toddy.":"Tiki 是調酒界一個熱鬧奔放的次文化。Martini 用 V 形杯。陳年烈酒用白蘭地杯享用，熱飲用 toddy 杯。","What is the main job of ice in a cocktail?":"冰塊在調酒中的主要作用是什麼？","Chilling the drink":"冰鎮飲品","Sweetening the drink":"為飲品增甜","Raising the strength":"提高濃度","Adding colour and a brighter look to the mix":"為飲品增添顏色和更明亮的外觀","The first and most important job of ice is to chill.":"冰塊首要也最重要的工作是冰鎮。","Its second job is dilution, which is part of balance. Ice adds neither sugar nor colour and, as it melts, it lowers rather than raises the strength.":"它的第二項工作是稀釋，這是平衡的一部分。冰塊既不增添糖，也不增添顏色，而且融化時是降低濃度，不是提高。","Why is ice close to 0 °C a problem?":"為什麼接近 0 °C 的冰是個問題？","It chills poorly and melts too fast":"冰鎮效果差，又融化得太快","It is too hard for the shaker and may damage it":"它對雪克杯來說太硬，可能造成損壞","It does not dilute at all":"它完全不會稀釋","It makes the drink sweeter":"它讓飲品更甜","'Wet' ice is not cold enough and waters the drink down.":"「濕」冰不夠冷，會把飲品沖淡。","To work well, ice must be very cold and dry. The problem is the opposite of no dilution: it dilutes too much. Ice does not affect sweetness.":"要發揮作用，冰必須非常冷而且乾。問題與不稀釋恰恰相反：它稀釋得太多。冰不影響甜度。","A Cuba Libre is served with only two ice cubes in a tall glass. What happens?":"一杯 Cuba Libre 用高杯供應，卻只放兩顆冰塊。會怎麼樣？","The ice melts rather than chills":"冰塊只是融化，沒有冰鎮效果","The drink stays colder and less diluted for longer":"飲品能更久地保持低溫、較少被稀釋","The drink becomes stronger":"飲品變得更烈","With a low ice-to-liquid ratio, the cubes melt and water the drink down.":"冰與液體的比例低時，冰塊會融化並把飲品沖淡。","Long drinks should be served in a glass full of cubes: plenty of ice chills better and melts more slowly. Less ice does not make the drink stronger, just warmer and more watery.":"長飲應該用裝滿冰塊的杯子供應：大量的冰冰鎮效果更好，融化也更慢。冰少不會讓飲品更烈，只會更溫、更水。","In which drinks is crushed ice meant to chill and dilute quickly?":"在哪些飲品中，碎冰的作用是快速冰鎮和稀釋？","Mojito and Caipirinha":"Mojito 和 Caipirinha","Martini and Manhattan":"Martini 和 Manhattan","Gin and tonic and whisky soda, served in a highball":"用高球杯供應的琴通寧和威士忌蘇打","Crushed ice chills and dilutes fast and gives the Mojito and Caipirinha their look.":"碎冰能快速冰鎮和稀釋，也賦予 Mojito 和 Caipirinha 它們的外觀。","Martinis and Manhattans are stirred over cubes and usually served without ice. Gin and tonic and whisky soda need a glass full of cubes, and Irish coffee is a hot drink.":"Martini 和 Manhattan 是加方冰塊攪拌的，通常不加冰供應。琴通寧和威士忌蘇打需要裝滿方冰塊的杯子，Irish coffee 則是熱飲。","Why do many bars prefer a 2:1 (sugar:water) syrup to a 1:1?":"為什麼許多酒吧偏好 2:1（糖：水）的糖漿，而不是 1:1？","More sweetness in less volume":"更少的體積就有更多的甜味","It is less sweet, so easier to measure":"它比較不甜，所以更容易量取","It keeps for months out of the fridge once opened":"開封後不放冰箱也能保存好幾個月","It adds acidity":"它增添酸度","A 2:1 syrup gives the same sweetness in less liquid, leaving room for other ingredients.":"2:1 的糖漿用較少的液體提供相同的甜度，為其他材料留出空間。","Using less syrup volume leaves space for more characterful ingredients. It is sweeter, not less sweet, per volume, and sugar adds no acidity.":"使用較少體積的糖漿，就能把空間留給更有特色的材料。以同樣體積來說它更甜，不是更不甜，而且糖不增添酸度。","What is orgeat?":"什麼是 orgeat？","An almond-flavoured syrup":"杏仁風味的糖漿","A gentian bitters":"龍膽苦精","A preserved citrus juice":"保存處理過的柑橘汁","An opaque, very sweet coconut cream liqueur":"不透明、非常甜的椰子奶油利口酒","Orgeat is a syrup flavoured with almond and rose water or orange flower water.":"Orgeat 是用杏仁加玫瑰水或橙花水調味的糖漿。","It is the classic example of a flavoured syrup, a way of adding complexity. It is non-alcoholic, so it is neither a bitters nor a liqueur, and it contains no juice.":"它是風味糖漿的經典例子，是增添複雜度的一種方式。它不含酒精，所以既不是苦精，也不是利口酒，也不含果汁。","How long does freshly squeezed citrus juice stay fresh, even stored correctly?":"現榨的柑橘汁即使保存得當，能保持新鮮多久？","A matter of hours":"幾個小時","About a week in the fridge, tightly sealed":"密封放冰箱大約一個星期","Several months":"好幾個月","Indefinitely, if chilled":"只要冷藏就無限期","Fresh juices oxidise and can deteriorate within hours.":"新鮮果汁會氧化，可能在幾小時內變質。","That is why the best bars prepare them in batches to suit their needs, sometimes several times a night in busy venues. Chilling slows the decline but does not stop it for days or months.":"所以最好的酒吧依需求分批準備，在生意忙的店一個晚上有時要榨好幾次。冷藏能減緩變質，但無法維持好幾天或好幾個月。","How are cocktail bitters used?":"調酒用苦精怎麼使用？","As a seasoning, in small amounts":"當作調味料，少量使用","As the main ingredient, replacing the spirit":"當作主要材料，取代烈酒","As a garnish":"當作裝飾物","Instead of ice":"用來代替冰塊","Cocktail bitters add an extra dimension but are never the main ingredient.":"調酒用苦精增添另一個層次，但從來不是主要材料。","They are extremely bitter and often highly aromatic: a few dashes are enough. In the balance of a drink they sit on the bitter side, against sweetness.":"它們極苦，常帶有濃郁的香氣：幾滴就夠了。在飲品的平衡中，它們位於苦的一側，與甜味相對。","What is the primary role of a garnish?":"裝飾物的首要角色是什麼？","Decorating the drink":"裝飾飲品","Sweetening the drink significantly":"大幅增加飲品的甜味","Masking the drink's main aromas with a different scent":"用不同的氣味掩蓋飲品的主要香氣","A garnish is first there to decorate, often adding a subtle aroma too.":"裝飾物首先是用來裝飾的，常常也增添淡淡的香氣。","The garnish's aroma should accentuate or complement one in the drink, not mask it, and it should add to the look, not detract. Sweetness and chilling are jobs for other ingredients.":"裝飾物的香氣應該突顯或襯托飲品中的某種香氣，而不是掩蓋它；它也應該為外觀加分，而不是扣分。甜味和冰鎮是其他材料的工作。","How should fresh fruit garnishes be managed?":"新鮮水果裝飾物應該怎麼管理？","Cut on the day, discarded at night's end":"當天切，當晚結束時丟棄","Cut at the start of the week and kept in the fridge until used up":"在一週開始時切好，放冰箱直到用完","Kept in syrup":"保存在糖漿中","Left at room temperature for days":"放在室溫下好幾天","Fresh garnishes are cut on the day and thrown away at the end of the night.":"新鮮的裝飾物當天切，並在當晚結束時丟掉。","Cut fruit soon loses its look and aroma. Preserved items like olives or maraschino cherries are less delicate, but that does not apply to fresh fruit.":"切開的水果很快就失去外觀和香氣。橄欖或馬拉斯奇諾櫻桃這類保存食品沒那麼嬌貴，但這不適用於新鮮水果。","In a Martini, what is usually the main 'weak' element?":"在 Martini 中，主要的「弱」元素通常是什麼？","Meltwater from the ice":"冰塊融化的水","Freshly squeezed citrus juice":"現榨的柑橘汁","In a Martini, ice melting during stirring is the main weak component.":"在 Martini 中，攪拌時融化的冰是主要的弱成分。","A Martini contains no mixer or juice: spirit and vermouth are stirred over ice, which chills and dilutes them. That is why stirring time matters so much.":"Martini 不含調和飲料或果汁：烈酒和香艾酒加冰攪拌，冰把它們冰鎮並稀釋。所以攪拌的時間非常重要。","A cocktail tastes too sweet. Which fix follows the rules of balance?":"一杯調酒喝起來太甜。哪一種修正符合平衡的原則？","Add citrus juice or bitters":"加入柑橘汁或苦精","Add a liqueur or another flavoured syrup":"加入利口酒或另一種風味糖漿","Remove the ice":"把冰拿掉","Change the glass":"換一個杯子","Sweetness is balanced by sour or bitter elements.":"甜味由酸或苦的元素來平衡。","Liqueurs and syrups would add more sweetness and make it worse. Ice and glass affect temperature, dilution and look, not the sweet-to-sour ratio.":"利口酒和糖漿會增加更多甜味，讓情況更糟。冰和杯子影響的是溫度、稀釋和外觀，不是甜與酸的比例。","Why is simple syrup preferred to sugar for sweetening a cocktail?":"為什麼為調酒增甜時，偏好用簡易糖漿而不是糖？","A ready-made ingredient is easier to measure accurately":"現成的材料更容易準確量取","The syrup also contains alcohol":"糖漿還含有酒精","Sugar is banned in bars":"酒吧禁止使用糖","Syrup chills the drink":"糖漿能冰鎮飲品","With a pre-made ingredient it is easier to be accurate, and many bars make their own.":"用預先做好的材料更容易做到準確，許多酒吧也自己製作。","Simple syrup is just sugar and water, with no alcohol. Sugar is not banned: some classics still use it. Ice does the chilling, not syrup.":"簡易糖漿只是糖和水，不含酒精。糖並沒有被禁止：有些經典酒譜仍然使用。負責冰鎮的是冰，不是糖漿。","Compared with shaking on cubed ice, what happens when stirring?":"與加方冰塊搖盪相比，攪拌時會怎麼樣？","It chills more slowly and dilution can be greater":"冰鎮得較慢，稀釋可能更多","It chills faster and dilutes less":"冰鎮得較快，稀釋較少","It does not dilute the drink at all":"完全不會稀釋飲品","It adds more air and makes the drink frothy":"加入更多空氣，讓飲品起泡","Stirring cools more slowly, so dilution can end up greater.":"攪拌降溫較慢，所以最後稀釋可能更多。","It is shaking that chills quickly with slight dilution. Any contact with ice brings some dilution. Air and a frothy texture come from shaking, not stirring.":"快速冰鎮而只略微稀釋的是搖盪。只要與冰接觸就會有一些稀釋。空氣和起泡的質地來自搖盪，不是攪拌。","After cubed ice has been used to shake or stir a drink, what happens to it?":"用來搖盪或攪拌飲品的方冰塊，之後怎麼處理？","It is thrown away":"丟掉","It goes into the glass with the drink":"與飲品一起倒進杯中","It is reused for the next drink":"留給下一杯飲品重複使用","It goes back into the ice well":"放回冰槽","Ice used to prepare a drink is discarded.":"調製飲品用過的冰要丟棄。","That ice is already partly melted and would upset the drink in the glass, which is served with fresh ice or none. Reusing it or returning it to the well would be unhygienic. The strainer is there precisely to hold it back.":"那些冰已經部分融化，會破壞杯中的飲品，飲品要用新的冰或不加冰供應。重複使用或放回冰槽都不衛生。隔冰匙正是用來把它擋住的。","How do the best bars handle citrus juice on busy nights?":"最好的酒吧在生意忙的晚上怎麼處理柑橘汁？","They squeeze batches, sometimes several a night":"分批榨汁，有時一個晚上好幾批","They squeeze once a week and freeze them":"一週榨一次並冷凍","They buy bottled, pasteurised lemon juice":"購買瓶裝的巴氏殺菌檸檬汁","They squeeze everything in the morning and leave it at room temperature":"早上全部榨好，放在室溫下","Fresh juice loses quality within hours, so it is made in batches as needed.":"新鮮果汁在幾小時內就會失去品質，所以依需求分批製作。","The best bartenders use only freshly squeezed citrus, not pasteurised juice. Juice oxidises fast and must be kept cold, not at room temperature. Squeezing once a week would not guarantee freshness.":"最好的調酒師只用現榨的柑橘汁，不用巴氏殺菌的果汁。果汁氧化得很快，必須保持低溫，不能放在室溫。一週榨一次無法保證新鮮。","Which juice is commonly bought ready-made, even in good bars?":"哪一種果汁即使在好酒吧也常買現成的？","Cranberry juice":"蔓越莓汁","Freshly squeezed grapefruit juice":"現榨葡萄柚汁","Some juices, such as cranberry, are normally bought pre-prepared.":"有些果汁，例如蔓越莓汁，通常是買預先製好的。","Lime and lemon should always be freshly squeezed in quality bars. Freshly squeezed grapefruit, by definition, is not bought ready-made. Cranberry is used, for example, in the Cosmopolitan.":"在講究品質的酒吧，萊姆和檸檬應該一律現榨。現榨葡萄柚汁依定義就不是買現成的。蔓越莓汁用於 Cosmopolitan 等飲品。","Besides decoration, what aromatic role does a garnish often have?":"除了裝飾，裝飾物在香氣上常有什麼作用？","To highlight or complement an aroma already in the drink":"突顯或襯托飲品中已有的某種香氣","To mask the spirit's aromas":"掩蓋烈酒的香氣","To supply most of the sweetness":"提供大部分的甜味","To replace the citrus juice":"取代柑橘汁","A garnish adds a subtle aroma that accentuates or complements one in the drink.":"裝飾物增添淡淡的香氣，突顯或襯托飲品中的某種香氣。","A garnish should add, not detract, so it should not mask anything. Sweetness and acidity come from syrups and juices, not decoration. Its aroma is delicate; it is not a main ingredient.":"裝飾物應該加分，而不是扣分，所以不應該掩蓋任何東西。甜味和酸度來自糖漿和果汁，不是裝飾。它的香氣很細緻；它不是主要材料。","Why must mint for garnishes be handled carefully?":"為什麼做裝飾用的薄荷必須小心處理？","It wilts or bruises easily":"它很容易枯萎或碰傷","It becomes toxic if crushed":"壓碎後會產生毒性","By law it must be locked away":"依法必須上鎖保存","It removes alcohol from the drink":"它會去除飲品中的酒精","Mint is delicate: it must be handled so it does not wilt or bruise.":"薄荷很嬌嫩：必須小心處理，以免枯萎或碰傷。","Mint is not toxic and is routinely muddled, gently, in drinks such as the Mojito. There are no storage-lock rules. It removes no alcohol: it just adds aroma and looks.":"薄荷沒有毒，在 Mojito 這類飲品中經常會輕輕搗壓。沒有上鎖保存的規定。它不會去除酒精：只增添香氣和外觀。","Which cocktail ingredient can bring both sweetness and bitterness?":"哪一種調酒材料能同時帶來甜味和苦味？","Vermouth contributes to both the sweet and the bitter side of a drink.":"香艾酒對飲品的甜和苦兩方面都有貢獻。","In the balance model, tonic water counts as a weak element. Simple syrup is only sweet, and lemon is sour. That is why vermouth is so useful in spirit-forward drinks.":"在平衡的模型中，通寧水算是弱元素。簡易糖漿只有甜，檸檬則是酸。所以香艾酒在烈酒主導型飲品中非常有用。","What is the great advantage of a cocktail, in terms of strong versus weak?":"就強與弱而言，調酒的最大好處是什麼？","Enjoying the spirit's flavours without its full alcohol":"不必承受全部的酒精，就能享受烈酒的風味","Making the spirit stronger":"讓烈酒更烈","Removing the spirit's taste completely":"完全去除烈酒的味道","Avoiding the use of ice":"避免使用冰塊","The weak part lowers the alcohol so the spirit's flavours can be enjoyed.":"弱的部分降低酒精，讓人能享受烈酒的風味。","A cocktail dilutes rather than strengthens. The aim is not to erase the spirit but to showcase it. Melting ice is in fact part of the weak element.":"調酒是稀釋，而不是增強。目標不是抹去烈酒，而是展現它。融化的冰其實是弱元素的一部分。","Which list contains only weak components of a cocktail?":"哪一組只包含調酒的弱成分？","Soda, tonic, juice, meltwater":"蘇打水、通寧水、果汁、融冰水","Gin, vermouth, soda water and melted ice":"琴酒、香艾酒、蘇打水和融化的冰","Rum, triple sec, lime juice and soda water":"蘭姆酒、triple sec、萊姆汁和蘇打水","Cocktail bitters, syrup, tonic and vodka":"調酒用苦精、糖漿、通寧水和伏特加","Weak components are the non-alcoholic liquids, including water from melted ice.":"弱成分是不含酒精的液體，包括冰融化的水。","Gin, rum and vodka are the strong part. Triple sec and vermouth contain alcohol and bring sweetness. Cocktail bitters act as a bitter seasoning, not a weak element.":"琴酒、蘭姆酒和伏特加是強的部分。Triple sec 和香艾酒含有酒精並帶來甜味。調酒用苦精是苦味調味料，不是弱元素。","What does a flavoured syrup do in a cocktail?":"風味糖漿在調酒中有什麼作用？","It sweetens and adds complexity":"增甜並增添複雜度","It raises the drink's alcoholic strength":"提高飲品的酒精濃度","It replaces ice for chilling":"取代冰塊來冰鎮","It removes bitterness without adding any sweetness":"去除苦味而不增添任何甜味","A flavoured syrup brings sweetness plus an extra flavour, so more complexity.":"風味糖漿帶來甜味加上額外的風味，所以更複雜。","Syrups are non-alcoholic and do not raise strength. They do not chill: that is the ice's job. They balance bitterness precisely because they are sweet, like almond orgeat.":"糖漿不含酒精，不會提高濃度。它們不冰鎮：那是冰的工作。它們正是因為甜才能平衡苦味，例如杏仁 orgeat。","Olives and maraschino cherries are less delicate than fresh fruit. What still applies to them?":"橄欖和馬拉斯奇諾櫻桃沒有新鮮水果那麼嬌貴。但哪一點仍然適用？","They still need proper storage":"仍然需要妥善保存","They must be thrown away each night":"必須每晚丟掉","They must be cut fresh for every drink":"每杯飲品都必須現切","They can be left out indefinitely":"可以無限期放在外面","Preserved ingredients are hardier but still need correct storage.":"保存食品較耐放，但仍需要正確保存。","Throwing everything away at night is the rule for cut fresh fruit, not preserved products. They do not need cutting for each drink. Leaving them out indefinitely would spoil them.":"每晚全部丟掉是切開的新鮮水果的規則，不是保存食品的。它們不需要每杯現切。無限期放在外面會讓它們變質。","Besides chilling and diluting fast, what does crushed ice give a Mojito or Caipirinha?":"除了快速冰鎮和稀釋，碎冰還帶給 Mojito 或 Caipirinha 什麼？","A distinctive look":"獨特的外觀","Extra sweetness":"額外的甜味","A higher alcohol level":"更高的酒精濃度","A frothy texture like that of egg white":"像蛋白那樣的泡沫質地","Crushed ice, as well as chilling and diluting, gives these cocktails their typical look.":"碎冰除了冰鎮和稀釋，也賦予這些調酒典型的外觀。","Ice adds no sugar: as it melts it adds water, a 'weak' component. For the same reason it lowers, not raises, the alcohol level. A frothy texture comes from shaken egg white, as in a Pisco Sour.":"冰不增添糖：融化時加的是水，是「弱」成分。基於同樣的理由，它降低而不是提高酒精濃度。泡沫質地來自搖盪的蛋白，例如 Pisco Sour。","Orgeat is an almond syrup. What else traditionally flavours it?":"Orgeat 是杏仁糖漿。傳統上還用什麼為它調味？","Rose water or orange flower water":"玫瑰水或橙花水","Coffee and vanilla in equal parts":"等量的咖啡和香草","A few dashes of bitters and a little olive brine":"幾滴苦精和一點橄欖鹽水","Orgeat combines almond with rose water or orange flower water.":"Orgeat 結合了杏仁與玫瑰水或橙花水。","It is an example of a flavoured syrup, which sweetens and adds complexity. Cranberry juice is a ready-made juice typical of the Cosmopolitan. Bitters and olive brine go into drinks, such as a dirty Martini, not into syrups.":"它是風味糖漿的例子，能增甜並增添複雜度。蔓越莓汁是 Cosmopolitan 典型的現成果汁。苦精和橄欖鹽水是加進飲品（例如 dirty Martini）的，不是加進糖漿。","According to the basic rule, what must a garnish NEVER do?":"依照基本原則，裝飾物絕對不能做什麼？","Spoil the look of the drink":"破壞飲品的外觀","Add an aroma to the drink":"為飲品增添香氣","Echo an aroma already present in the cocktail":"呼應調酒中已有的香氣","Be a preserved item, such as an olive or a maraschino cherry":"是保存食品，例如橄欖或馬拉斯奇諾櫻桃","A garnish is first of all decoration: it must add to the drink's appearance, never detract from it.":"裝飾物首先是裝飾：它必須為飲品的外觀加分，絕不能扣分。","A garnish often adds a light aroma that highlights or complements one in the drink: that is a plus, not a mistake. Olives and maraschino cherries are among the most common garnishes; they just need proper storage.":"裝飾物常增添淡淡的香氣，突顯或襯托飲品中的某種香氣：那是加分，不是錯誤。橄欖和馬拉斯奇諾櫻桃是最常見的裝飾物之一；只是需要妥善保存。","In a Sidecar (Cognac, lemon juice, triple sec), which ingredient plays the 'sweet' role?":"在 Sidecar（Cognac、檸檬汁、triple sec）中，哪一種材料扮演「甜」的角色？","The triple sec":"Triple sec","The Cognac":"Cognac","The lemon juice":"檸檬汁","The meltwater from the shaker ice":"雪克杯中冰塊融化的水","Triple sec is a liqueur, so it is sweet: here it takes the place of the simple syrup in a classic sour.":"Triple sec 是利口酒，所以是甜的：在這裡它取代了經典酸酒中的簡易糖漿。","Cognac is the 'strong' part, the main alcoholic element. Lemon juice is the sour part that balances the sweetness. Meltwater adds to the 'weak' side, not to sweetness.":"Cognac 是「強」的部分，也就是主要的酒精元素。檸檬汁是平衡甜味的酸的部分。融冰水屬於「弱」的一側，不是甜味。","Which two 'scales' does a bartender use to make a balanced drink?":"調酒師用哪兩個「天平」來調出平衡的飲品？","Strong vs weak, and sour/bitter vs sweet":"強對弱，以及酸／苦對甜","Hot vs cold, and sweet vs salty":"熱對冷，以及甜對鹹","Shaken vs stirred, and long vs short":"搖盪對攪拌，以及長飲對短飲","Light vs dark, and fresh vs preserved":"淺對深，以及新鮮對保存","Most cocktails pair strong and weak elements with a sweet one and a sour or bitter one.":"大多數調酒把強和弱的元素，與一個甜的元素和一個酸或苦的元素搭配起來。","'Strong' is the alcoholic part; 'weak' covers juice, soda, tonic and meltwater. Shaking or stirring, long or short, are choices of technique and serve, not balance. Temperature, salt and garnish type are not the two basic scales.":"「強」是含酒精的部分；「弱」涵蓋果汁、蘇打水、通寧水和融冰水。搖盪或攪拌、長飲或短飲，是技術和供應方式的選擇，不是平衡。溫度、鹽和裝飾物的類型不是那兩個基本的天平。","What goes into a Moscow Mule?":"Moscow Mule 裡有什麼？","Vodka, ginger beer, lime":"伏特加、薑汁啤酒、萊姆","Whisky, ginger ale, bitters":"威士忌、薑汁汽水、苦精","Gin, lemon juice, simple syrup and soda":"琴酒、檸檬汁、簡易糖漿和蘇打水","A Moscow Mule is vodka topped with ginger beer, with lime.":"Moscow Mule 是伏特加加滿薑汁啤酒，再加萊姆。","Rum, cola and lime make a Cuba Libre; whisky, ginger ale and bitters a Horse's Neck; gin, lemon, syrup and soda a Tom Collins. The Moscow Mule is traditionally served in a Mule mug.":"蘭姆酒、可樂和萊姆是 Cuba Libre；威士忌、薑汁汽水和苦精是 Horse's Neck；琴酒、檸檬、糖漿和蘇打水是 Tom Collins。Moscow Mule 傳統上用 Mule 杯供應。","A customer orders a Cuba Libre. What is made?":"一位顧客點了 Cuba Libre。要調什麼？","Rum and cola with lime, over ice":"蘭姆酒和可樂加萊姆，加冰","Rum, lime juice and syrup, shaken and strained":"蘭姆酒、萊姆汁和糖漿，搖盪後濾出","Rum, mint, lime, sugar and soda on crushed ice":"蘭姆酒、薄荷、萊姆、糖和蘇打水，加碎冰","White rum, pineapple and coconut cream":"白蘭姆酒、鳳梨和椰漿","The Cuba Libre is a highball of rum and cola with lime.":"Cuba Libre 是蘭姆酒和可樂加萊姆的高球。","The other options describe other rum drinks: the Daiquiri (a shaken sour), the Mojito (Collins family) and the Piña Colada (a tropical drink). The Cuba Libre is built straight in a glass full of ice.":"其他選項描述的是別的蘭姆酒飲品：Daiquiri（搖盪的酸酒）、Mojito（Collins 家族）和 Piña Colada（熱帶飲品）。Cuba Libre 直接在裝滿冰的杯中直調。","Which method is normally used to make a highball?":"高球通常用哪一種方法調製？","Built in the glass over ice":"在杯中加冰直調","Shaken, then double strained with Hawthorne and fine sieve":"搖盪，再用 Hawthorne 和細濾網雙重過濾","Stirred and served straight up":"攪拌後 straight up 供應","Blended with crushed ice":"與碎冰一起用果汁機打","A highball is built by pouring the ingredients into a glass full of ice.":"高球的做法是把材料倒進裝滿冰的杯子直調。","Building is the simplest method and suits a long drink with a mixer. Shaking and straining is typical of sours, stirring of spirit-forward drinks, blending of smooth-textured drinks.":"直調是最簡單的方法，適合加調和飲料的長飲。搖盪後濾出是酸酒的典型做法，攪拌是烈酒主導型飲品的，用果汁機打則用於質地滑順的飲品。","Which highball contains whisky, ginger ale and bitters?":"哪一款高球含有威士忌、薑汁汽水和苦精？","Old Fashioned served in a tumbler":"用平底杯供應的 Old Fashioned","The Horse's Neck is a highball of whisky, ginger ale and a few dashes of bitters.":"Horse's Neck 是威士忌、薑汁汽水加幾滴苦精的高球。","The Moscow Mule uses vodka and ginger beer. The Old Fashioned and Rob Roy are spirit-forward whisky cocktails with no mixer, so they are not highballs.":"Moscow Mule 使用伏特加和薑汁啤酒。Old Fashioned 和 Rob Roy 是不加調和飲料的烈酒主導型威士忌調酒，所以不是高球。","Which balance defines the sour family?":"哪一種平衡定義了酸酒家族？","Strong, sour, sweet":"強、酸、甜","Strong and weak only, with a fizzy mixer":"只有強和弱，加上有氣泡的調和飲料","Strong, vermouth, bitters":"強、香艾酒、苦精","Sweet and bitter with no alcohol":"甜和苦，不含酒精","A sour combines a spirit, fresh citrus juice and a sweetener.":"酸酒結合了烈酒、新鮮柑橘汁和甜味劑。","Strong plus mixer describes the highball; spirit, vermouth and bitters the spirit-forward family. A drink with no alcohol would have no strong component.":"強加調和飲料描述的是高球；烈酒、香艾酒和苦精是烈酒主導型家族。不含酒精的飲品就沒有強的成分。","Why is a sour shaken rather than stirred?":"為什麼酸酒要搖盪而不是攪拌？","To add air and a light texture":"加入空氣，帶來輕盈的質地","To dilute it as much as possible and lower the strength sharply":"盡量稀釋，大幅降低濃度","To keep it perfectly clear":"保持完全清澈","To avoid breaking the ice":"避免把冰打碎","Shaking mixes, chills and aerates, giving sours a light, airy texture.":"搖盪能混合、冰鎮並打入空氣，讓酸酒有輕盈蓬鬆的質地。","Shaking chills fast and dilutes only slightly; stirring is what can dilute more. Shaking breaks ice into shards, which is why double straining is used, and the air makes the drink less clear.":"搖盪冰鎮得快，只略微稀釋；可能稀釋更多的是攪拌。搖盪會把冰打成碎片，所以才用雙重過濾，而空氣會讓飲品較不清澈。","In which sour is egg white considered essential?":"在哪一款酸酒中，蛋白被認為不可或缺？","Tommy's Margarita with agave syrup":"使用龍舌蘭糖漿的 Tommy's Margarita","In a Pisco Sour, egg white is essential for a smooth, mouthfilling texture.":"在 Pisco Sour 中，蛋白是柔順飽滿質地不可或缺的材料。","In a Whisky Sour egg white is optional, while the Daiquiri, Tommy's and Cosmopolitan normally do not include it. Egg white adds texture rather than flavour.":"在 Whisky Sour 中蛋白是可選的，Daiquiri、Tommy's 和 Cosmopolitan 則通常不加。蛋白增添的是質地，而不是風味。","What are the core ingredients of a Whisky Sour?":"Whisky Sour 的核心材料是什麼？","Bourbon or rye, lemon, simple syrup":"Bourbon 或 rye、檸檬、簡易糖漿","Scotch, sweet vermouth, bitters":"Scotch、甜香艾酒、苦精","Whisky, sugar and bitters, stirred and served in a tumbler":"威士忌、糖和苦精，攪拌後用平底杯供應","A Whisky Sour combines Bourbon or rye, lemon juice and syrup, with optional egg white.":"Whisky Sour 結合了 Bourbon 或 rye、檸檬汁和糖漿，蛋白可加可不加。","Scotch, sweet vermouth and bitters make a Rob Roy; whisky, sugar and bitters an Old Fashioned; whisky and ginger ale with bitters a Horse's Neck. Only the Whisky Sour has the citrus juice typical of sours.":"Scotch、甜香艾酒和苦精是 Rob Roy；威士忌、糖和苦精是 Old Fashioned；威士忌和薑汁汽水加苦精是 Horse's Neck。只有 Whisky Sour 有酸酒典型的柑橘汁。","Which sweetener characterises Tommy's Margarita?":"Tommy's Margarita 的特色是哪一種甜味劑？","Agave syrup":"龍舌蘭糖漿","Almond and orange-flower orgeat":"杏仁橙花 orgeat","Sweet vermouth":"甜香艾酒","Tommy's uses tequila, lime juice and agave syrup.":"Tommy's 使用 tequila、萊姆汁和龍舌蘭糖漿。","With triple sec instead of agave you get the classic Margarita. Orgeat and vermouth are not part of this recipe.":"用 triple sec 取代龍舌蘭糖漿就是經典的 Margarita。Orgeat 和香艾酒不在這個酒譜中。","Which spirit is the base of a Sidecar?":"Sidecar 的基酒是哪一種烈酒？","Vodka with cranberry juice":"伏特加加蔓越莓汁","The Sidecar combines Cognac, lemon juice and triple sec.":"Sidecar 結合了 Cognac、檸檬汁和 triple sec。","The same structure with tequila gives a Margarita; with vodka and cranberry, a Cosmopolitan. Gin is the base of none of these three triple sec sours.":"同樣的結構用 tequila 就是 Margarita；用伏特加和蔓越莓汁就是 Cosmopolitan。琴酒不是這三款 triple sec 酸酒中任何一款的基酒。","A bartender swaps the syrup in a tequila sour for triple sec. Which classic results?":"一位調酒師把 tequila 酸酒中的糖漿換成 triple sec。得到哪一款經典調酒？","A Margarita":"Margarita","A Paloma":"Paloma","A Tommy's Margarita":"Tommy's Margarita","A tequila Collins topped with soda":"加滿蘇打水的 tequila Collins","Tequila, lime and triple sec make a Margarita.":"Tequila、萊姆和 triple sec 就是 Margarita。","Tommy's is the agave-syrup version, the one before the swap. The Paloma and Collins are long drinks with soda, not short sours.":"Tommy's 是龍舌蘭糖漿的版本，也就是替換之前的那一款。Paloma 和 Collins 是加蘇打水的長飲，不是短酸酒。","Which ingredient sets the Cosmopolitan apart from other triple sec sours?":"哪一種材料讓 Cosmopolitan 有別於其他 triple sec 酸酒？","Freshly squeezed lemon juice":"現榨檸檬汁","Salt rim":"鹽口杯","The Cosmopolitan adds cranberry juice to lime, on a vodka base.":"Cosmopolitan 以伏特加為基酒，在萊姆之外加入蔓越莓汁。","It thus changes both the sweetener (triple sec) and the sour element. Lemon juice is typical of the Sidecar, the salt rim of the Margarita, and egg white of the Pisco Sour.":"所以它同時改變了甜味劑（triple sec）和酸的元素。檸檬汁是 Sidecar 的典型材料，鹽口杯是 Margarita 的，蛋白是 Pisco Sour 的。","How can a Collins be described compared with a sour?":"與酸酒相比，Collins 可以怎麼描述？","A sour lengthened with soda":"用蘇打水拉長的酸酒","A sour without citrus juice":"沒有柑橘汁的酸酒","A sour served hot":"熱的酸酒","A sour stirred and served straight up in a Martini glass":"攪拌後用 Martini 杯 straight up 供應的酸酒","A Collins is a sour made long with soda and served over cubes.":"Collins 是用蘇打水做成長飲、並加方冰塊供應的酸酒。","It keeps the sour's spirit, citrus and sweetener: without juice it would no longer be a sour. It is a cold long drink, neither hot nor short without ice.":"它保留了酸酒的烈酒、柑橘和甜味劑：沒有果汁就不再是酸酒。它是冷的長飲，既不是熱飲，也不是不加冰的短飲。","Which spirit is used in a Tom Collins?":"Tom Collins 使用哪一種烈酒？","White rum":"白蘭姆酒","Highly rectified neutral vodka":"高度精餾的中性伏特加","The Tom Collins is the family classic: gin, lemon, syrup and soda.":"Tom Collins 是這個家族的經典：琴酒、檸檬、糖漿和蘇打水。","With Cognac it becomes a Pierre Collins, with rum a Pedro Collins, with vodka a Vodka Collins: changing only the spirit creates the variations.":"用 Cognac 就變成 Pierre Collins，用蘭姆酒是 Pedro Collins，用伏特加是 Vodka Collins：只換烈酒就產生各種變化版。","A customer asks for a Pierre Collins. Which spirit is needed?":"一位顧客點了 Pierre Collins。需要哪一種烈酒？","Golden rum":"金色蘭姆酒","Old Tom-style gin, sweeter than London Dry":"Old Tom 風格的琴酒，比 London Dry 甜","The Pierre Collins is the Cognac version of the Collins.":"Pierre Collins 是 Collins 的 Cognac 版本。","Rum gives the Pedro Collins, gin the Tom Collins. Pisco is the base of the Pisco Sour, not of a named Collins.":"蘭姆酒做的是 Pedro Collins，琴酒做的是 Tom Collins。Pisco 是 Pisco Sour 的基酒，不是哪一款有名字的 Collins 的基酒。","What sets a Mojito apart from a plain rum Collins?":"Mojito 與單純的蘭姆酒 Collins 有什麼不同？","Mint leaves and crushed ice":"薄荷葉和碎冰","Triple sec instead of simple syrup":"用 triple sec 取代簡易糖漿","No soda":"沒有蘇打水","Vermouth and bitters":"香艾酒和苦精","The Mojito adds mint leaves and is served over crushed ice.":"Mojito 加入薄荷葉，並加碎冰供應。","The Mojito is a long drink with soda: without it, it would not belong to the Collins family. Triple sec, vermouth and bitters belong to other families.":"Mojito 是加蘇打水的長飲：沒有蘇打水就不屬於 Collins 家族。Triple sec、香艾酒和苦精屬於其他家族。","Which ingredient characterises the Paloma?":"Paloma 的特色是哪一種材料？","Cranberry juice and orange triple sec":"蔓越莓汁和柳橙 triple sec","The Paloma combines tequila, lime and grapefruit soda (or grapefruit juice and soda).":"Paloma 結合了 tequila、萊姆和葡萄柚汽水（或葡萄柚汁加蘇打水）。","Ginger beer belongs to the Moscow Mule, cola to the Cuba Libre, cranberry and triple sec to the Cosmopolitan. Grapefruit is what makes the Paloma distinctive.":"薑汁啤酒屬於 Moscow Mule，可樂屬於 Cuba Libre，蔓越莓汁和 triple sec 屬於 Cosmopolitan。葡萄柚是讓 Paloma 與眾不同的材料。","Stirred over ice and strained":"加冰攪拌後濾出","Shaken with egg white and double strained":"與蛋白一起搖盪並雙重過濾","Built in the glass and topped with soda":"在杯中直調並加滿蘇打水","They are stirred over cubes, then strained and served straight up or over ice.":"它們加方冰塊攪拌，再濾出，以 straight up 或加冰供應。","Stirring controls dilution precisely and keeps a silky texture. Shaking with egg white is typical of some sours, soda of the Collins, and blending of smooth-textured drinks.":"攪拌能精確控制稀釋，並保持絲滑的質地。與蛋白一起搖盪是某些酸酒的典型做法，蘇打水是 Collins 的，用果汁機打則用於質地滑順的飲品。","A customer asks for a 'drier' Martini. What does the bartender do?":"一位顧客想要「更 dry」的 Martini。調酒師怎麼做？","Uses less vermouth":"少用一點香艾酒","Adds more vermouth to the mixing glass":"在攪拌杯中加更多香艾酒","Adds olive brine":"加入橄欖鹽水","Shakes it instead of stirring":"用搖盪取代攪拌","Less vermouth makes a Martini 'drier'.":"香艾酒越少，Martini 越「dry」。","More vermouth makes it 'wet', olive brine makes it 'dirty'. Changing the method alters texture and dilution, not how dry it is.":"香艾酒多就是「wet」，加橄欖鹽水就是「dirty」。改變調製方法會改變質地和稀釋度，不是它有多 dry。","What makes a Martini 'dirty'?":"什麼讓 Martini 變成「dirty」？","Olive brine":"橄欖鹽水","A grapefruit twist":"葡萄柚皮捲","Lots of sweet vermouth and a few dashes of orange bitters":"大量甜香艾酒和幾滴柳橙苦精","Ice left in the glass":"留在杯中的冰","A Martini with olive brine is called 'dirty'.":"加了橄欖鹽水的 Martini 稱為「dirty」。","A grapefruit twist is a garnish that changes the aroma, not the 'dirty' style. More vermouth makes a Martini 'wet', and serving it on ice changes the serve, not the name.":"葡萄柚皮捲是改變香氣的裝飾物，不是「dirty」的風格。香艾酒多會讓 Martini 變成「wet」，加冰供應改變的是供應方式，不是名稱。","Which spirit replaces rye in a Rob Roy?":"在 Rob Roy 中，哪一種烈酒取代了 rye？","Canadian rye whisky":"加拿大的 rye whisky","A Manhattan made with Scotch whisky is called a Rob Roy.":"用 Scotch 威士忌調的 Manhattan 稱為 Rob Roy。","With Irish whiskey the drink is an Emerald. Bourbon often replaces rye, but the drink is still a Manhattan, and Canadian whisky does not create a new name in this family.":"用愛爾蘭威士忌就是 Emerald。Bourbon 常取代 rye，但飲品仍然是 Manhattan，而加拿大威士忌在這個家族中不會產生新的名稱。","What is a 'Perfect Manhattan'?":"什麼是「Perfect Manhattan」？","Equal parts dry and sweet vermouth":"不甜和甜的香艾酒各半","A Manhattan with a spoon of maraschino syrup":"加一匙馬拉斯奇諾櫻桃糖漿的 Manhattan","Dry vermouth only":"只用不甜的香艾酒","A Manhattan with Irish whiskey":"用愛爾蘭威士忌的 Manhattan","A Perfect Manhattan uses equal parts dry and sweet vermouth.":"Perfect Manhattan 使用等量的不甜香艾酒和甜香艾酒。","Maraschino syrup gives a Sweet Manhattan, dry vermouth alone a Dry Manhattan, and Irish whiskey turns the drink into an Emerald.":"馬拉斯奇諾櫻桃糖漿做的是 Sweet Manhattan，只用不甜香艾酒是 Dry Manhattan，愛爾蘭威士忌則讓它變成 Emerald。","What do the Old Fashioned and Sazerac use to balance the spirit, instead of vermouth?":"Old Fashioned 和 Sazerac 不用香艾酒，而用什麼來平衡烈酒？","Sugar and bitters":"糖和苦精","Lemon juice and egg white":"檸檬汁和蛋白","Soda and lime":"蘇打水和萊姆","Triple sec and cranberry juice":"Triple sec 和蔓越莓汁","The Old Fashioned and Sazerac are balanced with sugar and bitters.":"Old Fashioned 和 Sazerac 用糖和苦精取得平衡。","Vermouth balances the Manhattan and Martini. Lemon and egg white belong to sours, soda and lime to highballs and Collins, triple sec and cranberry to the Cosmopolitan.":"香艾酒平衡的是 Manhattan 和 Martini。檸檬和蛋白屬於酸酒，蘇打水和萊姆屬於高球和 Collins，triple sec 和蔓越莓汁屬於 Cosmopolitan。","Which ingredients, in equal parts, make a Negroni?":"哪些材料等量組成 Negroni？","Gin, red vermouth, aperitif bitter":"琴酒、紅香艾酒、開胃苦味酒","Gin, dry vermouth and olive brine":"琴酒、不甜香艾酒和橄欖鹽水","Rye, sweet vermouth, cocktail bitters":"Rye、甜香艾酒、調酒用苦精","Vodka, triple sec, lime":"伏特加、triple sec、萊姆","A Negroni combines equal parts gin, red vermouth and an aperitif bitter.":"Negroni 結合了等量的琴酒、紅香艾酒和開胃苦味酒。","Gin, dry vermouth and brine describe a Dirty Martini; rye, sweet vermouth and bitters a Manhattan; vodka, triple sec and lime suggest a Cosmopolitan. In a Negroni the aperitif bitter is a main ingredient, not a few dashes.":"琴酒、不甜香艾酒和鹽水描述的是 Dirty Martini；rye、甜香艾酒和苦精是 Manhattan；伏特加、triple sec 和萊姆讓人想到 Cosmopolitan。在 Negroni 中，開胃苦味酒是主要材料，不是幾滴而已。","What makes cocktails different from almost every other drink?":"什麼讓調酒有別於幾乎所有其他飲品？","They are made at the point of service":"它們是在供應的當下調製的","They always contain at least three spirits":"它們一律含有至少三種烈酒","They are bottled at the distillery":"它們在蒸餾廠裝瓶","They are always served hot":"它們一律是熱飲","Cocktails are the only drinks made at the moment they are served.":"調酒是唯一在供應當下才製作的飲品。","Many cocktails contain a single spirit, such as the Daiquiri. They are not bottled at the distillery. Nearly all are served cold, with rare exceptions such as Irish coffee.":"許多調酒只含一種烈酒，例如 Daiquiri。它們不是在蒸餾廠裝瓶的。幾乎都是冷飲，只有 Irish coffee 這類少數例外。","When building a drink in the glass, how much ice is used?":"在杯中直調飲品時，用多少冰？","Glass full of cubes, filled to about 1 cm from the top":"杯中裝滿方冰塊，飲品加到離杯口約 1 公分","Two or three cubes to avoid dilution":"兩、三顆冰塊，以免稀釋","None: ice is served on the side":"不用：冰另外附上","Only crushed ice, up to half way":"只用碎冰，裝到一半","The glass is filled with cubed ice, with the drink about one centimetre from the top.":"杯子裝滿方冰塊，飲品離杯口大約一公分。","A few cubes would melt quickly, diluting instead of chilling. Ice on the side does not chill the drink. Crushed ice is only used in certain drinks, such as the Mojito and Caipirinha.":"幾顆冰塊很快就會融化，結果是稀釋而不是冰鎮。另外附上的冰無法冰鎮飲品。碎冰只用於某些飲品，例如 Mojito 和 Caipirinha。","Why is a shaken drink double strained while a stirred one usually is not?":"為什麼搖盪的飲品要雙重過濾，攪拌的通常不用？","Shaking breaks the ice into shards":"搖盪會把冰打成碎片","A stirred drink never contains ice":"攪拌的飲品從不含冰","The Julep strainer is finer than a sieve":"Julep 隔冰匙比濾網細","Shaking creates extra alcohol to hold back":"搖盪會產生需要擋住的額外酒精","Shaking breaks up the ice and the fine sieve removes the shards; stirring does not do this.":"搖盪把冰打碎，細濾網再去除碎片；攪拌不會這樣。","Stirred drinks are also made with cubed ice, which stays in the mixing glass. The Julep strainer is not finer than a sieve. Shaking does not create alcohol: it adds air and dilution.":"攪拌的飲品也是用方冰塊調製的，冰塊留在攪拌杯中。Julep 隔冰匙並不比濾網細。搖盪不會產生酒精：它增加的是空氣和稀釋。","What must be avoided when muddling a delicate ingredient such as mint?":"搗壓薄荷這類嬌嫩的材料時，必須避免什麼？","Overworking it":"處理過頭","Using a muddler":"使用搗棒","Muddling it in the shaker":"在雪克杯中搗壓","Releasing its aromatic oils":"釋出它的芳香精油","Delicate ingredients are easily overworked, so care is needed.":"嬌嫩的材料很容易處理過頭，所以要小心。","The muddler is exactly the right tool. Muddling can be done in the glass or shaker, depending on how the drink is made. Releasing juice and aromatic oils is the very point of muddling.":"搗棒正是合適的工具。依飲品的做法，可以在杯中或雪克杯中搗壓。釋出汁液和芳香精油正是搗壓的目的。","Which technique uses a blender with crushed ice to give a very smooth-textured drink?":"哪一種技術用果汁機加碎冰，做出質地非常滑順的飲品？","Building":"直調","Muddling":"搗壓","Double straining":"雙重過濾","In blending, the blades break up the crushed ice completely and create a smooth texture.":"用果汁機打時，刀片把碎冰完全打散，產生滑順的質地。","Building means pouring the ingredients into a glass with ice. Muddling crushes fruit or herbs. Double straining removes ice shards, the opposite of blending ice into the drink.":"直調是把材料倒進有冰的杯子。搗壓是壓碎水果或香草。雙重過濾去除碎冰，與把冰打進飲品恰恰相反。","How are new cocktails created within a family?":"同一個家族中的新調酒是怎麼創造出來的？","By swapping one ingredient in an already balanced recipe":"在已經平衡的酒譜中替換一種材料","By doubling every measure":"把每一份的量加倍","By removing the weak element":"去掉弱元素","By always using a new glass":"每次都用新的杯子","Starting from a balanced recipe and replacing one ingredient: that is how families are related.":"從平衡的酒譜出發，替換一種材料：各個家族就是這樣彼此相關的。","For example, swapping the spirit turns a Tom Collins into a Vodka Collins. Doubling the measures does not change the drink. Removing the weak element or just changing the glass does not create a new balanced recipe.":"例如換掉烈酒，Tom Collins 就變成 Vodka Collins。把份量加倍不會改變飲品。去掉弱元素或只換杯子，不會創造出新的平衡酒譜。","What distinguishes a long drink from a short drink?":"長飲與短飲有什麼區別？","A greater level of dilution":"稀釋程度更高","It contains more spirit":"含有更多烈酒","It is served without ice":"不加冰供應","It is always made in a mixing glass":"一律在攪拌杯中調製","Long drinks typically have much more dilution, with a mixer and plenty of ice.":"長飲通常稀釋得多得多，有調和飲料和大量的冰。","The extra volume comes from the weak element, not more spirit. Long drinks are served over cubed ice. The mixing glass is for stirred drinks, which are usually short.":"多出來的體積來自弱元素，不是更多的烈酒。長飲加方冰塊供應。攪拌杯用於攪拌類飲品，那些通常是短飲。","A gin and tonic belongs to which cocktail family?":"琴通寧屬於哪一個調酒家族？","Spirit plus mixer, served long over ice: a highball, the simplest family.":"烈酒加調和飲料，加冰做成長飲：這是高球，最簡單的家族。","A sour needs citrus and sweetener, shaken. A Collins is a sour lengthened with soda. Spirit-forward drinks are short and strong, not long with tonic.":"酸酒需要柑橘和甜味劑，並搖盪。Collins 是用蘇打水拉長的酸酒。烈酒主導型飲品短而烈，不是加通寧水的長飲。","What does egg white do in a sour?":"蛋白在酸酒中有什麼作用？","Gives a smooth, mouthfilling texture":"帶來柔順飽滿的質地","Raises the drink's acidity":"提高飲品的酸度","Replaces the syrup as the sweetener":"取代糖漿作為甜味劑","Turns the drink deep yellow":"讓飲品變成深黃色","Egg white makes a sour especially smooth and mouthfilling.":"蛋白讓酸酒格外柔順飽滿。","Acidity comes from the citrus juice, sweetness from the syrup. Egg white neither sweetens nor colours. It is essential in a Pisco Sour and optional in other sours.":"酸度來自柑橘汁，甜味來自糖漿。蛋白既不增甜，也不上色。它在 Pisco Sour 中不可或缺，在其他酸酒中則是可選的。","Which finishing touch is typical of the Margarita?":"哪一種最後的點綴是 Margarita 的典型做法？","A dusting of nutmeg":"撒一點肉豆蔻","An olive in the glass":"杯中放一顆橄欖","A top of soda water":"最後加一點蘇打水","The Margarita is traditionally served with a salt-rimmed glass.":"Margarita 傳統上用鹽口杯供應。","Nutmeg is a garnish grated over other drinks. The olive belongs to the Martini. Adding soda would turn the sour into a long, Collins-style drink.":"肉豆蔻是刨在其他飲品上的裝飾物。橄欖屬於 Martini。加蘇打水會把酸酒變成 Collins 風格的長飲。","What are the two possible ways to make a Collins?":"調製 Collins 有哪兩種可能的做法？","Shake strong, sour and sweet then top with soda, or build it in the glass":"把強、酸、甜搖盪後加滿蘇打水，或在杯中直調","Stir in a mixing glass and serve straight up":"在攪拌杯中攪拌，再 straight up 供應","Blend with crushed ice or serve it hot":"與碎冰一起用果汁機打，或做成熱飲","Shake everything including the soda, then double strain":"連蘇打水一起全部搖盪，再雙重過濾","A Collins can be shaken (without the soda) and then topped up, or built directly over ice.":"Collins 可以先搖盪（不含蘇打水）再加滿，也可以直接在冰塊上直調。","Serving straight up is typical of spirit-forward drinks, not a long drink. A Collins is served cold over cubes. Shaking soda would kill the bubbles and could burst the shaker open.":"Straight up 供應是烈酒主導型飲品的典型做法，不是長飲。Collins 加方冰塊冷飲供應。搖盪蘇打水會讓氣泡消失，還可能把雪克杯衝開。","Which Collins and spirit pairing is correct?":"哪一組 Collins 與烈酒的配對是正確的？","Pedro Collins: rum":"Pedro Collins：蘭姆酒","Pedro Collins: tequila":"Pedro Collins：tequila","Pierre Collins: Scotch whisky":"Pierre Collins：Scotch 威士忌","Tom Collins: vodka":"Tom Collins：伏特加","The Pedro Collins uses rum instead of gin.":"Pedro Collins 用蘭姆酒取代琴酒。","The Pierre Collins uses Cognac and the Tom Collins uses gin. The vodka version is simply called a Vodka Collins. Swapping the spirit is the easiest way to create Collins variations.":"Pierre Collins 使用 Cognac，Tom Collins 使用琴酒。伏特加版本就直接叫 Vodka Collins。換掉烈酒是創造 Collins 變化版最簡單的方法。","Compared with a Collins, what sets a punch apart?":"與 Collins 相比，punch 有什麼不同？","Juices instead of soda, plus bitters or spices":"用果汁取代蘇打水，再加苦精或香料","No citrus juice at all":"完全沒有柑橘汁","It is served short, without ice":"做成短飲，不加冰","It is made only with vermouth and bitters":"只用香艾酒和苦精製作","Punch has a sour base but uses juices (often tropical) instead of soda, and adds bitters or spices.":"Punch 以酸酒為基礎，但用果汁（常是熱帶果汁）取代蘇打水，並加入苦精或香料。","The sour base includes lemon or lime juice, so the second option is false. Punch is a long drink. Vermouth and bitters are more typical of spirit-forward drinks such as the Negroni.":"酸酒的基礎包含檸檬汁或萊姆汁，所以第二個選項是錯的。Punch 是長飲。香艾酒和苦精更是 Negroni 這類烈酒主導型飲品的典型材料。","Which spirit is punch most closely associated with today?":"如今 punch 與哪一種烈酒的關係最密切？","Today punch is most closely linked with rum, although other spirits can be used.":"如今 punch 與蘭姆酒的關係最密切，雖然也可以使用其他烈酒。","Gin, vodka and whisky can appear in a punch, but they are not the main association. Punch has a long, complicated history. Recipes and proportions vary enormously.":"琴酒、伏特加和威士忌都可以出現在 punch 中，但不是主要的聯想。Punch 有漫長而複雜的歷史。酒譜和比例差異極大。","A group of friends orders a punch to share. How is it served?":"一群朋友點了一份 punch 一起喝。怎麼供應？","In a large bowl with a ladle":"裝在大碗裡，附一支長柄勺","In shot glasses":"裝在 shot 杯裡","In a single Martini glass":"裝在一個 Martini 杯裡","In a sealed bottle opened at the table":"裝在密封的瓶中，在桌邊打開","As a sharing drink, punch comes in a large bowl and guests serve themselves with a ladle.":"作為共享的飲品，punch 裝在大碗裡，客人用長柄勺自己舀。","Shots are downed in one and not shared from a common vessel. The Martini glass is for one short drink. Cocktails are made to order, not delivered bottled.":"Shot 是一口喝完的，不是從共用容器分享的。Martini 杯用於一杯短飲。調酒是現點現做的，不是裝瓶送上的。","Compared with the other families, what characterises spirit-forward cocktails?":"與其他家族相比，烈酒主導型調酒有什麼特點？","They are higher in alcohol":"酒精濃度較高","They contain no spirit":"不含烈酒","They are always topped with soda":"一律加滿蘇打水","They rely on tropical juices and spices":"靠熱帶果汁和香料","Spirit-forward cocktails are higher in alcohol and celebrate their core spirit.":"烈酒主導型調酒酒精濃度較高，並彰顯它的核心烈酒。","The spirit is in fact the star. Soda belongs to highballs and Collins drinks. Tropical juices and spices point to punch.":"烈酒其實就是主角。蘇打水屬於高球和 Collins 類飲品。熱帶果汁和香料指向 punch。","Why is the amount of stirring so critical in a spirit-forward cocktail?":"為什麼攪拌的程度對烈酒主導型調酒這麼關鍵？","The ice controls the dilution":"冰控制著稀釋","Long stirring adds sugar":"攪拌久了會增添糖","It is needed to whip the egg white":"要靠它把蛋白打發","Brief stirring makes the alcohol evaporate":"攪拌太短會讓酒精蒸發","Ice chills and at the same time sets the dilution: too much or too little unbalances the drink.":"冰在冰鎮的同時也決定了稀釋：太多或太少都會讓飲品失衡。","Stirring adds no sugar. Egg white is used in shaken sours, not stirred drinks. Stirring time does not evaporate alcohol to any meaningful degree.":"攪拌不增添糖。蛋白用於搖盪的酸酒，不是攪拌類飲品。攪拌時間不會讓酒精有任何明顯的蒸發。","After stirring, how can a spirit-forward cocktail be served?":"攪拌後，烈酒主導型調酒可以怎麼供應？","Strained, either straight up or over cubed ice":"濾出後，以 straight up 或加方冰塊供應","Only over crushed ice":"只能加碎冰","Topped with soda in a highball":"用高球杯加滿蘇打水","It is strained off the ice and served straight up or over fresh cubes.":"把它從冰中濾出，以 straight up 或加新的方冰塊供應。","A Martini is usually served straight up and an Old Fashioned on ice: both are spirit-forward. Crushed ice is typical of drinks such as the Mojito. Soda and hot drinks belong to other families.":"Martini 通常 straight up 供應，Old Fashioned 則加冰：兩者都是烈酒主導型。碎冰是 Mojito 這類飲品的典型做法。蘇打水和熱飲屬於其他家族。","Which statement about the Martini's garnish is correct?":"關於 Martini 的裝飾物，下列哪一項正確？","It affects flavour more than in almost any other drink":"它對風味的影響幾乎比其他任何飲品都大","It is purely decorative and changes nothing":"它純粹是裝飾，不改變任何東西","It must always be a maraschino cherry":"一律必須是馬拉斯奇諾櫻桃","It is only added to the dirty version":"只有 dirty 的版本才加","In a Martini the garnish (lemon twist, grapefruit twist or olive) has a big impact on flavour.":"在 Martini 中，裝飾物（檸檬皮捲、葡萄柚皮捲或橄欖）對風味有很大的影響。","In such a pared-back drink, every added aroma shows. A maraschino cherry is not a classic Martini garnish. The dirty version is defined by olive brine, not by having a garnish.":"在這麼精簡的飲品中，每一種添加的香氣都很明顯。馬拉斯奇諾櫻桃不是經典的 Martini 裝飾物。Dirty 的版本是由橄欖鹽水定義的，不是有沒有裝飾物。","How is a Sweet Manhattan made?":"Sweet Manhattan 怎麼調？","By adding a spoon of maraschino syrup":"加一匙馬拉斯奇諾櫻桃糖漿","By using dry vermouth instead of sweet":"用不甜的香艾酒取代甜的","By swapping the rye for Irish whiskey":"把 rye 換成愛爾蘭威士忌","By using half dry and half sweet vermouth":"用一半不甜、一半甜的香艾酒","A spoon of maraschino syrup sweetens the Manhattan: that is the Sweet Manhattan.":"一匙馬拉斯奇諾櫻桃糖漿讓 Manhattan 變甜：這就是 Sweet Manhattan。","Dry vermouth makes a Dry Manhattan. Irish whiskey changes the name to Emerald. Half and half is the Perfect Manhattan.":"不甜的香艾酒做的是 Dry Manhattan。愛爾蘭威士忌讓名稱變成 Emerald。各半則是 Perfect Manhattan。","A customer wants a less sweet Manhattan. Which variation fits?":"一位顧客想要比較不甜的 Manhattan。哪一種變化版合適？","A Dry Manhattan, with dry vermouth":"Dry Manhattan，用不甜的香艾酒","A Sweet Manhattan, with maraschino syrup":"Sweet Manhattan，加馬拉斯奇諾櫻桃糖漿","A Rob Roy, made with Scotch whisky":"Rob Roy，用 Scotch 威士忌調製","A Manhattan with double the sweet vermouth":"甜香艾酒加倍的 Manhattan","Dry vermouth instead of sweet gives the Dry Manhattan, which is less sweet.":"用不甜的香艾酒取代甜的，就是 Dry Manhattan，比較不甜。","Maraschino syrup and double sweet vermouth would make the drink even sweeter. The Rob Roy changes the whisky, not the sweetness. The choice of vermouth is the main lever on sweetness.":"馬拉斯奇諾櫻桃糖漿和加倍的甜香艾酒會讓飲品更甜。Rob Roy 改變的是威士忌，不是甜度。香艾酒的選擇是調整甜度的主要手段。","What is a Manhattan made with Irish whiskey called?":"用愛爾蘭威士忌調的 Manhattan 叫做什麼？","With Irish whiskey instead of rye, the Manhattan becomes an Emerald.":"用愛爾蘭威士忌取代 rye，Manhattan 就變成 Emerald。","The Rob Roy uses Scotch whisky. The Perfect Manhattan changes the vermouth, not the whisky. The Pierre Collins is a Cognac Collins.":"Rob Roy 使用 Scotch 威士忌。Perfect Manhattan 改變的是香艾酒，不是威士忌。Pierre Collins 是 Cognac 的 Collins。","A customer asks for a wet Martini. What does the bartender do?":"一位顧客點了 wet Martini。調酒師怎麼做？","Uses more vermouth":"多用一點香艾酒","Serves it over crushed ice":"加碎冰供應","Tops it with tonic water":"加滿通寧水","More vermouth makes a Martini wetter; less makes it drier.":"香艾酒越多，Martini 越 wet；越少就越 dry。","Olive brine makes a dirty Martini. A Martini is usually served straight up, not over crushed ice. Tonic would turn it into a long drink.":"橄欖鹽水做的是 dirty Martini。Martini 通常 straight up 供應，不加碎冰。通寧水會把它變成長飲。","Which family does the Mojito belong to?":"Mojito 屬於哪一個家族？","Rum, lime, sugar and soda: the Mojito is a Collins enhanced with mint and served over crushed ice.":"蘭姆酒、萊姆、糖和蘇打水：Mojito 是加了薄荷、以碎冰供應的 Collins。","It is not spirit-forward because it is long and contains citrus. A punch would use juices instead of soda. A highball would lack the sour–sweet structure of a sour.":"它不是烈酒主導型，因為它是長飲並含有柑橘。Punch 會用果汁取代蘇打水。高球則沒有酸酒那種酸甜結構。","Which family does the Cosmopolitan belong to?":"Cosmopolitan 屬於哪一個家族？","Vodka, lime and triple sec as the sweetener, plus cranberry: it is a more complex sour.":"伏特加、萊姆，以 triple sec 為甜味劑，再加蔓越莓汁：它是較複雜的酸酒。","It has no soda or mixer, so it is neither a highball nor a Collins. It contains citrus and is shaken, so it is not spirit-forward. Like the Margarita and Sidecar, it comes from replacing syrup with triple sec.":"它沒有蘇打水或調和飲料，所以既不是高球，也不是 Collins。它含有柑橘並經過搖盪，所以不是烈酒主導型。和 Margarita、Sidecar 一樣，它來自用 triple sec 取代糖漿。","Which setting is ideal for a spirits tasting?":"哪一種環境最適合品飲烈酒？","Odour-free, with natural light and white surfaces":"沒有異味，有自然光和白色的檯面","A busy bar, to taste in real conditions":"熱鬧的酒吧，在真實情境中品嚐","A dark cellar lit by soft red light":"以柔和紅光照明的昏暗酒窖","A kitchen, so food can be paired at the same time":"廚房，這樣可以同時搭配食物","A neutral, well-lit room with white surfaces avoids outside influences on nose and eyes.":"中性、光線充足、有白色檯面的房間，能避免外在因素影響嗅覺和視覺。","Cooking smells, perfume or smoke in a bar or kitchen mask the sample's aromas. Coloured light makes colour impossible to judge. White surfaces provide a backdrop for checking clarity and shade.":"酒吧或廚房裡的烹調氣味、香水或菸味會掩蓋樣品的香氣。有色的燈光讓人無法判斷顏色。白色的檯面提供檢查清澈度和色調的背景。","Six different spirits are compared in a tasting. Why use the same type of glass for all of them?":"一場品飲要比較六款不同的烈酒。為什麼全部使用同一種杯子？","To make fair comparisons":"為了公平比較","Because the law requires it in every bar":"因為法律要求每家酒吧都這樣做","Because each different glass changes the alcoholic strength":"因為不同的杯子會改變酒精濃度","To save on washing up":"為了少洗一點杯子","Some glasses suit particular spirits, but in a tasting one model keeps comparisons fair.":"有些杯子適合特定的烈酒，但在品飲中用同一款才能讓比較公平。","Glass shape affects how aromas come across: changing it would skew the comparison. There is no legal requirement. The glass does not change the liquid's strength.":"杯形會影響香氣的呈現：更換杯子會讓比較失準。沒有法律要求。杯子不會改變液體的濃度。","What shape is a good spirits tasting glass?":"好的烈酒品飲杯是什麼形狀？","A stemmed tulip with room for water":"有杯腳的鬱金香杯，並有加水的空間","A straight, stemless shot glass":"直身、無杯腳的 shot 杯","A wide, shallow coupe that opens outwards":"向外敞開的寬淺碟形杯","A heavy, wide tumbler designed to hold ice":"為裝冰塊而設計的厚重寬口平底杯","A rounded bowl, sides narrowing to concentrate aromas, and a stem so the liquid is not warmed.":"圓潤的杯身、向上收窄的杯壁以集中香氣，還有杯腳，以免把酒液握熱。","A shot glass is too small for water and does not concentrate aromas. An open coupe disperses them. A tumbler is held with the hand around the liquid, which warms it.":"Shot 杯太小，沒有加水的空間，也不能集中香氣。敞口的淺碟杯會讓香氣散掉。平底杯是用手握住酒液所在的部位，會把它握熱。","How much spirit is recommended for a tasting sample?":"品飲樣品建議倒多少烈酒？","About 10 cL":"大約 10 cL","Enough to fill the glass halfway":"足以把杯子裝到半滿","A sample of about 1.5 cL (half a US fluid ounce) is enough.":"大約 1.5 cL（半美制液量盎司）的樣品就夠了。","Larger pours are pointless and leave little room for water. A half-full glass would make it hard to nose without being overwhelmed by alcohol. With many samples, small amounts also help you stay clear-headed.":"倒更多沒有意義，還讓加水的空間變小。半滿的杯子會讓人聞香時容易被酒精嗆到。樣品很多時，少量也有助於保持頭腦清醒。","Why does a spirit's appearance say little about its type, quality or age?":"為什麼烈酒的外觀不太能說明它的類型、品質或年數？","Colour can be altered afterwards":"顏色可以事後改變","All spirits share the same amber colour":"所有烈酒都是同樣的琥珀色","The glass always changes the shade":"杯子總會改變色調","Colour only appears once water is added":"加水之後才會出現顏色","Caramel, oak and filtration can add or remove colour, so appearance can mislead.":"焦糖色、橡木和過濾可以增添或去除顏色，所以外觀可能誤導人。","Spirits range from colourless to brown and beyond, so they do not share one colour. A good glass does not alter the shade. Appearance is in fact judged before adding water.":"烈酒從無色到棕色甚至更深都有，所以並不是同一種顏色。好的杯子不會改變色調。外觀其實是在加水之前判斷的。","What colour is every spirit as it comes off the still?":"所有烈酒離開蒸餾器時是什麼顏色？","Colourless, water-white":"無色，清澈如水","Gold, if the raw material is a grain":"金黃色，如果原料是穀物","Amber, if it comes from grapes":"琥珀色，如果來自葡萄","All spirits start clear: any colour is added after distillation.":"所有烈酒一開始都是清澈的：任何顏色都是蒸餾後添加的。","The raw material does not colour the spirit, because colour does not travel with vapour. Gold and amber come mainly from oak or caramel. That is why colour does not reveal origin.":"原料不會為烈酒上色，因為顏色不會隨蒸氣移動。金黃色和琥珀色主要來自橡木或焦糖色。所以顏色無法透露來源。","A premium spirit turns slightly hazy when water is added. What might explain it?":"一款高級烈酒加水後略微變混濁。可能的解釋是什麼？","It may be unfiltered: not necessarily a fault":"它可能未經過濾：不一定是缺陷","It is certainly cork-tainted":"它一定有軟木塞污染","It contains too many heads":"它含有太多酒頭","It has been sweetened with too much sugar":"它加了太多糖","Some premium spirits are unfiltered and can turn hazy when chilled or diluted.":"有些高級烈酒未經過濾，冰鎮或稀釋時可能變混濁。","Cork taint and heads are recognised on the nose (damp cardboard, solvent), not by haze. Sugar is detected on the palate. Generally a hazy spirit is seen as faulty, but this is a known exception.":"軟木塞污染和酒頭是靠嗅覺辨認的（濕紙板、溶劑），不是靠混濁。糖是在口中察覺的。一般來說混濁的烈酒被視為有缺陷，但這是已知的例外。","Why is a spirit not swirled in the glass as wine is?":"為什麼烈酒不像葡萄酒那樣在杯中搖晃？","Too much alcohol numbs the nose":"太多酒精會讓鼻子麻痺","The spirit would lose its colour":"烈酒會失去顏色","Bubbles would form and distort the taste":"會形成氣泡並扭曲味道","The tasting glass would break":"品飲杯會破","Swirling releases so much alcohol that the nose goes numb and can no longer pick up aromas.":"搖晃會釋放出太多酒精，讓鼻子麻痺，無法再捕捉香氣。","Colour does not change with movement. No significant bubbles form. Better to bring the glass up gently and take short sniffs.":"顏色不會因晃動而改變。不會形成明顯的氣泡。最好把杯子輕輕湊近，短促地聞。","A spirit smells strongly of solvent. What has the distiller probably done wrong?":"一款烈酒有強烈的溶劑味。蒸餾師可能做錯了什麼？","Kept too many heads in the hearts":"在酒心中留了太多酒頭","Kept too many tails in the hearts":"在酒心中留了太多酒尾","Used new oak casks":"使用了新橡木桶","Distilled to too high a strength":"蒸餾到太高的濃度","Solvent aromas are highly volatile compounds that belonged in the heads.":"溶劑香氣是高度易揮發的化合物，原本應該歸在酒頭。","Tails give plastic, cheese or sweat instead. New casks bring vanilla and spice, not solvent. A high distillation strength gives less aroma, not a solvent fault.":"酒尾帶來的則是塑膠、乳酪或汗味。新桶帶來香草和香料，不是溶劑味。高蒸餾濃度帶來的是較少的香氣，不是溶劑缺陷。","Smells of plastic, cheese or sweat point to which fault?":"塑膠、乳酪或汗味指向哪一種缺陷？","Too many tails in the spirit":"烈酒中有太多酒尾","Too many heads in the spirit":"烈酒中有太多酒頭","A bottle open for too long":"開瓶太久的酒","These are heavy aromas that belonged in the tails.":"這些是厚重的香氣，原本應該歸在酒尾。","Heads give a solvent smell instead. Cork taint gives musty, damp-cardboard notes. A bottle open too long smells less fresh and less complex, without these specific odours.":"酒頭帶來的則是溶劑味。軟木塞污染帶來霉味、濕紙板的氣息。開瓶太久的酒聞起來較不新鮮、較不複雜，但沒有這些特定的氣味。","A spirit smells musty, like damp cardboard. What is the most likely cause?":"一款烈酒有霉味，像濕紙板。最可能的原因是什麼？","A tainted cork or cask":"受污染的軟木塞或桶","Too many heads in the cut":"切取時留了太多酒頭","Too much added sugar":"加了太多糖","Too short a maturation":"熟成時間太短","This is cork taint, the same fault found in wine, caused by contaminated corks or casks.":"這是軟木塞污染，和葡萄酒中的缺陷相同，由受污染的軟木塞或桶造成。","Heads give solvent, not mustiness. Sugar changes sweetness and texture; it brings no musty smell. Short ageing gives little oak, not a fault. Fortunately these faults are fairly rare.":"酒頭帶來的是溶劑味，不是霉味。糖改變的是甜度和質地；不會帶來霉味。陳年短只是橡木味少，不是缺陷。幸好這些缺陷相當少見。","Which fault is most often encountered in a spirit?":"烈酒中最常遇到的是哪一種缺陷？","Excess heads":"酒頭過多","Excess tails":"酒尾過多","The most common fault is a spirit out of condition because the bottle has been open too long.":"最常見的缺陷是酒瓶開太久，烈酒狀態已經不佳。","Cork taint, heads and tails do occur but are relatively rare. A tired spirit smells less fresh and complex. It shows clearly when compared with a sample from a freshly opened bottle.":"軟木塞污染、酒頭和酒尾確實會出現，但相對少見。疲乏的烈酒聞起來較不新鮮、較不複雜。與剛開瓶的樣品比較時就會很明顯。","A vodka's aroma intensity is described as neutral. What does that mean?":"一款伏特加的香氣強度被描述為中性。這是什麼意思？","Very light, not absent":"非常清淡，但不是沒有","It has no aroma whatsoever":"它完全沒有任何香氣","It has been over-diluted":"它被過度稀釋了","Neutral means a very light intensity the distiller intended; with practice you can still tell vodkas apart.":"中性表示蒸餾師刻意追求的非常清淡的強度；經過練習，你仍然能分辨不同的伏特加。","Neutral does not mean aroma-free. It is not a fault but vodka's expected style. Dilution has nothing to do with it: it results from distilling to a very high strength.":"中性不代表沒有香氣。它不是缺陷，而是伏特加應有的風格。這與稀釋無關：它是蒸餾到非常高的濃度的結果。","How much water is usually added to a sample, and what is the key rule?":"樣品通常加多少水？關鍵的規則是什麼？","An equal volume (50:50), always done consistently":"等量（一比一），而且每次都一樣","A few drops, by feel, different for each sample":"幾滴，憑感覺，每個樣品都不同","Twice as much water as spirit":"水是烈酒的兩倍","None: water always spoils the aromas":"不加：水一定會破壞香氣","Add the same volume of water as spirit, and always dilute the same way for fair comparisons.":"加入與烈酒等量的水，並且每次都以相同方式稀釋，這樣比較才公平。","Diluting by feel would make samples incomparable. Twice as much water is not the recommended ratio. Water opens up aromas and protects the palate; only some fruit spirits may lose clarity.":"憑感覺稀釋會讓樣品無法比較。水是烈酒的兩倍不是建議的比例。水能讓香氣展開並保護味覺；只有某些水果烈酒可能失去清晰度。","With which type of spirit do some tasters prefer not to add water?":"有些品飲者偏好不在哪一類烈酒中加水？","Some fruit spirits":"某些水果烈酒","Peated whiskies":"泥煤威士忌","Aged rums":"陳年蘭姆酒","Aniseed spirits":"茴香烈酒","With some fruit spirits, water can make the aromas less clear.":"對某些水果烈酒來說，水可能讓香氣變得不那麼清晰。","Whiskies and rums are normally judged diluted by half. Aniseed spirits are actually drunk heavily diluted and turn cloudy with water. The exception concerns only the clarity of some fruit aromas.":"威士忌和蘭姆酒通常是稀釋一半後評判的。茴香烈酒其實是大幅稀釋後飲用的，加水會變混濁。這個例外只關乎某些水果香氣的清晰度。","A Cognac does not taste overtly sweet but has a slight syrupy feel. How is its sweetness described?":"一款 Cognac 喝起來沒有明顯的甜味，但有一絲糖漿般的口感。它的甜度怎麼描述？","A very small amount of sugar, noticeable through texture, makes a spirit off-dry.":"非常少量的糖，透過質地才察覺得到，讓烈酒成為微甜。","Dry would mean no added sugar. Medium is for clear but not defining sweetness, as in many rums. Sweet is reserved for liqueurs and a few flavoured spirits such as pastis.":"不甜表示沒有添加糖。中等用於清楚但不是主導的甜味，例如許多蘭姆酒。甜則保留給利口酒和少數調味烈酒，例如 pastis。","A whisky shows vanilla and fruit and seems sweet, but its texture is not at all syrupy. How is its sweetness described?":"一款威士忌有香草和果香，感覺是甜的，但質地一點也不像糖漿。它的甜度怎麼描述？","Dry: it is an illusion of sweetness":"不甜：那是甜味的錯覺","Sweet, because vanilla shows clearly":"甜，因為香草很明顯","Medium, like a rum":"中等，像蘭姆酒","It cannot be judged without reading the label":"不看酒標就無法判斷","Vanilla and fruit create an illusion of sweetness: without a syrupy texture, the spirit is described as dry.":"香草和果香製造了甜味的錯覺：沒有糖漿般的質地，這款烈酒就描述為不甜。","Sweetness measures added sugar, not aromas that suggest sweetness. Medium and sweet would need sugar actually present. Texture in the mouth is the right tool, not the label.":"甜度衡量的是添加的糖，不是讓人聯想到甜的香氣。中等和甜需要真的有糖。口中的質地才是正確的判斷工具，不是酒標。","When judging the length of the finish, what is taken into account?":"判斷餘韻的長度時，要考慮什麼？","Only the pleasant flavours that linger":"只考慮持續留存的宜人風味","Any sensation, including unpleasant ones":"任何感覺，包括不愉快的","Only the heat of the alcohol":"只考慮酒精的熱感","How long it was held before spitting":"吐酒前含在口中多久","Finish length only counts the positive flavours that persist.":"餘韻的長度只計算持續留存的正面風味。","Unpleasant flavours, sensations or textures do not lengthen the finish. Alcohol heat alone is not a flavour. Holding the spirit before spitting helps capture flavours, not measure the finish.":"不愉快的風味、感覺或質地不會讓餘韻變長。酒精的熱感本身不是風味。吐酒前把烈酒含在口中有助於捕捉風味，不是測量餘韻。","Peaty, medicinal and seaweed notes belong to which aroma group?":"泥煤、藥水味和海藻氣息屬於哪一個香氣類別？","Processing":"原料處理","Oak and maturation":"橡木和熟成","Cork faults":"軟木塞缺陷","Peat smoke arises during processing, while the sugary liquid is being made.":"泥煤煙產生於原料處理階段，也就是製作含糖液體的時候。","Barley itself smells of cereal and malt, not smoke, so this is not a raw-material aroma. Oak brings vanilla, toast and spice. Peat and medicinal notes are a deliberate style, not a fault.":"大麥本身聞起來是穀物和麥芽味，不是煙燻味，所以這不是原料的香氣。橡木帶來香草、烘烤和香料。泥煤和藥水味是刻意追求的風格，不是缺陷。","Notes of fruit cake, leather, mushroom and wood polish suggest what?":"水果蛋糕、皮革、蘑菇和木器亮光劑的氣息代表什麼？","Long maturation in oak":"在橡木桶中長期熟成","A very quick fermentation":"非常快速的發酵","A spirit fresh off the still":"剛離開蒸餾器的烈酒","These are aged aromas, linked to long contact with oak and oxygen.":"這些是陳年的香氣，與長期接觸橡木和氧氣有關。","Fermentation mainly gives fresh fruity esters, such as banana or pear. Heads give solvent. A newly made spirit has not had time to develop these evolved notes.":"發酵主要帶來新鮮的果香酯類，例如香蕉或梨。酒頭帶來溶劑味。新酒還沒有時間發展出這些演化後的氣息。","Which aroma is typically linked to corn as a raw material?":"哪一種香氣通常與玉米這種原料有關？","Butterscotch":"奶油糖","Rye bread":"黑麥麵包","Olive":"橄欖","Dried fig":"無花果乾","Corn suggests butterscotch, popcorn and sweetcorn.":"玉米讓人聯想到奶油糖、爆米花和甜玉米。","Rye bread is typical of rye, olive of agave, dried fig of grapes. Knowing these fingerprints helps you work out what a spirit is made from. That is why Bourbon, rich in corn, often shows such notes.":"黑麥麵包是黑麥的典型特徵，橄欖是龍舌蘭的，無花果乾是葡萄的。認識這些印記有助於判斷烈酒是用什麼做的。所以富含玉米的 Bourbon 常有這類氣息。","A taster dislikes juniper. How should the quality of a gin be judged?":"一位品飲者不喜歡杜松子。應該怎麼評判一款琴酒的品質？","Against shared criteria, beyond personal taste":"依據共通的標準，超越個人喜好","By always marking it down":"一律給它低分","By letting someone else judge it, without even tasting it":"讓別人來評，自己連嚐都不嚐","By rewarding the gin with the least juniper":"獎勵杜松子最少的琴酒","Quality is measured against trade criteria (balance, finish, expressiveness), not preferences.":"品質是依業界的標準（平衡、餘韻、表現力）衡量的，不是偏好。","Penalising a style you dislike is exactly the mistake to avoid. A gin with little juniper is not better for that. Let the spirit's style lead the judgement.":"因為自己不喜歡某種風格就扣分，正是應該避免的錯誤。杜松子少的琴酒並不會因此更好。讓烈酒的風格引導你的判斷。","What is meant by a spirit's expressiveness?":"烈酒的表現力指的是什麼？","Precision and clarity of flavours and texture":"風味和質地的精準度和清晰度","The greatest possible number of different aromas":"盡可能多的不同香氣","A high alcoholic strength":"高酒精濃度","A deep, bright colour":"深而明亮的顏色","Expressiveness is the ability to speak precisely of raw material or processing, even in a simple spirit.":"表現力是精準地表達原料或製程的能力，即使在簡單的烈酒中也一樣。","It is not the same as complexity: a spirit with few aromas can be very expressive. Strength and colour say nothing about it. It is a hallmark of the best characterful spirits.":"它與複雜度不同：香氣少的烈酒也可以非常有表現力。濃度和顏色與此無關。它是最好的有個性烈酒的標誌。","A single malt is heavily peated. Can it still be balanced?":"一款 single malt 泥煤味很重。它還能算平衡嗎？","Yes, if the peat does not overwhelm everything else":"可以，只要泥煤沒有壓過其他一切","No, a dominant aroma is always an imbalance":"不行，主導的香氣一律是失衡","Only if diluted with three times as much water":"只有用三倍的水稀釋才行","No, balance only applies to vodka":"不行，平衡只適用於伏特加","A leading element is compatible with balance as long as it does not smother the rest.":"只要沒有蓋過其餘部分，一個主導的元素與平衡並不衝突。","Balance can come from all components being moderate or from one well-integrated dominant element. Extra dilution is not the criterion. For vodka we speak more of purity, but balance applies to all spirits.":"平衡可以來自所有成分都適中，也可以來自一個融合良好的主導元素。額外的稀釋不是判斷標準。對伏特加我們多半談純淨度，但平衡適用於所有烈酒。","A spirit is balanced and has distinctive features for its category, but nothing more. What quality level does it deserve?":"一款烈酒是平衡的，並具有所屬類別的鮮明特徵，但僅此而已。它應得什麼品質等級？","Balance and distinctive features, with nothing extra, equal good.":"平衡加上鮮明特徵，沒有更多，就是良好。","Acceptable means an anonymous or unbalanced spirit. Very good needs particularly fine balance or more complexity and expressiveness, especially on the finish. Outstanding needs all of these at a high level.":"可接受表示平淡無奇或失衡的烈酒。非常好需要特別出色的平衡，或更多複雜度和表現力，尤其在餘韻上。傑出則需要這一切都達到很高的水準。","The four stages of making a spirit":"製作烈酒的四個階段","Every spirit, from the humblest to the most prestigious, goes through the same four stages. First, a raw material is chosen and processed to obtain a sugary liquid. Next, that liquid ferments and becomes alcoholic. Then it is distilled to concentrate the alcohol and the chosen aromas. Finally come the post-distillation operations, which get the product ready for the bottle.":"每一款烈酒，從最平凡的到最名貴的，都經過相同的四個階段。首先，選擇並處理原料，得到含糖的液體。接著，這種液體發酵，變成含酒精的液體。然後加以蒸餾，濃縮酒精和選定的香氣。最後是蒸餾後處理，讓產品做好裝瓶的準備。","At each of these stages the producer has choices to make, and every choice leaves its mark on the final style and quality. Sometimes there is plenty of freedom; sometimes the law sets strict rules for a particular type of spirit. Think of a kitchen recipe: the ingredients, the cooking and the plating all change the dish.":"在每一個階段，生產者都要做出選擇，而每個選擇都會在最終的風格和品質上留下印記。有時自由度很大；有時法律為特定類型的烈酒訂下嚴格的規定。想想廚房裡的食譜：食材、烹調和擺盤都會改變這道菜。","After fermentation the liquid is usually around 10% alcohol by volume, meaning that a tenth of its volume is alcohol: this is written 10% abv. In the USA the proof system is also used, where two degrees proof equal 1% abv. A bottle at 40% abv can therefore say 80 proof on its label.":"發酵後，液體的酒精體積百分比通常在 10% 左右，意思是它的體積有十分之一是酒精：寫成 10% abv。在美國還使用 proof 制度，2 度 proof 等於 1% abv。所以一瓶 40% abv 的酒可以在酒標上寫 80 proof。","Four stages: raw material, fermentation, distillation, post-distillation.":"四個階段：原料、發酵、蒸餾、蒸餾後處理。","At every stage a producer's choice shapes style and quality.":"在每個階段，生產者的選擇都塑造了風格和品質。","The law can limit choices for some spirits.":"對某些烈酒，法律會限制選擇。","Two degrees proof = 1% abv: 40% abv = 80 proof.":"2 度 proof = 1% abv：40% abv = 80 proof。","What a raw material gives the distiller":"原料帶給蒸餾師什麼","A spirit can be made from any farm product that contains carbohydrates: grapes, apples, grains, sugar cane, potatoes, agave. The raw material provides two things. The first is a store of carbohydrate, the food that yeast will turn into alcohol. Without that store there would be no fermentation, and so nothing to distil.":"任何含碳水化合物的農產品都能製成烈酒：葡萄、蘋果、穀物、甘蔗、馬鈴薯、龍舌蘭。原料提供兩樣東西。第一是碳水化合物的儲備，也就是酵母會轉化為酒精的食物。沒有這份儲備就沒有發酵，也就沒有東西可以蒸餾。","The second thing is flavour. The compounds that give aroma and taste are called congeners, and some come straight from the raw material. For example, every Tequila shares earthy, peppery notes that come from blue agave. Vodka is the exception: its producers strip out nearly all congeners, so the character of the raw material almost disappears.":"第二樣東西是風味。帶來香氣和味道的化合物稱為同屬物，其中一些直接來自原料。例如每一款 Tequila 都帶有來自藍色龍舌蘭的土壤和胡椒氣息。伏特加是例外：它的生產者去除幾乎所有同屬物，所以原料的特色幾乎消失。","Starting quality matters enormously. Distillation concentrates, and it concentrates everything: even a small flaw in the raw material can become obvious and unpleasant in the finished spirit. It is like reducing a sauce: if one ingredient was slightly off, the wrong taste gets stronger. A high-quality spirit therefore needs excellent ingredients.":"起點的品質極為重要。蒸餾會濃縮，而且濃縮一切：原料中即使是小小的瑕疵，在成品烈酒中也可能變得明顯而令人不悅。這就像把醬汁收乾：如果有一樣食材稍微走味，不對的味道會變得更強。所以高品質的烈酒需要優良的原料。","Any farm product with carbohydrates can become a spirit.":"任何含碳水化合物的農產品都能成為烈酒。","Raw materials give carbohydrates (yeast food) and congeners (flavours).":"原料提供碳水化合物（酵母的食物）和同屬物（風味）。","Vodka removes almost all congeners: little raw-material character.":"伏特加去除幾乎所有同屬物：原料特色很少。","Distillation concentrates flaws too: quality raw materials are essential.":"蒸餾也會濃縮瑕疵：優質的原料不可或缺。","Turning starch and inulin into sugar":"把澱粉和菊糖變成糖","Yeast can only feed on simple sugars. Some raw materials, such as grapes and sugar cane, already contain them: the juice just has to be extracted. Others store complex carbohydrates, too large for yeast to eat. That is the case for starch in grains and potatoes, and for inulin in the heart of the agave. Before fermentation, these must be converted into sugar.":"酵母只能以單醣為食。有些原料，例如葡萄和甘蔗，本來就含有單醣：只要把汁液取出來。另一些原料儲存的是複雜的碳水化合物，對酵母來說太大而吃不了。穀物和馬鈴薯中的澱粉，以及龍舌蘭心中的菊糖，就是這種情況。發酵前，必須先把它們轉化為糖。","For grains there are two routes. Barley is usually malted: the grains are dampened and kept warm until they sprout, and the young plant produces enzymes. Heat then stops the growth. Other grains are instead crushed and cooked in water, which makes the starch soluble; a little malted barley is then added, and its enzymes turn the starch into sugar.":"穀物有兩條路。大麥通常經過製麥：把穀粒浸濕並保持溫暖，直到發芽，幼芽會產生酵素。接著用熱停止生長。其他穀物則是壓碎後在水中烹煮，讓澱粉變得可溶；再加入少量麥芽大麥，由它的酵素把澱粉轉化為糖。","Potatoes follow a similar path: they are cooked in water until they break down into a cloudy liquid full of dissolved starch, then ready-made, bought-in enzymes are added. Many producers use these enzymes with grains too. For agave, heat alone does the job: the heart of the plant, the piña, is cooked so that its inulin turns into sugars, then it is crushed to release the sweet juice.":"馬鈴薯走的是類似的路：在水中烹煮到分解成充滿溶解澱粉的混濁液體，再加入外購的現成酵素。許多生產者對穀物也使用這些酵素。對龍舌蘭來說，光靠熱就行：植株的心，也就是 piña，經過烹煮讓菊糖變成糖，再壓碎以釋出甜汁。","Grapes and sugar cane already contain sugars yeast can use.":"葡萄和甘蔗本來就含有酵母能利用的糖。","Starch (grains, potatoes) and inulin (agave) must first become sugar.":"澱粉（穀物、馬鈴薯）和菊糖（龍舌蘭）必須先變成糖。","Malted barley: sprouting creates enzymes that convert starch.":"麥芽大麥：發芽產生能轉化澱粉的酵素。","Other grains and potatoes: cooking, then enzymes (from malt or bought in).":"其他穀物和馬鈴薯：先烹煮，再用酵素（來自麥芽或外購）。","Agave: cooking the piña turns inulin into sugars.":"龍舌蘭：烹煮 piña 把菊糖變成糖。","Fermentation begins when yeast is added to the sugary liquid. The yeast eats the sugar and produces alcohol, carbon dioxide and congeners. The carbon dioxide is a waste product: it is the bubbling that makes the vat look as if it is boiling. The alcohol and congeners, on the other hand, are exactly what distillation will later select.":"在含糖液體中加入酵母，發酵就開始了。酵母吃掉糖，產生酒精、二氧化碳和同屬物。二氧化碳是廢棄產物：就是它冒出的氣泡讓發酵槽看起來像在沸騰。酒精和同屬物則正是蒸餾之後要篩選的東西。","The fermented liquid is mostly water and alcohols. By far the most important alcohol is ethanol, but there are others too, such as methanol and fusel alcohols. Fermentation ends once all the sugar has been used up. Producers usually aim for a liquid of around 8–10% abv: about the strength of a sturdy beer.":"發酵液主要是水和醇類。最重要的醇遠遠是乙醇，但還有其他的，例如甲醇和雜醇。糖全部用完時，發酵就結束了。生產者通常以 8–10% abv 左右的液體為目標：大約是一款濃烈啤酒的濃度。","Many congeners are created during fermentation. One especially important group is the esters, which smell fruity. Here is a key point: distillation can only select and concentrate what is already there. If an aroma is missing after fermentation, it will not appear in the spirit. That is why nearly all producers use selected yeast that gives the same result every time.":"許多同屬物是在發酵中產生的。特別重要的一類是酯類，聞起來有果香。這裡有一個關鍵：蒸餾只能篩選並濃縮原本就存在的東西。如果發酵後缺少某種香氣，它就不會出現在烈酒中。所以幾乎所有生產者都使用每次都能得到相同結果的選育酵母。","Sugar + yeast → alcohol + carbon dioxide + congeners.":"糖 + 酵母 → 酒精 + 二氧化碳 + 同屬物。","Ethanol is the main alcohol; methanol and fusel alcohols are also present.":"乙醇是主要的醇；也有甲醇和雜醇。","The fermented liquid is usually 8–10% abv.":"發酵液通常是 8–10% abv。","Esters, formed in fermentation, give fruity aromas.":"發酵中形成的酯類帶來果香。","Distillation creates no aromas: selected yeast ensures consistency.":"蒸餾不會創造香氣：選育酵母確保一致性。","What distillation is for":"蒸餾的目的","Distillation has a clear purpose: to pick out some parts of the fermented liquid and leave others behind. The result is concentration. The most obvious part to concentrate is ethanol: a liquid of around 10% abv often becomes a spirit of around 75% abv. Some spirits stay lower, while others climb as high as 96%.":"蒸餾有明確的目的：挑出發酵液中的某些部分，並把其他部分留下。結果就是濃縮。最明顯要濃縮的部分是乙醇：10% abv 左右的液體往往變成 75% abv 左右的烈酒。有些烈酒較低，另一些則高達 96%。","But alcohol is not everything. Distillation is also about choosing which congeners to keep, meaning which aromas will carry the spirit's character. Distillers decide according to their own taste and the type of product: some spirits need plenty of aroma, others almost none. It is a little like a photographer choosing what to frame.":"但酒精不是一切。蒸餾也是在選擇保留哪些同屬物，也就是哪些香氣將承載烈酒的特色。蒸餾師依自己的品味和產品類型做決定：有些烈酒需要豐富的香氣，另一些幾乎不需要。這有點像攝影師選擇要把什麼框進畫面。","All newly made spirits have something in common. They come off the still colourless, clear as water, and dry, meaning they contain no sugar. The amber colour of many brandies or whiskies and the sweetness of some rums come later, from oak or from additions made afterwards. Anyone tasting a spirit fresh from the still finds only alcohol and aromas.":"所有新酒都有共同點。它們離開蒸餾器時是無色的，像水一樣清澈，而且不甜，也就是不含糖。許多白蘭地或威士忌的琥珀色，以及某些蘭姆酒的甜味，都是之後才有的，來自橡木或事後的添加。品嚐剛離開蒸餾器的烈酒，只會嚐到酒精和香氣。","Distillation selects and concentrates: ethanol and chosen congeners.":"蒸餾篩選並濃縮：乙醇和選定的同屬物。","A common level: from about 10% to about 75% abv; up to 96%.":"常見的幅度：從約 10% 到約 75% abv；最高到 96%。","A newly made spirit is colourless and dry.":"新酒無色且不甜。","Colour and sweetness only come after distillation.":"顏色和甜味都是蒸餾之後才有的。","Heat, condense, separate":"加熱、冷凝、分離","The principle is simple. Pure ethanol boils at a lower temperature than water: roughly 78 °C against 100 °C. It is said to be more volatile. When a mix of water and alcohol is boiled, the vapour that rises therefore holds more ethanol than the liquid it came from. Cooled and condensed, that vapour turns back into a liquid, but a stronger one.":"原理很簡單。純乙醇的沸點比水低：大約 78 °C 對 100 °C。我們說它更易揮發。把水和酒精的混合液煮沸時，升起的蒸氣所含的乙醇就比原本的液體多。這些蒸氣經冷卻和冷凝後變回液體，但濃度更高。","A real fermented liquid, however, holds more than water and ethanol: it has hundreds of components, called fractions, each with its own boiling point. To keep things simple they are split into four groups: congeners that boil before ethanol, ethanol together with congeners of a similar boiling point, congeners that boil after it, and finally water.":"不過真正的發酵液不只有水和乙醇：它有數百種成分，稱為餾分，每一種都有自己的沸點。為了簡化，把它們分成四組：比乙醇先沸騰的同屬物、乙醇和沸點相近的同屬物、在乙醇之後沸騰的同屬物，最後是水。","These groups match the parts a distiller separates. The heads are the most volatile compounds, with a solvent-like smell. The heart contains ethanol and the aromas that give character: this is the part that will be sold. The tails come last, with cheesy or plastic notes. What remains, mostly water, is the liquid waste.":"這幾組對應蒸餾師分離出來的各個部分。酒頭是最易揮發的化合物，帶有溶劑般的氣味。酒心含有乙醇和帶來特色的香氣：這是要販售的部分。酒尾最後出現，帶乳酪或塑膠氣息。剩下的大部分是水，就是廢液。","Ethanol (about 78 °C) is more volatile than water (100 °C).":"乙醇（約 78 °C）比水（100 °C）更易揮發。","The vapour is richer in ethanol than the boiling liquid.":"蒸氣所含的乙醇比沸騰的液體多。","Heads: solvent smell. Heart: ethanol and character.":"酒頭：溶劑氣味。酒心：乙醇和特色。","Tails: cheesy, plastic notes. Waste: mostly water.":"酒尾：乳酪、塑膠氣息。廢液：大部分是水。","Higher strength, less aroma":"濃度越高，香氣越少","There is a golden rule: the higher the strength a spirit is distilled to, the fewer aromas remain in it. As the concentration of ethanol rises, more and more congeners are left behind. Picture an ever finer sieve: in the end almost only alcohol gets through, and the scent of the raw material stays outside.":"有一條黃金法則：烈酒蒸餾的濃度越高，留在其中的香氣就越少。隨著乙醇的濃度升高，越來越多同屬物被留下不取。想像一個越來越細的篩子：到最後幾乎只有酒精能通過，原料的氣味被擋在外面。","In practice, a spirit collected at around 75% abv keeps plenty of congeners and has a medium or pronounced aroma intensity. At around 90% abv the aroma becomes light, as in some light rums or Scottish grain whisky. At 95–96% abv so few congeners remain that the spirit is neutral, which is why it is called neutral spirit.":"實際上，在 75% abv 左右收集的烈酒保留大量同屬物，香氣強度中等或明顯。在 90% abv 左右香氣變得清淡，例如某些清淡型蘭姆酒或蘇格蘭穀物威士忌。在 95–96% abv 時留下的同屬物極少，烈酒成為中性，所以稱為中性烈酒。","This choice explains much of the difference between spirits. A vodka starts from neutral spirit, which barely recalls its raw material. An Armagnac or a Bourbon, distilled to a lower strength, keeps plenty of character instead. So it is not only the type of still that matters, but above all how high a strength the distiller chooses to reach.":"這項選擇解釋了烈酒之間的大部分差異。伏特加從中性烈酒開始，幾乎讓人想不起它的原料。蒸餾到較低濃度的 Armagnac 或 Bourbon 則保有豐富的特色。所以重要的不只是蒸餾器的類型，更重要的是蒸餾師選擇達到多高的濃度。","Higher distillation strength means fewer congeners and less aroma.":"蒸餾濃度越高，同屬物越少，香氣也越少。","About 75% abv: medium or pronounced aroma.":"約 75% abv：香氣中等或明顯。","About 90% abv: light aroma (light rums, grain whisky).":"約 90% abv：香氣清淡（清淡型蘭姆酒、穀物威士忌）。","95–96% abv: neutral spirit, the basis of vodka.":"95–96% abv：中性烈酒，伏特加的基礎。","The parts of a pot still":"壺式蒸餾器的各個部分","A pot still looks like a big copper kettle. Copper is the favourite material because it is easy to shape and conducts heat well. At the bottom is the heat source, today nearly always steam, running through internal coils or an external jacket. Direct fire is now rare, although Cognac still uses it because the law requires it.":"壺式蒸餾器看起來像一個大銅壺。銅是最受青睞的材料，因為容易塑形，導熱也好。底部是熱源，如今幾乎都是蒸汽，流經內部的盤管或外部的夾套。直火現在很少見，不過 Cognac 仍在使用，因為法律這樣規定。","The core of the still is the pot, which holds the liquid to be distilled; a drain at the bottom empties it after each run. Above the pot rises the still head, where the vapours gather, narrowing into the swan neck. From there a pipe, the lyne arm, carries the vapours over to the condenser.":"蒸餾器的核心是壺身，裡面盛裝待蒸餾的液體；底部的排放口在每次蒸餾後把它排空。壺身上方是蒸餾器頂部，蒸氣在那裡聚集，再收窄成天鵝頸。從那裡有一條管子，也就是林恩臂，把蒸氣送到冷凝器。","In the condenser the vapours meet pipes full of a cold liquid, usually water, and turn back into liquid: out comes the newly made spirit. The most common type today is the shell and tube condenser; there is also an older design, a coiled pipe sitting in a tank of water, called a worm tub. The cooling water has to be constantly refreshed, or it warms up and stops working.":"在冷凝器中，蒸氣碰到裝滿冷液體（通常是水）的管子，變回液體：流出來的就是新酒。如今最常見的是殼管式冷凝器；還有一種較古老的設計，是浸在水槽中的盤繞管子，稱為蟲桶冷凝器（worm tub）。冷卻水必須不斷更新，否則會變熱而失去作用。","Nearly all pot stills are copper: easy to shape, a good heat conductor.":"幾乎所有壺式蒸餾器都是銅製的：容易塑形，導熱良好。","Heat is usually steam; Cognac must by law use direct fire.":"熱源通常是蒸汽；Cognac 依法必須使用直火。","Path: pot → still head → swan neck → lyne arm → condenser.":"路徑：壺身 → 蒸餾器頂部 → 天鵝頸 → 林恩臂 → 冷凝器。","The drain empties the pot after each run.":"排放口在每次蒸餾後排空壺身。","Condensers: shell and tube (common) or worm tub (older).":"冷凝器：殼管式（常見）或蟲桶式（較古老）。","Two distillations: low wines and cuts":"兩次蒸餾：低度酒與切取","A pot still works in batches: fill it, distil, empty it and start again. At least two runs are needed to make a spirit. In the first, the pot is filled with the fermented liquid, at around 10% abv, and brought to the boil. The aim is simple: remove a good part of the water. What remains in the pot, watery, is thrown away.":"壺式蒸餾器以批次運作：裝料、蒸餾、清空，再重新開始。製作烈酒至少需要蒸餾兩次。第一次，壺身裝入約 10% abv 的發酵液並煮沸。目的很簡單：去除大部分的水。留在壺身裡含水的東西會被丟棄。","Everything coming off the condenser is collected for several hours, until the flow drops to about 1% abv. The resulting liquid is called low wines and is only 25–30% abv. Why so low? To recover all the alcohol and the good aromas, a lot of water must be collected too, because the strength of the flow keeps falling as the pot runs out of alcohol.":"從冷凝器流出的一切都會收集好幾個小時，直到酒液濃度降到約 1% abv。得到的液體稱為低度酒，只有 25–30% abv。為什麼這麼低？要回收所有的酒精和好的香氣，就必須同時收集大量的水，因為隨著壺身裡的酒精減少，流出酒液的濃度會持續下降。","The second distillation creates a liquid that can be sold, and this is where the cuts matter. First come the heads, smelling of solvent, for about 10–15 minutes. When that smell fades, the distiller makes the first cut and collects the heart, which ends up at around 75% abv. When cheesy and plastic notes appear, a second cut separates the tails.":"第二次蒸餾做出可以販售的液體，切取就是在這裡發揮作用。先出現的是酒頭，帶溶劑味，大約持續 10–15 分鐘。這種氣味消退時，蒸餾師做第一次切取並收集酒心，最後的濃度約為 75% abv。出現乳酪和塑膠氣息時，第二次切取把酒尾分開。","A pot still works in batches: at least two distillations.":"壺式蒸餾器以批次運作：至少蒸餾兩次。","First distillation: remove water; it gives low wines at 25–30% abv.":"第一次蒸餾：去除水分；得到 25–30% abv 的低度酒。","Second distillation: cuts between heads, heart and tails.":"第二次蒸餾：在酒頭、酒心和酒尾之間切取。","The collected heart is typically around 75% abv.":"收集到的酒心通常約為 75% abv。","A cut is the moment the flow is redirected to another tank.":"切取就是把酒液改導向另一個槽的時刻。","Heads and tails go round again":"酒頭和酒尾再循環","Heads and tails do not go down the drain. The tails are collected in the same tank as the heads until the flow from the condenser falls to about 1% abv; then the still is shut down and the watery residue in the pot is thrown away. The contents of that tank have a clear future: they go into the next distillation.":"酒頭和酒尾不會倒掉。酒尾與酒頭收集在同一個槽中，直到冷凝器流出的酒液降到約 1% abv；接著關閉蒸餾器，壺身裡含水的殘液被丟棄。那個槽裡的東西去向很明確：進入下一次蒸餾。","Why keep them? Heads and tails contain congeners the distiller does not want, but also plenty of ethanol and some of the positive aromas. Throwing them away would waste alcohol and character. So on the next cycle, the pot for the second distillation is filled with the new low wines plus the heads and tails from the previous batch.":"為什麼要留著？酒頭和酒尾含有蒸餾師不想要的同屬物，但也含有大量乙醇和一些好的香氣。丟掉會浪費酒精和特色。所以在下一個循環，第二次蒸餾的壺身裡裝的是新的低度酒，加上上一批的酒頭和酒尾。","It is like a cook saving leftover stock for the next day's soup: nothing good is wasted. Where the cuts are made depends on the distiller's taste and the type of spirit. A wider cut leaves more intense aromas in the heart; a narrower one gives a cleaner, more delicate spirit.":"這就像廚師把剩下的高湯留到隔天煮湯：好東西一點也不浪費。在哪裡切取，取決於蒸餾師的品味和烈酒的類型。切取範圍較寬，酒心中的香氣較濃郁；較窄則做出更乾淨、更細緻的烈酒。","Heads and tails are collected together in a separate tank.":"酒頭和酒尾一起收集在另一個槽中。","They hold unwanted congeners but also ethanol and positive aromas.":"它們含有不想要的同屬物，但也有乙醇和好的香氣。","They are added to the low wines of the next second distillation.":"它們會加進下一次第二次蒸餾的低度酒中。","The watery residue in the pot is discarded.":"壺身裡含水的殘液會被丟棄。","The result: an aromatic spirit":"成果：香氣豐富的烈酒","In the second distillation a pot still does not separate the fractions precisely. Along with the ethanol, many congeners with a similar boiling point pass into the heart, and these give the spirit its personality. The typical result is a spirit with medium to pronounced aroma intensity. Think of a wide-meshed net: it holds back what is unwanted but lets plenty of flavour through.":"在第二次蒸餾中，壺式蒸餾器無法精確分離各個餾分。除了乙醇，許多沸點相近的同屬物也進入酒心，賦予烈酒個性。典型的成果是香氣強度中等到明顯的烈酒。想像一張網眼很大的網：它擋住不想要的東西，卻讓大量風味通過。","There is also a physical limit. In every batch all the alcohol must be recovered, and to do so water is collected too: the strength cannot climb forever. With a pot still it is impossible to reach 96% abv, the strength of neutral spirit. That is why no neutral vodka comes from a simple double distillation in a pot still.":"還有一個物理上的極限。每一批都必須回收所有的酒精，為此也會收集到水：濃度無法一直攀升。用壺式蒸餾器不可能達到 96% abv，也就是中性烈酒的濃度。所以沒有任何中性伏特加是來自壺式蒸餾器單純的二次蒸餾。","The price of this character is work. Every batch has to be loaded, heated, watched, cut and emptied, and then the cycle starts all over again. Producers who choose a pot still nearly always do so to get an expressive spirit, one where the raw material and fermentation can be recognised, rather than to make large volumes quickly.":"這種特色的代價是勞力。每一批都要裝料、加熱、看顧、切取和清空，然後整個循環重新開始。選擇壺式蒸餾器的生產者，幾乎都是為了得到表現力強、能辨認出原料和發酵特色的烈酒，而不是為了快速大量生產。","Imprecise separation: many congeners pass into the heart.":"分離不精確：許多同屬物進入酒心。","Result: medium to pronounced aroma intensity.":"成果：香氣強度中等到明顯。","A pot still cannot reach 96% abv.":"壺式蒸餾器達不到 96% abv。","Batch work: slower, but full of character.":"批次作業：較慢，但特色十足。","Inside a column still":"柱式蒸餾器的內部","A column still is a tall tower divided inside by many horizontal plates, stacked one above the other. On each plate sits a layer of boiling alcoholic liquid. Small porthole windows let the distiller look inside and keep an eye on every plate. Designs vary a great deal, but they all work on the same principles, like a block of flats where every floor does the same job.":"柱式蒸餾器是一座高塔，內部用許多水平的蒸餾板一層一層隔開。每一層蒸餾板上都有一層沸騰的含酒精液體。小小的觀察窗讓蒸餾師能看到內部，留意每一層蒸餾板。設計差異很大，但都依相同的原理運作，就像一棟每層樓都做同一件事的公寓大樓。","Each plate has a central hole topped by a bubble cap. Vapour rising from below passes through the hole, but the cap forces it to bubble through the liquid on the plate, keeping that liquid boiling. The new vapour, richer in the more volatile fractions, rises to the plate above. When the plate fills up, liquid overflows to the plate below through a pipe called the downcomer.":"每層蒸餾板都有一個中央的孔，上面蓋著泡罩。從下方上升的蒸氣穿過這個孔，但泡罩迫使它在蒸餾板上的液體中冒泡通過，讓液體保持沸騰。新的蒸氣含有更多較易揮發的餾分，上升到上一層蒸餾板。蒸餾板滿了之後，液體經由稱為降液管的管子溢流到下一層。","Column stills are usually heated with steam rather than with a flame. A heat exchanger is a common choice: boiling liquid from the base circulates through outside pipes heated by high-pressure steam, and the heat passes through the metal without the steam and liquid ever touching. In some larger stills, steam is injected directly inside instead.":"柱式蒸餾器通常用蒸汽加熱，而不是火焰。熱交換器是常見的選擇：底部沸騰的液體在外部管路中循環，由高壓蒸汽加熱，熱透過金屬傳遞，蒸汽和液體始終不接觸。在一些較大的蒸餾器中，蒸汽則直接注入內部。","A column is divided into many plates, each holding boiling liquid.":"蒸餾柱分成許多蒸餾板，每一層都有沸騰的液體。","Bubble cap: forces vapour through the liquid on the plate.":"泡罩：迫使蒸氣穿過蒸餾板上的液體。","Downcomer: carries overflowing liquid to the plate below.":"降液管：把溢出的液體帶到下一層蒸餾板。","Steam heat, often via a heat exchanger: steam and liquid never touch.":"蒸汽加熱，常透過熱交換器：蒸汽和液體不接觸。","Many distillations, non-stop":"許多次蒸餾，不間斷","A small distillation takes place on every plate, and they all happen at the same time. Vapour rises, liquid falls, and each plate concentrates the volatile fractions a little more than the one beneath it. Picture a staircase: at every step the vapour becomes more alcoholic, while water and heavy fractions drop back down.":"每一層蒸餾板上都進行一次小型蒸餾，而且全部同時發生。蒸氣上升，液體下降，每一層蒸餾板都比下面一層把易揮發的餾分再濃縮一點。想像一道樓梯：每上一階，蒸氣的酒精就更多，水和較重的餾分則往下落。","A column still runs continuously. Fermented liquid flows non-stop into the base, already pre-heated almost to boiling, because the base is the hottest part and powers all the activity. Heads come off in a steady stream near the top, usually from a plate just below it. Tails are drawn from one of the lower plates and watery waste leaves from the base.":"柱式蒸餾器連續運轉。發酵液不間斷地流入底部，並已預熱到接近沸騰，因為底部是最熱的部分，為所有活動提供動力。酒頭在靠近頂部處持續流出，通常來自頂部正下方的蒸餾板。酒尾從較低的某一層蒸餾板抽出，含水的廢液從底部排出。","As long as the volume coming in equals the volume going out, the column is in balance and can run without interruption; in practice it is stopped now and then for cleaning. Unlike a pot still, there is no need to recover all the alcohol from one batch before starting the next, which is why, with enough plates, it can reach as high as 96% abv.":"只要進入的體積等於流出的體積，蒸餾柱就處於平衡，可以不中斷地運轉；實際上會不時停機清潔。與壺式蒸餾器不同，它不必在開始下一批之前回收一批中所有的酒精，所以只要蒸餾板夠多，就能高達 96% abv。","Each plate is a distillation; they all happen together.":"每一層蒸餾板就是一次蒸餾；全部同時進行。","Liquid enters pre-heated at the base, the hottest part.":"液體預熱後從最熱的底部進入。","Heads near the top, tails from a low plate, waste from the base.":"酒頭靠近頂部，酒尾來自低層蒸餾板，廢液來自底部。","In balance it runs non-stop; it is stopped only for cleaning.":"處於平衡時不間斷運轉；只在清潔時停機。","Only a column still can reach 96% abv.":"只有柱式蒸餾器能達到 96% abv。","From neutral to pronounced":"從中性到香氣明顯","In a column, each congener rises until it reaches the plate where it is the least volatile; above that point its presence falls away quickly. The fractions therefore spread out over the height of the tower like neat layers. In theory, in a column with forty plates, the distiller can choose which plate to draw the heart from, and so which style to make.":"在蒸餾柱中，每種同屬物都會上升，直到抵達它成為最不易揮發者的那層蒸餾板；在那之上，它的含量迅速下降。所以餾分沿著塔的高度分布，像整齊的層次。理論上，在一座有四十層蒸餾板的蒸餾柱中，蒸餾師可以選擇從哪一層抽取酒心，也就是選擇做哪一種風格。","If the heart is drawn from a plate at around 75% abv, it still holds plenty of congeners and has a medium or pronounced intensity, very similar to a pot-still spirit at the same strength. This is the case for Armagnac, Bourbon and rhum agricole, all full of character even though they are made in column stills.":"如果從 75% abv 左右的蒸餾板抽取酒心，它仍含有大量同屬物，香氣強度中等或明顯，與相同濃度的壺式蒸餾烈酒非常相似。Armagnac、Bourbon 和 rhum agricole 就是這種情況，它們雖然用柱式蒸餾器製作，卻都特色十足。","Climbing from plate to plate, the strength rises and congeners fall. At around 90% abv the aroma is light, as in light rums and Scottish grain whisky. At 95–96% abv so few congeners remain that the spirit is neutral. So a column still does not mean neutrality: it can produce any style, from neutral to pronounced.":"一層一層往上，濃度升高，同屬物減少。在 90% abv 左右香氣清淡，例如清淡型蘭姆酒和蘇格蘭穀物威士忌。在 95–96% abv 時留下的同屬物極少，烈酒成為中性。所以柱式蒸餾器不等於中性：它能做出任何風格，從中性到香氣明顯都可以。","Fractions settle in layers up the height of the column.":"餾分沿著蒸餾柱的高度分層分布。","Heart at ~75%: medium/pronounced (Armagnac, Bourbon, rhum agricole).":"酒心約 75%：中等／明顯（Armagnac、Bourbon、rhum agricole）。","At ~90%: light (light rums, Scottish grain whisky).":"約 90%：清淡（清淡型蘭姆酒、蘇格蘭穀物威士忌）。","At 95–96%: neutral. A column can give any style.":"95–96%：中性。蒸餾柱能做出任何風格。","Oak or inert vessels":"橡木桶或惰性容器","After distillation come four groups of operations, usually in this order: maturation, adding other flavours, blending and finishing. Not every spirit goes through all of them: it depends on the law and the producer's choices. The first choice concerns the vessel the spirit rests in: an oak barrel or an inert container.":"蒸餾之後有四組操作，通常依這個順序：熟成、添加其他風味、調和和收尾處理。並非每種烈酒都經過全部四組：這取決於法規和生產者的選擇。第一項選擇關乎烈酒靜置的容器：橡木桶或惰性容器。","An oak barrel changes a spirit in several ways. It adds colour, from lemon to gold, and many aromas such as vanilla, coconut, cinnamon and clove. Over time oxygen enters through the wood and creates leather and mushroom notes, known as rancio, while the colour moves towards amber and brown. The charred layer inside also smooths away the harshness of a young spirit.":"橡木桶從好幾個方面改變烈酒。它增添顏色，從檸檬色到金黃色，以及許多香氣，例如香草、椰子、肉桂和丁香。隨著時間，氧氣透過木頭進入，產生稱為 rancio 的皮革和蘑菇氣息，顏色也轉向琥珀色和棕色。內部的炙燒層還能讓年輕烈酒的粗糙感變得柔順。","Every year some water and alcohol evaporate from the barrel: this is the 'angels' share'. Very old barrels can lose more than half their volume, but what remains is more concentrated and complex. Producers choose the barrel's age (a new one gives most colour and flavour), its previous contents, which can leave their taste, and the warehouse temperature.":"每年都有一些水和酒精從桶中蒸發：這就是「天使的分享」。極老的桶可能損失超過一半的體積，但留下來的更濃縮、更複雜。生產者要選擇桶的新舊（新桶給的顏色和風味最多）、它先前裝過的東西（可能留下味道），以及酒庫的溫度。","In the heat a spirit moves in and out of the wood faster: a Bourbon in Kentucky's scorching summers matures sooner and darker than a Scotch in Scotland. Even within one warehouse, the top is warmer than the bottom. When the effect of wood is not wanted, inert vessels of steel or glass are used: the spirit stays colourless and, after a short rest, almost unchanged. It is called 'unaged'.":"在高溫下，烈酒更快地進出木頭：肯塔基州酷熱夏天裡的 Bourbon，比蘇格蘭的 Scotch 熟成得更快、顏色更深。即使在同一座酒庫內，上層也比下層溫暖。不想要木頭的作用時，就使用鋼或玻璃的惰性容器：烈酒保持無色，短暫靜置後幾乎沒有變化。這稱為「未陳年」。","Order: maturation, other flavours, blending, finishing.":"順序：熟成、其他風味、調和、收尾處理。","Oak adds colour and flavours (vanilla, coconut, spice) and removes harshness.":"橡木增添顏色和風味（香草、椰子、香料），並去除粗糙感。","Oxygen and time create rancio; evaporation (angels' share) concentrates.":"氧氣和時間產生 rancio；蒸發（天使的分享）帶來濃縮。","Key choices: barrel age, previous contents, warehouse temperature.":"關鍵選擇：桶的新舊、先前裝過的東西、酒庫的溫度。","Inert vessels (steel, glass): no colour or flavour from the vessel.":"惰性容器（鋼、玻璃）：容器不帶來顏色或風味。","Adding other flavours":"添加其他風味","Many flavoured spirits and liqueurs take their scent from fruit or botanicals, meaning herbs and spices. The simplest method is maceration: the botanical is steeped in alcohol, often diluted with water, because alcohol that is too strong would extract unpleasant flavours. It can last from a few hours to several months, sometimes with a little heat. The result is sometimes called a tincture.":"許多調味烈酒和利口酒的香氣來自水果或植物性原料，也就是香草和香料。最簡單的方法是浸漬：把植物性原料浸泡在酒精中，酒精常先加水稀釋，因為濃度太高會萃取出不好的風味。浸漬可以持續幾小時到幾個月，有時稍微加熱。成品有時稱為酊劑（tincture）。","Maceration extracts colour and a full range of flavours, but it cannot isolate particular aromas. That is where redistillation comes in: diluted neutral spirit is placed in a pot still with the botanicals, sometimes after a short maceration, and distilled again. The aromas come off in order of volatility, and the distiller cuts the heart when the wanted ones are arriving.":"浸漬會萃取顏色和完整的風味，但無法分離出特定的香氣。這時就輪到再蒸餾：把稀釋過的中性烈酒與植物性原料一起放進壺式蒸餾器，有時先短暫浸漬，再蒸餾一次。香氣依揮發性的順序流出，蒸餾師在想要的香氣出現時切取酒心。","Some delicate botanicals, such as cucumber, are damaged by a still's normal temperatures. In a vacuum still liquids boil at a lower temperature, so those aromas survive. A product flavoured by redistillation is sometimes called a distillate. Finally, ready-made natural flavourings can be bought, or artificial flavourings blended into the spirit: the latter technique is sometimes called cold compounding.":"有些細緻的植物性原料，例如小黃瓜，會被蒸餾器的正常溫度破壞。在真空蒸餾器中，液體在較低的溫度沸騰，所以這些香氣得以保存。以再蒸餾調味的產品有時稱為餾出液（distillate）。最後，也可以購買現成的天然香料，或把人工香料調入烈酒：後一種技術有時稱為冷混法（cold compounding）。","Maceration: botanicals steeped in alcohol; gives colour and full flavour (tincture).":"浸漬：植物性原料浸泡在酒精中；帶來顏色和完整的風味（酊劑）。","Redistillation: neutral spirit + botanicals in a still; the heart is chosen (distillate).":"再蒸餾：中性烈酒 + 植物性原料放進蒸餾器；選取酒心（餾出液）。","Vacuum still: low temperatures protect delicate aromas like cucumber.":"真空蒸餾器：低溫保護小黃瓜這類細緻的香氣。","Bought-in flavourings, natural or artificial (cold compounding).":"外購的香料，天然或人工（冷混法）。","The vast majority of spirits on sale are blends. They combine spirits of different ages, or spirits made in different stills or matured in different conditions. The blender has two main goals: consistency and complexity. Think of a conductor bringing different instruments together to play the same symphony every time.":"市面上販售的烈酒絕大多數是調和的。它們結合不同年數的烈酒，或用不同蒸餾器製作、在不同環境中熟成的烈酒。調和師有兩個主要目標：一致性和複雜度。想像一位指揮家把不同的樂器匯集起來，每次都演奏出同一首交響曲。","Consistency is vital for a brand: buyers expect the same taste from one bottle to the next. It matters especially for oak-matured spirits, because the contents of one barrel can be very different from the barrel next to it. By mixing many barrels, the differences even out and the product stays recognisable, batch after batch.":"一致性對品牌至關重要：買家期待每一瓶的味道都相同。它對橡木桶熟成的烈酒尤其重要，因為一個桶的內容物可能與旁邊的桶非常不同。把許多桶混合起來，差異就被拉平，產品一批又一批都能保持可辨認的風格。","Complexity is the other goal. A very old spirit can be so intense that it lacks balance, while a young one may lack depth. Adding small amounts of old spirit to a younger one creates a balance neither has on its own. There is no fixed recipe, because components change or run out over the years, which is why blenders need the widest possible range of ingredients.":"複雜度是另一個目標。極老的烈酒可能濃郁到失去平衡，年輕的則可能缺乏深度。在較年輕的烈酒中加入少量老酒，能創造出兩者各自都沒有的平衡。沒有固定的配方，因為各個成分多年下來會改變或用完，所以調和師需要盡可能廣泛的材料。","Nearly all spirits on sale are blends.":"市面上幾乎所有烈酒都是調和的。","Goal 1: consistency between batches, vital with barrels.":"目標一：各批之間的一致性，對桶陳烈酒至關重要。","Goal 2: complexity, e.g. a little old spirit in a young one.":"目標二：複雜度，例如在年輕的酒中加一點老酒。","No fixed recipe: the widest possible range of components is needed.":"沒有固定配方：需要盡可能廣泛的成分。","Finishing before bottling":"裝瓶前的收尾處理","Finishing prepares a spirit for bottling and sale. Hardly anyone bottles the spirit just as it is. The first step is water: nearly all spirits are reduced to selling strength with completely pure water, because very high alcohol is hard to enjoy. Undiluted spirits do exist, but they are rare and aimed at enthusiasts.":"收尾處理讓烈酒做好裝瓶和販售的準備。幾乎沒有人把烈酒原樣裝瓶。第一步是水：幾乎所有烈酒都用完全純淨的水降到販售濃度，因為非常高的酒精濃度很難享用。未經稀釋的烈酒確實存在，但很少見，是針對愛好者的。","Colour can be adjusted with caramel, a tasteless food-grade colouring: only a tiny amount is needed to make batches of an oak-matured spirit look the same. Sugar can be added too, since every spirit starts out dry. In some brandies and rums it helps balance and style; in liqueurs, on the other hand, it is required by law.":"顏色可以用焦糖色調整，那是沒有味道的食用色素：只要極少量，就能讓橡木桶熟成烈酒的各批看起來相同。也可以加糖，因為所有烈酒一開始都是不甜的。在某些白蘭地和蘭姆酒中，糖有助於平衡和風格；在利口酒中，糖則是法律規定的。","Last comes filtration, which keeps the spirit clear right up to the glass. When chilled, a spirit can turn hazy: in chill-filtration it is cooled, the haze is allowed to form and is then removed. Activated charcoal is a far finer filter that strips out congeners and colour: it is used for some white rums and for vodka. Producers who skip filtering say so on the label: unfiltered or non-chill-filtered.":"最後是過濾，讓烈酒直到杯中都保持清澈。冰鎮時烈酒可能變混濁：冷凝過濾就是把它降溫，讓混濁物形成，再加以去除。活性碳是細得多的濾材，會去除同屬物和顏色：用於某些白蘭姆酒和伏特加。不做過濾的生產者會在酒標上標明：unfiltered 或 non-chill-filtered。","Pure water reduces to selling strength; undiluted spirits are rare.":"純水降到販售濃度；未稀釋的烈酒很少見。","Caramel: tasteless colouring for colour consistency.":"焦糖色：沒有味道的色素，用來保持顏色一致。","Sugar: for style (some brandies, rums) or by law (liqueurs).":"糖：為了風格（某些白蘭地、蘭姆酒）或依法規定（利口酒）。","Chill-filtration: removes the haze that forms in the cold.":"冷凝過濾：去除低溫時形成的混濁。","Activated charcoal: strips congeners and colour (white rums, vodka).":"活性碳：去除同屬物和顏色（白蘭姆酒、伏特加）。","From fruit to spirit: grapes, apples, pears and pomace":"從水果到烈酒：葡萄、蘋果、梨與果渣","Almost every fruit-growing region has its own fruit spirit, and any fruit can be used. What they all share is urgency: once picked, fruit starts to deteriorate and soon develops off-aromas that would end up in the glass. That is why distilleries work with fruit grown nearby. Usually the fruit is crushed and pressed, the sweet juice is fermented with yeast, and the result is distilled. Apples and pears follow the same route as grapes, and so do cherries, plums and berries.":"幾乎每個種水果的地區都有自己的水果烈酒，任何水果都可以使用。它們的共同點是時間緊迫：水果一採下就開始變質，很快產生會進到杯中的異味。所以蒸餾廠使用附近種植的水果。通常水果先壓碎、壓榨，甜汁用酵母發酵，再加以蒸餾。蘋果和梨走的路和葡萄相同，櫻桃、李子和莓果也是。","It may sound odd, but distillers usually prefer white grapes with high acidity and little aroma: they make rather plain wine, but distillation concentrates their delicate floral and fruity notes. The grapes are pressed, skins and seeds are set aside, and the juice ferments into wine. Since the harvest comes only once a year, that wine has to wait its turn. Acidity and alcohol protect it for a while, but not for ever, so it must be distilled within a few months.":"聽起來可能很奇怪，但蒸餾師通常偏好酸度高、香氣少的白葡萄：它們釀出的酒相當平淡，但蒸餾會濃縮它們細緻的花香和果香。葡萄經過壓榨，皮和籽被擱在一旁，汁液發酵成葡萄酒。因為一年只採收一次，葡萄酒必須排隊等待。酸度和酒精能保護它一段時間，但不是永遠，所以必須在幾個月內蒸餾。","Some producers take the opposite path and choose very aromatic grapes, giving spirits that smell intensely of the grape itself; pisco is the classic case. Then there is pomace, the skins left behind by winemakers. White grape skins are removed before fermentation, still moist with juice, so they are mixed with water and the liquid is fermented. Black grape skins ferment with the juice to colour red wine, so they reach the distillery already soaked in alcohol and can be distilled straight away.":"有些生產者走相反的路，選擇香氣非常濃郁的葡萄，做出有濃郁葡萄本身香氣的烈酒；pisco 就是經典的例子。然後是果渣，也就是釀酒師留下的葡萄皮。白葡萄的皮在發酵前就被移除，仍帶著葡萄汁的濕潤，所以要與水混合，再讓液體發酵。紅葡萄的皮與葡萄汁一起發酵，為紅酒上色，所以送到蒸餾廠時已經浸滿酒精，可以立刻蒸餾。","Make two spirits from the same grapes, one from the wine and one from the skins, and they will taste completely different: the skins bring herbaceous, spicy notes. A few fruits are not fermented at all but steeped in neutral spirit and redistilled, either because they give too little juice or to avoid fermentation aromas. Most top fruit spirits come from pot stills; most grape and apple brandies are aged in oak, while pomace and other fruit spirits usually rest in inert vessels.":"用同樣的葡萄做兩款烈酒，一款用葡萄酒，一款用葡萄皮，兩者的味道會完全不同：葡萄皮帶來草本、香料氣息。少數水果完全不發酵，而是浸泡在中性烈酒中再蒸餾，原因不是出汁太少，就是為了避免發酵的香氣。大多數頂級水果烈酒來自壺式蒸餾器；大多數葡萄和蘋果白蘭地在橡木桶中陳年，果渣和其他水果烈酒則通常在惰性容器中靜置。","Fruit spoils fast: it is grown near the distillery and processed quickly.":"水果很快就變質：種在蒸餾廠附近，並迅速加工。","Acidic, neutral white grapes are the usual choice; aromatic grapes give spirits such as pisco.":"通常選擇酸度高、中性的白葡萄；芳香型葡萄則做出 pisco 這類烈酒。","The wine must be distilled within a few months of fermentation.":"葡萄酒必須在發酵後幾個月內蒸餾。","White pomace is mixed with water and fermented; black pomace already contains alcohol. Skins give herbaceous, spicy notes.":"白葡萄果渣與水混合後發酵；紅葡萄果渣已含有酒精。葡萄皮帶來草本、香料氣息。","Grape and apple brandies are usually oak aged; pomace and other fruit spirits usually rest in inert vessels.":"葡萄和蘋果白蘭地通常經橡木桶陳年；果渣和其他水果烈酒通常在惰性容器中靜置。","Cognac: grapes, stills and ageing":"Cognac：葡萄、蒸餾器與陳年","Cognac comes from a delimited area just north of Bordeaux, in south-west France. Several grape varieties are allowed, yet Ugni Blanc dominates. On its own it makes thin, unremarkable wine, but once distilled it gives a signature aroma of raisins and violets. Its character also changes with where it grows, so each sub-region gives a different spirit. The finest areas surround the town of Cognac: Grande Champagne leads, followed by Petite Champagne and Borderies.":"Cognac 來自法國西南部、就在波爾多北邊的一個劃定產區。允許使用數個葡萄品種，但以白玉霓為主。它單獨釀出的酒單薄而平凡，但蒸餾後會帶來葡萄乾和紫羅蘭的招牌香氣。它的特色也隨種植地點而改變，所以每個子產區做出不同的烈酒。最好的區域環繞著 Cognac 鎮：以 Grande Champagne 居首，其次是 Petite Champagne 和 Borderies。","Distillation is tightly regulated. After the autumn harvest, everything must be distilled by the end of March. Cognac is distilled twice in copper pot stills heated by a direct flame, today usually gas. Instead of a modern condenser, the vapours pass through a coiled copper pipe sunk in a tank of cold water as big as the still: the worm tub. The parts have local names too: the olive-shaped chapiteau (still head) and the curving col de cygne (swan neck).":"蒸餾受到嚴格規範。秋季採收後，一切都必須在三月底前蒸餾完成。Cognac 在直火加熱（如今通常是瓦斯）的銅製壺式蒸餾器中蒸餾兩次。蒸氣不是通過現代的冷凝器，而是通過浸在與蒸餾器一樣大的冷水槽中的盤繞銅管：蟲桶冷凝器。各個部位也有當地的名稱：橄欖形的 chapiteau（蒸餾器頂部）和彎曲的 col de cygne（天鵝頸）。","Every Cognac spends at least two years in oak, often starting in new barrels and moving to older ones so the wood frames the fruit without masking it. Nearly all are blends of grape varieties, sub-regions and ages, and producers even use warehouses in different places to create variety. The oldest spirits are sometimes moved into glass demijohns once oak and oxygen have nothing more to give, then used sparingly in prestige blends. Most Cognacs are lightly sweetened before bottling.":"每款 Cognac 都在橡木桶中至少兩年，常先在新桶中，再移到較舊的桶，讓木頭襯托果香而不掩蓋它。幾乎都是葡萄品種、子產區和年數的調和，生產者甚至使用不同地點的酒庫來創造多樣性。最老的烈酒在橡木和氧氣已無法再帶來什麼時，有時會移到玻璃罈中，再少量用於頂級調和。大多數 Cognac 在裝瓶前會稍微加糖。","Labels speak of age and place. VS, VSOP, XO, Napoléon and Hors d'âge are age indications, and they always refer to the youngest spirit in the blend. As a tasting guide, VS shows fruit and oak and can feel a little sharp; VSOP is richer, with first notes of maturity; a fine XO combines raisin, flowers, oak and rancio with a silky feel. A sub-region name means all the grapes came from there, while Fine Champagne blends Grande Champagne (at least half) with Petite Champagne.":"酒標談的是年數和產地。VS、VSOP、XO、Napoléon 和 Hors d'âge 是年數標示，指的一律是調和中最年輕的烈酒。作為品飲的參考：VS 表現出果香和橡木味，口感可能有點銳利；VSOP 更豐富，開始出現成熟的氣息；優質的 XO 結合了葡萄乾、花香、橡木和 rancio，口感如絲。子產區名稱表示所有葡萄都來自那裡，Fine Champagne 則是 Grande Champagne（至少一半）與 Petite Champagne 的調和。","Ugni Blanc, grown north of Bordeaux, gives raisin and violet aromas.":"種在波爾多以北的白玉霓帶來葡萄乾和紫羅蘭香氣。","Double distilled in direct-fired copper pot stills with a worm tub, by the end of March.":"在直火加熱、配蟲桶冷凝器的銅製壺式蒸餾器中蒸餾兩次，三月底前完成。","At least two years in oak; almost always a blend; usually lightly sweetened.":"橡木桶中至少兩年；幾乎都是調和；通常稍微加糖。","Age terms refer to the youngest spirit in the blend.":"年數術語指的是調和中最年輕的烈酒。","Grande Champagne is the top sub-region; Fine Champagne = Grande (at least 50%) + Petite.":"Grande Champagne 是最頂級的子產區；Fine Champagne = Grande（至少 50%）+ Petite。","Armagnac: grapes, column stills and styles":"Armagnac：葡萄、柱式蒸餾器與類型","Armagnac is France's other great grape brandy, made south of Bordeaux. Small producers are the norm here rather than big companies, and the word Château on a label signals a single small estate. Ugni Blanc is again the most planted grape, but local distillers make far more use of the other permitted varieties. Baco often brings a characteristic aroma of prunes, while Folle Blanche gives pronounced floral and fruity notes.":"Armagnac 是法國另一款偉大的葡萄白蘭地，產於波爾多以南。這裡的常態是小生產者，而不是大公司，酒標上的 Château 一詞代表單一的小酒莊。白玉霓同樣是種植最多的葡萄，但當地的蒸餾師更常使用其他獲准的品種。巴科（Baco）常帶來典型的李子乾香氣，白福爾（Folle Blanche）則帶來明顯的花香和果香。","The big technical difference is the still. Pot stills are allowed but rarely used. Most Armagnac comes from a continuous column of its own kind, short and fitted with relatively few plates. Because the spirit leaves the column at a fairly low strength, it keeps plenty of congeners and comes out full of character. It is a useful reminder that a column still does not automatically mean a light or neutral spirit.":"技術上的重大差別在於蒸餾器。壺式蒸餾器是允許的，但很少使用。大多數 Armagnac 來自一種獨特的連續式蒸餾柱，矮而蒸餾板相對較少。因為烈酒離開蒸餾柱時濃度相當低，它保留大量同屬物，特色十足。這是很好的提醒：柱式蒸餾器不會自動等於清淡或中性的烈酒。","Maturation, blending and preparation for bottling look much like Cognac, and the age terms are similar, though the minimum ages differ slightly. Two styles set Armagnac apart. Vintage Armagnac is made only from grapes of a single harvest, so it is not a blend of different ages; it is common here and rare in Cognac. Blanche is Armagnac that never sees oak, made exactly like the others but bottled clear. Folle Blanche, with its expressive fruit, suits it perfectly.":"熟成、調和和裝瓶前的準備與 Cognac 很像，年數術語也相似，不過最低年數略有不同。有兩種類型讓 Armagnac 與眾不同。年份 Armagnac 只用單一採收年的葡萄製成，所以不是不同年數的調和；它在這裡很常見，在 Cognac 卻很少見。Blanche 是從不接觸橡木的 Armagnac，做法與其他的完全相同，但以清澈無色裝瓶。果香奔放的白福爾非常適合它。","On a label, look for the sub-region too: the two important names are Bas Armagnac and Ténarèze. Picture a bottle reading Château, Bas Armagnac and a year such as 1995: a small single estate, a highly regarded sub-region, and grapes all picked during that one autumn. Three words on the label tell the whole story of the bottle.":"在酒標上也要留意子產區：兩個重要的名稱是 Bas Armagnac 和 Ténarèze。想像一瓶標著 Château、Bas Armagnac 和 1995 這類年份的酒：單一的小酒莊、備受推崇的子產區，以及全在那一年秋天採收的葡萄。酒標上的三個詞就說完了這瓶酒的故事。","Made south of Bordeaux, mostly by small producers.":"產於波爾多以南，大多來自小生產者。","Ugni Blanc, plus Baco (prunes) and Folle Blanche (floral).":"白玉霓，加上巴科（李子乾）和白福爾（花香）。","Usually a short continuous column with few plates: a characterful, low-strength spirit.":"通常使用蒸餾板少的矮連續式蒸餾柱：有個性的低濃度烈酒。","Vintage Armagnacs are common; Blanche is unaged.":"年份 Armagnac 很常見；Blanche 未經陳年。","Key sub-regions: Bas Armagnac and Ténarèze.":"主要子產區：Bas Armagnac 和 Ténarèze。","Calvados: Normandy's apple brandy":"Calvados：諾曼第的蘋果白蘭地","Calvados is France's great apple brandy, and it comes from specific parts of Normandy, in the far north of the country. The climate there is too cool for grapes to grow well, so orchards take the place of vineyards. Apples are by far the main fruit, with pears playing a smaller role. As with Tequila, the raw material must be grown in the defined area, which ties every bottle to its landscape.":"Calvados 是法國偉大的蘋果白蘭地，來自法國最北部諾曼第的特定區域。那裡的氣候太涼，葡萄長不好，所以果園取代了葡萄園。蘋果遠遠是最主要的水果，梨只扮演較小的角色。和 Tequila 一樣，原料必須種在劃定的產區內，這把每一瓶酒與它的風土連結在一起。","The fruit is pressed, the juice is fermented, and the result is distilled. Producers use a range of pot stills and short column stills, all chosen to keep plenty of character rather than to make a light spirit. Like most grape and apple brandies, Calvados is then matured in oak. And here comes its personal twist: the oak vessels are usually large.":"水果經過壓榨，果汁發酵，再加以蒸餾。生產者使用各種壺式蒸餾器和矮蒸餾柱，選擇它們都是為了保留豐富的特色，而不是做出清淡的烈酒。和大多數葡萄和蘋果白蘭地一樣，Calvados 接著在橡木中熟成。而它獨特的地方就在這裡：橡木容器通常很大。","A large vessel has less wood surface for each litre of spirit, so it gives much less oak flavour than a standard barrel. That is why even a very old Calvados still smells clearly of apples, with the wood in a supporting role. Picture tasting two aged brandies blind: the one where fresh or baked apple keeps shining through after many years is very likely to be Calvados.":"大型容器每公升烈酒接觸的木頭表面較少，所以給的橡木風味比標準的桶少得多。這就是為什麼即使極老的 Calvados 仍然有清楚的蘋果香，木頭只是配角。想像盲品兩款陳年白蘭地：多年後仍然透出新鮮或烤蘋果香的那一款，非常可能就是 Calvados。","Normandy, northern France: too cool for vines.":"法國北部的諾曼第：對葡萄樹來說太涼。","Mainly apples, some pears, grown in the defined area.":"主要是蘋果，一些梨，種在劃定的產區內。","Pot stills or short columns: characterful spirits.":"壺式蒸餾器或矮蒸餾柱：有個性的烈酒。","Large oak vessels: little oak flavour, clear apple aroma even when old.":"大型橡木容器：橡木風味少，即使陳年已久仍有清楚的蘋果香。","Grappa: pomace the Italian way":"Grappa：義大利式的果渣烈酒","Pomace spirits are made all over the world, but Italy set the benchmark with grappa. The name is protected: only a pomace spirit made in Italy can be called grappa. A spirit made the same way in France or Spain has to use another name. On the label the word grappa always stands out, sometimes alongside the grape: many grappas come from a single variety, others from a mix.":"世界各地都生產果渣烈酒，但義大利以 grappa 立下了標竿。這個名稱受到保護：只有在義大利製作的果渣烈酒才能稱為 grappa。在法國或西班牙以同樣方式製作的烈酒必須用別的名稱。在酒標上，grappa 這個字總是很醒目，有時旁邊還標示葡萄品種：許多 grappa 來自單一品種，其他則來自混合品種。","Classic grappa is unaged: it rests briefly in inert vessels and is bottled colourless. The skins give it pronounced herbaceous notes, and young examples can feel a little sharp on the palate. Think of a freshly cut stem: green, lively and direct rather than round and mellow. It is an honest spirit that makes no secret of where it comes from.":"經典的 grappa 未經陳年：在惰性容器中短暫靜置，以無色裝瓶。葡萄皮賦予它明顯的草本氣息，年輕的酒款在口中可能略顯銳利。想像一根剛切下的莖：青綠、鮮活而直接，而不是圓潤醇和。它是一款坦率的烈酒，毫不隱藏自己的來歷。","The best producers move beyond this template in two ways. First, they let the grape variety speak: a grappa from aromatic Moscato (Muscat) adds pronounced floral and fruity notes on top of the herbaceous base. Second, they rest the spirit for a year or more in inert vessels such as steel or glass. It stays colourless, but the texture becomes fuller and smoother.":"最好的生產者用兩種方式超越這個樣板。第一，讓葡萄品種說話：用芳香的 Moscato（蜜思嘉）做的 grappa，在草本的基調上增添明顯的花香和果香。第二，讓烈酒在鋼或玻璃等惰性容器中靜置一年以上。它仍然無色，但質地變得更飽滿、更柔順。","Only a pomace spirit made in Italy can be called grappa.":"只有在義大利製作的果渣烈酒才能稱為 grappa。","Usually unaged: colourless, herbaceous, sometimes sharp.":"通常未經陳年：無色、草本，有時銳利。","Aromatic grapes such as Moscato add floral and fruity notes.":"Moscato 這類芳香型葡萄增添花香和果香。","A year or more in inert vessels: fuller and smoother, still colourless.":"在惰性容器中一年以上：更飽滿、更柔順，仍然無色。","Pisco: aromatic grapes from Chile and Peru":"Pisco：來自智利和秘魯的芳香型葡萄","Pisco is the grape brandy of Chile and Peru. Unlike most brandy makers, who pick neutral grapes, pisco producers deliberately choose highly aromatic varieties, especially members of the Muscat family. The aim is a spirit that smells vividly of the grape itself, so a good pisco brings flowers and ripe fruit to mind before you even take a sip.":"Pisco 是智利和秘魯的葡萄白蘭地。大多數白蘭地的生產者挑選中性葡萄，pisco 的生產者卻刻意選擇香氣非常濃郁的品種，尤其是蜜思嘉家族。目標是做出鮮明地散發葡萄本身香氣的烈酒，所以好的 pisco 還沒入口，就讓人想到花和成熟的水果。","Pisco is distilled in pot stills, which keep those aromas intact. Most pisco is unaged, and in Peru this is a legal requirement, so Peruvian pisco never sees wood. The best examples are prized for pure, pronounced fruity and floral aromas. Chile makes some wood-matured versions, but the time in wood is normally short so the spirit keeps its vibrant fruit.":"Pisco 在壺式蒸餾器中蒸餾，能完整保留這些香氣。大多數 pisco 未經陳年，在秘魯這是法律要求，所以秘魯的 pisco 從不接觸木頭。最好的酒款因純淨而明顯的果香和花香而受到珍視。智利生產一些經木桶熟成的版本，但在木桶中的時間通常很短，讓烈酒保有鮮活的果香。","Pisco also has a famous role behind the bar: it is the base of the Pisco Sour, a classic of the sour family made with lime juice, sugar syrup and egg white for a smooth, silky texture. Beyond pisco, unaged grape and pomace brandies are made in many countries, notably Spain, South Africa and Mexico, while Central Europe is renowned for pure, expressive spirits made from plums, cherries and berries.":"Pisco 在吧檯後也有著名的角色：它是 Pisco Sour 的基酒，這是酸酒家族的經典，用萊姆汁、糖漿和帶來柔順絲滑質地的蛋白調製。除了 pisco，許多國家都生產未陳年的葡萄和果渣白蘭地，尤其是西班牙、南非和墨西哥，中歐則以用李子、櫻桃和莓果製成、純淨而富表現力的烈酒聞名。","Grape brandy from Chile and Peru.":"智利和秘魯的葡萄白蘭地。","Highly aromatic grapes, especially the Muscat family.":"香氣非常濃郁的葡萄，尤其是蜜思嘉家族。","Distilled in pot stills.":"在壺式蒸餾器中蒸餾。","Mostly unaged, and legally so in Peru; Chile has some briefly wood-aged versions.":"大多未經陳年，在秘魯是法律規定；智利有一些短暫木桶陳年的版本。","The best show pure, pronounced fruity and floral aromas.":"最好的酒款表現出純淨而明顯的果香和花香。","From starch to sugar: malted barley and cooked grains":"從澱粉到糖：麥芽大麥與烹煮的穀物","Every whisky in the world shares two traits: it is made from grain and it is matured in oak. The main grains are barley, corn, wheat and rye. The catch is that a grain holds no sugar, only starch, an energy store meant to feed the young plant as it sprouts. Yeast cannot ferment starch, so before fermentation can begin, that starch has to be turned into sugar.":"全世界的威士忌都有兩項共同特徵：用穀物製成，並在橡木桶中熟成。主要的穀物是大麥、玉米、小麥和黑麥。問題在於穀物不含糖，只有澱粉，那是用來在發芽時供給幼苗的能量儲備。酵母無法發酵澱粉，所以發酵開始前，必須先把澱粉變成糖。","With barley, the plant does the work. The grains are kept somewhere warm and damp, they start to sprout and, as they grow, they release enzymes. After a few days this sprouting barley, called green malt, is heated to stop the growth, giving malted barley. Ground up and mixed with warm water, its enzymes convert the starch into sugar, producing a sweet liquid called wort.":"大麥由植物自己完成這項工作。穀粒放在溫暖潮濕的地方，開始發芽，並在生長時釋放酵素。幾天後，這種發芽的大麥（稱為綠麥芽）被加熱以停止生長，成為麥芽大麥。把它磨碎並與溫水混合，酵素就把澱粉轉化為糖，產生稱為麥汁的甜液。","Corn, rye and wheat are usually not malted. Instead they are ground, mixed with water and cooked at high temperature, which makes the starch soluble. Once the mix has cooled, a little crushed malted barley is added, and its enzymes are enough to convert all the starch. That is why even a whiskey made mostly from corn always includes a small share of malted barley: it is the enzyme engine.":"玉米、黑麥和小麥通常不製麥。它們是磨碎後與水混合，再以高溫烹煮，讓澱粉變得可溶。混合物冷卻後，加入少量壓碎的麥芽大麥，它的酵素就足以轉化所有的澱粉。所以即使是主要用玉米做的威士忌，也一定含有少量麥芽大麥：它是酵素的引擎。","All whiskies: grain + oak maturation.":"所有威士忌：穀物 + 橡木桶熟成。","Malting: barley sprouts, makes enzymes, then the green malt is heated.":"製麥：大麥發芽、產生酵素，接著加熱綠麥芽。","Other grains are cooked, then malted barley is added for its enzymes.":"其他穀物先烹煮，再加入麥芽大麥以取得酵素。","Wort is the sweet liquid ready for fermentation.":"麥汁是可以拿去發酵的甜液。","Bourbon: corn, low-strength distillation, new charred oak":"Bourbon：玉米、低濃度蒸餾、炙燒過的新橡木桶","Bourbon can be made anywhere in the USA, although the vast majority comes from Kentucky. The core rule is about grain: at least 51% must be corn. Corn on its own gives a fairly soft whiskey with sweetcorn aromas, so distillers add what they call flavouring grains. The particular grain recipe each distillery chooses is called the mash bill, and it works like a style signature.":"Bourbon 可以在美國任何地方製作，雖然絕大部分來自肯塔基州。核心的規定關乎穀物：至少 51% 必須是玉米。玉米單獨做出相當柔和、帶甜玉米香氣的威士忌，所以蒸餾師會加入所謂的調味穀物。每家蒸餾廠選擇的特定穀物配方稱為 mash bill，就像風格的簽名。","Each grain has a job. Malted barley is used in small amounts, mainly for its enzymes. Rye brings spicy, rye-bread notes, while wheat gives a softer, smoother character. So two bourbons with different proportions can feel quite far apart: one high in rye comes across as peppery, while one that uses wheat tastes rounder and gentler.":"每種穀物都有自己的任務。麥芽大麥用量少，主要是為了它的酵素。黑麥帶來辛香、黑麥麵包的氣息，小麥則帶來較柔和、順口的特色。所以兩款比例不同的 bourbon 喝起來可能相去甚遠：黑麥多的顯得帶胡椒味，使用小麥的則更圓潤溫和。","Most bourbon is distilled in column stills, but the law keeps the new spirit fairly low in strength, no higher than 80% abv, so plenty of aroma survives. It must then be matured in new, charred oak barrels, which give lots of vanilla, coconut and sweet spice. Hot Kentucky summers speed up the exchange with the wood, giving deep colour and quicker maturity.":"大多數 bourbon 用柱式蒸餾器蒸餾，但法律讓新酒的濃度保持得相當低，不超過 80% abv，所以保留了大量香氣。接著它必須在炙燒過的新橡木桶中熟成，這帶來大量的香草、椰子和甜香料。肯塔基州炎熱的夏天加快了與木頭的交換，帶來深邃的顏色和更快的成熟。","At least 51% corn; made anywhere in the USA, mostly Kentucky.":"玉米至少 51%；可在美國任何地方製作，大多在肯塔基州。","Rye = spice; wheat = softness; malted barley = enzymes.":"黑麥 = 辛香；小麥 = 柔和；麥芽大麥 = 酵素。","Low distillation strength + new charred oak = bold flavour and warmth.":"低蒸餾濃度 + 炙燒過的新橡木桶 = 強勁的風味和溫熱感。","New oak gives vanilla, coconut and sweet spice.":"新橡木桶帶來香草、椰子和甜香料。","Tennessee Whiskey and the Lincoln County Process":"Tennessee Whiskey 與 Lincoln County Process","Tennessee Whiskey is a close relative of bourbon. It shares the same foundations: at least 51% corn in the recipe and maturation in new, charred oak barrels. The difference lies in place and in one extra step. First, it can only be made and matured in the state of Tennessee, whereas bourbon can be produced anywhere in the United States.":"Tennessee Whiskey 是 bourbon 的近親。它有相同的基礎：配方中玉米至少 51%，並在炙燒過的新橡木桶中熟成。差別在於產地和一個額外的步驟。首先，它只能在田納西州製作和熟成，bourbon 則可以在美國任何地方生產。","That extra step is called the Lincoln County Process. Before it goes into barrel, the freshly made spirit trickles slowly through a bed of maple-wood charcoal. The charcoal holds back some of the rough edges of the young spirit. Think of it as a sieve that sands down the corners: what reaches the barrel is already softer and rounder.":"那個額外的步驟稱為 Lincoln County Process。入桶之前，剛做好的新酒慢慢滴流過一層楓木炭。木炭擋住年輕烈酒的一些粗糙稜角。可以把它想成一個把稜角磨圓的篩子：進到桶裡的酒已經更柔和、更圓潤。","The typical result is a whiskey with a notably smooth texture and aromas of sweetcorn, vanilla and sometimes banana. Charcoal filtering is a legal requirement for anyone who wants to put Tennessee Whiskey on the label, with a single distillery exempted. Don't confuse it with the activated charcoal used for some white spirits: here the whiskey keeps its character and still takes its colour from the barrel.":"典型的成果是質地格外柔順的威士忌，帶有甜玉米、香草，有時還有香蕉的香氣。凡是想在酒標上標示 Tennessee Whiskey 的人，木炭過濾都是法律要求，只有一家蒸餾廠獲得豁免。不要把它和某些白色烈酒使用的活性碳混淆：在這裡威士忌保有自己的特色，顏色也仍然來自桶。","Same basics as bourbon: 51% corn, new charred oak.":"與 bourbon 相同的基礎：51% 玉米、炙燒過的新橡木桶。","Only in the state of Tennessee.":"只在田納西州。","Lincoln County Process: maple charcoal filtering before the barrel.":"Lincoln County Process：入桶前用楓木炭過濾。","Effect: a softer, smoother spirit.":"效果：更柔和、更柔順的烈酒。","American rye whiskey is made in almost exactly the same way as bourbon. Only one detail changes, but it is a decisive one: at least 51% of the grain must be rye rather than corn. Otherwise the steps are the same, from cooking the grains with a little malted barley to maturing the spirit in new, charred oak barrels.":"美國的 rye whiskey 做法幾乎和 bourbon 一模一樣。只有一個細節不同，卻是決定性的：穀物中至少 51% 必須是黑麥，而不是玉米。除此之外步驟都相同，從加少量麥芽大麥烹煮穀物，到在炙燒過的新橡木桶中熟成。","That big share of rye changes everything in the glass. Where bourbon talks of sweetcorn and vanilla, rye leans on lively spice, lemon zest and rye bread. On the palate it often feels drier and more peppery. For fans of classic whiskey cocktails, it is a choice that brings extra character and an easily recognisable spicy edge.":"這麼高比例的黑麥改變了杯中的一切。bourbon 說的是甜玉米和香草，rye 靠的則是活潑的辛香、檸檬皮和黑麥麵包。在口中它常顯得更不甜、更帶胡椒味。對經典威士忌調酒的愛好者來說，這個選擇帶來更多特色和容易辨認的辛香風格。","Rye whiskey is enjoying a strong revival. More and more distilleries are making it and the style is evolving quickly, with versions that are richer or lighter in rye. Rye labels can also carry terms such as straight, which point to precise maturation rules, exactly as they do for bourbon.":"Rye whiskey 正強勢復興。越來越多蒸餾廠投入生產，風格也快速演變，有黑麥比例較高或較低的版本。Rye 的酒標也可以標示 straight 這類術語，它們指向明確的熟成規定，和 bourbon 完全一樣。","At least 51% rye; otherwise made like bourbon.":"黑麥至少 51%；其餘做法與 bourbon 相同。","Aromas: spice, lemon zest, rye bread.":"香氣：香料、檸檬皮、黑麥麵包。","A fast-evolving, increasingly popular style.":"快速演變、越來越受歡迎的風格。","Reading an American whiskey label":"讀懂美國威士忌的酒標","Straight is one of the most useful words: it means a whiskey matured for at least two years in new oak barrels, with no added colour or flavouring. It applies to rye as well as bourbon. If a straight bourbon contains whiskey younger than four years, an age statement must appear on the label. So no age statement means at least four years.":"Straight 是最有用的字之一：它表示威士忌在新橡木桶中熟成至少兩年，不添加色素或香料。它適用於 bourbon，也適用於 rye。如果 straight bourbon 含有不滿四年的威士忌，酒標上就必須有年數標示。所以沒有年數標示就代表至少四年。","In the USA alcohol is often shown in proof: two degrees of proof equal 1% abv. A label reading 90 proof therefore means 45% abv, and 100 proof means 50% abv. Sour mash, on the other hand, describes a technique: the acidic residue left in the base of the column still is added back to the fermenter. It is not required by law, but it is widely used by American distillers.":"在美國，酒精常以 proof 表示：2 度 proof 等於 1% abv。所以酒標上的 90 proof 表示 45% abv，100 proof 表示 50% abv。Sour mash 描述的則是一種技術：把留在柱式蒸餾器底部的酸性殘液加回發酵槽。法律並未要求，但美國的蒸餾師廣泛使用。","Two terms suggest higher quality. Single barrel means a whiskey bottled from just one barrel that the distiller considers exceptional, so each release may vary a little. Small batch means a blend made from a small number of selected casks. Be careful: how small a batch must be is not defined by law, so it is left to the producer.":"有兩個術語暗示較高的品質。Single barrel 表示威士忌只取自蒸餾師認為特別出色的單一個桶，所以每一批可能略有不同。Small batch 表示用少數精選桶做成的調和。要小心：一批要多小，法律並沒有定義，所以由生產者決定。","Straight: at least 2 years in new oak, no added colour or flavour.":"Straight：新橡木桶中至少 2 年，不添加色素或香料。","Proof ÷ 2 = % abv (90 proof = 45%).":"Proof ÷ 2 = % abv（90 proof = 45%）。","Sour mash: acidic still residue added back to the fermenter.":"Sour mash：把蒸餾器的酸性殘液加回發酵槽。","Single barrel = one cask; small batch = a few casks, not legally defined.":"Single barrel = 單一個桶；small batch = 少數幾個桶，沒有法律定義。","Three years in oak, in Scotland":"在蘇格蘭的橡木桶中三年","To be called Scotch, a whisky must be made in Scotland and matured in oak barrels for at least three years. The rule applies to every type, from single malt to the simplest blend. In Scotland it is spelt whisky, without an e, as in Canada; in Ireland and the USA it is usually whiskey. A small spelling detail that already says a lot on a label.":"要稱為 Scotch，威士忌必須在蘇格蘭製作，並在橡木桶中熟成至少三年。這項規定適用於每一種類型，從 single malt 到最簡單的調和威士忌。在蘇格蘭寫成不帶 e 的 whisky，加拿大也是；在愛爾蘭和美國通常寫成 whiskey。一個小小的拼字細節，在酒標上就已透露不少。","Scotland's climate is cool, and that changes the pace of maturation. The spirit moves in and out of the staves more slowly than in Kentucky's hot summers, so colour and oak flavours build up gently. A Scotch therefore needs more time to reach a similar level of maturity, but it often gains finesse and complexity along the way.":"蘇格蘭的氣候涼爽，這改變了熟成的步調。烈酒進出桶板的速度比在肯塔基州炎熱的夏天裡慢，所以顏色和橡木風味是緩緩累積的。因此 Scotch 需要更多時間才能達到相近的成熟度，但過程中往往增添了細緻感和複雜度。","During the years in barrel, some of the liquid evaporates: this is the famous angels' share. What remains becomes more concentrated and richer. Meanwhile, oxygen passing through the wood reacts with the spirit and creates new aromas. The legal minimum of three years is just a starting point: many Scotch whiskies stay in cask for much longer.":"在桶中的歲月裡，一部分液體會蒸發：這就是著名的天使的分享。留下來的變得更濃縮、更豐富。同時，穿過木頭的氧氣與烈酒反應，產生新的香氣。三年的法定最低要求只是起點：許多 Scotch 威士忌在桶中存放的時間長得多。","All Scotch: made in Scotland, at least 3 years in oak.":"所有 Scotch：在蘇格蘭製作，橡木桶中至少 3 年。","Spelling: whisky in Scotland and Canada; whiskey in Ireland and the USA.":"拼法：蘇格蘭和加拿大是 whisky；愛爾蘭和美國是 whiskey。","Cool climate = slower maturation than in Kentucky.":"涼爽的氣候 = 熟成比肯塔基州慢。","Malt whisky: barley, stills and casks":"麥芽威士忌：大麥、蒸餾器與桶","Single malt Scotch is made only from malted barley and distilled in pot stills, nearly always twice. It must come from a single distillery, but it is not the contents of one cask: it is a blend of younger and older spirits from the same place. The barley always gives a malty, cereal note, and sometimes much more than that.":"Single malt Scotch 只用麥芽大麥製成，並在壺式蒸餾器中蒸餾，幾乎都是兩次。它必須來自單一蒸餾廠，但不是單一個桶的內容物：它是同一個地方較年輕和較老的烈酒的調和。大麥總是帶來麥芽和穀物的氣息，有時還不只如此。","That something more can be peat smoke. Peat is damp, partly decayed vegetation cut from the ground and then dried. If it is burnt to heat the green malt at the end of malting, its aromatic smoke clings to the grains and carries right through to the glass. Still shape matters too: short stills give more pronounced spirits, tall ones lighter styles.":"那多出來的東西可能是泥煤煙。泥煤是從地裡切下來、潮濕且部分腐爛的植物，再經過乾燥。如果在製麥的最後燃燒它來加熱綠麥芽，它芳香的煙會附著在穀粒上，並一路帶進杯中。蒸餾器的形狀也有影響：矮蒸餾器做出香氣更明顯的烈酒，高的則風格較清淡。","New oak is rarely used in Scotland: second-hand casks are preferred. Most come from the bourbon industry and give subtle coconut, vanilla and spice. Fewer are ex-Sherry casks, seasoned with wine in Jerez before shipping, and they bring dried fruit and orange peel. Finally, some whiskies spend their last months in a different cask that held Port, Sherry or another wine: this is a wood finish.":"蘇格蘭很少使用新橡木桶：偏好二手桶。大多數來自 bourbon 產業，帶來淡淡的椰子、香草和香料。數量較少的是 Sherry 桶，運送前先在 Jerez 用葡萄酒潤桶，它們帶來果乾和橙皮。最後，有些威士忌最後幾個月在另一個裝過 Port、Sherry 或其他葡萄酒的桶中度過：這就是 wood finish（過桶）。","Single malt: 100% malted barley, pot stills, one distillery.":"Single malt：100% 麥芽大麥、壺式蒸餾器、單一蒸餾廠。","Peat burnt during malting = smoky whisky.":"製麥時燃燒泥煤 = 煙燻味的威士忌。","Ex-bourbon: coconut, vanilla, spice. Ex-Sherry: dried fruit, orange peel.":"Bourbon 桶：椰子、香草、香料。Sherry 桶：果乾、橙皮。","Wood finish: a short final spell in an ex-wine or ex-spirit cask.":"Wood finish：最後在裝過葡萄酒或烈酒的桶中短暫存放。","Grain whisky and Blended Scotch":"穀物威士忌與 Blended Scotch","Alongside malt, Scotland makes grain whisky. It is made from a mix of grains, distilled to a high strength in column stills and has a light flavour intensity. It is rarely sold on its own: almost all of it goes into Blended Scotch. Think of grain whisky as the canvas on which malt whisky paints the brightest colours.":"除了麥芽威士忌，蘇格蘭也生產穀物威士忌。它用混合穀物製成，在柱式蒸餾器中蒸餾到高濃度，風味強度清淡。它很少單獨販售：幾乎都用於 Blended Scotch。可以把穀物威士忌想成畫布，麥芽威士忌在上面畫出最鮮豔的色彩。","A Blended Scotch combines malt whisky and grain whisky from different distilleries. The blender has two aims: to keep the taste the same from one batch to the next, and to create a complexity that no single component has on its own. That takes a wide palette of whiskies: bold or delicate malts, peated or not, young or mature, from different casks.":"Blended Scotch 結合了來自不同蒸餾廠的麥芽威士忌和穀物威士忌。調和師有兩個目標：讓每一批的味道保持相同，並創造出任何單一成分都沒有的複雜度。這需要種類豐富的威士忌：濃烈或細緻的麥芽威士忌、有泥煤或沒有的、年輕或成熟的、來自不同的桶。","Most Blended Scotch is young, little more than three years old, and made for everyday drinking. Yet it would be a mistake to think of blends as inferior by definition. There are outstanding Blended Scotch whiskies, built on very old components, that rank among the finest whiskies Scotland makes. The word blend describes a method, not a quality level.":"大多數 Blended Scotch 很年輕，只比三年多一點，是為日常飲用而做的。然而，認為調和威士忌依定義就比較差，會是個錯誤。有些傑出的 Blended Scotch 威士忌以非常老的成分建構，名列蘇格蘭最好的威士忌。Blend 這個字描述的是方法，不是品質等級。","Grain whisky: mixed grains, column still, high strength, light flavour.":"穀物威士忌：混合穀物、柱式蒸餾器、高濃度、風味清淡。","Blended Scotch = malt + grain from different distilleries.":"Blended Scotch = 來自不同蒸餾廠的麥芽 + 穀物威士忌。","Blending aims: consistency and complexity.":"調和的目標：一致性和複雜度。","Blend does not mean lower quality.":"調和不代表品質較低。","Reading a Scotch label":"讀懂 Scotch 的酒標","Single means all the whisky comes from one distillery. Malt means it is made only from malted barley and distilled in pot stills. So Single Malt means malt from one distillery, while Blended Scotch Whisky signals a mix of malt and grain. An age statement, say 12 years, always refers to the youngest whisky in the bottle.":"Single 表示所有威士忌都來自單一蒸餾廠。Malt 表示只用麥芽大麥製成，並在壺式蒸餾器中蒸餾。所以 Single Malt 表示來自單一蒸餾廠的麥芽威士忌，Blended Scotch Whisky 則表示麥芽威士忌和穀物威士忌的混合。年數標示，例如 12 years，指的一律是瓶中最年輕的威士忌。","When a whisky gets cold, or when water is added, it can turn hazy. To avoid this, many producers chill it before bottling, let the haze form and filter it out: this is chill-filtration. Producers who write non-chill-filtered skip this step, believing it also strips out some flavour and texture. Not everyone agrees, but it is a stylistic choice.":"威士忌變冷或加水時，可能變混濁。為了避免這種情況，許多生產者在裝瓶前把它降溫，讓混濁物形成，再濾除：這就是冷凝過濾。標示 non-chill-filtered 的生產者略過了這個步驟，因為他們認為它也會去除一些風味和質地。並非人人都同意，但這是風格上的選擇。","Two more terms tell you what has not been added. Natural colour means no caramel was used to adjust the colour: it all comes from the casks. Cask strength means the whisky was bottled without being diluted with water, so it is often well above 40%. These are niche bottlings, aimed at enthusiasts who like to add a few drops of water themselves.":"還有兩個術語告訴你沒有添加什麼。Natural colour 表示沒有用焦糖色調整顏色：顏色全都來自桶。Cask strength 表示威士忌未加水稀釋就裝瓶，所以常遠高於 40%。這些是小眾的裝瓶，針對喜歡自己加幾滴水的愛好者。","Single = one distillery.":"Single = 單一蒸餾廠。","Age statement = the youngest whisky in the blend.":"年數標示 = 調和中最年輕的威士忌。","Non-chill-filtered: no chill-filtration before bottling.":"Non-chill-filtered：裝瓶前沒有冷凝過濾。","Natural colour = no caramel; cask strength = undiluted.":"Natural colour = 沒有焦糖色；cask strength = 未稀釋。","The Scotch whisky regions":"Scotch 威士忌的產區","Scotland is divided into five whisky regions: Highland, Speyside, Lowland, Campbeltown and the island of Islay. The region name often appears on single malt labels but rarely on blends, which bring together whiskies from many distilleries. Each region name, then, mainly helps you place a distillery on the map of Scotland.":"蘇格蘭分成五個威士忌產區：Highland、Speyside、Lowland、Campbeltown 和 Islay 島。產區名稱常出現在 single malt 的酒標上，但很少出現在調和威士忌上，因為後者匯集了許多蒸餾廠的威士忌。所以每個產區名稱主要是幫你在蘇格蘭地圖上找到蒸餾廠的位置。","What does a region name really tell you? With certainty, only where the distillery is. It is not a reliable guide to style: light and powerful, peated and unpeated whiskies sit side by side within one region, because the distillery's own choices matter more, from the malt to the shape of the stills and the casks.":"產區名稱真正告訴你什麼？能確定的只有蒸餾廠在哪裡。它不是判斷風格的可靠依據：清淡的和強勁的、有泥煤的和沒有的威士忌，在同一個產區內並存，因為蒸餾廠自己的選擇更重要，從麥芽到蒸餾器的形狀和桶。","The exception is Islay. On this island off the west coast, the great majority of whiskies carry the distinct smoky aroma of peat. If a customer wants a clearly smoky single malt, Islay on the label is the most reliable clue. For the other regions it is better to read the distillery's notes or, better still, taste.":"例外是 Islay。在這座西岸外的島上，絕大多數威士忌都帶有鮮明的泥煤煙燻香氣。如果顧客想要煙燻味鮮明的 single malt，酒標上的 Islay 是最可靠的線索。至於其他產區，最好閱讀蒸餾廠的說明，或者更好的做法是直接品嚐。","Five regions: Islay, Campbeltown, Highland, Speyside, Lowland.":"五個產區：Islay、Campbeltown、Highland、Speyside、Lowland。","Common on single malt labels, rare on blends.":"常見於 single malt 的酒標，很少出現在調和威士忌上。","The region shows where the distillery is, not the style.":"產區表示蒸餾廠在哪裡，不是風格。","Exception: Islay, mostly peaty.":"例外：Islay，大多帶泥煤味。","Canada: blends of corn and flavouring whiskies":"加拿大：玉米威士忌與調味威士忌的調和","Canadian whisky, spelt without an e as in Scotland, is dominated by blends. The typical recipe works like a soup: plenty of light stock plus a small dose of tasty ingredients. The stock is a light whisky, usually made from corn and distilled to a high strength; the tasty ingredients are more pronounced whiskies, known as flavouring whiskies.":"加拿大威士忌和蘇格蘭一樣拼成不帶 e，以調和威士忌為主。典型的配方就像一鍋湯：大量清淡的高湯，加上少量美味的配料。高湯是清淡的威士忌，通常用玉米製成並蒸餾到高濃度；美味的配料是香氣較明顯的威士忌，稱為調味威士忌（flavouring whisky）。","The most widely used flavouring whisky is made from rye. That is why, in Canada, labels may say Canadian Rye Whisky or Rye Whisky whatever the share of rye in the final blend. This is an important difference from American rye whiskey, which must be made from at least 51% rye.":"使用最廣的調味威士忌是用黑麥做的。所以在加拿大，不論最終調和中黑麥的比例是多少，酒標都可以寫 Canadian Rye Whisky 或 Rye Whisky。這是與美國 rye whiskey 的重要差別，後者必須用至少 51% 的黑麥製成。","Canadian styles vary a lot. The big brands, with a high share of corn whisky, often have a very soft, easy character. Whiskies with a higher share of spirit from other grains are more pronounced and flavoursome. For a customer who finds a Canadian blend too gentle, the answer is to look for a style richer in flavouring whiskies.":"加拿大的風格差異很大。大品牌因為玉米威士忌的比例高，特色往往非常柔和易飲。其他穀物烈酒比例較高的威士忌則香氣更明顯、風味更濃。對覺得加拿大調和威士忌太溫和的顧客，答案是找調味威士忌比例較高的風格。","Canada = mostly blends.":"加拿大 = 大多是調和威士忌。","Light, high-strength corn base + a little flavouring whisky.":"清淡、高濃度的玉米基底 + 少量調味威士忌。","Canadian Rye: allowed whatever the rye share.":"Canadian Rye：不論黑麥比例多少都可以使用。","More corn = softer; more other grains = bolder.":"玉米越多 = 越柔和；其他穀物越多 = 越鮮明。","Ireland: blends, malts and triple distillation":"愛爾蘭：調和威士忌、麥芽威士忌與三次蒸餾","In Ireland it is spelt whiskey, with an e, as in the USA. Most Irish whiskeys are blends that combine pot still and column still spirits. Some malt whiskey is also made in pot stills. In general the Irish style is lighter than the Scottish one, and peat is rarely used, even for the malts.":"在愛爾蘭寫成帶 e 的 whiskey，和美國一樣。大多數愛爾蘭威士忌是結合壺式蒸餾和柱式蒸餾烈酒的調和。也有一些麥芽威士忌用壺式蒸餾器製作。整體來說，愛爾蘭的風格比蘇格蘭的清淡，泥煤也很少使用，即使是麥芽威士忌也一樣。","One reason for this lightness is the tradition of triple distillation. Where Scottish malt whisky usually goes through the pot still twice, the Irish tradition calls for three times. Each extra pass makes the spirit purer and more delicate, rather like a fabric that becomes softer each time it is washed again.":"這種清淡感的原因之一是三次蒸餾的傳統。蘇格蘭麥芽威士忌通常通過壺式蒸餾器兩次，愛爾蘭的傳統則是三次。每多一次，烈酒就更純淨、更細緻，有點像一塊布每多洗一次就更柔軟。","Another hallmark is unmalted barley, used alongside malted barley. It gives aromas described as spicy, fruity or oily, and a distinctive texture. In recent years the number of Irish distilleries has grown strongly, and so has the variety of styles: today Ireland offers much more than a single light profile.":"另一個標誌是未發芽大麥，與麥芽大麥一起使用。它帶來被形容為辛香、果香或油潤的香氣，以及獨特的質地。近年來愛爾蘭蒸餾廠的數量大幅成長，風格的多樣性也是：如今愛爾蘭提供的遠不只是單一的清淡輪廓。","Most are blends of pot and column still spirits.":"大多是壺式和柱式蒸餾烈酒的調和。","Malts traditionally triple distilled in pot stills.":"麥芽威士忌傳統上在壺式蒸餾器中三次蒸餾。","Lighter than Scotch; peat is rare.":"比 Scotch 清淡；泥煤很少見。","Unmalted barley: spicy, fruity, oily notes.":"未發芽大麥：辛香、果香、油潤的氣息。","Japan: malt, grain and blended whiskies":"日本：麥芽、穀物與調和威士忌","Japan has adopted the Scottish production model. Distilleries make grain whisky in column stills and malt whisky in pot stills. With these two base spirits they create and sell both malt whiskies and blended whiskies. Anyone who already knows Scotch will easily recognise the same categories and the same steps.":"日本採用了蘇格蘭的生產模式。蒸餾廠用柱式蒸餾器做穀物威士忌，用壺式蒸餾器做麥芽威士忌。用這兩種基礎烈酒，他們製作並販售麥芽威士忌和調和威士忌。已經認識 Scotch 的人，很容易認出相同的類別和相同的步驟。","Similar, however, does not mean a copy. Japanese whiskies have their own character: they tend towards a purer, cleaner style, with fewer malty, cereal notes than many Scotch whiskies. Picture the difference between a rustic country loaf and a very fine white loaf: the same base, but a cleaner result.":"不過相似不代表複製。日本威士忌有自己的特色：它們偏向更純淨、更乾淨的風格，麥芽和穀物氣息比許多 Scotch 威士忌少。想像質樸的鄉村麵包和非常細緻的白麵包之間的差別：同樣的基礎，成果卻更乾淨。","To sum up the five great whisky countries: the USA focuses on corn, rye and new oak; Scotland on malt, grain and used casks; Canada on light blends lifted by flavouring whiskies; Ireland on light blends and triple distillation; and Japan on the Scottish model, reinterpreted with a purer style.":"總結五大威士忌國家：美國著重玉米、黑麥和新橡木桶；蘇格蘭著重麥芽、穀物和舊桶；加拿大著重以調味威士忌提味的清淡調和；愛爾蘭著重清淡的調和和三次蒸餾；日本則採用蘇格蘭模式，並以更純淨的風格重新詮釋。","Scottish model: grain in column stills, malt in pot stills.":"蘇格蘭模式：穀物用柱式蒸餾器，麥芽用壺式蒸餾器。","Both malt and blended whiskies are sold.":"麥芽威士忌和調和威士忌都有販售。","Purer style, fewer malty cereal notes than Scotch.":"風格更純淨，麥芽和穀物氣息比 Scotch 少。","Cane juice or molasses?":"甘蔗汁還是糖蜜？","Every rum starts with sugar cane, a plant that lives for several years in hot countries. The stems are cut close to the ground, leaving the roots in place so the plant can regrow. Those hard stems are packed with sugar that is easy to extract: a trip through a mill gives a sweet liquid, sugar cane juice. From here the paths split. Some distillers ferment the juice directly, but most work with a different product, molasses.":"所有蘭姆酒都從甘蔗開始，這種植物在炎熱的國家能活好幾年。莖要貼近地面砍下，把根留在原處，讓植株能重新生長。這些堅硬的莖充滿容易萃取的糖：經過壓榨機就得到甜液，也就是甘蔗汁。路從這裡分開。有些蒸餾師直接發酵甘蔗汁，但大多數使用另一種產品：糖蜜。","Freshly pressed juice can ferment straight away, and the rums made from it have very obvious vegetal, grassy and fruity aromas: think of freshly cut grass. Molasses, on the other hand, is what remains once the sugar industry has heated the juice and crystallised out as much sugar as it can. It is a thick, sticky residue of varying quality: molasses from the early stages of refining is better than what comes off at the end.":"新鮮壓榨的汁可以立刻發酵，用它做的蘭姆酒有非常明顯的植物、青草和果香：想想剛割下的草。糖蜜則是製糖業把甘蔗汁加熱、盡可能讓糖結晶析出之後剩下的東西。它是濃稠黏膩、品質不一的殘餘物：精煉初期的糖蜜比最後產出的好。","Molasses is so concentrated in sugar that it must be thinned with water before yeast can get to work. Fermentation does more than make alcohol: it also creates congeners, and many rum producers try to boost the fruity esters. Jamaica takes this furthest. Highly aromatic fermentations followed by pot still distillation produce what are called high-ester rums, with an intense, almost pungent fruitiness.":"糖蜜的糖濃度很高，必須先用水稀釋，酵母才能開始作用。發酵不只是製造酒精：它也產生同屬物，許多蘭姆酒生產者會設法提高帶果香的酯類。牙買加把這一點做到極致。香氣濃郁的發酵加上壺式蒸餾，產生所謂的高酯蘭姆酒，果香濃烈到近乎刺激。","All rums are made from sugar cane.":"所有蘭姆酒都用甘蔗製成。","Most rums are made from molasses, a by-product of sugar making.":"大多數蘭姆酒用糖蜜製成，它是製糖的副產品。","Cane juice rums: vegetal, grassy and fruity aromas.":"甘蔗汁蘭姆酒：植物、青草和果香。","Molasses must be diluted with water before fermentation.":"糖蜜在發酵前必須加水稀釋。","Ester-rich fermentation + pot still = high-ester rums (a Jamaican speciality).":"富含酯類的發酵 + 壺式蒸餾器 = 高酯蘭姆酒（牙買加的特產）。","Stills, marks and finishing touches":"蒸餾器、mark 與收尾調整","Rum has very few production rules: the only real limit is that the spirit cannot be rectified so far that it becomes neutral. Pot stills and columns of every shape are used, sometimes in the same distillery. To make sense of it all, think in terms of two families. Each individual newly made rum is called a mark. There are light marks and heavy marks, and the balance between them shapes much of the final style.":"蘭姆酒的生產規定非常少：唯一真正的限制是烈酒不能精餾到變成中性。各種形狀的壺式蒸餾器和蒸餾柱都有人使用，有時在同一家蒸餾廠裡。為了理清頭緒，可以分成兩個家族來想。每一款個別的新製蘭姆酒稱為 mark。有輕盈型 mark（light mark）和厚重型 mark（heavy mark），兩者之間的平衡大致決定了最終的風格。","Light marks come off column stills at high strength, often above 90% abv, and have a light aroma intensity. They are the backbone of many unaged rums, yet once matured in oak they also play a big part in golden rums. Heavy marks are distilled to a lower strength, usually in pot stills, many of them one of a kind. They can be very fruity or rich and savoury. Some are made in short columns, as with many cane juice rums, to highlight the cane character.":"輕盈型 mark 從柱式蒸餾器流出時濃度很高，常超過 90% abv，香氣強度清淡。它們是許多未陳年蘭姆酒的骨幹，但在橡木桶中熟成後，在金色蘭姆酒中也扮演重要角色。厚重型 mark 蒸餾到較低的濃度，通常使用壺式蒸餾器，其中許多是獨一無二的。它們可以果香非常濃郁，或豐厚鹹鮮。有些用矮蒸餾柱製作，許多甘蔗汁蘭姆酒就是如此，以突顯甘蔗的特色。","After distillation some rums stay unaged while others go into oak, more often reused casks than new ones. The finest heavy marks, after long ageing, develop bruised fruit, over-ripe banana and rancio notes. Many are so intense that they are not bottled alone; blenders use them to add depth. Rum is almost always a blend, even when it comes from a single distillery, and the style depends on which family of marks makes up the majority.":"蒸餾後，有些蘭姆酒維持未陳年，另一些則進入橡木桶，用重複使用的桶比新桶更常見。最好的厚重型 mark 經過長期陳年，會發展出碰傷的水果、過熟香蕉和 rancio 氣息。許多都非常濃烈，不會單獨裝瓶；調和師用它們來增添深度。蘭姆酒幾乎都是調和的，即使來自單一蒸餾廠，而風格取決於哪一個家族的 mark 占多數。","Once the blend is made up, three finishing touches are available. First, a briefly aged rum can be filtered through activated charcoal to strip its colour while keeping some of the smoothness it gained. Second, caramel is widely used, and some dark rums owe much of their colour to it. Third, many rums, especially oak-matured ones, are sweetened before release. The sugar flatters fruity and rancio notes, but too much of it can swamp the rum.":"調和完成後，有三種收尾調整可用。第一，短暫陳年的蘭姆酒可以用活性碳過濾，去除顏色，同時保留得到的一些柔順感。第二，焦糖色使用很廣，有些深色蘭姆酒的顏色大部分來自它。第三，許多蘭姆酒，尤其是橡木桶熟成的，在上市前會加糖。糖能襯托果香和 rancio 氣息，但太多會把蘭姆酒蓋過。","The one clear rule: rum cannot be a neutral spirit.":"唯一明確的規定：蘭姆酒不能是中性烈酒。","Light marks: column stills, often above 90% abv, light aroma.":"輕盈型 mark：柱式蒸餾器，常高於 90% abv，香氣清淡。","Heavy marks: low strength, usually pot stills, pronounced aroma.":"厚重型 mark：低濃度，通常用壺式蒸餾器，香氣明顯。","Almost all rums are blends of different marks.":"幾乎所有蘭姆酒都是不同 mark 的調和。","Possible finishing: charcoal filtration, caramel, added sugar.":"可能的收尾調整：木炭過濾、焦糖色、加糖。","White, golden, dark":"白色、金色、深色","Because there are so few laws on rum styles, people often talk about colour. It is a handy, visual approach that shoppers love, but it needs care: colour can be removed by filtration or added with caramel. It works best for rums that blend spirits from several distilleries or several islands. So picture three shelves: white, golden or amber, and dark.":"因為關於蘭姆酒風格的法規很少，人們常用顏色來談。這是方便又直觀的做法，消費者很喜歡，但要小心：顏色可以用過濾去除，也可以用焦糖色添加。它最適用於調和了數家蒸餾廠或數個島嶼烈酒的蘭姆酒。所以可以想像三層貨架：白色、金色或琥珀色，以及深色。","White rums are as colourless as water, even though some have spent time in oak and then been decolourised. Most are light, though a few are very aromatic. Golden or amber rums take most of their colour from the wood, with a little caramel to keep the shade consistent, and often have medium sweetness. The key decision for their makers is the ratio of light to heavy marks.":"白蘭姆酒像水一樣無色，雖然有些在橡木桶中存放過再脫色。大多數很清淡，但少數香氣非常濃郁。金色或琥珀色蘭姆酒的顏色大部分來自木頭，再加一點焦糖色來保持色調一致，並常有中等的甜度。對生產者來說，關鍵的決定是輕盈型與厚重型 mark 的比例。","Dark rums are two very different worlds. On one side are golden rums aged for a long time, which turn brown and develop the black banana, leather and meaty notes of rancio. On the other side is the majority: rums that owe their colour mainly to heavy doses of caramel and are young or even unaged. The palate gives them away: the best taste of cane, but show none of the aromas or texture of long maturation.":"深色蘭姆酒是兩個非常不同的世界。一邊是長期陳年的金色蘭姆酒，顏色轉為棕色，並發展出黑香蕉、皮革和肉味等 rancio 氣息。另一邊是多數：顏色主要來自大量焦糖色、年輕甚至未陳年的蘭姆酒。口感會洩露真相：其中最好的有甘蔗味，卻沒有長期熟成的香氣或質地。","Colour is a practical guide, not a legal category.":"顏色是實用的參考，不是法定類別。","White: colourless, sometimes aged then filtered.":"白色：無色，有時陳年後再過濾。","Golden: colour from oak, caramel for consistency, medium sweetness.":"金色：顏色來自橡木，焦糖色用來保持一致，甜度中等。","Dark: either long ageing (rancio) or, more often, lots of caramel.":"深色：不是長期陳年（rancio），就是更常見的大量焦糖色。","Spanish, French and British traditions, and Brazil":"西班牙、法國和英國的傳統，以及巴西","The Caribbean was colonised by Britain, France and Spain, and each left its mark on rum. The British tradition is tied to the Navy, which served a daily ration of rum diluted with water, sweetened and mixed with lime. That called for a characterful rum built on heavy marks. Jamaica supplied very fruity high-ester marks that lift a blend; Guyana supplied rich, weighty marks ideal for long ageing. Barbados offers a softer, smoother style.":"加勒比海曾被英國、法國和西班牙殖民，三者都在蘭姆酒上留下印記。英式傳統與海軍有關，海軍每天配給用水稀釋、加糖並加萊姆的蘭姆酒。這需要以厚重型 mark 建構、特色十足的蘭姆酒。牙買加供應果香非常濃郁、能為調和提味的高酯 mark；蓋亞那供應豐厚、有重量、適合長期陳年的 mark。巴貝多則提供更柔和、更柔順的風格。","The French tradition belongs to Martinique and Guadeloupe. France favoured beet sugar from its own farmers, so the cane juice on these islands was not needed for sugar and was distilled directly instead. Short columns produce rums with a strong vegetal character and plenty of esters. The whites are among the most aromatic rums on sale, designed for mixing; the golden ones stay drier than the Spanish style, usually dry or off-dry.":"法式傳統屬於馬丁尼克和瓜地洛普。法國偏好本國農民的甜菜糖，所以這些島上的甘蔗汁不需要拿去製糖，而是直接蒸餾。矮蒸餾柱做出植物特色強烈、酯類豐富的蘭姆酒。白色的是市面上香氣最濃郁的蘭姆酒之一，為混調而設計；金色的比西班牙風格更不甜，通常是不甜或微甜。","The Spanish style aims for light to medium intensity and a smooth palate. In Cuba, producers used the new column stills to make high-strength marks and then gave them a short spell in oak to soften them. That created the Cuban-style white rum, now the most popular white style and a cocktail favourite. Spanish-style golden rums use lots of light marks, show vanilla from the oak and often a touch of sugar. Panama, Guatemala and Venezuela follow this style too.":"西班牙風格追求清淡到中等的香氣強度和柔順的口感。在古巴，生產者用新的柱式蒸餾器做出高濃度的 mark，再讓它們在橡木桶中短暫存放而變得柔和。這創造了古巴風格的白蘭姆酒，如今是最受歡迎的白蘭姆酒風格，也是調酒的最愛。西班牙風格的金色蘭姆酒使用大量輕盈型 mark，帶有橡木的香草味，常有一點糖。巴拿馬、瓜地馬拉和委內瑞拉也走這種風格。","Brazil is the world's largest rum producer, thanks to cachaça, which is made from sugar cane juice. More of it is made than all the vodka on the planet, yet nearly all of it is drunk at home. With volumes like that, styles vary a lot: most is unaged and often lightly sweetened, and the best shares the vegetal, grassy and fruity aromas of other cane juice rums distilled to a low strength.":"巴西是全世界最大的蘭姆酒生產國，靠的是用甘蔗汁製成的 cachaça。它的產量比地球上所有的伏特加還多，卻幾乎都在國內喝掉。產量這麼大，風格差異也很大：大多未經陳年，並常略微加糖，其中最好的與其他低濃度蒸餾的甘蔗汁蘭姆酒一樣，有植物、青草和果香。","British: heavy marks; Jamaica fruity, Guyana rich, Barbados smooth.":"英式：厚重型 mark；牙買加果香、蓋亞那豐厚、巴貝多柔順。","French: Martinique and Guadeloupe, cane juice, vegetal and dry.":"法式：馬丁尼克和瓜地洛普，甘蔗汁，帶植物氣息且不甜。","Spanish: light and smooth; Cuban-style white is the most popular.":"西班牙式：清淡柔順；古巴風格的白蘭姆酒最受歡迎。","Brazil: cachaça from cane juice, mostly unaged.":"巴西：用甘蔗汁做的 cachaça，大多未經陳年。","Reading a rum label":"讀懂蘭姆酒的酒標","Rum label terms are loosely defined because no single set of rules applies everywhere. Age statements are the clearest example: a big number on the bottle might refer to the youngest rum, the oldest one or some kind of average, depending on the producer. Even abbreviations borrowed from other spirits guarantee nothing. So when you see a number, read the back label or look into what it really means.":"蘭姆酒的酒標術語定義鬆散，因為沒有一套規定適用於所有地方。年數標示是最清楚的例子：酒瓶上的大數字可能指最年輕的蘭姆酒、最老的，或某種平均值，依生產者而定。即使是借自其他烈酒的縮寫也不保證任何事。所以看到數字時，請讀背標，或查清楚它真正的意思。","Two terms, however, clearly signal a cane juice rum. In the Caribbean, rhum agricole may appear only on rums from Martinique and Guadeloupe. Cachaça is the cane juice rum of Brazil. In both cases expect marked vegetal, grassy and fruity aromas, the kind anyone would recognise from sniffing a freshly cut stalk of cane.":"不過有兩個術語清楚地表示甘蔗汁蘭姆酒。在加勒比海，rhum agricole 只能出現在馬丁尼克和瓜地洛普的蘭姆酒上。Cachaça 是巴西的甘蔗汁蘭姆酒。兩者都可以預期鮮明的植物、青草和果香，就是聞過剛砍下的甘蔗莖的人都認得的那種氣味。","Finally, overproof marks a rum bottled at an unusually high strength. It comes from an old British method: sailors mixed rum with gunpowder and checked whether it would burn. It only did so from about 57% abv upwards, and that level was set as 100 proof; weaker rum was under proof, stronger rum over proof. The word still appears on labels, but it is no longer an official measure, and it is not the same as the American proof system.":"最後，overproof 表示以特別高的濃度裝瓶的蘭姆酒。它來自古老的英國做法：水手把蘭姆酒與火藥混合，看能不能點燃。只有約 57% abv 以上才點得著，這個濃度就定為 100 proof；較淡的蘭姆酒是 under proof，較烈的是 over proof。這個字仍出現在酒標上，但已不是官方的度量，也與美國的 proof 制度不同。","Age statements on rum mean different things for different producers.":"蘭姆酒的年數標示因生產者而有不同的意思。","Rhum agricole: cane juice rum from Martinique and Guadeloupe.":"Rhum agricole：馬丁尼克和瓜地洛普的甘蔗汁蘭姆酒。","Cachaça: cane juice rum from Brazil.":"Cachaça：巴西的甘蔗汁蘭姆酒。","Overproof: very high strength; British 100 proof ≈ 57% abv.":"Overproof：濃度非常高；英國的 100 proof ≈ 57% abv。","From agave plant to spirit":"從龍舌蘭植株到烈酒","Agave is a plant native to Central America, with hundreds of species. All of them have a hard core from which long, spiky, waxy leaves grow. In that core the plant stores its reserves as inulin, a type of carbohydrate. Agave lives a long time, sometimes fifteen to twenty years, then flowers just once, uses up all its reserves and dies. Growers therefore need to harvest at the right moment, just before flowering.":"龍舌蘭是原產於中美洲的植物，有數百個品種。它們都有堅硬的核心，長出又長又帶刺、覆著蠟質的葉片。植株在這個核心裡以菊糖（一種碳水化合物）的形式儲存養分。龍舌蘭壽命很長，有時十五到二十年，然後只開一次花，耗盡所有儲備後死亡。所以種植者必須在對的時刻採收，也就是開花之前。","At that stage the agave has its most complex aromas, recalling bell pepper, vegetables and pepper, and the highest level of inulin. At harvest the plant is cut from its roots and the leaves are trimmed away, leaving the core, the piña, which looks like a giant pineapple. Inulin cannot be fermented as it is, though: heat is needed to turn it into sugars. That is why the piña is cut up and always cooked.":"在這個階段，龍舌蘭有最複雜的香氣，讓人想到甜椒、蔬菜和胡椒，菊糖含量也最高。採收時把植株從根部砍下並修掉葉片，留下核心，也就是 piña，看起來像巨大的鳳梨。不過菊糖無法直接發酵：需要熱才能把它變成糖。所以 piña 要切開，而且一定要烹煮。","There are two traditional methods. For Tequila, the piña is steamed slowly in brick ovens; for Mezcal, it is often roasted in stone-lined pits. Many Tequila producers now use pressurised steam ovens, which are much faster but risk burning the agave. After cooking, the piña is crushed, once with a large stone wheel and now often with mechanical mills, then rinsed with water to wash out every last bit of sugar.":"傳統的方法有兩種。Tequila 是把 piña 放在磚爐中慢慢蒸煮；Mezcal 則常在鋪石的窯坑中烘烤。許多 Tequila 生產者現在使用加壓蒸汽爐，速度快得多，但有把龍舌蘭燒焦的風險。烹煮後，piña 要壓碎，過去用大石輪，現在常用機械磨碎機，再用水沖洗，把最後一點糖都洗出來。","Making up the sweet liquid for fermentation is called formulation. The best producers also put piña fibres into the fermenter to boost the agave character. Then comes distillation: quality agave spirits are usually double distilled in pot stills, often to low strengths, sometimes under 60% abv. Finally, most rest in inert vessels or very large oak vats. Small barrels are rare, because oak easily drowns out the agave.":"配製發酵用的甜液稱為調配（formulation）。最好的生產者還會把 piña 的纖維放進發酵槽，加強龍舌蘭的特色。接著是蒸餾：優質的龍舌蘭烈酒通常在壺式蒸餾器中蒸餾兩次，常蒸餾到低濃度，有時低於 60% abv。最後，大多數在惰性容器或非常大的橡木槽中靜置。小桶很少見，因為橡木很容易蓋過龍舌蘭。","Agave stores inulin in its core, the piña.":"龍舌蘭把菊糖儲存在核心，也就是 piña。","Harvest just before flowering: best aromas and most inulin.":"在開花前採收：香氣最好，菊糖最多。","Cooking turns inulin into sugar: steaming (Tequila) or pit roasting (Mezcal).":"烹煮把菊糖變成糖：蒸煮（Tequila）或窯坑烘烤（Mezcal）。","Quality: fibres in the ferment, double pot distillation, low strength.":"品質：發酵時帶纖維、壺式二次蒸餾、低濃度。","Oak must be used carefully: it easily masks agave.":"橡木必須謹慎使用：它很容易掩蓋龍舌蘭。","Tequila: blue agave and categories":"Tequila：藍色龍舌蘭與類別","Tequila and Mezcal are geographical indications, a bit like Cognac and Armagnac: they set where the agave grows and how the spirit is made. Tequila is the biggest agave spirit by volume and is dominated by large companies, yet it may use only one variety, blue agave. This must be grown in one of five permitted Mexican states. The most important is Jalisco, home of the blue agave, which takes seven to ten years to mature.":"Tequila 和 Mezcal 是地理標示，有點像 Cognac 和 Armagnac：它們規定龍舌蘭種在哪裡，以及烈酒怎麼製作。Tequila 是產量最大的龍舌蘭烈酒，由大公司主導，卻只能使用一個品種：藍色龍舌蘭。它必須種在墨西哥五個獲准的州之一。最重要的是哈利斯科州（Jalisco），藍色龍舌蘭的故鄉，這種龍舌蘭需要七到十年才成熟。","One variety does not mean one flavour: blue agave changes with where it grows, and agave from higher altitudes can be fruitier. The best Tequilas come from agave slow-cooked in brick ovens, fermented with its fibres, double distilled in pot stills and collected at a low strength. The result is a warming texture and an intense agave character. As with wine, place and production choices matter as much as the variety.":"一個品種不代表一種風味：藍色龍舌蘭隨種植地點而變，來自較高海拔的可能更有果香。最好的 Tequila 用在磚爐中慢煮的龍舌蘭製成，帶著纖維發酵，在壺式蒸餾器中蒸餾兩次，並在低濃度收集。成果是溫熱的口感和濃郁的龍舌蘭特色。和葡萄酒一樣，產地和生產選擇與品種同樣重要。","On the label, the share of agave comes first. 100% agave means every fermented sugar came from the plant. A bottle that simply says Tequila needs only 51% agave sugars; the rest can come from other sources, which dilute the agave character. These are sometimes called mixto, but that word is not a labelling term. Anyone looking for true agave flavour should therefore reach for a 100% agave Tequila.":"在酒標上，龍舌蘭的比例排在第一位。100% agave 表示每一分發酵的糖都來自這種植物。只寫 Tequila 的酒瓶只需要 51% 的龍舌蘭糖；其餘可以來自其他來源，這會稀釋龍舌蘭的特色。這些酒有時被稱為 mixto，但這個字不是標示術語。所以想要真正龍舌蘭風味的人，應該選 100% agave 的 Tequila。","Then come the categories. Blanco (or Silver): no ageing requirement. Gold (Joven/Oro): unaged, but coloured and softened with abocado, a caramel-based additive that mimics the effect of wood. Reposado: at least two months in oak, usually very large vats. Añejo: at least one year in oak barrels. Extra Añejo: at least three years in barrels. More wood brings smoothness, but also the risk of hiding the agave.":"接著是類別。Blanco（或 Silver）：沒有陳年要求。Gold（Joven/Oro）：未經陳年，但用 abocado 上色並柔化，這是一種以焦糖色為基礎、模仿木頭效果的添加物。Reposado：在橡木中至少兩個月，通常是非常大的木槽。Añejo：在橡木桶中至少一年。Extra Añejo：在桶中至少三年。木頭越多越柔順，但也有掩蓋龍舌蘭的風險。","Tequila: blue agave only, five states, mainly Jalisco.":"Tequila：只用藍色龍舌蘭，五個州，主要是哈利斯科州。","100% agave: all sugars from agave; plain Tequila: at least 51%.":"100% agave：所有的糖都來自龍舌蘭；一般的 Tequila：至少 51%。","Blanco: no ageing required; Gold: coloured with abocado.":"Blanco：不要求陳年；Gold：用 abocado 上色。","Reposado 2 months, Añejo 1 year, Extra Añejo 3 years in oak.":"Reposado 2 個月、Añejo 1 年、Extra Añejo 3 年，都在橡木中。","Mezcal: many agaves, smoke and tradition":"Mezcal：多種龍舌蘭、煙燻與傳統","In Mexico every agave spirit is loosely called mezcal, but on a label Mezcal refers only to one specific geographical indication. It covers several states, the most important being Oaxaca in the south. Unlike Tequila, production is still dominated by small producers, and several agave species are allowed. The most widely used is espadín, the main variety in Oaxaca, where the vast majority of Mezcal comes from.":"在墨西哥，每一種龍舌蘭烈酒都泛稱為 mezcal，但在酒標上，Mezcal 只指一個特定的地理標示。它涵蓋數個州，最重要的是南部的瓦哈卡州（Oaxaca）。與 Tequila 不同，生產仍以小生產者為主，並允許使用數種龍舌蘭。使用最廣的是 espadín，它是瓦哈卡州的主要品種，而絕大部分的 Mezcal 都來自那裡。","Smoke is Mezcal's signature. Traditionally a fire is lit in a stone-lined pit; once it has burnt out, the piñas are laid in the hot hole, covered with earth and left to cook in the heat held by the stones. Steaming adds no flavour, but roasting does, which is why Mezcal smells smoky, with very variable intensity. Smoke, earth and vegetal notes, plus fibres in the ferment and small pot stills, create its unique profile.":"煙燻味是 Mezcal 的招牌。傳統上在鋪石的窯坑中生火；火燒盡後，把 piña 放進熱坑，用土蓋起來，靠石頭留住的熱烹煮。蒸煮不增添風味，烘烤卻會，所以 Mezcal 聞起來有煙燻味，強度差異很大。煙燻、土壤和植物氣息，加上發酵時的纖維和小型壺式蒸餾器，造就了它獨特的輪廓。","Three categories help identify traditional methods. Mezcal allows any cooking method, including pressurised steam ovens, and any still, even a column. Artisanal Mezcal allows only pits or brick ovens, limited mills, fermentation with fibres in stone, wood or clay vessels, and directly heated metal or clay pot stills. Ancestral Mezcal goes further: pits only, no mechanical mills, fibres in distillation as well, and directly heated clay stills.":"有三個類別幫助辨認傳統做法。Mezcal 允許任何烹煮方式，包括加壓蒸汽爐，以及任何蒸餾器，甚至蒸餾柱。Artisanal Mezcal 只允許窯坑或磚爐、有限的磨碎機、在石製、木製或陶製容器中帶纖維發酵，以及直火加熱的金屬或陶製壺式蒸餾器。Ancestral Mezcal 更進一步：只能用窯坑、不用機械磨碎機、蒸餾時也帶纖維，並使用直火加熱的陶製蒸餾器。","Mezcal: a geographical indication, mainly Oaxaca.":"Mezcal：地理標示，主要在瓦哈卡州。","Several agave species allowed; espadín is the most used.":"允許數種龍舌蘭；espadín 用得最多。","Pit roasting = smoky notes, the easiest way to tell it from Tequila.":"窯坑烘烤 = 煙燻氣息，是與 Tequila 區分最簡單的方法。","Three classes: Mezcal, Artisanal, Ancestral (increasingly traditional).":"三個等級：Mezcal、Artisanal、Ancestral（越來越傳統）。","Raw materials and converting starch":"原料與澱粉轉化","Having started out in Eastern Europe, vodka is now one of the best-selling spirits almost everywhere. Its secret is neutrality: it clashes with nothing and mixes easily, whether in simple long drinks or in cocktails. In theory it can be made from any material of agricultural origin, but in practice cost and consumer expectations narrow the choice to a handful of raw materials, mainly grains and potatoes.":"伏特加發源於東歐，如今幾乎在各地都是最暢銷的烈酒之一。它的祕密是中性：它不與任何東西衝突，容易混搭，不論是簡單的長飲還是調酒。理論上它可以用任何農業來源的原料製成，但實際上成本和消費者的期待把選擇縮小到少數幾種原料，主要是穀物和馬鈴薯。","Grains, a key crop in Eastern Europe, are widely used: barley, wheat and rye. Their starch cannot be fermented, though; it must first be turned into sugar. Malted barley can supply the enzymes needed, but many distillers now buy commercially prepared enzymes and add them to grains that have been crushed and cooked in water. It is a bit like using ready-made baking yeast rather than raising your own starter.":"穀物是東歐的重要作物，使用很廣：大麥、小麥和黑麥。不過它們的澱粉無法發酵；必須先變成糖。麥芽大麥可以提供所需的酵素，但許多蒸餾師現在購買商業製備的酵素，加進壓碎並在水中煮過的穀物裡。這有點像使用現成的烘焙酵母，而不是自己養酵種。","In Poland, potatoes are a traditional raw material. The tuber stores starch and needs a two-step process. First it is cooked in water until it falls apart, making the starch soluble and giving a cloudy liquid; then bought-in enzymes are added to turn that starch into sugar. Beyond these classic bases, some producers experiment with other materials, either to cut costs or to stand out. In recent years, grapes have been a notable example.":"在波蘭，馬鈴薯是傳統的原料。這種塊莖儲存澱粉，需要兩步驟的過程。首先在水中煮到散開，讓澱粉變得可溶，得到混濁的液體；接著加入外購的酵素，把澱粉變成糖。除了這些經典的基礎原料，有些生產者也嘗試其他原料，不是為了降低成本，就是為了與眾不同。近年來，葡萄是值得注意的例子。","In theory any agricultural material; in practice mainly grains and potatoes.":"理論上任何農業原料都可以；實際上主要是穀物和馬鈴薯。","Grains used: barley, wheat, rye.":"使用的穀物：大麥、小麥、黑麥。","Starch must be converted: malted barley or, more often, bought-in enzymes.":"澱粉必須轉化：用麥芽大麥，或更常見的外購酵素。","Potatoes (a Polish tradition): cooked in water, then enzymes.":"馬鈴薯（波蘭的傳統）：在水中烹煮，再加酵素。","Distillation, filtration and dilution":"蒸餾、過濾與稀釋","Vodka is made from neutral spirit, distilled to a very high strength: at least 95% abv in the USA and 96% in the EU. At that level so few congeners remain that the aroma is neutral. Only a column still with enough plates can get there; a pot still cannot. Some distillers add further steps for an even purer, smoother spirit, and the process is usually continuous.":"伏特加用中性烈酒製成，蒸餾到非常高的濃度：在美國至少 95% abv，在歐盟至少 96%。在這個水準留下的同屬物極少，香氣是中性的。只有蒸餾板夠多的柱式蒸餾器才能做到；壺式蒸餾器不行。有些蒸餾師再加上其他步驟，讓烈酒更純淨、更柔順，而整個過程通常是連續的。","There are variations. Some small distillers make a first distillate in a pot still and finish the second distillation in a column, which has no effect on the final flavour. Others do not distil at all and buy in neutral spirit, a widely traded commodity. Simply diluted, it can feel slightly rough, so it is often diluted and run through a hybrid still, a pot linked to a rectifying column, to give a silkier texture.":"也有不同的做法。有些小型蒸餾師用壺式蒸餾器做第一次蒸餾，再用蒸餾柱完成第二次蒸餾，這對最終的風味沒有影響。另一些人完全不蒸餾，而是買進中性烈酒，這是交易廣泛的大宗商品。只是稀釋的話口感可能略顯粗糙，所以常在稀釋後通過混合式蒸餾器（連接精餾柱的壺身），得到更絲滑的質地。","After distillation, many producers simply dilute, believing distillation alone gives the purity they want. Others use two techniques: filtering through activated charcoal, which removes any remaining unwanted congeners, and additives, bought from specialist suppliers to create the desired texture and sometimes a very faint aroma. Last comes dilution. At 40% abv nearly 60% of the bottle is added water, so that water must be extremely pure.":"蒸餾後，許多生產者只是稀釋，因為他們認為光靠蒸餾就能得到想要的純淨度。另一些人使用兩種技術：用活性碳過濾，去除任何剩餘的、不想要的同屬物；以及添加物，向專業供應商購買，用來創造想要的質地，有時還有非常淡的香氣。最後是稀釋。在 40% abv 時，瓶中將近 60% 是加入的水，所以水必須極為純淨。","Neutral spirit: at least 95% abv (USA) or 96% (EU).":"中性烈酒：至少 95% abv（美國）或 96%（歐盟）。","A column still with many plates is essential; a pot still alone cannot do it.":"蒸餾板很多的柱式蒸餾器不可或缺；只靠壺式蒸餾器做不到。","Hybrid still: redistilling bought-in spirit for a silkier texture.":"混合式蒸餾器：把買進的烈酒再蒸餾，得到更絲滑的質地。","Activated charcoal removes congeners; additives fine-tune texture.":"活性碳去除同屬物；添加物微調質地。","About 60% of the bottle is water, so it must be very pure.":"瓶中約 60% 是水，所以水必須非常純淨。","Vodka styles and homelands":"伏特加的風格與故鄉","Unflavoured vodkas fall into two broad styles. Neutral vodkas have the lightest possible flavour. They are not entirely tasteless, but they should be smooth, light and dry on the palate. Characterful vodkas keep a little more flavour and a fuller, more mouth-filling texture. Even here the aromas stay so delicate that they can still be called neutral; the difference lies mostly in how the vodka feels in the mouth.":"未調味的伏特加大致分為兩種風格。中性伏特加的風味盡可能清淡。它們並非完全沒有味道，但在口中應該柔順、輕盈、不甜。有個性的伏特加保有多一點風味，質地也更飽滿豐潤。即使如此，香氣仍然非常細緻，還是可以稱為中性；差別主要在於伏特加在口中的感覺。","By pairing delicate flavours with a full, smooth texture, producers create many subtly different premium vodkas. Here is a useful tasting clue: if an unflavoured vodka shows aromas that cannot honestly be called neutral, they were most probably added after distillation. Flavoured vodkas are a separate family; almost every producer offers at least one, and they belong with flavoured spirits.":"把細緻的風味與飽滿柔順的質地結合起來，生產者創造出許多有微妙差異的高級伏特加。這裡有一個實用的品飲線索：如果未調味的伏特加表現出實在不能稱為中性的香氣，那很可能是蒸餾後添加的。調味伏特加是另一個家族；幾乎每位生產者都至少有一款，它們歸在調味烈酒之中。","Historically, vodka is linked to Russia, Poland, Finland and Sweden. These countries still make large volumes, and many of the most highly regarded vodkas come from there, often from grain or, in Poland, from potatoes. Today, though, vodka is made all over the world at every quality level, and almost every producing country has outstanding examples. Origin matters, but it is no longer an exclusive guarantee of quality.":"在歷史上，伏特加與俄羅斯、波蘭、芬蘭和瑞典相連。這些國家至今仍生產大量伏特加，許多評價最高的伏特加也來自那裡，常用穀物，在波蘭則用馬鈴薯。不過如今全世界都生產各種品質等級的伏特加，幾乎每個生產國都有傑出的例子。產地很重要，但已不再是品質的獨家保證。","Neutral style: minimal flavour, smooth, light and dry.":"中性風格：風味極淡，柔順、輕盈、不甜。","Characterful style: still delicate flavours but a fuller texture.":"有個性的風格：風味仍然細緻，但質地更飽滿。","Clearly non-neutral aromas = almost always added after distillation.":"明顯非中性的香氣 = 幾乎都是蒸餾後添加的。","Traditional homes: Russia, Poland, Finland, Sweden; excellent vodka is now made everywhere.":"傳統故鄉：俄羅斯、波蘭、芬蘭、瑞典；如今到處都有出色的伏特加。","Gin botanicals: juniper comes first":"琴酒的植物性原料：杜松子排第一","Gin is a spirit flavoured with plant ingredients known as botanicals: herbs, seeds, roots, peels and spices. Of all of them, only one is required by law: the juniper berry. It gives gin that resinous, almost pine-forest scent that makes it recognisable from the first sip. For everything else, the distiller has complete freedom.":"琴酒是用稱為植物性原料（botanicals）的植物材料調味的烈酒：香草、種子、根、果皮和香料。其中只有一種是法律要求的：杜松子。它賦予琴酒那種帶樹脂、近乎松林的氣味，讓人從第一口就認得出來。其餘的一切，蒸餾師完全自由。","Alongside juniper, a handful of botanicals turn up in almost every recipe. Coriander seeds bring spicy, citrusy notes; citrus peels such as lemon or orange add freshness. Angelica root and orris root have earthy, floral notes and help bind the other aromas together, rather like foundations holding a house in place.":"除了杜松子，有幾種植物性原料幾乎出現在每一個配方中。芫荽籽帶來辛香、柑橘般的氣息；檸檬或柳橙等柑橘皮增添清新感。歐白芷根和鳶尾根有土壤和花香氣息，並幫助把其他香氣結合在一起，有點像撐住房子的地基。","Because the law insists only on juniper, distillers have experimented enormously in recent years: floral, spicy and citrus-led gins, gins with local herbs or unusual fruits. Gin can also be made by adding artificial flavourings, but the best gins come from redistilling with real botanicals. After flavouring, most gins rest in inert vessels and are bottled colourless.":"因為法律只堅持要有杜松子，蒸餾師近年來做了大量的嘗試：花香型、辛香型和柑橘主導的琴酒，使用當地香草或特殊水果的琴酒。琴酒也可以用添加人工香料的方式製作，但最好的琴酒來自與真正的植物性原料一起再蒸餾。調味後，大多數琴酒在惰性容器中靜置，並以無色裝瓶。","There is, however, a small but growing trend: some producers rest their gin in oak casks. These gins take on a pale lemon colour and some woody notes on top of the botanicals. They remain the exception: if you spot a golden gin on a back bar, it is worth asking whether it has spent time in wood.":"不過有一股規模小但持續成長的趨勢：有些生產者讓琴酒在橡木桶中靜置。這些琴酒帶上淡檸檬色，並在植物香氣之上多了一些木質氣息。它們仍是例外：如果你在後吧檯看到金黃色的琴酒，值得問一問它是否在木桶中存放過。","Juniper is the only compulsory botanical.":"杜松子是唯一強制使用的植物性原料。","Most common botanicals: coriander, citrus peel, angelica, orris.":"最常見的植物性原料：芫荽籽、柑橘皮、歐白芷根、鳶尾根。","The best gins are made by redistillation.":"最好的琴酒是以再蒸餾製作的。","Usually colourless; pale lemon if oak-aged.":"通常無色；經橡木桶陳年則是淡檸檬色。","The base spirit: EU versus USA":"基酒：歐盟與美國的差別","Gin does not start from a raw material but from a ready-made spirit to which botanicals are added. Nearly all gin distillers begin with neutral spirit, which is highly rectified and has no real character of its own. The reason is simple: against a neutral background, like a blank canvas, the scents of juniper and the other botanicals stand out clearly.":"琴酒不是從原料開始，而是從現成的烈酒開始，再加入植物性原料。幾乎所有琴酒蒸餾師都從中性烈酒開始，它經過高度精餾，本身沒有什麼特色。理由很簡單：在中性的背景上，就像一張空白的畫布，杜松子和其他植物性原料的氣味清楚地突顯出來。","In the European Union this choice is a legal requirement: gin must be made from neutral spirit. In the United States the rules are looser. There, a distiller may also use other distilled spirits with some character, or distil the gin straight from a fermented alcoholic liquid without going through a neutral spirit first.":"在歐盟，這項選擇是法律要求：琴酒必須用中性烈酒製作。在美國，規定較寬鬆。那裡的蒸餾師也可以使用其他有些特色的蒸餾烈酒，或直接用發酵的含酒精液體蒸餾琴酒，不必先經過中性烈酒。","This difference is not just technical: it shows up on labels. The same term can mean different things on either side of the Atlantic, as you will see with 'Distilled Gin'. For revision, two rules are enough: in Europe a neutral base is compulsory; in America there is more freedom over both the base and the method.":"這個差別不只是技術上的：它會反映在酒標上。同一個術語在大西洋兩岸可能有不同的意思，「Distilled Gin」就是一例。複習時記住兩條規則就夠了：在歐洲，中性基酒是強制的；在美國，基酒和做法都有更多自由。","Gin starts from a finished spirit, not a raw material.":"琴酒從成品烈酒開始，不是從原料。","EU: neutral spirit is compulsory.":"歐盟：中性烈酒是強制的。","USA: other spirits or direct distillation from a fermented liquid allowed.":"美國：允許使用其他烈酒，或直接用發酵液蒸餾。","Three ways to redistil with botanicals":"與植物性原料一起再蒸餾的三種方式","The traditional way to flavour gin is redistillation: neutral spirit is distilled again together with the botanicals, and their aromas rise with the vapour. There are three approaches, each giving a different result. The first is the most direct: neutral spirit, diluted with water, goes into the pot still together with the botanicals, which sit in the liquid.":"為琴酒調味的傳統方式是再蒸餾：把中性烈酒與植物性原料一起再蒸餾一次，它們的香氣隨蒸氣上升。有三種做法，各有不同的結果。第一種最直接：加水稀釋過的中性烈酒與植物性原料一起放進壺式蒸餾器，植物性原料浸在液體中。","Some distillers leave the botanicals to steep in the spirit for a while before heating begins. The longer the contact, the more flavour is extracted, and the fuller and more intense the gin becomes. It is a little like a herbal tea: a few extra minutes and the cup becomes much more flavourful.":"有些蒸餾師在開始加熱前，先讓植物性原料在烈酒中浸泡一段時間。接觸越久，萃取的風味越多，琴酒也就越飽滿、越濃郁。這有點像泡花草茶：多泡幾分鐘，杯中的味道就濃得多。","The second approach places the botanicals in a basket fitted in the pipe that links the still to the condenser. The botanicals never touch the boiling liquid: only the alcoholic vapours pass through them and pick up their aromas. Less is extracted, so the gin is lighter and more delicate. These stills are sometimes called 'Carterhead' stills.":"第二種做法把植物性原料放在籃子裡，籃子裝在連接蒸餾器和冷凝器的管路中。植物性原料從不接觸沸騰的液體：只有含酒精的蒸氣穿過它們，帶走香氣。萃取得較少，所以琴酒更清淡、更細緻。這種蒸餾器有時稱為「Carterhead」蒸餾器。","The third approach distils botanicals separately, one by one or in small groups. When distilled together they interact and their aromas change during the process; on their own they give purer flavours. Some distillers run most botanicals together and then add a single separate distillate to make it stand out; others process every botanical individually and blend everything at the end.":"第三種做法把植物性原料分開蒸餾，一種一種或分成小組。一起蒸餾時它們會交互作用，香氣在過程中改變；單獨蒸餾則得到更純淨的風味。有些蒸餾師把大部分植物性原料一起蒸餾，再加入單獨一種餾出液來突顯它；另一些則把每種植物性原料個別處理，最後全部調和。","Botanicals in the liquid (with steeping): fuller gin.":"植物性原料浸在液體中（先浸泡）：琴酒較飽滿。","Basket in the vapour path: lighter gin.":"籃子放在蒸氣的路徑上：琴酒較清淡。","Separate distillation: purer flavours, then blending.":"分開蒸餾：風味更純淨，之後再調和。","Together, botanicals interact and change during distillation.":"放在一起時，植物性原料在蒸餾過程中交互作用並改變。","Label terms: London Dry, Distilled Gin, Old Tom":"酒標術語：London Dry、Distilled Gin、Old Tom","'London Dry Gin', or simply 'Dry Gin', is the most tightly defined style in the European Union. All of its flavour must come from redistillation with botanicals: nothing is added afterwards. It also cannot be sweetened. Despite the name, it is not a place of origin: a London Dry can be made anywhere, as long as the method is followed. The term usually appears prominently on the front label.":"「London Dry Gin」，或簡稱「Dry Gin」，是歐盟定義最嚴格的類型。它所有的風味都必須來自與植物性原料一起再蒸餾：之後不添加任何東西。它也不能加糖。雖然叫這個名字，它卻不是產地：London Dry 可以在任何地方製作，只要遵守這套做法。這個術語通常醒目地標在正標上。","'Distilled Gin' is a curious case, because its meaning changes from one continent to the other. In the European Union it means a gin redistilled with botanicals that may still have further flavourings added after redistillation. In the United States, by contrast, 'Distilled Gin' means all the flavour must come from redistillation, a requirement closer to the European London Dry.":"「Distilled Gin」是有趣的例子，因為它的意思在兩個大陸之間不同。在歐盟，它表示與植物性原料一起再蒸餾的琴酒，但再蒸餾後仍可以添加其他香料。在美國則相反，「Distilled Gin」表示所有風味都必須來自再蒸餾，這項要求更接近歐洲的 London Dry。","'Old Tom' is a style older than dry gins, dating from before tastes moved towards dry. It is not a legally defined term, but on a label it is normally used to signal a sweetened gin. In a historic cocktail that calls for Old Tom, using a London Dry would therefore give a drier, sharper drink than intended.":"「Old Tom」是比不甜琴酒更古老的風格，出現在口味轉向不甜之前。它不是有法律定義的術語，但在酒標上通常用來表示加糖的琴酒。所以在指定使用 Old Tom 的歷史調酒中，改用 London Dry 會讓飲品比原本的設計更不甜、更銳利。","London Dry: redistillation only, no sweetening; not a place of origin.":"London Dry：只靠再蒸餾，不加糖；不是產地。","EU Distilled Gin: flavours may be added after redistillation.":"歐盟的 Distilled Gin：再蒸餾後可以添加風味。","US Distilled Gin: all flavour from redistillation.":"美國的 Distilled Gin：所有風味都來自再蒸餾。","Old Tom: historic, not legally defined, signals sweetened gin.":"Old Tom：歷史風格，沒有法律定義，表示加糖的琴酒。","Flavour and colour: natural or artificial":"風味與顏色：天然或人工","Flavours added to a spirit fall into two broad families: natural and artificial. Natural flavours come from fruit or botanicals, meaning herbs and spices. Two main techniques extract them. Maceration leaves the material soaking in alcohol, from a few hours to several months, sometimes with gentle heat. The resulting liquid is sometimes called a 'tincture'.":"加進烈酒的風味分為兩大家族：天然和人工。天然風味來自水果或植物性原料，也就是香草和香料。萃取它們的主要技術有兩種。浸漬是把材料泡在酒精中，從幾小時到幾個月，有時稍微加熱。得到的液體有時稱為「酊劑」（tincture）。","Maceration extracts both colour and a broad range of flavours, but it cannot isolate one particular aroma. If the alcohol is too strong it may also pull out unpleasant flavours, which is why it is often diluted first. Redistillation, instead, puts spirit and botanicals back in the still: the distiller takes the hearts cut when the wanted aromas come through. The result is sometimes called a 'distillate'.":"浸漬會萃取顏色和範圍廣泛的風味，但無法分離出某一種特定的香氣。如果酒精太烈，還可能帶出不好的風味，所以常先稀釋。再蒸餾則是把烈酒和植物性原料放回蒸餾器：蒸餾師在想要的香氣出現時切取酒心。成品有時稱為「餾出液」（distillate）。","Some delicate botanicals are damaged by the heat of a normal still. For them, a vacuum still is used: in a vacuum liquids boil at lower temperatures, so fragile aromas such as cucumber are captured more successfully. Other producers do not handle botanicals at all and buy ready-made natural flavourings from specialist suppliers.":"有些細緻的植物性原料會被一般蒸餾器的熱破壞。對它們要使用真空蒸餾器：在真空中液體在較低的溫度沸騰，所以小黃瓜這類脆弱的香氣能更成功地捕捉下來。另一些生產者完全不處理植物性原料，而是向專業供應商購買現成的天然香料。","Artificial flavours are man-made but imitate flavours found in nature; they are simply blended into the spirit, a technique known as 'cold compounding'. Colour, too, can be natural or artificial. Colour extracted from plants is unstable and can vary from bottle to bottle, so even premium producers often use some artificial colouring, which is behind the vivid shades of many liqueurs.":"人工香料是人造的，但模仿自然界中的風味；它們只是單純調入烈酒，這種技術稱為「冷混法」（cold compounding）。顏色也可以是天然或人工的。從植物萃取的顏色不穩定，可能每一瓶都不一樣，所以連高級生產者也常使用一些人工色素，許多利口酒鮮豔的色調就是這樣來的。","Maceration = tincture: colour and broad flavour, no isolating.":"浸漬 = 酊劑：顏色和廣泛的風味，無法分離。","Redistillation = distillate: the hearts cut is chosen.":"再蒸餾 = 餾出液：選取酒心。","Vacuum still: low temperatures for fragile aromas.":"真空蒸餾器：低溫，適合脆弱的香氣。","Artificial flavours = cold compounding; natural colours are unstable.":"人工香料 = 冷混法；天然顏色不穩定。","Spiced rum and flavoured vodka":"香料蘭姆酒與調味伏特加","Spiced rum is a very popular category. The typical base is a golden rum that has already been sweetened, with spices added. Producers rarely reveal the recipe, but vanilla and cinnamon appear among the declared flavours of several brands. If natural flavours are used, maceration is the likely method: redistilling would damage the aged rum character and strip out its colour.":"香料蘭姆酒是非常受歡迎的類別。典型的基酒是已經加過糖的金色蘭姆酒，再加入香料。生產者很少公開配方，但香草和肉桂出現在好幾個品牌標明的風味中。如果使用天然風味，可能的做法是浸漬：再蒸餾會破壞陳年蘭姆酒的特色，並去除它的顏色。","Flavoured vodka has a long tradition in Eastern Europe, its historic home. For centuries it has been flavoured with honey, fruit and spices, nearly always by maceration. Some recipes survive to this day: the best-known example is vodka flavoured with bison grass, an aromatic herb with hay-like, vanilla notes.":"調味伏特加在它的歷史故鄉東歐有悠久的傳統。數百年來，人們用蜂蜜、水果和香料為它調味，幾乎都是以浸漬進行。有些配方流傳至今：最知名的例子是用野牛草調味的伏特加，那是一種帶乾草和香草氣息的芳香草本植物。","The modern boom is more recent: today nearly every vodka brand has at least one flavoured version, with vanilla, fruit, pepper or even chilli. Inexpensive vodkas usually rely on artificial or ready-made natural flavourings. Premium products work with the raw ingredients: they macerate fruit or botanicals in neutral spirit and then redistil, giving pure, precise flavours.":"現代的熱潮則是較近的事：如今幾乎每個伏特加品牌都至少有一款調味版本，有香草、水果、胡椒，甚至辣椒。平價的伏特加通常靠人工香料或現成的天然香料。高級產品則使用原始材料：把水果或植物性原料浸漬在中性烈酒中，再重新蒸餾，得到純淨、精確的風味。","Spiced rum: sweetened golden rum + spices (often vanilla, cinnamon).":"香料蘭姆酒：加糖的金色蘭姆酒 + 香料（常是香草、肉桂）。","Spiced rum is macerated: redistilling would remove colour and character.":"香料蘭姆酒用浸漬：再蒸餾會去除顏色和特色。","Traditional vodka: Eastern Europe, maceration, bison grass.":"傳統伏特加：東歐、浸漬、野牛草。","Premium modern vodka: maceration then redistillation.":"高級的現代伏特加：先浸漬，再重新蒸餾。","Aniseed spirits: pastis and absinthe":"茴香烈酒：pastis 與苦艾酒","Aniseed spirits are made all around the Mediterranean: pastis and absinthe in France, ouzo in Greece, raki in Turkey. They share one compound, anethole, which gives the typical aniseed taste. It comes mainly from three plants: aniseed, fennel and star anise. They usually start from neutral spirit, are unaged, and are coloured with both natural and artificial colours.":"地中海沿岸各地都生產茴香烈酒：法國的 pastis 和苦艾酒、希臘的 ouzo、土耳其的 raki。它們有一種共同的化合物：茴香腦（anethole），帶來典型的茴香味。它主要來自三種植物：茴香籽、茴香和八角。它們通常從中性烈酒開始，不經陳年，並用天然和人工色素上色。","Anethole also has a striking effect. When water is added, it comes out of solution and forms a milky, opaque suspension: the clear liquid turns cloudy in the glass. This is called 'louching'. Because these spirits are drunk heavily diluted, watching the louche appear is a traditional part of how they are served.":"茴香腦還有一種引人注目的效果。加水時，它從溶液中析出，形成乳白、不透明的懸浮液：清澈的液體在杯中變混濁。這稱為「乳濁現象」（louching）。因為這些烈酒是大幅稀釋後飲用的，看著乳濁出現是傳統飲用方式的一部分。","Pastis is the best known of the aniseed spirits. As well as aniseed, fennel and star anise, it must contain liquorice. It must be sweetened, so most pastis is medium or sweet, and it is usually coloured yellow, green or green-brown. Historically, pastis took the place of absinthe when absinthe was banned.":"Pastis 是最知名的茴香烈酒。除了茴香籽、茴香和八角，它還必須含有甘草。它必須加糖，所以大多數 pastis 是中等或甜，並通常染成黃色、綠色或綠棕色。在歷史上，苦艾酒被禁時，pastis 取代了它的位置。","Absinthe was banned for decades because of social and political pressure in the late nineteenth century. It is allowed again but has no legal definition. The traditional method resembles pastis with two differences: it is not sweetened, since each drinker sweetens it to taste, and it should contain wormwood, a floral, bitter plant. Bottled very strong, it is meant to be diluted to no more than wine strength.":"苦艾酒因為十九世紀末的社會和政治壓力而被禁了數十年。如今它再度獲准，但沒有法律定義。傳統的做法與 pastis 相似，有兩點不同：它不加糖，因為由每位飲用者依口味自行加糖；而且應該含有苦艾，一種帶花香和苦味的植物。它裝瓶時濃度非常高，是要稀釋到不超過葡萄酒的濃度來喝的。","Anethole from aniseed, fennel and star anise.":"茴香腦來自茴香籽、茴香和八角。","Louching: water turns the spirit cloudy and opaque.":"乳濁現象：水讓烈酒變得混濁不透明。","Pastis: liquorice compulsory, always sweetened.":"Pastis：甘草是強制的，一律加糖。","Absinthe: wormwood, unsweetened, no legal definition.":"苦艾酒：苦艾、不加糖、沒有法律定義。","Bitters: aperitif, digestif, cocktail":"苦味酒：開胃、消化、調酒用","Bitters are spirits, usually with a neutral base, that have an obvious bitter taste from one or more botanicals. Common bittering ingredients include quinine, gentian, bitter orange and artichoke. A useful tasting detail: bitterness cannot be smelled, because only the tongue detects it. Other aromatic botanicals and sugar are added to balance it.":"苦味酒（bitters）是通常以中性烈酒為基底的烈酒，因一種或多種植物性原料而有明顯的苦味。常見的苦味材料包括奎寧、龍膽、苦橙和朝鮮薊。一個實用的品飲細節：苦味是聞不到的，因為只有舌頭能察覺。其他芳香的植物性原料和糖是加來平衡它的。","Bitters fall into three broad categories. Aperitif bitters are often brightly coloured, with bitterness balanced by sweetness. They are drunk before a meal, usually in a long drink with soda or in a cocktail. Picturing a bright red glass with ice and a slice of orange helps fix the idea.":"苦味酒大致分為三類。開胃苦味酒常有鮮豔的顏色，苦味由甜味平衡。它們在餐前飲用，通常做成加蘇打水的長飲或用於調酒。想像一杯加了冰塊和一片柳橙的鮮紅色飲品，有助於記住這個概念。","Digestif bitters generally have pronounced bitterness and intense flavour. They began as an aid to digestion and are still enjoyed after a meal, often neat. Cocktail bitters, finally, are high in strength, highly concentrated and intensely bitter: they are not drunk on their own but used in dashes, like a seasoning, to add an extra dimension to a cocktail.":"消化苦味酒通常有明顯的苦味和濃郁的風味。它們最初是用來幫助消化的，至今仍在餐後享用，常是純飲。最後，調酒用苦精濃度高、高度濃縮、苦味強烈：它們不單獨飲用，而是像調味料一樣以滴數使用，為調酒增添另一個層次。","Common bittering agents: quinine, gentian, bitter orange, artichoke.":"常見的苦味劑：奎寧、龍膽、苦橙、朝鮮薊。","Bitterness is detected only on the palate, not the nose.":"苦味只在口中察覺，聞不到。","Aperitif: colourful, sweeter, in long drinks or cocktails.":"開胃苦味酒：色彩鮮豔、較甜，用於長飲或調酒。","Digestif: bitter and intense. Cocktail: strong, concentrated, in dashes.":"消化苦味酒：苦而濃郁。調酒用苦精：濃烈、濃縮，以滴數使用。","A liqueur's base and flavourings":"利口酒的基酒與調味料","A liqueur is, in short, a flavoured spirit that has been sweetened. Most start from neutral spirit, a clean backdrop that lets the added flavours shine. Some liqueurs, however, choose a characterful base: there are liqueurs built on Cognac or on Scotch whisky, where the starting spirit can be tasted and becomes part of the style.":"簡單來說，利口酒就是加了糖的調味烈酒。大多數從中性烈酒開始，那是讓添加的風味發光的乾淨背景。不過有些利口酒選擇有個性的基酒：有建立在 Cognac 或 Scotch 威士忌上的利口酒，嚐得出起點的烈酒，而它也成為風格的一部分。","There is no limit on flavourings. Some producers focus on a single taste, such as one fruit or seed; others use complex, often secret recipes with dozens of herbs and spices. One special ingredient is cream: it needs complex techniques so that it does not form lumps in the bottle. Cream liqueurs are among the very few truly opaque alcoholic drinks.":"調味料沒有限制。有些生產者專注於單一的味道，例如一種水果或種子；另一些使用複雜、常是保密的配方，含數十種香草和香料。有一種特別的材料是鮮奶油：它需要複雜的技術才不會在瓶中結塊。奶油利口酒是極少數真正不透明的酒精飲料。","To find your way among hundreds of liqueurs, it helps to group them by their main flavour. The four most useful groups are: herb; fruit; seed, nut and kernel; and cream. Faced with an unfamiliar bottle, just ask which family its dominant flavour comes from: that makes it much easier to compare two liqueurs and decide how to use them.":"要在數百種利口酒中找到方向，依主要風味分類很有幫助。最實用的四個類別是：香草；水果；種子、堅果和果核；以及奶油。面對一瓶陌生的酒，只要問它的主導風味來自哪一個家族：這樣比較兩款利口酒並決定怎麼使用就容易得多。","Liqueur = flavoured spirit + sweetened.":"利口酒 = 調味烈酒 + 加糖。","Base usually neutral; sometimes characterful (Cognac, Scotch).":"基酒通常是中性的；有時有個性（Cognac、Scotch）。","No limit on flavours; cream needs special techniques.":"風味沒有限制；鮮奶油需要特殊技術。","Groups: herb; fruit; seed, nut and kernel; cream.":"類別：香草；水果；種子、堅果和果核；奶油。","Always sweet, often coloured":"一定是甜的，常有顏色","What sets a liqueur apart from a plain flavoured spirit is sugar. The legal minimum varies from country to country, but the outcome is always the same: every liqueur is correctly described as sweet. In tasting, then, there is no such thing as a dry liqueur; if a product is not sweet, it is another kind of flavoured spirit.":"讓利口酒有別於單純調味烈酒的是糖。法定的最低量因國家而異，但結果總是相同：每一款利口酒的正確描述都是甜。所以在品飲中，沒有不甜的利口酒這回事；如果產品不甜，它就是另一種調味烈酒。","Colour, on the other hand, is optional but very common. Artificial colours are widely used, which is why bar shelves display liqueurs in electric blue, emerald green or ruby red. Natural colour extracted from plants exists, but it is unstable, so many producers support or replace it with approved food colourings.":"顏色則不是必要的，但非常常見。人工色素使用很廣，所以酒吧的層架上陳列著寶藍色、翠綠色或寶石紅色的利口酒。從植物萃取的天然顏色確實存在，但不穩定，所以許多生產者用核准的食用色素輔助或取代它。"});(window.TWG_I18N_F=window.TWG_I18N_F||{})["zh-hant/s2"]=1;
